ntext2D::GetImageData (Coverity CIDs 1703922, 1703918) r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nA zero width or height already throws IndexSizeError earlier.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339440\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp"], "git_node": "1ab48edec29de5fa5d82dcdb16fd70b58690d75a", "git_parents": ["e98b1ab7ffa04be0f5646e9ad6f3dacb6ddc93cf"], "node": "62d284f615bd013e6ed64103428793fcd0778df3", "parents": ["ddfa0b045a542f07cda3334d7789af1d3dd4fc6a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088798 - Return false from PathCairo hit tests when the transform isn't invertible (Coverity CIDs 1603789, 1603786) r=lsalzman\n\nThis matches the Skia backend, instead of hit testing against the\nuntransformed point.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339438\n", "files": ["gfx/2d/PathCairo.cpp"], "git_node": "9daa76f8a1e796d5ad865aa8316126591fca4ccb", "git_parents": ["1ab48edec29de5fa5d82dcdb16fd70b58690d75a"], "node": "e07c68f18c578f215f23a49692b0f0fdf0d4ad35", "parents": ["62d284f615bd013e6ed64103428793fcd0778df3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Chevobbe \u003cnchevobbe@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089384 - [DevTools Release Tasks - Cycle 161] Update MDN compat data. r=devtools-reviewers,jdescottes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339802\n", "files": ["devtools/shared/compatibility/dataset/css-properties.json"], "git_node": "54b5cfe5576fdca3910f2e71295663f4de4a202a", "git_parents": ["9daa76f8a1e796d5ad865aa8316126591fca4ccb"], "node": "b6d1d6ba3c39b298b73ff1b687ddf06ee7d68f2c", "parents": ["e07c68f18c578f215f23a49692b0f0fdf0d4ad35"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088809 - Remove the null checks after std::make_unique in the heap snapshot writer (Coverity CIDs 1704204, 1704203, 1704199) r=devtools-reviewers,jdescottes\n\nstd::make_unique is infallible, so these checks are dead code.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339448\n", "files": ["devtools/shared/heapsnapshot/HeapSnapshot.cpp"], "git_node": "cff5eec3570844f8b9d2484c4cf50b659c4d9b40", "git_parents": ["54b5cfe5576fdca3910f2e71295663f4de4a202a"], "node": "7b0ae3def39efecad38bab5d525a7672c5ac4d4f", "parents": ["b6d1d6ba3c39b298b73ff1b687ddf06ee7d68f2c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089077 - Update the documentation skill's API-reference notes for the landed jsdoc plugins. r=sylvestre DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339660\n", "files": [".agents/skills/documentation/references/js-api-references.md", ".claude/skills/documentation/references/js-api-references.md"], "git_node": "146c194b2dd17440151f52b885e6966615b9d7db", "git_parents": ["cff5eec3570844f8b9d2484c4cf50b659c4d9b40"], "node": "5e026e69396056ee9fd100153561c875bfae4eab", "parents": ["7b0ae3def39efecad38bab5d525a7672c5ac4d4f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088885 - Add size mismatch log to RenderAndroidImageReaderImageTextureHost::EnsureLockable() r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nMOZ_RELEASE_ASSERT() is relaxed to MOZ_ASSERT().\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339743\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderAndroidImageReaderImageTextureHost.cpp"], "git_node": "a7dc4a62b2abccbf99373fffcff989141c3ed738", "git_parents": ["146c194b2dd17440151f52b885e6966615b9d7db"], "node": "46bbf50d0970272737f99976e3328b5cc35c7791", "parents": ["5e026e69396056ee9fd100153561c875bfae4eab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2087615 [Wayland] Align allocated wl_shm pool to page size r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\" at dev request for causing Bug 2088923\n\nThis reverts commit 46b72140a33df474e32b8df00c2ccc12873c32bd.\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.cpp"], "git_node": "f5652fc5dd26fb6716bc5434376052eb88446c8c", "git_parents": ["a7dc4a62b2abccbf99373fffcff989141c3ed738"], "node": "0c094062a7edb73d80f46516d91778a3856d9413", "parents": ["46bbf50d0970272737f99976e3328b5cc35c7791"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Farre \u003cfarre@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088091 - onnavigate should fire after onbeforeunload. r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338774\n", "files": ["docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "dom/navigation/Navigation.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/navigation-api/navigate-event/navigate-navigation-back-cross-document.html.ini"], "git_node": "0aeb3c835ab367266218679b25fe4edfccb6eca5", "git_parents": ["f5652fc5dd26fb6716bc5434376052eb88446c8c"], "node": "75bb790e8fc7b3eb0aa6e5c55aa50355b1d7269d", "parents": ["0c094062a7edb73d80f46516d91778a3856d9413"], "tags": []}, {"author": "csalinezh \u003ccsalinezh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084416 - Resolve presses in text-control padding like single clicks. r=masayuki\n\nCurrently, A double click in a text control's padding or empty area\nselected no word, and a long press there left the caret where it was\nwhile showing its Paste menu. MoveCaretToEventPoint resolves single\nclicks with only SKIP_HIDDEN, whereas SelectByTypeAtPoint and\nAccessibleCaretManager::SelectWordOrShortcut also set\nIGNORE_NATIVE_ANONYMOUS_SUBTREE, with which a point on the text\ncontrol's own frame resolves outside the control.\n\nIGNORE_NATIVE_ANONYMOUS_SUBTREE was added for bug 1872302 so that moving\nthe document's caret up or down a line can't enter text controls.\nFrames within a text control use that control's independent selection,\nwhere the editor's content belongs. Add\nnsIFrame::GetContentOffsetsFromPointForSelection, which resolves the\npoint for such frames as a single click does, but never outside the\nroot of the independent selection, e.g. to an ancestor with\n`user-select: all`, and use it in both places. Caret dragging, which\nalso sets the flag, first constrains its frame to the selection's\nanchor subtree, and is unaffected.\n\nA double click there now selects the word where the click before it\nputs the caret. A long press there places the caret at that position\nwith its Paste menu, as in contenteditable and other content\n(bug 1448730); whether it should select the word is left to a\nfollow-up.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336882\n", "files": ["layout/base/AccessibleCaretManager.cpp", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.h", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/selection/resources/text-control-selection-around-text.html", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/selection/text-control-longpress-around-text.html", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/selection/text-control-multiclick-around-text.html"], "git_node": "38ef96739f1da056b4063360ac7bc078bedf4871", "git_parents": ["0aeb3c835ab367266218679b25fe4edfccb6eca5"], "node": "c9203b1d45347986fdefea55a54ca38f83227895", "parents": ["75bb790e8fc7b3eb0aa6e5c55aa50355b1d7269d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087980 - Make some nsIPrincipal IPC parameters non-nullable and simplify some of the validation. r=nika,ipc-reviewers\n\nThis just the diff of the next patch a bit smaller.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339176\n", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/file/uri/BlobURLProtocolHandler.cpp", "dom/ipc/ContentChild.cpp", "dom/ipc/ContentChild.h", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.h", "dom/ipc/PContent.ipdl", "ipc/glue/BackgroundParentImpl.cpp", "ipc/glue/BackgroundParentImpl.h", "toolkit/components/antitracking/ContentBlockingUserInteraction.cpp", "toolkit/components/url-classifier/nsUrlClassifierDBService.cpp"], "git_node": "fc7f91a35976d4f84bd3b21ca2b1b0a4fbc29de4", "git_parents": ["38ef96739f1da056b4063360ac7bc078bedf4871"], "node": "b7ac087f509852d82057653cdbfbd39781e31bc5", "parents": ["c9203b1d45347986fdefea55a54ca38f83227895"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053674 - Part 1: Always clear the ORB frontend context state. r=bthrall\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333097\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/JSValidatorChild.cpp"], "git_node": "84bac6db614e93ca6cc60a77ba2c0a2b2540c7c5", "git_parents": ["fc7f91a35976d4f84bd3b21ca2b1b0a4fbc29de4"], "node": "2f4df7bca0b4d650c9cd61c156dc429f1f4f2bd4", "parents": ["b7ac087f509852d82057653cdbfbd39781e31bc5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053674 - Part 2: Add shareScriptData option to the FrontendContext creation. r=bthrall\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333098\n", "files": ["dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "js/public/experimental/CompileScript.h", "js/src/frontend/FrontendContext.cpp", "js/src/frontend/FrontendContext.h", "js/src/jsapi-tests/testFrontendErrors.cpp", "js/src/vm/JSScript.cpp"], "git_node": "3094d0eb8b6be452a30bae9eccbbb0f753aab5f6", "git_parents": ["84bac6db614e93ca6cc60a77ba2c0a2b2540c7c5"], "node": "4959b13e77481688ddac6bd75b793aff95c6f806", "parents": ["2f4df7bca0b4d650c9cd61c156dc429f1f4f2bd4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053674 - Part 3: Do not hold the script data in ORB process. r=bthrall\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333099\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/JSOracleChild.h"], "git_node": "bf8c55f59e23812a1db519ad98d4904721ebffd7", "git_parents": ["3094d0eb8b6be452a30bae9eccbbb0f753aab5f6"], "node": "0f472a43bc9640ffa0f806ff14976401fd42e9ca", "parents": ["4959b13e77481688ddac6bd75b793aff95c6f806"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082798 - Test; r=smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332575\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/fullscreen/file_fullscreen-iframe-multiple-middle.html", "dom/base/test/fullscreen/mochitest.toml", "dom/base/test/fullscreen/test_fullscreen_iframe_nested_multiple.html"], "git_node": "8568bdeb83555a63d9a5d8b9050f5f4c322cf152", "git_parents": ["bf8c55f59e23812a1db519ad98d4904721ebffd7"], "node": "a3ea0f51bb2d4480138dd3cb12f450d8d2d5021b", "parents": ["0f472a43bc9640ffa0f806ff14976401fd42e9ca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082798 - Test reentrancy during fullscreen exit; r=smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333688\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/fullscreen/mochitest.toml", "dom/base/test/fullscreen/test_fullscreen_exit_reentrancy.html"], "git_node": "fe55b9df0020f594721cdfbf75b41260c5f89a19", "git_parents": ["8568bdeb83555a63d9a5d8b9050f5f4c322cf152"], "node": "a754455f9a202ec68af69ae047e7b5c37090c171", "parents": ["a3ea0f51bb2d4480138dd3cb12f450d8d2d5021b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083909 - Add test; r=smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334288\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/base/test/test_window_proxy_unlinked_inner.html"], "git_node": "1eec093a77ae0450bd842d3ccbe881449debb382", "git_parents": ["fe55b9df0020f594721cdfbf75b41260c5f89a19"], "node": "be411b1b862fc32cd3b8262bdcf49f22c69ae43c", "parents": ["a754455f9a202ec68af69ae047e7b5c37090c171"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Damien Carver \u003cdcarver@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086657 - Add a logModule option to console.createInstance, separate from the prefix. r=devtools-reviewers,ochameau\n\nThe prefix option of console.createInstance has two jobs. It names the\nMOZ_LOG module of the console, and it is the label printed before each\nmessage, in stdout and in the console events DevTools shows. These jobs\nconflict: a readable label, for example one containing a colon, is often\na module name MOZ_LOG cannot parse, and a label computed at run time\ncreates a new module for each value.\n\nThe new logModule option names the MOZ_LOG module, so the prefix can be\njust a label. In stdout and in ConsoleEvent.prefix, each message is now\npreceded by \"\u003clogModule\u003e: \u003cprefix\u003e: \". Messages sent to MOZ_LOG only get\nthe prefix, since MOZ_LOG already prints the module name.\n\nA console created with a prefix and no logModule behaves as before: its\nprefix names the MOZ_LOG module. This keeps existing callers working, in\nthe tree and outside it (e.g. comm-central), until they move to\nlogModule. This use is deprecated.\n\nCode that must run on several versions of Firefox can pass the same\nvalue as logModule and prefix. Older versions ignore logModule and use\nthe prefix as the module. This version uses logModule as the module and\ndoesn't print the same name twice.\n\nA console with neither a logModule nor a prefix still logs to the\n\"console\" module.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337641\n", "files": ["dom/chrome-webidl/ConsoleInstance.webidl", "dom/console/Console.cpp", "dom/console/Console.h", "dom/console/ConsoleInstance.cpp", "dom/console/tests/browser_console_to_mozlog.js", "dom/console/tests/xpcshell/test_console_logModule.js", "dom/console/tests/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml", "toolkit/components/backgroundtasks/tests/BackgroundTask_console.sys.mjs", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.dom.d.ts"], "git_node": "4c5bc49c2b9623d09f45198bc1d122be57f66702", "git_parents": ["1eec093a77ae0450bd842d3ccbe881449debb382"], "node": "eeb1e291743ee34ffeecef99cc75b042af034450", "parents": ["be411b1b862fc32cd3b8262bdcf49f22c69ae43c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087984 - Use Maybe\u003cnsID\u003e/nsIDRef for operationID r=baku,cookie-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D288359\n", "files": ["dom/cookiestore/CookieStoreNotificationWatcher.cpp", "dom/cookiestore/CookieStoreNotificationWatcher.h", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp", "netwerk/cookie/CookieNotification.cpp", "netwerk/cookie/CookieNotification.h", "netwerk/cookie/CookiePersistentStorage.cpp", "netwerk/cookie/CookieService.cpp", "netwerk/cookie/CookieService.h", "netwerk/cookie/CookieServiceChild.cpp", "netwerk/cookie/CookieServiceParent.cpp", "netwerk/cookie/CookieServiceParent.h", "netwerk/cookie/CookieStorage.cpp", "netwerk/cookie/CookieStorage.h", "netwerk/cookie/nsICookieNotification.idl", "netwerk/test/gtest/TestCookie.cpp"], "git_node": "12aa0d4d37605212534aafb0a6fd44541b4952c2", "git_parents": ["4c5bc49c2b9623d09f45198bc1d122be57f66702"], "node": "81a7eab947d47f0881cbf91371eddb709a2bd60d", "parents": ["eeb1e291743ee34ffeecef99cc75b042af034450"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2053674 - Part 3: Do not hold the script data in ORB process. r=bthrall\" for causing spidermonkey bustages at FrontendContext\n\nThis reverts commit bf8c55f59e23812a1db519ad98d4904721ebffd7.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2053674 - Part 2: Add shareScriptData option to the FrontendContext creation. r=bthrall\"\n\nThis reverts commit 3094d0eb8b6be452a30bae9eccbbb0f753aab5f6.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2053674 - Part 1: Always clear the ORB frontend context state. r=bthrall\"\n\nThis reverts commit 84bac6db614e93ca6cc60a77ba2c0a2b2540c7c5.\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/JSOracleChild.h", "dom/ipc/JSValidatorChild.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "js/public/experimental/CompileScript.h", "js/src/frontend/FrontendContext.cpp", "js/src/frontend/FrontendContext.h", "js/src/jsapi-tests/testFrontendErrors.cpp", "js/src/vm/JSScript.cpp"], "git_node": "94563da9859afe86f6d9473a8783141c57e37a72", "git_parents": ["12aa0d4d37605212534aafb0a6fd44541b4952c2"], "node": "01ad3f9a72244f1ba063d3d9a08fe3003823866c", "parents": ["81a7eab947d47f0881cbf91371eddb709a2bd60d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088320 - Check the sparse profile and cache of git `run-task` tasks r=taskgraph-reviewers,jcristau\n\ncheck_run_task_caches stopped at the first of --gecko-shallow-clone and\n--gecko-sparse-profile, and common_setup passes the shallow flag first, so the\nsparse profile of a git task was never checked. check_run_task_caches now reads\nboth flags.\n\nrun-task only ever widens a cached git checkout\n(https://github.com/taskcluster/taskgraph/pull/1039), so sparse and full git\ntasks share the pool's checkouts-git cache and do not need a checkouts-sparse\none.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339024\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/test_transforms_task.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/task.py"], "git_node": "5d0976662ac04eb8fbca82b03c1ad97e31bfd751", "git_parents": ["94563da9859afe86f6d9473a8783141c57e37a72"], "node": "6cdb5f8dc60ba7fd33cc05bf76be45113188396d", "parents": ["01ad3f9a72244f1ba063d3d9a08fe3003823866c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088320 - Use sparse profiles for git `run-task` tasks r=taskgraph-reviewers,jcristau\n\nFor git checkouts, run-task reads the patterns from GECKO_SPARSE_PATTERNS\ninstead of from the profile.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339025\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/test_transforms_job.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/job/run_task.py"], "git_node": "37d1f2620134b19486e2d5b850abb2f918fcc94f", "git_parents": ["5d0976662ac04eb8fbca82b03c1ad97e31bfd751"], "node": "a1f632905ab4ed6df31259e7b69db054e7e03631", "parents": ["6cdb5f8dc60ba7fd33cc05bf76be45113188396d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088985: Update the audio receive stream's sync group in place r=pehrsons\n\nRecreating the stream reset its inbound-rtp counters under the same\nstats id whenever another transceiver changed the A/V sync pairing,\ne.g. when a video transceiver is stopped.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339560\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/libwebrtcglue/AudioConduit.cpp"], "git_node": "cbecddbf24f0283654be18f30c1c4f048972d0ed", "git_parents": ["37d1f2620134b19486e2d5b850abb2f918fcc94f"], "node": "eb25c411d466677b9b3eeecebc38b13fd46b5c1d", "parents": ["a1f632905ab4ed6df31259e7b69db054e7e03631"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082099 - Only reject cross-site speculation-rules prefetches. r=necko-reviewers,jesup\n\nThe spec separates prefetches by network partition key, so same-site\ncross-origin prefetches share the document's partition and need none of the\ncross-site isolation. Gate on the site instead of the origin, and rename\ndom.speculation_rules.same_origin_only to dom.speculation_rules.same_site_only\naccordingly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331538\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/client-hints/redirect.https.sub.html.ini"], "git_node": "334fda58944b1fd5fe59092bffd740c4338ea1e9", "git_parents": ["cbecddbf24f0283654be18f30c1c4f048972d0ed"], "node": "2da70219772c564e71d113788b70bacd7a6ab001", "parents": ["eb25c411d466677b9b3eeecebc38b13fd46b5c1d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077601 - Serve a prefetch-activated navigation from the record's own cache entry. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nLooking up the navigation URL in the HTTP cache can return a different\nNo-Vary-Search-equivalent entry than the one the prefetch stored. Open the\nentry the prefetch record holds instead, read-only, so the navigation gets the\nrecord's response as the spec requires. Records reached through redirects keep\nthe existing lookup for now.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331540\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.h", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentLoadListener.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/no-vary-search/prefetch-single.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "843ac1437de08f95b477a50849cf649b97a6d110", "git_parents": ["334fda58944b1fd5fe59092bffd740c4338ea1e9"], "node": "0ae682bae842348668657c27d6cef20fe85dbe91", "parents": ["2da70219772c564e71d113788b70bacd7a6ab001"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082095 - Reject non-trustworthy and cross-site redirects of speculation-rules prefetches. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nThe spec rejects a prefetch whose current URL is not potentially trustworthy\non every redirect hop, not only the first one. Cross-site prefetches are also\nnot supported yet (the isolated, uncredentialed partition isn't implemented),\nso while dom.speculation_rules.same_site_only is set, don't follow a redirect\noff the document's site either.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331541\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.cpp"], "git_node": "225bd93a5d0b2f004446eb67531cde00fc535514", "git_parents": ["843ac1437de08f95b477a50849cf649b97a6d110"], "node": "44c8d8318eeba824daa9f282bee89dbc53ded84c", "parents": ["0ae682bae842348668657c27d6cef20fe85dbe91"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080083 - Use a keepalive fetch to unblock the in-flight prefetch in prefetch-single-with-hint.https.html. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nFirefox cancels the page's in-flight requests when a navigation starts, so the\nplain fetch sent from onbeforeunload never reached the server and the in-flight\nprefetch was never released.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333897\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/no-vary-search/prefetch-single-with-hint.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prefetch/no-vary-search/prefetch-single-with-hint.https.html"], "git_node": "c605673f3fa9e29d19548db00fb8efde53d0b5ec", "git_parents": ["225bd93a5d0b2f004446eb67531cde00fc535514"], "node": "4da9faefaeda1e79a05014e9db4e7e640b464457", "parents": ["44c8d8318eeba824daa9f282bee89dbc53ded84c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081210 - Add gtests for GMP service creation racing the main thread and shutdown. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335182\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestGMPServiceCreation.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "2c805dd1fc856dda96c351c5b3d8edbfc2a3e3c6", "git_parents": ["c605673f3fa9e29d19548db00fb8efde53d0b5ec"], "node": "990e5bfcacde18f6a65c97781e39c9951f0063e7", "parents": ["4da9faefaeda1e79a05014e9db4e7e640b464457"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081210 - Guard GMPServiceParent::mStorageBaseDir with mMutex. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nIt is set on the main thread but will be read from any thread.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335183\n", "files": ["dom/media/gmp/GMPServiceParent.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPServiceParent.h"], "git_node": "49c98a9f7fe002a10ba2788d63e4b5fe821d1615", "git_parents": ["2c805dd1fc856dda96c351c5b3d8edbfc2a3e3c6"], "node": "282b2ac6a4c8af30b09f3103089d820020065c4c", "parents": ["990e5bfcacde18f6a65c97781e39c9951f0063e7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081210 - Factor out GMPServiceParent::RejectPendingInitPromise. r=aosmond,media-playback-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335184\n", "files": ["dom/media/gmp/GMPServiceParent.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPServiceParent.h"], "git_node": "744edaa7d429c5363c7420a6bfe18973bb83889b", "git_parents": ["49c98a9f7fe002a10ba2788d63e4b5fe821d1615"], "node": "bbc4c56c68be4981b6daec00dfaa4447a49490fd", "parents": ["282b2ac6a4c8af30b09f3103089d820020065c4c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081210 - Create the GMP service without waiting for the main thread. r=aosmond,media-playback-reviewers\n\nPublish the singleton under a lock from any thread and run the main thread only setup as a task, inline on main. Skip the setup and shut the service down if shutdown was confirmed first.\n\nThis removes the SyncRunnable that deadlocked against nsComponentManager waiting for the pending service.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335185\n", "files": ["dom/media/gmp/GMPService.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPService.h", "dom/media/gmp/GMPServiceChild.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPServiceChild.h", "dom/media/gmp/GMPServiceParent.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPServiceParent.h"], "git_node": "624f2c9b893125f9ec7b3463bed1d219cde499a6", "git_parents": ["744edaa7d429c5363c7420a6bfe18973bb83889b"], "node": "638b5804300fac62c6d0c0768f9f296c5c84ed9b", "parents": ["bbc4c56c68be4981b6daec00dfaa4447a49490fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081210 - Annotate the lock order of the GMP service singleton. r=aosmond,media-playback-reviewers\n\nMove the singleton state into GeckoMediaPluginService so that mMutex can be annotated as acquired after sSingletonMutex, and annotate the last member it protects.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339530\n", "files": ["dom/media/gmp/GMPService.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPService.h", "dom/media/gmp/GMPServiceParent.h"], "git_node": "6bde6f4274e0457f427e027fe157b99c1271e6c4", "git_parents": ["624f2c9b893125f9ec7b3463bed1d219cde499a6"], "node": "de3fa711e044fcc1b30cb0900dea74afaa5192ee", "parents": ["638b5804300fac62c6d0c0768f9f296c5c84ed9b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081210 - Undo the GMP service main thread registrations if setup fails. r=aosmond,media-playback-reviewers\n\nThe service is not removed from the component manager, which may have cached it, so stop its observers from keeping it alive and from acting on notifications.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339531\n", "files": ["dom/media/gmp/GMPService.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPService.h", "dom/media/gmp/GMPServiceChild.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPServiceChild.h", "dom/media/gmp/GMPServiceParent.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPServiceParent.h"], "git_node": "78f0929b2fdc634c50c7f1e4a1073317307efbbe", "git_parents": ["6bde6f4274e0457f427e027fe157b99c1271e6c4"], "node": "96c3a5c44e28978fdb05fd68a20028d540e33e98", "parents": ["de3fa711e044fcc1b30cb0900dea74afaa5192ee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089458 - Let streaming upload ride the trains r=necko-reviewers,sunil\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339834\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "665ca08c14410c56b5b6eea18fd27cbfe0b6938b", "git_parents": ["78f0929b2fdc634c50c7f1e4a1073317307efbbe"], "node": "0ff9044da52f9208a51749c7659c93f0bd4b3a39", "parents": ["96c3a5c44e28978fdb05fd68a20028d540e33e98"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088945 - Enable cross document view transitions on Release, r=farre,webidl\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339534\n", "files": ["dom/tests/mochitest/general/test_interfaces.js", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "e41d684390f161b13c544e8ab37f415a3b495608", "git_parents": ["665ca08c14410c56b5b6eea18fd27cbfe0b6938b"], "node": "38e8d24325f3ba11c5f607d4ba5705d01d7fd97f", "parents": ["0ff9044da52f9208a51749c7659c93f0bd4b3a39"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jari Jalkanen \u003cjjalkanen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078279 - Adjust file stream handling. r=jld,dom-storage-reviewers,necko-reviewers,jesup\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336874\n", "files": ["dom/file/FileBlobImpl.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "netwerk/base/nsFileStreams.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsIFileStreams.idl"], "git_node": "78568bb40a84295bc0a1efd59e1306b50036bf06", "git_parents": ["e41d684390f161b13c544e8ab37f415a3b495608"], "node": "322b71f0cf79e9737d8a12c142292f886cc108a6", "parents": ["38e8d24325f3ba11c5f607d4ba5705d01d7fd97f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053674 - Part 1: Always clear the ORB frontend context state. r=bthrall\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333097\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/JSValidatorChild.cpp"], "git_node": "646a119f467c8b67e37141f71f43c65ce8e6c4ab", "git_parents": ["78568bb40a84295bc0a1efd59e1306b50036bf06"], "node": "be30283a788d7b250e41bf942fa6a3f02cce8ec7", "parents": ["322b71f0cf79e9737d8a12c142292f886cc108a6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053674 - Part 2: Add shareScriptData option to the FrontendContext creation. r=bthrall\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333098\n", "files": ["dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "js/public/experimental/CompileScript.h", "js/src/frontend/FrontendContext.cpp", "js/src/frontend/FrontendContext.h", "js/src/jsapi-tests/testFrontendErrors.cpp", "js/src/vm/JSScript.cpp"], "git_node": "badd4844726c5a6e011ed8932bcd27f0478ade92", "git_parents": ["646a119f467c8b67e37141f71f43c65ce8e6c4ab"], "node": "2a34287c85b7ea9579deceec2d8f9b62f220f0f2", "parents": ["be30283a788d7b250e41bf942fa6a3f02cce8ec7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053674 - Part 3: Do not hold the script data in ORB process. r=bthrall\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333099\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/JSOracleChild.h"], "git_node": "c8c4af0475bcc8dc6e984acb87d33e210fff74bb", "git_parents": ["badd4844726c5a6e011ed8932bcd27f0478ade92"], "node": "c0cf685df87b20efed0cd52d09b0ee831e89aa11", "parents": ["2a34287c85b7ea9579deceec2d8f9b62f220f0f2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072078 - Part 0: Remove wrong assertion. r=bthrall\n\nRequests retrieved from the in-memory cache still can be marked not-passed\nin low-memory situation etc.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334430\n", "files": ["dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp"], "git_node": "edce5724e92da7e714ca1f3f7ffb9328e9e6f82c", "git_parents": ["c8c4af0475bcc8dc6e984acb87d33e210fff74bb"], "node": "8bdfbef4db49d7a0abed2ec76a97b186b53812bb", "parents": ["c0cf685df87b20efed0cd52d09b0ee831e89aa11"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072078 - Part 1: Do not in-memory cache script requests with redirects. r=bthrall\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334431\n", "files": ["dom/script/ScriptLoadHandler.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "js/loader/ScriptLoadRequest.cpp", "js/loader/ScriptLoadRequest.h"], "git_node": "41eb9f4ab58f916361d4c5b54a72324265185305", "git_parents": ["edce5724e92da7e714ca1f3f7ffb9328e9e6f82c"], "node": "ba2032cf494fc8cfbda543225583e3d12b8f4e46", "parents": ["8bdfbef4db49d7a0abed2ec76a97b186b53812bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072078 - Part 2: Update the redirect test to verify the in-memory cache usage. r=bthrall\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334432\n", "files": ["dom/tests/browser/browser_scriptCache_redirect.js"], "git_node": "b1ce11648f95436e55239529fa3893df06d64088", "git_parents": ["41eb9f4ab58f916361d4c5b54a72324265185305"], "node": "1ed7b93684d09ed70ec2fa4396c927718df68eca", "parents": ["ba2032cf494fc8cfbda543225583e3d12b8f4e46"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bob Owen \u003cbobowencode@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078499 - Compare inherited ACEs in ChildAclMatchesAclInheritedFromParent instead of just counts. r=yjuglaret\n\nThe child can still have inherited ACEs from its previous directory that happen\nto match the count of those that would be inherited from the new parent.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331994\n", "files": ["xpcom/io/nsLocalFileWin.cpp", "xpcom/io/nsLocalFileWin.h", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestFile.cpp"], "git_node": "05948009d5b84d8fd89a0db21849368d4b472617", "git_parents": ["b1ce11648f95436e55239529fa3893df06d64088"], "node": "02b6aff5368617e5a9ca63ca0601bc38e19db8e4", "parents": ["1ed7b93684d09ed70ec2fa4396c927718df68eca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bob Owen \u003cbobowencode@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084295 p1 - Add BrokerGeckoServices to allow the sandbox broker to use Gecko code. r=sandbox-reviewers,ipc-reviewers,handyman\n\nThis is like TargetGeckoServices, but for the broker. The services are set from\nSandboxBroker::GeckoDependentInitialize, before any sandboxed process is\nlaunched. The font file validator service will be used in a later patch.\n\nThe executable exports the function to set the BrokerGeckoServices, which xul\nlooks up, rather than it being passed in BootstrapConfig. This means that a\nbroken installation with mismatched executable and xul versions doesn't crash\nbefore it can be updated. For the same reason, BrokerGeckoServices has a size,\nso that members can be added later.\n\nGTest now calls SandboxBroker::GeckoDependentInitialize for all tests, because\nmany of them launch sandboxed processes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335734\n", "files": ["ipc/glue/test/gtest/TestUtilityProcess.cpp", "security/sandbox/chromium-shim/sandbox/win/BrokerGeckoClient.cpp", "security/sandbox/chromium-shim/sandbox/win/BrokerGeckoClient.h", "security/sandbox/chromium-shim/sandbox/win/BrokerGeckoServices.h", "security/sandbox/moz.build", "security/sandbox/win/src/sandboxbroker/sandboxBroker.cpp", "testing/gtest/mozilla/GTestRunner.cpp"], "git_node": "49b2013136de4defdbc43a008412024d536f4511", "git_parents": ["05948009d5b84d8fd89a0db21849368d4b472617"], "node": "c4da8c4892e892ba2ad9d5f0396db00be2094946", "parents": ["02b6aff5368617e5a9ca63ca0601bc38e19db8e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bob Owen \u003cbobowencode@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084295 p2 - Add sandbox font file rules that are validated by Gecko. r=sandbox-reviewers,handyman\n\nThis allows a single set of rules to replace the individual font file rules.\nThe rules use a new policy opcode, which always matches in the target, so that\nthe request is sent to the broker. In the broker, the opcode uses\nBrokerGeckoServices to validate the requested path against installed font\nfiles, so paths that are not font files fall through to any later rules.\n\nMost of the implementation is in new chromium-shim files, so that the patch\nto the chromium code is mainly declarations.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335735\n", "files": ["security/sandbox/chromium-shim/patches/57_add_font_file_rule.patch", "security/sandbox/chromium-shim/sandbox/win/src/font_file_policy.cc", "security/sandbox/chromium-shim/sandbox/win/src/font_file_policy.h", "security/sandbox/chromium-shim/sandbox/win/src/font_file_policy_opcode.cc", "security/sandbox/chromium-shim/sandbox/win/src/font_file_policy_opcode.h", "security/sandbox/chromium/sandbox/win/src/filesystem_policy.cc", "security/sandbox/chromium/sandbox/win/src/filesystem_policy.h", "security/sandbox/chromium/sandbox/win/src/policy_engine_opcodes.cc", "security/sandbox/chromium/sandbox/win/src/policy_engine_opcodes.h", "security/sandbox/chromium/sandbox/win/src/policy_low_level.h", "security/sandbox/chromium/sandbox/win/src/sandbox_policy.h", "security/sandbox/chromium/sandbox/win/src/sandbox_policy_base.h", "security/sandbox/moz.build", "security/sandbox/win/gtest/TestConfigHelpers.cpp"], "git_node": "37ffba497f235d332a777b05218b0051d2fe003e", "git_parents": ["49b2013136de4defdbc43a008412024d536f4511"], "node": "1b7c59fe3b913f6f1cb208a0a5cf77cba7d3f9a0", "parents": ["c4da8c4892e892ba2ad9d5f0396db00be2094946"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bob Owen \u003cbobowencode@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084295 p3 - Add a set of installed font file paths built from DirectWrite. r=gfx-reviewers,jfkthame,bradwerth\n\nThis will be used by the sandbox broker to validate font file access from child\nprocesses. It is built and rebuilt off the main thread, but only once enabled.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335736\n", "files": ["gfx/tests/gtest/TestFontPathSet.cpp", "gfx/tests/gtest/moz.build", "gfx/thebes/FontPathSet.cpp", "gfx/thebes/FontPathSet.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxDWriteFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/moz.build"], "git_node": "9267e6c30d1db9405112a8d6018fbfbe45c1b947", "git_parents": ["37ffba497f235d332a777b05218b0051d2fe003e"], "node": "c14e3bfff83151aa05814d7afa7801e778e37b5f", "parents": ["1b7c59fe3b913f6f1cb208a0a5cf77cba7d3f9a0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bob Owen \u003cbobowencode@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084295 p4 - Add a broker font file validator using the installed font path set. r=sandbox-reviewers,handyman\n\nThis is behind a pref, which is off by default. No policies use the font file\nrules yet.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335737\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "security/sandbox/win/gtest/TestConfigHelpers.cpp", "security/sandbox/win/gtest/TestFontFileValidator.cpp", "security/sandbox/win/gtest/moz.build", "security/sandbox/win/src/sandboxbroker/ConfigHelpers.cpp", "security/sandbox/win/src/sandboxbroker/ConfigHelpers.h", "security/sandbox/win/src/sandboxbroker/FontFileValidator.cpp", "security/sandbox/win/src/sandboxbroker/FontFileValidator.h", "security/sandbox/win/src/sandboxbroker/moz.build", "security/sandbox/win/src/sandboxbroker/sandboxBroker.cpp"], "git_node": "2c46caedbac2ae2b9b0a6456a8d52a630bc6dff7", "git_parents": ["9267e6c30d1db9405112a8d6018fbfbe45c1b947"], "node": "8d2a99a4fc6f521ab3c8c5dfbefb5dbccf20b464", "parents": ["c14e3bfff83151aa05814d7afa7801e778e37b5f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bob Owen \u003cbobowencode@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084295 p5 - Use the font file rules for the GPU process. r=sandbox-reviewers,handyman\n\nWhen enabled, this replaces the individual rules for user fonts.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335738\n", "files": ["security/sandbox/win/src/sandboxbroker/sandboxBroker.cpp"], "git_node": "4de798d35a3bf303d2c5ee2f0076a4b45927d1d7", "git_parents": ["2c46caedbac2ae2b9b0a6456a8d52a630bc6dff7"], "node": "67e55532265ed45f194387b0d396c382176d4d32", "parents": ["8d2a99a4fc6f521ab3c8c5dfbefb5dbccf20b464"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bob Owen \u003cbobowencode@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084295 p6 - Use the font file rules for content processes. r=sandbox-reviewers,handyman\n\nWhen enabled, this replaces the rules for the contents of the user and system\nfont directories, which also gives access to user fonts installed elsewhere.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335739\n", "files": ["security/sandbox/win/src/sandboxbroker/sandboxBroker.cpp"], "git_node": "1734c2c9e1f1f417b4380c740b758932e4585af7", "git_parents": ["4de798d35a3bf303d2c5ee2f0076a4b45927d1d7"], "node": "15418c5957fe03dce87d0324a6b5100d05b94efa", "parents": ["67e55532265ed45f194387b0d396c382176d4d32"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bob Owen \u003cbobowencode@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084294 - Enable the sandbox font file rules on Nightly. r=sandbox-reviewers,handyman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335740\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "376e8de9e3c5a8a7f4d2e473160e5fd125d54f76", "git_parents": ["1734c2c9e1f1f417b4380c740b758932e4585af7"], "node": "b96969a378767e2e7ce473b162d9e9da4fb4b955", "parents": ["15418c5957fe03dce87d0324a6b5100d05b94efa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089037 - Move the callback into nsCompressedAudioVideoImageDetector instead of copying it (Coverity CID 1534039) r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339625\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/OpaqueResponseUtils.h"], "git_node": "b7a36c9ed9a8fb3b2abe731a53ed0b7deb03aab5", "git_parents": ["376e8de9e3c5a8a7f4d2e473160e5fd125d54f76"], "node": "380130ce4abd2357916dac01b141cb4d1ada950a", "parents": ["b96969a378767e2e7ce473b162d9e9da4fb4b955"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089042 - Initialize the byte count logged by nsHttpConnection::OnSocketReadable when there is no transaction (Coverity CID 1513180) r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339628\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpConnection.cpp"], "git_node": "e470626d0e30a6014d7cc06448426d172160c39e", "git_parents": ["b7a36c9ed9a8fb3b2abe731a53ed0b7deb03aab5"], "node": "4c852cff5a64d76098a0d60e3a8b85cd2604bfd6", "parents": ["380130ce4abd2357916dac01b141cb4d1ada950a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089040 - Use RemoveElementsBy to purge expired CORS preflight cache entries (Coverity CID 1642904) r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339629\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/nsCORSListenerProxy.cpp"], "git_node": "6121c8202882b4932e132379daf03d971d15cc73", "git_parents": ["e470626d0e30a6014d7cc06448426d172160c39e"], "node": "9754a8f0373f9ad5c04f60fbf0d7f107d8cd09c2", "parents": ["4c852cff5a64d76098a0d60e3a8b85cd2604bfd6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089069 - Make icon attribute handling dynamic. r=smaug\n\nThis should simplify the blocked bug (current patch relies on the\nprecise timing the icon attribute is set in SyncAttributesToWidget()).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339661\n", "files": ["dom/xul/ChromeObserver.cpp", "dom/xul/ChromeObserver.h", "xpfe/appshell/AppWindow.cpp"], "git_node": "e1d17f5dcc200745961875a55772a048b07a6e7c", "git_parents": ["6121c8202882b4932e132379daf03d971d15cc73"], "node": "836409daa6d9340c6c911be57e17459dd1dafecc", "parents": ["9754a8f0373f9ad5c04f60fbf0d7f107d8cd09c2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089261 - Update metadata for html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/au