"branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088980 - Handle IPP GpiAuthProvider warmUp errors r=android-reviewers,Roger\n\nWhen IPP asks us to warm up GPI, we should handle any possible errors that may happen there and resolve it to `onComplete(true)` or `onComplete(false)`\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339563\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/ipprotection/auth/gpi/IPProtectionGpiProvider.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/ipprotection/IPProtectionGpiProviderTest.kt"], "git_node": "90a80ee6859f6a455d95210a2e8a2752d365cf9f", "git_parents": ["826851912610ca14679ba18879de6cfaa6cd887c"], "node": "7b3ce09315c1f846f3c703d5df859c099166a697", "parents": ["f8af6d0620740c9fc5051a5f46b05623778c4046"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2080083, Bug 2082095, Bug 2077601, Bug 2082099 - Use a keepalive fetch to unblock the in-flight prefetch in prefetch-single-with-hint.https.html. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\" for causing wpt tests failures at flight prefetch\n\nThis reverts commit c605673f3fa9e29d19548db00fb8efde53d0b5ec.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2082095 - Reject non-trustworthy and cross-site redirects of speculation-rules prefetches. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\"\n\nThis reverts commit 225bd93a5d0b2f004446eb67531cde00fc535514.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2077601 - Serve a prefetch-activated navigation from the record's own cache entry. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\"\n\nThis reverts commit 843ac1437de08f95b477a50849cf649b97a6d110.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2082099 - Only reject cross-site speculation-rules prefetches. r=necko-reviewers,jesup\"\n\nThis reverts commit 334fda58944b1fd5fe59092bffd740c4338ea1e9.\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.h", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentLoadListener.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/client-hints/redirect.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/no-vary-search/prefetch-single-with-hint.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/no-vary-search/prefetch-single.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prefetch/no-vary-search/prefetch-single-with-hint.https.html"], "git_node": "7ca388f545a7083ec40eacd58c52231bb5c67caa", "git_parents": ["90a80ee6859f6a455d95210a2e8a2752d365cf9f"], "node": "9aaffb4eecbc3b9899cde0cf97bd0596d74c2622", "parents": ["7b3ce09315c1f846f3c703d5df859c099166a697"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2087441 - make a single bugbug query, and share its results. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\" for causing Bug 2089466\n\nThis reverts commit 56a7ee279fe275a1f1a75c086039bd5ac5e24cab.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2087441 - Poll bugbug for push schedules every 2 seconds rather than 10. r=marco,taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\"\n\nThis reverts commit 9e422c56e93f269592e4ef1e515251c8944516b0.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2087441 - Record markers for bugbug requests in decision task resource usage profiles. r=marco,taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\"\n\nThis reverts commit a5dd47c3be5fb7d32a8253f87c9e765accacd791.\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/decision.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/test_decision.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/test_optimize_strategies.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/test_util_bugbug.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/util/bugbug.py", "taskcluster/mach_commands.py"], "git_node": "12a5e3a338165cd3537295d76a3cfad3e274f50d", "git_parents": ["7ca388f545a7083ec40eacd58c52231bb5c67caa"], "node": "7d6423fe0ccfc7b52b95cfbf5d4c7daedc9b51ab", "parents": ["9aaffb4eecbc3b9899cde0cf97bd0596d74c2622"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2084294, Bug 2084295 - Enable the sandbox font file rules on Nightly. r=sandbox-reviewers,handyman\" for causing failures at sandboxBroker.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit 376e8de9e3c5a8a7f4d2e473160e5fd125d54f76.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2084295 p6 - Use the font file rules for content processes. r=sandbox-reviewers,handyman\"\n\nThis reverts commit 1734c2c9e1f1f417b4380c740b758932e4585af7.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2084295 p5 - Use the font file rules for the GPU process. r=sandbox-reviewers,handyman\"\n\nThis reverts commit 4de798d35a3bf303d2c5ee2f0076a4b45927d1d7.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2084295 p4 - Add a broker font file validator using the installed font path set. r=sandbox-reviewers,handyman\"\n\nThis reverts commit 2c46caedbac2ae2b9b0a6456a8d52a630bc6dff7.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2084295 p3 - Add a set of installed font file paths built from DirectWrite. r=gfx-reviewers,jfkthame,bradwerth\"\n\nThis reverts commit 9267e6c30d1db9405112a8d6018fbfbe45c1b947.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2084295 p2 - Add sandbox font file rules that are validated by Gecko. r=sandbox-reviewers,handyman\"\n\nThis reverts commit 37ffba497f235d332a777b05218b0051d2fe003e.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2084295 p1 - Add BrokerGeckoServices to allow the sandbox broker to use Gecko code. r=sandbox-reviewers,ipc-reviewers,handyman\"\n\nThis reverts commit 49b2013136de4defdbc43a008412024d536f4511.\n", "files": ["gfx/tests/gtest/TestFontPathSet.cpp", "gfx/tests/gtest/moz.build", "gfx/thebes/FontPathSet.cpp", "gfx/thebes/FontPathSet.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxDWriteFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/moz.build", "ipc/glue/test/gtest/TestUtilityProcess.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "security/sandbox/chromium-shim/patches/57_add_font_file_rule.patch", "security/sandbox/chromium-shim/sandbox/win/BrokerGeckoClient.cpp", "security/sandbox/chromium-shim/sandbox/win/BrokerGeckoClient.h", "security/sandbox/chromium-shim/sandbox/win/BrokerGeckoServices.h", "security/sandbox/chromium-shim/sandbox/win/src/font_file_policy.cc", "security/sandbox/chromium-shim/sandbox/win/src/font_file_policy.h", "security/sandbox/chromium-shim/sandbox/win/src/font_file_policy_opcode.cc", "security/sandbox/chromium-shim/sandbox/win/src/font_file_policy_opcode.h", "security/sandbox/chromium/sandbox/win/src/filesystem_policy.cc", "security/sandbox/chromium/sandbox/win/src/filesystem_policy.h", "security/sandbox/chromium/sandbox/win/src/policy_engine_opcodes.cc", "security/sandbox/chromium/sandbox/win/src/policy_engine_opcodes.h", "security/sandbox/chromium/sandbox/win/src/policy_low_level.h", "security/sandbox/chromium/sandbox/win/src/sandbox_policy.h", "security/sandbox/chromium/sandbox/win/src/sandbox_policy_base.h", "security/sandbox/moz.build", "security/sandbox/win/gtest/TestConfigHelpers.cpp", "security/sandbox/win/gtest/TestFontFileValidator.cpp", "security/sandbox/win/gtest/moz.build", "security/sandbox/win/src/sandboxbroker/ConfigHelpers.cpp", "security/sandbox/win/src/sandboxbroker/ConfigHelpers.h", "security/sandbox/win/src/sandboxbroker/FontFileValidator.cpp", "security/sandbox/win/src/sandboxbroker/FontFileValidator.h", "security/sandbox/win/src/sandboxbroker/moz.build", "security/sandbox/win/src/sandboxbroker/sandboxBroker.cpp", "testing/gtest/mozilla/GTestRunner.cpp"], "git_node": "a83758b846d7969e8f1440b830e7ed09807b31ef", "git_parents": ["12a5e3a338165cd3537295d76a3cfad3e274f50d"], "node": "16a9048b6d93c84cf5aed2c6ebc04ee9b854aa92", "parents": ["7d6423fe0ccfc7b52b95cfbf5d4c7daedc9b51ab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089479 - Report attributes added through SVG DOM setters as additions in SVGElement::DidChangeValue (Coverity CID 1696585) r=firefox-svg-reviewers,longsonr\n\nBug 769207 part 3 replaced HasAttr(aName) with aName, which is never\nnull, so DidChangeValue always reported Modification while\nWillChangeValue reported Addition for the same change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339853\n", "files": ["dom/svg/SVGElement.cpp"], "git_node": "4c318908037d34b2d72444167744e27b345d4e45", "git_parents": ["a83758b846d7969e8f1440b830e7ed09807b31ef"], "node": "66bb2762c8550de3329e84d7c3e83b862e942866", "parents": ["16a9048b6d93c84cf5aed2c6ebc04ee9b854aa92"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Johannes Salas Schmidt \u003cjoschmidt@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088438 - Don't disable the Rust logins backend when the migration attempts are exhausted. r=credential-management-reviewers,theidkamp,dimi\n\nWriting `signon.storage.rust.enabled` unenrolled the client from the Nimbus experiment that sets it. The migrator now leaves the pref alone and keeps the JSON store primary while the attempt limit is reached.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339115\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/passwordmgr/LoginStorageMigrator.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/passwordmgr/test/unit/test_LoginStorageMigrator.js", "toolkit/components/passwordmgr/test/unit/test_LoginStorageMigrator_nimbus.js"], "git_node": "9a8e6a4e6815cc42259f5eb89d8948ae80a86860", "git_parents": ["4c318908037d34b2d72444167744e27b345d4e45"], "node": "3476a895ee69fdddb4c72977f85f2fdeccfa4e4c", "parents": ["66bb2762c8550de3329e84d7c3e83b862e942866"], "tags": []}, {"author": "giorga \u003cgiorga@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088565 - [customizable menu] Don't show the quit button in the \"Customizable menu\" screen if disabled in settings r=android-reviewers,petru\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339860\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/deletebrowsingdata/QuitMenuItemProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/deletebrowsingdata/QuitMenuItemProviderTest.kt"], "git_node": "0e2c2d4b5cc6ef0f02f43f2585947452ce17bf8e", "git_parents": ["9a8e6a4e6815cc42259f5eb89d8948ae80a86860"], "node": "f04fcc80636ca31e8a38a8d3ccd9d45ab3c768c9", "parents": ["3476a895ee69fdddb4c72977f85f2fdeccfa4e4c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088866 - Fire mutation observer when innerText setter modifies the input string. r=smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339825\n", "files": ["dom/html/nsGenericHTMLElement.cpp"], "git_node": "5e63dc9482c9b906c54f75b3281aaaf9f215fda1", "git_parents": ["0e2c2d4b5cc6ef0f02f43f2585947452ce17bf8e"], "node": "ad72a32b46f3aca60449fa4ede0ca046db8569ca", "parents": ["f04fcc80636ca31e8a38a8d3ccd9d45ab3c768c9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "AndiAJ \u003candiaj@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088861 - Create two new verifyTheAddressCaptureNotNowButtonTest and verifyTheUpdateAddressCaptureTest regression UI tests r=aaronmt\n\nBoth UI tests successfully passed 25x on Firebase \u2705\nAll UI tests successfully passed 1x on Firebase \u2705\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339498\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/assets/pages/addressForm.html", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/BrowserPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/BrowserPageSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SettingsAutofillSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/AddressAutofillTest.kt"], "git_node": "05aaaaeac20734eec6ddf38affc98b75736e3936", "git_parents": ["5e63dc9482c9b906c54f75b3281aaaf9f215fda1"], "node": "c59f0036416cf99db94d196564714a1ed5cca12e", "parents": ["ad72a32b46f3aca60449fa4ede0ca046db8569ca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088586 - Enable `intl.tsf.hack.allow_to_stop_hacking_on_build_17643_or_later` pref in all channels r=m_kato\n\nIt was introduced in bug 1481153 because Microsoft fixed that\n`TS_E_NOLAYOUT` returned by `ITextStoreACP::GetTextExtent` was not\nreturned to TIP.\n\nAfter shipping that, we have not gotten any bug reports from unexpected\nIME users for 4 years. (We still do the hack on the latest Windows for\nknown issues.)\n\nSo, let's enable it in all channels.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339775\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "99cd1ff01320970c1c7ae7192d27605eca51043c", "git_parents": ["05aaaaeac20734eec6ddf38affc98b75736e3936"], "node": "39bcf92c95e60db07486719ad19f3e51b3981870", "parents": ["c59f0036416cf99db94d196564714a1ed5cca12e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mauro Ferreiro Monteagudo \u003cmferreiro@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066310 - Stop keeping the Taskbar Tab registry entry in the tabbrowser. r=iholmes,hsohaney,tabbrowser-reviewers,nsharpley\n\nThe tabbrowser now only keeps the name and container of the Taskbar Tab,\nand the title strings move to Web Apps. Formatting stays synchronous so the\ntitle still updates immediately when the profile changes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337026\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/types/globals.ts", "browser/components/taskbartabs/TaskbarTabs.sys.mjs", "browser/components/taskbartabs/TaskbarTabsUtils.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "e55299d6d087d78b7253dd165ff1413148c3d7d1", "git_parents": ["99cd1ff01320970c1c7ae7192d27605eca51043c"], "node": "7888263f9284ecd6fcec4b7811a5b1c0e26238e1", "parents": ["39bcf92c95e60db07486719ad19f3e51b3981870"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mauro Ferreiro \u003cmferreiro@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066310 - Test the Taskbar Tab window title when the profile or container changes while it is open. r=iholmes\n\nThe container name is no longer cached with the title, so a renamed or\nremoved container shows up the next time the title is refreshed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337027\n", "files": ["browser/components/taskbartabs/test/browser/browser_taskbarTabs_title.js"], "git_node": "c99ee74aa85a6244f6f76bf54021c3b9b306e5c3", "git_parents": ["e55299d6d087d78b7253dd165ff1413148c3d7d1"], "node": "ef0e9cc07ff26d400d128465460ef0b876481521", "parents": ["7888263f9284ecd6fcec4b7811a5b1c0e26238e1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mauro Ferreiro \u003cmferreiro@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2024973 - Move platform-specific TaskbarTabsPin code into per-platform classes. r=hsohaney\n\nTaskbarTabsPin now delegates to TaskbarTabsPinWin, TaskbarTabsPinMsix or\nTaskbarTabsPinLinux, which only override the steps their platform needs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339473\n", "files": ["browser/components/taskbartabs/TaskbarTabsPin.sys.mjs", "browser/components/taskbartabs/TaskbarTabsPinBase.sys.mjs", "browser/components/taskbartabs/TaskbarTabsPinLinux.sys.mjs", "browser/components/taskbartabs/TaskbarTabsPinMsix.sys.mjs", "browser/components/taskbartabs/TaskbarTabsPinWin.sys.mjs", "browser/components/taskbartabs/TaskbarTabsWindowManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/taskbartabs/docs/architecture.md", "browser/components/taskbartabs/moz.build", "browser/components/taskbartabs/test/xpcshell/test_taskbarTabs_pinLinux.js", "browser/components/taskbartabs/test/xpcshell/test_taskbarTabs_pinMsix.js", "browser/components/taskbartabs/test/xpcshell/test_taskbarTabs_pinWindows.js"], "git_node": "6723f90a08de36bbb2fa2a1e707d228f5f48ab32", "git_parents": ["c99ee74aa85a6244f6f76bf54021c3b9b306e5c3"], "node": "22c23e480da7d853f5cb6c2d3166f1e7bc6891e4", "parents": ["ef0e9cc07ff26d400d128465460ef0b876481521"], "tags": []}, {"author":