"testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/cue_function/white-space_pre.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/cue_function/white-space_pre_wrapped-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/cue_function/white-space_pre_wrapped.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/default_styles/bold_object_default_font-style-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/default_styles/bold_object_default_font-style.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/default_styles/inherit_as_default_value_inherits_values_from_media_element-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/default_styles/inherit_as_default_value_inherits_values_from_media_element.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/default_styles/italic_object_default_font-style-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/default_styles/italic_object_default_font-style.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/default_styles/underline_object_default_font-style-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/default_styles/underline_object_default_font-style.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/size_50-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/size_50.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/snap-to-line-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/snap-to-line.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/too_many_cues-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/too_many_cues.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/too_many_cues_wrapped-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/too_many_cues_wrapped.html"], "git_node": "fd5b08b865b5c0db99ad7fe176059c8536d7885e", "git_parents": ["1929aaddae036f06bc739454fc52a8c87b7cc425"], "node": "7a3d5ddf6ee8ed6c3890e2c2c5c6324a993e81ea", "parents": ["b664c6874f1a12ee65301dd7f0a2398771b8aacf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084309 [wpt PR 63902] - [css-color] Split nested light-dark() image test by wrapper function, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-color] Split nested light-dark() image test by wrapper function (#63902)\n\nThe one test for light-dark() inside compound images put image-set(),\n-webkit-cross-fade() and a second image-set() in a single value, so a\nbrowser without -webkit-cross-fade() (Firefox) failed it before the\nimage-set() nesting was exercised. The value was also invalid per spec:\ncss-images-4 says \"The image-set() function can not be nested inside of\nitself, either directly or indirectly (as an argument to another \u003cimage\u003e\ntype).\"\n\nReplace it with one test per wrapper shape, sharing a helper that reads\nthe expected and unexpected dummy:// URLs off the value: light-dark()\ninside image-set(), image-set() inside light-dark(), light-dark() inside\n-webkit-cross-fade(), and light-dark() inside -webkit-cross-fade()\ninside image-set(). Chromium passes all 35 tests (32 before).\n\nFixes #58875\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 490b42b50bb82fc43eac961fabbbbc1150f98aec\nwpt-pr: 63902\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-color/light-dark-image.html"], "git_node": "f69541721f20e03cc3c5fd4d83e00a0f5b23d6c9", "git_parents": ["fd5b08b865b5c0db99ad7fe176059c8536d7885e"], "node": "1209119151e17834ea7489396307481c8864dc29", "parents": ["7a3d5ddf6ee8ed6c3890e2c2c5c6324a993e81ea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084309 [wpt PR 63902] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63902\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-color/crashtests/firefox-bug-2072488.html.ini"], "git_node": "950c42452334103cdd9b73d365b36bbf8d3bd9cd", "git_parents": ["f69541721f20e03cc3c5fd4d83e00a0f5b23d6c9"], "node": "f7491641dba8ae9267ac3ccf50d4848465d815ff", "parents": ["1209119151e17834ea7489396307481c8864dc29"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084035 [wpt PR 63886] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328067, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nTest what still crosses between same-origin documents with and without a Document-Isolation-Policy\n\nSame-origin documents with and without a Document-Isolation-Policy are in different agent clusters.\nThe existing tests cover synchronous access, javascript: URLs, the navigate event, and posting a\nSharedArrayBuffer or WebAssembly.Module to a frame. These new tentative tests cover the rest of\nwhat crosses between such documents:\n\n- broadcast-channel and message-channel: a SharedArrayBuffer posted on a BroadcastChannel or a\n  MessageChannel arrives at same-origin documents with the same policy and shares memory with them,\n  including a frame with a policy in another frame tree of the browsing context group, and fires\n  messageerror at those without one. Other messages reach both.\n- window-reuse: when an initial about:blank document navigates to a same-origin document, the new\n  document only reuses its Window if they have the same policy. This covers frames, and popups\n  opened by a document with a policy; agent-cluster covers popups opened by one without. That\n  reuse requiring the same agent cluster is part of\n  https://github.com/WICG/document-isolation-policy/issues/11\n- partial-deployment: same-origin documents with and without a policy can still post messages to\n  each other, use each other's cross-origin Window and Location members, navigate each other, and\n  share localStorage.\n- origin-agent-cluster: a document with a policy is origin-keyed even with Origin-Agent-Cluster: ?0,\n  and doesn't decide whether same-origin documents without one in its browsing context group are.\n- cross-origin-frame: a document with a policy and no Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy can embed a\n  cross-origin frame without Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy, or with Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy:\n  same-origin, as Fetch's check allows navigations when the embedder policy is \"unsafe-none\".\n\nWebKit passes all of them.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328067\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d28517d0f40cdd697dfdb4957837a34d206d7259\nwpt-pr: 63886\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/broadcast-channel.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/cross-origin-frame.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/message-channel.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/origin-agent-cluster.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/partial-deployment.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/window-reuse.tentative.https.html"], "git_node": "31100aea46c21422df7421c81f2b769577e4ac53", "git_parents": ["950c42452334103cdd9b73d365b36bbf8d3bd9cd"], "node": "3f646715364b2e6af02c70b8955d5f3a6928fe04", "parents": ["f7491641dba8ae9267ac3ccf50d4848465d815ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084035 [wpt PR 63886] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63886\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/document-isolation-policy/broadcast-channel.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/document-isolation-policy/cross-origin-frame.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/document-isolation-policy/message-channel.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/document-isolation-policy/origin-agent-cluster.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/document-isolation-policy/partial-deployment.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/document-isolation-policy/window-reuse.tentative.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "e7f84531fb146277ab2c4e0cdd92e66a3900ed21", "git_parents": ["31100aea46c21422df7421c81f2b769577e4ac53"], "node": "d20fc2793fa74af8732265ba929b6fc473afe4e2", "parents": ["3f646715364b2e6af02c70b8955d5f3a6928fe04"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084006 [wpt PR 63879] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328054, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nA cross-document navigation from another agent cluster fires navigate\n\nHTML only fires navigate for a cross-document navigation when the initiator is same origin-domain\nwith the navigated document, so a document only gets to intercept or cancel navigations started by\ndocuments that could script it anyway. Before Document-Isolation-Policy that also meant the same\nagent cluster. Now a same-origin document can be in another agent cluster, where it can't script\nthe navigated document, yet 323812@main fired navigate for it when it was in another process.\n\nAs in Chromium, a cross-document navigation now only fires navigate when its initiator passes\nIsPlatformObjectSameOrigin, which includes the agent cluster check. Documents of one agent cluster\nshare a process, so an initiator in another process never does. The exception is a site that\nLockdown Mode gives a second process in the same browsing context group, as both processes still\nget the same agent cluster. A follow-up will key agent clusters on Lockdown Mode and similar modes.\n\nSo navigations from another process only fire navigate for fragment navigations, which fire it\nwhoever started them, with sourceElement nulled across agent clusters. The handling of cancelled\ncross-document navigations from another process goes away, along with\nSiteIsolation.CancelledNavigateEventFromAnotherProcessLetsParentFinishLoading, and form data no\nlonger needs to cross processes. Within a process, FrameLoader now uses IsPlatformObjectSameOrigin\nfor this check too.\n\nSee https://github.com/WICG/document-isolation-policy/issues/11\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328054\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9996538077db8ac27d6a9814445af1afec22aeb5\nwpt-pr: 63879\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/agent-cluster.tentative.https.html"], "git_node": "c0f18ef7eeea6860d2ce527856b5241c5b6100f1", "git_parents": ["e7f84531fb146277ab2c4e0cdd92e66a3900ed21"], "node": "bc6a335107a41bf8c80eadc45b9aae733d557165", "parents": ["d20fc2793fa74af8732265ba929b6fc473afe4e2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084006 [wpt PR 63879] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63879\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/document-isolation-policy/agent-cluster.tentative.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "01d4bdc5d6c3580c9309781ad49947f49d02e0a5", "git_parents": ["c0f18ef7eeea6860d2ce527856b5241c5b6100f1"], "node": "fd561e2cafc613b1b4cc5083154a8612f72e8894", "parents": ["bc6a335107a41bf8c80eadc45b9aae733d557165"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084317 [wpt PR 63904] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328109, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nGeolocation should be blocked in non-secure contexts\n\nGeolocation::shouldBlockGeolocationRequests() treated a document as secure if its URL had a secure\nscheme or if it was a secure context. The URL check dates from 2016, when a mixed content check\naccompanied it. Being a secure context was added as an alternative in 2021 for WKWebView's custom\nURL schemes. Since the mixed content check was removed in 2025, an https: frame in an http: page\ncould use geolocation once the page allowed it with allow=\"geolocation\". Such a frame is not a\nsecure context, and geolocation is a powerful feature, which the Permissions specification denies\noutside of secure contexts.\n\nThe check now only looks at whether the document is a secure context. That still covers documents\nwith a custom URL scheme handler, and those with a scheme registered as secure, as both are\npotentially trustworthy.\n\nDocuments with a local origin, such as file:, were exempt since 2017, when the check only looked at\nthe URL's scheme. Local schemes are potentially trustworthy, so such documents are secure contexts\nunless they are in a frame of a non-secure context, which other APIs also deny. The exemption is\nremoved.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328109\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1af41dcff1cdf3fb3349919105c73076a58c9b15\nwpt-pr: 63904\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/geolocation/non-secure-context-https-iframe.http.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/geolocation/resources/report-getCurrentPosition.html"], "git_node": "7895eb77c2f7c42d356e3a200bec845ec08afaae", "git_parents": ["01d4bdc5d6c3580c9309781ad49947f49d02e0a5"], "node": "5649c779a3ff6c290ff20f33e7a3a2dffb3277b3", "parents": ["fd561e2cafc613b1b4cc5083154a8612f72e8894"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084021 [wpt PR 63880] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328061, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nA navigation to the current URL gets the wrong navigationType when document.domain is set\n\nHTML turns a navigation to the active document's URL into a replace when the initiator is same\norigin with that document. FrameLoader::loadURL() checked same origin-domain instead, so\ndocument.domain changed the result: a cross-origin initiator that set document.domain like the\ndocument got \"replace\", and a same-origin initiator where only one of them set it got \"push\".\n\nFor a navigation to another document, the session history itself was right, as\nFrameLoader::shouldTreatURLAsSameAsCurrent() decides it with a same-origin check. But the history\nhandling FrameLoader::loadURL() computes is what the Navigation API reports as the navigation's\nnavigationType, which was wrong in both cases. A fragment navigation also decides its session\nhistory with it, so for the cross-origin initiator it replaced the current entry instead of adding\none.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328061\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3a2408289a18d10d3ddb50549ef2039df5ebcbf0\nwpt-pr: 63880\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/navigating-across-documents/navigate-iframe-to-same-url-with-document-domain.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/navigating-across-documents/navigate-iframe-to-same-url-with-document-domain.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/navigating-across-documents/resources/set-document-domain.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/navigating-across-documents/resources/set-document-domain.html.headers"], "git_node": "87ece5290e1dada38595a8f689ba6fe355c0bb1b", "git_parents": ["7895eb77c2f7c42d356e3a200bec845ec08afaae"], "node": "d1d0444126a383e5f96e1bcd94280af3b97ae30f", "parents": ["5649c779a3ff6c290ff20f33e7a3a2dffb3277b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084021 [wpt PR 63880] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63880\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/navigating-across-documents/navigate-iframe-to-same-url-with-document-domain.html.ini"], "git_node": "3f8609d5affa5710e656b29ea1356f10b1b5384c", "git_parents": ["87ece5290e1dada38595a8f689ba6fe355c0bb1b"], "node": "32bf7555cf362ee87f53fe71fbb8096945a3ce22", "parents": ["d1d0444126a383e5f96e1bcd94280af3b97ae30f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084670 [wpt PR 63938] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328190, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nlocation.replace() of a frame in another process adds a session history entry\n\nWhen a document navigates a frame in another process, the UI process hands the\nnavigation to the frame's process once its policy is decided. When the frame\nstays in its process, which with site isolation's shared process is the usual\ncase for a cross-site frame, that hand-off didn't forward the navigation's\nlockHistory and lockBackForwardList. So location.replace() added a session\nhistory entry.\n\nThe navigation also lost its history handling on the way to the UI process.\nWhichever process it ended up in, the new document's\nnavigation.activation.navigationType was \"push\" after location.replace(). And\nnavigation.navigate() with history: \"replace\" didn't lock the back/forward list\nof its navigation action, so it added an entry when it moved to another process.\n\nThe hand-off now forwards the lock flags. A NavigationAction made from a\nFrameLoadRequest now takes the request's history handling, so the navigation\naction WebRemoteFrameClient::changeLocation() sends to the UI process keeps it.\nA NavigationAPIReplace load locks the back/forward list of its navigation\naction.\n\nThis doesn't change how \"auto\" is resolved for a navigation from another\nprocess, for instance for a frame that isn't completely loaded yet.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328190\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 02f5da61b96a03debc12e3c6d37614ac504fd2d2\nwpt-pr: 63938\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/history/the-location-interface/location-replace-cross-site.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/history/the-location-interface/resources/cross-site-navigation-helper.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/navigation-methods/navigate-replace-cross-site.html"], "git_node": "3ac79271769cc6b142df00cd36330f030c90c421", "git_parents": ["3f8609d5affa5710e656b29ea1356f10b1b5384c"], "node": "f3dc16d9e521878bb63003faf33cb08b2d1814e5", "parents": ["32bf7555cf362ee87f53fe71fbb8096945a3ce22"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084670 [wpt PR 63938] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63938\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/history/the-location-interface/location-replace-cross-site.html.ini"], "git_node": "28387b2129b3a46b04b38fe1b028e7b3bd130f4f", "git_parents": ["3ac79271769cc6b142df00cd36330f030c90c421"], "node": "8861622ebc21c2823ee2928476342e1735ba5c7f", "parents": ["f3dc16d9e521878bb63003faf33cb08b2d1814e5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vitor Roriz \u003cv.r.roriz@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084674 [wpt PR 63948] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=290307, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=290307 (#63948)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: bd418e2232f6fe8cb9845c7c2c7e3ec6c1a324e2\nwpt-pr: 63948\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-highlight-api/painting/custom-highlight-painting-anonymous-block-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-highlight-api/painting/custom-highlight-painting-anonymous-block-001.html"], "git_node": "0b2e9e9dbebde3a61ef15a7a21b6598d101b1283", "git_parents": ["28387b2129b3a46b04b38fe1b028e7b3bd130f4f"], "node": "21b0cf8439b26a197acda0a1dfcba061d8ec2b6f", "parents": ["8861622ebc21c2823ee2928476342e1735ba5c7f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084682 [wpt PR 63941] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328202, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDedicated workers of documents with a Document-Isolation-Policy aren't cross-origin isolated\n\nSince 324033@main a document with a Document-Isolation-Policy is in a cross-origin isolated\nprocess and crossOriginIsolated returns true there. Its dedicated workers share its agent cluster,\nbut they didn't get its policy, so their crossOriginIsolated returned false.\n\nDocument-Isolation-Policy has a dedicated worker take its owner's policy. The worker now gets it\nfrom its owner and, as HTML requires, takes its owner's cross-origin isolation, except that a data:\nURL worker is never cross-origin isolated.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328202\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5d23b743bb487d18c51ea0f016b4b22c0895a813\nwpt-pr: 63941\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/dedicated-worker.tentative.https.html"], "git_node": "4444df0e7a868d447e61e10a593a750af9e2635c", "git_parents": ["0b2e9e9dbebde3a61ef15a7a21b6598d101b1283"], "node": "7ffa195da3ec8537bfc876516c6bd11f5454071d", "parents": ["21b0cf8439b26a197acda0a1dfcba061d8ec2b6f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084682 [wpt PR 63941] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63941\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/document-isolation-policy/dedicated-worker.tentative.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "e59097c448e2bd37429e09c16123b77152dbb901", "git_parents": ["4444df0e7a868d447e61e10a593a750af9e2635c"], "node": "202ae71020c202c50b4e2465cff10e41e671293a", "parents": ["7ffa195da3ec8537bfc876516c6bd11f5454071d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Domenic Denicola \u003cd@domenic.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084486 [wpt PR 63923] - Reject two-value caret colors beginning with auto, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nReject two-value caret colors beginning with auto\n\nThe CSS UI 4 grammar is auto | \u003ccolor\u003e [auto | \u003ccolor\u003e]?, so auto is a standalone alternative rather than an allowed first component in the two-value form. Move those cases into invalid parsing coverage and remove their computed-value expectations. Keep single auto and color-plus-auto controls.\n\nhttps://drafts.csswg.org/css-ui-4/#propdef-caret-color\n\nCo-authored-by: codex \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e7d77cd1e0353d7b37ce35eb912b6992df8dfab0\nwpt-pr: 63923\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/parsing/caret-color-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/parsing/caret-color-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/parsing/caret-color-valid.html"], "git_node": "fccc528d7e6cceff1e4748cfee623aa3acade555", "git_parents": ["e59097c448e2bd37429e09c16123b77152dbb901"], "node": "d6f617c8a0b2ba58400c7b10e437cf5ed109dca7", "parents": ["202ae71020c202c50b4e2465cff10e41e671293a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "rogerkorantenng \u003crogerkorantenng@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084339 [wpt PR 63908] - script: Use create_a_potential_cors_request_with_claim in processingoptions.rs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nscript: Use create_a_potential_cors_request_with_claim in processingoptions.rs\n\nSigned-off-by: rogerkorantenng \u003crogerkorantenng@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3849d6d1f059d367bbb542c36074d188f51500a1\nwpt-pr: 63908\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/preload/link-blob-url-revoked.window.js"], "git_node": "ad5a7e261586f97d6b2bc215d5082ba89f2be550", "git_parents": ["fccc528d7e6cceff1e4748cfee623aa3acade555"], "node": "9a8d918c612970eb924e0da454eaf3d510c76025", "parents": ["d6f617c8a0b2ba58400c7b10e437cf5ed109dca7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084339 [wpt PR 63908] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63908\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/preload/link-blob-url-revoked.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "0fd7ceebad8ac434288a674541cbc65271ee2b71", "git_parents": ["ad5a7e261586f97d6b2bc215d5082ba89f2be550"], "node": "740fa1f8cb2a95476d24ae7a55002ba8048de26a", "parents": ["9a8d918c612970eb924e0da454eaf3d510c76025"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Graham \u003cjames@hoppipolla.co.uk\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084697 [wpt PR 63949] - Add tini to the Docker image and decision task, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd tini to the Docker image and decision task\n\nThis ensures that we reap zombie processes\n\n--\nUpdate the docker image used in CI\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a52409560c3b0458e8e684c6b5c595395e613356, deb8599d98ce8f7968012c0a3128ebafc18abba3\nwpt-pr: 63949\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/.taskcluster.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/ci/tc/decision.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/ci/tc/tasks/test.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/ci/tc/tests/test_valid.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/docker/Dockerfile"], "git_node": "40771836743b75d60248042a99e9364501a4c06e", "git_parents": ["0fd7ceebad8ac434288a674541cbc65271ee2b71"], "node": "4154d818a6cb00f300c962401202a1fb23a96e70", "parents": ["740fa1f8cb2a95476d24ae7a55002ba8048de26a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084700 [wpt PR 63957] - script: Acknowledge that `text` attribute of `\u003cbody\u003e` affects preshints, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nscript: Acknowledge that `text` attribute of `\u003cbody\u003e` affects preshints\n\nNow we will correctly update presentational hints when the value of that\nattribute changes dynamically.\n\nSigned-off-by: Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 64f13635ce4a216afe11c471db29f5692359eebc\nwpt-pr: 63957\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/non-replaced-elements/the-page/body_text_dynamic.html"], "git_node": "693a74728d2100a03cb63923bfafa51a9ea1f8c0", "git_parents": ["40771836743b75d60248042a99e9364501a4c06e"], "node": "8e9f3490a3b70691c2c685150e6b9f486f7f1aae", "parents": ["4154d818a6cb00f300c962401202a1fb23a96e70"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084700 [wpt PR 63957] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63957\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/rendering/non-replaced-elements/the-page/crashtests/body-huge-attr-value-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "4d3893c6d8dfb20240b8cd41a6062316c5af4206", "git_parents": ["693a74728d2100a03cb63923bfafa51a9ea1f8c0"], "node": "11409682c171188f66775c537abe8526a572aad7", "parents": ["8e9f3490a3b70691c2c685150e6b9f486f7f1aae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Karl Dubost \u003ckarlcow@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084703 [wpt PR 63977] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328210, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\ncomposedPath() in a listener on a use element exposes its user agent shadow root (#63977)\n\nFor a click on the shape drawn by a use element, composedPath() in a\nlistener on the use returns the use shadow root, and lists the use\ntwice:\n\n    use \u003e ShadowRoot \u003e use \u003e svg \u003e body \u003e html \u003e document \u003e window\n\nFirefox and Chrome return:\n\n    use \u003e svg \u003e body \u003e html \u003e document \u003e window\n\nSVG 2 says the use shadow tree is closed:\n\n    The shadow tree is closed (not inspectable by script): its shadow\n    root's mode is \"closed\".\n\nhttps://w3c.github.io/svgwg/svg2-draft/struct.html#UseShadowTree\n\nFor a closed tree, composedPath() leaves its nodes out when the listener\nis outside it. The DOM steps also look for the current target starting\nfrom the end of the event path:\n\nhttps://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-event-composedpath\n\nThe nodes of the use shadow tree report the use as their current target,\nso the event path has several entries for it. WebKit used the first\none, the copy inside the shadow tree, and filtered the path from there.\nUse the last one, the use itself.\n\nThe listener still runs once per click. Only the path was wrong.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328210\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 07274ec72c56840adbe8ec3a6568669561e1048c\nwpt-pr: 63977\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/struct/scripted/use-composedpath-closed-shadow-tree.html"], "git_node": "abddaaa50842fffbb23d28b563c1053d3ff8d9ca", "git_parents": ["4d3893c6d8dfb20240b8cd41a6062316c5af4206"], "node": "b1b584b964f080239ed9891739ff4cc7da374b24", "parents": ["11409682c171188f66775c537abe8526a572aad7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yury Semikhatsky \u003cyurys@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084338 [wpt PR 63907] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=264733, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nelement.checkVisibility() does not work for unslotted elements\n\ncheckVisibility() now returns false for light DOM children that are not\nassigned to a slot, and for content of a closed \u003cdetails\u003e, including an open\n\u003cdetails\u003e nested inside a closed one. Add test coverage for these cases so\nthe bug can be closed.\n\nTests upstream: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/63023\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=264733\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324155@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a699fb16767be39ba3e61a8e8b6bef60383f08ee\nwpt-pr: 63907\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom-view/checkVisibility.html"], "git_node": "abf86dd2ae903bce69c2a1257c0972b3be913e9b", "git_parents": ["abddaaa50842fffbb23d28b563c1053d3ff8d9ca"], "node": "402c7bd749c215eadf2b3ea9f2b6a1df4ef11a55", "parents": ["b1b584b964f080239ed9891739ff4cc7da374b24"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003cahmad.saleem792+github@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085381 [wpt PR 63989] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=320579, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[XHR] Final response charset is recomputed for every received data chunk\n\ndidReceiveData() resolved the final response charset into m_responseEncoding on\nevery chunk, costing a media type parse and a String allocation per network\ncallback. It was only read by finalResponseCharset() feeding createDecoder(),\nwhich runs once per load, and neither input can change in between:\noverrideMimeType() and the responseType setter throw once the state reaches\nLOADING.\n\nResolve the charset directly from the two inputs in finalResponseCharset(), per\n\u003chttps://xhr.spec.whatwg.org/#final-charset\u003e, and remove m_responseEncoding.\nThis also drops a second extractCharsetFromMediaType() call that could never\nmatch, since its input was that same parser's output. No behavior change.\n\nAdd coverage for a charset spanning chunk boundaries; the existing\noverrideMimeType() tests all use single-chunk responses.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=320579\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/318297@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a4a39d815dc034c8c6422341fc31b23bca24dbd4\nwpt-pr: 63989\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/xhr/overridemimetype-chunked-response.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/xhr/resources/content-in-chunks.py"], "git_node": "d8b193790475e83fd11c0d22b9caad6d8dc17f83", "git_parents": ["abf86dd2ae903bce69c2a1257c0972b3be913e9b"], "node": "12fe37fdbc442339aab34097e915d32937b68564", "parents": ["402c7bd749c215eadf2b3ea9f2b6a1df4ef11a55"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Sneddon \u003cgsnedders@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077061 [wpt PR 63156] - Make the STP download timeout, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd timeouts to HTTP downloads\n\nGive httputils.get() and get_download_to_descriptor() a (connect, read)\ntimeout, defaulting to (60, 60) seconds. The read timeout bounds the gap\nbetween bytes rather than the total time, so slow but steady downloads\nare unaffected, while a stalled connection now fails (and so is retried\nby get_download_to_descriptor) instead of hanging forever.\n\n--\nRetry the Safari Technology Preview download\n\nDownload the STP disk image with get_download_to_descriptor() so that\nit gets its retries with backoff, and so that it is streamed to disk\nrather than buffered in memory.\n\nThe file is now always saved as SafariTechnologyPreview.dmg rather than\nusing the filename from the response; nothing relied on that name, as\nthe extracted app is named after the contents of the image.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: cc7809f37b865cb4389180ecff74e06df86f9697, d0e37a8c50d5897133832801461df18a4819641b\nwpt-pr: 63156\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wpt/browser.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wpt/httputils.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wpt/tests/test_httputils.py"], "git_node": "81e3d072422e08ef9f999be0e2f260698ce8da7b", "git_parents": ["d8b193790475e83fd11c0d22b9caad6d8dc17f83"], "node": "35b04868e6918b6f0afabb2fde9e1d35a54382a0", "parents": ["12fe37fdbc442339aab34097e915d32937b68564"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Sneddon \u003cgsnedders@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084029 [wpt PR 63882] - Increase reliability of wpt-fyi-notify workflow, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nConvert workflows/wpt_fyi_notify.yml to a matrix\n\nWe no longer need the `if: ${{ !cancelled() }}` as we don't need to\nensure we post to both servers: `fail-fast: false` achieves that.\n\n--\nMove workflows/wpt_fyi_notify.yml to ubuntu-slim\n\nThere's no need to run on the full Ubuntu VMs, the lightweight CPU/RAM\nconstrained containers are fine.\n\n--\nAdd retry to workflows/wpt_fyi_notify.yml\n\nWe occasionally see this failing, timing out; allow it to retry up to\n10 times, every 30s. (Ideally we'd do something smarter with\nexponential backoff, but we can't do that with\nfjogeleit/http-request-action.)\n\n--\nIncrease workflows/wpt_fyi_notify.yml timeout to 60s\n\nThis may be the actual thing we need to avoid the timeouts we\noccasionally see, and not the retries.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 06d0f6c9dc15a24c94a85f1b16642ef65c94f8b5, 9f94a5426b63d6335d6f9cb45c02f2ac640984ae, 498727c26bdb655741cfa166b32dcc7067d23ec6, dd4ff15247b39788bc522fd9350026ad6cbe32ae\nwpt-pr: 63882\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/.github/workflows/wpt_fyi_notify.yml"], "git_node": "97dfc41aa57dfbf5190d978b5b365af2b2964d94", "git_parents": ["81e3d072422e08ef9f999be0e2f260698ce8da7b"], "node": "8f28b69eb00c3fb4a4b03bedd673da7dcc2a7772", "parents": ["35b04868e6918b6f0afabb2fde9e1d35a54382a0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084299 [wpt PR 63900] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328102, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nBlob's text() should decode its data as it arrives\n\nSince 324134@main, Blob's text() reads the whole blob into an ArrayBuffer and then decodes it as\nUTF-8. FileReaderLoader allocates that ArrayBuffer at the blob's full size when the load starts,\nzero-fills it, copies each chunk into it, and only decodes once the last chunk has arrived.\n\nAdd FileReaderLoader::ReadAsUTF8Text, which passes each chunk to a TextResourceDecoder that always\nuses UTF-8 and appends the result to a StringBuilder. Blob's text() no longer allocates or\nzero-fills a buffer of the blob's size, and memory grows with the decoded text as it arrives rather\nthan all being allocated up front. Peak memory is about the same as before: each decoded chunk is\nstill copied into the StringBuilder, and the StringBuilder grows by reallocating. Reserving its\ncapacity from the blob's size would avoid that for ASCII, but would use more memory than before for\nother text, since StringBuilder doubles its capacity when it widens to 16-bit.\n\nFor this to work, TextResourceDecoder has to handle a byte order mark split across chunks. When the\nfirst chunk was shorter than three bytes, decode() passed it to the codec right away, so a byte\norder mark that continued in the next chunk was missed: a UTF-8 one was decoded as U+FEFF, and data\nafter a UTF-16 one was decoded as UTF-8. It now holds on to the data until there is enough to tell\nwhether it starts with a byte order mark. This also fixes responseText and JSON responses of\nXMLHttpRequest, and EventSource, which decode their data as it arrives too.\n\nThe network process sends each blob part that is a blob itself as its own chunk, so the new Blob\nsubtests split a byte order mark and a multi-byte sequence across such parts. The new XMLHttpRequest\nand EventSource tests use xhr/resources/content-in-chunks.py, added in 318297@main, to split the\nbyte order mark across network chunks.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328102\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b0912c91005c07733ba19a2d93c712e8547df31a\nwpt-pr: 63900\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/FileAPI/blob/Blob-text.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/eventsource/format-bom-split.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/xhr/split-byte-order-mark.any.js"], "git_node": "97359c04708269ad08b5380b5256b9dfd52d0cab", "git_parents": ["97dfc41aa57dfbf5190d978b5b365af2b2964d94"], "node": "2c0572f20255282ff9ef372b497b89d4f52030ee", "parents": ["8f28b69eb00c3fb4a4b03bedd673da7dcc2a7772"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084299 [wpt PR 63900] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63900\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/FileAPI/blob/Blob-constructor-endings.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/FileAPI/blob/Blob-stream-byob-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/eventsource/format-bom-split.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/xhr/split-byte-order-mark.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "f3697e7ae91f5a636c3e4e120da289d2d581215d", "git_parents": ["97359c04708269ad08b5380b5256b9dfd52d0cab"], "node": "ccf56f5b40f8fec59d10015f2158118e595ca236", "parents": ["2c0572f20255282ff9ef372b497b89d4f52030ee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Karl Dubost \u003ckarlcow@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085388 [wpt PR 64004] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327912, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[SVG text] Enable the SVG 2 text layout algorithm by default (#64004)\n\nTurn on SVG2TextLayoutAlgorithmEnabled.\n\nTest changes:\n- svg/batik/text/xmlSpace.svg: a collapsible space that follows a preserved space is now kept, as\n  the line layout decides whitespace. This matches Chrome and Firefox.\n- svg/batik/text/textLayout.svg: spacingAndGlyphs with word-spacing now dumps the stretched\n  positions of each word instead of unstretched positions under a single transform. The rendering is\n  the same.\n- svg/batik/text/textLength.svg: spacingAndGlyphs with text-anchor now dumps the start of the\n  stretched text, for example 225 - 50 / 2 = 200 for textLength=\"50\" at x=\"225\", instead of the\n  unstretched anchored position under a transform. The rendering is the same.\n- svg/custom/glyph-transformation-with-hkern.svg, svg/text/font-size-below-point-five.svg,\n  svg/zoom/page/zoom-mask-with-percentages.svg: 0.01px width differences.\n- GTK and WPE: 1px text box size differences in svg/ text tests.\n- WPT textLength-list-x-spacingAndGlyphs.svg: fix the test. It expected the explicit x positions to\n  move with the glyph stretching. That is wrong per spec, which applies absolute positions after\n  textLength, and Chrome and Firefox fail the test on wpt.fyi. The test and the reference now expect\n  each glyph to stretch in place at its x position. What the test is about, textLength applying\n  across the whole element instead of to each chunk (webkit.org/b/61855), is not affected.\n- mozilla/svg/text/textLength-5.svg and WPT textLength-list-y-spacing.svg now pass.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327912\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324088@main\n\nCo-authored-by: Antti Koivisto \u003cantti@apple.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a99194dae454c71137666ae3736f97851c354e51\nwpt-pr: 64004\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/text/reftests/textLength-list-x-spacingAndGlyphs-ref.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/text/reftests/textLength-list-x-spacingAndGlyphs.svg"], "git_node": "e279489df302d8f61e400e529b9a83bdbb0a88cd", "git_parents": ["f3697e7ae91f5a636c3e4e120da289d2d581215d"], "node": "5aa7028ad48cfef185934d41f61b26fc8d9a0564", "parents": ["ccf56f5b40f8fec59d10015f2158118e595ca236"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085388 [wpt PR 64004] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64004\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/svg/text/reftests/textLength-list-x-spacingAndGlyphs.svg.ini"], "git_node": "2cbfa2349260f5907b4a41c407a403c713cd339b", "git_parents": ["e279489df302d8f61e400e529b9a83bdbb0a88cd"], "node": "32d81db3dd12ed404ff054f0ddd31eb139587cd6", "parents": ["5aa7028ad48cfef185934d41f61b26fc8d9a0564"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yusuke Suzuki \u003cysuzuki@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059990 [wpt PR 61678] - IndexedDB: assert a self-referential array key path exhausts the stack, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nIndexedDB: assert a self-referential array key path exhausts the stack\n\nThe \"array loop -\u003e stringify becomes ['']\" case built a self-referential\narray and used it as an object store key path:\n\n    let loop_array = [];\n    loop_array.push(loop_array);\n\nA sequence key path is converted with the WebIDL sequence\u003cDOMString\u003e\nconversion, so each item goes through ToString. For item 0 that is\nToString(loop_array), which is Array.prototype.toString -\u003e\nArray.prototype.join, and join converts element 0 with ToString again.\n\nECMA-262 defines no cycle detection for Array.prototype.join\n(https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-array.prototype.join), so that recursion is\nunbounded and the conversion cannot complete. The case asserted that the\nkey path becomes [''] and each value is used as its own key, which only\nhappens in an engine that the engine is not implementing the spec\ncorrectly and doing some implementation-dependent behavior.\n\nAssert the outcome the specification implies instead. The conversion\nexceeds an implementation limit and reports an error rather than quietly\nproducing ['']. Every engine signals stack exhaustion with a RangeError.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c492ed5a32d21ff7e6b9662079405d67c4be5291\nwpt-pr: 61678\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/IndexedDB/keypath.any.js"], "git_node": "d1326e36385ab390b4bfe9aa2ab104374a93ad60", "git_parents": ["2cbfa2349260f5907b4a41c407a403c713cd339b"], "node": "16e5972274e0927b2ce8c3481454bf8b2ed37cd6", "parents": ["32d81db3dd12ed404ff054f0ddd31eb139587cd6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059990 [wpt PR 61678] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61678\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/IndexedDB/keypath.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "919ac0880cb8d8bc580472d43cb34bcbc22bb26a", "git_parents": ["d1326e36385ab390b4bfe9aa2ab104374a93ad60"], "node": "608eb76c0b1e0ce39100bfb33096ec5dbd697f08", "parents": ["16e5972274e0927b2ce8c3481454bf8b2ed37cd6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Sapin \u003csimon@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084878 [wpt PR 63944] - Don\u2019t update shadow DOM of disconnected \u003cinput\u003e, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDon\u2019t update shadow DOM of disconnected \u003cinput\u003e\n\nThis skips some work unnecessary because another update will be triggered\nwhen (if) the element is later connected to a document and rendered.\n\nThis changes https://browserbench.org/Speedometer3.1/ score from 11.2 to 11.4\non my laptop.\n\nSigned-off-by: Simon Sapin \u003csimon@igalia.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0ed321dcab3b3943d281b56ddc71c9f1a5feecab\nwpt-pr: 63944\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/replaced-elements/the-input-element/input-update-while-disconnected-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/replaced-elements/the-input-element/input-update-while-disconnected.html"], "git_node": "642613d8945d5792bb682b6178fa1eac2fcb7e74", "git_parents": ["919ac0880cb8d8bc580472d43cb34bcbc22bb26a"], "node": "14c39b94ca40dc457d1dddfb9bddd7ee2385bbf1", "parents": ["608eb76c0b1e0ce39100bfb33096ec5dbd697f08"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085392 [wpt PR 63993] - layout: Treat `\u003cmeter\u003e` and `\u003cprogress\u003e` as widgets, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nlayout: Treat `\u003cmeter\u003e` and `\u003cprogress\u003e` as widgets\n\nMostly, the effects are:\n- They will be atomic if they have `display: inline`. All browsers agree\n  with this.\n- They won't stretch by default if they have `display: block`. Gecko\n  agrees, Blink and WebKit don't.\n- They will be be considered as \"compressible replaced\", as required by\n  the spec.\n\nSigned-off-by: Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 62a5c28767d5d9258f6fd07da5473f15889c8cd7\nwpt-pr: 63993\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-meter-element/meter-widget-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-meter-element/meter-widget.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-progress-element/progress-widget-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-progress-element/progress-widget.html"], "git_node": "9765a8ce3c6f7fc6c047c83cc8edb9febbf476a7", "git_parents": ["642613d8945d5792bb682b6178fa1eac2fcb7e74"], "node": "3b550eb577afea4458de28b26d173afc69173d41", "parents": ["14c39b94ca40dc457d1dddfb9bddd7ee2385bbf1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083557 [wpt PR 63852] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327148, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSVG timeline resets to 0 when it is paused and seeked before it begins (#63852)\n\nThis patch aligns WebKit with Gecko / Firefox and Blink / Chromium.\n\nIf pauseAnimations() and setCurrentTime() are both called on an \u003csvg\u003e before\nits timeline begins, SMILTimeContainer::begin() seeks the animations to the\npreset time but never sets m_accumulatedActiveTime. While paused, elapsed()\nreturns m_accumulatedActiveTime, so getCurrentTime() reports 0. After\nunpauseAnimations(), the timeline restarts from 0 instead of from the seeked\ntime.\n\nFix this by setting m_accumulatedActiveTime to the preset start time in\nbegin() when the container is already paused.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327148\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324084@main\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 80a141ea4d7128b90c74b44349a93b30dffce7f3\nwpt-pr: 63852\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/animations/pause-and-seek-before-begin.html"], "git_node": "700019f731ece6076a675194aaf8630ffe2b94bd", "git_parents": ["9765a8ce3c6f7fc6c047c83cc8edb9febbf476a7"], "node": "1f1c85b99f713a6d381f9b18755c391c930d7d52", "parents": ["3b550eb577afea4458de28b26d173afc69173d41"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085395 [wpt PR 64005] - script: Acknowledge that `cellspacing` attribute of `\u003ctable\u003e` affects preshints, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nscript: Acknowledge that `cellspacing` attribute of `\u003ctable\u003e` affects preshints\n\nNow we will correctly update presentational hints when the value of that\nattribute changes dynamically.\n\nTesting: Adding a new test\n\nSigned-off-by: Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f6880eca1af36e5572d433b6032915d1fd7e3725\nwpt-pr: 64005\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/non-replaced-elements/tables/table-attribute-cellspacing-dynamic.html"], "git_node": "a71a640e041591eb57829aaf3cefc3da07ad0fa5", "git_parents": ["700019f731ece6076a675194aaf8630ffe2b94bd"], "node": "9f35286b91a67d8bc423c893dfc0863d17695cd5", "parents": ["1f1c85b99f713a6d381f9b18755c391c930d7d52"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080689 [wpt PR 63544] - Test range, meter, and progress orientation in sideways-lr, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nTest range, meter, and progress orientation in sideways-lr\n\nFor https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/13054.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7e4fe2d95f962bc69d1f99546e01420bd6e94af3\nwpt-pr: 63544\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/forms/meter-appearance-native-sideways-lr-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/forms/meter-appearance-native-sideways-lr-rtl-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/forms/meter-appearance-native-sideways-lr-rtl.optional.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/forms/meter-appearance-native-sideways-lr.optional.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/forms/progress-appearance-native-sideways-lr-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/forms/progress-appearance-native-sideways-lr-rtl-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/forms/progress-appearance-native-sideways-lr-rtl.optional.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/forms/progress-appearance-native-sideways-lr.optional.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/forms/progress-appearance-none-sideways-lr-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/forms/progress-appearance-none-sideways-lr-rtl-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/forms/progress-appearance-none-sideways-lr-rtl.optional.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/forms/progress-appearance-none-sideways-lr.optional.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/forms/range-input-appearance-native-sideways-lr-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/forms/range-input-appearance-native-sideways-lr-rtl-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/forms/range-input-appearance-native-sideways-lr-rtl.optional.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/forms/range-input-appearance-native-sideways-lr.optional.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/forms/range-input-appearance-none-sideways-lr-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/forms/range-input-appearance-none-sideways-lr-rtl-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/forms/range-input-appearance-none-sideways-lr-rtl.optional.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/forms/range-input-appearance-none-sideways-lr.optional.html"], "git_node": "0d231632804645f70d3ba46279b17e70bba425c2", "git_parents": ["a71a640e041591eb57829aaf3cefc3da07ad0fa5"], "node": "b6ccce20ad875707f12eb0cf5aed56afdf07524e", "parents": ["9f35286b91a67d8bc423c893dfc0863d17695cd5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080689 [wpt PR 63544] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63544\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-writing-modes/forms/meter-appearance-native-sideways-lr-rtl.optional.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-writing-modes/forms/meter-appearance-native-sideways-lr.optional.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-writing-modes/forms/progress-appearance-native-sideways-lr-rtl.optional.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-writing-modes/forms/progress-appearance-native-sideways-lr.optional.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-writing-modes/forms/progress-appearance-none-sideways-lr-rtl.optional.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-writing-modes/forms/progress-appearance-none-sideways-lr.optional.html.ini"], "git_node": "b66d0517d13aa17372129259fdeffc55cc7012fa", "git_parents": ["0d231632804645f70d3ba46279b17e70bba425c2"], "node": "b6ebb9e3fa67a341d52b907bfff25a1a087988fc", "parents": ["b6ccce20ad875707f12eb0cf5aed56afdf07524e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085071 [wpt PR 63951] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=301858, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nUpdate \u003coption\u003e when descendants change\n\nHTMLOptionElement::childrenChanged() only sees changes to the children of an\n\u003coption\u003e. When text deeper down changes, as in\n\u003coption\u003e\u003cspan\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/option\u003e, the \u003cselect\u003e does not update its rendering,\nbutton text, or validity, and the observers of a \u003cdatalist\u003e are not notified.\n\nElements now have an IsInSelectOrDataListSubtree state flag. \u003cselect\u003e and\n\u003cdatalist\u003e elements set it when they are created, and other elements get it\nfrom their parent in their insertion, removing, and moving steps. When the\nchildren of an element with that flag change, ContainerNode::childrenChanged()\ncalls the new Element::descendantsChanged() on it and on each of its ancestors\nwith the flag, up to the outermost \u003cselect\u003e or \u003cdatalist\u003e. Elsewhere this costs\na flag check. As HTMLOptionElement::childrenChanged() did for the \u003cselect\u003e,\nchanges made while cloning are skipped.\n\nHTMLOptionElement::descendantsChanged() replaces\nHTMLOptionElement::childrenChanged(). HTMLDataListElement::descendantsChanged()\nreplaces HTMLDataListElement::childrenChanged(), as well as the walk over all\nancestors that HTMLOptionElement::childrenChanged() did on each change to find\n\u003cdatalist\u003e elements. A \u003cdatalist\u003e now also notifies its observers when the\nparser inserts its children, as it already did when the parser inserted text\ninto its options.\n\nFollow-ups will use this for changes to descendants of the \u003cselect\u003e's \u003cbutton\u003e,\nof \u003cselectedcontent\u003e, and of the \u003clegend\u003e of an \u003coptgroup\u003e, and for changes to\nthe alt attribute of \u003cimg\u003e elements.\n\nThis makes dynamic-content-change-rendering.html pass.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=301858\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 07c5c48bb488a04864a393e6da4d63067a3a1c89\nwpt-pr: 63951\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/select-validity-option-descendants.html"], "git_node": "0c059803fe1c28d4aed26cb23b58cddd4a14eb12", "git_parents": ["b66d0517d13aa17372129259fdeffc55cc7012fa"], "node": "c41f85a00c665de3fdee5337f582ba18faa8de11", "parents": ["b6ebb9e3fa67a341d52b907bfff25a1a087988fc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085071 [wpt PR 63951] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63951\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/select-validity-option-descendants.html.ini"], "git_node": "0ceaf99278b3ed5739702c85e20cf07b9bd2faea", "git_parents": ["0c059803fe1c28d4aed26cb23b58cddd4a14eb12"], "node": "52a891f343297335cfce6a3ea90731f843f8d7f8", "parents": ["c41f85a00c665de3fdee5337f582ba18faa8de11"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085401 [wpt PR 64030] - Test about:blank popups with a non-secure opener, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nTest about:blank popups with a non-secure opener\n\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327702 (follow-up to #63718).\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: be1d6fb98e203c8b32ac15dfae373aea8644ec67\nwpt-pr: 64030\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/origin/origin-keyed-agent-clusters/about-blank-popup-insecure-opener.tentative.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/origin/origin-keyed-agent-clusters/about-blank-popup.https.sub.html"], "git_node": "a62193ab2fa742eba24a3ddaca10114f0a1de10c", "git_parents": ["0ceaf99278b3ed5739702c85e20cf07b9bd2faea"], "node": "73f80c778e8a0db8d38e9d63bf2cbe0ed148cf07", "parents": ["52a891f343297335cfce6a3ea90731f843f8d7f8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085401 [wpt PR 64030] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64030\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/origin/origin-keyed-agent-clusters/about-blank-popup-insecure-opener.tentative.sub.html.ini"], "git_node": "3de534f25bc6fb2d81e448993eca19abdd918c78", "git_parents": ["a62193ab2fa742eba24a3ddaca10114f0a1de10c"], "node": "c57f05cbe87af5e30bfe9a715c93bf5da68b01ba", "parents": ["73f80c778e8a0db8d38e9d63bf2cbe0ed148cf07"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085402 [wpt PR 63983] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328319, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSerializing a SharedArrayBuffer only requires a cross-origin isolated process\n\nHTML only lets cross-origin isolated contexts serialize a SharedArrayBuffer.\nSerializedScriptValue also allows it whenever\nJSC::Options::useSharedArrayBuffer() is set, as it is in cross-origin isolated\nprocesses to expose the constructor. So contexts in those processes that aren't\ncross-origin isolated could serialize one too, such as a cross-origin frame\nwithout allow=\"cross-origin-isolated\", or a frame with a\nDocument-Isolation-Policy that may not use that feature.\n\nThose processes no longer set the option. WebCore instead exposes the\nconstructor on each of their global objects through the new\nJSGlobalObject::exposeSharedArrayBuffer(), as HTML exposes it throughout a\ncross-origin isolated agent cluster. The option remains for tests.\n\nOn Cocoa platforms, setting the option had no effect in processes in Lockdown\nMode or without the JIT, such as those for Enhanced Security (because\nJSC::Options::initialize() only takes effect the first time). The new\nallowSharedArrayBuffer option keeps the constructor out of them.\n\nAs in HTML, a worklet now has its document's cross-origin isolated capability,\nso an AudioWorklet can still serialize a SharedArrayBuffer.\naudioworklet-postmessage-sharedarraybuffer.https.html already passed, so its\nSkip is removed.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328319\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 652ec617f3d9fcc34d4c3b399d6bc30be2ef2c85\nwpt-pr: 63983\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/cross-origin-isolated-permissions-policy.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/infrastructure/safe-passing-of-structured-data/shared-array-buffers/window-iframe-not-cross-origin-isolated.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/infrastructure/safe-passing-of-structured-data/shared-array-buffers/window-iframe-not-cross-origin-isolated.https.html.headers"], "git_node": "05b18f8bd49f4a7187caae50d23380265c6ed673", "git_parents": ["3de534f25bc6fb2d81e448993eca19abdd918c78"], "node": "9230e7b525733b303997764a5e77d586e5e91ac8", "parents": ["c57f05cbe87af5e30bfe9a715c93bf5da68b01ba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085402 [wpt PR 63983] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63983\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/document-isolation-policy/cross-origin-isolated-permissions-policy.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/infrastructure/safe-passing-of-structured-data/shared-array-buffers/window-iframe-not-cross-origin-isolated.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "6e81c3dd25755ecb1cd3e4f569371bf37144c679", "git_parents": ["05b18f8bd49f4a7187caae50d23380265c6ed673"], "node": "a7e02c457d741615ee4f4ab561cbc9e30263ab9e", "parents": ["9230e7b525733b303997764a5e77d586e5e91ac8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085404 [wpt PR 63992] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328351, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nEventSource should not use a UTF-16 byte order mark\n\nHTML decodes event streams with UTF-8 decode, which strips a UTF-8 byte order mark but ignores a\nUTF-16 one. EventSource's TextResourceDecoder switched to UTF-16 when the stream started with a\nUTF-16 byte order mark, so the rest of the stream was decoded as UTF-16 and no events were\ndispatched.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328351\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e88a6af55a16641f6d238d7e0804719000dfe164\nwpt-pr: 63992\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/eventsource/format-bom-utf-16.any.js"], "git_node": "bdcca18ad26277f8c7223b5cd14f9865edfc13f7", "git_parents": ["6e81c3dd25755ecb1cd3e4f569371bf37144c679"], "node": "2b499408b4c2651de772fa10e47909ea25b40062", "parents": ["a7e02c457d741615ee4f4ab561cbc9e30263ab9e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Robertson \u003cjamestherobertson@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082790 [wpt PR 63736] - navigateEvent.userInitiated should be true for non-simulated clicks, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nnavigateEvent.userInitiated should be true for non-simulated clicks\n\n--\nnavigateEvent.userInitiated should be true for non-simulated clicks\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3b2d7960d2295336df4448bd87fbec5b15d1966b, d2cc128e55ae2dab4b5dd804c5bfad163c392df2\nwpt-pr: 63736\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/navigate-event/navigate-anchor-cross-origin-userInitiated.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/navigate-event/navigate-anchor-same-origin-cross-document-userInitiated.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/navigate-event/navigate-anchor-with-target-userInitiated.html"], "git_node": "48e4757c2e43a17ca5cf51d6f845e7cfcd4dc7ba", "git_parents": ["bdcca18ad26277f8c7223b5cd14f9865edfc13f7"], "node": "be5bcf5fdfec62675e904f4ae5611ef35b93bf26", "parents": ["2b499408b4c2651de772fa10e47909ea25b40062"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082790 [wpt PR 63736] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63736\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/navigation-api/navigate-event/navigate-form-onformdata-navigate-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/navigation-api/navigate-event/potentially-reset-focus-no-document-element-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "8d3088e0a257b04b7346b7e778d3a49d4944ce1d", "git_parents": ["48e4757c2e43a17ca5cf51d6f845e7cfcd4dc7ba"], "node": "66b2ab8e72390239cddc051f79ec281d2085d5dc", "parents": ["be5bcf5fdfec62675e904f4ae5611ef35b93bf26"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Romain Menke \u003c11521496+romainmenke@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085405 [wpt PR 63998] - [css-color] guard against naive f32 implementations for `Lab` to `xyz` conversion, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-color] guard against naive f32 implementations for lab to xyz conversion (#63998)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ac6f144e056423fe18efafe318bca0d3bf374756\nwpt-pr: 63998\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-color/parsing/color-computed-color-mix-function.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-color/parsing/color-computed-relative-color.html"], "git_node": "f5d17d6c1aa1cc355031e20409ef7b3f0747bf6c", "git_parents": ["8d3088e0a257b04b7346b7e778d3a49d4944ce1d"], "node": "ba13d4ef499e0adbbeb7131ab7c96d15f398315d", "parents": ["66b2ab8e72390239cddc051f79ec281d2085d5dc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085405 [wpt PR 63998] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63998\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-color/parsing/color-computed-color-mix-function.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-color/parsing/color-computed-relative-color.html.ini"], "git_node": "df3743d53efe0259c21d3e84facadb4ec0369268", "git_parents": ["f5d17d6c1aa1cc355031e20409ef7b3f0747bf6c"], "node": "b152d807f11f320dbc565fcb3caee8749456d1ac", "parents": ["ba13d4ef499e0adbbeb7131ab7c96d15f398315d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eriko Kurimoto \u003celkurin@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085407 [wpt PR 64043] - Revert \"Avoid dangling reference in HTMLAnchorElementBase::NavigateToHyperlink.\", a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRevert \"Avoid dangling reference in HTMLAnchorElementBase::NavigateToHyperlink.\"\n\nThis reverts commit 280ca3161bda00f116803a7064aba3ce91a7d59e.\n\nReason for revert: Causing a failure on linux-blink-leak-rel due to\nexternal/wpt/trusted-types/navigate-to-javascript-url-009-crash.html\n\nFailure Link: https://ci.chromium.org/ui/p/chromium/builders/ci/Mac13%20Tests/42984/overview\n\nOriginal change's description:\n\u003e Avoid dangling reference in HTMLAnchorElementBase::NavigateToHyperlink.\n\u003e\n\u003e Fixed: 565674529\n\u003e Change-Id: Ia3248d945dc01328e8f354ec28d7cfcadafb87f3\n\u003e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8464608\n\u003e Auto-Submit: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Commit-Queue: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Reviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Commit-Queue: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1706396}\n\nBug: 565674529\nNo-Presubmit: true\nNo-Tree-Checks: true\nNo-Try: true\nChange-Id: Id6e28582a83f7405347ab0ecd207748885599fbf\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8482891\nAuto-Submit: Eriko Kurimoto \u003celkurin@chromium.org\u003e\nBot-Commit: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\nOwners-Override: Eriko Kurimoto \u003celkurin@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1706622}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0d6e3d4f45eed83c1e2a3701ce37bd3fd316af1c\nwpt-pr: 64043\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/trusted-types/navigate-to-javascript-url-009-crash.html"], "git_node": "c4924cfdd809756e9e2796af3bb1b589372cbf57", "git_parents": ["df3743d53efe0259c21d3e84facadb4ec0369268"], "node": "2754c9ac4a7b10cd796cc78460ed48aed6f989d9", "parents": ["b152d807f11f320dbc565fcb3caee8749456d1ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085408 [wpt PR 64044] - Show caret and allow keyboard selection in readonly inputs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nShow caret and allow keyboard selection in readonly inputs\n\nDisallowing keyboard selection (arrow keys or shift+arrow keys)\ninterferes with keyboard users and ATs. This patch allows selection to\nbe modified by the keyboard but does not allow the user to modify the\ntext inside the input.\n\nThe caret will now become visible, but will not blink. This matches\nfirefox's behavior.\n\nFixed: 40801366\nChange-Id: Id451449bc2c46b9a8404325720f5e64cbfc36ebf\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8227384\nReviewed-by: David Grogan \u003cdgrogan@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1708274}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 87c35d10ab8913a1f7f2d2b6683c05e5cca556f7\nwpt-pr: 64044\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/textfieldselection/selection-readonly-keyboard.tentative.html"], "git_node": "3f72749989765231584182cc6e7b96b826a4736a", "git_parents": ["c4924cfdd809756e9e2796af3bb1b589372cbf57"], "node": "26801275e59d210df83c97928c11fc8f557d9666", "parents": ["2754c9ac4a7b10cd796cc78460ed48aed6f989d9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085411 [wpt PR 64031] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328334, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nLocation-object navigations check the wrong document to decide whether they replace\n\nSome of HTML's rules for turning \"auto\" history handling into \"replace\" depend\non the navigated document: it is the initial about:blank document of a child\nnavigable, or, for a Location-object navigation without transient activation, it\nisn't completely loaded yet. Location::setLocation() checked the latter against\nthe first window's frame and activation instead of the navigated document and\nthe incumbent's activation. For a frame in another process, the process with its\ndocument applied neither rule, so such navigations added a session history\nentry.\n\nLocation::setLocation() now only records whether the incumbent has transient\nactivation, as the new ReplaceIfNotCompletelyLoaded, and the navigated frame\nchecks whether its document is completely loaded: NavigationScheduler does so\nfor a frame in the same process, and FrameLoader::load() when the frame's\nprocess gets the navigation from another process after its policy decision.\nThere it also applies the initial about:blank rule. Form submissions to a frame\nin another process now leave \"auto\" to that process too.\n\nSo navigating a frame that has finished loading no longer replaces just because\nthe document doing it hasn't. Within a process,\nNavigationScheduler::mustLockBackForwardList() still also replaces other script\nnavigations of a document that hasn't finished loading, such as window.open()\ninto an existing frame; across processes only HTML's rules apply.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328334\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324419@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ee314e68f97daf421fcefd2448968efa77512014\nwpt-pr: 64031\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/history/the-location-interface/location-replace-cross-site.html"], "git_node": "c00b2dcc58951ec69b126aee40b8d5246194def4", "git_parents": ["3f72749989765231584182cc6e7b96b826a4736a"], "node": "d484ed038f44d81cc0b00129924e78a2440d3b52", "parents": ["26801275e59d210df83c97928c11fc8f557d9666"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085411 [wpt PR 64031] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64031\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/history/the-location-interface/cross-origin-location-stringify-crash.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/history/the-location-interface/location-replace-cross-site.html.ini"], "git_node": "7c1b51923a115f63e693fee46dfa934b234bcdc2", "git_parents": ["c00b2dcc58951ec69b126aee40b8d5246194def4"], "node": "62339e260035a2110735b926396bec8e68ecf737", "parents": ["d484ed038f44d81cc0b00129924e78a2440d3b52"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085412 [wpt PR 64038] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328472, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nUpdate \u003cselect\u003e when descendants of its \u003cbutton\u003e change\n\nThe native appearance of a \u003cselect\u003e with a \u003cbutton\u003e shows the text of that\n\u003cbutton\u003e, and assistive technologies get it as the value of the \u003cselect\u003e, but\nonly changes to the children of the \u003cbutton\u003e or of \u003cselectedcontent\u003e updated\nthem.\n\nUsing the mechanism of 324413@main, HTMLButtonElement::descendantsChanged()\nreplaces HTMLButtonElement::childrenChanged(), so changes anywhere in the\n\u003cbutton\u003e, including inside \u003cselectedcontent\u003e, update the \u003cselect\u003e.\nHTMLSelectedContentElement::childrenChanged() is no longer needed.\n\nHTMLSelectElement::buttonElementChildrenChanged() now also invalidates the\nstyle of the \u003cselect\u003e, as RenderMenuList only measures the text again once that\nstyle is resolved. Without it, the width that 322716@main bases on the text of\nthe \u003cbutton\u003e didn't change after the first rendering. This is the same fix\n262791@main made for \u003coption\u003e.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328472\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 19da05009ce7443ead2a6fbd9d035db61cae25c4\nwpt-pr: 64038\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-auto-button-descendant-mutation-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-auto-button-descendant-mutation.html"], "git_node": "808cb7aac5edef64b5d557aa2ab4936a1d017db8", "git_parents": ["7c1b51923a115f63e693fee46dfa934b234bcdc2"], "node": "f29e9a2c33611ab2e2600c43261a7b09675d8645", "parents": ["62339e260035a2110735b926396bec8e68ecf737"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085412 [wpt PR 64038] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64038\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-auto-button-descendant-mutation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-disabled.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-base-appearance-writing-modes.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-picker-icon-open-state.html.ini"], "git_node": "368bac4eebd0b1fa5297eaa6660d8a46ab5e867e", "git_parents": ["808cb7aac5edef64b5d557aa2ab4936a1d017db8"], "node": "1e148282f8cbd74910286d98061a823efef4a359", "parents": ["f29e9a2c33611ab2e2600c43261a7b09675d8645"], "tags": []}, {"author": "youennf \u003cyouennf@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083278 [wpt PR 63787] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=302253, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAAC AudioEncoder produces incorrect decoder config description (#63787)\n\nInstead of outputting directly what the cocoa audio encoder provides us as cookie,\nwe parse it for AAC to align with WebCodecs specification.\n\nThis aligns with Chrome and Firefox.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=302253\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 265268d3dc447243cd728b50318f2f8b4a60a49e\nwpt-pr: 63787\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/audio-encoder-aac-description.html"], "git_node": "9be3c1709660ddf332383aa7d4cc985ddbc9a02f", "git_parents": ["368bac4eebd0b1fa5297eaa6660d8a46ab5e867e"], "node": "f41cab39e922abdd5be0783facc6a2b2e9fc1143", "parents": ["1e148282f8cbd74910286d98061a823efef4a359"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083278 [wpt PR 63787] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63787\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/audio-encoder-aac-description.html.ini"], "git_node": "4118bca8013d5cbd27c04756f177b5de1a84e820", "git_parents": ["9be3c1709660ddf332383aa7d4cc985ddbc9a02f"], "node": "7bf56b8f1efb80b5dbf85e6c143d542ac953c292", "parents": ["f41cab39e922abdd5be0783facc6a2b2e9fc1143"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Blink WPT Bot \u003cblink-w3c-test-autoroller@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077444 [wpt PR 63193] - [payments] Add fieldtrial config for PaymentRequest ClientSecurityState, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[payments] Add fieldtrial config for PaymentRequest ClientSecurityState (#63193)\n\nThis change also adds an android web view flag and updates to tests so\nthey don't get blocked by LNA.\n\nWant-Code-Review: all\nBug: 562091236\nChange-Id: I26f383780e8cecadcbd5a973914b4a3b203bc75e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8478636\nCommit-Queue: Stephen McGruer \u003csmcgruer@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stephen McGruer \u003csmcgruer@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Darwin Yang \u003cdarwinyang@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Jayden Nikifork \u003cnikifork@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1709551}\n\nCo-authored-by: Darwin Yang \u003cdarwinyang@google.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8b6ae3f6cae1dfd86e0315152f5a826aa1942b86\nwpt-pr: 63193\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/common/get-host-info.sub.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/connection-allowlist/tentative/payment-request-app-manifest-blocked.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/connection-allowlist/tentative/payment-request-head-blocked.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/connection-allowlist/tentative/payment-request-manifests-allowed.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/connection-allowlist/tentative/payment-request-payment-manifest-blocked.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/connection-allowlist/tentative/payment-request-payment-manifest-redirect-allowed.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/connection-allowlist/tentative/payment-request-payment-manifest-redirect-blocked.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/payment-method-manifest/pmi-redirect-origins.https.sub.window.js"], "git_node": "54827dc097a18c19bf9755402ddda1769cea7740", "git_parents": ["4118bca8013d5cbd27c04756f177b5de1a84e820"], "node": "22e0b7bfb43eff2ff8834407b28eec31186bde23", "parents": ["7bf56b8f1efb80b5dbf85e6c143d542ac953c292"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077444 [wpt PR 63193] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63193\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/ai/language_detection/availability-detached-crash.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/the-window-object/self-et-al.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "cb9e079fcf600dbb5a1239931a35b18229ad7d45", "git_parents": ["54827dc097a18c19bf9755402ddda1769cea7740"], "node": "04b260effd2f2d7eaa6ccbd4e15672451343d028", "parents": ["22e0b7bfb43eff2ff8834407b28eec31186bde23"], "tags": []}, {"author": "youennf \u003cyouennf@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082576 [wpt PR 63707] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327664, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd support for VideoFrame.rotation (#63707)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 22f057fd265a79c7717089d1673104ae62007feb\nwpt-pr: 63707\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/videoFrame-rotation.any.js"], "git_node": "07839b8cf4e0291b54af5562a0a106a03247f53c", "git_parents": ["cb9e079fcf600dbb5a1239931a35b18229ad7d45"], "node": "1221aa6190ed736369cea84eafea0e2cf2f71d7c", "parents": ["04b260effd2f2d7eaa6ccbd4e15672451343d028"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082576 [wpt PR 63707] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63707\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/videoFrame-rotation.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "b477a12288b2baeffad14b8360aaa630df0cc304", "git_parents": ["07839b8cf4e0291b54af5562a0a106a03247f53c"], "node": "b77b719582cc187cf26dda87d618b1fdecdbda7d", "parents": ["1221aa6190ed736369cea84eafea0e2cf2f71d7c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Shannon Booth \u003c35911232+shannonbooth@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085416 [wpt PR 63995] - Add `Cache-Control` headers for the test262 harness scripts, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd `Cache-Control` headers for the test262 harness scripts (#63995)\n\nEvery test262 test loads many common JavaScript files. Use\n`Cache-Control: max-age=3600` (like in resources/*.headers) so that long\nruns don't fetch and compile them again for each test.\n\nThe vendored harness gets __dir__.headers files instead so that they\nalso cover harness files added by later test262 syncs.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9d04a65194e5a3b676bbdece00a66916da1de7e0\nwpt-pr: 63995\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/resources/test262/test262-provider.js.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/resources/test262/test262-reporter.js.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/third_party/test262/.rsync-exclude", "testing/web-platform/tests/third_party/test262/harness/__dir__.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/third_party/test262/harness/sm/__dir__.headers"], "git_node": "593fa5ccfe8a9e5a244f06806587a27145d524b7", "git_parents": ["b477a12288b2baeffad14b8360aaa630df0cc304"], "node": "9020d0672f021d2fa971d1485bc87da6a3a1ee66", "parents": ["b77b719582cc187cf26dda87d618b1fdecdbda7d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byungwoo Lee \u003cblee@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080850 [wpt PR 63555] - Add 'trusted-types-eval' variants to trusted types eval tests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd 'trusted-types-eval' variants to trusted types eval tests\n\nWith CSP script-src 'trusted-types-eval' and an enforced\nrequire-trusted-types-for 'script', eval(), the Function constructor,\nsetTimeout() and setInterval() with a string should behave the same\nas without a script-src, since the trusted types check runs first,\nand 'trusted-types-eval' is checked after it [1].\n\nAdd variants '?default' for the original configuration (only an enforced\nrequire-trusted-types-for 'script'), and '?trusted-types-eval' for the\nsame cases with script-src 'trusted-types-eval', to the existing tests\nfor eval with trusted types:\n- eval-csp-tt-default-policy.html\n- eval-csp-tt-default-policy-mutate.html\n- eval-csp-tt-no-default-policy.html\n- tt-block-eval.html\n\nThis CL also adds tests for setTimeout() and setInterval() with the\nsame variants:\n- setTimeout-setInterval-csp-tt-default-policy.html\n- setTimeout-setInterval-csp-tt-no-default-policy.html\n\n[1] https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/#can-compile-strings\n\nBug: 388437274\nForce-WPT-Export: true\nChange-Id: I41b08916cac0bf7f4e691cd5f4649ac5cfc792fc\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8555857\nReviewed-by: Antonio Sartori \u003cantoniosartori@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Byungwoo Lee \u003cblee@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1717433}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 377b4f48faf02c5dab34baf847a045de65bf5601\nwpt-pr: 63555\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/lint.ignore", "testing/web-platform/tests/trusted-types/eval-csp-tt-default-policy-mutate.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/trusted-types/eval-csp-tt-default-policy.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/trusted-types/eval-csp-tt-no-default-policy.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/trusted-types/setTimeout-setInterval-csp-tt-default-policy.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/trusted-types/setTimeout-setInterval-csp-tt-no-default-policy.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/trusted-types/tt-block-eval.html"], "git_node": "6777ca77091dbfcfa316f5604d5e7b8fce21cdb6", "git_parents": ["593fa5ccfe8a9e5a244f06806587a27145d524b7"], "node": "df650869dd0807e200082fefdcd0b1969c6efd44", "parents": ["9020d0672f021d2fa971d1485bc87da6a3a1ee66"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byungwoo Lee \u003cblee@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080844 [wpt PR 63448] - Update wpt tests for CSP script-src 'trusted-types-eval', a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nUpdate wpt tests for CSP script-src 'trusted-types-eval'\n\nRewrite the 'trusted-types-eval' wpt tests to use a separate\npromise_test() with a EventWatcher for each subtest. Previously,\nall subtests shared securitypolicyviolation listeners, so a\nsubtest could pass or fail because of another subtest's\nviolation.\n\nAlso add subtests for scripts injected via setTimeout() and\nsetInterval().\n\nBug: 388437274\nForce-WPT-Export: true\nChange-Id: Ib76d9162b7438174f4ae7d9241297a925ce46900\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8529548\nReviewed-by: Antonio Sartori \u003cantoniosartori@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Byungwoo Lee \u003cblee@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1717436}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 43340088fc8841cbfcbc534ab86dc4e6710e2c88\nwpt-pr: 63448\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/script-src/script-src-trusted_types_eval_with_report_only_require_trusted_types_eval.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/script-src/script-src-trusted_types_eval_with_require_trusted_types_eval.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/script-src/script-src-trusted_types_eval_without_require_trusted_types_eval.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/script-src/support/script-src-trusted_types_eval_with_report_only_require_trusted_types_eval_DedicatedWorker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/script-src/support/script-src-trusted_types_eval_with_require_trusted_types_eval_DedicatedWorker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/script-src/support/script-src-trusted_types_eval_without_require_trusted_types_eval_DedicatedWorker.js"], "git_node": "4104706843b057520ccb8b893911a284956152c6", "git_parents": ["6777ca77091dbfcfa316f5604d5e7b8fce21cdb6"], "node": "88ce2c7bbb3a57cdab2d6187f48e33466d6ff517", "parents": ["df650869dd0807e200082fefdcd0b1969c6efd44"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hyowon Kim \u003chyowon@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081289 [wpt PR 63593] - Fix horizontal offset in clip-text table cell WPT ref, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix horizontal offset in clip-text table cell WPT ref\n\nThe test text is shifted 1px right by the default td padding, but the\nref only adjusts the vertical offset. Add left: 1px to the ref so the\ntest passes within its fuzzy limits.\n\nBug: 503018958\nChange-Id: I1a514f021a537d7de1d8766146f58d54ff2f782d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8555797\nCommit-Queue: Hyowon Kim \u003chyowon@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Xianzhu Wang \u003cwangxianzhu@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1717461}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 05e0c59d428c20f95d5f971e3e3a2eb6430a51cb\nwpt-pr: 63593\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-backgrounds/background-clip/clip-text-background-table-cell-ref.html"], "git_node": "f3bb519138aee5c45bf491315062950774ed3da3", "git_parents": ["4104706843b057520ccb8b893911a284956152c6"], "node": "05d975b6237e97372d4ba9c20dd75e007c03a762", "parents": ["88ce2c7bbb3a57cdab2d6187f48e33466d6ff517"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081289 [wpt PR 63593] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63593\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-backgrounds/background-clip/clip-text-background-table-cell.html.ini"], "git_node": "2cae48ce0aa86cad1e0c4f10ef98a75e6319e765", "git_parents": ["f3bb519138aee5c45bf491315062950774ed3da3"], "node": "fb90b66f8e41291766a27361e0473829bbc2d56b", "parents": ["05d975b6237e97372d4ba9c20dd75e007c03a762"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083554 [wpt PR 63851] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327174, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nCSSStyleDeclaration.setProperty() wrongly fails to override an existing !important custom property when called without priority (#63851)\n\nThis patch aligns WebKit with Gecko / Firefox and Blink / Chromium.\n\nIf a declaration block contains `--x: 1 !important`, then calling\n`style.setProperty(\"--x\", \"2\")` should replace it with a normal `--x: 2`.\nThis follows the CSSOM \"set a CSS declaration\" steps, and it's what we\nalready do for standard properties. For custom properties, WebKit ignored\nthe call: MutableStyleProperties::addParsedProperty() refused to replace an\nimportant custom property with a non-important one.\n\nThe check isn't needed for parsing a declaration block either. In\n`--x: 1 !important; --x: 2`, CSSParser::filterProperties() already removes\nthe duplicate and keeps the important value before anything is added. So\nremove the custom-property special case and always call setProperty().\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327174\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324083@main\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4a6fc4d5311a3caef9f9ff5fe243b3b1f67621c9\nwpt-pr: 63851\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom/setproperty-custom-property-override-important.html"], "git_node": "10a3c230d8e18a9dbbbbb676cb20b628016f37e8", "git_parents": ["2cae48ce0aa86cad1e0c4f10ef98a75e6319e765"], "node": "0bac127c9886a06bbea1af12a2cf89974905c17f", "parents": ["fb90b66f8e41291766a27361e0473829bbc2d56b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083554 [wpt PR 63851] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63851\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/cssom/CSSImportRule-insertRule-styleSheet-parentStyleSheet.html.ini"], "git_node": "26f8a7960a52dd7c65c1e68a9ccea790bad62fad", "git_parents": ["10a3c230d8e18a9dbbbbb676cb20b628016f37e8"], "node": "c21b5491576a13a51c97e84246f8711202d422b0", "parents": ["0bac127c9886a06bbea1af12a2cf89974905c17f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Shannon Booth \u003cshannon.ml.booth@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085430 [wpt PR 64047] - Test COEP with a cross-origin iframe navigating to its own blob: URL, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nTest COEP with a cross-origin iframe navigating to its own blob: URL\n\nThe CORP check only applies to HTTP(S) navigation responses, so the\nblob: navigation must not be blocked.\n\nSee https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/13087.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 138aa099be1bb21ae7e247fb104014f6965772e4\nwpt-pr: 64047\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/cross-origin-embedder-policy/cross-origin-iframe-navigates-to-own-blob.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/cross-origin-embedder-policy/cross-origin-iframe-navigates-to-own-blob.https.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/cross-origin-embedder-policy/resources/navigate-to-own-blob.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/cross-origin-embedder-policy/resources/navigate-to-own-blob.html.headers"], "git_node": "b446227afc82db0bfe2ff8ad998e21fbce00866c", "git_parents": ["26f8a7960a52dd7c65c1e68a9ccea790bad62fad"], "node": "51e46bc628958c9adc360b955e2219d54e6c501e", "parents": ["c21b5491576a13a51c97e84246f8711202d422b0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084290 [wpt PR 63898] - Add more tests for paginated OOFs., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd more tests for paginated OOFs.\n\nIncrease test coverage.\n\nBug: 40267498\nChange-Id: I35795fb06c47a8ef6132ab7b775484048d6dbe46\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8606492\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1722097}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a8762f78879da6365695a63f1bae31c3475526f1\nwpt-pr: 63898\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/abspos-001-print-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/abspos-001-print.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/abspos-002-print-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/abspos-002-print.html"], "git_node": "88de95df120973c867461504b849666ca72a93ef", "git_parents": ["b446227afc82db0bfe2ff8ad998e21fbce00866c"], "node": "47e095cefb06d73cc3984a7ab765e7d000ead23f", "parents": ["51e46bc628958c9adc360b955e2219d54e6c501e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084292 [wpt PR 63899] - Tests for fragmented nested OOFs with containing block size dependencies., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nTests for fragmented nested OOFs with containing block size dependencies.\n\nBug: 40267498\nChange-Id: Ie4bb16bb19fefa7dce7182637a05bb9a82908917\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8610229\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1722102}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 514913ff14fde47147cc4fa84444d86dc8bc3112\nwpt-pr: 63899\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/out-of-flow-in-multicolumn-128.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/out-of-flow-in-multicolumn-129.html"], "git_node": "ea1eeb49761b2800f2deff008d4410748c515b57", "git_parents": ["88de95df120973c867461504b849666ca72a93ef"], "node": "5f5c525c4db5879f4a3b1a35401b084ec5af2a95", "parents": ["47e095cefb06d73cc3984a7ab765e7d000ead23f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriele Cabrini \u003cgabrielecabriniii@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084304 [wpt PR 63901] - script: Update rendering after setRangeText() on textarea and input, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nscript: Update rendering after setRangeText() on textarea and input\n\nSigned-off-by: Gabriele Cabrini \u003cgabrielecabriniii@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b076de379dfb71854471ffdfd59983b4db4a720c\nwpt-pr: 63901\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/textfieldselection/setRangeText-repaint-input-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/textfieldselection/setRangeText-repaint-input.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/textfieldselection/setRangeText-repaint-textarea-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/textfieldselection/setRangeText-repaint-textarea.html"], "git_node": "47627e9fb24854627d3d1e0ba60c0212622b663a", "git_parents": ["ea1eeb49761b2800f2deff008d4410748c515b57"], "node": "24dafc642cc5cbe25256ae689a58239ef8932235", "parents": ["5f5c525c4db5879f4a3b1a35401b084ec5af2a95"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084304 [wpt PR 63901] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63901\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/textfieldselection/textarea-setRangeText-utf16-code-unit-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "d30797aa2c6c0025fa1d9db0600863a23070e338", "git_parents": ["47627e9fb24854627d3d1e0ba60c0212622b663a"], "node": "d255bb2e3b2d2e7c5362e5f0d3d63147624deb0a", "parents": ["24dafc642cc5cbe25256ae689a58239ef8932235"], "tags": []}, {"author": "yug \u003cyugagarwal105@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083645 [wpt PR 63860] - wpt: Run fetch-resources test over HTTPS, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nwpt: Use HTTPS for fetch-resources test\n\nSigned-off-by: yug \u003cyugagarwal105@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5e1722065fd75198b42bdff93fa470203f67c381\nwpt-pr: 63860\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/fetching/fetch-resources.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/fetching/fetch-resources.sub.html"], "git_node": "baf2cc5b41e7d3434ef9173bcd3f2bb6534f5b1c", "git_parents": ["d30797aa2c6c0025fa1d9db0600863a23070e338"], "node": "517ce81a6dfc2d082118e78af2c7d0c39165a7c4", "parents": ["d255bb2e3b2d2e7c5362e5f0d3d63147624deb0a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083645 [wpt PR 63860] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63860\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/fetching/fetch-resources.sub.html.ini"], "git_node": "7bb4f0e1c4c9965a25a3e5b79d1c72de98c2af48", "git_parents": ["baf2cc5b41e7d3434ef9173bcd3f2bb6534f5b1c"], "node": "023154d4f543bf4d8324611c040197d66b4e2cef", "parents": ["517ce81a6dfc2d082118e78af2c7d0c39165a7c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mxmgorin \u003c102797145+mxmgorin@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083371 [wpt PR 63792] - webgl: Allow drawing to a framebuffer without a color attachment, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nwebgl: Allow drawing to a framebuffer without a color attachment\n\nSigned-off-by: mxmgorin \u003c102797145+mxmgorin@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 69f2bba61ce7e9469ccbce53de4644a89f6b7dff\nwpt-pr: 63792\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webgl/framebuffer-without-color-attachment.html"], "git_node": "be4b5cbed3873c951111d19cd7a9ee3b0f96fe1a", "git_parents": ["7bb4f0e1c4c9965a25a3e5b79d1c72de98c2af48"], "node": "0758b72c4159cdf5ad0f6ada11054405d2b9204f", "parents": ["023154d4f543bf4d8324611c040197d66b4e2cef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "injun choi \u003ctkfydtls464@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085442 [wpt PR 63445] - Prevent ::backdrop generation outside the top layer, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nPrevent ::backdrop generation outside the top layer\n\nWith OverlayProperty enabled, an element with overlay: auto and a\n::backdrop rule can generate a backdrop outside the top layer.\nCheck that the element is in the top layer before generating\nits ::backdrop.\n\nBug: 571284302\nChange-Id: Iedbb4d18a56e29fac6377268215f92f282469954\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8534727\nReviewed-by: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715358}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 50c79227828081dbbf52cc999635f8ca5f443295\nwpt-pr: 63445\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-position/overlay/backdrop-outside-top-layer.html"], "git_node": "8481a15874a30a04d1802c1802a8c7c436efa7c8", "git_parents": ["be4b5cbed3873c951111d19cd7a9ee3b0f96fe1a"], "node": "e4c459d66f204fd3383627d389517de6e5d46829", "parents": ["0758b72c4159cdf5ad0f6ada11054405d2b9204f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080507 [wpt PR 63444] - [HiC] Suppress snapshot generation for drawables in top layer, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[HiC] Suppress snapshot generation for drawables in top layer\n\nPrior to this CL, the IsInTopLayer() was only applied to the element\nwith the `drawable` attribute, without checking its ancestor chain.\n\nFixed: 568903801\nChange-Id: I89449aa561a6e0a6107575082e11ef2b5d75d453\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8523664\nCommit-Queue: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1716033}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8336f81eac614fa3166554d0fc8197b23dc1b055\nwpt-pr: 63444\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/error-conditions.tentative.html"], "git_node": "94d5780726422ae35f68f17eb1f7ad9cbe468292", "git_parents": ["8481a15874a30a04d1802c1802a8c7c436efa7c8"], "node": "9752df491fdeea6201aa7b39ffd1d831cfe5d987", "parents": ["e4c459d66f204fd3383627d389517de6e5d46829"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080574 [wpt PR 63519] - [html-in-canvas] Sync CanvasPaintEvent&ElementGeometryUpdateEvent IDL, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[html-in-canvas] Sync CanvasPaintEvent&ElementGeometryUpdateEvent IDL\n\nThis patch syncs CanvasPaintEvent and ElementGeometryUpdateEvent\nfrom the explainer:\n* Added [Exposed=Window] (and [RuntimeEnabled=CanvasDrawElement])\n* Added [SameObject, SaveSameObject] to CanvasPaintEvent.changedElements\n* Added [SaveSameObject] to ElementGeometryUpdateEvent.elements\n\nChange-Id: I39404b96dae965bef7dc8a5a216412d1dd852981\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8550257\nCommit-Queue: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Chris Harrelson \u003cchrishtr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1716231}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 143d46141da040a5f0f234bed3780930c2a171f5\nwpt-pr: 63519\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-transform-update-element-image.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-changedElements.tentative.html"], "git_node": "64a2eb9d742b04075f592bd03a1f210000ce72dd", "git_parents": ["94d5780726422ae35f68f17eb1f7ad9cbe468292"], "node": "464acec5f14ba0b6a9d4daf86ab019abc85a10b1", "parents": ["9752df491fdeea6201aa7b39ffd1d831cfe5d987"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080574 [wpt PR 63519] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63519\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-changedElements.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "28e0b89532898da2a269528ad21f036b03505108", "git_parents": ["64a2eb9d742b04075f592bd03a1f210000ce72dd"], "node": "7b919ac003b8f117cc84624004df478fa587e5db", "parents": ["464acec5f14ba0b6a9d4daf86ab019abc85a10b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082869 [wpt PR 63749] - [iframe] Fix flakiness in navigation test, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[iframe] Fix flakiness in navigation test\n\n`responsive-iframe-navigation.html` was flaky for two reasons:\n1. When the initial `200px` iframe content finished layout before the\n   first rendering frame, `ResizeObserver` did not observe the initial\n   `150px` default height. Previously, this was only handled at the end\n   of the test for `origin=cross`, causing failures in `origin=same` and\n   intermediate checks in `origin=cross`.\n2. In the first `load` event, navigating immediately via `postMessage`\n   without waiting for a rendering frame could commit the cross-origin\n   navigation and reset the height to `150px` before `ResizeObserver`\n   captured the `200px` height.\n\nThis patch waits for a rendering frame via `waitForAtLeastOneFrame()`\nbefore navigating and before finishing the test, and checks the\ncollected `ResizeObserver` heights at the end while allowing the leading\n`150px` height to be omitted for both `same` and `cross` origins.\n\nFixed: 572584968\nChange-Id: I8b81e117d66e63ffde8caeb18ee37356720d50ad\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8587115\nCommit-Queue: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1720139}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5edee123b80966efff9d9628758d374714efdefd\nwpt-pr: 63749\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/responsive-iframe-navigation.html"], "git_node": "727b86dfebb57df3ff4722a5413d9702d12f3334", "git_parents": ["28e0b89532898da2a269528ad21f036b03505108"], "node": "5b839620830a9322b50ca1ad0f64f35e6a2bda6c", "parents": ["7b919ac003b8f117cc84624004df478fa587e5db"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082869 [wpt PR 63749] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63749\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/responsive-iframe-navigation.html.ini"], "git_node": "75f51051ab96f383096e44806b9708f5ec1aa7e3", "git_parents": ["727b86dfebb57df3ff4722a5413d9702d12f3334"], "node": "228be801917a48f83a9398d4cd27937ee65e949e", "parents": ["5b839620830a9322b50ca1ad0f64f35e6a2bda6c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085449 [wpt PR 64042] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328484, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nUpdate \u003coptgroup\u003e when its \u003clegend\u003e changes\n\nWhen the first element child of an \u003coptgroup\u003e is a \u003clegend\u003e, its text is the\nlabel of the \u003coptgroup\u003e. Changes to that text, or to which \u003clegend\u003e comes first,\ndid not update the \u003cselect\u003e: a native list box kept the width of the old label,\nand assistive technologies kept getting the old label.\n\nUsing the mechanism of 324413@main, HTMLLegendElement::descendantsChanged()\ncalls the new HTMLOptGroupElement::legendElementChanged(). The \u003coptgroup\u003e also\nremembers its \u003clegend\u003e, and its childrenChanged() calls legendElementChanged()\nwhen that changes, instead of invalidating its user agent shadow tree for every\nchange to its element children. legendElementChanged() does what a change to the\nlabel attribute does.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328484\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 382e224576e5a4b699eaf49559e3050b268a5b73\nwpt-pr: 64042\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-optgroup-legend-label-mutation-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-optgroup-legend-label-mutation.html"], "git_node": "d978c0165ec9a2a8b859bbcd84975eca38ac9c17", "git_parents": ["75f51051ab96f383096e44806b9708f5ec1aa7e3"], "node": "08926a3a019de7686c8aa606834df36e4315e429", "parents": ["228be801917a48f83a9398d4cd27937ee65e949e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085452 [wpt PR 64035] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328468, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nXMLHttpRequest JSON responses should always be decoded as UTF-8\n\nXMLHttpRequest parses a JSON response with parse JSON from bytes, which decodes the bytes as UTF-8\nwhatever charset the response or overrideMimeType() declares. XMLHttpRequest::createDecoder()\nchecked for a charset before looking at the response type, so a JSON response with, say,\ncharset=windows-1252 was decoded as windows-1252. Text responses are unchanged: they do use that\ncharset, with UTF-8 as the fallback.\n\nTo make UTF-8 decode easier to ask for, add TextResourceDecoder::createUTF8(), which creates a\nplain-text decoder that always uses UTF-8, and remove setAlwaysUseUTF8(). Its callers created a\ndecoder with a MIME type and UTF-8 as the fallback encoding, and then called setAlwaysUseUTF8().\nOnce the decoder always uses UTF-8, the MIME type and fallback make no difference: it only strips a\nUTF-8 byte order mark, and a CSS @charset rule can no longer change the encoding. Callers that\ndecode all their data at once now use TextResourceDecoder::textFromUTF8() instead. Apart from\nXMLHttpRequest, this does not change behavior. Also use PAL::UTF8Encoding() for the remaining UTF-8\nfallbacks in XMLHttpRequest::createDecoder().\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328468\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f7aa30662b46ef818105189a216a1fe51d77b772\nwpt-pr: 64035\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/xhr/json.any.js"], "git_node": "bfb0f451f493738f09e81402bc15c4341813a591", "git_parents": ["d978c0165ec9a2a8b859bbcd84975eca38ac9c17"], "node": "fdc2644862b3102c94049ed554f6bc70721a6db1", "parents": ["08926a3a019de7686c8aa606834df36e4315e429"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085457 [wpt PR 64046] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328490, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nQueue Document-Isolation-Policy CORP violation reports for network loads\n\nA cross-origin no-cors response from the network that Document-Isolation-Policy\nor Document-Isolation-Policy-Report-Only blocks now queues a \"dip\" report.\nReportingObserver can observe it, and it goes to the report-to endpoint if there\nis one. Its body is that of a Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy CORP violation,\nwithout the blocked URL's fragment, as Fetch's serialize a response URL for\nreporting requires.\n\nThe network process now gets a load's whole policy rather than just its value,\nsince it needs the report-only value and the endpoints.\n\nA response that Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy and Document-Isolation-Policy both\nblock gets a report for each, as the specification's \"blocked-by-coep-and-dip\"\nresult requires. Unlike the specification, an enforced policy also reports what\nit blocks without a report-only policy, see\nhttps://github.com/WICG/document-isolation-policy/issues/10\n\nNot covered yet, also for Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy:\n- The loads of a dedicated worker report to its owner document rather than to\n  the worker.\n- Memory cache hits, service worker responses, and the Cache API queue no\n  reports.\n\nreporting-subresource-corp.tentative.https.html now passes its document cases,\nbut like reporting-cache-storage-corp.tentative.https.html it still times out,\nso both stay skipped.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328490\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 681f4b8988a7c949b6129dec8d2483ddba6a61d0\nwpt-pr: 64046\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/reporting.tentative.https.html"], "git_node": "1a2e3af59d338a0bdc009f85700f33c3c8a3cf93", "git_parents": ["bfb0f451f493738f09e81402bc15c4341813a591"], "node": "c0c16a2750616aaaf20bf92a1cce55f87351a9fc", "parents": ["fdc2644862b3102c94049ed554f6bc70721a6db1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085457 [wpt PR 64046] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64046\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/document-isolation-policy/reporting.tentative.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "aef77dbd371c7bb458b914d84c2284c5d8f836cc", "git_parents": ["1a2e3af59d338a0bdc009f85700f33c3c8a3cf93"], "node": "d4d4032914cc74aff938396500f85fe00df7e0ce", "parents": ["c0c16a2750616aaaf20bf92a1cce55f87351a9fc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085458 [wpt PR 64050] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328502, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nUpdate \u003coption\u003e when the alt attribute of a descendant \u003cimg\u003e changes\n\nThe label of an \u003coption\u003e, which the native appearance of a \u003cselect\u003e renders,\nincludes the alt text of \u003cimg\u003e descendants. Changing that alt attribute is not a\nchange to anyone's children, so 324413@main does not cover it: a drop-down kept\nshowing the old text, and a list box kept the width of the old text.\n\nHTMLImageElement::attributeChanged() now calls notifyDescendantsChanged() on the\nparent of an \u003cimg\u003e inside a \u003cselect\u003e or \u003cdatalist\u003e when its alt attribute\nchanges. Elsewhere this costs a flag check.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328502\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1b9fa4515ab9d233e106c43f6d8f9edbaf93d2c8\nwpt-pr: 64050\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-option-element/dynamic-img-alt-change-rendering-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-option-element/dynamic-img-alt-change-rendering.html"], "git_node": "8e270b9d29a721bf214365a55a19c97e520f8756", "git_parents": ["aef77dbd371c7bb458b914d84c2284c5d8f836cc"], "node": "fa3038b28043729353072998ab7eabd86391c908", "parents": ["d4d4032914cc74aff938396500f85fe00df7e0ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085458 [wpt PR 64050] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64050\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-option-element/dynamic-img-alt-change-rendering.html.ini"], "git_node": "07552c06c05084efced4d0cdb149a1b13c4d713b", "git_parents": ["8e270b9d29a721bf214365a55a19c97e520f8756"], "node": "35e74551031a91528ebfe78454e6026531fbc36a", "parents": ["fa3038b28043729353072998ab7eabd86391c908"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Seokho Song \u003cseokho@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077376 [wpt PR 63173] - Remove .tentative. from custom highlight universal selector wpt cases, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRemove .tentative. from custom highlight universal selector wpt cases\n\nThe spec PR is merged.\n\nhttps://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/pull/14301\n\nBug: 408003366\nChange-Id: I634e2ea9b0c455116eaab6649dca3241aa704f41\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8492331\nCommit-Queue: Seokho Song \u003cseokho@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1709670}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4b1d365663d29fb656e5f96e1d114327da98406f\nwpt-pr: 63173\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-highlight-api/custom-highlight-universal-deep-chain-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-highlight-api/custom-highlight-universal-deep-chain-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-highlight-api/custom-highlight-universal-deep-chain-001.tentative-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-highlight-api/custom-highlight-universal-deep-chain-001.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-highlight-api/custom-highlight-universal-escaped-star.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-highlight-api/custom-highlight-universal-escaped-star.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-highlight-api/custom-highlight-universal-inheritance-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-highlight-api/custom-highlight-universal-inheritance-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-highlight-api/custom-highlight-universal-inheritance-001.tentative-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-highlight-api/custom-highlight-universal-inheritance-001.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-highlight-api/custom-highlight-universal-no-named-rule-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-highlight-api/custom-highlight-universal-no-named-rule-001.tentative.html", "t