ode": "b37525ba1f957642a158dcd7f2efa941b356a21d", "parents": ["ab827be20669addde5bee619347b97f3390142d1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090473 - Update android nightly application-services version bump to 96b6f69902d143d6257c176c6e49e8c21e6d314b r=release-managers,dmeehan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340582\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/ApplicationServices.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "87c503b6bc17ef36889cea09575ef22cc0902cfb", "git_parents": ["8493ed2cc78f06c234b5561278947dc1930d96c1"], "node": "aab1fe11caea4cd3f84d95bc313c2ec884a17784", "parents": ["b37525ba1f957642a158dcd7f2efa941b356a21d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Logan Rosen \u003cloganrosen@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090437 - Let the File menu's close label finish localizing in test_menu_close_tab_count. r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,dao\n\nThe task opened the File menu with two tabs selected and never waited for\nmenu_close's label to be translated. A late \"Close 2 Tabs\" translation could\nthen land after the next task's update and fail its label check.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340572\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/browser-menubar/browser_file_close_tabs.js"], "git_node": "8d7102c0c2af1c13c80f6fe3713c51e2aa44dbc4", "git_parents": ["87c503b6bc17ef36889cea09575ef22cc0902cfb"], "node": "92e128f147e778f693e6473d57985f182aa879ce", "parents": ["aab1fe11caea4cd3f84d95bc313c2ec884a17784"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ahanot \u003cahanot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090302 - Send the browser user agent from the New Tab ads-client. r=jonesetc,mconley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340520\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/AdsClient.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_AdsClient.js"], "git_node": "fc46c8f3833a60227d5879e7ecb64885d721d2cc", "git_parents": ["8d7102c0c2af1c13c80f6fe3713c51e2aa44dbc4"], "node": "aac99ee8b7b207bb098b9bbc28b1d823d61b1cd6", "parents": ["92e128f147e778f693e6473d57985f182aa879ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090007 - Remove some unneeded handling of attributes in SyncAttributesToWidget(). r=smaug\n\nMost of them are redundant because ChromeObserver::Init() does the right\nthing. Note that we rely on sizing the popup windows after initial\nlayout already so I think the dominantclientsize stuff can go away.\n\nWe do have extensive tests for popup sizing, but I can keep the\nspecial-case if this causes trouble I guess.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339662\n", "files": ["dom/xul/ChromeObserver.cpp", "dom/xul/ChromeObserver.h", "xpfe/appshell/AppWindow.cpp", "xpfe/appshell/AppWindow.h"], "git_node": "17e224079e49a2f64c3168fdec04c8901f8eff76", "git_parents": ["fc46c8f3833a60227d5879e7ecb64885d721d2cc"], "node": "7ab20d05ab2e8a9359e32c9f165beaec1244e840", "parents": ["aac99ee8b7b207bb098b9bbc28b1d823d61b1cd6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kartikaya Gupta \u003ckgupta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088617 - Don't require full Xcode install on macOS. r=sylvestre DONTBUILD\n\nInstalling Xcode from the App Store requires an Apple Account, which\ncan be annoying to set up. Instead, we can use the xcode CLI tools\nto build Firefox, and that doesn't require an Apple Account.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339252\n", "files": ["docs/setup/macos_build.md"], "git_node": "526b650ec91265583cf782f0d579ca4b7417abb1", "git_parents": ["17e224079e49a2f64c3168fdec04c8901f8eff76"], "node": "518b75acb1e5c99143dda9911976b1ec047965ae", "parents": ["7ab20d05ab2e8a9359e32c9f165beaec1244e840"], "ta