489fae4ce720d27560\nsq -\u003e 432eb137f67445abe3c7f3489fae4ce720d27560\nsr -\u003e 432eb137f67445abe3c7f3489fae4ce720d27560\nsv-SE -\u003e 432eb137f67445abe3c7f3489fae4ce720d27560\nta -\u003e 432eb137f67445abe3c7f3489fae4ce720d27560\nte -\u003e 432eb137f67445abe3c7f3489fae4ce720d27560\nth -\u003e 432eb137f67445abe3c7f3489fae4ce720d27560\ntl -\u003e 432eb137f67445abe3c7f3489fae4ce720d27560\ntr -\u003e 432eb137f67445abe3c7f3489fae4ce720d27560\ntrs -\u003e 432eb137f67445abe3c7f3489fae4ce720d27560\nuk -\u003e 432eb137f67445abe3c7f3489fae4ce720d27560\nur -\u003e 432eb137f67445abe3c7f3489fae4ce720d27560\nuz -\u003e 432eb137f67445abe3c7f3489fae4ce720d27560\nvi -\u003e 432eb137f67445abe3c7f3489fae4ce720d27560\nwo -\u003e 432eb137f67445abe3c7f3489fae4ce720d27560\nxh -\u003e 432eb137f67445abe3c7f3489fae4ce720d27560\nzam -\u003e 432eb137f67445abe3c7f3489fae4ce720d27560\nzh-CN -\u003e 432eb137f67445abe3c7f3489fae4ce720d27560\nzh-TW -\u003e 432eb137f67445abe3c7f3489fae4ce720d27560\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "bf37da71656139b8ecea5e50567e8d62727cd853", "git_parents": ["19032008fc22abbd066fe89bf21f1d1f92f3e1bf"], "node": "ee3aa5ec9cce7955b0e8a0bb5aa43eccd3716653", "parents": ["e05e00e25d7bc9c515b1285fc77b29f0b3a03fd9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090574. Remove the reference frame pushed for transformed view transition captures. r=emilio,layout-reviewers\n\nBug 1965924 pushed an identity reference frame for the capture of a transformed\nelement, because nsDisplayTransform didn't create a reference frame for an\nidentity transform and the capture ended up offset by the element's position.\nSince bug 2021812, a non-zero origin always gets its own translate-only\nreference frame, so the capture is in the right place without it.\n\nThis code was needed to make some wpt's pass when it was added. Those tests\nserve as a test for this and show that it is no longer needed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340593\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderCommandBuilder.h", "layout/painting/nsDisplayList.cpp"], "git_node": "5b6ff849024a5d9a3b35bd99171168fd64ea557b", "git_parents": ["bf37da71656139b8ecea5e50567e8d62727cd853"], "node": "8bf16106b25ad0a828e3368b0a7651170cc88245", "parents": ["ee3aa5ec9cce7955b0e8a0bb5aa43eccd3716653"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090635 - [riscv64] Test the tag of a Value in memory through its upper word. r=csmantle\n\nThe Address and BaseIndex forms of the tag tests loaded the whole Value,\nextracted the sign-extended tag with srai and compared it with a small\nconstant. The upper 32 bits of a Value are the tag shifted left by 15, so\nfor the types whose payload fits in 32 bits (int32, boolean, null,\nundefined, magic) and for the double and GC thing range tests, lw of the\nupper word compares directly with a constant that one lui loads. The\nequality tests of the pointer types keep the extraction because their\npayload reaches into the upper word.\n\nThe GC thing test of a pre-barrier on a slot was\n\n  ld    t4, 0x38(a0)\n  srai  t4, t4, 47\n  li    t5, -5\n  bltu  t4, t5, skip\n\nand becomes\n\n  lw    t4, 0x3c(a0)\n  lui   t5, 0xfffd8\n  bltu  t4, t5, skip\n\nThis is what x64 does with a cmp32 of the upper word, and what arm64 does\nsince bug 2086092.\n\nIn a JetStream 3 run on a SpacemiT K3 this removes one instruction from\n74,500 tests, 21,500 of them in Baseline code and 52,900 in Ion code:\n55,800 GC thing tests, mostly in pre-barriers, 14,900 int32 guards, 3,200\nboolean tests and 500 others. It also shortens the dependency chain before\nthe branch.\n\nFound with riscvlint.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340626\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/riscv64/MacroAssembler-riscv64-inl.h", "js/src/jit/riscv64/MacroAssembler-riscv64.h"], "git_node": "12bbc16ef7f4018ed4c8c97c4897968cd773611d", "git_parents": ["5b6ff849024a5d9a3b35bd99171168fd64ea557b"], "node": "a39468a73ef2b489da4c62c27da16e481c8d8efc", "parents": ["8bf16106b25ad0a828e3368b0a7651170cc88245"], "tags": []}, {"author": "virsworld \u003cvirpatel71@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069010 - Use bounded spans for preference callback lists. r=gstoll,firefox-style-system-reviewers,necko-reviewers,media-playback-reviewers,layout-reviewers,padenot,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333982\n", "files": ["caps/nsScriptSecurityManager.cpp", "docshell/shistory/nsSHistory.cpp", "dom/base/nsFocusManager.cpp", "dom/base/nsNameSpaceManager.cpp", "dom/media/CubebUtils.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/PDMFactorySupport.cpp", "dom/security/nsContentSecurityUtils.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxPlatform.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxPlatformFontList.cpp", "js/xpconnect/src/XPCJSContext.cpp", "layout/base/nsPresContext.cpp", "layout/style/nsComputedDOMStyle.cpp", "modules/libpref/Preferences.cpp", "modules/libpref/Preferences.h", "modules/libpref/test/gtest/Basics.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsIOService.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsSocketTransportService2.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpHandler.cpp", "toolkit/components/resistfingerprinting/nsRFPService.cpp"], "git_node": "b42f9826fdd6959ec57b257eb766ca6080f1e4a6", "git_parents": ["12bbc16ef7f4018ed4c8c97c4897968cd773611d"], "node": "39218c8ddd5a1849437ca4459271198c358d938d", "parents": ["a39468a73ef2b489da4c62c27da16e481c8d8efc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2069010 - Use bounded spans for preference callback lists. r=gstoll,firefox-style-system-reviewers,necko-reviewers,media-playback-reviewers,layout-reviewers,padenot,dshin\" for causibg gtest process-crashes.\n\nThis reverts commit b42f9826fdd6959ec57b257eb766ca6080f1e4a6.\n", "files": ["caps/nsScriptSecurityManager.cpp", "docshell/shistory/nsSHistory.cpp", "dom/base/nsFocusManager.cpp", "dom/base/nsNameSpaceManager.cpp", "dom/media/CubebUtils.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/PDMFactorySupport.cpp", "dom/security/nsContentSecurityUtils.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxPlatform.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxPlatformFontList.cpp", "js/xpconnect/src/XPCJSContext.cpp", "layout/base/nsPresContext.cpp", "layout/style/nsComputedDOMStyle.cpp", "modules/libpref/Preferences.cpp", "modules/libpref/Preferences.h", "modules/libpref/test/gtest/Basics.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsIOService.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsSocketTransportService2.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpHandler.cpp", "toolkit/components/resistfingerprinting/nsRFPService.cpp"], "git_node": "a82bcf39e8d23e7b06e021044db52f74210862ce", "git_parents": ["b42f9826fdd6959ec57b257eb766ca6080f1e4a6"], "node": "05b293386ebf0feea3f0e4220ebc2dd0b7904abc", "parents": ["39218c8ddd5a1849437ca4459271198c358d938d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794173918, "git_changesets": ["55e94d6647b0fc06312aa1e9800ba54ba862e0f3", "d9d2b674be104583fd79424ee0f67339256335c8", "ddbaa616c2fcbe34a9ee7b01965e39144f636b71", "9ac81ad071b436fac05d3481a829eaff7a4edf21", "38bc925fac77dc47810c96bd7a50f5bf98b6025c", "bf97ea568f0202681c02ff25918e3ef2dd7d4175", "ec7a4079b713d9f01bf93a208693c1e33afcc9ad", "a899ce0d009790d2b022938ad7f1b617232df18f", "6b7609477280e6951695e590142edd5f83a54cf5", "19032008fc22abbd066fe89bf21f1d1f92f3e1bf", "bf37da71656139b8ecea5e50567e8d62727cd853", "5b6ff849024a5d9a3b35bd99171168fd64ea557b", "12bbc16ef7f4018ed4c8c97c4897968cd773611d", "b42f9826fdd6959ec57b257eb766ca6080f1e4a6", "a82bcf39e8d23e7b06e021044db52f74210862ce"], "user": "agoloman@mozilla.com"}, "45738": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jan-Niklas Jaeschke \u003cjjaschke@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2028219 - Part 1: Make CalcUnpaginatedBSize start at the cell's own row. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nCalcUnpaginatedBSize walked from the row group's first row on every paginated\ncell reflow, which is quadratic in the number of rows. It also compared the\ncell's table-wide row index with a counter starting at 0 for the row group, so\npercentage block-sizes in cells of any row group after the first resolved\nagainst the wrong rows.\n\nCo-authored-by: Mayank Bansal \u003cmayankleoboy1@gmail.com\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336990\n", "files": ["layout/tables/nsTableCellFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-tables/table-cell-percent-height-row-groups-print-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-tables/table-cell-percent-height-row-groups-print.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-tables/table-cell-percent-height-rowspan-fragmented-print-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-tables/table-cell-percent-height-rowspan-fragmented-print.html"], "git_node": "9044ced4570fc376ac31682325f9cd62e682cdf8", "git_parents": ["a82bcf39e8d23e7b06e021044db52f74210862ce"], "node": "2b547b0b98f8efaec0a796b9242291212993a591", "parents": ["05b293386ebf0feea3f0e4220ebc2dd0b7904abc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Niklas Jaeschke \u003cjjaschke@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2028219 - Part 2: Stop letting a forced break in a table row group disable its break-inside: avoid. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nA forced break only overrides break-inside: avoid at its own break point\n(https://drafts.csswg.org/css-break-3/#forced-breaks). SplitRowGroup only\nchecks break-inside: avoid at the first row that doesn't fit, and a forced\nbreak before that row would already have ended the page.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340376\n", "files": ["layout/tables/nsTableRowGroupFrame.cpp", "layout/tables/nsTableRowGroupFrame.h", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/table/table-row-break-inside-avoid-later-forced-break-print-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/table/table-row-break-inside-avoid-later-forced-break-print.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/table/table-row-group-break-inside-avoid-forced-break-moved-by-rowspan-print-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/table/table-row-group-break-inside-avoid-forced-break-moved-by-rowspan-print.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/table/table-row-group-break-inside-avoid-later-forced-break-print-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/table/table-row-group-break-inside-avoid-later-forced-break-print.html"], "git_node": "e77cbd7a49c97a0d9785e716d97db58fa2ed2d76", "git_parents": ["9044ced4570fc376ac31682325f9cd62e682cdf8"], "node": "d97b1f2c955ee6710615c22d13d47dab439d43e4", "parents": ["2b547b0b98f8efaec0a796b9242291212993a591"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090654 - [riscv64] Canonicalize NaNs with fmin. r=csmantle\n\nThe shared canonicalizeDoubleNaN and canonicalizeFloatNaN compare the\nregister with itself, branch over a constant load when it is not NaN and\nload JS::GenericNaN() otherwise. On RISC-V, fmin returns the canonical NaN\nwhen both operands are NaN, which is JS::GenericNaN(), and otherwise the\nsmaller operand, so fmin with the register as all three operands does the\nsame in one instruction and no branch. riscv64 rounding already uses fmin\nthis way for NaNs. Canonicalizing a double loaded from a typed array goes\nfrom\n\n  feq.d  t4, ft10, ft10\n  bnez   t4, done\n  fli.d  ft10, nan\ndone:\n\nto\n\n  fmin.d ft10, ft10, ft10\n\nThe shared versions stay for the other architectures; the style check does\nnot allow a shared definition next to a riscv64 one, so riscv64 defines\nthese in MacroAssemblerRiscv64Compat, as arm64 does for the stack pointer\nfunctions.\n\nIn a JetStream 3 run on a SpacemiT K3 this shortens 1,460 canonicalizations\n(796 of doubles and 666 of floats) by two instructions and a branch each,\n1,200 of them in Ion code.\n\nFound with riscvlint.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340637\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/MacroAssembler-inl.h", "js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.h", "js/src/jit/riscv64/MacroAssembler-riscv64.h"], "git_node": "904b14c262490bdb708320fb2d5758d0cb30fc15", "git_parents": ["e77cbd7a49c97a0d9785e716d97db58fa2ed2d76"], "node": "afa2526c46115b92b0c5815dd7c6ab3bd75866bc", "parents": ["d97b1f2c955ee6710615c22d13d47dab439d43e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2044348 - Enable headingoffset by default r=dom-core-reviewers,jjaschke\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340303\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/idlharness.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "5032e8c5b5035e2ee00f8fc8bd8aa28a85a6b017", "git_parents": ["904b14c262490bdb708320fb2d5758d0cb30fc15"], "node": "6d4b8f9df85ba85f222ca7f94847fe2006e8b362", "parents": ["afa2526c46115b92b0c5815dd7c6ab3bd75866bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2044348 - Enable headingoffset by default r=dom-core-reviewers,jjaschke\" for causing failures @sINode.cpp.\n\nThis reverts commit 5032e8c5b5035e2ee00f8fc8bd8aa28a85a6b017.\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/idlharness.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "9c05aea2c855cebcdf1a18d8504c20588109b5e6", "git_parents": ["5032e8c5b5035e2ee00f8fc8bd8aa28a85a6b017"], "node": "c5b9bb422198af606e9b0c60547dab4624524970", "parents": ["6d4b8f9df85ba85f222ca7f94847fe2006e8b362"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Bumping Firefox l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD CLOSED TREE\n\nach -\u003e e0bf1538744648ca6f6b3e087bd450bfbb39d61f\naf -\u003e e0bf1538744648ca6f6b3e087bd450bfb