e02c678a6058304dc66d2044a5d", "parents": ["7f99e52ce57a44c8cd06e4802a328902adc195a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072073 - Backport arm64e.x1 support to clang 22. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nThe macOS 27 SDK's linker stubs declare an arm64e.x1 target that ld64.lld rejects as an unknown architecture,\nfailing every link against the SDK. clang 23 and trunk already have the upstream fix.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332000\n", "files": ["build/build-clang/clang-22.json", "build/build-clang/llvmorg-24-init-8352-gb8007a8e4020.patch"], "git_node": "e0cabf73464cc7309ce4aa6c8722cab01f9a5535", "git_parents": ["e6649794ee8255ef01ba1a370ff7bd4075cd21e6"], "node": "de6392e544f04681f58dc0128fba0b53df768717", "parents": ["aaa6fdb04d786e02c678a6058304dc66d2044a5d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072073 - Backport the stack_protector_ignore attribute to clang 22. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille,ahochheiden\n\nThe macOS 27 SDK applies __attribute__((stack_protector_ignore)) unconditionally in its os_log macros, which\nclang 22 rejects with -Wunknown-attributes. clang 23 and trunk already have it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332001\n", "files": ["build/build-clang/clang-22.json", "build/build-clang/llvmorg-23-init-1731-ga63696edca8b.patch"], "git_node": "ee0de25f8bf772e50240c449f1aa70628cf299ca", "git_parents": ["e0cabf73464cc7309ce4aa6c8722cab01f9a5535"], "node": "8a1c8d80ea1a5e3a02c43a96ff6f8ea715e4c768", "parents": ["de6392e544f04681f58dc0128fba0b53df768717"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072073 - Teach cctools-port's libtapi about arm64e.x1. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nThe macOS 27 SDK's .tbd stubs list arm64e.x1 targets, which libtapi rejects as an unknown architecture, so\nld64 cannot link against the SDK. PGO/LTO macOS builds still link with ld64. This ports the TextAPI part of\nLLVM b8007a8e4020: the architecture table gets a separate name column so the slice can be named arm64e.x1.\nlibtapi's fallback for arm64 links keeps picking the arm64e slice.\n\nUpstream PR: https://github.com/tpoechtrager/apple-libtapi/pull/53\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332002\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/misc.yml", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-cctools-port.sh", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/libtapi-arm64e-x1.patch"], "git_node": "254c15b5ac00551061d2aa8c7a03ac4e17a9bf80", "git_parents": ["ee0de25f8bf772e50240c449f1aa70628cf299ca"], "node": "a1bd3b36031e23b0fa44adeb31755a2b22b271ad", "parents": ["8a1c8d80ea1a5e3a02c43a96ff6f8ea715e4c768"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072073 - Update macOS SDK to 27.2. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,mac-reviewers,sergesanspaille,spohl,ahochheiden\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332003\n", "files": ["build/docs/toolchains.md", "build/macosx/catalog.py", "build/moz.configure/toolchain.configure", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/configure/macos_fake_sdk/SDKSettings.plist", "taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/custom-car.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/macos-sdk.yml"], "git_node": "7473b2886dc9974eea23b7273397a40c33e5098b", "git_parents": ["254c15b5ac00551061d2aa8c7a03ac4e17a9bf80"], "node": "eb59c86ee05ff12328c20985a55697e40ebb5299", "parents": ["a1bd3b36031e23b0fa44adeb31755a2b22b271ad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072073 - Keep cpython from using pipe2 and dup3 on macOS. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille,glandium\n\nThe macOS 27 SDK declares pipe2 and dup3, so configure picks them up, but the libSystem of older macOS\nreleases does not export them; with pipe2 the freshly built python dies in dyld during make libinstall.\n\nThis backports upstream's configure fix from 3.13 and 3.14 (gh-153711) to the 3.10 and 3.11 sources we build.\nEach macOS python task passes its version's patch to build-cpython.sh; 3.13 and later already have the fix.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332004\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/python.yml", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-cpython.sh", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/cpython-3.10-macos-dup3-pipe2.patch", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/cpython-3.11-macos-dup3-pipe2.patch"], "git_node": "20b9636b76c24cd03e258e1ca6085a9643aa6dee", "git_parents": ["7473b2886dc9974eea23b7273397a40c33e5098b"], "node": "285c2f681d2f60dd24f26abac7583210b628ccfd", "parents": ["eb59c86ee05ff12328c20985a55697e40ebb5299"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072073 - Disable -Wcpp for macOS x86_64 builds. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille,ahochheiden\n\nlibc++ in the macOS 27 SDK emits a #warning that deployment targets below 11.0 are no longer supported. We\nstill target 10.15 on Intel, and #warning is not suppressed in system headers, so this is the only way to keep\n-Werror builds and the clang-plugin -verify tests compiling. -Wcpp is clang's alias for -W#warnings; the # in\nthe canonical spelling gets shell-quoted on its way through cargo build scripts and clang then treats it as a\nfile name. bindgen does not see the warning flags, so BINDGEN_SYSTEM_FLAGS carries it too. The toolchain\nbuilds get the same flag through macos-setup.sh, build-clang.py and build-llvm-common.sh so their logs stay\nreadable.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332005\n", "files": ["build/build-clang/build-clang.py", "build/moz.configure/bindgen.configure", "build/moz.configure/warnings.configure", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-llvm-common.sh", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/macos-setup.sh"], "git_node": "ff4d11ecdaf3161379f40b32df2177c4bd09f283", "git_parents": ["20b9636b76c24cd03e258e1ca6085a9643aa6dee"], "node": "62abfd7bd87311da7ca203ea0206c7dbc08db930", "parents": ["285c2f681d2f60dd24f26abac7583210b628ccfd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089872 - Use FxHashMap for the webrender_api display list interners and spatial offsets. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nThe display list builder interners and spatial offset map used std's\ndefault SipHash hasher; the webrender crate uses FxHash everywhere.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340215\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "gfx/wr/Cargo.lock", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/Cargo.toml", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_list.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/interning.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": "fcd6cce8e3222e0c4d5fdabfd1c00106845ada3f", "git_parents": ["ff4d11ecdaf3161379f40b32df2177c4bd09f283"], "node": "a7cb87a80c1a5de748dd5900c040dc59292bc14a", "parents": ["62abfd7bd87311da7ca203ea0206c7dbc08db930"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-central repo-update remote-settings tld-suffixes ct-logs r=release-managers,RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340763\n", "files": ["netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/ct/CTKnownLogs.h", "security/manager/tools/log_list.json", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters/addons-mlbf.bin", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters/addons-mlbf.bin.meta.json", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters/softblocks-addons-mlbf.bin", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters/softblocks-addons-mlbf.bin.meta.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/ai-window-prompts.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": "85b1196a93169e3d33b797b655d33c0e8778d4ac", "git_parents": ["fcd6cce8e3222e0c4d5fdabfd1c00106845ada3f"], "node": "46b492f4be2df8aa9c1c78a9522925985cb96075", "parents": ["a7cb87a80c1a5de748dd5900c040dc59292bc14a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090794 - Skip the system prompt when checking browser_aitab.js's stored exchange for URL tokens. a=test-only\n\nThe aitab system-instructions prompt now quotes the URL token format in its own text. AITab leaves system\nmessages untokenized, so only the other messages are expected to be free of tokens.\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_aitab.js"], "git_node": "57ddffbde75b2d111c485543e9a4043405dfcc62", "git_parents": ["85b1196a93169e3d33b797b655d33c0e8778d4ac"], "node": "72e2fd1d1ea6638d795dc857bc1b36d65954fe5f", "parents": ["46b492f4be2df8aa9c1c78a9522925985cb96075"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2065376 - Hand a double tap to the root content APZC enclosing it. r=botond\n\nA top level content document loaded in the parent process, such as about:license,\nshares browser.xhtml's layers id, so its root content APZC is not the root APZC\nof that layers id. Double tapping the document reached OnDoubleTap on an APZC\nwhich is root content but not the layers id root, tripping the\nIsRootForLayersId() assertion, and double tapping one of its subframes was\nredirected to browser.xhtml's root APZC instead of to the document.\n\nMove the choice of the APZC which handles a double tap into\nAPZCTreeManager::FindDoubleTapHandlerFor(). It walks up handoff parents within\nthe hit APZC's layers id, following fixed content to the scroll container it is\nfixed to, and picks the first root content APZC, so that a double tap on\nbrowser.xhtml doesn't zoom such a document. Failing that, the topmost APZC of\nthe layers id handles it only if it has an enclosing document, as an OOPIF's\ndoes. The IsRootForLayersId() assertion now lives in the branch of OnDoubleTap\nwhere GetOopifToRootContentTransform() requires it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321744\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/src/APZCTreeManager.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/APZCTreeManager.h", "gfx/layers/apz/src/AsyncPanZoomController.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/TestTreeManager.cpp"], "git_node": "da3736dac7cd20b8f47751e3854668e83f88b8c1", "git_parents": ["57ddffbde75b2d111c485543e9a4043405dfcc62"], "node": "32905168e7c9831bc0bea3b837564c20de5642b7", "parents": ["72e2fd1d1ea6638d795dc857bc1b36d65954fe5f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090782 - Reshuffle bits so FULLSCREEN_KEYBOARD_LOCK doesn't conflict with HEADING_LEVEL_BITS r=dom-core-reviewers,avandolder\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340749\n", "files": ["dom/base/rust/lib.rs"], "git_node": "a958c8b9eedda0e88a925d6f0a488c8f7df76c8e", "git_parents": ["da3736dac7cd20b8f47751e3854668e83f88b8c1"], "node": "559e861834ddcabe5221da635283af9a9de02371", "parents": ["32905168e7c9831bc0bea3b837564c20de5642b7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Import translations from https://github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n CLOSED TREE\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-ca/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-fy-rNL/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-ca/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/addons/src/main/res/values-brh/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/addons/src/main/res/values-fy-rNL/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/addons/src/main/res/values-nl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/downloads/src/main/res/values-fy-rNL/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/res/values-ca/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-ca/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-brh/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ca/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-el/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-fy-rNL/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-hu/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ka/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-nn-rNO/strings.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/values-fy-rNL/strings.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/values-zh-rTW/strings.xml"], "git_node": "c4dbd69dd656cd1ccc828983ed6dbf0f0b7c5ad8", "git_parents": ["a958c8b9eedda0e88a925d6f0a488c8f7df76c8e"], "node": "a18a2e71431c053365732dc027c44388677a692f", "parents": ["559e861834ddcabe5221da635283af9a9de02371"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088002 - Re-type storage of Imm64 to int64_t. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338670\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/riscv64/MacroAssembler-riscv64.cpp", "js/src/jit/shared/Assembler-shared.h", "js/src/jit/x64/MacroAssembler-x64-inl.h", "js/src/jit/x64/MacroAssembler-x64.h"], "git_node": "dbbf09890ff34a79d7456f758376067fe40a5a17", "git_parents": ["c4dbd69dd656cd1ccc828983ed6dbf0f0b7c5ad8"], "node": "f2835008305a479c7fb0ea2adc608d7366ed7c1f", "parents": ["a18a2e71431c053365732dc027c44388677a692f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073734 - part 1: Add log of `WidgetKeyboardEvent::GetShortcutKeyCandidates` result r=smaug\n\nThis helps to debug the further patches.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339871\n", "files": ["widget/TextEvents.h", "widget/WidgetEventImpl.cpp"], "git_node": "22bdf20d0b43bb11817d9e249ebcd0819d6f04c5", "git_parents": ["dbbf09890ff34a79d7456f758376067fe40a5a17"], "node": "f36c9c09b2f7ac5e526ae65575303902f930d0ac", "parents": ["f2835008305a479c7fb0ea2adc608d7366ed7c1f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073734 - part 2: Make `WidgetKeyboardEvent::GetShortcutKeyCandidates` never contain same candidate r=smaug\n\nIt may return same candidate twice or more. It's currently no problem\nwithout wasting to handle redundant candidates. However, when we need\nto show the result to users, it shouldn't return the same candidates.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339872\n", "files": ["widget/WidgetEventImpl.cpp"], "git_node": "8b6303f16d8486feb8ae077277d835e2bfa0c2ed", "git_parents": ["22bdf20d0b43bb11817d9e249ebcd0819d6f04c5"], "node": "740db9c4e1e43a323c5c843d12411582d750a91c", "parents": ["f36c9c09b2f7ac5e526ae65575303902f930d0ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073734 - part 3: Make `WidgetKeyboardEvent::GetShortcutKeyCandidates` ignore ASCII control characters and surrogate pairs r=smaug\n\nUI shouldn't show ASCII control characters and `KeyEventHandler` does\nnot support shortcut keys whose \"character\" is a surrogate pair.\nTherefore, `WidgetKeyboardEvent::GetShortcutKeyCandidates` shouldn't\nreturn them as candidates.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339873\n", "files": ["dom/events/KeyEventHandler.cpp", "widget/WidgetEventImpl.cpp"], "git_node": "bbc01b461aea8a199210fb59ab4b7be1d2b1a987", "git_parents": ["8b6303f16d8486feb8ae077277d835e2bfa0c2ed"], "node": "6c0b8dd00ce1ae4717368e363af7025f3e93bdf7", "parents": ["740db9c4e1e43a323c5c843d12411582d750a91c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073734 - part 4-1: Move the numeric key handling in `WidgetKeyboardEvent::GetShortcutKeyCandidates` below r=smaug\n\nLet's combine `!IsShift()` block and its `else` block.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339874\n", "files": ["widget/WidgetEventImpl.cpp"], "git_node": "98f7bf5b79e08bc858be84daa454ad27ec5db2c9", "git_parents": ["bbc01b461aea8a199210fb59ab4b7be1d2b1a987"], "node": "196f12f8e572e10b8dfc56e9b038fdfdc72cefec", "parents": ["6c0b8dd00ce1ae4717368e363af7025f3e93bdf7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073734 - part 4-2: Merge `if (!IsShift())` block and its `else` block r=smaug\n\nWe can combine them, although we need to the cached `isShift` twice\nper iteration. It shouldn't be a problem because the loop count is at\nmost 3.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339875\n", "files": ["widget/WidgetEventImpl.cpp"], "git_node": "e574fac8cf872122803b3f06a4e6a27cb4e1ee5e", "git_parents": ["98f7bf5b79e08bc858be84daa454ad27ec5db2c9"], "node": "77c1d5c2e406ea08830829b02205c89ac36b2d39", "parents": ["196f12f8e572e10b8dfc56e9b038fdfdc72cefec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073734 - part 5: Add a new `KeyboardEvent` API to suggest registerable shortcut keys which can run with the event r=spohl,webidl,smaug\n\n`about:keyboard` should show a list to shortcut key combinations\nwhich can be executed by the key press because the users may install\nsome keyboard layouts which may introduce ASCII punctuations with\ndifferent `Shift` state and Unicode characters may be available only\nsome of the installed keyboard layouts. Therefore, the best shortcut\nkey of the key combination may be different between users. For avoiding\nthis issue, the API suggests the shortcut key list from preferred ones.\n\nIf the character is an ASCII punctuation and it's introduced with\n`Shift` state, shortcut key without `Shift` is preferred because\nother keyboard layout may not require the `Shift` state for the\ncharacter but we don't allow `Shift` + unshifted character combination\n(bug 433907).\n\nIf the character is a Unicode character, it may not be available with\nthe other keyboard layouts. Therefore, ASCII characters are preferred.\n\nOn the other hand, the character may introduce only a Unicode character.\nTo support such key, we should allow it to return a Unicode character\ntoo.\n\nThe key difference of new API and\n`WidgetKeyboardEvent::GetShortcutKeyCandidates()` is, the priority\nof the shortcut keys in the list. `GetShortcutKeyCandidates() honors\nthe user's intention. However, the new API honors how much keyboard\nlayout may be able to generate the combination. Therefore, the new\nAPI would love ASCII characters much.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330950\n", "files": ["dom/events/KeyboardEvent.cpp", "dom/events/KeyboardEvent.h", "dom/webidl/KeyboardEvent.webidl", "testing/mochitest/tests/SimpleTest/EventUtils.js", "widget/TextEvents.h", "widget/WidgetEventImpl.cpp", "widget/tests/test_keycodes.xhtml"], "git_node": "a117228d3d188ea86211f901b5ca1cfa5970b294", "git_parents": ["e574fac8cf872122803b3f06a4e6a27cb4e1ee5e"], "node": "1a58173c746bf932abc3da1a20202b78172f68ae", "parents": ["77c1d5c2e406ea08830829b02205c89ac36b2d39"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073734: Test that every registerable shortcut key runs a \u003ckey\u003e element for the same key press. r=masayuki\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331478\n", "files": ["widget/tests/test_keycodes.xhtml"], "git_node": "78eb12e74a3525841a50e0634fac8de752920532", "git_parents": ["a117228d3d188ea86211f901b5ca1cfa5970b294"], "node": "e3b58e57fcbb6eab3eb4531dc3b9192219aa8f57", "parents": ["1a58173c746bf932abc3da1a20202b78172f68ae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1994229 - Prefer external composite promotion for DRM video r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\n- Propagate DRM source information from texture hosts to WebRender and the renderer.\n- Prioritize external composition for DRM video and bypass the YUV promotion stability delay.\n- Apply existing HDR promotion exceptions to DRM sources.\n- Exclude DRM YUV underlays from cancellation for backdrop filters or mix-blend-mode.\n- Exempt DRM surfaces from the SDR YUV external-composite limit without consuming the slot reserved for non-DRM video.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339415\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/d3d11/TextureD3D11.cpp", "gfx/layers/opengl/MacIOSurfaceTextureHostOGL.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/WebRenderTypes.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/src/bindings.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/composite.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/composite.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/image.rs"], "git_node": "650f88ec2dbee9741aec7c89462ab41e7f0df4f2", "git_parents": ["78eb12e74a3525841a50e0634fac8de752920532"], "node": "a900bed77f238e38dcb75819e2bc94d93306439e", "parents": ["e3b58e57fcbb6eab3eb4531dc3b9192219aa8f57"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Hammond \u003cmhammond@skippinet.com.au\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087935 - Avoid lone surrogate pairs from web-originating content crashing the browser when used with logins. r=joschmidt,dimi,android-reviewers,jonalmeida,android-build-system-reviewers,RyanVM\n\nI've not seen any actual crash reports about this, although did see many for places\nand tabs (bug 2087927). However, because things like the username and password come\ndirectly from web form fields, there is a chance that lone surrogate pairs will be involved.\nCurrently, if that happens the browser will crash. Instead of fixing up the string and adding\n login field (which seems wrong - the username or password would not match in practice) we\n just log and ignore the exception.\n\nThis only fixes Android. Desktop side-steps this because it uses a TextEncoder which always fixes these string.\nNo idea about iOS.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338638\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/service/sync-logins/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/sync-logins/src/main/java/mozilla/components/service/sync/logins/SyncableLoginsStorage.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/sync-logins/src/test/java/mozilla/components/service/sync/logins/GeckoLoginStorageDelegateTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/sync-logins/src/test/java/mozilla/components/service/sync/logins/SyncableLoginsStorageTest.kt"], "git_node": "867575b3b45de380c28445843af076b468f69b08", "git_parents": ["650f88ec2dbee9741aec7c89462ab41e7f0df4f2"], "node": "1a0b411d248cfd22c15dad975113cb0bcd134636", "parents": ["a900bed77f238e38dcb75819e2bc94d93306439e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Bone \u003cpbone@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083531 - Add some assertions to dirty page scanning r=glandium\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335455\n", "files": ["memory/build/mozjemalloc.cpp"], "git_node": "4baab6a650a9d34c585dbf0117e67f2344c21fa0", "git_parents": ["867575b3b45de380c28445843af076b468f69b08"], "node": "0b3dde6291a09c6ac8430250001d4988c8727e52", "parents": ["1a0b411d248cfd22c15dad975113cb0bcd134636"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087343. Disable image/test/mochitest/test_cache_eviction.html on android ccov builds again. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340230\n", "files": ["image/test/mochitest/mochitest.toml"], "git_node": "2d8addd1d26a160b4c9d23104ec710d018d8f059", "git_parents": ["4baab6a650a9d34c585dbf0117e67f2344c21fa0"], "node": "510a779135356a7af41b7c6b59a079a630dce15d", "parents": ["0b3dde6291a09c6ac8430250001d4988c8727e52"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Resonance \u003cres0nancee@pm.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083466 - Request a SystemClockDriver graph for remote audio tracks in RTCRtpReceiver. r=karlt,webrtc-reviewers,bwc\n\nRTCRtpReceiver requested an AUDIO_THREAD_DRIVER graph for audio\nreceivers. When the receiver was the first user of the window's graph,\nMediaTrackGraphImpl::Init() therefore created an AudioCallbackDriver and\nRunInStableState() started it, opening an output stream as soon as the\ntransceiver was created, although the remote track is not rendered until\nthe page attaches it to a sink, which it may never do.\n\nRequest a SYSTEM_THREAD_DRIVER graph for audio receivers as for video\nreceivers, and leave it to CheckDriver() to create an AudioCallbackDriver\nwhen one is needed. The requested driver only matters when the receiver\ncreates the graph.\n\nOn its own this changes little: CheckDriver() still wants an\nAudioCallbackDriver whenever an audio track is present, and switches to\none in the first graph iteration, with two output channels until an\noutput is added rather than CubebUtils::MaxNumberOfChannels().\nhttps://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334988 will make\nCheckDriver() require an AudioCallbackDriver only when an audio\noutput is present; with an AUDIO_THREAD_DRIVER request,\nthe graph would then start an output stream\nat creation only for CheckDriver() to stop it again.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338008\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCRtpReceiver.cpp"], "git_node": "58ec5dbda8497a62b4312e8ca39674a77fcc958e", "git_parents": ["2d8addd1d26a160b4c9d23104ec710d018d8f059"], "node": "6daccf7496356557033da340583bc6475101025f", "parents": ["510a779135356a7af41b7c6b59a079a630dce15d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090652 - [riscv64] Load a constant that is a rotated LUI value with lui and rori. r=csmantle\n\nWith Zbb, the port of LLVM's RISCVMatInt in AssemblerMatInt.cpp builds a\nconstant with addi and rori when it is a rotated negative 12-bit\nimmediate. A constant that is a rotated 32-bit value with its low 12\nbits clear, which LUI loads, can be built the same way with lui and\nrori, and LLVM doesn't try that. Boxed constant Values are such\nconstants: true, 0xfffc000000000001, goes from\n\n  li    t4, -1\n  slli  t4, t4, 50\n  addi  t4, t4, 1\n\nto\n\n  lui   t4, 0x7fff\n  rori  t4, t4, 26\n\nIn a JetStream 3 run on a SpacemiT K3 this shortens 105,500 constants by\nan instruction each, 91,200 of them in Baseline code and 14,200 in Ion\ncode: mostly true, the int32s 1, 2 and 3, and magic Values. riscvlint\nfinds none left that lui and rori would build in fewer instructions.\n\nThe new test checks every rotation of a few such values, and their\nneighbours, as Wasm i64 constants.\n\nhttps://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/240099 adds the same to LLVM,\nand ExtractLuiRotateInfo finds the rotation the way it does there,\nwithout a loop.\n\nFound with riscvlint.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340635\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/const-i64-rotated.js", "js/src/jit/riscv64/AssemblerMatInt.cpp"], "git_node": "84a802db1a85534bbf5fe57401649869cf9d8ce7", "git_parents": ["58ec5dbda8497a62b4312e8ca39674a77fcc958e"], "node": "f829a53609aa6a2e347582ffc23457b2c655b496", "parents": ["6daccf7496356557033da340583bc6475101025f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090641 - [riscv64] Get the chunk of a GC thing Value with Zbb andn. r=csmantle\n\ngetGCThingValueChunk loaded ValueGCThingPayloadChunkMask, 0x7ffffff00000,\nin three instructions and then anded it in. The complement of the mask is\na run of ones from bit 47 around to bit 19, which rotated right by 20 is\n0xfffffffff8000000, a value lui loads. So with Zbb, movePtr builds the\ncomplement in two instructions, lui and rori since bug 2090652, and andn\nclears its bits. The nursery check of a post-barrier goes from\n\n  lui   t4, 0x8000\n  addiw t4, t4, -1\n  slli  t4, t4, 20\n  and   t4, t4, a2\n  ld    t4, 0(t4)\n\nto\n\n  lui   t4, 0xf8000\n  rori  t4, t4, 44\n  andn  t4, a2, t4\n  ld    t4, 0(t4)\n\nAs before, only the last instruction depends on the Value. Three shifts\nwould also take three instructions, but would add three cycles instead of\none to the check. On a SpacemiT K3 X100 core, a dependent mask and chunk\nload takes 4 cycles before and after this change (6 with shifts), and\nindependent ones take 1.12 cycles each instead of 1.44. Hardware without\nZbb keeps the old sequence.\n\nIn a JetStream 3 run on a SpacemiT K3 this removes one instruction from\neach of 66,500 nursery checks in post-barriers, 42,500 of them in Baseline\ncode and 24,000 in Ion code.\n\nFound with riscvlint.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340632\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/riscv64/MacroAssembler-riscv64.h"], "git_node": "3877d9553a3165f7b266d27a42f4b2afa18bb1c9", "git_parents": ["84a802db1a85534bbf5fe57401649869cf9d8ce7"], "node": "89de1a923deb6ac086e2051452a4eb329101c2e2", "parents": ["f829a53609aa6a2e347582ffc23457b2c655b496"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1975505 - Part 3 - Move the `tools/ts` node packages to the top level `package.json` r=Standard8\n\nTwo package directories with their own `typescript` would drift apart. The\n`postinstall` that builds `@typescript/dom-lib-generator` moves with them,\nand `npm run test:ts` runs the `tools/ts` jest tests. Nothing depended on\n`globals`, so its override is dropped. `webidl2` is under the W3C license\nand gets a `node-licenses` exception.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334780\n", "files": [".gitignore", ".hgignore", "package-lock.json", "package.json", "tools/lint/node-licenses.yml", "tools/ts/mach_commands.py", "tools/ts/package-lock.json", "tools/ts/package.json"], "git_node": "0db31eb8dd73a80fdbd8adf17dcc2301893033e1", "git_parents": ["3877d9553a3165f7b266d27a42f4b2afa18bb1c9"], "node": "3bef84a7f5afc524d658d5779aa1d0b95b0d8efd", "parents": ["89de1a923deb6ac086e2051452a4eb329101c2e2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Bumping Firefox l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD CLOSED TREE\n\nach -\u003e 4b4d8d5537e6403127638594b0a82d89a17629a1\naf -\u003e 4b4d8d5537e6403127638594b0a82d89a17629a1\nan -\u003e 4b4d8d5537e6403127638594b0a82d89a17629a1\nar -\u003e 4b4d8d5537e6403127638594b0a82d89a17629a1\nast -\u003e 4b4d8d5537e6403127638594b0a82d89a17629a1\naz -\u003e 4b4d8d5537e6403127638594b0a82d89a17629a1\nbe -\u003e 4b4d8d5537e6403127638594b0a82d89a17629a1\nbg -\u003e 4b4d8d5537e6403127638594b0a82d89a17629a1\nbn -\u003e 4b4d8d5537e6403127638594b0a82d89a17629a1\nbo -\u003e 4b4d8d5537e6403127638594b0a82d89a17629a1\nbqi -\u003e 4b4d8d5537e6403127638594b0a82d89a17629a1\nbr -\u003e 4b4d8d5537e6403127638594b0a82d89a17629a1\nbrx -\u003e 4b4d8d5537e6403127638594b0a82d89a17629a1\nbs -\u003e 4b4d8d5537e6403127638594b0a82d89a17629a1\nca -\u003e 4b4d8d5537e64031276