arionetteRefTestExecutor.do_test() opened a new focused window, but didn't\nswitch Marionette to it, so the test ran in a window without focus, and\nrequestFullscreen() was denied with FullscreenDeniedNotFocusedTab. Switch to\nthe new window, as do_testharness() does.\n\nUpdate the expectations to reflect this change. The fullscreen reftests and\nlist-box-important-colors.html now pass, and the customizable-select reftests\nintermittently pass on Linux ASAN.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340242\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/fullscreen/rendering/backdrop-iframe.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fullscreen/rendering/backdrop-inherit.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fullscreen/rendering/exit-fullscreen-scroll-to-unscrollable-area-overflow-hidden.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fullscreen/rendering/exit-fullscreen-scroll-to-unscrollable-area-overflow-x-hidden.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fullscreen/rendering/fullscreen-root-fills-page.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/checkmark-animation-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-custom-button.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-dark-mode.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-default-button.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-disabled-option.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-font-inheriting.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-optgroup-legend.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-optgroup-rendering.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-option-with-label.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-picker-select-border.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-switching-invalidation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-writing-mode-vertical-lr.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-writing-mode-vertical-rl.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-open-invalidation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-option-images.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-picker-icon-open-state.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-picker-pseudo-before-after.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-pseudo-ordering.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/list-box-important-colors.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/wptrunner/executors/executormarionette.py"], "git_node": "35c86dbee187c1ffb27fa9c64a55bb3a96d7d508", "git_parents": ["10b0b5dc04d70c06542caa5574d56212f12ab528"], "node": "0b946e4d8bfbf64373ea7c39c394a475402a0bb8", "parents": ["3933d0928f4b8c2aeefd56c1ff1d4891985d0525"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Goutam Tamvada \u003cgtamvada@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2033918 - Restore EV treatment to HARICA 2015 roots. r=bwilson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340982\n", "files": ["security/certverifier/ExtendedValidation.cpp"], "git_node": "d85f864c6d7ae354ca43a28aa1b06e9524a01275", "git_parents": ["35c86dbee187c1ffb27fa9c64a55bb3a96d7d508"], "node": "127fe7edfe482573895f0b216a00f1157cabeaf2", "parents": ["0b946e4d8bfbf64373ea7c39c394a475402a0bb8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091018 - Run the ruff, codespell and rumdl lint jobs when python/sites/lint.txt changes r=linter-reviewers,ahochheiden DONTBUILD\n\nruff, ruff-format, codespell and rumdl are pinned in python/sites/lint.txt,\nbut bumping one of them did not schedule the matching lint job, nor make\nmozlint check the whole tree.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340980\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/source-test/mozlint.yml", "tools/lint/codespell.yml", "tools/lint/md.yml", "tools/lint/ruff-format.yml", "tools/lint/ruff.yml"], "git_node": "8f5049e004d34411e161196bd9547a5b2f3c7511", "git_parents": ["d85f864c6d7ae354ca43a28aa1b06e9524a01275"], "node": "74082c3959099808553f17fc73de31b365829eb7", "parents": ["127fe7edfe482573895f0b216a00f1157cabeaf2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Adam Vandolder \u003cavandolder@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1998954 - Use new push/replace path for frames. r=dom-core-reviewers,farre\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D271774\n", "files": ["docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "dom/base/nsFrameLoader.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/navigating-across-documents/navigate-iframe-to-same-url-with-document-domain.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/navigation-api/__dir__.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/navigation-api/navigate-event/navigate-to-srcdoc.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/navigation-api/navigation-history-entry/entries-after-blank-navigation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/navigation-api/navigation-history-entry/entries-after-blob-navigation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/navigation-api/navigation-methods/traverseTo-navigates-multiple-iframes.html.ini"], "git_node": "adda4fa7f24fc5553e8278038b3a39c4cd43f696", "git_parents": ["8f5049e004d34411e161196bd9547a5b2f3c7511"], "node": "2ce8720bc6f4063ace19f8c20252f88906e27ae9", "parents": ["74082c3959099808553f17fc73de31b365829eb7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Adam Vandolder \u003cavandolder@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088943 - Use the inherited principal URI for about:srcdoc SHEs when checking same-origin for the Navigation API. r=dom-core-reviewers,vhilla,necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339566\n", "files": ["docshell/base/CanonicalBrowsingContext.cpp", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "docshell/shistory/SessionHistoryEntry.cpp", "docshell/shistory/SessionHistoryEntry.h", "docshell/shistory/nsSHistory.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsNetUtil.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsNetUtil.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/navigation-api/navigation-history-entry/entries-after-srcdoc-navigation.html.ini"], "git_node": "fe56b58ce029dfd7a2950b410a5d0a502b934a16", "git_parents": ["adda4fa7f24fc5553e8278038b3a39c4cd43f696"], "node": "32b66b46a02753b4a6a3905dcda86ca91c7e04bd", "parents": ["2ce8720bc6f4063ace19f8c20252f88906e27ae9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nora Liu \u003cnliu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085001 - Inline true/false/null/[]/{} class field initializers r=spidermonkey-reviewers,mgaudet\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338016\n", "files": ["js/src/frontend/BytecodeEmitter.cpp", "js/src/frontend/BytecodeEmitter.h", "js/src/frontend/Parser.cpp", "js/src/frontend/Parser.h", "js/src/frontend/SharedContext.h"], "git_node": "2b88f8e069e83431d7d7a9faa37a33c73334dbf8", "git_parents": ["fe56b58ce029dfd7a2950b410a5d0a502b934a16"], "node": "ce0fcf8fcf7ed795b756c083158cc39b85b1135b", "parents": ["32b66b46a02753b4a6a3905dcda86ca91c7e04bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2084649 - Track the embedding frameloader in BrowserParent. r=smaug\" for causing bp-nu failures at BrowserBridgeParent\n\nThis reverts commit a3cb459d1d39d134f9b697afe24494acbf297dd9.\n", "files": ["docshell/shistory/nsSHistory.cpp", "dom/base/nsFrameLoader.cpp", "dom/base/nsFrameLoader.h", "dom/ipc/BrowserBridgeParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.h"], "git_node": "ce04697aaf1b507cb66713e37ba25cdbb604fb39", "git_parents": ["2b88f8e069e83431d7d7a9faa37a33c73334dbf8"], "node": "c025ad11aa4e6a7bb5129d02728c9894484a3514", "parents": ["ce0fcf8fcf7ed795b756c083158cc39b85b1135b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2084004 - Consolidate FedCM enablement checks in WebIdentityParent. r=emz\" for causing vendor media failures at media/libsoundtouch/moz.yaml\n\nThis reverts commit 64dfbf99a033e6ff69e964570615f212ecf21009.\n", "files": ["dom/credentialmanagement/identity/WebIdentityParent.cpp"], "git_node": "4c4ef66ea3d4507d5c7eb1ecd6614debd23f756a", "git_parents": ["ce04697aaf1b507cb66713e37ba25cdbb604fb39"], "node": "d205d13098a5b156163c0636bd6ed89929c3fb9a", "parents": ["c025ad11aa4e6a7bb5129d02728c9894484a3514"], "tags": []}, {"author": "scottdowne \u003csdowne@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090994 - newtab fixing spaces preview images r=jaws\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340983\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Spaces/_Spaces.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/assets/spaces-preview-activity.png", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/assets/spaces-preview-kit-activity.png", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/assets/spaces-preview-kit-stories.png", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/assets/spaces-preview-kit-widgets.png", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/assets/spaces-preview-stories.png", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/assets/spaces-preview-widgets.png"], "git_node": "48d72ce06267bf38ff352f6b7003db63f966cc78", "git_parents": ["4c4ef66ea3d4507d5c7eb1ecd6614debd23f756a"], "node": "6940b9b98650bd9b2272f931a89d44f53e883e4b", "parents": ["d205d13098a5b156163c0636bd6ed89929c3fb9a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Gaudet \u003cmgaudet@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084355 - Avoid re-enquing suppressed microtasks when the debugger has stashed the queue r=smaug\n\nThis kind of issue has been around for a while; pre-SM owned microtask\nI believe it would have been just duplicate promise handler runs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336189\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/chrome/chrome.toml", "dom/base/test/chrome/test_bug2084355.html", "dom/base/test/file_bug2084355.html", "dom/base/test/mochitest.toml", "xpcom/base/CycleCollectedJSContext.cpp", "xpcom/base/CycleCollectedJSContext.h"], "git_node": "8a278d32949daafd6245bf89a232a1a3bf5ba70f", "git_parents": ["48d72ce06267bf38ff352f6b7003db63f966cc78"], "node": "5b11351833a1a1563a27dcd2ec1b51bb78b288af", "parents": ["6940b9b98650bd9b2272f931a89d44f53e883e4b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090941 - Stop implementing nsIBaseWindow on nsWebBrowser. r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nnsWebBrowser's nsIBaseWindow implementation refers to the content area it\nhosts, while nsDocShellTreeOwner's refers to the containing window.\n\nThat distinction gets in the way of merging both objects, and we\ndon't really need it.\n\nThe only consumers (BrowserChild and the windowless browser code in\nnsAppShellService) can just operate on the docshell directly or call\nnsWebBrowser::Close().\n\nnsDocShellTreeOwner::SetPositionDesktopPix used to also move the web\nbrowser's docshell to the requested screen position, which made no sense\n(the docshell position always relative to its widget), so that's gone.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340901\n", "files": ["docshell/base/nsDocShellTreeOwner.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserChild.cpp", "toolkit/components/browser/nsIWebBrowser.idl", "toolkit/components/browser/nsWebBrowser.cpp", "toolkit/components/browser/nsWebBrowser.h", "xpfe/appshell/nsAppShellService.cpp"], "git_node": "ba0940c6fcb23096aad5e2088365e03d9d2ad45a", "git_parents": ["8a278d32949daafd6245bf89a232a1a3bf5ba70f"], "node": "6d3c70c79f6d1ecf94a5c51248f50f31b7e4fa8f", "parents": ["5b11351833a1a1563a27dcd2ec1b51bb78b288af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086738 - Reset the media session position when the track title changes. r=Roger,android-reviewers\n\nBrowserStorePlayer receives store states through a conflated flow, so a title change and the new track's first\nposition report can reach it as one state, and it took that fresh position for the previous track's. The\nreducer sees the actions in order, so it now resets the position to 0 when the metadata title changes, and the\nplayer no longer tracks stale positions itself. The duration and rate are kept, since Gecko also sends a new\ntitle when the page title changes on a page without media session metadata, and the next position report can\nbe a long way off.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339350\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/state/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/state/reducer/MediaSessionReducer.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/state/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/state/state/MediaSessionState.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/state/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/state/action/MediaSessionActionTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/media/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/media/player/BrowserStorePlayer.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/media/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/media/player/BrowserStorePlayerTest.kt"], "git_node": "0212230187e4a0a7fc3f4b3f9381aa6e12ad5a4a", "git_parents": ["ba0940c6fcb23096aad5e2088365e03d9d2ad45a"], "node": "7932a5fae4816b52ead822a19ec175194b242578", "parents": ["6d3c70c79f6d1ecf94a5c51248f50f31b7e4fa8f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Segun Famisa \u003csfamisa@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086448 - Rework IP protection onboarding to determine the prompt details before showing the prompt r=jonalmeida,android-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337425\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BrowserFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/HomeFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ipprotection/helpers/IsoPromoDeadline.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ipprotection/store/IPProtectionOnboardingPrompt.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ipprotection/store/IPProtectionPromptStore.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ipprotection/ui/IPProtectionBottomSheet.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ipprotection/ui/IPProtectionBottomSheetFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/continuous/ContinuousOnboardingFeature.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/navigation/nav_graph.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ipprotection/store/IPProtectionOnboardingPromptTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/continuous/ContinuousOnboardingFeatureTest.kt"], "git_node": "0904b043ac58e30784106fda6b9f07e0ed29ec84", "git_parents": ["0212230187e4a0a7fc3f4b3f9381aa6e12ad5a4a"], "node": "401f68b4740acc375290a7d41f88dd11a8d0460d", "parents": ["7932a5fae4816b52ead822a19ec175194b242578"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089867 - Don't intersect the clip rect with the primitive's bounds in ps_quad_mask. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nThe primitive's bounds are in its own space, which is not the clip's space when the clip is in a different coordinate system, so the mask was emptied.\n\nThis made the facial features disappear on https://diana-adrianne.com/purecss-francine/ and regressed with bug 1998432, when the clip mask started using the primitive's local coverage rect as its bounds.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340752\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/res/ps_quad_mask.glsl", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/nested-rotation-elliptical-clip-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/nested-rotation-elliptical-clip.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/reftest.list"], "git_node": "1decb865107ecb2b761d39e9b55371da466305ec", "git_parents": ["0904b043ac58e30784106fda6b9f07e0ed29ec84"], "node": "0602827c8f9f69435d61e70a2494dd8ce3b4041d", "parents": ["401f68b4740acc375290a7d41f88dd11a8d0460d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084408 - Intern clips and polygons in the display list builder r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nClip chain building, slice partitioning and hit testing read clip keys, so\nclips and clip-path polygons get a scene builder store as well as a render\nbackend one. The rect and spatial node stay on the clip node, so every\nrectangle clip of a mode shares one entry. A foreign mask image gives the node\nan empty rect, clipping everything out as dropping the item did.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340767\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/border.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/clip.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/dl_interner.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/hit_test.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/intern.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/profiler.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_builder_thread.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_building.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/slice_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_item.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_list.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/interned_prims.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/interning.rs", "gfx/wr/wrshell/src/wrench.rs"], "git_node": "ce5269797b58fa05d613ff52ef3d24f3ba30f3fd", "git_parents": ["1decb865107ecb2b761d39e9b55371da466305ec"], "node": "7ea48c63b21fa77377df376cf87742c7587c5532", "parents": ["0602827c8f9f69435d61e70a2494dd8ce3b4041d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090866 - Move the delta stats into the generate resolve callback in TextGenerator::Generate (Coverity CID 1702186) r=ai-platform-reviewers,valentinp\n\nThe handler set by SetDeltaHandler() holds its own reference to stats, and\nnothing reads the local after the capture, so the capture can take it rather\nthan bump the shared_ptr refcount.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340871\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/ml/textgeneration/TextGenerator.cpp"], "git_node": "7bc1fdbf9e2aeb8ff74e12d0bf503e7f8dd1e431", "git_parents": ["ce5269797b58fa05d613ff52ef3d24f3ba30f3fd"], "node": "b5d76571abdcbb168bf83c1c4602ccfdd8360df2", "parents": ["7ea48c63b21fa77377df376cf87742c7587c5532"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "no bug - update to ruff 0.17.4 r=linter-reviewers,ahochheiden DONTBUILD\n\nno python change\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340972\n", "files": ["python/sites/lint.txt", "python/sites/python-test.txt"], "git_node": "f2fb04982a609aecd2d58af4d53e4de9e1715a46", "git_parents": ["7bc1fdbf9e2aeb8ff74e12d0bf503e7f8dd1e431"], "node": "dd6d2807cfcd0ce5480b452d53e16f5ff3dd0b76", "parents": ["b5d76571abdcbb168bf83c1c4602ccfdd8360df2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090944 - Ignore RUSTSEC-2026-0459 libsqlite3-sys advisory r=supply-chain-reviewers,afranchuk DONTBUILD\n\nGecko builds libsqlite3-sys with in_gecko and links third_party/sqlite3, so\nthe bundled SQLite the advisory is about is not compiled.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340989\n", "files": [".cargo/audit.toml"], "git_node": "f0eec3bcae14a92bfc2b11dd75f153778c39d26e", "git_parents": ["f2fb04982a609aecd2d58af4d53e4de9e1715a46"], "node": "cee6ead315a75c0c50d289f5cd7af20281d0a039", "parents": ["dd6d2807cfcd0ce5480b452d53e16f5ff3dd0b76"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dana Keeler \u003cdkeeler@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088996 - avoid CERTCertificate when finding potential issuers in cert verification r=jschanck,supply-chain-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340554\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "security/certverifier/CertVerifier.h", "security/certverifier/NSSCertDBTrustDomain.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/SSLServerCertVerification.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/metrics.yaml", "security/manager/ssl/nsIX509CertDB.idl", "security/manager/ssl/rsclientcerts/Cargo.toml", "security/manager/ssl/rsclientcerts/src/cryptoki.rs", "security/manager/ssl/rsclientcerts/src/lib.rs", "security/manager/ssl/rsclientcerts/src/manager.rs", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/test_crlite_preexisting.js", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/test_crlite_preexisting_tls.js", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/test_intermediate_basic_usage_constraints.js", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/test_intermediate_preloads.js", "supply-chain/audits.toml", "third_party/rust/pkcs11-bindings/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/pkcs11-bindings/.cargo_vcs_info.json", "third_party/rust/pkcs11-bindings/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/pkcs11-bindings/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/pkcs11-bindings/Cargo.toml.orig", "third_party/rust/pkcs11-bindings/build.rs"], "git_node": "093d61dc23c859511538d96139824a194408bcd7", "git_parents": ["f0eec3bcae14a92bfc2b11dd75f153778c39d26e"], "node": "67baf015533a362b5c70a2d83b3cdbf9ac85a0f6", "parents": ["cee6ead315a75c0c50d289f5cd7af20281d0a039"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Nibler \u003cdev@tnibler.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071554 - Allow runWithMSE after document load r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nSkip waiting for the load event when the document is already complete.\nKeep the existing wait for callers that run before document completion.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329761\n", "files": ["dom/media/mediasource/test/mediasource.js"], "git_node": "e35f44214000f0dbcf36d93e51500d4b4d5aa8b0", "git_parents": ["093d61dc23c859511538d96139824a194408bcd7"], "node": "7f17469911cac00673df68cfcab7fe61a5708c1f", "parents": ["67baf015533a362b5c70a2d83b3cdbf9ac85a0f6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Nibler \u003cdev@tnibler.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072130 - Add test for MP4 seeking in various keyframe constellations r=alwu,media-playback-reviewers\n\nThese tests replicate different instances of broken seeking, for example\nbug 1709081, bug 1932283, bug 1481496, bug 1539182.\n\nFor H264, Firefox currently treats all I and SI slices as IDR frames i.e,\nvalid points to start decoding with blank decoder state.\nThis often times doesn't work, manifesting in full stalls or a frozen image\nuntil the next real keyframe is reached, or jumping further forward than the\ntarget seek time (including to the end of the stream).\nIn these cases the files are not at fault and seeking issues are a bug,\nreproduced in the single-idr and idr-then-nidr tests.\n\nsync-lies and single-idr-no-stss are \"broken\" MP4 files, where the container\ndesignates samples as sync that are not actually keyframes at the codec level.\nSeeking to these not-keyframes will not work and causes varying issues across\nuser reports.\nFirefox, Chromium and Safari currently handle this by ignoring keyframe flags in\nthe container and parsing NAL types themselves. The tests ensure this workaround\nwon't break. HEVC, AV1 and VP9 are included for completeness.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329764\n", "files": ["dom/media/mediasource/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/generate.sh", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/idr-then-nidr-h264-0.mp4", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/idr-then-nidr-h264-0.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/idr-then-nidr-h264-1.mp4", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/idr-then-nidr-h264-1.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/idr-then-nidr-h265-0.mp4", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/idr-then-nidr-h265-0.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/idr-then-nidr-h265-1.mp4", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/idr-then-nidr-h265-1.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/single-idr-av1-0.mp4", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/single-idr-av1-0.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/single-idr-av1-1.mp4", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/single-idr-av1-1.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/single-idr-h264-0.mp4", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/single-idr-h264-0.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/single-idr-h264-1.mp4", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/single-idr-h264-1.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/single-idr-h265-0.mp4", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/single-idr-h265-0.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/single-idr-h265-1.mp4", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/single-idr-h265-1.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/single-idr-vp9-0.mp4", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/single-idr-vp9-0.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/single-idr-vp9-1.mp4", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/single-idr-vp9-1.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/sync-lies-av1-0.mp4", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/sync-lies-av1-0.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/sync-lies-h264-0.mp4", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/sync-lies-h264-0.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/sync-lies-h265-0.mp4", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/sync-lies-h265-0.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/sync-lies-vp9-0.mp4", "dom/media/mediasource/test/seek-odd-keyframes/sync-lies-vp9-0.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/mediasource/test/test_SeekToNonIDR_mp4.html", "dom/media/test/mochitest_seek.toml", "dom/media/test/no-stss-1-keyframe/av1.mp4", "dom/media/test/no-stss-1-keyframe/av1.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/test/no-stss-1-keyframe/generate.sh", "dom/media/test/no-stss-1-keyframe/h264.mp4", "dom/media/test/no-stss-1-keyframe/h264.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/test/no-stss-1-keyframe/h265.mp4", "dom/media/test/no-stss-1-keyframe/h265.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/test/no-stss-1-keyframe/vp9.mp4", "dom/media/test/no-stss-1-keyframe/vp9.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/test/test_seek_nokeyframes.html"], "git_node": "8df9ff29399d37453e087e470d2dd8b31be3fbac", "git_parents": ["e35f44214000f0dbcf36d93e51500d4b4d5aa8b0"], "node": "a58c158534a929d240babfa65c6826ca331e5ae4", "parents": ["7f17469911cac00673df68cfcab7fe61a5708c1f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Nibler \u003cdev@tnibler.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072130 Pt. 1 - Don't treat all H264 I-frames as IDR, verify H265 keyframes too r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nKeyframes are determined by analyzing H264 bitstream instead of relying\non container information. However, the result of this analysis is\noverridden to consider all types of I-frames as recover/random access\npoints.\nThe spec does not require that decoding can start at any non-IDR frame,\nand valid files containing non-IDR I-frame can fail to decode after\nseeking if the last \"keyframe\" is in fact not a real IDR.\nFor H265, inaccurate sync sample flags in the MP4 container cause the\nsame issues as for the other codecs, so the bitstream analysis should\nbe done on all platforms, not just Apple. Apple remains as a special\ncase, as VideoToolbox is less permissive and can only start decoding on\ntrue IDR frames, other random access points like CRA_NUT are not\nallowed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326110\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestMP4Demuxer.cpp", "dom/media/mp4/MP4Demuxer.cpp"], "git_node": "c6f932cc8801895a22934531fad59bd0f62f8ac6", "git_parents": ["8df9ff29399d37453e087e470d2dd8b31be3fbac"], "node": "8ca5d465f499faee5f207c107c41262bae866376", "parents": ["a58c158534a929d240babfa65c6826ca331e5ae4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Nibler \u003cdev@tnibler.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072130 Pt. 2 - Retry seek from earlier keyframe on End Of Stream, on all platforms r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326111\n", "files": ["dom/media/mp4/MP4Demuxer.cpp"], "git_node": "4ba70e8e6ba60b190ca8de2eaed2e6aef03ed30b", "git_parents": ["c6f932cc8801895a22934531fad59bd0f62f8ac6"], "node": "500a0cf00cf8c15024984b54e664cffd1f1ee250", "parents": ["8ca5d465f499faee5f207c107c41262bae866376"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Nibler \u003cdev@tnibler.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080453 - Rework MP4 seek logic, use keyframe lookup table r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nThis change replaces the linear search used to find keyframes with a\nlookup table of keyframe timestamps and indices.\n`MP4SampleIndex` holds a map of keyframe times that is initially\npopulated using `stss` entries or `trun` flags.\n`SampleIterator` uses this map to jump to the last keyframe before the\ntarget seek time, and `MP4TrackDemuxer::GetNextSample` verifies\nkeyframes by inspecting the actual sample contents.\nThe results of this analysis is saved in the keyframe map, so that for\nsubsequent seeks to nearby timestamps `SampleIterator::Seek`\nimmediately jumps to a known good keyframe.\nLinear search is still used if the keyframe map is incomplete or the\nlookup fails for other reasons, but it will generally only do the\nexpensive copying and parsing once per sample.\nThe same applies to `MP4TrackDemuxer::SkipToNextRandomAccessPoint`.\n\nTo handle the quite exotic case of an `stss` table missing the first\nkeyframe in a file, `MP4SampleIndex` now ignores sync sample flags when\nfirst ingesting samples. Previously, anything before the first sync\nsample would have been dropped and thus not playable.\n\nNew tests to verify seeks resolve correctly while not reading more\nthan what's necessary from the MediaSource, among which:\n - `no-stss-4-keyframes`: 4 keyframes, but missing `stss` so that all\n   samples appear sync at the container level.\n - `bad-stss`: `stss` missing a keyframe, entries for non-keyframe\n   I-frames, or both.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332834\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestMP4Demuxer.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/frag_bframes.mp4", "dom/media/gtest/moz.build", "dom/media/gtest/mp4_demuxer/TestKeyframeMap.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/mp4_demuxer/moz.build", "dom/media/gtest/nonzero_first_pts.mp4", "dom/media/mp4/MP4Demuxer.cpp", "dom/media/mp4/SampleIterator.cpp", "dom/media/mp4/SampleIterator.h", "dom/media/test/bad-stss/generate.sh", "dom/media/test/bad-stss/stss-1st-wrong-h264.mp4", "dom/media/test/bad-stss/stss-1st-wrong-h264.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/test/bad-stss/stss-1st-wrong-h265.mp4", "dom/media/test/bad-stss/stss-1st-wrong-h265.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/test/bad-stss/stss-2nd-wrong-h264.mp4", "dom/media/test/bad-stss/stss-2nd-wrong-h264.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/test/bad-stss/stss-2nd-wrong-h265.mp4", "dom/media/test/bad-stss/stss-2nd-wrong-h265.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/test/bad-stss/stss-extra-entries-h264.mp4", "dom/media/test/bad-stss/stss-extra-entries-h264.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/test/bad-stss/stss-extra-entries-h265.mp4", "dom/media/test/bad-stss/stss-extra-entries-h265.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/test/mochitest_seek.toml", "dom/media/test/no-stss-4-keyframes/av1.mp4", "dom/media/test/no-stss-4-keyframes/av1.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/test/no-stss-4-keyframes/generate.sh", "dom/media/test/no-stss-4-keyframes/h264.mp4", "dom/media/test/no-stss-4-keyframes/h264.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/test/no-stss-4-keyframes/h265.mp4", "dom/media/test/no-stss-4-keyframes/h265.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/test/no-stss-4-keyframes/vp9.mp4", "dom/media/test/no-stss-4-keyframes/vp9.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/test/test_seek_between_keyframes.html"], "git_node": "bc208b5437da13d8e22c38e89d49d23b97a206cf", "git_parents": ["4ba70e8e6ba60b190ca8de2eaed2e6aef03ed30b"], "node": "21098182d61f78a2f4734599aad88c2aebfc1c0e", "parents": ["500a0cf00cf8c15024984b54e664cffd1f1ee250"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eitan Isaacson \u003ceitan@monotonous.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050939 - Remove invisible select subtree. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,Jamie,devtools-reviewers,morgan,ochameau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D309162\n", "files": ["accessible/base/HTMLMarkupMap.inc", "accessible/base/nsAccessibilityService.cpp", "accessible/base/nsCoreUtils.cpp", "accessi