s": []}, {"author": "AndiAJ \u003candiaj@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089556 - Create a new edit bookmark folders related regression UI tests r=aaronmt,android-reviewers,giorga\n\nThe UI test successfully passed 25x on Firebase \u2705\nAll UI tests successfully passed 1x on Firebase \u2705\n\n\u2757 The test tag addition needs to be reviewed by someone from the development team\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340294\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/BookmarksSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/BookmarksTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/bookmarks/BookmarksTestTag.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/bookmarks/ui/EditFolderScreen.kt"], "git_node": "36d649b8b34b554355816022aa426e68e3eceb55", "git_parents": ["d266642e7aae9fa7769422c11b1c112d6897ee57"], "node": "42fae39675f434fb70eac9d807f89bd643235418", "parents": ["e2bd1ec63731b13069b9851c002e9c5f576748bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "AndiAJ \u003candiaj@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070837 - Fix verifyCopyPDFTextOptionTest efficiency UI test r=aaronmt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340301\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/BrowserPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/BrowserPageSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/TextSelectionTest.kt"], "git_node": "bc08cb5e981f90eba183ef79f1160f4a9fee9c86", "git_parents": ["36d649b8b34b554355816022aa426e68e3eceb55"], "node": "85c876fda787092bc4d927899ac64e70c8a5f1c4", "parents": ["42fae39675f434fb70eac9d807f89bd643235418"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mike a. \u003cmavduevskiy@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089927 - Add a Nimbus kill switch for passwords import. r=matt-tighe,android-reviewers\n\nThe secret setting stays as an override on Nightly and debug builds. The two\nflags are combined on every read, so the Nimbus value keeps applying after the\nsecret setting has been toggled.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340268\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/nimbus.fml.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/SecretSettingsFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/logins/fragment/SavedLoginsFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/Settings.kt"], "git_node": "ec0da9fee4c4958553f1daa1f67c3806d61743d5", "git_parents": ["bc08cb5e981f90eba183ef79f1160f4a9fee9c86"], "node": "a16fad3fa25fb7266410658824099142c3bd544e", "parents": ["85c876fda787092bc4d927899ac64e70c8a5f1c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089267 - Make `AutoDeleteRangesHandler::Run` handle error of `FallbackToDeleteRangesWithTransaction` r=m_kato\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340835\n", "files": ["editor/libeditor/HTMLEditorDeleteHandler.cpp"], "git_node": "521a9a00ef5e8d5b91773591a2536df68886bf5e", "git_parents": ["ec0da9fee4c4958553f1daa1f67c3806d61743d5"], "node": "1be6e718b96ad8f444416f456b31be40cc52168f", "parents": ["a16fad3fa25fb7266410658824099142c3bd544e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086303: Show \"(set in macOS keyboard settings)\" in about:keyboard for unchangeable shortcuts assigned in System Settings. r=Jamie\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337342\n", "files": ["browser/components/customkeys/content/customkeys.js", "browser/components/customkeys/tests/browser/browser_aboutKeyboard_systemAssigned.js"], "git_node": "88f3f904f443aa089def2e750cd353bf05f98b03", "git_parents": ["521a9a00ef5e8d5b91773591a2536df68886bf5e"], "node": "d093f5bc7b3c17c33b7e6a5ae65c90a602288424", "parents": ["1be6e718b96ad8f444416f456b31be40cc52168f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086303: Make a shortcut assigned in System Settings replace the built-in shortcut of internal menu items. r=Jamie,mac-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nThe built-in shortcuts of Undo, Redo, Cut, Copy, Paste and Select All are handled in ShortcutKeyDefinitions.cpp, because their key elements, or the commands those point to as in the Library window, are internal. So rewriting the key element did not stop them, and both the assigned and the built-in shortcut worked. While another shortcut is assigned to such an item, the menu bar now stops its built-in shortcut, so the key does nothing.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337857\n", "files": ["widget/cocoa/nsMenuBarX.mm", "widget/cocoa/nsMenuItemX.h", "widget/cocoa/nsMenuItemX.mm"], "git_node": "cd8b1382296cc6a982d98f61c23e3383fe43550b", "git_parents": ["88f3f904f443aa089def2e750cd353bf05f98b03"], "node": "8babe70ccb9ce60f73daf7cca57945a75142c08b", "parents": ["d093f5bc7b3c17c33b7e6a5ae65c90a602288424"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lars Eggert \u003cleggert@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085009 - Create the DNS service on the main thread if needed when starting a SOCKS proxy lookup r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\n`nsSOCKSSocketInfo::StartDNS` runs on the socket thread and used `components::DNS::Service()`, which fails in the parent process if the DNS service hasn't been created yet. The connect then failed with no NSPR error set.\n\nUse `GetOrInitDNSService()`, as other socket-thread DNS consumers do. It creates the service on the main thread with a sync runnable if needed. Also set `PR_BAD_ADDRESS_ERROR` on both remaining `StartDNS` failure paths (no service, `AsyncResolveNative` failure), so the consumer always gets a real error, matching how `ConnectToProxy` reports a failed proxy lookup.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340887\n", "files": ["netwerk/socket/moz.build", "netwerk/socket/nsSOCKSIOLayer.cpp"], "git_node": "be9d4004d24a19c9f2f4a0faa451948f60ff0f4e", "git_parents": ["cd8b1382296cc6a982d98f61c23e3383fe43550b"], "node": "8b1b28b8c4a3fd333d321d46928ebb541eb30410", "parents": ["8babe70ccb9ce60f73daf7cca57945a75142c08b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091271 - [riscv64] Spell register moves and zeroing as mv. r=csmantle\n\nThe ISA manual spells a register move as mv (addi rd, rs, 0), and a\nzeroing is a move from zero (addi rd, zero, 0, which is also li rd, 0).\nThose are the forms a core can be expected to recognize. The SpacemiT\nK3's X100 eliminates most mv at rename but runs or rd, rs, zero or ori\nrd, rs, 0 as a one-cycle operation: a chain of two adds and two moves\ntakes 3.07 cycles with mv and 4.0 with either. Nor does it treat xor rd,\nrs, rs as a zeroing idiom: the xor waits for rs's last writer, where a\nmove from zero waits for nothing.\n\nThe riscv64 backend copied sp with or_ in setupUnalignedABICall, before\nevery call into C++ that realigns the stack, and made the copies in\nma_addPtrTestOverflow with ori. These now use ma_mv. Shared code zeroes\na register the x86 way, with an xor32, xorPtr or xor64 of the register\nwith itself, in about twenty places from CacheIR to the Wasm baseline\ncompiler. On riscv64 those now move from zero.\n\nIn a JetStream 3 run on a SpacemiT K3 this respells 37,843 of the 37,865\nmoves and zeroings that riscvlint finds: 27,058 copies of sp, 10,493 xor\nzeroings and 292 ori moves. The 22 left are an andi with 0 or -1, or an\nslt or sltu of a register with itself, whose operands only happen to\nmake them a zeroing or a move.\n\nFound with riscvlint.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341238\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/riscv64/MacroAssembler-riscv64-inl.h", "js/src/jit/riscv64/MacroAssembler-riscv64.cpp"], "git_node": "512783c8f57785ac4ff358aae8cf92b24faa6db3", "git_parents": ["be9d4004d24a19c9f2f4a0faa451948f60ff0f4e"], "node": "69a1412c0059016930fcbf116b38239cf99be6df", "parents": ["8b1b28b8c4a3fd333d321d46928ebb541eb30410"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090571 - [loong64] Part 1: Introduce assembler-only VRegister. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nThis part only adds the struct, which will be used in later parts.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340586\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/loong64/Architecture-loong64.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.h"], "git_node": "a67243c903e5c609940691550c8a599b7e9f92f1", "git_parents": ["512783c8f57785ac4ff358aae8cf92b24faa6db3"], "node": "cc1c189e6ade0e24d7c3f000236f85f7754d2ca4", "parents": ["69a1412c0059016930fcbf116b38239cf99be6df"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090571 - [loong64] Part 2: Switch to VRegister for vector registers in Loong64 backend. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nThis involves three parts of changes:\n\n* Make all as_v* methods take VRegister argument for VR.\n* Make ma_v{ld,st} take VRegister.\n* Teach ScratchSimd128Scope and ScratchSimd128Scope2 how to cast to\n  VRegister.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340587\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/Assembler-loong64.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/CodeGenerator-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64-inl.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.h"], "git_node": "9f49fb07ad173989204f47c5bfaeb797fd275beb", "git_parents": ["a67243c903e5c609940691550c8a599b7e9f92f1"], "node": "093d5f63b41f659c1468e2213160e1ec0d59b8a3", "parents": ["cc1c189e6ade0e24d7c3f000236f85f7754d2ca4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tymur Boiko \u003ctboiko@nvidia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068257 - [Linux][Vulkan Video] Disable direct export with older system FFmpeg. r=stransky,media-playback-reviewers\n\nSystem FFmpeg can reach Vulkan direct export without the DRM mapping\nfixes in FFmpeg 25e187f849 (FFmpeg 8.2-dev, libavcodec 62.29.101),\ncausing corruption or crashes. Require libavcodec newer than 62.29.101\nfor direct export on all GPU vendors. Use the Vulkan copy path for\nolder libraries and retain AMD's stricter 63.20.101 requirement.\n\nRemove the obsolete bundled-ffvpx version guard and its unused constant;\nthe updated ffvpx (FFmpeg 9.0.1, libavcodec 63.1.101) already includes\nthe required fixes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340895\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegLibWrapper.h", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp"], "git_node": "56e2225f44a740583ba129f0276d015d1c967e7b", "git_parents": ["9f49fb07ad173989204f47c5bfaeb797fd275beb"], "node": "d2760ddf07582a6f843e2858ee43982872003d19", "parents": ["093d5f63b41f659c1468e2213160e1ec0d59b8a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paraspandey-debugs \u003cp.pandey250806@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090681 - Replace FieldText with a design token in aboutMemory.css. r=dao,desktop-theme-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341255\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/aboutmemory/content/aboutMemory.css"], "git_node": "478f8d4e1e218df776f00cec3e3fedea02dfb36d", "git_parents": ["56e2225f44a740583ba129f0276d015d1c967e7b"], "node": "d2fd23f148b099cbc270cf51ae5f8763e2263363", "parents": ["d2760ddf07582a6f843e2858ee43982872003d19"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090941 - Merge nsDocShellTreeOwner into nsWebBrowser. r=farre\n\nNow that nsWebBrowser no longer has its own nsIBaseWindow implementation,\nthere's no reason for the tree owner to be a separate object.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340902\n", "files": ["docshell/base/moz.build", "docshell/base/nsDocShellTreeOwner.cpp", "docshell/base/nsDocShellTreeOwner.h", "toolkit/components/browser/nsWebBrowser.cpp", "toolkit/components/browser/nsWebBrowser.h", "toolkit/content/widgets/browser-custom-element.mjs"], "git_node": "f7a53531dd4f25594cb6c776b047977a6f9434dc", "git_parents": ["478f8d4e1e218df776f00cec3e3fedea02dfb36d"], "node": "346f8282090a31943b855c91ca3169a7cd605a94", "parents": ["d2fd23f148b099cbc270cf51ae5f8763e2263363"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090941 - Remove nsIWebBrowser. r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nIt's only used from C++, which can use nsWebBrowser directly.\nSetOriginAttributes was dead, as were the NS_WEBBROWSER_CID and\nNS_WEBBROWSER_CONTRACTID definitions.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340903\n", "files": ["docshell/shistory/nsISHistory.idl", "dom/ipc/BrowserChild.cpp", "toolkit/components/browser/moz.build", "toolkit/components/browser/nsEmbedCID.h", "toolkit/components/browser/nsIWebBrowser.idl", "toolkit/components/browser/nsIWebBrowserChrome.idl", "toolkit/components/browser/nsWebBrowser.cpp", "toolkit/components/browser/nsWebBrowser.h", "toolkit/components/find/nsIWebBrowserFind.idl", "toolkit/components/windowwatcher/nsWindowWatcher.cpp", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.xpcom.d.ts", "xpfe/appshell/nsAppShellService.cpp", "xpfe/appshell/nsIWindowlessBrowser.idl"], "git_node": "841f57672821e27fb522ddeb0cf550c3c6488964", "git_parents": ["f7a53531dd4f25594cb6c776b047977a6f9434dc"], "node": "0d2f5471f117acc4f79b0cd5fd5b04bd7eccd93a", "parents": ["346f8282090a31943b855c91ca3169a7cd605a94"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Max Inden \u003cmail@max-inden.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090940 - Use Ipv6Only for Happy Eyeballs when IPv4 is disabled. r=kershaw,necko-reviewers\n\nSymmetric to the IPv6-disabled case. Without it, e.g. the connectivity\nservice's IPv6 probe runs as DualStackPreferV6 and the state machine sends an\nA query that SetupDnsFlags then refuses.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340904\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/HappyEyeballsConnectionAttempt.cpp"], "git_node": "d8704ac5d60cc73d3c95e81213dcfb6ebcb73237", "git_parents": ["841f57672821e27fb522ddeb0cf550c3c6488964"], "node": "0852c0b74aa73780492880f0ba3a3bb750b586ec", "parents": ["0d2f5471f117acc4f79b0cd5fd5b04bd7eccd93a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Harvey \u003cdale@arandomurl.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089499 - Use moz-src for toolkit/components/antitracking r=urlbar-reviewers,emz,adw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339876\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-siteProtections.js", "browser/base/content/browser-trustPanel.js", "browser/base/content/test/browser-protectionsUI/browser_protectionsUI.js", "browser/base/content/test/browser-protectionsUI/head.js", "browser/base/content/test/browser-trustPanel/browser_trust_panel.js", "browser/base/content/test/browser-trustPanel/browser_trust_panel_telemetry.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/head.js", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/components.conf", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/moz.build", "toolkit/components/antitracking/components.conf", "toolkit/components/antitracking/moz.build", "toolkit/components/antitracking/test/browser/browser_contentBlockingAllowListPrincipal.js", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.modules.d.ts", "tools/@types/generated/tspaths.json", "tools/lint/extra-js-modules/allowlist.txt"], "git_node": "54228742ddc348a020296b6623722de4ac6b4adb", "git_parents": ["d8704ac5d60cc73d3c95e81213dcfb6ebcb73237"], "node": "630f85fefec5d78b9433b8809fb187f6599b11c2", "parents": ["0852c0b74aa73780492880f0ba3a3bb750b586ec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mike a. \u003cmavduevskiy@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087414 - Part 1: Default formActionOrigin when importing CSV passwords without a target. r=android-reviewers,sfamisa\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338294\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/password-parser-csv/src/main/java/mozilla/components/lib/password/parser/csv/CsvPasswordsFileParser.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/password-parser-csv/src/test/java/mozilla/components/lib/password/parser/csv/CsvPasswordsFileParserTest.kt"], "git_node": "98927e7fcc6f4c6097f5085a4a37da0b2c2781e7", "git_parents": ["54228742ddc348a020296b6623722de4ac6b4adb"], "node": "4c09166bf5aa33e48501d2714f5cdf21697a870d", "parents": ["630f85fefec5d78b9433b8809fb187f6599b11c2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mike a. \u003cmavduevskiy@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087414 - Part 2: Support the user_name column from Dashlane Android CSV exports. r=android-reviewers,matt-tighe,sfamisa\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339899\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/password-parser-csv/src/main/java/mozilla/components/lib/password/parser/csv/CsvPasswordsFileParser.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/password-parser-csv/src/test/java/mozilla/components/lib/password/parser/csv/CsvPasswordsFileParserTest.kt"], "git_node": "2ee16ed9b00fdc3bacc11e9b09fbc7df56628eb2", "git_parents": ["98927e7fcc6f4c6097f5085a4a37da0b2c2781e7"], "node": "36db12ae35cc9f06d6269de8ca0bf308c264371e", "parents": ["4c09166bf5aa33e48501d2714f5cdf21697a870d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mike a. \u003cmavduevskiy@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087414 - Part 3: Run the CSV passwords parser tests against the known export formats. r=android-reviewers,matt-tighe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339900\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/password-parser-csv/src/test/java/mozilla/components/lib/password/parser/csv/CsvPasswordsFileParserTest.kt"], "git_node": "637ac54c6c08ad5a189d521d7e78d08c549ecbdb", "git_parents": ["2ee16ed9b00fdc3bacc11e9b09fbc7df56628eb2"], "node": "8c451ff1b88f0714899be6ab01d77dfbde8e3a19", "parents": ["36db12ae35cc9f06d6269de8ca0bf308c264371e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mike a. \u003cmavduevskiy@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041577 - Part 1: Add general file importer and parser concept modules. r=android-reviewers,android-build-system-reviewers,matt-tighe\n\nThese modules are intended to unite the functionality of the feature specific modules like\nconcept-bookmarks-file and concept-password-file and replace them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337793\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/.buildconfig.yml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/file-importer/README.md", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/file-importer/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/file-importer/lint-baseline.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/file-importer/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/file-importer/src/main/java/mozilla/components/concept/fileimporter/FileImporter.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/file-importer/src/main/java/mozilla/components/concept/fileimporter/FileImporterError.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/file-importer/src/test/java/mozilla/components/concept/fileimporter/FileImporterErrorTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/file-importer/src/test/resources/robolectric.properties", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/file-parser/README.md", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/file-parser/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/file-parser/lint-baseline.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/file-parser/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/file-parser/src/main/java/mozilla/components/concept/fileparser/FileParser.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/file-parser/src/main/java/mozilla/components/concept/fileparser/FileParserError.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/bookmark-parser-jsoup/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/bookmark-parser-jsoup/src/main/java/mozilla/components/lib/bookmark/parser/jsoup/BookmarksParseError.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/bookmark-parser-jsoup/src/test/java/mozilla/components/lib/bookmark/parser/jsoup/BookmarksParseErrorTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/bookmark-parser-jsoup/src/test/resources/robolectric.properties", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/password-parser-csv/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/password-parser-csv/src/main/java/mozilla/components/lib/password/parser/csv/PasswordsParseError.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/password-parser-csv/src/test/java/mozilla/components/lib/password/parser/csv/PasswordsParseErrorTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/password-parser-csv/src/test/resources/robolectric.properties", "mobile/android/fenix/.buildconfig.yml", "taskcluster/config.yml"], "git_node": "6d1de821c830071a9789b49a5166b9d6cb8f6cd4", "git_parents": ["637ac54c6c08ad5a189d521d7e78d08c549ecbdb"], "node": "94ef83dac9b88d36dac8f16de