ser": "agoloman@mozilla.com"}, "45755": {"changesets": [{"author": "Moritz Beier \u003cmbeier@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1920110 - Move assertSearchStringIsInUrlbar to UrlbarTestUtils and remove resetApplicationProvidedEngines. r=urlbar-reviewers,jteow\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341327\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/tests/UrlbarTestUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_searchTerms.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_searchTerms_backgroundTabs.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_searchTerms_moveTab.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_searchTerms_revert.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_searchTerms_searchMode.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_searchTerms_searchModeSwitcher.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_searchTerms_strings.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_searchTerms_switch_tab.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/head.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-searchMode/browser_searchModeSwitcher_appProvidedEngines.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_persist_searchMode.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/head-common.js"], "git_node": "8c39e0203538b439041ca7db18fed373e9ecb2e0", "git_parents": ["5d45f3e29ea97028031d29a53666028d6305bf93"], "node": "93f843a7618a624120eae89b59d09f011a702215", "parents": ["d1c93b38d715dd337b70fecfcf69312586f8b5e5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082192 - Extract response body streams on the worker thread before the Worker Launcher handoff. r=dom-worker-reviewers,edenchuang\n\nFetchEventOp::ResolvedCallback now takes the body and alternativeBody\nstreams off the InternalResponse itself, rather than leaving that to\nGetIPCSynthesizeResponseArgs on the Worker Launcher thread.\nSynthesizeResponseArgs carries the streams independently of the\nInternalResponse, and SerializeChildToParentInternalResponseBody is\nnow unused and removed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335667\n", "files": ["dom/fetch/InternalResponse.cpp", "dom/fetch/InternalResponse.h", "dom/serviceworkers/FetchEventOpProxyChild.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerOp.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerOpPromise.h"], "git_node": "0f05d7cae0baa612eda38ab478cc00d36882de1e", "git_parents": ["8c39e0203538b439041ca7db18fed373e9ecb2e0"], "node": "30e8caa82cf8de9faa25b4ad3d56f630cd18eb24", "parents": ["93f843a7618a624120eae89b59d09f011a702215"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nhadji \u003cnhadji@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090949 - Clone the sentry, trigger-comm-central, updatebot and release-notify-testrail kinds with Git, r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nBug 2084959 let these kinds be scheduled on Git-backed pushes. This removes the\n`clone-with: hg` that kept their checkout on Mercurial, so they use the default\nGit clone like the other migrated kinds.\n\nsentry and trigger-comm-central run with `checkout: false`, so nothing is cloned\nfor them either way. On Mercurial-backed pushes the line only made them start\nunder run-task-hg; they now start under run-task-git like every migrated kind.\nOn Git-backed pushes their task definitions do not change: the full task graph\nis identical with and without the line on the enterprise-firefox parameter set.\n\nupdatebot and release-notify-testrail check out the tree; their tasks need\nlevel 3 secrets or scopes, so a try run can only show the checkout.\n\nTested on try (push b3dd291c7f97): sentry-mach-release ran green under\nrun-task-git (W3vY8zpAROajeR_tI2TI7g); trigger-comm-central-tb-rust started\nunder run-task-git and stopped at the hook trigger level 1 may not call\n(CL9n_J0XQ_W-SYWGqN7L5Q); updatebot-cron, with its level 3 scopes dropped for\nthe push, cloned Gecko from GitHub and stopped at its secrets\n(VW_rIaAMQWCqerSrh-I7eQ); release-notify-testrail-create-milestone-fenix-beta\ncloned from GitHub and ran its script to the end, short of the level 3 Slack\nscope (bi-OKxW4T32mwobJLV5U7A).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341072\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/release-notify-testrail/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/sentry/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/trigger-comm-central/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/updatebot/kind.yml"], "git_node": "9518f1d0c87d41568b23c84d1cb910d804e2d3fd", "git_parents": ["0f05d7cae0baa612eda38ab478cc00d36882de1e"], "node": "44df76a8f4d8ff5743aa5f5fa8b2f78e465eab6e", "parents": ["30e8caa82cf8de9faa25b4ad3d56f630cd18eb24"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nhadji \u003cnhadji@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090949 - Clone the system-symbols-upload, system-symbols-reprocess and toolchain-symbols-upload kinds with Git, r=taskgraph-reviewers,ahal\n\nThese are the three symbol kinds left on Mercurial. system-symbols-upload and\nsystem-symbols-reprocess lost their scheduling guard in bug 2084959 and only\nkept `clone-with: hg`; toolchain-symbols-upload still had both lines. They now\nuse the default Git clone, the change already made to upload-symbols in\nD334031 (bug 2081108). All three only run from cron, so this also lets the\ntoolchain symbol uploads run on Git-backed repositories.\n\nTested on try (push 6c9f7cf9558b): system-symbols-archlinux-upload-symbols,\nsystem-symbols-archlinux-reprocess-symbols and toolchain-win64-dxc-upload-symbols\nran green, each starting under run-task-git and cloning from the Git repository,\nthe two upload tasks with the upload-symbols sparse profile (tasks\nDTh9xslgTxabht8TcJ8SKg, O-kW-1_cQoWOablxAxp0Iw and BRYXQ3MvTBmMWN1HN2ILkg).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341073\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/system-symbols-reprocess/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/system-symbols-upload/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/toolchain-symbols-upload/kind.yml"], "git_node": "0eed1355525a5a7c45c974dfd60eff54e1474abc", "git_parents": ["9518f1d0c87d41568b23c84d1cb910d804e2d3fd"], "node": "c8b5c13b322c9c7e79626882e236da926ec4f49c", "parents": ["44df76a8f4d8ff5743aa5f5fa8b2f78e465eab6e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lars Eggert \u003clars@eggert.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089558 - Don't fail HTTP/2 streams serviced for writing after END_STREAM or RST_STREAM. r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nFailing them discarded response data still buffered for a slow consumer.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340043\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/Http2Session.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http2StreamBase.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_http2_fin_buffered.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "175dba81dc80d48a135a31e587b9c34b021e425f", "git_parents": ["0eed1355525a5a7c45c974dfd60eff54e1474abc"], "node": "da4135ce814c27ef1e8ba7a86d52d4b5ddd5a669", "parents": ["c8b5c13b322c9c7e79626882e236da926ec4f49c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088457 - Connection Allowlists: Block navigations. r=webdriver-reviewers,whimboo,nika,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339521\n", "files": ["docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "dom/security/ConnectionAllowlistsService.cpp", "dom/security/nsContentSecurityManager.cpp", "remote/shared/listeners/ParentWebProgressListener.sys.mjs", "testing/web-platform/meta/connection-allowlist/tentative/navigation-anchor-new-tab.sub.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/connection-allowlist/tentative/navigation-window-open.sub.window.js.ini", "toolkit/content/aboutNetError.mjs", "toolkit/content/errors/net-errors.mjs", "tools/ts/config/error_list.json", "xpcom/base/ErrorList.py"], "git_node": "270fd9c57d317223430bec3bd30dceb46e5ba1a3", "git_parents": ["175dba81dc80d48a135a31e587b9c34b021e425f"], "node": "5c22d5a2dc2f5a7c25350d0a3c72c28cd0c2725d", "parents": ["da4135ce814c27ef1e8ba7a86d52d4b5ddd5a669"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088457 - Connection Allowlists: Test for the error page being displayed for blocked navigations. r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339522\n", "files": ["dom/security/test/connection-allowlist/browser/browser.toml", "dom/security/test/connection-allowlist/browser/browser_error_page.js", "dom/security/test/connection-allowlist/browser/file_error_page.html", "dom/security/test/connection-allowlist/browser/file_error_page.html^headers^", "dom/security/test/moz.build"], "git_node": "5e7660454e8e5afd4a32c187bea7549ef4d45343", "git_parents": ["270fd9c57d317223430bec3bd30dceb46e5ba1a3"], "node": "9c16f892db8f777238db18338d1670698d18aacc", "parents": ["5c22d5a2dc2f5a7c25350d0a3c72c28cd0c2725d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090097 - Connection Allowlists: Exempt trusted internal schemes. r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340403\n", "files": ["dom/security/ConnectionAllowlistsService.cpp", "dom/security/test/connection-allowlist/browser/browser.toml", "dom/security/test/connection-allowlist/browser/browser_video_document.js", "dom/security/test/connection-allowlist/browser/file_video.webm", "dom/security/test/connection-allowlist/browser/file_video.webm^headers^"], "git_node": "153721947ffc8742044caad69a8787667b6554fe", "git_parents": ["5e7660454e8e5afd4a32c187bea7549ef4d45343"], "node": "423e4c6c8972a0184ab698351e0a9aa23f42fc90", "parents": ["9c16f892db8f777238db18338d1670698d18aacc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090950 - Refresh the Lando token when a try push is refused. r=sheehan,conduit-reviewers\n\nLando derives permissions from the groups recorded at login, so a cached\ntoken keeps getting refused after the user's access changes. On a 403, drop\nthe cached token, and if it came from the cache, log in again and retry.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341314\n", "files": ["tools/tryselect/lando.py", "tools/tryselect/test/test_lando_api.py"], "git_node": "c264b9c5657e7a331a4fe90be50750fa28008538", "git_parents": ["153721947ffc8742044caad69a8787667b6554fe"], "node": "61519993ac138b81f5b8df14a080200b60b2ef78", "parents": ["423e4c6c8972a0184ab698351e0a9aa23f42fc90"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ed Lee \u003cedilee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090256 - introduce aiwindow agents for newer best practices r=omarg,ai4dev-reviewers,tetchart,marco\n\ngenerated from 25 minutes of opus 5.5\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340481\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/AGENTS.md"], "git_node": "87d5e5d33392d64e758b5e4e5853ae6eadb20bf0", "git_parents": ["c264b9c5657e7a331a4fe90be50750fa28008538"], "node": "1e298e43c3ca90a671e79b6629a56e19304e478f", "parents": ["61519993ac138b81f5b8df14a080200b60b2ef78"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085197: Return null for missing MAR items. r=yjuglaret,application-update-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338608\n", "files": ["modules/libmar/src/mar_read.c", "modules/libmar/tests/TestMARFindItem.cpp", "modules/libmar/tests/moz.build", "testing/cppunittest.toml"], "git_node": "cc444fdfb42aae0aa28d42d7eef2814cfba8100a", "git_parents": ["87d5e5d33392d64e758b5e4e5853ae6eadb20bf0"], "node": "15ddfd533cd743382a787cd239ef922ed8d83e07", "parents": ["1e298e43c3ca90a671e79b6629a56e19304e478f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mcarare \u003c48995920+mcarare@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091401 - Simplify coroutine handling in HomeScreen, BrowserFragment and LockObserver. r=android-reviewers,giorga\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341366\n", "files": ["mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/focus/biometrics/LockObserver.kt", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/focus/fragment/BrowserFragment.kt", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/focus/shortcut/HomeScreen.kt", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/focus/shortcut/HomeScreenTest.kt"], "git_node": "50d56b69ad608147e4d06f908dd9af1111be2358", "git_parents": ["cc444fdfb42aae0aa28d42d7eef2814cfba8100a"], "node": "6685b1db66159fb0cfc974064f1ec1c2ea536258", "parents": ["15ddfd533cd743382a787cd239ef922ed8d83e07"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1920110 - Move assertSearchStringIsInUrlbar to UrlbarTestUtils and remove resetApplicationProvidedEngines. r=urlbar-reviewers,jteow\" for causing bc failures @browser_persist_searchMode.js.\n\nThis reverts commit 8c39e0203538b439041ca7db18fed373e9ecb2e0.\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/tests/UrlbarTestUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_searchTerms.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_searchTerms_backgroundTabs.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_searchTerms_moveTab.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_searchTerms_revert.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_searchTerms_searchMode.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_searchTerms_searchModeSwitcher.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_searchTerms_strings.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/browser_searchTerms_switch_tab.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarInput/head.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-searchMode/browser_searchModeSwitcher_appProvidedEngines.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_persist_searchMode.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/head-common.js"], "git_node": "2ba7dc6726308da8d2106fbb4e63434920df9697", "git_parents": ["50d56b69ad608147e4d06f908dd9af1111be2358"], "node": "99cb731685e60d4c037f1ff293a747cc44e80f48", "parents": ["6685b1db66159fb0cfc974064f1ec1c2ea536258"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Banner \u003cstandard8@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087174 - When restyling searches in urlbar history, ignore the partner code parameter. r=daleharvey,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341361\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderPlaces.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_search_engine_restyle.js", "toolkit/components/search/SearchEngine.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/search/SearchService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/search/tests/xpcshell/test_parseSubmissionURL.js"], "git_node": "4482a4337e0b2cd2acec404190211e41c07b2918", "git_parents": ["2ba7dc6726308da8d2106fbb4e63434920df9697"], "node": "5293ed24797c3593d089aa876706baea0b076375", "parents": ["99cb731685e60d4c037f1ff293a747cc44e80f48"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dmitry Gozman \u003cdgozman@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2044428 - Don't shut down the worker script loader while a script is being evaluated. r=dom-worker-reviewers,edenchuang\n\nProcessPendingRequests() removes a request from mLoadedRequests before\nevaluating it, so AllScriptsExecuted() returns true for the whole of\nEvaluateScript() even though the loader is still busy. If the worker is\ncancelled meanwhile, the StrongWorkerRef callback runs TryShutdown(),\nwhich shuts the loader down and nulls mWorkerRef underneath\nEvaluateScript(), which then crashes dereferencing it.\n\nThis happens when JS runs inside JS::Compile(). For example,\na Debugger.onNewScript hook runs on the worker thread\nand processes the worker's control runnables through the interrupt\ncallback, so terminating the worker while its script is being compiled\nreliably hits it.\n\nFix: track in-flight evaluations in mEvaluatingScriptCount and have\nAllScriptsExecuted() take it into account, so that the shutdown is\ndeferred to the TryShutdown() at the end of ProcessPendingRequests().\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335065\n", "files": ["dom/workers/ScriptLoader.cpp", "dom/workers/ScriptLoader.h", "dom/workers/test/WorkerDebugger_terminate_in_onNewScript_debugger.js", "dom/workers/test/WorkerDebugger_terminate_in_onNewScript_worker.js", "dom/workers/test/chrome.toml", "dom/workers/test/test_WorkerDebugger_terminate_in_onNewScript.xhtml"], "git_node": "6480f784b9e59d7199d8bad0591a70e8a48949a3", "git_parents": ["4482a4337e0b2cd2acec404190211e41c07b2918"], "node": "65a52245b50f5d9668cce86afb345b644ff3b239", "parents": ["5293ed24797c3593d089aa876706baea0b076375"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Hynson \u003cmhynson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077160 - Fix browser_tab_preview.js tabGroupPanelVerticalOffsetOptions failure - Simplifies the logic to show the preview panel - Ensures horizontal tabs test runs with CIs tagged vertical-tabs r=tabbrowser-reviewers,jsudiaman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334614\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tab_preview.js"], "git_node": "dd99b4334a5e684fcac587bf52d49ee096e7fc1c", "git_parents": ["6480f784b9e59d7199d8bad0591a70e8a48949a3"], "node": "1a9c201887fed9ddc47e8f9ce2cbfed59bbeeb66", "parents": ["65a52245b50f5d9668cce86afb345b644ff3b239"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083276 - Update metadata for /encrypted-media/* tests.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341411\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-keystatuses-multiple-sessions.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-clear-encrypted.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-multisession.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-playduration-keystatus.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "0b1890e589f13e2aa595981365f608474f67789f", "git_parents": ["dd99b4334a5e684fcac587bf52d49ee096e7fc1c"], "node": "a09659662ac0fe852f23d07c65ebd933d8be8f7d", "parents": ["1a9c201887fed9ddc47e8f9ce2cbfed59bbeeb66"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Luong \u003cgabriel.luong@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091286 - Reduce the initial delay of the Collections to Tab Groups migration worker to 15 seconds r=android-reviewers,npoon\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341260\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/collections/migration/CollectionsToTabGroupsMigrationWorker.kt"], "git_node": "9967e3b8d85e56c127e6486c23d9a2a3eaf93193", "git_parents": ["0b1890e589f13e2aa595981365f608474f67789f"], "node": "6bae6070b0f2c84609dde94aa01f2af08c7b2d7c", "parents": ["a09659662ac0fe852f23d07c65ebd933d8be8f7d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Luong \u003cgabriel.luong@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090856 - Migrate collections to tab groups from oldest to newest r=android-reviewers,npoon\n\n- Collections are stored newest first, so the oldest collection got the last theme in the cycle and the tab groups were listed in the reverse order of the collections\n- Migrate the oldest collection first so the themes cycle from Yellow and the tab groups keep the collections' order\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341254\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/collections/migration/CollectionsToTabGroupsMigration.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/collections/migration/CollectionsToTabGroupsMigrationTest.kt"], "git_node": "1752f7b171316e5233ce487929e2cdd8ff3b5ccc", "git_parents": ["9967e3b8d85e56c127e6486c23d9a2a3eaf93193"], "node": "bee64e571bcdcb7ab9f5c5a382b9c5ca1b838873", "parents": ["6bae6070b0f2c84609dde94aa01f2af08c7b2d7c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "scottdowne \u003csdowne@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2019460 - Newtab remove discoverystream.enabled pref, and all branching logic, and keep the true paths r=mconley,ini\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D284941\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/newtab/test/browser/abouthomecache/browser.toml", "browser/components/newtab/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/extensions/newtab/common/Reducers.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/docs/v2-system-addon/preferences.md", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/ActivityStream.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/DiscoveryStreamFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/PrefsFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TopStoriesFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_activation_window.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_context_menu_link_open.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_customize_menu_content.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_discovery_card.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_discovery_render.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_highlights_section.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_newtab_last_LinkMenu.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_ohttpImages.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/ActivityStream.test.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/DiscoveryStreamFeed.test.js", "netwerk/test/browser/browser_wallpaper_protocol_library.js", "testing/profiles/common/user.js"], "git_node": "6046b414b85518a278073695f309710cc0accd47", "git_parents": ["1752f7b171316e5233ce487929e2cdd8ff3b5ccc"], "node": "eced9af38b828ca25ac12770a2a2a442ae0be8f4", "parents": ["bee64e571bcdcb7ab9f5c5a382b9c5ca1b838873"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mitchell Plyler \u003cmlplyler@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090204 - Move smart shortcuts updates to its own update interval r=thecount\n\nSmart shortcuts and therefore organic topsites shares a tick with other sufaces, and that tick is currently set at 5 minutes. Based on anecdotal feedback and to save some compute, we want to test slowing down the rerank rate while keeping the other surface ticks untouched. This patch adds a interval check to newtabtrainhopconfig. If the cause of the topsites refresh call is a system tick or a sponsored topsites refresh, we check if the interval has passed since the last organic topsite refersh. For all other refresh call types or if the interval has passed, we rerank as before, and otherwise, we used a cached ranking. There has always been a race condition where multiple triggers could cause a topsite rerank and this could cause the cache to misalign from what is sent to newtab. This becomes more important as the refresh rate is potentially slowed down. We solve for this race by only caching a shortcuts state that is sent to newtab. There is also a case where a topsite appears in the cached list but not in the current eligible list. We solve for this case by infilling the best eligible based on the cached ranking.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340414\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/SmartShortcutsRanker/RankShortcuts.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TopSitesFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_ShortcutRanker.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_TopSitesFeed.js"], "git_node": "f906d0840ae375112550f42542562b9828a37eae", "git_parents": ["6046b414b85518a278073695f309710cc0accd47"], "node": "92cda6f7aa0b1b963fbef8a9715337d3b61e6eaf", "parents": ["eced9af38b828ca25ac12770a2a2a442ae0be8f4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090955 - Fix clang-tidy lint for dom/base r=dom-core-reviewers,hsivonen\n\nHeader is not self-compilable, and a constructor can use the\ncompiler-generated version.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341368\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsNodeSupportsWeakRefTearoff.cpp", "dom/base/nsNodeSupportsWeakRefTearoff.h"], "git_node": "bedd57cad3a5a34be9816fb4036ed566f86d9637", "git_parents": ["f906d0840ae375112550f42542562b9828a37eae"], "node": "ff8876f524fd2dee3ac600b73cd96f088f6b85df", "parents": ["92cda6f7aa0b1b963fbef8a9715337d3b61e6eaf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090955 - Fix clang-tidy lint for dom/bindings/BindingDeclarations.h r=dom-core-reviewers,vhilla\n\nUse compiler-generated version for default constructor.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341369\n", "files": ["dom/bindings/BindingDeclarations.h"], "git_node": "a87bba095ed16d5309bb4f9a5ddfb0b3d8af39cb", "git_parents": ["bedd57cad3a5a34be9816fb4036ed566f86d9637"], "node": "b1084d980b6555dc2f66d5f98d725b4f7ea70ab7", "parents": ["ff8876f524fd2dee3ac600b73cd96f088f6b85df"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090955 - Fix clang-tidy lint for dom/bindings/TypedArray.h r=dom-core-reviewers,hsivonen\n\nUse std::remove_cvref_t instead of std::remove_ref_t and\nstd::remove_cv_t\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341370\n", "files": ["dom/bindings/TypedArray.h"], "git_node": "6d445a94abbbe7498dd863d383db303b77651094", "git_parents": ["a87bba095ed16d5309bb4f9a5ddfb0b3d8af39cb"], "node": "a8b9bb2ce27cdd814b588636f2bfd7a1dbc4e2bb", "parents": ["b1084d980b6555dc2f66d5f98d725b4f7ea70ab7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090955 - Fix clang-tidy lint on dom/file/uri/BlobURLProtocolHandler.* r=dom-core-reviewers,vhilla\n\nActually just making the ehader self-compilable\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341371\n", "files": ["dom/file/uri/BlobURLProtocolHandler.cpp", "dom/file/uri/BlobURLProtocolHandler.h"], "git_node": "a9d0444b20fb2395a567be8c23e52fd59851d139", "git_parents": ["6d445a94abbbe7498dd863d383db303b77651094"], "node": "914bf1e3b4e1b1dbccdf17cbc7908c72f49a177d", "parents": ["a8b9bb2ce27cdd814b588636f2bfd7a1dbc4e2bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Janika \u003cjneuberger@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084690 - P1. Move the debug settings of the desktop mozconfigs into common-debug r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,enterprise-reviewers,ahochheiden,gerard-majax\n\nLike common-opt, common-debug holds the settings of a debug build without\nthe branding, so that builds with a different branding (e.g. enterprise builds) can\nshare them. No functional change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338534\n", "files": ["browser/config/mozconfigs/linux64/common-debug", "browser/config/mozconfigs/linux64/debug", "browser/config/mozconfigs/macosx64/common-debug", "browser/config/mozconfigs/macosx64/debug", "browser/config/mozconfigs/win64-aarch64/common-debug", "browser/config/mozconfigs/win64-aarch64/debug", "browser/config/mozconfigs/win64/common-debug", "browser/config/mozconfigs/win64/debug"], "git_node": "00e859492fa8e9bf6b7193fcfff44f59f28750bd", "git_parents": ["a9d0444b20fb2395a567be8c23e52fd59851d139"], "node": "152a0465ab10f4e66bfa70f95a8a5d573561d763", "parents": ["914bf1e3b4e1b1dbccdf17cbc7908c72f49a177d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088107 - Set the Widevine service certificate with correct property name with MediaCodec NDK. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338776\n", "files": ["dom/media/eme/mediadrm/MediaDrmRemoteCDMParent.cpp", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/encrypted-media/drm-set-server-certificate.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/encrypted-media/drm-set-server-certificate.https.html"], "git_node": "3098bb04bbb962ebe4c4bb4c44761604ba7548d5", "git_parents": ["00e859492fa8e9bf6b7193fcfff44f59f28750bd"], "node": "cd306e70f357a5cb46132fc5939428149018559b", "parents": ["152a0465ab10f4e66bfa70f95a8a5d573561d763"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Exploding-Joysticks \u003cExplodingJoysticks@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1831048 - Part 15: Fix 233 'misc-unused-parameters' warnings under /editor r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nhttps://clang.llvm.org/extra/clang-tidy/checks/misc/unused-parameters.html\n\nEverything found by ./mach static-analysis was manually inspected and changed if needed.\n\nAmend: Some small fixes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338525\n", "files": ["editor/composer/ComposerCommandsUpdater.cpp", "editor/composer/nsEditingSession.cpp", "editor/libeditor/AutoClonedRangeArray.cpp", "editor/libeditor/CSSEditUtils.cpp", "editor/libeditor/EditorBase.cpp", "editor/libeditor/EditorCommands.cpp", "editor/libeditor/EditorCommands.h", "editor/libeditor/EditorEventListener.cpp", "editor/libeditor/EditorEventListener.h", "editor/libeditor/EditorLineBreak.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditSubActionHandler.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditor.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditor.h", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditorCommands.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditorDeleteHandler.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditorDocumentCommands.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditorMutationObserver.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLStyleEditor.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLTableEditor.cpp", "editor/libeditor/InternetCiter.cpp", "editor/libeditor/MoveSiblingsTransaction.cpp", "editor/libeditor/TextEditor.cpp", "editor/libeditor/TextEditorDataTransfer.cpp", "editor/spellchecker/EditorSpellCheck.cpp", "editor/spellchecker/TextServicesDocument.cpp", "editor/txmgr/tests/TestTXMgr.cpp"], "git_node": "4a49a8bb0d00df4f68d1dd8a7d037eac7529f7cc", "git_parents": ["3098bb04bbb962ebe4c4bb4c44761604ba7548d5"], "node": "e27b57cf56c43d1d1ce18f40a07191fa15a0442e", "parents": ["cd306e70f357a5cb46132fc5939428149018559b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2019460 - Newtab remove discoverystream.enabled pref, and all branching logic, and keep the true paths r=mconley,ini\" for causing bc failures @browser_policy_firefoxhome.js.\n\nThis reverts commit 6046b414b85518a278073695f309710cc0accd47.\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/newtab/test/browser/abouthomecache/browser.toml", "browser/components/newtab/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/extensions/newtab/common/Reducers.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/docs/v2-system-addon/preferences.md", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/ActivityStream.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/DiscoveryStreamFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/PrefsFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TopStoriesFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_activation_window.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_context_menu_link_open.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_customize_menu_content.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_discovery_card.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_discovery_render.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_highlights_section.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_newtab_last_LinkMenu.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_ohttpImages.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/ActivityStream.test.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/DiscoveryStreamFeed.test.js", "netwerk/test/browser/browser_wallpaper_protocol_library.js", "testing/profiles/common/user.js"], "git_node": "9bf32c6226abd7499855200c1bb4f3545b450d3d", "git_parents": ["4a49a8bb0d00df4f68d1dd8a7d037eac7529f7cc"], "node": "d1b3ec99e489ec611b8413a8e9dd73839d04a095", "parents": ["e27b57cf56c43d1d1ce18f40a07191fa15a0442e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Pages \u003cjpages@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052688 - Add testcase. r=rhunt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311220\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/tail-calls/active-trap-code-lifetime.js"], "git_node": "ebe02a4df8ed34dec2cbdb173bf29a877d5ffe48", "git_parents": ["9bf32c6226abd7499855200c1bb4f3545b450d3d"], "node": "7ea773fabd924c7ccb008c058480d8acac5d3788", "parents": ["d1b3ec99e489ec611b8413a8e9dd73839d04a095"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091232 - Give copy_cached_dep tasks eager cache indexes. r=taskgraph-reviewers,jcristau\n\ntaskgraph's add_optimization adds the completion index routes and the index-search optimization but not the\neager_indexes attribute that add_eager_cache_index_tasks reads; only the gecko_taskgraph wrapper sets it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341214\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/python.toml", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/test_transforms_copy_cached_dep.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/copy_cached_dep.py"], "git_node": "0b093b060417e5ce0a5bd22bb20e9299bc2a0cb3", "git_parents": ["ebe02a4df8ed34dec2cbdb173bf29a877d5ffe48"], "node": "62fe737b0e2dba6c5d21317558f7db8485255af5", "parents": ["7ea773fabd924c7ccb008c058480d8acac5d3788"], "tags": []}, {"author": "acreskeyMoz \u003cacreskey@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076691 - Drop speculation-rules prefetch records on Clear-Site-Data \"prefetchCache\". r=sunil,jjaschke,avandolder,manuel\n\n\"cache\" and \"*\" also clear them, per the prefetch spec. Documents are matched\non their partitioned principal so third-party responses don't clear them.\nSpec: https://github.com/WICG/nav-speculation/blob/55f0c9565659d4af2fda2cb93060c17a04feb7fd/prefetch.bs#L808-L834\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335353\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/PrefetchLog.h", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/clear-prefetch-cache-after-clear-site-data-cache.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prefetch/clear-prefetch-cache-after-clear-site-data-cache.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prefetch/clear-prefetch-cache-after-clear-site-data-cross-site.tentative.https.html", "toolkit/components/clearsitedata/ClearSiteData.cpp", "toolkit/components/clearsitedata/ClearSiteData.h"], "git_node": "5a6630669c3acbcf8173f2e2b27daf9e078ee126", "git_parents": ["0b093b060417e5ce0a5bd22bb20e9299bc2a0cb3"], "node": "5b119b26dc1b5707296ab735d623d678496e98cc", "parents": ["62fe737b0e2dba6c5d21317558f7db8485255af5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090955 - Fix clang-tidy analysis of js/public/Proxy.h r=spidermonkey-reviewers,mgaudet\n\nMaking a default constructor compiler-generated.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341372\n", "files": ["js/public/Proxy.h"], "git_node": "e96d54641b6d181814eec6399a2ce52413078da0", "git_parents": ["5a6630669c3acbcf8173f2e2b27daf9e078ee126"], "node": "8a2632811c26314f37bd06febdc134efda134b60", "parents": ["5b119b26dc1b5707296ab735d623d678496e98cc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091252 - Annotate a test as passing.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341482\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-shadow/part/interaction-with-nested-pseudo-class.html.ini"], "git_node": "69a11bc3619c0097882b51fbffd64f6844489948", "git_parents": ["e96d54641b6d181814eec6399a2ce52413078da0"], "node": "195000301d0352b2d414525a715e0e52b8189cf0", "parents": ["8a2632811c26314f37bd06febdc134efda134b60"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eitan Isaacson \u003ceitan@monotonous.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088679 - Refactor atk roles backward compat. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,morgan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339290\n", "files": ["accessible/atk/AccessibleWrap.cpp"], "git_node": "cb82c445d36a51fa4243bf86e9b1ecf7f7d7577d", "git_parents": ["69a11bc3619c0097882b51fbffd64f6844489948"], "node": "8774a99306068ecde375e83228b60c214cc24421", "parents": ["195000301d0352b2d414525a715e0e52b8189cf0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ting-Yu Lin \u003ctlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088751 - Make the fullscreen element and its ::backdrop cover scrollbar-gutter. r=layout-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nPer the CSSWG resolution [1], top-layer fixed-pos boxes cover the root\nscrollbars and scrollbar-gutter. This patch does it only for the fullscreen\nelement and its ::backdrop to fix the webcompat issue in Bug 2061066.\n\n`scrollbar-gutter-fullscreen-003.html` covers the change in `nsDisplayList.cpp`.\n\n[1] https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/9904#issuecomment-2161022451\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340243\n", "files": ["layout/generic/AbsoluteContainingBlock.cpp", "layout/generic/ReflowInput.cpp", "layout/generic/ViewportFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/ViewportFrame.h", "layout/painting/nsDisplayList.cpp", "layout/style/RestyleManager.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/scrollbar-gutter-fullscreen-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scrollbar-gutter-fullscreen-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scrollbar-gutter-fullscreen-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scrollbar-gutter-fullscreen-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scrollbar-gutter-fullscreen-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scrollbar-gutter-fullscreen-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scrollbar-gutter-fullscreen-004-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scrollbar-gutter-fullscreen-004.html"], "git_node": "cc108a570c6ea93d975aac0e870c13bc1a5b3229", "git_parents": ["cb82c445d36a51fa4243bf86e9b1ecf7f7d7577d"], "node": "313cb6958ccbe549c16d5ae8cf57cc4e72c34637", "parents": ["8774a99306068ecde375e83228b60c214cc24421"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Holbert \u003cdholbert@cs.stanford.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088486 - Make Selection::Repaint do its iteration over a copy of the ranges instead of the main array. r=jjaschke\n\nOur call to SelectFrames can mutate mStyledRanges, including changing its\nlength. So, to avoid walking off the end of the array and aborting, it's safer\nto iterate over a copy of the array, just as we do in\nSelection::DeleteFromDocument().\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341481\n", "files": ["dom/base/Selection.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-highlight-api/crashtests/firefox-bug-2088486.html"], "git_node": "e8cabcfefea7be14e3b0dd8bdebc5b93283ddd51", "git_parents": ["cc108a570c6ea93d975aac0e870c13bc1a5b3229"], "node": "a421cf5578535a13687dcc15f6067344e30931f2", "parents": ["313cb6958ccbe549c16d5ae8cf57cc4e72c34637"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088122 - Part 1. Remove the previous key request that Android before 10 appends to a key request. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338780\n", "files": ["dom/media/eme/ProtobufReader.cpp", "dom/media/eme/ProtobufReader.h", "dom/media/eme/mediadrm/MediaDrmRemoteCDMParent.cpp", "dom/media/eme/moz.build", "dom/media/gtest/TestProtobufReader.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "000dc3541666c72bc74071979f51c2d4c6377aa6", "git_parents": ["e8cabcfefea7be14e3b0dd8bdebc5b93283ddd51"], "node": "04c75f7c914d261966f8c2adc98c245a7e4b1712", "parents": ["a421cf5578535a13687dcc15f6067344e30931f2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088122 - Part 2. Handle an empty session ID from AMediaDrm_openSession before Android 12. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nThe NDK before Android 12 reports success without a session ID when the\nplugin fails to open one.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338781\n", "files": ["dom/media/eme/mediadrm/MediaDrmRemoteCDMParent.cpp"], "git_node": "7d798181b90b67a33d5613526ddad8a3178b77f7", "git_parents": ["000dc3541666c72bc74071979f51c2d4c6377aa6"], "node": "6d35a74a03fa2742125a1ecbd66b04d952fa8fb6", "parents": ["04c75f7c914d261966f8c2adc98c245a7e4b1712"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088122 - Part 3. Route key request events without a session ID before Android 10. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nThe NDK before Android 10 does not report the session of an event. Use\nthe sessions that were given a service certificate, in order.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338782\n", "files": ["dom/media/eme/ProtobufReader.cpp", "dom/media/eme/ProtobufReader.h", "dom/media/eme/mediadrm/MediaDrmRemoteCDMParent.cpp", "dom/media/eme/mediadrm/MediaDrmRemoteCDMParent.h", "dom/media/gtest/TestProtobufReader.cpp"], "git_node": "5c0cfc01eacfb3266e32e834e429768c0feb53b0", "git_parents": ["7d798181b90b67a33d5613526ddad8a3178b77f7"], "node": "c886ed61fb1d7dc117fd7ef48d46b76a1a5349d7", "parents": ["6d35a74a03fa2742125a1ecbd66b04d952fa8fb6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088122 - Part 4. Report the content keys in a license as usable on Android before 29. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nThe key status listener needs Android 29.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338783\n", "files": ["dom/media/eme/ProtobufReader.cpp", "dom/media/eme/ProtobufReader.h", "dom/media/eme/mediadrm/MediaDrmRemoteCDMParent.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestProtobufReader.cpp"], "git_node": "0c7cb9f61343d49dbdb632bf5d5edbea9e0a8ef9", "git_parents": ["5c0cfc01eacfb3266e32e834e429768c0feb53b0"], "node": "11ac1ed7d86e0530e15331644264e97ccb8352d6", "parents": ["c886ed61fb1d7dc117fd7ef48d46b76a1a5349d7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan Varga \u003cjvarga@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086032 - Add security.csp.url-hashes.enabled and security.csp.strict-dynamic-url.enabled prefs; r=tschuster\n\nGate support for CSP url hashes (url-hash-source) and the 'strict-dynamic-url'\nkeyword separately. How url sources are spelled is still being discussed, and\nurl hashes may be replaced by another kind of url source, while\n'strict-dynamic-url' doesn't depend on that and can stay enabled. Both prefs\nare disabled by default. The next patch adds a CI variant which enables them,\nand the following patches implement the features behind them.\n\nSpec PR: https://github.com/w3c/webappsec-csp/pull/784\nIssue: https://github.com/w3c/webappsec-csp/issues/826\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337042\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "60ff515e929471c6a59fa257413b8b63a085e707", "git_parents": ["0c7cb9f61343d49dbdb632bf5d5edbea9e0a8ef9"], "node": "9c5795aedd1164dc31bc310825b0f6f96c7f254e", "parents": ["11ac1ed7d86e0530e15331644264e97ccb8352d6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "kpatenio \u003ckpatenio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055883 - show pre-tabs spacer for tiled windows on Linux to ease window dragging r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341049\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/browser-shared.css"], "git_node": "d55027704632d40a6d7de8b5239f941e5a3f480d", "git_parents": ["60ff515e929471c6a59fa257413b8b63a085e707"], "node": "2f4913d51054c32d16da441af4bfa8a61f3648ab", "parents": ["9c5795aedd1164dc31bc310825b0f6f96c7f254e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "unifolia \u003cjlewis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088305 - Add an aitab-image component for Smart Page images. r=omarg\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340492\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-image/aitab-image.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-image/aitab-image.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-image/aitab-image.stories.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-page.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/jar.mn", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aitab_blocks.js"], "git_node": "0b98491ca9bbe0dc3fe8e70ec595461a676763b8", "git_parents": ["d55027704632d40a6d7de8b5239f941e5a3f480d"], "node": "89284aeb9ecfb08d33e10b4de1ef4721da4741d9", "parents": ["2f4913d51054c32d16da441af4bfa8a61f3648ab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Helena \u003chballent@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088620 - Tighten macOS GPU sandbox windowserver access. r=mac-reviewers,sandbox-reviewers,haik,bradwerth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339271\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLContext.cpp", "dom/canvas/moz.build", "dom/canvas/test/webgl-mochitest/mochitest-no-angle.toml", "dom/canvas/test/webgl-mochitest/mochitest.toml", "dom/canvas/test/webgl-mochitest/test_backends.html", "dom/canvas/test/webgl-mochitest/test_backends_no_angle.html", "dom/canvas/test/webgl-mochitest/test_pixel_pack_buffer.html", "gfx/ipc/GPUProcessHost.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxPlatform.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "security/sandbox/common/test/SandboxTestingChildTests.h", "security/sandbox/mac/Sandbox.mm", "security/sandbox/mac/SandboxPolicyGPU.h"], "git_node": "6497019f0eed62107d659b209ad5675bec07690d", "git_parents": ["0b98491ca9bbe0dc3fe8e70ec595461a676763b8"], "node": "55cd873272487fd4dca61f9748217fe0050a8481", "parents": ["89284aeb9ecfb08d33e10b4de1ef4721da4741d9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi Lee \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089497 - Skip stored credit cards that cannot be decrypted when looking for a duplicate of a submitted card. r=joschmidt,credential-management-reviewers\n\nOne unreadable card failed the whole duplicate search, so the submit handler\nrejected and no save doorhanger was shown, leaving the user no way to replace\nthe broken card.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340262\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_creditCard_decryption_failure.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_rust_autofill_credit_card_adapter.js", "toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillStorageBase.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/RustAutofillCreditCardStorage.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "1be9dea5580f028952b3f2833cab32338a4746f4", "git_parents": ["6497019f0eed62107d659b209ad5675bec07690d"], "node": "5a3e1d6d5e9c893d5f16eed3db6e0ef02b041b38", "parents": ["55cd873272487fd4dca61f9748217fe0050a8481"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2085197: Return null for missing MAR items. r=yjuglaret,application-update-reviewers\" for causing cppunit failures.\n\nThis reverts commit cc444fdfb42aae0aa28d42d7eef2814cfba8100a.\n", "files": ["modules/libmar/src/mar_read.c", "modules/libmar/tests/TestMARFindItem.cpp", "modules/libmar/tests/moz.build", "testing/cppunittest.toml"], "git_node": "8a0837dcc10795eda3dc9c7cbac6224fc1f3a88b", "git_parents": ["1be9dea5580f028952b3f2833cab32338a4746f4"], "node": "8c0ce4a2161b0ee98b6154793d701b334a93b4d2", "parents": ["5a3e1d6d5e9c893d5f16eed3db6e0ef02b041b38"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrej Glavic \u003caglavic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090309 - Remove the WebPageTest layer from mozperftest. r=perftest-reviewers,mozperftest-reviewers,kshampur\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340525\n", "files": ["python/mozperftest/mozperftest/argparser.py", "python/mozperftest/mozperftest/perfdocs/templates/index.md", "python/mozperftest/mozperftest/system/__init__.py", "python/mozperftest/mozperftest/test/__init__.py", "python/mozperftest/mozperftest/test/webpagetest.py", "python/mozperftest/mozperftest/tests/data/WPT_fakekey.txt", "python/mozperftest/mozperftest/tests/data/samples/test_perftest_WPT_init_file.js", "python/mozperftest/mozperftest/tests/support.py", "python/mozperftest/mozperftest/tests/test_webpagetest.py", "python/mozperftest/mozperftest/utils.py", "python/mozperftest/perfdocs/config.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/perftest/linux.yml", "testing/perfdocs/generated/index.md", "testing/perfdocs/generated/mozperftest.md", "testing/performance/perftest.toml", "testing/performance/perftest_WPT_chrome_init_file.js", "testing/performance/perftest_WPT_firefox_init_file.js"], "git_node": "0f68825485f8d26c83c431dbccafa4c8e7917e01", "git_parents": ["8a0837dcc10795eda3dc9c7cbac6224fc1f3a88b"], "node": "e6569d4a3dd1eb0ed82de124d2274ec4a21f68a3", "parents": ["8c0ce4a2161b0ee98b6154793d701b334a93b4d2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "hannajones \u003chjones@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059669 - Add gradient for sun theme preview in dark mode r=desktop-theme-reviewers,hjones,mossop\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329974\n", "files": ["browser/components/profiles/tests/browser/browser_edit_profile_theme_picker_test.js", "browser/themes/ThemesList.sys.mjs", "browser/themes/test/unit/test_ThemesList.js", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/test_theme_picker.html"], "git_node": "3c5a69fd8da58f31dbeb7185bc6e0ae86307f939", "git_parents": ["0f68825485f8d26c83c431dbccafa4c8e7917e01"], "node": "7bfcdc939ae31d9b4156fbdb002e1c6b6389615e", "parents": ["e6569d4a3dd1eb0ed82de124d2274ec4a21f68a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cameron Dawson \u003ccameron@dawsoncode.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088612 - Tag backfill and confirm-failure tasks with a manifests scope r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,jcristau\n\nBackfills and confirm-failure retriggers can run a task with only a subset\nof its test manifests under the same label as the full task, so Treeherder\ncannot tell them apart. Add a `manifests` task tag set to \"full\" when the\ninjected manifests match the chunk the task would run on its own push, and\n\"partial\" otherwise. Confirm-failure tasks always run a single manifest and\nare tagged \"partial\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339250\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/actions/backfill.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/actions/confirm_failure.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/test_actions.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/test_actions_backfill.py"], "git_node": "c0c21e85400fb2eb7cd0fa7b2597017e6e060b60", "git_parents": ["3c5a69fd8da58f31dbeb7185bc6e0ae86307f939"], "node": "e3327d9f2ca965e234752a1fd26c56c0085b897d", "parents": ["7bfcdc939ae31d9b4156fbdb002e1c6b6389615e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rolf Rando \u003crrando@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090345 - fix domain scoping bug r=mak,urlbar-reviewers\n\nThis fixes a bug with the optional domain scoping semantic search feature.\n\nBefore\nhttps://cnn.com/world/news would do semantic search only for the keyword 'news'\nWith the fix, it will look for 'world news'\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340556\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderSemanticHistorySearch.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_UrlbarProviderSemanticHistorySearch.js"], "git_node": "7301555587ca1676892852ccbd95231912184a09", "git_parents": ["c0c21e85400fb2eb7cd0fa7b2597017e6e060b60"], "node": "d85387992ecd93f765c724fdf93624b00e9cadd4", "parents": ["e3327d9f2ca965e234752a1fd26c56c0085b897d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrej Glavic \u003caglavic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2015144 - Add the tp6m-essential pageload tests on Android emulators for try. r=perftest-reviewers,kshampur\n\nAdd browsertime-tp6m-essential to the android-em-14-arm64 test set as tier 3\nFenix tasks, without a conditioned profile like the A55s. They don't run on\nany project by default, only when selected on try.\n\nGeckoView and the reference browser haven't been verified on the emulators,\nso limit them to android-hw platforms.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338840\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/browsertime/mobile.yml", "taskcluster/test_configs/test-sets.yml", "testing/perfdocs/generated/raptor.md"], "git_node": "e39301925286e16cf69164d5d304021ca1b0ab0a", "git_parents": ["7301555587ca1676892852ccbd95231912184a09"], "node": "2e0e2316f09161fc1fd477385769003b3b009517", "parents": ["d85387992ecd93f765c724fdf93624b00e9cadd4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087119 - Register and unregister tab notes window listeners without waiting for the database, r=tabbrowser-reviewers,sthompson.\n\nListeners added after the database opened dropped canonical URLs reported\nmeanwhile; removed after it closed, a quick re-enable lost them. TabNotes\ninitializes lazily, so neither waits. Restored tabs are now checked after\nSessionStore.promiseAllWindowsRestored, which the wait covered by chance.\nTabNotes.deinit forgets its init immediately, else a re-enable during the\nclose queries the closing connection; it also closes an in-flight init, and\na new init waits for the close to avoid NS_ERROR_STORAGE_BUSY.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338038\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabnotes/TabNotes.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabnotes/TabNotesController.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "b07c9fb80ba07546a31ff675f7305df97d3a10e0", "git_parents": ["e39301925286e16cf69164d5d304021ca1b0ab0a"], "node": "7b2a343e65e56ad6a907539b7bbe463333d7d747", "parents": ["2e0e2316f09161fc1fd477385769003b3b009517"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Dean-Kawamura \u003cbdk@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091419 - remove old auth state check, r=sfamisa,android-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341434\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/service/firefox-accounts/src/main/java/mozilla/components/service/fxa/AccountStorage.kt"], "git_node": "c8acf33d67e1b60b59f717086571684de7bbd727", "git_parents": ["b07c9fb80ba07546a31ff675f7305df97d3a10e0"], "node": "a3ba77b2285dd436b3587e3bc5a40e961eb99b2d", "parents": ["7b2a343e65e56ad6a907539b7bbe463333d7d747"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Adam Vandolder \u003cavandolder@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089815 - Delay reporting speculation rules parse errors until it is safe to run script. r=dom-core-reviewers,jjaschke\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341492\n", "files": ["dom/base/SpeculationRuleSet.cpp"], "git_node": "03895568676d9522c4f2c752311924209eaccd2d", "git_parents": ["c8acf33d67e1b60b59f717