 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nml -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nmr -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nms -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nmy -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nnb-NO -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nne-NP -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nnl -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nnn-NO -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\noc -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\npa-IN -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\npl -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\npt-BR -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\npt-PT -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nrm -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nro -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nru -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nsk -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nsl -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nson -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nsq -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nsr -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nsv-SE -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nta -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nte -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nth -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\ntl -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\ntr -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\ntrs -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nuk -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nur -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nuz -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nvi -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nwo -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nxh -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nzam -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nzh-CN -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\nzh-TW -\u003e 4dbb293af5820231d85747677e494dfa26b7aacc\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "a733401bf4d546410d2cd768c870ebb7defb652f", "git_parents": ["a5e4a2891f1856a1ad3f092d5c623a5bf27f2124"], "node": "059756d1d5f0ee4120a2f844ab0e7dc43ebe0b7e", "parents": ["4f3f4e2581cafc84730a1811be5f5f3262ba347a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087950 - Make rbx the x64 JIT scratch register and move R1 to r11. r=jandem\n\nScratchReg is r11, so every scratch use that is not already 64-bit pays a REX\nbyte for the register number alone. It is among the most used registers in\nBaseline and Ion code. rbx is the only low register without a fixed role in\nthe JIT ABI, apart from being Baseline's R1, so swap the two: ScratchReg\nbecomes rbx, and R1, CallTempReg2, ABINonArgReg1, WasmJitEntryReturnScratch\nand the temporaries that the trampolines, the x64 div/mod helpers and the\nwasm catch-handler path hard-code as rbx move to r11.\n\nMeasured on JetStream 3 in the x86-64 shell from a dump of every JIT code\nblob, per instruction to factor out run-to-run differences in what gets\ncompiled: Baseline code is 0.80% smaller (1.01% in total bytes, 109.1 MB -\u003e\n108.0 MB), Ion code 0.6-1.1% smaller and WasmBaseline code 1.06% smaller.\nWasmIon code grows 0.29% (--no-threads, 85.3 MB) now that rbx is no longer\nallocatable there, and the trampolines grow 1-2% because R1 now needs REX.\n\nThe codegen tests that name the scratch register now expect rbx. With rbx no\nlonger allocatable in wasm code, Ion drops the extra move in the Linux\nselect test and uses rsi where the Windows-only select test expected rbx.\n\nrbx is callee-saved, so SavedNonVolatileRegisters now adds it on x64:\nregexp code is called directly from C++ and clobbers it as ScratchReg,\nbut it dropped out of the saved set once it was no longer allocatable.\n\nFound via x86lint.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338644\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/binop-divrem-with-constant-x64-ion-codegen.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/binop-x64-ion-codegen.js", "js/src/jit/RegisterSets.h", "js/src/jit/x64/Assembler-x64.h", "js/src/jit/x64/MacroAssembler-x64.cpp", "js/src/jit/x64/SharedICRegisters-x64.h", "js/src/jit/x64/Trampoline-x64.cpp", "js/src/jit/x86-shared/Architecture-x86-shared.h", "js/src/jit/x86-shared/MacroAssembler-x86-shared.cpp"], "git_node": "dcc99f83daa5cabad099a42e2d694e09e01e22aa", "git_parents": ["a733401bf4d546410d2cd768c870ebb7defb652f"], "node": "38a84ec8bfbdd9a80b81970299caebc6cd948f05", "parents": ["059756d1d5f0ee4120a2f844ab0e7dc43ebe0b7e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090351 - Fix assertions in `HTMLEditUtils::ScanInclusiveNextThingWithIgnoringUnnecessaryLineBreak` and `HTMLEditor::EnsureNoFollowingUnnecessaryLineBreak` r=m_kato\n\nCurrently, we use inline editing host as ancestor limiter to check\nwhether a line break is a padding for empty block, for making an empty\nline or unnecessary. Therefore, it depends on the surrounding content of\nthe inline editing host that the utilities return actual value or\nguessed value. So, the assertions need to assume the cases.\n\nAccording to Chrome, the behavior is not ideal to preserve and control\nthe layout of surrounding content. Let's add a WPT to check it in\nwpt.fyi to file an issue about how browsers should work.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341232\n", "files": ["editor/libeditor/HTMLEditUtils.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditor.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/editing/other/trailing-linebreak-of-inline-editing-host.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/editing/crashtests/inserthtml-after-select-input-outside-editing-host.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/editing/other/trailing-linebreak-of-inline-editing-host.tentative.html"], "git_node": "5a9a9b276634aed90c4f8182a75c77539211369e", "git_parents": ["dcc99f83daa5cabad099a42e2d694e09e01e22aa"], "node": "03c8c4f172e439f025efa523755725878059d82e", "parents": ["38a84ec8bfbdd9a80b81970299caebc6cd948f05"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089774 - Use a non-movable load for UnsafeGetReservedSlot. r=iain\n\nThis adds `LoadReservedFixedSlotResult` and uses it instead of `LoadFixedSlotResult`\nfor the `UnsafeGetReservedSlot` intrinsic.\n\nAlso renames `LoadFixedSlotTypedResult` to `LoadReservedFixedSlotTypedResult`\nfor consistency.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341262\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/BaselineCacheIRCompiler.cpp", "js/src/jit/CacheIR.cpp", "js/src/jit/CacheIROps.yaml", "js/src/jit/IonCacheIRCompiler.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpCacheIRTranspiler.cpp", "js/src/vm/PortableBaselineInterpret.cpp"], "git_node": "5f9d103c01dc6dd3ffa1a5523f85d701f901352f", "git_parents": ["5a9a9b276634aed90c4f8182a75c77539211369e"], "node": "6fe65d24b9c08834e285f57d9d5076a4dbad5c36", "parents": ["03c8c4f172e439f025efa523755725878059d82e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Laura Lopez \u003cllopez@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088662 - Capitalize \"Private Windows\" and add serial comma in about:privatebrowsing info body. r=bolsson,fluent-reviewers DONTBUILD\n\nThe info body on the redesigned about:privatebrowsing page\n(about-private-browsing-nova-info-body) now reads \"Closing all your\nPrivate Windows deletes your cookies, history, and site data.\" This\nmatches the capitalization of \"Private Windows\" in\nabout-private-browsing-nova-info-subheader2 on the same screen, and the\nserial comma used in about-private-browsing-felt-privacy-v1-info-body.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339334\n", "files": ["browser/locales/en-US/browser/aboutPrivateBrowsing.ftl"], "git_node": "519dc7582892a86c8c45cda958b1ed5097e6c09b", "git_parents": ["5f9d103c01dc6dd3ffa1a5523f85d701f901352f"], "node": "ed5bba1cbd2d441a9f6b78ec2d781728d24ce4cb", "parents": ["6fe65d24b9c08834e285f57d9d5076a4dbad5c36"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Adam Vandolder \u003cavandolder@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091266 - Fix flaky WPTs following frame load changes. r=dom-core-reviewers,jjaschke\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341691\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/history/the-history-interface/joint_session_history/001.html.ini"], "git_node": "949954c23a02f864ce0a7807163995c1d71e60b3", "git_parents": ["519dc7582892a86c8c45cda958b1ed5097e6c09b"], "node": "ed7d195e7d314d3387ff4e2b20947af2a8aea687", "parents": ["ed5bba1cbd2d441a9f6b78ec2d781728d24ce4cb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090436 - Update opus to 0145a6248c2171bb6c4e03fb54fe016b5123e37e r=kinetik\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340561\n", "files": ["media/libopus/celt/celt_decoder.c", "media/libopus/celt/celt_lpc.c", "media/libopus/celt/fixed_debug.h", "media/libopus/celt/fixed_generic.h", "media/libopus/moz.build", "media/libopus/moz.yaml", "media/libopus/silk/enc_API.c", "media/libopus/src/opus_decoder.c", "media/libopus/src/opus_encoder.c"], "git_node": "75d00989eaee7ddf9901f035c02b84edf013468b", "git_parents": ["949954c23a02f864ce0a7807163995c1d71e60b3"], "node": "30debb3fe55adc9d68b111262a0bd4d0ba72d52b", "parents": ["ed7d195e7d314d3387ff4e2b20947af2a8aea687"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Makoto Kato \u003cm_kato@ga2.so-net.ne.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091233 - Optimize requestUiThreadCallback. r=geckoview-reviewers,jonalmeida\n\nWhen posting a Runnable task to the Android UI thread, we use\n`GeckoThread.requestUiThreadCallback()`. Finally, `RunAndroidUiTasks`\nwill be called to run tasks in the queue. `requestUiThreadCallback()` is\ncalled multiple times, and then postDelayed() is called multiple times\ntoo, even if we have already scheduled a task to run\n`RunAndroidUiTasks`. This is not necessary, and we can optimize it by\nonly calling postDelayed() once.\n\nAndroid 17's new concurrent message queue always allocates a `Message`\nobject, not recycling it. So we should avoid calling `postDelayed()`\nmultiple times to reduce memory allocation.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341244\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/gecko/GeckoThread.java", "widget/android/AndroidUiThread.cpp"], "git_node": "9ed67c1fc818a1917383d83fcb2da003fc60345d", "git_parents": ["75d00989eaee7ddf9901f035c02b84edf013468b"], "node": "983cd75466ee1181f68a48dda375a7d9eaecdcc6", "parents": ["30debb3fe55adc9d68b111262a0bd4d0ba72d52b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Justin Tracey \u003cjtracey@thunderbird.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091547 - Return the error from Available in TCPSocket::OnInputStreamReady. r=valentin,necko-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341618\n", "files": ["dom/network/TCPSocket.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_tls_server.js"], "git_node": "e9a511686c2bec6b5cf024b399c06ddc58912a10", "git_parents": ["9ed67c1fc818a1917383d83fcb2da003fc60345d"], "node": "6e93572c7999c09a87c215834f901b98ce53a19f", "parents": ["983cd75466ee1181f68a48dda375a7d9eaecdcc6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2090172: Hold a strong reference to the main-thread XHR across worker abort. r=dom-worker-reviewers,edenchuang\" assertion failures @ dom/xhr/XMLHttpRequestWorker.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit dcfe4882cc7f8caf3afacde608038d0e7e8e70fc.\n", "files": ["dom/xhr/XMLHttpRequestWorker.cpp"], "git_node": "d66e6707624b206337887268962d8ac93844e04f", "git_parents": ["e9a511686c2bec6b5cf024b399c06ddc58912a10"], "node": "221b21f7ffc49dd7266283cf9155c18fbdc6181c", "parents": ["6e93572c7999c09a87c215834f901b98ce53a19f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2074521 - Don't clone a non-seekable streaming upload body in nsHttpTransaction r=necko-reviewers,valentin\" for causing WD failures @ /webdriver/tests/bidi/network/get_data/data_type.py\n\nThis reverts commit 29048bc19ae78bc8ec0df607e21463ee59ae181d.\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpTransaction.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_fetch_streaming_upload.js"], "git_node": "ac7a43f7dcd999da375828a9c54281d7de7cb51d", "git_parents": ["d66e6707624b206337887268962d8ac93844e04f"], "node": "e051b15c1d5925a88ae97bc2aba180fc30896863", "parents": ["221b21f7ffc49dd7266283cf9155c18fbdc6181c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2073679 - Don't fall back to sharing a seekable upload stream with the socket thread r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\" for causing WD failures @ /webdriver/tests/bidi/network/get_data/data_type.py\n\nThis reverts commit 97e43dd508b8a6583cc24a3fbd612996d8a71c6c.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2073679 - Reject an upload stream that NormalizeUploadStream can't make cloneable r=necko-reviewers,nika\"\n\nThis reverts commit 35466dcd6cbd55a000d7ef1a2c96941f4495cc7d.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2073679 - Report a slice as cloneable only when its wrapped stream is r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\"\n\nThis reverts commit b579a69612a61d71ea1c3d1a49febed39908de6d.\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/HttpBaseChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpTransaction.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_upload_stream_normalization.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml", "xpcom/io/SlicedInputStream.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestSlicedInputStream.cpp"], "git_node": "17429979681d2732ca302b3f402599791b41d6b4", "git_parents": ["ac7a43f7dcd999da375828a9c54281d7de7cb51d"], "node": "f4be77b81684d2eec295f36207ec1825658b36fe", "parents": ["e051b15c1d5925a88ae97bc2aba180fc30896863"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091136 - Always merge OSR block parameters with entry block parameters in BacktrackingAllocator. r=iain\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341297\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/BacktrackingAllocator.cpp", "js/src/jit/BacktrackingAllocator.h"], "git_node": "cb416fb199415efc4f883fd57ef8a5f2d05f83be", "git_parents": ["17429979681d2732ca302b3f402599791b41d6b4"], "node": "5c2fafcef8acda795663234e70cd31801e212dc1", "parents": ["f4be77b81684d2eec295f36207ec1825658b36fe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Niklas Jaeschke \u003cjjaschke@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1996221 - Support the Navigation API in javascript: URL documents. r=vhilla\n\nA javascript: navigation replaces the active session history entry,\nkeeping its navigation key and URL. The new document's Navigation\nentries are the previous document's with that entry replaced.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338111\n", "files": ["docshell/base/CanonicalBrowsingContext.cpp", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "docshell/shistory/SessionHistoryEntry.cpp", "docshell/shistory/SessionHistoryEntry.h", "dom/navigation/Navigation.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/navigation-api/navigation-history-entry/entries-after-javascript-url-navigation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/navigation-api/navigation-history-entry/entries-in-new-javascript-url-iframe.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/navigating-across-documents/javascript-url-nested-history.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/navigating-across-documents/javascript-url-object-embed-history.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/navigating-across-documents/resources/page-with-iframe.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/navigation-activation/activation-javascript-url.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/navigation-history-entry/entries-after-javascript-url-navigation-forward.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/navigation-history-entry/entries-after-traversing-to-javascript-url-entry.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/navigation-history-entry/entries-in-new-javascript-url-window.html"], "git_node": "b9414683d2fb5c1e02d40d8bde82209e286c4ed4", "git_parents": ["cb416fb199415efc4f883fd57ef8a5f2d05f83be"], "node": "c4c7b44375210ce96c7da1bc660cdd87447621bd", "parents": ["5c2fafcef8acda795663234e70cd31801e212dc1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Moritz Beier \u003cmbeier@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058919 - Sync should transfer Firefox Suggest settings. r=adw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341312\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js"], "git_node": "a0bdb5c39a8120362eaa6606bff2e7786fc30a4b", "git_parents": ["b9414683d2fb5c1e02d40d8bde82209e286c4ed4"], "node": "8d586d261711495fa56adc1766363ef83beb5a7c", "parents": ["c4c7b44375210ce96c7da1bc660cdd87447621bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andy Wingo \u003cwingo@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090867 - Refactor BigInt multiplication to work on Digits spans r=mgaudet\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340863\n", "files": ["js/src/vm/BigIntType.cpp", "js/src/vm/BigIntType.h"], "git_node": "52df0ee6735cd66c616d207f6a429d0b0a6ae65c", "git_parents": ["a0bdb5c39a8120362eaa6606bff2e7786fc30a4b"], "node": "51eaa591f5b29f7e09618ee3902e7694fb9112cd", "parents": ["8d586d261711495fa56adc1766363ef83beb5a7c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091431 - Calculate pretenuring recovery heuristics separately per trace kind r=spidermonkey-reviewers,iain\n\nWe can make this more precise by calculating this separately for each trace\nkind. Note that we only use alloc sites for objects; for strings and big ints\nwe disable nursery allocation on the zone.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341453\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/GC.cpp", "js/src/gc/Pretenuring.cpp", "js/src/gc/Pretenuring.h", "js/src/gc/Sweeping.cpp"], "git_node": "18a25888de6189b1f17ec244e9d2025a0b1c528a", "git_parents": ["52df0ee6735cd66c616d207f6a429d0b0a6ae65c"], "node": "909b42f0a01956b18823b72c7f3f421183b507b3", "parents": ["51eaa591f5b29f7e09618ee3902e7694fb9112cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Erik Rediger \u003cjrediger@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091327 - mach glean dev: Skip `workspace.dependencies` if it is extended (lists a version) r=chutten\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341317\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/glean/build_scripts/mach_commands.py"], "git_node": "5f5da5d5d30ec9db3ad275ca8ec5d83564b36755", "git_parents": ["18a25888de6189b1f17ec244e9d2025a0b1c528a"], "node": "0d4327c39759027a7e9fc8f5e318046c883a6cc0", "parents": ["909b42f0a01956b18823b72c7f3f421183b507b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086055 - Part 2: Size test-verify-path chunks from how long verifying a test of each flavor takes, r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,bhearsum.\n\nTen tests per chunk is too much for mochitests and too little for xpcshell\ntests. Chunks now aim to run as long as dynamically chunked tasks, count only\nthe tests test-verify-path verifies, and each takes the same mix of suites.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338889\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/test_transforms_test.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/test/chunk.py", "testing/mozharness/mozharness/mozilla/testing/per_test_base.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/desktop_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/test/test_mozilla_per_test_base.py"], "git_node": "4eb995448df06c53446a835931a1195184302373", "git_parents": ["5f5da5d5d30ec9db3ad275ca8ec5d83564b36755"], "node": "68d29c041d9ee690bde9c6f0c5a6b46b130c933e", "parents": ["0d4327c39759027a7e9fc8f5e318046c883a6cc0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086055 - Part 3: Account for the build type when sizing test-verify-path chunks, r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum.\n\nVerifying a test takes about twice as long on debug builds. TSan builds are not\nmeasured, so they are scaled as the harness timeouts are.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338890\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/test_transforms_test.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/test/chunk.py"], "git_node": "ee84ce15f1a5f80af3a413b4bc022f3fbf8c1da6", "git_parents": ["4eb995448df06c53446a835931a1195184302373"], "node": "c4fd83eb5f3c0e9b2dfc7fb80be422d5e76deb09", "parents": ["68d29c041d9ee690bde9c6f0c5a6b46b130c933e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084900 [Linux] Add BufferSurface::SupportsDirectComposition() flag to configure direct offload to Wayland compositor r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\"\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337035\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/BufferSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/BufferSurface.h"], "git_node": "3d44c06c4abcf1a2ac06f7507ce753467d83335c", "git_parents": ["ee84ce15f1a5f80af3a413b4bc022f3fbf8c1da6"], "node": "34716ed1e7ee135d110dc2a9a11afea750f3611d", "parents": ["c4fd83eb5f3c0e9b2dfc7fb80be422d5e76deb09"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084900 [Linux] Export BufferSurface from WaylandBuffer r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337036\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/WaylandBuffer.h"], "git_node": "e15916921210198a0c6847608ce548e7168d9ded", "git_parents": ["3d44c06c4abcf1a2ac06f7507ce753467d83335c"], "node": "caa3ac9d7021a088531309c4a2bb7a4b20a43e8a", "parents": ["34716ed1e7ee135d110dc2a9a11afea750f3611d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084900 [Linux] Implement SHMBufSurface::MapPlane() and remove YCbCrDescriptor from SHMSurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337037\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.h"], "git_node": "605a589f6686b4d0526625f2d70defb1339a1fe6", "git_parents": ["e15916921210198a0c6847608ce548e7168d9ded"], "node": "12d8855fcbc9e3ac9658f0a4122b0ff62d18eb6d", "parents": ["caa3ac9d7021a088531309c4a2bb7a4b20a43e8a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084900 [Linux] Merge WaylandTextureHost and RenderDMABUFTextureHost to RenderLinuxTextureHost r=lsalzman,gfx-reviewers\n\nImplement RenderLinuxTextureHost as unified texture host for both DMABuf and SHM backends.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337038\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/NativeLayerWayland.cpp", "gfx/layers/NativeLayerWayland.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderDMABUFTextureHost.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderDMABUFTextureHost.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderLinuxTextureHost.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderLinuxTextureHost.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderWaylandTextureHost.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderWaylandTextureHost.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/moz.build"], "git_node": "c72770c1e48cbcb6a9f1eb2df38cb7fd2a022ef8", "git_parents": ["605a589f6686b4d0526625f2d70defb1339a1fe6"], "node": "35ee191390a30af76aa856e6ec5d8526dfb67fcf", "parents": ["12d8855fcbc9e3ac9658f0a4122b0ff62d18eb6d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084900 [Linux] Use RenderLinuxTextureHost for Wayland compositor and make direct composition optional r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\n- Replace RenderWaylandTextureHost/RenderDMABUFTextureHost with RenderLinuxTextureHost\n- Configure direct composition per host state, as it depends on compositor support & buffer format.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337039\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/composite/TextureHost.cpp", "gfx/layers/opengl/DMABUFTextureHostOGL.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorLayerNative.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorNative.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderTextureHost.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderTextureHostWrapper.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderTextureHostWrapper.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RendererOGL.cpp"], "git_node": "c54f63eb322d4694cc6028d78ace54cee9783ff6", "git_parents": ["c72770c1e48cbcb6a9f1eb2df38cb7fd2a022ef8"], "node": "cb693894806fd18f9a6accefa795f4f2d0b975c1", "parents": ["35ee191390a30af76aa856e6ec5d8526dfb67fcf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Raushan Kumar \u003craus7n@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090063 - Remove the unused aDelay argument of _cleanPopup in browserPlacesViews.js. r=mak,places-reviewers\n\nThe only caller passing aDelay was _populateLivemarkPopup, removed with livemarks support in bug 1501811. This also removes the now-dead delayed-removal branch and the _delayedRemovals handling in _onPopupShowing.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340409\n", "files": ["browser/components/places/content/browserPlacesViews.js"], "git_node": "d70096981616f9533cce91f39962887556cefd6d", "git_parents": ["c54f63eb322d4694cc6028d78ace54cee9783ff6"], "node": "5a80e56e9f594928831b6ee6533c9455e7e645e9", "parents": ["cb693894806fd18f9a6accefa795f4f2d0b975c1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Harvey \u003cdale@arandomurl.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1457069 - Store opensearch url to prevent duplicate installs. r=search-reviewers,Standard8\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339213\n", "files": ["browser/components/search/OpenSearchManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/search/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/search/test/browser/browser_openSearchManager_installURL.js", "toolkit/components/search/OpenSearchEngine.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/search/SearchService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/search/tests/xpcshell/test_opensearch.js"], "git_node": "cea87170c0586d495a2724219f000ed984bae9e1", "git_parents": ["d70096981616f9533cce91f39962887556cefd6d"], "node": "cec538c2cf60f934137a6babba765f054effc50a", "parents": ["5a80e56e9f594928831b6ee6533c9455e7e645e9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nina Pypchenko \u003cnpypchenko@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081015 - Part 1: Register custom widgets as an AI Controls feature. r=fchasen,settings-reviewers,omc-reviewers,tgiles,sachung\n\nCustom widgets have been added to AI Controls as a feature of their\nown, with the pref `browser.ai.control.generatedWidgets`. Blocking it,\nor blocking all AI, only sets the control pref, so the user stays in the\nFirefox Labs feature. Installed widgets keep running, since\n`extensions.widgets.generated.enabled` is left alone.\n\nThe feature only counts as allowed while the Labs pref is on, so AI\nControls treats it as unavailable for users outside Labs. Making the\nfeature available again never enrols anyone.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340780\n", "files": ["browser/components/StartupTelemetry.sys.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/OnDeviceModelManager.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/tests/aiFeatures/browser.toml", "browser/components/preferences/tests/aiFeatures/browser_aiFeatures_generated_widgets.js", "browser/components/tests/unit/test_startupTelemetry_aiControlBlocking.js", "browser/components/uitour/UITour.sys.mjs", "browser/components/widgets/GeneratedWidgetsFeature.sys.mjs", "browser/components/widgets/moz.build", "modules/libpref/init/all.js"], "git_node": "cdeb33f5dbc3e62a5a3c39ed6d568e30cc6b9fb6", "git_parents": ["cea87170c0586d495a2724219f000ed984bae9e1"], "node": "f43d8b011431d7ce271cbc22c6afb5846ddbffbc", "parents": ["cec538c2cf60f934137a6babba765f054effc50a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nina Pypchenko \u003cnpypchenko@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081015 - Part 2: Refuse widget generation while custom widgets are blocked. r=fchasen\n\n`WidgetGenerator.generate()` now stops with the new\n`GENERATION_ERRORS.BLOCKED` code while custom widgets are blocked in\nAI Controls. The block is checked before the account token is\nrequested, so a blocked user is never asked to sign in.\n\nA block during generation stops it after the current model reply,\nwhich is thrown away, so no further request reaches the server. The\ndeveloper endpoint pref still skips the account token, but not the\nblock.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340781\n", "files": ["browser/components/widgets/WidgetGenerator.sys.mjs", "browser/components/widgets/tests/browser/browser_generated_widgets.js"], "git_node": "baacdc9eb9f13f152fd730cbe4dbe70fd334dc7b", "git_parents": ["cdeb33f5dbc3e62a5a3c39ed6d568e30cc6b9fb6"], "node": "dfbb0dc3d5734d7f21d63e1618ada207c0d4e66a", "parents": ["f43d8b011431d7ce271cbc22c6afb5846ddbffbc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nina Pypchenko \u003cnpypchenko@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081015 - Part 3: Add custom widgets to the AIControls policy. r=fchasen,mkaply\n\nThe `AIControls` policy has a new `CustomWidgets` key for the control\npref `browser.ai.control.generatedWidgets`, which follows `Default`\nlike the other features.\n\nAs with Smart Window, \"available\" leaves the feature's own switch,\n`browser.widgets.generated.enabled`, alone: users opt in through\nFirefox Labs. \"blocked\" only sets the control pref, locked if the\npolicy is, which is enough to refuse generation and hide the Widget\nStudio panel.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340782\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/schemas/policies-schema.json", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_aicontrols_custom_widgets.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_simple_pref_policies.js", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "b5b5a755e7e761a62f3438108eb9c4b014eb50d8", "git_parents": ["baacdc9eb9f13f152fd730cbe4dbe70fd334dc7b"], "node": "b0785bee5c371c0427b395aa15a31dfc27aaa87e", "parents": ["dfbb0dc3d5734d7f21d63e1618ada207c0d4e66a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nina Pypchenko \u003cnpypchenko@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081015 - Part 4: Add the custom widgets row to AI Controls. r=fchasen,fluent-reviewers,settings-reviewers,tgiles,flod\n\nAI Controls has a new \"Custom widgets\" group beneath the sidebar\nchatbot, with one row offering Available, Enabled and Blocked. The group\nonly shows while `browser.widgets.generated.enabled` is on, even with\nthe `aiControlsShowUnavailable` debug pref set, and the \"Block AI\nenhancements\" dialog lists custom widgets only for those users. A user\nin Labs reads \"Enabled\" until they choose \"Available\" or block it.\n\nThe strings are in `browser/locales-preview/widgets.ftl` until the copy\nis confirmed, and the \"Learn more\" link points at the AI Controls\nsupport article for now.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340783\n", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/config/aiFeatures.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/main.js", "browser/components/preferences/preferences.xhtml", "browser/components/preferences/tests/aiFeatures/browser_aiFeatures_generated_widgets.js", "browser/locales-preview/widgets.ftl"], "git_node": "93d83f562e6cdfb7fcfed0e4c0f17b57c29cd616", "git_parents": ["b5b5a755e7e761a62f3438108eb9c4b014eb50d8"], "node": "b61f0a8108fa3a23f43e7654dbe4703105100c09", "parents": ["b0785bee5c371c0427b395aa15a31dfc27aaa87e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2084900 [Linux] Use RenderLinuxTextureHost for Wayland compositor and make direct composition optional r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\" for causing build bustages @ RenderCompositorLayerNative.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit c54f63eb322d4694cc6028d78ace54cee9783ff6.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2084900 [Linux] Merge WaylandTextureHost and RenderDMABUFTextureHost to RenderLinuxTextureHost r=lsalzman,gfx-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit c72770c1e48cbcb6a9f1eb2df38cb7fd2a022ef8.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2084900 [Linux] Implement SHMBufSurface::MapPlane() and remove YCbCrDescriptor from SHMSurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 605a589f6686b4d0526625f2d70defb1339a1fe6.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2084900 [Linux] Export BufferSurface from WaylandBuffer r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit e15916921210198a0c6847608ce548e7168d9ded.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2084900 [Linux] Add BufferSurface::SupportsDirectComposition() flag to configure direct offload to Wayland compositor r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\"\"\n\nThis reverts commit 3d44c06c4abcf1a2ac06f7507ce753467d83335c.\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/NativeLayerWayland.cpp", "gfx/layers/NativeLayerWayland.h", "gfx/layers/composite/TextureHost.cpp", "gfx/layers/opengl/DMABUFTextureHostOGL.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorLayerNative.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorNative.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderDMABUFTextureHost.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderDMABUFTextureHost.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderLinuxTextureHost.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderLinuxTextureHost.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderTextureHost.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderTextureHostWrapper.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderTextureHostWrapper.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderWaylandTextureHost.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderWaylandTextureHost.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RendererOGL.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/moz.build", "widget/gtk/BufferSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/BufferSurface.h", "widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.h", "widget/gtk/WaylandBuffer.h"], "git_node": "480fb602603da28734932210ab18b48b39ee72ac", "git_parents": ["93d83f562e6cdfb7fcfed0e4c0f17b57c29cd616"], "node": "da0b42c37ad9665242210b78da74a2c064900fae", "parents": ["b61f0a8108fa3a23f43e7654dbe4703105100c09"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084130 - Check that the items an intended-duplicate-accesskey lists share its accesskey. r=reusable-components-reviewers,mkennedy\n\nThe check also rejects an empty value, so it skips WebExtension items by their class, since they can't name the items they collide with, and ext-menus.js stops setting the attribute on them. Thunderbird's ext-menus.js still sets it empty on items with the same class, which stays accepted.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335598\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/parent/ext-menus.js", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_menus_accesskey.js", "toolkit/content/tests/chrome/test_menu_accesskey_conflicts.xhtml", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/test_panel_item_accesskey.html", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/test_panel_list_accesskey_conflicts.html", "toolkit/content/widgets/accesskey-check.mjs"], "git_node": "26f8a754053ac5c555ea71437256531200bf1c0a", "git_parents": ["480fb602603da28734932210ab18b48b39ee72ac"], "node": "754f186ee72caef6e6fc57d26dc06ac860a6437c", "parents": ["da0b42c37ad9665242210b78da74a2c064900fae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Manuel Bucher \u003cmanuel@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086196 - Enable TouchPoints, ScreenAvail, and Efficient Canvas Randomization in bFPP on Android r=bvandersloot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341497\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/resistfingerprinting/RFPTargetsDefaultBaseline.inc", "toolkit/components/resistfingerprinting/nsRFPService.cpp"], "git_node": "a8e3f6ccdac92308d9689703e1a19d61657a3886", "git_parents": ["26f8a754053ac5c555ea71437256531200bf1c0a"], "node": "150ca76ae32e1e73990f613d8c8c1af093a86336", "parents": ["754f186ee72caef6e6fc57d26dc06ac860a6437c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080094 - On macOS, disable leak-checking for the FontData struct. r=layout-reviewers,jwatt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341586\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/FontData.h"], "git_node": "c78be08c248068b3b358ec26b21d584cf134836c", "git_parents": ["a8e3f6ccdac92308d9689703e1a19d61657a3886"], "node": "7d2ffc32fd31176fa6265e8c65aafd584df9acf4", "parents": ["150ca76ae32e1e73990f613d8c8c1af093a86336"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2003029 - Match remote tabs against each search word instead of the whole search string. r=mak,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341294\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderRemoteTabs.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_remote_tabs.js"], "git_node": "510308a1721ea6be7ddd7de19816ca5e8ac79ed2", "git_parents": ["c78be08c248068b3b358ec26b21d584cf134836c"], "node": "919e8bc45d2df0d81a173829c1e581c7581a3bbe", "parents": ["7d2ffc32fd31176fa6265e8c65aafd584df9acf4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090042 - Move the desktop-theme skills' token, contrast and pixel-diff scripts into toolkit/themes/tools. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles\n\nA move with only the import paths fixed. The dashed names take underscores so the mach command in the next patch can import them; screen-grab.py moves too, since probelib.run_steps() runs it from its own directory.\n\nThe skills cite the old paths until the last patch of this bug points them at `./mach theme`; two of those citations lose their link markup, which the docs build reports as broken.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340510\n", "files": [".agents/skills/desktop-theme-colors/references/system-color-pairs.md", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-colors/scripts/contrast.py", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-colors/scripts/pair-walk.py", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-probing/scripts/firefox-probe.py", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-probing/scripts/marker-probe.py", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-probing/scripts/probelib.py", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-probing/scripts/screen-grab.py", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-screenshots/scripts/pixel-diff.py", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-tokens/SKILL.md", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-tokens/scripts/token-resolve.py", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-colors/references/system-color-pairs.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-colors/scripts/contrast.py", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-colors/scripts/pair-walk.py", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-probing/scripts/firefox-probe.py", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-probing/scripts/marker-probe.py", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-probing/scripts/probelib.py", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-probing/scripts/screen-grab.py", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-screenshots/scripts/pixel-diff.py", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-tokens/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-tokens/scripts/token-resolve.py", "toolkit/themes/tools/contrast.py", "toolkit/themes/tools/pair_walk.py", "toolkit/themes/tools/pixel_diff.py", "toolkit/themes/tools/probelib.py", "toolkit/themes/tools/screen-grab.py", "toolkit/themes/tools/token_resolve.py"], "git_node": "f20a06ec2136d7afe2171903983231d8884033d2", "git_parents": ["510308a1721ea6be7ddd7de19816ca5e8ac79ed2"], "node": "a2b9a219e7d91e039e157675f02f0ecfea0bef98", "parents": ["919e8bc45d2df0d81a173829c1e581c7581a3bbe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090260 - Generalize desktop-theme-tokens' keyless-condition example and state token_resolve.py's scope. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340486\n", "files": [".agents/skills/desktop-theme-tokens/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-tokens/SKILL.md", "toolkit/themes/tools/token_resolve.py"], "git_node": "5e4f97cef9a672dd78e3a5be8c68f84eb044604a", "git_parents": ["f20a06ec2136d7afe2171903983231d8884033d2"], "node": "203828fd5326eb8b5132a1e1cb6fdf9eece297ef", "parents": ["a2b9a219e7d91e039e157675f02f0ecfea0bef98"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090260 - Cover a widened selector beside a narrowed one in the desktop-theme skills. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340488\n", "files": [".agents/skills/desktop-theme-colors/SKILL.md", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-layout/SKILL.md", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-probing/references/probe-recipes.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-colors/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-layout/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-probing/references/probe-recipes.md"], "git_node": "324c128a780639dcbe25b12ab927048d08c1c556", "git_parents": ["5e4f97cef9a672dd78e3a5be8c68f84eb044604a"], "node": "b0a7428151525789773c612788684b7a7b39237e", "parents": ["203828fd5326eb8b5132a1e1cb6fdf9eece297ef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090682 - Drop the desktop-theme-tokens advice to delete a needless stylelint disable, which mach lint now reports. r=ai4dev-reviewers,suhaib\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340718\n", "files": [".agents/skills/desktop-theme-tokens/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-tokens/SKILL.md"], "git_node": "cf0cff965a61826b0a61de32f5c7c9a0dd6ecc94", "git_parents": ["324c128a780639dcbe25b12ab927048d08c1c556"], "node": "ac4ae758e1ed21312f4e1f61bdf2d013077902d4", "parents": ["b0a7428151525789773c612788684b7a7b39237e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086549 - part 1 - Allow fixed drop targets in draggable lists r=android-reviewers,jdelorenzo\n\nAdd fixedItems to createListInteractionState.\nItems in it cannot be dragged but, unlike ignoredItems, other\nitems can still be moved next to or dropped onto them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338847\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractableList.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractableListTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractionStateUpdateTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/docs/changelog.md"], "git_node": "72cd7dbfa3712d3a8ae4d7e9ef9b938640d0deee", "git_parents": ["cf0cff965a61826b0a61de32f5c7c9a0dd6ecc94"], "node": "4389fb2896d5e56c93fed8101cddb7f9c8d7caec", "parents": ["ac4ae758e1ed21312f4e1f61bdf2d013077902d4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086549 - part 2 - Keep dragged list items under the finger when scrolled out of view r=android-reviewers,jdelorenzo,android-tabs-reviewers\n\nThe list gives the position of an item only while it is visible.\nOnce the dragged item was out of view, it was moved as if at the\ntop of the list, away from the finger.\nRemember its last position instead, similar to the functionality\nfrom the tabs tray. Measure it relative to the list, as the grid does,\nso that it stays right if the list moves while the item is dragged.\nThe dragged item has to stay composed for this when it is scrolled out of\nview. The containers of lists and grids now keep it composed themselves,\ninstead of each place showing the items doing so.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338850\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/README.md", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractableGrid.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractableList.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/PinnedWhile.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractableDragItemContainerTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractableListTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/docs/changelog.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ui/tabpage/TabLayout.kt"], "git_node": "b2b4c9744e0e3c8c3a86242ec86e8ed3e4ab36af", "git_parents": ["72cd7dbfa3712d3a8ae4d7e9ef9b938640d0deee"], "node": "503b4383fbdf28621db12a167195853aa7171965", "parents": ["4389fb2896d5e56c93fed8101cddb7f9c8d7caec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086549 - part 3 - Stop list items jumping when moved while dragged or after being dropped r=android-reviewers,jdelorenzo\n\nWith live reordering, items are moved in the list while they are dragged.\nWithout it, the list moves the dragged item only after the user let go\nof it. In both cases items could jump.\n\nThe list is laid out again only after an item is moved, but the index\nkept for the dragged item was read right after moving it, so it always\nwas one move behind. The check for scrolling when moving the first\nvisible item would look at the wrong item, and so would the offset\ncomputed for the dragged item.\nFind the dragged item by its key in the list instead of keeping its index\nup to date. This makes InteractionState.List.copyWithNewIndex unused, so\nremove it, and InteractionState.List.Active.index stays the index the\nitem had when the drag started.\nThe helper to find the item, getLazyGridItemInfo, was a copy of the grid one\ntaking a grid state. Lists now have getLazyListItemInfo taking a list state,\nand getLazyGridItemInfo is only declared on InteractionState.Grid.\n\nWith live reordering, the placement animation of the dragged item started\nfrom where it was before the move, making it jump back there and then to\nthe finger. Don't animate the placement of the dragged item, as the tabs\ntray already does.\n\nWhen the list moves the item only after the user let go of it, the item was\ndrawn in the wrong place for a frame, because the slide started from the\nposition the item had before the list moved it. The list also played its\nown animation on top.\nThe item should stay where it was let go of and slide into its new place.\nTo avoid the issue we can offset the item while the list places it, by\nthe distance between where it was let go of and where the list puts it.\nThe item is then drawn where it was let go of, and slides into its place\nas the offset shrinks to zero.\nThe list's own animation is turned off for this item, as it would add to\nours and move the item away from where it was let go of.\nListInteractionState.previousItemAnimatableOffset is replaced by\nListInteractionState.computeDroppedItemOffset for this.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338848\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractableList.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractionState.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractableDragItemContainerTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractableListTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractionStateTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuScreen.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/utils/CustomizeMenuPreviewData.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/docs/changelog.md"], "git_node": "09138a47bc7a1d7d3c682628a97f8e768be13a25", "git_parents": ["b2b4c9744e0e3c8c3a86242ec86e8ed3e4ab36af"], "node": "9882ee4d150c5e72b581b3beadbde83a48f4167e", "parents": ["503b4383fbdf28621db12a167195853aa7171965"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086549 - part 4 - Show the customize menu screen as a lazy list r=android-reviewers,jdelorenzo\n\nDragging list items is only supported for lazy lists, so show all the\nitems of the customize menu screen in one LazyColumn, spaced as in the\ndesign.\nThe list takes the whole width of the screen, so that it can be scrolled\nfrom anywhere, also beside its items, which are no wider than before.\nThe items are centered in the window, also when beside a notch larger\nthan the navigation bar.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338852\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenu.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuListItemGroup.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuScreen.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuContentTest.kt"], "git_node": "49e0e5091c97186fc361abaf495e1eab259452f2", "git_parents": ["09138a47bc7a1d7d3c682628a97f8e768be13a25"], "node": "cea09d8a6da0f5f5c5bae68565129a8b9e8e7c4c", "parents": ["9882ee4d150c5e72b581b3beadbde83a48f4167e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086549 - part 5 - Reorder the shown sections of the customize menu screen by dragging them r=android-reviewers,android-build-system-reviewers,jdelorenzo\n\nSections shown in the menu, including the mandatory ones, can be long\npressed and dragged to reorder them. While dragged, a section is faded\nand its place stays empty. The section is moved, and the new structure of\nthe menu saved, when the user lets go of it.\nHidden sections cannot be moved, and letting go of a section over them\nleaves it where it was.\nAs the sections differ in height, the list is scrolled by dragging a section\npast its start or end with its center in an area a tenth of the window height\nhigh there, instead of the areas of a third of the first visible section lists\nuse by default, which could leave dragging a section neither reordering nor\nscrolling the list.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338853\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/.buildconfig.yml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractableList.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractableListTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenu.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuDragState.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuGroups.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuScreen.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuContentTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuGroupsTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/MoveGroupsHandlerTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/docs/changelog.md", "mobile/android/focus-android/.buildconfig.yml"], "git_node": "83db9d7135d04b63143d68e8a5f5153d696bc9c0", "git_parents": ["49e0e5091c97186fc361abaf495e1eab259452f2"], "node": "33f7de2ed3efdac061174a75e00cdcb7854a21bd", "parents": ["cea09d8a6da0f5f5c5bae68565129a8b9e8e7c4c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086550 - part 1 - Report when a drag ends in draggable lists r=android-reviewers,jdelorenzo\n\nAdd ItemInteractionHandler.onDragEnd, called instead of onDragCancel when\nthe user lets go of a dragged item without dropping it onto another item.\nonDragCancel is still called when the gesture is cancelled. By default\nonDragEnd calls onDragCancel so existing handlers work as before.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338854\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractableGrid.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractableList.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/ItemInteractionHandler.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractableGridTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractableListTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractionTestHelper.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/ItemInteractionHandlerTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/docs/changelog.md"], "git_node": "25efb022b354f0fcba7322057abf9a26ea1848ae", "git_parents": ["83db9d7135d04b63143d68e8a5f5153d696bc9c0"], "node": "f1d202e57d54c19618e9d447795002bcbb2319ae", "parents": ["33f7de2ed3efdac061174a75e00cdcb7854a21bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086550 - part 2 - Allow dragging the sections of the customize menu screen into and out of the hidden sections r=android-reviewers,jdelorenzo\n\nSections can be dragged over the hidden sections, or into the area to\ndrag them into when none are hidden, to hide them. Hidden sections can\nbe reordered between them or dragged out of there to show them again.\nWhile the only hidden section is dragged, the area to drag sections into\nis shown above the place it was taken from.\nMandatory sections cannot be hidden: let go of over the hidden sections\nthey are put back where they were, as is any section let go of below\nthe hidden sections.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338855\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractableList.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenu.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuDragState.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuDropTarget.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuGroups.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuHiddenArea.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuScreen.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuContentTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuDropTargetTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuGroupsTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/MoveGroupsHandlerTest.kt"], "git_node": "513b037d9739f3f273107a20f9ee6415ccbc464d", "git_parents": ["25efb022b354f0fcba7322057abf9a26ea1848ae"], "node": "6f5de54498bba0f04641412a69eb62cfd9d6e53b", "parents": ["f1d202e57d54c19618e9d447795002bcbb2319ae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086551 - Inform the user that a mandatory section of the customize menu screen cannot be hidden r=android-reviewers,android-l10n-reviewers,giorga,parker\n\nMandatory sections let go of over the hidden sections already go back\nwhere they were. The screen now also dispatches\nAttemptedRemovalOfMandatorySection, once for each drag, which the Fenix\nmiddleware handles by showing a \"Can't hide this section\" snackbar.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338856\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/store/CustomizableMenuAction.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/store/CustomizableMenuStore.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuDragState.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/store/CustomizableMenuStoreTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuContentTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/compose/customize/CustomizeMenuFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/CustomizeMenuMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/CustomizeMenuMiddlewareTest.kt"], "git_node": "8d515644c9ff5e263ffb844808dbab35d6057d68", "git_parents": ["513b037d9739f3f273107a20f9ee6415ccbc464d"], "node": "2241601022d4bd405e8ff1bac5ae0c9763f119ac", "parents": ["6f5de54498bba0f04641412a69eb62cfd9d6e53b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086552 - part 1 - Show where a dragged section of the customize menu screen would be dropped r=android-reviewers,giorga\n\nA line in the space between the sections shows where a dragged section is\ndropped, also where it was taken from if it would be put back there. The\nempty area to drag sections into to hide them is highlighted when the\nsection would be dropped there.\nFor the line to show where the section was taken from, the section takes no\nspace while it is dragged, for the sections below it to take its place. The\narea to drag sections into is then shown in the place of the last hidden\nsection when this is dragged.\nFor no more space to be left there than between other sections, the list no\nlonger adds the space between its items, which are given the space above\nthemselves instead.\nThe dragged section taking no space must not make the areas in which dragging\nscrolls the list zero high, when it is the first visible item and they are\nsized from it by default: size them from another item then.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338857\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractableList.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractableListTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenu.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuDragState.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuDropTarget.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuGroupContent.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuScreen.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuContentTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuDropTargetTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/docs/changelog.md"], "git_node": "3b01eb2c8c6d3a69292c3ee5444257d67af15f36", "git_parents": ["8d515644c9ff5e263ffb844808dbab35d6057d68"], "node": "e74210fa2d031b68648bfd97697234ff4e2f9135", "parents": ["2241601022d4bd405e8ff1bac5ae0c9763f119ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086552 - part 2 - Vibrate when the indication of where a dragged section of the customize menu screen is dropped changes r=android-reviewers,giorga\n\nThe user feels it whenever the line, or the highlighted area, showing where\nthe dragged section is dropped appears or moves to another place, also\nwhere the section was taken from.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338858\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuDragState.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuContentTest.kt"], "git_node": "3a396616ff3b471fa29d94cf67ccdf5269a8c21c", "git_parents": ["3b01eb2c8c6d3a69292c3ee5444257d67af15f36"], "node": "ce8fef336c8c44a352b0fa9a742766f21fc86286", "parents": ["e74210fa2d031b68648bfd97697234ff4e2f9135"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086545 - Stop the navigation section of the browser menu following the toolbar once the user moved it r=android-reviewers,giorga\n\nThe navigation section is shown on the toolbar's side of the browser menu,\nalso for a customized menu if it was saved first or last. This moved it\nback if the user put it on the other side of the menu.\nSave whether the user moved it and only then keep it where it was saved,\nuntil the menu is restored to its default structure, also if it is then on\nthe toolbar's side. Otherwise always show it on the toolbar's side.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338859\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/CustomizedMenuInfo.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuCustomizationRepository.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/configuration/BrowserMenuConfiguration.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/CustomizeMenuMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/proto/browser_menu_customization.proto", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/CustomizedMenuInfoTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuCustomizationRepositoryTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/configuration/BrowserMenuConfigurationTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/CustomizeMenuMiddlewareTest.kt"], "git_node": "b1091d5ac12823c4cedbde1c0ad316bcecfa3a75", "git_parents": ["3a396616ff3b471fa29d94cf67ccdf5269a8c21c"], "node": "8160e47810181f1f05efa44288e1626eea5cb733", "parents": ["ce8fef336c8c44a352b0fa9a742766f21fc86286"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082394 - Build the browser menu from the custom or default structure once the customization is read r=android-reviewers,giorga\n\nThe customization was read only after the first page was drawn, so a\nbrowser menu opened before that showed the default structure instead of\nthe one the user customized. When the menu can be customized, its items\nare now built only once the customization was read, which the menu\nalready waited for to show them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338860\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/MenuMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/MenuMiddlewareTest.kt"], "git_node": "a97e59c35f55b2df2ae7edb2a2e7b7c1c11868a2", "git_parents": ["b1091d5ac12823c4cedbde1c0ad316bcecfa3a75"], "node": "b22ec2bdb09815f6870b3179223c5aace3419400", "parents": ["8160e47810181f1f05efa44288e1626eea5cb733"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088564 - Allow dragging sections by their handle without having to long press r=android-reviewers,jdelorenzo\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339502\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/MenuItemColors.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenu.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuDragGestures.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuDragState.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuGroupContent.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuScreen.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/utils/Constants.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuContentTest.kt"], "git_node": "63370c5f50d7afcd36d15c9e9f4a913a5fbff06b", "git_parents": ["a97e59c35f55b2df2ae7edb2a2e7b7c1c11868a2"], "node": "50224530a4f3908483462a407c06db54dc6df54a", "parents": ["b22ec2bdb09815f6870b3179223c5aace3419400"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090877 - Let the draggable list decide where dragged sections of the customize menu screen are dropped r=android-reviewers,jdelorenzo\n\nThe customize menu screen measured where the hidden sections title, the\narea to drag sections into, the reset button and the last hidden section\nwere placed, to change where the list would drop a dragged section. That\nwas a second way of finding drop targets, next to the list's own.\n\nAdd interceptInteractionMode to createListInteractionState. It is called\nwith what the list finds for a dragged item whenever the item is dragged,\nand returns the interaction to use instead, which the list shows and acts\nupon when the item is let go of.\nThe screen uses it for its rules: sections are hidden only when dragged\nover the hidden sections, mandatory sections cannot be hidden, and a\nsection let go of below the hidden sections is put back. The area to drag\nsections into is its own list item, so where the hidden sections are is\nread from the layout of the list instead of being measured. The list now\ntells the screen where the section is moved to when it is let go of.\n\nAs for the list's own targets, the drop target is found again only when\nthe dragged section moves, and from where the items are laid out rather\nthan from where they are drawn while animated. A section dragged by its\nhandle is picked up and moved at once, before the list lays it out taking\nno space: no drop target is found until it does, for the line not to show\nfirst where the section was taken from.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340879\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractableList.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/draggable/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/draggable/InteractableListTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenu.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuDragState.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuDropTarget.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuGroups.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuHiddenArea.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuScreen.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/DraggedGroupPosition.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/CustomizeMenuDropTargetTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/DraggedGroupPositionTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/FakeLazyListLayoutInfo.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/menu/ui/customize/MoveGroupsHandlerTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/docs/changelog.md"], "git_node": "4fe43bf0e84034dbe2bdd54602d54a781e5ca95d", "git_parents": ["63370c5f50d7afcd36d15c9e9f4a913a5fbff06b"], "node": "777c420b00897d2a32ca3591479100396852c0da", "parents": ["50224530a4f3908483462a407c06db54dc6df54a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "giorga \u003cgiorga@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088468 - [customizable menu] Show a new tabs menu section initially as hidden. r=android-reviewers,petru\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339486\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/metrics.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/menu/NewPrivateTabMenuItemProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/menu/NewTabMenuItemProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuItemProvidersFactory.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/compose/customize/CustomizeMenuFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/configuration/BrowserMenuConfiguration.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/configuration/FenixMenuItem.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/MenuTelemetryMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/store/MenuAction.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/menu/NewPrivateTabMenuItemProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/menu/NewTabMenuItemProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuItemProvidersFactoryTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuTelemetryMiddlewareTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/configuration/BrowserMenuConfigurationTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/middleware/CustomizeMenuMiddlewareTest.kt"], "git_node": "89f5f452dcce3a413fd8a064a07f7630b1ec2e2e", "git_parents": ["4fe43bf0e84034dbe2bdd54602d54a781e5ca95d"], "node": "9e9e0e73ae6f43507ef5bfd386131ce9c3cd45a3", "parents": ["777c420b00897d2a32ca3591479100396852c0da"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086548 - part 1 - Record where users launch menu customization from r=android-reviewers,giorga\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339827\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/metrics.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/CustomizationFragment.kt"], "git_node": "2d21a9a01a842c112cfa53d07f487bf5e36e0da3", "git_parents": ["89f5f452dcce3a413fd8a064a07f7630b1ec2e2e"], "node": "638c1bf0485511c9c1cf541156009b2451e20510", "parents": ["9e9e0e73ae6f43507ef5bfd386131ce9c3cd45a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086548 - part 2 - Name the menu sections by what they hold r=android-reviewers,giorga\n\nInitially we didn't have good names to use.\nNow we can rely on the names UX and product would want in a11y and telemetry.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339828\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/configuration/BrowserMenuConfiguration.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/configuration/Custo