: "default", "desc": "Bug 2087684 [wpt PR 64268] - Tidy tests related to not-restored reasons API., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nTidy tests related to not-restored reasons API.\n\nFix a bunch of titles.\n\nApply clang-format (because the follow-on CL will rename the files and\nthat will for a format).\n\nMove test-helper.js to resources/\n\nChange-Id: Iae44719b51ae523a9bd6e383abf46d3e0ff19ed3\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8667979\nAuto-Submit: Fergal Daly \u003cfergal@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mingyu Lei \u003cleimy@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Mingyu Lei \u003cleimy@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1728331}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a8f306ee4399724f33399dfdcac7da296f3cc05a\nwpt-pr: 64268\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/abort-block-bfcache.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-attributes.tentative.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-bfcache-reasons-stay.tentative.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-bfcache.tentative.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-cross-origin-bfcache.tentative.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-fetch.tentative.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-iframes-without-attributes.tentative.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-navigation-failure.tentative.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-not-bfcached.tentative.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-redirect-on-history.tentative.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-reload.tentative.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-same-origin-bfcache.tentative.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-same-origin-replace.tentative.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/resources/test-helper.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/test-helper.js"], "git_node": "1154fe5bcf242b8f360d6804ffea3c5081e4c03b", "git_parents": ["fe07fd995fa3ce0d5a9fbbb8206f2bf0c5732584"], "node": "b26297112ab3b37283ff60212b0ff22d46376150", "parents": ["28fbe7662297e778248bf1b8f64a68f789e3b6e1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087684 [wpt PR 64268] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64268\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-attributes.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-bfcache-reasons-stay.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-bfcache.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-cross-origin-bfcache.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-iframes-without-attributes.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-not-bfcached.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-redirect-on-history.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-reload.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-same-origin-bfcache.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-same-origin-replace.tentative.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "465829e4cae9edf3d4804997443cb4d24666dc53", "git_parents": ["1154fe5bcf242b8f360d6804ffea3c5081e4c03b"], "node": "7b4ad2bc80a0426f01851e94b283351542c3423b", "parents": ["b26297112ab3b37283ff60212b0ff22d46376150"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086273 [wpt PR 64271] - Add the declarative windowfeatures attribute, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd the declarative windowfeatures attribute\n\nThis patch implements the declarative `windowfeatures` content\nattribute on `\u003ca\u003e`, `\u003carea\u003e`, and `\u003cform\u003e`, reflected in IDL as\n`windowFeatures` and gated behind the existing `WindowOpenSplitTab`\nruntime enabled feature.\n\nThe attribute is parsed using the common window features tokenizer,\nsupporting `split`, `splitposition`, `splitsize`, `popup`,\n`width`/`height` (`innerwidth`/`innerheight`), and `left`/`top`\n(`screenx`/`screeny`). Legacy UI bar features and opener/referrer\nfeatures (`noopener`, `noreferrer`, `opener`, `attributionsrc`, etc.)\nare ignored, and the legacy `window.open()` popup heuristic is not\napplied.\n\nWhen `windowfeatures` requests a `split` or `popup` and no effective\n`target` is specified, `target=\"_blank\"` is implied (which also implies\n`noopener` unless `rel=\"opener\"` is present). If the navigation targets\nan existing navigable (such as `_self`, `_parent`, `_top`, or an\nexisting named frame), `windowfeatures` has no effect.\n\nRelevant links:\n- https://chromestatus.com/feature/5136319775899648\n- https://github.com/mfreed7/split-tabs\n\nBug: 570412924\nChange-Id: Ied5f1dd716eff9a1166b4520bdc3b767e30ac4e9\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8614308\nCommit-Queue: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mike Wasserman \u003cmsw@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1728433}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3c22e6d86f049b2e9bc0db1372dcdc8a024734bd\nwpt-pr: 64271\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/the-window-object/open-close/declarative-windowfeatures.tentative.html"], "git_node": "975bfde1e2b54501a9ea329f58187cd97f7461a4", "git_parents": ["465829e4cae9edf3d4804997443cb4d24666dc53"], "node": "0897a5c02a2dd7202781b15faef8174ddbb12ffb", "parents": ["7b4ad2bc80a0426f01851e94b283351542c3423b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086273 [wpt PR 64271] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64271\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/the-window-object/open-close/declarative-windowfeatures.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "812a613662111da7ac398318fce07171364c9583", "git_parents": ["975bfde1e2b54501a9ea329f58187cd97f7461a4"], "node": "ea5d8abaedbf8c904a3bd84249593457d87d5ebd", "parents": ["0897a5c02a2dd7202781b15faef8174ddbb12ffb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sergio Villar Senin \u003csvillar@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087688 [wpt PR 64217] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328655, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebXR] Render state updates reach the device one frame late\n\nThe code applied the updateRenderState changes at the start of the next\nframe in order not to miss the first frame. The problem was that the\ndata sent to the device with each frame request (active layers, etc...)\nis built precisely when the render state is applied.\n\nWhen a page updates its render state during a frame, the request for the\nnext frame had therefore already gone out with the old state. The device\nonly learned about the new state with the request after that, one frame\nlate, even though the page's own callbacks already saw the new state.\n\nApplying the pending state at the end of the frame, as specs mandate,\nmakes the next request carry the new state. The existing call is left as\nis because it's needed for the cases in which the updateRenderState is\ncalled outside the rAF (like the first frame or a setTimeout);\n\nAdded some extra checks to render_state_update WPT test to verify that\nthe updates happen when they should.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328655\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324700@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e6e7eeaac46268e6b7868fd585e7a5ead1f14594\nwpt-pr: 64217\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webxr/render_state_update.https.html"], "git_node": "08ac8d902048b168787de4b9064c6ef959527b91", "git_parents": ["812a613662111da7ac398318fce07171364c9583"], "node": "594c1000bfd4cb5aed5d6273b556ac384176d130", "parents": ["ea5d8abaedbf8c904a3bd84249593457d87d5ebd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087688 [wpt PR 64217] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64217\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webxr/render_state_update.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "4041d6ed1eee48b07d1d35512ea7de29869dbeae", "git_parents": ["08ac8d902048b168787de4b9064c6ef959527b91"], "node": "d325c12759b950d74b5f29223f855568ae264560", "parents": ["594c1000bfd4cb5aed5d6273b556ac384176d130"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sergio Villar Senin \u003csvillar@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087690 [wpt PR 64215] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=315208, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebXR Layers] Enable texture array support for non-projection layers\n\nSupport for texture arrays was added in d158677@main. With this commit\nquad, cylinder and equirect composition layers created with\ntextureType=\"texture-array\" now also allocate a GL_TEXTURE_2D_ARRAY\ninstead of a regular texture so JS could render into them via\nXRWebGLBinding.getSubImage.\n\nThree things were needed:\n\n1. determineLayout(): the \"stereo\" requested layout was always rewritten\n   to \"stereo-left-right\". For texture arrays the requested layout must\n   be preserved, i.e., each array slice already is a full per-view\n   texture, there is no side-by-side packing,\n\n2. allocate{Color|Depth}TexturesForLayer() and initializeViewport():\n   both were duplicating the layout/textureType decision tree to either\n   reject \"texture-array\" or compute a per-eye half-viewport. All of\n   that is already baked into the swapchain (size, target, array length)\n   at construction time, so there is no need to treat each case\n   separatedely as described in the specs. The backing will return the\n   right object to use for rendering.\n\n3. createCompositionLayerSwapchains(): the texture array length was\n   using session.views().size(), conflating session view count with\n   per-layer view count. That was valid for projection layers but it was\n   causing issues with other composition layers. In particular we were\n   getting invalid value errors (\"Offset overflows texture dimensions\")\n   due to not properly handling stereo layouts.\n\nApart from that, this change also requires adjustments in the layer\nbacking code as we were calling endFrame() in some swapchains without\npreviously calling startFrame() because the latter may early return in\nthose cases in which the platform code has not yet produced valid\nLayerData for a layer that has been added via updateRenderState. That\nwas not a problem for other swapchains but it matters for the texture\narray one because it performs an extra blit in endFrame() which requires\naccess to valid m_textureSets data.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=315208\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/313872@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a250f763d3ef55da6f051d2799dd41b62f2165e4\nwpt-pr: 64215\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webxr/layers/xrCylinderLayer_textureType.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webxr/layers/xrEquirectLayer_textureType.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webxr/layers/xrQuadLayer_textureType.https.html"], "git_node": "5e17c5ebd0167ed0799136906061d98ab5e7539b", "git_parents": ["4041d6ed1eee48b07d1d35512ea7de29869dbeae"], "node": "1460b7cc2378f962b8b7199381ee8f9880b23c9d", "parents": ["d325c12759b950d74b5f29223f855568ae264560"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087690 [wpt PR 64215] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64215\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webxr/layers/xrCylinderLayer_textureType.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webxr/layers/xrEquirectLayer_textureType.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webxr/layers/xrQuadLayer_textureType.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "9be8f26fb22d14c4262654168f2c6d63b862f7bd", "git_parents": ["5e17c5ebd0167ed0799136906061d98ab5e7539b"], "node": "0009fbfe5974f51943f5090162da01f65d208c3d", "parents": ["1460b7cc2378f962b8b7199381ee8f9880b23c9d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sergio Villar Senin \u003csvillar@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087692 [wpt PR 64214] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=314547, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebXR Layers] Enable texture array support for projection layer\n\nThe WebXR Layers API allows author to specify a XRTextureType in the\nlayer init parameters. By default it's a regular WebGL texture but\nauthors can decide to use a texture array instead. Texture arrays would\neventually be very useful in combination with the multiview extension to\nimprove the performance of stereo rendering.\n\nIn WPE and GTK ports the current texture sharing mechanisms\n(DMABuf/GBM/AndroidHardwareBuffer) don't allow natively sharing a\ntexture array. That's why we were forced to create a new type of\nswapchain which provides a valid texture array to JavaScript but that\nblits the multiple layers of a single texture array in a larger side by\nside single texture that would be used to share the rendered content\nwith the UI process.\n\nWe're already working on a new way to share textures between processes\nusing Vulkan. Vulkan natively supports sharing texture arrays since the\nVkImageCreateInfor structure used to create VkImages already contain an\nattribute to specify the number of array layers. In theory we could get\nrid of this extra blit (and higher memory allocation) with Vulkan.\nLeaving the door open to further changes that could also accomodate\nother texture sharing mechanisms in other ports.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=314547\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/313477@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 315da827a1bcad3039760a09a46fa95e97a0aba3\nwpt-pr: 64214\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webxr/layers/xrProjectionLayer_textureType.https.html"], "git_node": "4ecf451667075640109b68d79b217329e22b28d2", "git_parents": ["9be8f26fb22d14c4262654168f2c6d63b862f7bd"], "node": "7474bd47fdacccbb5060329e0fe151d70c00d223", "parents": ["0009fbfe5974f51943f5090162da01f65d208c3d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087692 [wpt PR 64214] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64214\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webxr/layers/xrProjectionLayer_textureType.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "c8464c0d1f4d48feba6655b8e7751dd61d81835c", "git_parents": ["4ecf451667075640109b68d79b217329e22b28d2"], "node": "d9cba8286d82fa2bcabbc28f5ad4672e97f66382", "parents": ["7474bd47fdacccbb5060329e0fe151d70c00d223"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sergio Villar Senin \u003csvillar@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087697 [wpt PR 64213] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=314558, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebXR Layers] Only first frame is rendered in threejs samples\n\nWebXRRenderState's copy constructor (used by clone(), which builds the\npending render state in WebXRSession::updateRenderState) did not copy\nm_layers (apart from m_outputCanvas and m_compositionEnabled). As a\nconsequence, any follow-up updateRenderState() call that only updates\nunrelated fields (e.g. depthNear) cloned the active state, populated\nonly the requested fields, and then replaced the active render state at\nthe end of the frame with one that has an empty layers list.\n\nAs the list of layers to render was empty, nothing was submitted to the\ncompositor. That was the reason why no updates where shown after those\nupdateRenderState calls.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=314558\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/313069@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7644af99db740407bd5147109630630ee4cdd9a5\nwpt-pr: 64213\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webxr/layers/xrSession_updateRenderState_preservesLayers.https.html"], "git_node": "72162ebccc8d692cef2f76dc56676835f07a90dd", "git_parents": ["c8464c0d1f4d48feba6655b8e7751dd61d81835c"], "node": "f35ffb107a5638ebecc339aff946cb771768ef53", "parents": ["d9cba8286d82fa2bcabbc28f5ad4672e97f66382"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087697 [wpt PR 64213] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64213\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webxr/layers/xrSession_updateRenderState_preservesLayers.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "397dab4e25515bdb14bf5ce935edc2f422a3de6e", "git_parents": ["72162ebccc8d692cef2f76dc56676835f07a90dd"], "node": "eceec241071d781c53d2560a346f4903ccefbfd3", "parents": ["f35ffb107a5638ebecc339aff946cb771768ef53"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sergio Villar Senin \u003csvillar@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087698 [wpt PR 64212] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=313958, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebXR Layers] Add init and setter param validation for equirect layer\n\nThe equirect layer is defined by a set of values that define its shape.\nThey can be specified at construction time in the init structure and/or\nmodified later using the layer setters.\n\nThose values must be validated as not every value is valid. Specs do not\nhave an explicit validation phase for them but they do specify the\nlimits so we'll have to add some clamping\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=313958\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/312595@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 16fb7d25c438c5b467e48fc352dc58b8d7471ee7\nwpt-pr: 64212\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webxr/layers/xrEquirectLayer_paramValidation.https.html"], "git_node": "3309b5accf81f0409ed5a6969fbcef69dc6794b3", "git_parents": ["397dab4e25515bdb14bf5ce935edc2f422a3de6e"], "node": "4a15fc5a9618aa0e45a28494e2610a2da84ce14a", "parents": ["eceec241071d781c53d2560a346f4903ccefbfd3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087698 [wpt PR 64212] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64212\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webxr/layers/xrEquirectLayer_paramValidation.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "fb6d5cf1be00af27319bf6e89a4d03046926e70e", "git_parents": ["3309b5accf81f0409ed5a6969fbcef69dc6794b3"], "node": "c37d4175c993ee751a43e0fa7bda9af166931ea5", "parents": ["4a15fc5a9618aa0e45a28494e2610a2da84ce14a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sergio Villar Senin \u003csvillar@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087700 [wpt PR 64211] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=314556, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebXR Layers] Nothing is rendered in threejs XR examples\n\nSoon after creating a projection layer the size of the textures backing\nthat layer should be available and exposed to JS. However the current\ncode was waiting for the first texture to be created and available to\nset the size. It's fine to set the available size at creation time as\nspecs describes them as the \"recommended width/height of color textures\nfor this layer\" based on what the device says and the scale factor.\n\nThat was the reason why threejs examples were failing, because they were\nchecking the size of the textures soon after creating the layer without\nwaiting for the first rAF.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=314556\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/313067@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 332b7754c502198bfea3250f2c7fcb902f1de10d\nwpt-pr: 64211\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webxr/layers/xrProjectionLayer_initialTextureSize.https.html"], "git_node": "c6f8e7dc5511b38d9b95f304249ca8f7fcee9a90", "git_parents": ["fb6d5cf1be00af27319bf6e89a4d03046926e70e"], "node": "a67a5bc5d6165d4b9b7c170fbe23478a0a9caa1a", "parents": ["c37d4175c993ee751a43e0fa7bda9af166931ea5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087700 [wpt PR 64211] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64211\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webxr/layers/xrProjectionLayer_initialTextureSize.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "9b006798a282d2b646061b81ac0f2cf27672f879", "git_parents": ["c6f8e7dc5511b38d9b95f304249ca8f7fcee9a90"], "node": "ce555866bdc54ce642694c252b9ac11667650f2d", "parents": ["a67a5bc5d6165d4b9b7c170fbe23478a0a9caa1a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sergio Villar Senin \u003csvillar@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087702 [wpt PR 64210] - [WebXR Layers] Add Cylinder layer support, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebXR Layers] Add Cylinder layer support\n\nThis implements the required changes to create cylinder layers on UIProcess\nside and share them with the WebProcess so that web authors could use\nthem in their WebXR experiences. No new IPC is needed since this uses\nthe changes from ee9f80f3@main in which all composition layers started\nusing the same message to create new layers.\n\nAs in the case of other composition layers, texture arrays are not\nsupported yet but they'll be eventually added.\n\nThe only platform implementation supporting the cylinder layer will\ninitially be the OpenXR one which supports the cylinder layer via\nthe XR_KHR_composition_layer_cylinder extension.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=313421\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/312596@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f24118f2e5567dfc17106933a91e9b1b08727d7c\nwpt-pr: 64210\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webxr/layers/xrCylinderLayer_paramValidation.https.html"], "git_node": "69abba0862f3a92c17fb9d803a87011268ff5d4c", "git_parents": ["9b006798a282d2b646061b81ac0f2cf27672f879"], "node": "0d8df2832efc4dac30cf001788f075dce59e80af", "parents": ["ce555866bdc54ce642694c252b9ac11667650f2d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087702 [wpt PR 64210] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64210\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webxr/layers/xrCylinderLayer_paramValidation.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "2afa798f04fca2869e398cf7bda5879996f24c6b", "git_parents": ["69abba0862f3a92c17fb9d803a87011268ff5d4c"], "node": "f02d0409b18269fe29f0ecaa83a7146cd1ecb817", "parents": ["0d8df2832efc4dac30cf001788f075dce59e80af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sergio Villar Senin \u003csvillar@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087704 [wpt PR 64208] - [WebXR] Add support for maxRenderLayers, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebXR] Add support for maxRenderLayers\n\nXR compositors can handle a limitted amount of compositor layers,\nusually 16. However there is no limit to the amount of layers\nthat a WebXR author can create and pass to updateRenderState via the\nlayers field. That's why the WebXR Layers spec defines a new attribute\nfor the XRSession called maxRenderLayers that authors can check to avoid\npassing more layers than the number specified by that attribute.\n\nNote that layer creation should not be limitted, what is limitted is the\nnumber of active layers, i.e., the ones set in updateRenderLayers which\nare the ones finally passed down to the XR compositor.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=309770\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/310429@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 979d30bdd7763cd0f68bee5ac21beebcb7102994\nwpt-pr: 64208\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webxr/layers/xrWebGLBinding_maxLayers.https.html"], "git_node": "87da8c55867b72d64398f1884503f48d0cf9eb8b", "git_parents": ["2afa798f04fca2869e398cf7bda5879996f24c6b"], "node": "a6440df95c3dd78586a9215482020affd49080bd", "parents": ["f02d0409b18269fe29f0ecaa83a7146cd1ecb817"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087704 [wpt PR 64208] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64208\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webxr/layers/xrWebGLBinding_maxLayers.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "8121dd97de7b0c9d9b558909e38080399705a835", "git_parents": ["87da8c55867b72d64398f1884503f48d0cf9eb8b"], "node": "fb71666d5903c5d9ab7d058419dbf5885631472e", "parents": ["a6440df95c3dd78586a9215482020affd49080bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Claudio Saavedra \u003ccsaavedra@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087705 [wpt PR 64015] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323050, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-box] Test margin-trim on blocks nested in inlines after content\n\nWebKit: [margin-trim] Block-start margin of a block nested in an inline\nbox is trimmed when the block is not at the block-start edge\n\nlayoutBlockChildFromInlineLayout sets LayoutState::marginTrimBlockStart\nfor every block nested in an inline box when the container has\nmargin-trim: block-start and can collapse margins with its children,\nwithout checking that the block is still at the block-start edge. The\ninline formatting context clears atBeforeSideOfBlock in the margin state\nonce a line with content or a block with content has been placed, so a\nlater block arrives with the flag set while MarginInfo says it is no\nlonger at the edge, and marginValuesForChild discards its block-start\nmargin. A self-collapsing block in that position loses both margins.\n\nWith assertions enabled this hits ASSERT_IMPLIES(marginTrimBlockStart(),\natBeforeSideOfBlock()) in collapseMarginsWithChildInfo, which is why\ncss-box/margin-trim/block-container-block-in-inline-001.html and -006.html\nare gardened as crashes: the margins those two tests misplace happen to\nbe zero or to be trimmed by the block-end edge anyway, so builds without\nassertions render them correctly.\n\nRequire canCollapseWithMarginBefore instead, which also checks\natBeforeSideOfBlock, matching layoutBlockChildren where the flag is only\nseeded at the block-start edge and cleared by layoutBlockChild after the\nfirst child with content.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323050\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324423@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ad1b842f892f3af0699d727575757840741d82fe\nwpt-pr: 64015\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-box/margin-trim/block-container-block-in-inline-008.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-box/margin-trim/block-container-block-in-inline-009.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-box/margin-trim/block-container-block-in-inline-010.html"], "git_node": "73882be634406d774d744b582e3f43a33b827055", "git_parents": ["8121dd97de7b0c9d9b558909e38080399705a835"], "node": "0104afe44657f049475a83d93b208ba11ec8bd81", "parents": ["fb71666d5903c5d9ab7d058419dbf5885631472e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087705 [wpt PR 64015] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64015\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-box/margin-trim/block-container-block-in-inline-009.html.ini"], "git_node": "69afbce522d8859b5c00aba7729438a9120439df", "git_parents": ["73882be634406d774d744b582e3f43a33b827055"], "node": "4191ad1efd2d527e8eae09030b582cd828551825", "parents": ["0104afe44657f049475a83d93b208ba11ec8bd81"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Sneddon \u003cgsnedders@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087706 [wpt PR 64197] - Fix NameError in resources/test/conftest.py, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix NameError in resources/test/conftest.py\n\nRegression introduced in cecc16187e.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f64eafa5ac38502c78b9eb04951ce19fa58c96f6\nwpt-pr: 64197\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/resources/test/conftest.py"], "git_node": "6546e4fd1a6db64fd56d863d8f94f6150d3a92b6", "git_parents": ["69afbce522d8859b5c00aba7729438a9120439df"], "node": "e7c6cc1780c849b981b090eac0e9f81cadde26e0", "parents": ["4191ad1efd2d527e8eae09030b582cd828551825"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sharon Yang \u003cyangsharon@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086355 [wpt PR 64266] - Freeze changed scrollbars when sizing position-try candidates, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFreeze changed scrollbars when sizing position-try candidates\n\nPreviously when evaluating position-try candidates, a real layout that\ncommitted side effects was being run. This included an option that\nrequired a scrollbar, which was persisted on the\nPaintLayerScrollableArea and affected the next candidate's\nmeasurements.\n\nThis is fixed by following the pattern in LayoutOOFNode(), which\nrecords the scrollbars before computing the dimensions. If they change,\nthe changed scrollbars are frozen and recomputed until stable.\n\nThis fixes the following tests:\n- external/wpt/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-fallback-bottom-left.html\n- external/wpt/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-fallback-bottom-right.html\n\nThe following test was added:\nBug: 382679385\n- external/wpt/css/css-anchor-position/position-try-fallbacks-scrollbar.html\n\nBug: 382679385\nChange-Id: I1dda22a44c29fbc33c5ac2fa091fa1e4c7a86dcb\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8301035\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Sharon Yang \u003cyangsharon@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1728568}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7f8d49b5a82606efc771f43d10aad5bce5ccbfeb\nwpt-pr: 64266\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/position-try-fallbacks-scrollbar.html"], "git_node": "c6be4d2ec7e9232e0bd4b635398e3b2333c1786b", "git_parents": ["6546e4fd1a6db64fd56d863d8f94f6150d3a92b6"], "node": "65ae772006f5030c2bac2d5bd69ba236a9d4d11e", "parents": ["e7c6cc1780c849b981b090eac0e9f81cadde26e0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Shubham Gupta \u003cshubhamg13.work@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085321 [wpt PR 63681] - Add `checkTextEntry` to `LargestContentfulPaint` `Helpers`, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd checkEntry()/checkTextEntry() helpers; delegate checkImage() to checkEntry()\n\ncheckEntry() generalizes checkImage(): the same parameters plus a 'skipLoadTime'\noption for entries without a load phase, whose loadTime must be 0 (the\nfunction-valued |expectedSize| and |timeLowerBound| parameters are resolved\nafter the 'skip' early-return). The startTime/renderTime checks run before the\nsize checks; the PaintTimingMixin checks now skip engines that do not expose\npaintTime. checkImage() keeps the existing call sites working by delegating to\ncheckEntry().\n\nThe 'sizeLowerBound' option is replaced by 'sizeRange': |expectedSize| is a\nsize lower bound, or a [lowerBound, upperBound] pair, so the single-bound case\nbecomes a plain number (first-letter-background). checkTextEntry() passes its\n|expectedSize| through with 'skipLoadTime', so the size is compared in one\nplace and the text entry's loadTime is checked to be 0. The tests that\nre-implemented these assertions locally now call it: observe-text,\nobserve-mathml, observe-random-namespace, observe-css-generated-text (drops its\nlocal checkText()), text-with-display-style and larger-text.\n\n--\nSimplify helper\n\nSigned-off-by: Shubham Gupta \u003cshubhamg13.work@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b7dff84adb869827c665e63e1839840caac2dd84, 11d9420e9fdd44810523c1c6fec99843b9ed6030\nwpt-pr: 63681\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/largest-contentful-paint/first-letter-background.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/largest-contentful-paint/larger-text.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/largest-contentful-paint/observe-css-generated-text.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/largest-contentful-paint/observe-mathml.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/largest-contentful-paint/observe-random-namespace.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/largest-contentful-paint/observe-text.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/largest-contentful-paint/resources/largest-contentful-paint-helpers.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/largest-contentful-paint/text-with-display-style.html"], "git_node": "ebfee7be3635f3544f26867bc4077b7c57bcf165", "git_parents": ["c6be4d2ec7e9232e0bd4b635398e3b2333c1786b"], "node": "7be8921e10ac27e040bc7e0261909079c5aef981", "parents": ["65ae772006f5030c2bac2d5bd69ba236a9d4d11e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Shubham Gupta \u003cshubhamg13.work@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081236 [wpt PR 63591] - Remains of `Remove LCP mouseover heuristic code.` - #47766, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRemains of `Remove LCP mouseover heuristic code.- #47766`\n\nSigned-off-by: Shubham Gupta \u003cshubhamg13.work@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3b3e763e92976d6df99ad9972c9b29c1b7bf2cef\nwpt-pr: 63591\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/largest-contentful-paint/resources/mouseover-utils.js"], "git_node": "010412479f51dca5ed4218053ba87381f8f4197c", "git_parents": ["ebfee7be3635f3544f26867bc4077b7c57bcf165"], "node": "54dc03692d8a185e44f913229dca92bc15cc88a3", "parents": ["7be8921e10ac27e040bc7e0261909079c5aef981"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087712 [wpt PR 64221] - layout: Properly clear cached widget layouts, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nlayout: Properly clear cached widget layouts\n\nWidgets layouts were stored inside of\n`IndependentFormattingContextContents` in a separate slot that wasn't\nreachable from layout invalidation. This change makes it so that they\nare stored with the `ServoAnonymousBox` pseudo which ensure that they\nare cleared properly by layout cache invalidation after restyles. This\nprevents stale cached layout data from escaping a layout.\n\nSigned-off-by: Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7215e6bc4a1eafd125d7b6e88ab580d51f06adb6\nwpt-pr: 64221\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/crashtests/reinsert-audio-element-onerror-crash.html"], "git_node": "7c7ce3f821288f26bed51a07249225cd47f173d9", "git_parents": ["010412479f51dca5ed4218053ba87381f8f4197c"], "node": "7be1deab06dec893ec1d63acdcbb37faa8887d48", "parents": ["54dc03692d8a185e44f913229dca92bc15cc88a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086717 [wpt PR 64265] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=329116, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDocument-Isolation-Policy should not require the cross-origin-isolated permission\n\nA document with a Document-Isolation-Policy was only cross-origin isolated if it\nwas allowed to use the \"cross-origin-isolated\" permissions policy feature, whose\ndefault allowlist is 'self'. But the policy isolates the document itself, so its\ncross-origin isolation shouldn't depend on that feature:\nhttps://github.com/WICG/document-isolation-policy/issues/12\n\nThe documents it embeds still need the feature. So a document without a policy\nin a cross-origin isolated browsing context group is only cross-origin isolated\nif the feature is delegated to it, also through a frame with a policy.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=329116\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6a32a99dc1d326e7f6ce7d39535870e8bd3569de\nwpt-pr: 64265\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/cross-origin-isolated-permissions-policy-nested.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/cross-origin-isolated-permissions-policy-nested.tentative.https.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/cross-origin-isolated-permissions-policy.tentative.https.html"], "git_node": "ce8ed92ca7c3fb5978429bfe6b7199f594997177", "git_parents": ["7c7ce3f821288f26bed51a07249225cd47f173d9"], "node": "fbe3aaa4586be00ca51e9b939ce30652b2356b3b", "parents": ["7be1deab06dec893ec1d63acdcbb37faa8887d48"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086717 [wpt PR 64265] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64265\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/document-isolation-policy/cross-origin-isolated-permissions-policy-nested.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/document-isolation-policy/cross-origin-isolated-permissions-policy.tentative.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "6464be3bf79d21d3e440784301a2de9b1bd49044", "git_parents": ["ce8ed92ca7c3fb5978429bfe6b7199f594997177"], "node": "f5a7aca8bd42677a599e87c6ef70e494896f791f", "parents": ["fbe3aaa4586be00ca51e9b939ce30652b2356b3b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maxim Gorin \u003ccode@mxmgorin.dev\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087714 [wpt PR 64225] - webgl: Don't throw SecurityError while the image is loading, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nwebgl: Don't throw SecurityError for images that are still loading\n\nSigned-off-by: Maxim Gorin \u003ccode@mxmgorin.dev\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3c59cd64f2b7f8790077968889a8bd201dcb6b70\nwpt-pr: 64225\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webgl/texImage2D-image-not-loaded.html"], "git_node": "2d1d9d33c06a4f94916c8b60f0f2ec4d8b3a6304", "git_parents": ["6464be3bf79d21d3e440784301a2de9b1bd49044"], "node": "4ae6f5797495ac915cdb2fff56528a95fb24fae3", "parents": ["f5a7aca8bd42677a599e87c6ef70e494896f791f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Claudio Saavedra \u003ccsaavedra@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084495 [wpt PR 63927] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327806, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nGrid with a subgrid whose item has an aspect-ratio and a percentage height crashes in Grid::gridItemArea()\n\nRenderGrid::computeAspectRatioDependentAndBaselineItems() collects the items\nwhose grid area has to be refreshed once the rows are sized. It reuses the\nbaseline-item traversal, which descends into subgrids, so an item of a subgrid\nends up in the list and updateGridAreaIncludingAlignment() then looks it up in\nthis grid's placement table, which only holds direct children. The lookup\nasserts, and in release builds returns an indefinite span whose end line\nindexes the positions vector out of bounds.\n\nOnly put direct children in the list: a subgrid places its own items and\nrefreshes their grid area when it lays itself out. An item of a subgrid that\ninherits this grid's rows still makes the column sizes depend on the row sizes,\nso give it the second-pass min-content contribution a direct child gets, and\nlet gridAreaBreadthForGridItemIncludingAlignmentOffsets() translate the span\nthrough subgrids so that pass can read the item's row size.\n\nUngardens six grid-lanes subgrid tests, which now pass, and adds a WPT for a\nplain grid, which crashed the same way, covering a fixed row, a percentage\nheight and a row whose size is only known after row sizing.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327806\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324206@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 93d85554e80df4816e5505cc8e93fd2867ce3e65\nwpt-pr: 63927\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/subgrid/subgrid-item-aspect-ratio-001.html"], "git_node": "27c5b5794dcfafed16f495208f0d99ee6843b178", "git_parents": ["2d1d9d33c06a4f94916c8b60f0f2ec4d8b3a6304"], "node": "87e974731173c589ed5e80756d6ca8fbd615b113", "parents": ["4ae6f5797495ac915cdb2fff56528a95fb24fae3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084495 [wpt PR 63927] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63927\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/subgrid/subgrid-item-aspect-ratio-001.html.ini"], "git_node": "e99b2d4cdad423721a69e5e6eb16f35af08b4f74", "git_parents": ["27c5b5794dcfafed16f495208f0d99ee6843b178"], "node": "da5df38f494765c0b6ce74ccf5742fa6d5b7aef8", "parents": ["87e974731173c589ed5e80756d6ca8fbd615b113"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byungwoo Lee \u003cblee@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086372 [wpt PR 64290] - Skip CSP check on inline handler set in document without window, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSkip CSP check on inline handler set in document without window\n\nFix a regression the commit f5f363bd6bba6d155cfbc24f14f862cd60644baf\nintroduced - false-positive CSP violation on the active document for an\ninline event handler attribute set in a document without a browsing\ncontext (e.g. a document created by DOMParser.parseFromString, an owner\ndocument of template contents).\n\nShouldBlockInlineScriptAttributeSet() checked allow-inline by using\nthe CSP in the element's ExecutionContext, which is the active\ndocument's window that holds the CSP list for the active document. But\na document without a browsing context has an empty CSP list.\n\nSo ShouldBlockInlineScriptAttributeSet() now gets the CSP from the\nelement's document's window, and does not block nor report when there\nis no window.\n\nBug: 576126165\nChange-Id: I752ab38e09d613789eb3506b3a7c38d599724617\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8637073\nReviewed-by: Antonio Sartori \u003cantoniosartori@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Byungwoo Lee \u003cblee@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1728709}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: dcbd71020cf887e762e24590f9ba5682976c2a34\nwpt-pr: 64290\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/securitypolicyviolation/no-violation-for-inline-handler-in-document-without-browsing-context.html"], "git_node": "bf041984bee570f4c5f42b95394eec55b4d1aaf1", "git_parents": ["e99b2d4cdad423721a69e5e6eb16f35af08b4f74"], "node": "1cce184a79a80a7ea3cd674f60a6445fa5f1e680", "parents": ["da5df38f494765c0b6ce74ccf5742fa6d5b7aef8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byungwoo Lee \u003cblee@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086498 [wpt PR 64252] - Omit unknown source code location in inspector CSP issue, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nOmit unknown source code location in inspector CSP issue\n\nWhen GatherSecurityPolicyViolationEventData() collects the CSP\nviolation event data into SecurityPolicyViolationEventInit, it\ntreats the received source location as unknown if its line number\nis zero, so ContentSecurityPolicy::ReportViolation dispatches and\nreports the violation without a source location.\n\nBut GatherSecurityPolicyViolationEventData() returned the source\nlocation as is, so the inspector CSP issue got a source code location\nwith a non-empty URL and an unknown line number (-1 in the protocol)\nfor the violation (e.g. a CSS background image fetched by style\nrecalculation after the document is parsed).\n\nReturn null when GatherSecurityPolicyViolationEventData() receives an\nunknown source location, so that the inspector CSP issue omits the\nsourceCodeLocation field for the violation.\n\nBug: 577884869\nChange-Id: I367817ded6f794c16d77b1e449bd7d61e355e5da\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8657479\nReviewed-by: Antonio Sartori \u003cantoniosartori@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Byungwoo Lee \u003cblee@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1728711}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: fc4dd1c7fc13dac62139edd65d0c8fa004f12cd0\nwpt-pr: 64252\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/reporting-api/reporting-api-sends-reports-on-violation-for-css-background-image.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/reporting-api/reporting-api-sends-reports-on-violation-for-css-background-image.https.sub.html.sub.headers"], "git_node": "5655035a2003e8a56408f9a320010fc529540798", "git_parents": ["bf041984bee570f4c5f42b95394eec55b4d1aaf1"], "node": "9375cbfd89266e120629ccae16bc5c36c5006203", "parents": ["1cce184a79a80a7ea3cd674f60a6445fa5f1e680"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086498 [wpt PR 64252] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64252\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/content-security-policy/reporting-api/reporting-api-sends-reports-on-violation-for-css-background-image.https.sub.html.ini"], "git_node": "85dd6812aab706baf900c5e9a77fb7832f05e68c", "git_parents": ["5655035a2003e8a56408f9a320010fc529540798"], "node": "a68c022f776fe9e74cb75e4eae1a7758c5cec53d", "parents": ["9375cbfd89266e120629ccae16bc5c36c5006203"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matt Hargett \u003cplaztiksyke@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086567 [wpt PR 63661] - WebNN: cover float32 underflow boundaries, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebNN: cover float32 underflow boundaries (#63661)\n\n* test(webnn): cover float32 underflow boundaries\n\nAdd runtime and constant scalar/vector packets under the existing Exp, Sqrt, Mul and Div ULP budgets. Validate high-precision references, browser CoreML contexts, faulty readback and flushing controls, and repaired RustNN execution.\n\n* test(webnn): hoist float32 underflow mul/div data to top level\n\nReview feedback: rename unaryPackets to unaryTestCases, and move the\nmul/div operands and expected values out of the loop body into\nbinaryTestCases plus scalar and vector data, like the unary cases.\n\nThe generated test list (names, graphs, data, tolerances) is identical\nbefore and after, checked by evaluating the file with a stub harness and\ncomparing the output. WPT lint and node --check pass.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ce5ca39646886a9349fc42913f843ec6e1c8a36f\nwpt-pr: 63661\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/conformance_tests/float32-underflow.https.any.js"], "git_node": "abffe66b49994812d349d923072aaf07ee192be0", "git_parents": ["85dd6812aab706baf900c5e9a77fb7832f05e68c"], "node": "a1a994e54787f6767884fa3dd6719c9aebee9948", "parents": ["a68c022f776fe9e74cb75e4eae1a7758c5cec53d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Narfinger \u003cNarfinger@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087719 [wpt PR 64250] - script: Enter realm in `ByteTeeReadIntoRequestMicrotask::handler` and `ByteTeeReadRequestMicrotask::handler`, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nadded crashtest\n\nSigned-off-by: Narfinger \u003cNarfinger@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n\n--\nUpdate tests/wpt/tests/streams/readable-byte-streams/crashtests/tee-from-scroll-crash.html\n\nCo-authored-by: Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e\nSigned-off-by: Narfinger \u003cNarfinger@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n\n--\nfix whitespace\n\nSigned-off-by: Narfinger \u003cNarfinger@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 630c6cd87b1e0a2a068937249aa4316ee45cd0ea, 5aedc31247a0636c6207bd3087e114ed7576b654, d574da8afa2976320d80119074d7ce20c264a1c5\nwpt-pr: 64250\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/streams/readable-byte-streams/crashtests/tee-from-scroll-crash.html"], "git_node": "f4c09bb55c49548a7cfdc29d952f17c5f3df96ae", "git_parents": ["abffe66b49994812d349d923072aaf07ee192be0"], "node": "6f65f3e08358cbea1fe244c1daa694deb3a3244f", "parents": ["a1a994e54787f6767884fa3dd6719c9aebee9948"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087232 [wpt PR 64294] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321086, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[block-in-inline] Float inside a block nested in an inline box intrudes at the wrong position\n\nFloats coming out of a block level box on a line were handed to the inline formatting context at the\nline's top left, but the block's own border box does not sit there: setTopLeft() a few lines above puts it\nat { marginStart, borderBoxTop }, where borderBoxTop is its collapsed margin-before. Floats therefore\nlanded that far above where they paint, and lines below the block failed to avoid them.\n\nLineBuilder deliberately rolls the line top back by the pending margin before calling in, which is why the\noffset has to be re-added here rather than being absent from both sides.\n\nThis reproduces in the default configuration, since block-in-inline ships: with the block nested in an\ninline box the probe below the float went to offsetTop -1 and offsetLeft 0, instead of 99 and 34.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321086\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/318678@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ffb842abf9e61b3eb34c8ddd68d09a6e763829d3\nwpt-pr: 64294\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/CSS2/floats/float-in-block-in-inline-position-001.html"], "git_node": "863d951e85efedfd4b29c6691eb240abd510317a", "git_parents": ["f4c09bb55c49548a7cfdc29d952f17c5f3df96ae"], "node": "3467a0a1318f876850033e3f8470bf5c9938d15a", "parents": ["6f65f3e08358cbea1fe244c1daa694deb3a3244f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087232 [wpt PR 64294] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64294\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/floats/float-in-block-in-inline-position-001.html.ini"], "git_node": "40c5e8871ae621a4cda97f0abfefda2762f9ff44", "git_parents": ["863d951e85efedfd4b29c6691eb240abd510317a"], "node": "f1fb21beed4d648a26b96338a658210c01059cb4", "parents": ["3467a0a1318f876850033e3f8470bf5c9938d15a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087346 [wpt PR 64300] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328928, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nJSON documents and application manifests should always be decoded as UTF-8\n\nJSON is UTF-8, and the application/json registration defines no charset parameter: per RFC 8259\nsection 11, adding one has no effect on compliant recipients. The manifest specification likewise\nparses a manifest with parse JSON bytes to an Infra value, which decodes the bytes as UTF-8. WebKit\nonly made UTF-8 the default for both: an HTTP charset or a UTF-16 byte order mark still changed the\nencoding, and so did a user-chosen encoding for a JSON document.\n\nUse TextResourceDecoder::createUTF8() for both. DocumentWriter picks it for a JSON MIME type, which\nalso makes its check against the parent frame's encoding unnecessary. CachedApplicationManifest uses\nit and drops its setEncoding() override. The memory cache reloads a resource when a request's\ncharset would give its decoder a different encoding. Rename hasEqualEncodingForCharset(), which it\nuses for that, to charsetWouldChangeEncoding(), and have it return false for a decoder that always\nuses UTF-8, so that a manifest is not reloaded for nothing.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328928\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324849@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 974000f6ee3a74fa4d98f6854db375311cc366a9\nwpt-pr: 64300\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/encoding/json-document-utf8.html"], "git_node": "3f8d81428bd60582342a33bc5387073a73c8f0c8", "git_parents": ["40c5e8871ae621a4cda97f0abfefda2762f9ff44"], "node": "8adb08b77c6f69b7f2f40d5324fae962b5215352", "parents": ["f1fb21beed4d648a26b96338a658210c01059cb4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087239 [wpt PR 64295] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321087, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[block-in-inline] Self collapsing block nested in an inline box loses its margin when the root has a border\n\nLineBuilder::initialize() skips a pending margin when the margin state is still at the before side of the\nblock, on the grounds that it can collapse out through that edge. That is only half the condition.\nRenderBlockFlow::MarginInfo says:\n\n    bool canCollapseWithMarginBefore() const { return m_atBeforeSideOfBlock && m_canCollapseMarginBeforeWithChildren; }\n\nWhen the root has a border or padding the margin cannot collapse through its before edge, so a self\ncollapsing block on a previous line has already committed it and the line has to move down by it. Skipping\nit dropped the margin outright: the block painted below while the content following it stayed at the\ncontainer's top.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321087\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/318646@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5d5df59e49930188135cd1716f424106566ec2c7\nwpt-pr: 64295\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/CSS2/normal-flow/block-in-inline-self-collapsing-margin-001.html"], "git_node": "dbcc3f8a88cdb1e621e74d39c62128899834a7cb", "git_parents": ["3f8d81428bd60582342a33bc5387073a73c8f0c8"], "node": "3014bc56fefe72e32cbf855cacb5c5daba5f49eb", "parents": ["8adb08b77c6f69b7f2f40d5324fae962b5215352"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087239 [wpt PR 64295] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64295\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/normal-flow/block-in-inline-self-collapsing-margin-001.html.ini"], "git_node": "a471a35337688da093ea47659a08232e284a9f6f", "git_parents": ["dbcc3f8a88cdb1e621e74d39c62128899834a7cb"], "node": "a096bcf631ee7320820f7efeee0794ad20e30f4c", "parents": ["3014bc56fefe72e32cbf855cacb5c5daba5f49eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087245 [wpt PR 64296] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321083, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[block-in-inline] Baseline alignment ignores the offset of a block level box nested in an inline box\n\nLineLayout::firstLineBaseline() returns a block-in-inline's own baseline, but callers expect a baseline measured from the container's border box.\nRenderBlock's equivalents add the child's logicalTop() for exactly this reason:\n\n    if (auto baseline = child-\u003efirstLineBaseline())\n        return LayoutUnit { (child-\u003elogicalTop() + baseline.value()).toInt() };\n\nSo anything above the block level box - the container's padding-before, or a preceding line - is dropped\nfrom the exported baseline.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321083\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/318656@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8323693c7f5a5990585693f866cd84a950ed5d55\nwpt-pr: 64296\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/baseline-rules/first-baseline-block-in-inline-001.html"], "git_node": "f42eef2d886cff4af593dc3026391a651f2a42d6", "git_parents": ["a471a35337688da093ea47659a08232e284a9f6f"], "node": "fa68b368df977c8898535cad2f79a6807c70efef", "parents": ["a096bcf631ee7320820f7efeee0794ad20e30f4c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087245 [wpt PR 64296] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64296\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/baseline-rules/first-baseline-block-in-inline-001.html.ini"], "git_node": "d6e25cc6e07a38aea9a26b44cbfa0be3248fab64", "git_parents": ["f42eef2d886cff4af593dc3026391a651f2a42d6"], "node": "965870bd4ec065cb37532959161be9d455f3f8fa", "parents": ["fa68b368df977c8898535cad2f79a6807c70efef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087251 [wpt PR 64297] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321088, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[block-in-inline] Trailing whitespace is not collapsed before a block nested in an inline box\n\nisLastLineWithInlineContent() looks past the line's own content for more inline items to decide whether\nthis is the last line with inline content. A block level box is not \"contentful\" per\nisContentfulOrHasDecoration(), which only accepts atomic inline level boxes and line breaks, so the scan\nstepped straight over it, found the content after the block and concluded the line was not last.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321088\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/318653@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2a0cbb720dca89db6e17702805bb2bb1f49e4ef9\nwpt-pr: 64297\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/white-space/trailing-space-before-block-in-inline-001.html"], "git_node": "eb02a829b6e8f52e3f9d81b042c55dfbd9d6a5f2", "git_parents": ["d6e25cc6e07a38aea9a26b44cbfa0be3248fab64"], "node": "e55727624bf1d4e898be6bfbbf7de422408964f7", "parents": ["965870bd4ec065cb37532959161be9d455f3f8fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087251 [wpt PR 64297] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64297\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-text/white-space/trailing-space-before-block-in-inline-001.html.ini"], "git_node": "156e488d79657fd4ae6b3a7a39f1d64f7b428ee5", "git_parents": ["eb02a829b6e8f52e3f9d81b042c55dfbd9d6a5f2"], "node": "7749cc7fbcb684c750d5b8d13ff0a7482bd40845", "parents": ["e55727624bf1d4e898be6bfbbf7de422408964f7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087255 [wpt PR 64298] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321089, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[block-in-inline] Empty orthogonal block nested in an inline box stretches the line\n\nRenderBox::logicalTop() is\n\n    writingMode().isHorizontal() ? y() : x()\n\nresolved in the *child's* writing mode. For a vertical-rl child in a horizontal-tb container it therefore\nreturns the child's physical x, which in an rtl container is its right edge. That value was returned as the\nblock's logical top, became borderBoxTop in layoutWithFormattingContextForBlockInInline, was stored as the\nblock's vertical margin and the line inherited it as its height:\n\n    renderer x=769 y=0  -\u003e  childLogicalTop=769  -\u003e  marginBefore=769  -\u003e  line height 769\n\nRenderBlock::logicalTopForChild() is `isHorizontalWritingMode() ? child.y() : child.x()`, i.e. resolved\nagainst the container, which is what the caller means. Needs all three of rtl, an orthogonal writing mode\nand an empty block - with content in the block a different path computes the size.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321089\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/318659@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f4d0cb0800507836035fed9251d67fe671b1a6e1\nwpt-pr: 64298\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/orthogonal-block-in-inline-line-height-001.html"], "git_node": "e9dcce000988024712a2b301543abcd8dd00307c", "git_parents": ["156e488d79657fd4ae6b3a7a39f1d64f7b428ee5"], "node": "651e30ce51b9e73f34e7f483c308a70bee5119de", "parents": ["7749cc7fbcb684c750d5b8d13ff0a7482bd40845"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087255 [wpt PR 64298] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64298\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-writing-modes/orthogonal-block-in-inline-line-height-001.html.ini"], "git_node": "36b152c7bfb9089de9cb9f1c76ed000d652ec1f9", "git_parents": ["e9dcce000988024712a2b301543abcd8dd00307c"], "node": "d9c2480a1695d2c6c730a4b381c5885cc92a9deb", "parents": ["651e30ce51b9e73f34e7f483c308a70bee5119de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087344 [wpt PR 64299] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328519, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nA selected \u003coption\u003e inserted inside a wrapper element does not get selected\n\nWhen a selected \u003coption\u003e is inserted into a \u003cselect\u003e without the multiple\nattribute, the other options are to be deselected.\nHTMLSelectElement::optionToSelectFromChildChangeScope() only did that for\n\u003coption\u003e children of the \u003cselect\u003e and of inserted \u003coptgroup\u003e children. For\nother options, as in \u003cselect\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003coption selected\u003e, recalcListItems() kept\nthe last selected option in tree order instead, and a selected \u003coption\u003e child\ninserted together with a later wrapped selected option won over it.\n\nThe insertion and moving steps of a selected \u003coption\u003e now report it to the new\nHTMLSelectElement::selectedOptionAdded(). They run in tree order, so the option\nreported last wins. Once the change is complete,\nHTMLSelectElement::descendantsChanged() from 324413@main selects it, as does\nHTMLSelectElement::childrenChanged() for changes made while cloning, which skip\ndescendantsChanged(). That leaves optionToSelectFromChildChangeScope() with only\nscrolling to the selection after an insertion, which childrenChanged() now does\nitself.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328519\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324902@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 83deb5653d50121ab61529b8d4cc6b1fa5825fd5\nwpt-pr: 64299\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/option-selectedness-wrapper.html"], "git_node": "5cda8478a8638672b70fed2b751a69e97c0881fe", "git_parents": ["36b152c7bfb9089de9cb9f1c76ed000d652ec1f9"], "node": "70bb6e530b1bc23b32d328fe9c964a9d3d2bf5d8", "parents": ["d9c2480a1695d2c6c730a4b381c5885cc92a9deb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087344 [wpt PR 64299] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64299\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/option-selectedness-wrapper.html.ini"], "git_node": "19d707c88a6e80cf8445961001d7a8fd2e6cd31c", "git_parents": ["5cda8478a8638672b70fed2b751a69e97c0881fe"], "node": "e9af4fdfc41de03ff946832e97dfe7931e6d5bc2", "parents": ["70bb6e530b1bc23b32d328fe9c964a9d3d2bf5d8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Sneddon \u003cgsnedders@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087724 [wpt PR 64352] - Set Taskcluster priorities for the critical path, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSet Taskcluster priorities for the critical path\n\nTaskcluster's queue claims tasks by priority, then by the time they\nbecame pending.\n\nPreviously, every task used the default priority, so tasks triggered\nlater in a task group were significantly delayed. This caused Firefox\ntest jobs to run long after the Chrome ones (as they were only queued\nafter download-firefox-* ran), and that sink tasks could end up stuck\nfor many hours blocking PRs.\n\nWe sometimes even saw these failing on PRs due to hitting the 24-hour\ntask group deadline; sometimes this was with the sink task not running\n(despite everything else running successfully), and sometimes even\nwith Firefox test jobs not running.\n\nTherefore, we make the sink task run at highest priority, to make sure\nPRs always resolve their status and don't risk timeouts from that task\nalone; and we make the decision task and download-firefox-* tasks run\nat very-high, so the jobs that depend on them can get into the queue\nas soon as possible. Everything else keeps the default lowest\npriority.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 16aa4808d68f49c9eb6f2feeaa7a29f230bf4430\nwpt-pr: 64352\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/.taskcluster.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/ci/tc/decision.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/ci/tc/tasks/test.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/ci/tc/tests/test_valid.py"], "git_node": "3501c65b7861524f4aab5cb39b5bfb25efac5091", "git_parents": ["19d707c88a6e80cf8445961001d7a8fd2e6cd31c"], "node": "9b5057eb2e7168b1bc4898c13eae2b5856a27344", "parents": ["e9af4fdfc41de03ff946832e97dfe7931e6d5bc2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Sneddon \u003cgsnedders@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087726 [wpt PR 64354] - Run firefox nightly and chrome canary full runs on epochs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRun firefox nightly and chrome canary full runs on epochs\n\nThese two browsers ran a full suite on every master push, which\naccounts for the overwhelming majority of the load on the Taskcluster\npool, where we are increasingly hitting timeouts.\n\nTo mitigate this in the short-term, we move them to a new\nepochs/three_hourly trigger.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ceec05f81f5a6e3329292dc4112410321859a315\nwpt-pr: 64354\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/.taskcluster.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/ci/tc/tasks/test.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/ci/tc/testdata/epochs_three_hourly_push_event.json", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/ci/tc/tests/test_valid.py"], "git_node": "46756079d0cc09bd77a82f451956f683506e2b20", "git_parents": ["3501c65b7861524f4aab5cb39b5bfb25efac5091"], "node": "169627a26b3d6cd6f34192a5bb3e24d74cab7b66", "parents": ["9b5057eb2e7168b1bc4898c13eae2b5856a27344"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sharon Yang \u003cyangsharon@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087727 [wpt PR 64315] - Revert \"Freeze changed scrollbars when sizing position-try candidates\", a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRevert \"Freeze changed scrollbars when sizing position-try candidates\"\n\nThis reverts commit 9aad139294e1ca4aca0a6cac17dce55e858bd019.\n\nReason for revert: Error in merge conflict resolution resulted in much of FlagExpectations/surface-embed to be deleted erroneously\n\nFailure Link: no failures yet\n\nOriginal change's description:\n\u003e Freeze changed scrollbars when sizing position-try candidates\n\u003e\n\u003e Previously when evaluating position-try candidates, a real layout that\n\u003e committed side effects was being run. This included an option that\n\u003e required a scrollbar, which was persisted on the\n\u003e PaintLayerScrollableArea and affected the next candidate's\n\u003e measurements.\n\u003e\n\u003e This is fixed by following the pattern in LayoutOOFNode(), which\n\u003e records the scrollbars before computing the dimensions. If they change,\n\u003e the changed scrollbars are frozen and recomputed until stable.\n\u003e\n\u003e This fixes the following tests:\n\u003e - external/wpt/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-fallback-bottom-left.html\n\u003e - external/wpt/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-fallback-bottom-right.html\n\u003e\n\u003e The following test was added:\n\u003e Bug: 382679385\n\u003e - external/wpt/css/css-anchor-position/position-try-fallbacks-scrollbar.html\n\u003e\n\u003e Bug: 382679385\n\u003e Change-Id: I1dda22a44c29fbc33c5ac2fa091fa1e4c7a86dcb\n\u003e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8301035\n\u003e Reviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Commit-Queue: Sharon Yang \u003cyangsharon@igalia.com\u003e\n\u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1728568}\n\nBug: 382679385\nNo-Presubmit: true\nNo-Tree-Checks: true\nNo-Try: true\nChange-Id: I5a66e7935c3daeae8f3420992dfb1fb40b695c04\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8672519\nCommit-Queue: Sharon Yang \u003cyangsharon@igalia.com\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Sharon Yang \u003cyangsharon@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Christian Biesinger \u003ccbiesinger@chromium.org\u003e\nBot-Commit: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1728610}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 70dae60789ef6220d9b4e60c92c5b2107b4e2b93\nwpt-pr: 64315\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/position-try-fallbacks-scrollbar.html"], "git_node": "58f53f408064d8ce378d188487e9f3fb203634b0", "git_parents": ["46756079d0cc09bd77a82f451956f683506e2b20"], "node": "112a56aba0e42e7ec29f57382462f8c2a287b09f", "parents": ["169627a26b3d6cd6f34192a5bb3e24d74cab7b66"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Felipe Piubello \u003cpiubellofelipe97@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084131 [wpt PR 63894] - DevTools: Allow touch capacities above 16, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDevTools: Allow touch capacities above 16\n\nThe maximum number of contacts stored in one WebTouchEvent does not limit the device capacity exposed through navigator.maxTouchPoints. Remove that unrelated upper bound while retaining positive-value validation.\n\nCover the 16/17 boundary and larger values through both DevTools protocol and WebDriver BiDi, including the current CDP int32 limit.\n\nBug: 572515591\nChange-Id: I59e57557c33087b5842f06da2956944728afbec3\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.linux:Linux Tests|webdriver_wpt_tests\nCq-Include-Trybots: luci.chromium.try\u200b:android-15-chrome-blink-rel,linux-webdriver-bidi-rel\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8554101\nCommit-Queue: Julio Piubello \u003cjulio@gitstart.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Danil Somsikov \u003cdsv@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Julio Piubello \u003cjulio@gitstart.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1730325}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2dbdf47ef1280a4db3d2840bef51105ce3025d48\nwpt-pr: 63894\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/emulation/set_touch_override/contexts.py"], "git_node": "fed7f8d0446074cf2ca88908a09cd54fe1447419", "git_parents": ["58f53f408064d8ce378d188487e9f3fb203634b0"], "node": "f11cb2cc387069530d1199d2d15b6b2ec1ed2035", "parents": ["112a56aba0e42e7ec29f57382462f8c2a287b09f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084131 [wpt PR 63894] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63894\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/emulation/set_touch_override/contexts.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/emulation/set_touch_override/global.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/emulation/set_touch_override/invalid.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/emulation/set_touch_override/user_contexts.py.ini"], "git_node": "5f7bacdf62fc31839bab4f4f1bcc754ac4b23bc0", "git_parents": ["fed7f8d0446074cf2ca88908a09cd54fe1447419"], "node": "22f81a50469207051df0e353943ba59d6d3c5453", "parents": ["f11cb2cc387069530d1199d2d15b6b2ec1ed2035"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Christoph Schwering \u003cschwering@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087728 [wpt PR 64333] - [Blink] Fix dynamic form association during parsing, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Blink] Fix dynamic form association during parsing\n\nThis CL fixes a bug which leads to an inconsistency between\n`HTMLInputElement.form` and `HTMLFormElement.elements`.\n\nIn the following snippet, `t` should be associated with `f` because `t`\nis parsed while the form element pointer is `f`:\n\n\u003cform id=f\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=d\u003e\n    \u003cscript\u003e\n      document.body.appendChild(document.getElementById('d'));\n    \u003c/script\u003e\n    \u003cinput id=t\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/form\u003e\n\nIndeed, `t.form === f`, but `f.elements.length === 0`.\n\nThis is because HTMLFormElement::DidAssociateByParser() is a no-op\nduring parsing.\n\nThis CL fixes this issue.\n\nBug: 347059988, 578370708\nChange-Id: Ia0c3cb605ed52f5d6ff0952fb108ad1c6a6a6964\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8666000\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Christoph Schwering \u003cschwering@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1730867}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8548e92382323b94b16a0ce524b5675d1b464a74\nwpt-pr: 64333\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/form-control-infrastructure/parser-reparented-open-element.html"], "git_node": "5ea6da77241b19a7d5fa2e0c633948518e1aa9ae", "git_parents": ["5f7bacdf62fc31839bab4f4f1bcc754ac4b23bc0"], "node": "faa1e11292a9eb15c0b2c37ba1af389de12e0a49", "parents": ["22f81a50469207051df0e353943ba59d6d3c5453"], "tags": []}, {"author": "youennf \u003cyouennf@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087729 [wpt PR 64344] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328479, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd support for VideoFrame flip (#64344)\n\nWe add WebIDL needed support for flip.\nThis allows to create mirrored VideoFrames from JS so we remove the internals API and we move LayoutTests/http/wpt/webcodecs/videoframe-rotation-then-flip.html tests to existing webcodecs WPT tests.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328479\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324809@main\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d000bd7558db482be61fd38c178e578d9fca7b1c\nwpt-pr: 64344\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/videoFrame-orientation-drawImage.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/videoFrame-orientation-utils.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/videoFrame-orientation-webgl-i420.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/videoFrame-orientation.any.js"], "git_node": "433e825f0c7520a58aff10483ed20f6af95b6c6b", "git_parents": ["5ea6da77241b19a7d5fa2e0c633948518e1aa9ae"], "node": "24ee4aa8d212a2498272f3cba1622af3c1f010d7", "parents": ["faa1e11292a9eb15c0b2c37ba1af389de12e0a49"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087729 [wpt PR 64344] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64344\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/videoFrame-orientation-drawImage.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/videoFrame-orientation-imageBitmap.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/videoFrame-orientation-webgl-i420.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/videoFrame-orientation-webgl.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/videoFrame-orientation.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "392cffcb53143050e1fdeded5b675f8fdc6263e4", "git_parents": ["433e825f0c7520a58aff10483ed20f6af95b6c6b"], "node": "f6a977e74aa49f7647160294539cc57e553b1161", "parents": ["24ee4aa8d212a2498272f3cba1622af3c1f010d7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sharon Yang \u003cyangsharon@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087730 [wpt PR 64308] - Reland \"Freeze changed scrollbars when sizing position-try candidates\", a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nReland \"Freeze changed scrollbars when sizing position-try candidates\"\n\nThis is a reland of commit 9aad139294e1ca4aca0a6cac17dce55e858bd019\n\nOriginal change's description:\n\u003e Freeze changed scrollbars when sizing position-try candidates\n\u003e\n\u003e Previously when evaluating position-try candidates, a real layout that\n\u003e committed side effects was being run. This included an option that\n\u003e required a scrollbar, which was persisted on the\n\u003e PaintLayerScrollableArea and affected the next candidate's\n\u003e measurements.\n\u003e\n\u003e This is fixed by following the pattern in LayoutOOFNode(), which\n\u003e records the scrollbars before computing the dimensions. If they change,\n\u003e the changed scrollbars are frozen and recomputed until stable.\n\u003e\n\u003e This fixes the following tests:\n\u003e - external/wpt/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-fallback-bottom-left.html\n\u003e - external/wpt/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/select-appearance-fallback-bottom-right.html\n\u003e\n\u003e The following test was added:\n\u003e Bug: 382679385\n\u003e - external/wpt/css/css-anchor-position/position-try-fallbacks-scrollbar.html\n\u003e\n\u003e Bug: 382679385\n\u003e Change-Id: I1dda22a44c29fbc33c5ac2fa091fa1e4c7a86dcb\n\u003e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8301035\n\u003e Reviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Commit-Queue: Sharon Yang \u003cyangsharon@igalia.com\u003e\n\u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1728568}\n\nBug: 382679385\nChange-Id: Iaa0a6da825effe41c469c1215b2f7b1fd23ef36b\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8670605\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Sharon Yang \u003cyangsharon@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1729711}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1181702414578d2f6aec40b5264879f762f7ab83\nwpt-pr: 64308\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/position-try-fallbacks-scrollbar.html"], "git_node": "92d01c49646ba47051b79fc738974b9a1e10d815", "git_parents": ["392cffcb53143050e1fdeded5b675f8fdc6263e4"], "node": "b3eaeaf2b2e0091e4bf9cb23e86358e1c3ec19e0", "parents": ["f6a977e74aa49f7647160294539cc57e553b1161"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087731 [wpt PR 64357] - Serialize CSSUnparsedValue directly in toString, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSerialize CSSUnparsedValue directly in toString\n\nCSSUnparsedValue previously relied on the base CSSStyleValue::toString()\nimplementation, which converted the object into a CSSValue via\nToCSSValue() and validated declaration-value syntax. When invoked off the\nmain thread, this entered CSS parser code paths that depend on\nmain-thread-only data structures.\n\nThis change overrides CSSUnparsedValue::toString() to serialize segments\nand tokens directly per specification, avoiding unnecessary CSS value\nconversion and parsing during stringification. In addition, explicit\nthread affinity checks are added to ToCSSValue() and\nConsumeUnparsedDeclaration() to ensure declaration parsing remains on\nthe main thread.\n\nBug: 577378379\nChange-Id: I8d0dea7bd85a8153c4bac5598f12c1db5d05f477\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8668175\nReviewed-by: Kevin Babbitt \u003ckbabbitt@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1730961}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0636997b9c857339a8eb28a49d8e0709128dfddf\nwpt-pr: 64357\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-typed-om/stylevalue-subclasses/cssUnparsedValue-empty.any.js"], "git_node": "df0b51a6072b863e6ca4f9aa3e3bd538add6a4d1", "git_parents": ["92d01c49646ba47051b79fc738974b9a1e10d815"], "node": "cdd2f6499d98c45a583917db8e83813f7301fbe3", "parents": ["b3eaeaf2b2e0091e4bf9cb23e86358e1c3ec19e0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Lee \u003cjonathanjlee@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087732 [wpt PR 64339] - Mark `infrastructure/assumptions/blank.html` as flaky on Firefox, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMark `infrastructure/assumptions/blank.html` as flaky on Firefox\n\nThe expectation was updated in #64227, but the true behavior is flaky\ninstead of consistently failing. Update one more time so that CI isn't\nfailing with `UNEXPECTED-PASS`.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 90bb6a74f207854339c81164496a81436c16f630\nwpt-pr: 64339\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/infrastructure/metadata/infrastructure/assumptions/blank.html.ini"], "git_node": "8c63b3dbe134043a5f0b6e022e61a1d169e70b1c", "git_parents": ["df0b51a6072b863e6ca4f9aa3e3bd538add6a4d1"], "node": "329af2e63840a49ca32a3ae4f99f906f3c5f6ca9", "parents": ["cdd2f6499d98c45a583917db8e83813f7301fbe3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Christopher Cameron \u003cccameron@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089296 [wpt PR 64314] - blink: Plumb canvas HDR metadata to Skia image encoders, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nblink: Plumb canvas HDR metadata to Skia image encoders\n\nWhen encoding a canvas via toDataURL, toBlob, or convertToBlob, convert\nits gfx::HDRMetadata to skhdr::Metadata and pass it to SkJpegEncoder,\nSkPngRustEncoder, and SkWebpEncoder via Options::fHdrMetadata.\n\nAdd a test to ensure that when we encode a canvas with HDR metadata to\nan image, the resulting image draws values brighter than white.\n\nIn ImageEncoderUtils::GetColorInfoForEncoder, indicate that extended\nrange content should be encoded as PQ.\n\nTAG=agy\nCONV=07d52b57-215d-40f6-aae6-c94aa32bbea1\n\nBug: 515698973\nChange-Id: I7aea586a8539a5189fe55293a5f80ec57cc0ef54\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8626547\nCommit-Queue: ccameron chromium \u003cccameron@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Khushal Sagar \u003ckhushalsagar@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1729629}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 81db4108ed9849bacd218027d3d9cd9b8b88317b\nwpt-pr: 64314\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/wide-gamut-canvas/encode-hdr.html"], "git_node": "d2676e903a6d35e988bb31ba60a1206495a64109", "git_parents": ["8c63b3dbe134043a5f0b6e022e61a1d169e70b1c"], "node": "52b5b58e6ab52c287a3900c20637fb4983990345", "parents": ["329af2e63840a49ca32a3ae4f99f906f3c5f6ca9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089296 [wpt PR 64314] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64314\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/wide-gamut-canvas/encode-hdr.html.ini"], "git_node": "da3798e21a414eedf9fd1abd15c5bf50727d62ab", "git_parents": ["d2676e903a6d35e988bb31ba60a1206495a64109"], "node": "6f3a802e8f14fc7063001ab9ab0a0b1262830a41", "parents": ["52b5b58e6ab52c287a3900c20637fb4983990345"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089297 [wpt PR 64353] - Fix SVGAngle.valueAsString to use CSS number serialization, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix SVGAngle.valueAsString to use CSS number serialization\n\nThis patch updates SVGAngle::ValueAsString() to serialize numbers and\nunits via CSSNumericLiteralValue::Serialize(), matching SVGLength and\nfixing -0 (\"0deg\") and scientific notation (\"1e+06deg\" instead of\n\"1.00000e+6deg\") serialization per SVG 2 and CSSOM.\n\nIt also clamps overflowing SVGAngle unit conversions and calculations\nto finite float bounds so SVGAngle values remain finite and round-trip\nvia valueAsString.\n\nIncorporates changes from WebKit commit\nhttps://commits.webkit.org/321460@main by Ahmad Saleem.\n\nChange-Id: I46be191fa48556e4ba343a244d536793f27f675a\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8665359\nReviewed-by: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1730607}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: cb8c205ff4d413ec4145a96a7b393446499e218b\nwpt-pr: 64353\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/types/scripted/SVGAngle-valueAsString.html"], "git_node": "bd31900193a5cc15bcad0fe521c606ca34cdefc3", "git_parents": ["da3798e21a414eedf9fd1abd15c5bf50727d62ab"], "node": "1b1372c412986340bf8033f7cb96e4bfdafae0b4", "parents": ["6f3a802e8f14fc7063001ab9ab0a0b1262830a41"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089297 [wpt PR 64353] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64353\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/svg/types/scripted/SVGAngle-valueAsString.html.ini"], "git_node": "c8ea081ae28855178532cb26a7db5f80807ad958", "git_parents": ["bd31900193a5cc15bcad0fe521c606ca34cdefc3"], "node": "39cb63c5a42e5a7c537f016e37444a63715158c3", "parents": ["1b1372c412986340bf8033f7cb96e4bfdafae0b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090745 - [wpt-sync] Update web-platform-tests to cb8c205ff4d413ec4145a96a7b393446499e218b, a=testonly\n\nMANUAL PUSH: wpt sync bot\n\nwpt-head: cb8c205ff4d413ec4145a96a7b393446499e218b\nwpt-type: landing\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/aria/aamtests/aria_errormessage_not_exposed_condition.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/aria/aamtests/aria_errormessage_not_exposed_condition_dynamic.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/connection-allowlist/tentative/service-worker-dedicated-worker.https.sub.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/connection-allowlist/tentative/service-worker-shared-worker.https.sub.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/content-security-policy/font-src/shared-stylesheet-font-cache-bypass-strict-first.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/floats/float-in-block-in-inline-position-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/normal-flow/block-in-inline-self-collapsing-margin-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/normal-flow/nested-inline-boxes-around-block-in-inline-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/visudet/inline-block-baseline-with-block-in-inline-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/baseline-rules/first-baseline-block-in-inline-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/transform-024.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-animations/inherited-animation-opacity.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-animations/inherited-animation-transform.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/box-decoration-break-clone-block-in-inline-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-multicol/multicol-nested-011.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-baseline-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/unrelated-gesture-scroll-during-snap.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-view-transitions/offscreen-element-modified-before-coming-onscreen.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-writing-modes/orthogonal-block-in-inline-line-height-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/device-bound-session-credentials/debug-header.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/device-memory/idlharness.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encoding/json-document-utf8.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/clearkey-mp4-playback-temporary-multikey-sequential-readyState.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fullscreen/api/fullscreen-change-event-shape.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fullscreen/rendering/backdrop-object.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/the-window-object/open-close/open-features-tokenization-noopener.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/the-window-object/window-aliases.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/the-window-object/window-indexed-access-vs-named-access.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/the-window-object/window-open-invalid-url.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/content-not-culled.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-object-fit-nested-canvas.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/text/2d.text.measure.lang.inherit.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/document-isolation-policy/cross-origin-isolated-permissions-policy.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/sizes/sizes-2d.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-img-element/sizes/sizes-auto-2d.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/interactive-elements/the-summary-element/interactive-content.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/popovers/popover-removal-hides.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/modulepreload-referrerpolicy.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/webappapis/dynamic-markup-insertion/opening-the-input-stream/url.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/intersection-observer/scroll-margin-dynamic.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/intersection-observer/scroll-margin-percent.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/long-animation-frame/loaf-cross-origin-isolated.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/longtask-timing/idlharness.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mozilla-sync", "testing/web-platform/meta/payment-method-manifest/link-header-target-url.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/payment-method-manifest/pmi-redirects.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-attributes.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-bfcache-reasons-stay.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-bfcache.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-cross-origin-bfcache.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-iframes-without-attributes.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-not-bfcached.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-redirect-on-history.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-reload.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-same-origin-bfcache.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/performance-timeline/not-restored-reasons/performance-navigation-timing-same-origin-replace.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/push-api/window-pushManager-non-secure-context.http.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/push-api/window-pushManager.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/push-api/worker-subscribe.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/screen-wake-lock/wakelock-document-hidden.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/no-vary-search/prefetch-single-with-hint.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/speculation-measurement/performance-speculations-preconnect.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/speculation-measurement/performance-speculations-unused-preload.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/storage-access-api/requestStorageAccess-service-worker.sub.https.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/idlharness.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/touch-events/hover-state-caused-by-compatibility-mouse-events.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/wasm/core/relaxed-simd/relaxed_madd_nmadd.wast.js.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/serialization-to-shared-and-service-workers.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/videoFrame-orientation-imageBitmap.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/websockets/send-many-64K-messages-with-backpressure.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webtransport/datagrams2.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/bidi/start_alignment.html.ini"], "git_node": "05011039e90c7ad9da43058d683f555c65be9f76", "git_parents": ["c8ea081ae28855178532cb26a7db5f80807ad958"], "node": "ec0589f1f5c3be49f896fab763ccada876331788", "parents": ["39cb63c5a42e5a7c537f016e37444a63715158c3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2019782 - Remove animation-only style traversal. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-reviewers,hiro,boris\n\nThis wasn't that terrible. Keep the before_change_style in the\nElementData (note that it doesn't take extra space because the jemalloc\nbucket size is 32 bytes), and use it from our descendants instead.\n\nMain tricky bit is the fixme for bug 2091537, which forces us to add\nthat rather awful tracking of \"animation-only recascade\".\n\nFor now I think I'd like to land this tho, it's a lot better than what\nwe have today.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341572\n", "files": ["dom/base/Element.cpp", "dom/base/Element.h", "layout/style/GeckoBindings.cpp", "layout/style/GeckoBindings.h", "layout/style/RestyleManager.h", "layout/style/ServoStyleSet.cpp", "layout/style/ServoTypes.h", "servo/components/style/data.rs", "servo/components/style/dom.rs", "servo/components/style/gecko/wrapper.rs", "servo/components/style/invalidation/element/restyle_hints.rs", "servo/components/style/matching.rs", "servo/components/style/style_resolver.rs", "servo/components/style/traversal.rs", "servo/components/style/traversal_flags.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/glue.rs"], "git_node": "5d9460dae7d00daa75f9a7d88f223aefff65809b", "git_parents": ["05011039e90c7ad9da43058d683f555c65be9f76"], "node": "f3ab7f1736741c8229c91cf3e80bbf1b35b1682a", "parents": ["ec0589f1f5c3be49f896fab763ccada876331788"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1570474 - Fix clicking on the context menu item in browser_urlbar_selection.js and re-enable on Mac. r=Standard8,urlbar-reviewers\" for causing bc failures @ browser_urlbar_selection.js\n\nThis reverts commit 1c36ae4eb6832bc6b5838dc3db4ecf416ac677b3.\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-editing/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-editing/browser_urlbar_selection.js"], "git_node": "73631e3fe3a51a80e8d4a67f2b8f49fafc7b4245", "git_parents": ["5d9460dae7d00daa75f9a7d88f223aefff65809b"], "node": "7dd647d1e6a2015ff809a2bacd8effaa6de4d9de", "parents": ["f3ab7f1736741c8229c91cf3e80bbf1b35b1682a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091272 - Use a better hash for Sanitizer names. r=dom-core-reviewers,keithamus\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341365\n", "files": ["dom/security/sanitizer/SanitizerTypes.h"], "git_node": "7a81190e0379334756130bb0f8e74733772cbfd3", "git_parents": ["73631e3fe3a51a80e8d4a67f2b8f49fafc7b4245"], "node": "679f6fda10523ea0979fd6de7d3cceaeae3cd715", "parents": ["7dd647d1e6a2015ff809a2bacd8effaa6de4d9de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091633 - [riscv64] Emit the code word after ebreak only in simulator builds. r=csmantle\n\nebreak has no immediate field, so break_ follows it with lui zero, code\nto carry the code. Only the simulator reads the code, to tell stops,\nwatchpoints and tracepoints from other breaks. Hardware traps at the\nebreak and never reaches the lui, so emit it only in simulator builds.\n\nIn a JetStream 3 run on a SpacemiT K3 this removes 75,558 words, 302 KB\nof JIT code: 40,297 in Wasm code, 30,878 in Ion code, 4,016 in Baseline\ncode and 367 in trampolines. All of them follow a breakpoint() with code\n0.\n\nFound with riscvlint.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341705\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/riscv64/Assembler-riscv64.cpp"], "git_node": "5f922a344d71c07d91f1880ec31d360536bc1d51", "git_parents": ["7a81190e0379334756130bb0f8e74733772cbfd3"], "node": "63669d1a69d9208424b6861b973ba8c31cef2e22", "parents": ["679f6fda10523ea0979fd6de7d3cceaeae3cd715"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091045 - [riscv64] Shift the operand of halfword atomics when Zbb is unavailable. r=csmantle\n\nWithout Zbb, AtomicShiftToOffset shifted the uninitialized destination register\ninstead of the operand, so halfword read-modify-write and compare-exchange\noperations used garbage. The simulator enables Zbb by default, so no test ran\nthis path. Accept --riscv-ext on every platform, as --arm-hwcap is, so that\njit-tests can add a variant that only runs on riscv64.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341006\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/atomics/bug1983499.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/atomic.js", "js/src/jit/riscv64/MacroAssembler-riscv64.cpp", "js/src/shell/js.cpp"], "git_node": "a56eb0b68359fe20aaee49125b669876f32072b9", "git_parents": ["5f922a344d71c07d91f1880ec31d360536bc1d51"], "node": "2fe14902ef7ac1c64866c907ca859f91787a22a6", "parents": ["63669d1a69d9208424b6861b973ba8c31cef2e22"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2084900 [Linux] Use RenderLinuxTextureHost for Wayland compositor and make direct composition optional r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\" or causing reftest failures\n\nThis reverts commit 9ccb307dba3ef16ea20a609dd82b7c04286c58e7.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2084900 [Linux] Merge WaylandTextureHost and RenderDMABUFTextureHost to RenderLinuxTextureHost r=lsalzman,gfx-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 94ccf09d24a95cd5adf5d38569e0fc39dc05c1ae.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2084900 [Linux] Implement SHMBufSurface::MapPlane() and remove YCbCrDescriptor from SHMSurface r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 8318552e677edeaba1b7d94db85a7f8bf5ddeab7.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2084900 [Linux] Export BufferSurface from WaylandBuffer r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit b3d5d92511de9a8efc1a4ae7c9c9ba97f3e8c2c1.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2084900 [Linux] Add BufferSurface::SupportsDirectComposition() flag to configure direct offload to Wayland compositor r=emilio,gtk-reviewers\"\"\n\nThis reverts commit 374b08bae655287c3f0525354e034611d6ca2abf.\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/NativeLayerWayland.cpp", "gfx/layers/NativeLayerWayland.h", "gfx/layers/composite/TextureHost.cpp", "gfx/layers/opengl/DMABUFTextureHostOGL.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorLayerNative.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositorNative.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderDMABUFTextureHost.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderDMABUFTextureHost.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderLinuxTextureHost.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderLinuxTextureHost.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderTextureHost.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderTextureHostWrapper.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderTextureHostWrapper.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderWaylandTextureHost.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderWaylandTextureHost.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RendererOGL.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/moz.build", "widget/gtk/BufferSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/BufferSurface.h", "widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/SHMBufSurface.h", "widget/gtk/WaylandBuffer.h"], "git_node": "165ca697d99d2d8a05fc689158201cd7f332ff2f", "git_parents": ["a56eb0b68359fe20aaee49125b669876f32072b9"], "node": "f6b52826df235c2ae8713a8a40025b5eed4db3df", "parents": ["2fe14902ef7ac1c64866c907ca859f91787a22a6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087045 - Update wpt metadata in color-computed-relative-color.html. r=sasha\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-color/parsing/color-computed-relative-color.html.ini"], "git_node": "da8abb5dc2c47aaadddcb4d28fff95f1458dad9a", "git_parents": ["165ca697d99d2d8a05fc689158201cd7f332ff2f"], "node": "242658e9255c0aafbf05eecfcd349a3496e9ecaf", "parents": ["f6b52826df235c2ae8713a8a40025b5eed4db3df"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090745 - Update wpt metadata on worker-subscribe.https.window.html on aarch64. r=sasha\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/push-api/worker-subscribe.https.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "e458bf99373606f78c69ee6014ac6eec5291744d", "git_parents": ["da8abb5dc2c47aaadddcb4d28fff95f1458dad9a"], "node": "ceb5154dff21d867b23bae5da5b8eedaf9a51d94", "parents": ["242658e9255c0aafbf05eecfcd349a3496e9ecaf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Henri Sivonen \u003chsivonen@hsivonen.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091721 - Fix release date for Rust 1.99.0 in docs. r=sylvestre\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341785\n", "files": ["docs/writing-rust-code/update-policy.md"], "git_node": "2b8320d8218b72c9021e6580abca2e8966ab1483", "git_parents": ["e458bf99373606f78c69ee6014ac6eec5291744d"], "node": "f531e17587a4fd0b27864dc6bec1cf2b501fe949", "parents": ["ceb5154dff21d867b23bae5da5b8eedaf9a51d94"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Segun Famisa \u003csfamisa@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091691 - Update Gradle to version 9.9.1 r=android-reviewers,android-build-system-reviewers,pollymce,adhingra\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341763\n", "files": ["gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties", "mobile/android/android-components/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties", "mobile/android/fenix/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties", "mobile/android/focus-android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties"], "git_node": "2e7cdf867a8dcf52c981b82335c794b5d63ba78f", "git_parents": ["2b8320d8218b72c9021e6580abca2e8966ab1483"], "node": "d7cad09c997bdfc970a836e6c5da6f8806e11cd2", "parents": ["f531e17587a4fd0b27864dc6bec1cf2b501fe949"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2012815 - Declare a tab's splitViewId in session.schema.json. r=sfoster,sessionstore-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339516\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/session.schema.json"], "git_node": "d10482fa4d14a0467808391b3dd4e743a3c4eae7", "git_parents": ["2e7cdf867a8dcf52c981b82335c794b5d63ba78f"], "node": "3c1127c021489e49ebc0d158fd49ff8572435bcc", "parents": ["d7cad09c997bdfc970a836e6c5da6f8806e11cd2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1991409 - Declare the session state properties Firefox writes in session.schema.json, and reject undeclared ones. r=sfoster,sessionstore-reviewers\n\nThe schema moves to draft 2020-12 for `unevaluatedProperties`: draft-07's `additionalProperties: false` beside an `allOf` ignores the properties the `allOf` declares, so every closed window failed validation.\n\n`required` now lists only what every write has. Closed windows, closed tabs and tabs that haven't restored yet are written back as they were loaded, and the session history reader treats an entry's `title` and `hasUserInteraction` as optional.\n\nPrivate, taskbar tab and mini windows are never written, so `isPrivate`, `isTaskbarTab` and `isMiniWindow` stay undeclared.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339517\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/session.schema.json"], "git_node": "629aec83c40a138516b770395ca53d423257c6d3", "git_parents": ["d10482fa4d14a0467808391b3dd4e743a3c4eae7"], "node": "04187726bae6ecd027ae5c9360c2de9533a2bae4", "parents": ["3c1127c021489e49ebc0d158fd49ff8572435bcc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088825 - Validate session state against session.schema.json on each write when browser.sessionstore.debug.validate_state is set. r=sfoster,sessionstore-reviewers\n\nSessionStore.validateState stops warning about an invalid state: SessionSaver reports it, and test_session_schema.js, its other caller, logs the errors itself.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339518\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionSaver.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "testing/mochitest/browser-test.js"], "git_node": "d1cd946b496c93504d2897127e376cbe69b9e834", "git_parents": ["629aec83c40a138516b770395ca53d423257c6d3"], "node": "3c890445fdf7d519b662b1978ddee1a78e620161", "parents": ["04187726bae6ecd027ae5c9360c2de9533a2bae4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088825 - Validate written session state in the session store browser tests. r=sfoster,sessionstore-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339519\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser.toml", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_394759_purge.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_491168.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_491577.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_formdata_format.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_oldformat.toml", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_restore_cookies_noOriginAttributes.js", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_startup_telemetry.toml"], "git_node": "ec31fb47e960d42da4fdc9d5469cc78a93ef614d", "git_parents": ["d1cd946b496c93504d2897127e376cbe69b9e834"], "node": "c567029ad9da46616f4277fc19b5dcc710aacfe6", "parents": ["3c890445fdf7d519b662b1978ddee1a78e620161"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088825 - Document why most session state properties are optional. r=sfoster,sessionstore-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339520\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/types/sessionstore.ts"], "git_node": "eb40b47fe7ab8550643c4c6d504ec28ab913caaa", "git_parents": ["ec31fb47e960d42da4fdc9d5469cc78a93ef614d"], "node": "c1ee6479dac79ddb4a9131c651c8da4ea125bcaf", "parents": ["c567029ad9da46616f4277fc19b5dcc710aacfe6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087206 - Part 3 - Ignore key presses on disabled focused controls. r=reusable-components-reviewers,hjones,emilio\n\nControls that keeps focus after becoming disabled still handle key presses.\n\nThis change makes nsGenericHTMLElement::HandleKeyboardActivation and\nHTMLInputElement::PostHandleEvent clear pending keyboard activation and skip\ndefault key handling while the control is disabled.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338542\n", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLInputElement.cpp", "dom/html/nsGenericHTMLElement.cpp", "dom/html/test/test_disabled_focus.html", "toolkit/content/widgets/datetimebox.js"], "git_node": "5dcac056bfbc1812f75b8b5e766d6b685d7d9665", "git_parents": ["eb40b47fe7ab8550643c4c6d504ec28ab913caaa"], "node": "e5ebbebaa7cc54f5b15c259ae50cde9830cfb154", "parents": ["c1ee6479dac79ddb4a9131c651c8da4ea125bcaf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Harvey \u003cdale@arandomurl.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091321 - Use moz-src for toolkit/components/cleardata r=geckoview-reviewers,extension-reviewers,m_kato,rpl\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341313\n", "files": ["browser/modules/Sanitizer.sys.mjs", "mobile/shared/modules/geckoview/GeckoViewStorageController.sys.mjs", "testing/specialpowers/content/SpecialPowersParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/cleardata/ClearDataService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/cleardata/components.conf", "toolkit/components/cleardata/moz.build", "toolkit/components/extensions/Extension.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/extensions/parent/ext-browsingData.js", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.modules.d.ts", "tools/@types/generated/tspaths.json", "tools/lint/extra-js-modules/allowlist.txt"], "git_node": "204f579def9ded958be07f6aa7806e5f3e46e993", "git_parents": ["5dcac056bfbc1812f75b8b5e766d6b685d7d9665"], "node": "bb1d196941fd8218dc3811e86d51100cb0779059", "parents": ["e5ebbebaa7cc54f5b15c259ae50cde9830cfb154"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091511 - Implement document.parsed/contentLoaded/loaded r=dom-core-reviewers,webidl,hsivonen\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341525\n", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/Document.h", "dom/webidl/Document.webidl", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/documents/resource-metadata-management/document-promises-with-defer-script.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/documents/resource-metadata-management/document-promises-with-document-open-inside-domcontentloaded-of-parsed-document.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/documents/resource-metadata-management/document-promises-with-document-open-inside-domcontentloaded.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/documents/resource-metadata-management/document-promises-with-document-open.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/documents/resource-metadata-management/document-promises.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/idlharness.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/documents/resource-metadata-management/document-promises-with-defer-script.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/documents/resource-metadata-management/document-promises-with-document-open-inside-domcontentloaded-of-parsed-document.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/documents/resource-metadata-management/document-promises-with-document-open-inside-domcontentloaded.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/documents/resource-metadata-management/document-promises-with-document-open.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/documents/resource-metadata-management/document-promises.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/document-load-promises.tentative.idl"], "git_node": "fd4f14b77dcb1c1daadf0f2476d1729cd39a78d6", "git_parents": ["204f579def9ded958be07f6aa7806e5f3e46e993"], "node": "f02e55a700525aa90b9b784b98de607a54593ef3", "parents": ["bb1d196941fd8218dc3811e86d51100cb0779059"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091697 - Stop the heading offset walk at any shadow root with no host r=dom-core-reviewers,jjaschke\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341764\n", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLHeadingElement.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/sections/headingoffset-nested-shadow-roots-crash.html"], "git_node": "cca90bd8e5c3c059edb71f059d17e056a95fa568", "git_parents": ["fd4f14b77dcb1c1daadf0f2476d1729cd39a78d6"], "node": "1bfa99c53a99b30686d16fcb652812b573865ead", "parents": ["f02e55a700525aa90b9b784b98de607a54593ef3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2044348 - Enable headingoffset by default r=dom-core-reviewers,jjaschke\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340303\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/idlharness.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "51d5cddf4194b250ceb5b34bac85b6972065a2e1", "git_parents": ["cca90bd8e5c3c059edb71f059d17e056a95fa568"], "node": "0620a1dd63cc5cc29d7f494529435711a4ac2d46", "parents": ["1bfa99c53a99b30686d16fcb652812b573865ead"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089602 - Keep default permissions when clearing a site's permissions. r=permissions-reviewers,timhuang\n\nThe permission cleaners called removePermission on default permissions,\nwhich writes an entry to the database that hides the default for good.\nAdd removePermissionsExceptDefaults so bulk clears skip defaults, like\nthe other bulk removal methods already do. removePermission keeps its\nbehaviour for explicit removals.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340914\n", "files": ["extensions/permissions/PermissionManager.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsIPermissionManager.idl", "toolkit/components/cleardata/ClearDataService.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "616d4909633f25d0ccad85f2c101b385f9d2d4c4", "git_parents": ["51d5cddf4194b250ceb5b34bac85b6972065a2e1"], "node": "9fb2436630b7a54a13d2ce7d5c5a3b2aa7ef1bb5", "parents": ["0620a1dd63cc5cc29d7f494529435711a4ac2d46"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089602 - Test that clearing a site's permissions keeps default permissions. r=permissions-reviewers,timhuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340915\n", "files": ["extensions/permissions/test/unit/test_permmanager_removePermissionsExceptDefaults.js", "extensions/permissions/test/unit/xpcshell.toml", "toolkit/components/cleardata/tests/unit/test_permissions.js"], "git_node": "81319f111c32b7a9afc62447f5a47e271463d625", "git_parents": ["616d4909633f25d0ccad85f2c101b385f9d2d4c4"], "node": "7e9f55497d6eaaf4b68530b8173cf0a9772d2854", "parents": ["9fb2436630b7a54a13d2ce7d5c5a3b2aa7ef1bb5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082302 - Parse processing instructions in HTML r=keithamus,hsivonen\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334017\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp", "dom/base/test/test_bug744830.html", "dom/locales/en-US/chrome/layout/htmlparser.properties", "parser/html/javasrc/Tokenizer.java", "parser/html/javasrc/TreeBuilder.java", "parser/html/nsHtml5Parser.cpp", "parser/html/nsHtml5StreamParser.cpp", "parser/html/nsHtml5StringParser.cpp", "parser/html/nsHtml5Tokenizer.cpp", "parser/html/nsHtml5Tokenizer.h", "parser/html/nsHtml5TokenizerCppSupplement.h", "parser/html/nsHtml5TokenizerHSupplement.h", "parser/html/nsHtml5TreeBuilder.cpp", "parser/html/nsHtml5TreeBuilder.h", "parser/html/nsHtml5TreeBuilderCppSupplement.h", "parser/html/nsHtml5TreeOperation.cpp", "parser/html/nsHtml5TreeOperation.h", "parser/htmlparser/tests/mochitest/mochitest.toml", "parser/htmlparser/tests/mochitest/test_processing_instruction_parsing.html", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/syntax/serializing-html-fragments/processing-instructions.html.ini"], "git_node": "68f9ff82252b9ae4b996778632cac8adbaa70370", "git_parents": ["81319f111c32b7a9afc62447f5a47e271463d625"], "node": "0b99f5d384e4d95143898ff1fca02058c83bbd3f", "parents": ["7e9f55497d6eaaf4b68530b8173cf0a9772d2854"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090203 - Document token categories and autofix mappings on the use-design-tokens rule page. r=hjones\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340422\n", "files": ["docs/code-quality/lint/linters/stylelint-plugin-mozilla/rules/use-design-tokens.md"], "git_node": "e6279bc0c34146d47c5cd5625fb7472cc0b93af3", "git_parents": ["68f9ff82252b9ae4b996778632cac8adbaa70370"], "node": "2a77e657e07b9c3d262ccef02c25a6878602fbc3", "parents": ["0b99f5d384e4d95143898ff1fca02058c83bbd3f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090203 - Point desktop-theme-tokens' lint notes at the use-design-tokens rule page. r=ai4dev-reviewers,padenot DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340423\n", "files": [".agents/skills/desktop-theme-tokens/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-tokens/SKILL.md"], "git_node": "e02bd005751fb83ceca678251bac91d05404b1f0", "git_parents": ["e6279bc0c34146d47c5cd5625fb7472cc0b93af3"], "node": "8c67df8b5568e3a494f1a3177d35ada71962498b", "parents": ["2a77e657e07b9c3d262ccef02c25a6878602fbc3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090203 - Document the in-tree defaults, current tools and restart behaviour of the firefox-devtools-mcp server. r=jdescottes\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340418\n", "files": ["docs/ai-agent-tools/firefox-devtools-mcp.md"], "git_node": "0160faa3d13e30335e1637f32be44c985c3c604c", "git_parents": ["e02bd005751fb83ceca678251bac91d05404b1f0"], "node": "e8e82546cba540adf8430febfc4370c52b5a4dc3", "parents": ["8c67df8b5568e3a494f1a3177d35ada71962498b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090203 - Point desktop-theme-probing's devtools MCP notes at the firefox-devtools-mcp docs. r=ai4dev-reviewers,padenot DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340419\n", "files": [".agents/skills/desktop-theme-probing/references/devtools-mcp.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-probing/references/devtools-mcp.md"], "git_node": "30cf230573e201ec58ba3dae971914d28f4142ef", "git_parents": ["0160faa3d13e30335e1637f32be44c985c3c604c"], "node": "5efee2774d9b66930a1debc9a62dea4c1ba81f66", "parents": ["e8e82546cba540adf8430febfc4370c52b5a4dc3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Harvey \u003cdale@arandomurl.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091310 - Use moz-src for toolkit/components/backgroundhangmonitor r=Gijs\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341302\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/backgroundhangmonitor/components.conf", "toolkit/components/backgroundhangmonitor/moz.build", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.modules.d.ts", "tools/@types/generated/tspaths.json", "tools/lint/extra-js-modules/allowlist.txt"], "git_node": "1ace8f6de38e9ed6cd8a0d6ba321ee13c3ba4e72", "git_parents": ["30cf230573e201ec58ba3dae971914d28f4142ef"], "node": "93dbe8494659e1f06b578fe7d9be9f79d9565ae7", "parents": ["5efee2774d9b66930a1debc9a62dea4c1ba81f66"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maryam \u003cmomar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062028 - Add the tracker allow list prefs to the privacy capabilities matrix r=mraiber\n\nTheir strict-mode values come from the initial values in\nCATEGORY_PREFS.strict rather than from a feature-string token, so parse\nthose from ContentBlockingPrefs.sys.mjs and apply the feature-string\nassignments on top, matching setPrefExpectations().\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D320008\n", "files": ["docs/_addons/etp_matrix.py"], "git_node": "2b52cf626e3203e001aab68daca85f50bcf13f4e", "git_parents": ["1ace8f6de38e9ed6cd8a0d6ba321ee13c3ba4e72"], "node": "5a3a8fae457797f2e1bcdde511b9dac952ab4f05", "parents": ["93dbe8494659e1f06b578fe7d9be9f79d9565ae7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Moritz Beier \u003cmbeier@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1570474 - Fix clicking on the context menu item in browser_urlbar_selection.js and re-enable on Mac. r=Standard8,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341720\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-editing/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-editing/browser_urlbar_selection.js"], "git_node": "da06ee89372106ee2469dbb18e9314f5eef2b6f8", "git_parents": ["2b52cf626e3203e001aab68daca85f50bcf13f4e"], "node": "5ba48d268eae7ec914c774581308f23a78eee6e1", "parents": ["5a3a8fae457797f2e1bcdde511b9dac952ab4f05"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066381 - Remove unused AudioNodeTrack::AdvanceAndResume. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nThe only caller was removed in bug 1259831. It is also the only writer of\nMediaTrack::mMainThreadCurrentTime outside the graph's main thread state\nupdates, which stands in the way of making that a mirror.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322623\n", "files": ["dom/media/webaudio/AudioDestinationNode.cpp", "dom/media/webaudio/AudioNodeTrack.cpp", "dom/media/webaudio/AudioNodeTrack.h"], "git_node": "62fc2612f062d226fbb167e852a45d09e3ce69db", "git_parents": ["da06ee89372106ee2469dbb18e9314f5eef2b6f8"], "node": "e477a4caf57fff51f7a22a9f94000a45ebc852cc", "parents": ["5ba48d268eae7ec914c774581308f23a78eee6e1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066381 - Add per-track canonicals for current time and ended state. r=karlt,media-playback-reviewers,webrtc-reviewers,bwc\n\nThis allows time and ended updates on any control thread, not only main thread.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322624\n", "files": ["dom/media/DeviceInputTrack.cpp", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.h", "dom/media/gtest/TestAudioTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/TestDeviceInputTrack.cpp", "dom/media/mediasink/AudioDecoderInputTrack.cpp", "dom/media/webaudio/AudioNodeExternalInputTrack.cpp", "dom/media/webaudio/AudioNodeTrack.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/MediaEngineWebRTCAudio.cpp", "media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/mediapipeline_unittest.cpp"], "git_node": "ee14ed78358c85e8114f718c7603f56a55778f12", "git_parents": ["62fc2612f062d226fbb167e852a45d09e3ce69db"], "node": "42699c8edd10302cf9e33b823dae9ad9e687a37d", "parents": ["e477a4caf57fff51f7a22a9f94000a45ebc852cc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066381 - Simplify MediaStreamRenderer current time tracking. r=karlt,media-playback-reviewers\n\nInstead of calculating offsets between current time updates on main thread\nwhile playing, we use a dedicated SourceMediaTrack that is suspended while\nnot rendering, and mirror its current time. The graph then does the time\nkeeping across pause/resume cycles.\n\ncurrentTime and timeupdate are synchronous with pause() and play() by spec,\nbut the mirror is async and may still advance until the suspend takes effect\non the graph thread. So the mirror is relayed to the media element through a\nWatchable only while currentTime is progressing.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336851\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.h", "dom/media/mediaelement/HTMLMediaElement.cpp"], "git_node": "7097cc18590ef9031214c6b9dae8fc252dd010d0", "git_parents": ["ee14ed78358c85e8114f718c7603f56a55778f12"], "node": "e5e1dc95612d553ce685551eb7eadc90fde0e3e9", "parents": ["42699c8edd10302cf9e33b823dae9ad9e687a37d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066381 - Remove the MediaTrackGraph's main thread current time. r=padenot\n\nMediaStreamRenderer was the only user of the graph's main thread graph time,\nand now mirrors the current time of a track it owns instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338720\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.h", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraphImpl.h"], "git_node": "98183bf061e038826769f2f6724443717c34d363", "git_parents": ["7097cc18590ef9031214c6b9dae8fc252dd010d0"], "node": "796a7a400b88147007183464f15f4528e93d0f94", "parents": ["e5e1dc95612d553ce685551eb7eadc90fde0e3e9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066381 - Mirror OscillatorNode's track ended state. r=karlt,media-playback-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322625\n", "files": ["dom/media/webaudio/OscillatorNode.cpp", "dom/media/webaudio/OscillatorNode.h"], "git_node": "bb3f55102b2e64ed70fbf29b9f83aac8799daf18", "git_parents": ["98183bf061e038826769f2f6724443717c34d363"], "node": "5a61fd2b6973fb97eca00e0b8d3ac742481b60c8", "parents": ["796a7a400b88147007183464f15f4528e93d0f94"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066381 - Mirror ConstantSourceNode's track ended state. r=karlt,media-playback-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322626\n", "files": ["dom/media/webaudio/ConstantSourceNode.cpp", "dom/media/webaudio/ConstantSourceNode.h"], "git_node": "799e4c64a62d4acb2ff3eff6dfced81711351373", "git_parents": ["bb3f55102b2e64ed70fbf29b9f83aac8799daf18"], "node": "c5efb084e3773ebdf99383e9a2a92b1c24db571c", "parents": ["5a61fd2b6973fb97eca00e0b8d3ac742481b60c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066381 - Mirror AudioBufferSourceNode's track ended state. r=karlt,media-playback-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322627\n", "files": ["dom/media/webaudio/AudioBufferSourceNode.cpp", "dom/media/webaudio/AudioBufferSourceNode.h"], "git_node": "6e8266789b98fb433f81b633f8a79198f6dcbf38", "git_parents": ["799e4c64a62d4acb2ff3eff6dfced81711351373"], "node": "8d1b4a9795a4cad4cd6936e712471c1e67344234", "parents": ["c5efb084e3773ebdf99383e9a2a92b1c24db571c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066381 - Mirror AudioDestinationNode's track ended state. r=karlt,media-playback-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322628\n", "files": ["dom/media/webaudio/AudioDestinationNode.cpp", "dom/media/webaudio/AudioDestinationNode.h"], "git_node": "6cbde7a649249fcf03abf509bfb33c78de531881", "git_parents": ["6e8266789b98fb433f81b633f8a79198f6dcbf38"], "node": "baa2eec839bad7ee363c4e05ce9ed210e213bd12", "parents": ["8d1b4a9795a4cad4cd6936e712471c1e67344234"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066381 - Mirror the destination track's current time for AudioContext. r=karlt,media-playback-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322629\n", "files": ["dom/media/webaudio/AudioContext.cpp", "dom/media/webaudio/AudioDestinationNode.cpp", "dom/media/webaudio/AudioDestinationNode.h"], "git_node": "412b1c4734dc958e769feb1641398472b83a168f", "git_parents": ["6cbde7a649249fcf03abf509bfb33c78de531881"], "node": "919c1354d1f6a29b24f89dbb0f75cc35ea663d4a", "parents": ["baa2eec839bad7ee363c4e05ce9ed210e213bd12"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2066381 - Remove the main thread track update mechanism. r=karlt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322630\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.h", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraphImpl.h"], "git_node": "807fdeecbddc9a6c02082aaa9fa7b358c800f348", "git_parents": ["412b1c4734dc958e769feb1641398472b83a168f"], "node": "ba93fd7a45632a08f47de90a99772fb5decd8862", "parents": ["919c1354d1f6a29b24f89dbb0f75cc35ea663d4a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2044348 - Enable headingoffset by default r=dom-core-reviewers,jjaschke\" for causing dt failures @ browser_webconsole_object_inspector_entries.js\n\nThis reverts commit 51d5cddf4194b250ceb5b34bac85b6972065a2e1.\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/idlharness.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "ed6d3f99f328e82752bfaa45ac3aa38f88662724", "git_parents": ["807fdeecbddc9a6c02082aaa9fa7b358c800f348"], "node": "71e19f586307e691c26d06a3e2e33780a538571a", "parents": ["ba93fd7a45632a08f47de90a99772fb5decd8862"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2091697 - Stop the heading offset walk at any shadow root with no host r=dom-core-reviewers,jjaschke\" for causing dt failures @ browser_webconsole_object_inspector_entries.js\n\nThis reverts commit cca90bd8e5c3c059edb71f059d17e056a95fa568.\n", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLHeadingElement.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/sections/headingoffset-nested-shadow-roots-crash.html"], "git_node": "7954bda3d2322d77f4775690c77cd4b100fdafe3", "git_parents": ["ed6d3f99f328e82752bfaa45ac3aa38f88662724"], "node": "004c3d490e5fdc17254fea5f9a349d366d9b5372", "parents": ["71e19f586307e691c26d06a3e2e33780a538571a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teow \u003cjteow@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2032010 - Remove flakyWaitForManyIdles from the urlbar quick actions tests - r=daleharvey,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341805\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-quickactions/browser_commands.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-quickactions/browser_tab_refocus.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/head-common.js"], "git_node": "6be84aa46b40d6d387ce443dd1184d4e93350bc5", "git_parents": ["7954bda3d2322d77f4775690c77cd4b100fdafe3"], "node": "153d18dcc26fba18f238da741b703722cc9370b6", "parents": ["004c3d490e5fdc17254fea5f9a349d366d9b5372"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephanie Cunnane \u003cscunnane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1857369 - Remove redundant pref setup from search telemetry browser tests. r=search-reviewers,Standard8\n\nDrop the categorization-enabled pushes that match the firefox.js default, and set the SPA process count once in initSinglePageAppTest.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341683\n", "files": ["browser/components/search/test/browser/telemetry/browser_search_telemetry_categorization_experiment_info.js", "browser/components/search/test/browser/telemetry/browser_search_telemetry_categorization_missing_impression.js", "browser/components/search/test/browser/telemetry/browser_search_telemetry_domain_categorization_ad_values.js", "browser/components/search/test/browser/telemetry/browser_search_telemetry_domain_categorization_extraction.js", "browser/components/search/test/browser/telemetry/browser_search_telemetry_domain_categorization_no_sponsored_values.js", "browser/components/search/test/browser/telemetry/browser_search_telemetry_domain_categorization_ping_submission.js", "browser/components/search/test/browser/telemetry/browser_search_telemetry_domain_categorization_region.js", "browser/components/search/test/browser/telemetry/browser_search_telemetry_domain_categorization_reporting.js", "browser/components/search/test/browser/telemetry/browser_search_telemetry_spa_in_content.js", "browser/components/search/test/browser/telemetry/browser_search_telemetry_spa_multi_provider.js", "browser/components/search/test/browser/telemetry/browser_search_telemetry_spa_multi_tab.js", "browser/components/search/test/browser/telemetry/head.js"], "git_node": "941e15323b19a64f0dd7a6bbd06f71b100df947e", "git_parents": ["6be84aa46b40d6d387ce443dd1184d4e93350bc5"], "node": "95741ec5f6f88545544e0051d468ac94340e5e2a", "parents": ["153d18dcc26fba18f238da741b703722cc9370b6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073679 - Report a slice as cloneable only when its wrapped stream is r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nSlicedInputStream::GetCloneable() returned true whenever the wrapped stream\nimplemented nsICloneableInputStream, but implementing that interface does not\nmean a stream can be cloned right now: nsMultiplexInputStream and\nnsBufferedInputStream both refuse once they have been read from.  Callers that\ncheck before cloning, such as NS_InputStreamIsCloneable(), were told yes and\nthen got a failure out of Clone().  Delegate to the wrapped stream, the way\nnsBufferedInputStream already does.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328176\n", "files": ["xpcom/io/SlicedInputStream.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestSlicedInputStream.cpp"], "git_node": "9a590624fdb6695c822588832c943a082574c7bf", "git_parents": ["941e15323b19a64f0dd7a6bbd06f71b100df947e"], "node": "add319190c581824dd4017f359c77eda64520518", "parents": ["95741ec5f6f88545544e0051d468ac94340e5e2a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073679 - Reject an upload stream that NormalizeUploadStream can't make cloneable r=necko-reviewers,nika\n\nNormalizeUploadStream() promises that a parent-process upload stream is\ncloneable, seekable and synchronous, but the nsIBufferedInputStream and\nnsIMultiplexInputStream branches normalized the streams they wrap and then\nreturned the wrapper untouched, even when the wrapper itself could not be\ncloned because it had already been read from.  Callers that rely on the\nguarantee, such as HttpBaseChannel::CloneUploadStream and\nnsHttpTransaction::Init, are then left unable to clone it.\n\nCheck whether the stream can be used as-is first, and fail when a wrapper\nwould otherwise be returned unchanged, as that means it has been read from\nand can't be rebuilt without losing the data it has buffered.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328177\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/HttpBaseChannel.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_upload_stream_normalization.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "3f58b4aaf582d4fca9b033b56bc4ec7cd569d9f1", "git_parents": ["9a590624fdb6695c822588832c943a082574c7bf"], "node": "47e3afa17b9b5cf2ccdb9959881b8db6823596a2", "parents": ["add319190c581824dd4017f359c77eda64520518"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073679 - Clear nsMultiplexInputStream's read state when seeking back to the start. r=xpcom-reviewers,jstutte\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341822\n", "files": ["xpcom/io/nsMultiplexInputStream.cpp", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestMultiplexInputStream.cpp"], "git_node": "7a138365c95397e2c976c4bc015be69926fbd670", "git_parents": ["3f58b4aaf582d4fca9b033b56bc4ec7cd569d9f1"], "node": "8f21861eaf9a4b8b546524a87b3f12d8fe84bf31", "parents": ["47e3afa17b9b5cf2ccdb9959881b8db6823596a2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073679 - Don't fall back to sharing a seekable upload stream with the socket thread r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nnsHttpTransaction::Init() reads the channel's own upload stream when it cannot\nclone it, which leaves the socket thread reading a stream the main thread may\nrewind for a redirect or an auth retry.  InternalSetUploadStream now refuses an\nupload stream that can't be cloned, so in the parent process make the fallback\nan error for seekable streams rather than sharing them, and assert that it\nisn't reached.  A stream the channel cannot rewind, such as an async pipe, is\nstill read directly.\n\nThe socket process is exempt: it reads its own deserialized copy of the body,\nwhich nothing else touches and which may not be cloneable (a file stream sent\nas a descriptor never is outside the parent).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328178\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpTransaction.cpp"], "git_node": "6022313d0d3c7f94eda2639020089af8abbe0ef4", "git_parents": ["7a138365c95397e2c976c4bc015be69926fbd670"], "node": "3503b6835fac0881976eb0ad9335d7812ea389d9", "parents": ["8f21861eaf9a4b8b546524a87b3f12d8fe84bf31"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074521 - Don't clone a non-seekable streaming upload body in nsHttpTransaction r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nA streaming body is usually an async pipe.  Cloning it adds a second reader\nthat nobody ever reads, so the pipe holds on to every segment written to it\nand buffers the whole upload in memory instead of staying at one pipe's\ncapacity.  HttpBaseChannel::CloneUploadStream already refuses to tee an upload\nstream for exactly that reason.\n\nOnly a parent-process fetch() with a ReadableStream body could hit this: a\ncontent-process streaming body crosses IPC as a DataPipeReceiver, which is not\ncloneable, so the clone attempt failed there anyway.\n\nA pipe can't be rewound, so the channel never touches it once the transaction\nhas it.  A streaming body can also be a Blob's own seekable stream, which the\nchannel may rewind for a redirect or an auth retry, so keep cloning that one.\nAdd a Blob stream case to test_fetch_streaming_upload.js.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328179\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpTransaction.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_fetch_streaming_upload.js"], "git_node": "bb91826f8579dbb2170e738aa62fc2ebf625ef90", "git_parents": ["6022313d0d3c7f94eda2639020089af8abbe0ef4"], "node": "a39a833ffb03ebeed550bc06107d516d3f6620c6", "parents": ["3503b6835fac0881976eb0ad9335d7812ea389d9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1906916 - Hide Manage Passwords in the context menu when password management is disabled by policy. r=credential-management-reviewers,joschmidt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340059\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/nsContextMenu.sys.mjs", "browser/base/content/test/browser-contextMenu/browser_contextmenu_input.js"], "git_node": "9da777a0dbf5db48978bc16cca6209cb71e4a4f4", "git_parents": ["bb91826f8579dbb2170e738aa62fc2ebf625ef90"], "node": "15f54a442dc0b005a228c6cc9a5ca3aaa325271e", "parents": ["a39a833ffb03ebeed550bc06107d516d3f6620c6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1891314 - Don't let the tab drag feedback panel intercept drag events. r=emilio,desktop-theme-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341845\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/tabs.css"], "git_node": "c6cecdbc28bf31586888fddcd55973733a072c91", "git_parents": ["9da777a0dbf5db48978bc16cca6209cb71e4a4f4"], "node": "a137568a0da6bc97772c9ce60df949ad7cc067fa", "parents": ["15f54a442dc0b005a228c6cc9a5ca3aaa325271e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marco Bonardo \u003cmbonardo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090014 - Remove the aAllowMissing argument of _getDOMNodeForPlacesNode. r=places-reviewers,Standard8\n\nMost callers already passed true, so the lookup just returns the entry and each caller decides what a missing one means.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340346\n", "files": ["browser/components/places/content/browserPlacesViews.js"], "git_node": "085b0afa52224d658bf44861a373f6a52d5aea8a", "git_parents": ["c6cecdbc28bf31586888fddcd55973733a072c91"], "node": "439b7137e49410a5789183d18ea8a6eb3e935fd9", "parents": ["a137568a0da6bc97772c9ce60df949ad7cc067fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marco Bonardo \u003cmbonardo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090014 - Forget removed menu items in Places views so _domNodes stays bounded. r=places-reviewers,Standard8\n\nEntries were only dropped when the whole result was replaced, so live queries kept every replaced node, and its DOM, alive.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340311\n", "files": ["browser/components/places/content/browserPlacesViews.js", "browser/components/places/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/places/tests/browser/browser_menu_domnodes_cleanup.js"], "git_node": "7259812b842fa0257e95b7d99e176067ae3a2c63", "git_parents": ["085b0afa52224d658bf44861a373f6a52d5aea8a"], "node": "84092b983d9fe05e612eaa78b1aa6b8d500df914", "parents": ["439b7137e49410a5789183d18ea8a6eb3e935fd9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Francesco Lodolo \u003cflod@lodolo.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090595 - Fix outdated links in UseOfCaptureEventsWarning, UseOfReleaseEventsWarning, r=bolsson DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340600\n", "files": ["dom/locales/en-US/chrome/dom/dom.properties"], "git_node": "e6253d35bc62032435716b2ebfd0746f8b2af138", "git_parents": ["7259812b842fa0257e95b7d99e176067ae3a2c63"], "node": "3f3ba6e38a0c448d19802bd2b20ff207764833ff", "parents": ["84092b983d9fe05e612eaa78b1aa6b8d500df914"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aleix Pol i Gonzalez \u003caleix.pol@codethink.co.uk\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088971 - Support complex border-area clipping in software painting r=emilio,layout-reviewers\n\nRender border coverage into an alpha mask for background colors and\nimages with dashed, dotted, or double borders. Ignore border colors\nand transparency when generating the mask.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333346\n", "files": ["layout/painting/nsCSSRendering.cpp", "layout/painting/nsCSSRendering.h", "layout/painting/nsDisplayList.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-backgrounds/background-clip/clip-border-area-complex-color.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-backgrounds/background-clip/clip-border-area-complex.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-backgrounds/background-clip/clip-border-area-double.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-backgrounds/background-clip/clip-border-area-multiple-backgrounds.html.ini"], "git_node": "7c21a28e9d8e46678442932a8cabcd99ef4f1325", "git_parents": ["e6253d35bc62032435716b2ebfd0746f8b2af138"], "node": "166b05cd3872ec9311101a77725610982a31f2f3", "parents": ["3f3ba6e38a0c448d19802bd2b20ff207764833ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aleix Pol i Gonzalez \u003caleix.pol@codethink.co.uk\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088992 - Reduce the amount of work when border-area clipping r=gw\n\nWhen possible, draw the border-area per segment, avoiding the interior\nrender and supporting batching across elements. It allows reusing the border\nsegment textures and rendering logic.\nReuses the border cache.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338062\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/border.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/borders.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs"], "git_node": "4984466a96241401e12337241d6fdf50c252822e", "git_parents": ["7c21a28e9d8e46678442932a8cabcd99ef4f1325"], "node": "b5eccdc983f5ab235ae46f0e84388207e5c8c6ca", "parents": ["166b05cd3872ec9311101a77725610982a31f2f3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Luong \u003cgabriel.luong@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091192 - Enable the Collections to Tab Groups migration by default r=android-reviewers,mobiletest-reviewers,npoon,aaronmt\n\n- Disable the migration by default in UI tests so it does not migrate the collections created by the tests\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341261\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/nimbus.fml.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/helpers/FeatureSettingsHelper.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/helpers/FeatureSettingsHelperDelegate.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/helpers/HomeActivityTestRule.kt"], "git_node": "ca1bdd8ca5a24e90be7d344ae7cbf3dc0f1a31fd", "git_parents": ["4984466a96241401e12337241d6fdf50c252822e"], "node": "f326ea7efed5bff2ee0d67b6ad2105c403f340a9", "parents": ["b5eccdc983f5ab235ae46f0e84388207e5c8c6ca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2090595 - Fix outdated links in UseOfCaptureEventsWarning, UseOfReleaseEventsWarning, r=bolsson\" for causing build bustages\n\nThis reverts commit e6253d35bc62032435716b2ebfd0746f8b2af138.\n", "files": ["dom/locales/en-US/chrome/dom/dom.properties"], "git_node": "b6dd4f3c57d9f38aae87f563101ff6ace9cf739f", "git_parents": ["ca1bdd8ca5a24e90be7d344ae7cbf3dc0f1a31fd"], "node": "9ea319d4ac7b847c41ad0dcc97866c80c0ff3fc7", "parents": ["f326ea7efed5bff2ee0d67b6ad2105c403f340a9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2088992 - Reduce the amount of work when border-area clipping r=gw\" for causing build bustages\n\nThis reverts commit 4984466a96241401e12337241d6fdf50c252822e.\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/border.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/borders.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs"], "git_node": "314226e52580f274d24dff57f4da9557f96eebc2", "git_parents": ["b6dd4f3c57d9f38aae87f563101ff6ace9cf739f"], "node": "7ffef3049bbc6c271849c84004c9bca617c97139", "parents": ["9ea319d4ac7b847c41ad0dcc97866c80c0ff3fc7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2088971 - Support complex border-area clipping in software painting r=emilio,layout-reviewers\" for causing build bustages\n\nThis reverts commit 7c21a28e9d8e46678442932a8cabcd99ef4f1325.\n", "files": ["layout/painting/nsCSSRendering.cpp", "layout/painting/nsCSSRendering.h", "layout/painting/nsDisplayList.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-backgrounds/background-clip/clip-border-area-complex-color.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-backgrounds/background-clip/clip-border-area-complex.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-backgrounds/background-clip/clip-border-area-double.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-backgrounds/background-clip/clip-border-area-multiple-backgrounds.html.ini"], "git_node": "73ad41f65f858f967ed5bf457e308151ba77cc97", "git_parents": ["314226e52580f274d24dff57f4da9557f96eebc2"], "node": "b6f138df05331e42781ed5716b225e23030ece02", "parents": ["7ffef3049bbc6c271849c84004c9bca617c97139"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Francesco Lodolo \u003cflod@lodolo.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090595 - Fix outdated links in UseOfCaptureEventsWarning, UseOfReleaseEventsWarning, r=bolsson DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340600\n", "files": ["dom/locales/en-US/chrome/dom/dom.properties"], "git_node": "1b0484beac7e5e8a6ba38c0a68434245d29ba6e0", "git_parents": ["73ad41f65f858f967ed5bf457e308151ba77cc97"], "node": "43fbe611affe8639fb5769ad42063e4c2b0383f9", "parents": ["b6f138df05331e42781ed5716b225e23030ece02"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ed Lee \u003cedilee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089036 - allow experimenting with smart bar defaulting to search r=flozia,urlbar-reviewers,mak\n\nadd feature config enum classifier override allowing pref testing. have urlbar still show ask entry when pinned\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339635\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/IntentClassifier.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_intent_classifier.js", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderAiChat.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_UrlbarProviderAiChat.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml"], "git_node": "1dbd04ad309cc2fec84db82ddec0b2cbb1f32067", "git_parents": ["1b0484beac7e5e8a6ba38c0a68434245d29ba6e0"], "node": "3ac83334a2071dfa03e2c092a6ed818f3e06f261", "parents": ["43fbe611affe8639fb5769ad42063e4c2b0383f9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mcarare \u003c48995920+mcarare@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089593 - Safely retrieve active File request in FilePicker.onPermissionsResult r=android-reviewers,pollymce\n\nUpdate onPermissionsResult to safely cast currentRequest as a File or fall back to getActiveFilePromptRequest().\nIf no active File request is found, log a warning and dismiss the prompt request to avoid potential unsafe casting exceptions.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340342\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/prompts/file/FilePicker.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/prompts/file/FilePickerTest.kt"], "git_node": "8b30b6e9f77df77b4884da8f7e388b169b8b7daf", "git_parents": ["1dbd04ad309cc2fec84db82ddec0b2cbb1f32067"], "node": "d248abab32adc707a3898c5347e4222bf935c01a", "parents": ["3ac83334a2071dfa03e2c092a6ed818f3e06f261"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091784 - Remove Kotlin opt-ins that no longer guard an experimental API r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nNothing inside these declarations uses an API that still requires the opt-in, so neither the Kotlin compiler\nnor Android lint reports an opt-in diagnostic without them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341870\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/engine-gecko/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/engine/gecko/GeckoEngine.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/ipprotection/store/reducer/Reducers.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/ipprotection/StorageStoreSyncTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/summarize/SummarizationStoreTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/llm-mlpa/src/test/java/mozilla/components/lib/llm/mlpa/service/FetchClientMlpaServiceTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/support/utils/src/test/java/mozilla/components/support/utils/ColorUtilsTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/FenixApplication.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/NimbusComponents.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/IPProtectionMenuBinding.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/experiments/prefhandling/NimbusGeckoPrefHandler.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ipprotection/store/IPProtectionPreferencesMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ipprotection/store/IPProtectionSnackbarMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/IPProtectionFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/ipprotection/IPProtectionLocations.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/ipprotection/IPProtectionLocationsFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/addons/ExtensionsMenuItemProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/crashes/CrashContentIntegrationTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/debugsettings/ipprotection/KnownCountryRepositoryTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/TopSitesRefresherTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/collections/migration/CollectionsToTabGroupsMigrationIntegrationTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/recentvisits/RecentVisitsFeatureTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ipprotection/store/IPProtectionSnackbarMiddlewareTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/reviewprompt/ShowPlayStoreReviewPromptTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/ipprotection/IPProtectionLocationsScreenTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/settingssearch/DefaultFenixSettingsIndexerTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/PbmLockStatusBindingTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/redux/store/TabsTrayStoreTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/benchmark/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/benchmark/TabsTrayBenchmark.kt"], "git_node": "697ef08ce7fc039749705279c3a0dff3f5a0fc8a", "git_parents": ["8b30b6e9f77df77b4884da8f7e388b169b8b7daf"], "node": "b1a0e22d78511a9f22f5b45e270ada2b5638b45e", "parents": ["d248abab32adc707a3898c5347e4222bf935c01a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Tang \u003cdanielzgtg.opensource@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2035730 - Increase localhost/llama.cpp maxLength to 32768 r=Mardak\n\nThe previous max, 8192, made summarization near-useless because we only\nneed it for *long* articles.\n\nTested working with llama.cpp 5aeac37a35b44fde4bdffaec9159f2fcb253b622 .\n32768 seems stable, while 45000 causes connection resets.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335078\n", "files": ["browser/components/genai/GenAI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/genai/tests/browser/browser_chat_shortcuts.js"], "git_node": "872f32670bd7430bbfdd084d5b0b1e824b61f48d", "git_parents": ["697ef08ce7fc039749705279c3a0dff3f5a0fc8a"], "node": "165e856e5d41e0bd007b0cc5f6ed67233cfbad8d", "parents": ["b1a0e22d78511a9f22f5b45e270ada2b5638b45e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "acreskeyMoz \u003cacreskey@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087664 - Include the prefetch wait in navigation timing for navigations served from an in-flight prefetch. r=sunil,necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nNavigation timing showed no time to first byte because cacheReadStart was never set on cache hits and did not reflect when the prefetched response became available.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339543\n", "files": ["netwerk/ipc/DocumentLoadListener.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpChannelChild.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/navigation-timing-requestStart-responseStart.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "5413ff281859e55ae5f588e81de795e299ce0277", "git_parents": ["872f32670bd7430bbfdd084d5b0b1e824b61f48d"], "node": "2b68ea1d57dc2aa7b04b3d207bd2a6a5025b0c70", "parents": ["165e856e5d41e0bd007b0cc5f6ed67233cfbad8d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Avoid using `NonNull::from_ref()` for now. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis Rust API stabilized in version 1.89.0, but Servo still uses 1.88.0\nas the minimum supported Rust version.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341383\n", "files": ["servo/components/selectors/tree.rs"], "git_node": "6cc15c94579edcad8b99f5bb68d49146cf3c2c68", "git_parents": ["5413ff281859e55ae5f588e81de795e299ce0277"], "node": "733c389ced664f4ca9f0c5bc8a5f7b225533f494", "parents": ["2b68ea1d57dc2aa7b04b3d207bd2a6a5025b0c70"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Remove `layout.grid.enabled` Servo pref. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nGecko has already removed it, and Servo was setting it to true, so it\ncan just be removed.\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/479\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341384\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/properties/shorthands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/specified/box.rs"], "git_node": "4f12b66cca550cf8f2e55c51735b17e3624affb4", "git_parents": ["6cc15c94579edcad8b99f5bb68d49146cf3c2c68"], "node": "c23c2c64fa3a19f7f951af9a627b05fcec383981", "parents": ["733c389ced664f4ca9f0c5bc8a5f7b225533f494"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nico Burns \u003cnico@nicoburns.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Enable the `sideways-rl` and `sideways-lr` writing modes in Servo builds. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nEnables the `sideways-rl` and `sideways-lr` writing modes in Servo\nbuilds.\n\nThese are still gated behind the `layout.writing-mode.enabled` pref\nwhich Servo doesn't enable. So there shouldn't be any Servo-side effect\nuntil Servo implements `writing-mode` and enables that pref. Blitz\n[just landed `writing-mode` support][1], and will be able to take\nadvantage of these values once they're available.\n\n[1]: https://github.com/DioxusLabs/blitz/pull/1090\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/481\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341385\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/logical_geometry.rs"], "git_node": "58bb15afc94adb3dea6579263fa914eecd4eb2da", "git_parents": ["4f12b66cca550cf8f2e55c51735b17e3624affb4"], "node": "e765db79469eb1200d5d480703563a386f4b9d64", "parents": ["c23c2c64fa3a19f7f951af9a627b05fcec383981"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nico Burns \u003cnico@nicoburns.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Enable text-indent's `hanging` and `each-line` keywords behind a pref. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nBlitz already implements these except style support. Servo can keep them\noff until implemented.\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/483\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341386\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/values/specified/text.rs"], "git_node": "ce77b8505a9add4da3a608d48bdb07d579890ff2", "git_parents": ["58bb15afc94adb3dea6579263fa914eecd4eb2da"], "node": "f63fcd10c3c4cb84242cb82b6523e56902b6b07d", "parents": ["e765db79469eb1200d5d480703563a386f4b9d64"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Adjust `display: contents` to `none` on some elements. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nIt was happening for Gecko, but not for Servo.\nSpec: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-display-3/#unbox\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/484\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341387\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/style_adjuster.rs"], "git_node": "f6816089e8ec69d69568a7ac2259d996b2d47fe2", "git_parents": ["ce77b8505a9add4da3a608d48bdb07d579890ff2"], "node": "7315b6327a1fd0960513d35b36d7b98c975e7769", "parents": ["f63fcd10c3c4cb84242cb82b6523e56902b6b07d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nico Burns \u003cnico@nicoburns.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Enable `justify-items:legacy` propagation for Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis value was added for implementing the legacy `\u003ccenter\u003e` and `align`\nattribute. Unlike other `justify-items` it inherits. Gecko, Servo, and\nBlitz all use the older `text-align: -moz-left` solution for that. But\nGecko implements this property at style-level only. This PR simply\nimplements that style adjustment for Servo builds as well.\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/482\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341388\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/matching.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/properties.mako.rs", "servo/components/style/style_adjuster.rs"], "git_node": "24453e105f59444fd69a1d607e024cd3145c5e49", "git_parents": ["f6816089e8ec69d69568a7ac2259d996b2d47fe2"], "node": "c683d66e0c5195526cab0b0919f830063916baa2", "parents": ["7315b6327a1fd0960513d35b36d7b98c975e7769"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Add `layout.writing-mode.sideways.enabled` pref for Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis will allow servo to enable `writing-mode` excluding the sideways\nvalues (`sideways-lr` and `sideways-rl`).\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/486\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341389\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/logical_geometry.rs"], "git_node": "bd0cf679e890e38cf97bb6baee007fb726b1d095", "git_parents": ["24453e105f59444fd69a1d607e024cd3145c5e49"], "node": "e881c3eb3738a46e0f76cf08e936ddf1fa00f83a", "parents": ["c683d66e0c5195526cab0b0919f830063916baa2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nico Burns \u003cnico@nicoburns.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Don't expose internal properties to content via `layout.unimplemented`. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThree internal properties: `-moz-default-appearance`,\n`-moz-min-font-size-ratio` and `-x-text-scale` are pref-gated behind\n`layout.unimplemented`.\n\nBut `enabled_for_all_content()` check which should prevent these\nproperties from being usable in `author` stylesheets treats any property\nwith a pref as enabled being for all content when that pref is set\n(disregarding the usual `enabled_in` check). The `enabled_in` check\nalready restricts these properties to UA/chrome sheets\n(`-moz-default-appearance`, `-moz-min-font-size-ratio`), or to being\nnever parsed at all (`-x-text-scale`) so the pref check is unnecessary.\n\nThis affects Blitz which enables `layout.unimplemented` and has been\nexposing these internal-only properties to web content.\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/491\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341390\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml"], "git_node": "479d5431bfa531c1dbf05b9cdb00cfbcee792fad", "git_parents": ["bd0cf679e890e38cf97bb6baee007fb726b1d095"], "node": "89ae787398bb7643bd8fe6048e27a52ef931e63c", "parents": ["e881c3eb3738a46e0f76cf08e936ddf1fa00f83a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nico Burns \u003cnico@nicoburns.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Split `layout.unimplemented` into individual prefs. Align pref names with Gecko convention. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis PR makes two changes:\n\n- Splits the `layout.unimplemented` into individual prefs for groups of\nrelated properties\n- Renames some prefs (adds `.css` to them) to align with Gecko\nconvention (other Servo prefs already followed this).\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/492\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341391\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/logical_geometry.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/properties/shorthands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/specified/position.rs"], "git_node": "b32b5c1480f37ccd3d537a9ad9a48132b3898392", "git_parents": ["479d5431bfa531c1dbf05b9cdb00cfbcee792fad"], "node": "63a1648533d1060ec7c1989cb53b0ea7a5a2c89a", "parents": ["89ae787398bb7643bd8fe6048e27a52ef931e63c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Euclid Ye \u003ceuclid.ye@huawei.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Enable text-decoration-line:spelling-error/grammar-error for Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/488\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341392\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/values/specified/text.rs"], "git_node": "4e34ae841b9b00ea0af150ea6db26f7d51613802", "git_parents": ["b32b5c1480f37ccd3d537a9ad9a48132b3898392"], "node": "ca8ab5b14285b9342024d24fe30b72da8388c0c3", "parents": ["63a1648533d1060ec7c1989cb53b0ea7a5a2c89a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nico Burns \u003cnico@nicoburns.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Enable most text properties on Servo behind prefs. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nEnable most of the text related properties in `servo` builds of Stylo\n(behind prefs).\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/493\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341393\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/logical_geometry.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/properties/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/shorthands.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/shorthands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/specified/font.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/text.rs"], "git_node": "ba046e5cbe6cfb487077fc911dcf56b5d1e87039", "git_parents": ["4e34ae841b9b00ea0af150ea6db26f7d51613802"], "node": "764158b16dc69219ba9ca94ce09e5b3dfce19571", "parents": ["ca8ab5b14285b9342024d24fe30b72da8388c0c3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nico Burns \u003cnico@nicoburns.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Enable `::first-line` for Servo behind `layout.css.first-line.enabled`. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis is also for Blitz+Winkin.\n\n- Enables the `::first-line` pseudo element at compile time\n- Pref-gates parsing it behind the `layout.css.first-line.enabled` pref\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/495\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341394\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/data.rs", "servo/components/style/dom.rs", "servo/components/style/servo/selector_parser.rs"], "git_node": "ab61e150353de1d7f20383b4d384f9ec4a79ec43", "git_parents": ["ba046e5cbe6cfb487077fc911dcf56b5d1e87039"], "node": "dcd8f2bc2501be707828cc4f1da48d9730b9c816", "parents": ["764158b16dc69219ba9ca94ce09e5b3dfce19571"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nico Burns \u003cnico@nicoburns.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Add `TElement::set_may_have_animations` method. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nAdds a `TElement::set_may_have_animations` method that is called by\nStylo (in Servo configuration) when it stores an animation set. Gecko\nmanages it's own animations so doesn't need this method.\n\nThis enables a very significant performance optimization (up to 80-90%\nfaster parallel traversal) which avoids taking the contended\n`DocumentAnimationSet::sets` RwLock during traversal, with some\ncorresponding Servo (and Blitz) side changes (coming soon).\n\nBenchmark results are on the linked Servo PR.\n\nThis PR also contains a couple of minor related pref-orientated tweaks:\n- `has_active_animations_or_transitions` method that avoids a\ndouble-lookup\n- `#[inline]` on `AnimationSetKey` constructors\n\nServo PR: https://github.com/servo/servo/pull/49137\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/496\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341395\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/dom.rs", "servo/components/style/matching.rs", "servo/components/style/servo/animation.rs"], "git_node": "637b4909a0681b1ef755f07141659662771d1273", "git_parents": ["ab61e150353de1d7f20383b4d384f9ec4a79ec43"], "node": "81dddc603803251e8a7d5d795ba0ec032088ce71", "parents": ["dcd8f2bc2501be707828cc4f1da48d9730b9c816"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nico Burns \u003cnico@nicoburns.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Fix WASM build of Stylo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nRecent Stylo added a dependency on the `rand` crate for the new CSS\n`random()` function. It depends on `rand` with default features which\nbreaks wasm builds of Stylo (as this pulls in `getrandom` as a source of\nrandomness, which doesn't work on wasm). However, it does not actually\nneed default features as it only uses rand with a custom seed.\n\nThis PR disables default-features on the `rand` dependency.\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/498\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341396\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/Cargo.toml"], "git_node": "f650fc35723463228f32587518b101cd3bb6ea43", "git_parents": ["637b4909a0681b1ef755f07141659662771d1273"], "node": "d6c1fb226f4089a77594670073ea74718dc76dc8", "parents": ["81dddc603803251e8a7d5d795ba0ec032088ce71"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Skrzypczak \u003cglennskyzl@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Add `interactivity` longhand and enable `-moz-inert` for Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/497\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341397\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/servo/selector_parser.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/computed/ui.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/ui.rs"], "git_node": "19b4d7097bad87eb3d90125ded1fe9092d2a7405", "git_parents": ["f650fc35723463228f32587518b101cd3bb6ea43"], "node": "2c46415a269220fa3ea9a7446c8f331f3ad6fdb3", "parents": ["d6c1fb226f4089a77594670073ea74718dc76dc8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nico Burns \u003cnico@nicoburns.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Group media data into a struct + add getters/setters for the entire struct. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis is aimed at trying to reduce the proliferation of getters/setters\nfor individual media data properties by:\n\n- Grouping them into a struct\n- Adding getters/setters for the entire struct.\n\nIt also (IMO) makes the `Device` constructor a lot nicer as you get\nfield names rather than having to try to match up function parameter\norder.\n\nIn future we could consider removing the individual getters/setters (or\nmaking them private where they are called internally by Stylo), but this\nPR does not yet do that.\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/412\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341398\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/device/servo.rs", "servo/components/style/servo/media_features.rs"], "git_node": "e0887b51132dd9f83ee2794e509c25223ec0d96a", "git_parents": ["19b4d7097bad87eb3d90125ded1fe9092d2a7405"], "node": "61d8bf4561742c0f209e0f5c630a92cf5703c7af", "parents": ["2c46415a269220fa3ea9a7446c8f331f3ad6fdb3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nico Burns \u003cnico@nicoburns.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Enable `background-clip: text` behind a pref. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nBlitz would like to implement this.\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/501\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341399\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/values/specified/background.rs"], "git_node": "ff1c0f9293422bca460ce287f73e5d61c435fb6a", "git_parents": ["e0887b51132dd9f83ee2794e509c25223ec0d96a"], "node": "9ce71f2428ccc7bb0f460fa4f029a9a9a95e4843", "parents": ["61d8bf4561742c0f209e0f5c630a92cf5703c7af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nico Burns \u003cnico@nicoburns.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Enable `-webkit-text-fill-color` behind a pref. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nEnables the `-webkit-text-fill-color` property in Servo behind the\n`layout.css.webkit-text-fill-color.enabled` pref.\n\nThis turns out to be very commonly used to set the text color to\n`transparent` in combination with `background-clip: text`, and if you\ndon't support `-webkit-text-fill-color` then the `background-clip: text`\neffect gets painted over by the regular text. The reason for this is\nthat setting `color: transparent` leads to poor rendering in browsers\nthat don't support `background-clip: text`, but it is historically true\nthat all browsers which support `-webkit-text-fill-color` also support\n`background-clip: text`, making it safe to set `-webkit-text-fill-color:\ntransparent`.\n\nServo should ship these two features together.\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/504\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341400\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml"], "git_node": "2596b2d7874633d9f4747b45dbd16414780e2ff9", "git_parents": ["ff1c0f9293422bca460ce287f73e5d61c435fb6a"], "node": "3f77cb7a798ccee399ba606654d0c4503a136d8c", "parents": ["9ce71f2428ccc7bb0f460fa4f029a9a9a95e4843"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Skrzypczak \u003cglenn.skrzypczak@uni-rostock.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Parse the `-moz-topmost-modal` pseudoclass on Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/503\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341401\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/servo/selector_parser.rs"], "git_node": "c2dc51aa3e8c0d6ba5ecd830c60713ffc0574647", "git_parents": ["2596b2d7874633d9f4747b45dbd16414780e2ff9"], "node": "291d1c00e81e7e916b9b83a0ead835092f4987a9", "parents": ["3f77cb7a798ccee399ba606654d0c4503a136d8c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Skrzypczak \u003cglenn.skrzypczak@uni-rostock.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Parse the `:in-range` pseudoclass on Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/508\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341402\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/servo/selector_parser.rs"], "git_node": "268be185aec2a7fb4b51ab4936f8d789f68b9300", "git_parents": ["c2dc51aa3e8c0d6ba5ecd830c60713ffc0574647"], "node": "fbc22f02547214ffc345fde811fa08ae57a073cb", "parents": ["291d1c00e81e7e916b9b83a0ead835092f4987a9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Shubham Gupta \u003cshubhamg13.work@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Enable text-underline-offset property in Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/499\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341403\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml"], "git_node": "8ce4ab842e7d7244252cfc3bb299bc18e4755401", "git_parents": ["268be185aec2a7fb4b51ab4936f8d789f68b9300"], "node": "51f7fd7871662815e5740036d6162d937ba5d1b3", "parents": ["fbc22f02547214ffc345fde811fa08ae57a073cb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Josef Guenther \u003cjosef@aciragroup.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Enable counter-set behind the counters pref. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\ncounter-set is the only counter property that is still Gecko-only. This\nputs it behind the same pref as counter-reset and counter-increment\n(`layout.css.counters.enabled`). It already compiles for Servo, so the\nchange is just the gate, and nothing changes for Gecko.\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/510\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341404\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml"], "git_node": "b3a4b263ee18b29839214a39f247d530bddc0896", "git_parents": ["8ce4ab842e7d7244252cfc3bb299bc18e4755401"], "node": "b6b66ba0db4eeff967a45ff761f54ce688518fea", "parents": ["51f7fd7871662815e5740036d6162d937ba5d1b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Josef Guenther \u003cjosef@aciragroup.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Enable hyphenate-limit-chars behind the hyphens pref. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nhttps://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/493 enabled hyphens and hyphenate-character,\nbut hyphenate-limit-chars stayed Gecko-only. This puts it behind the same pref\n(`layout.css.hyphens.enabled`). It already compiles for Servo, so the change\nis just the gate, and nothing changes for Gecko.\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/511\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341405\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml"], "git_node": "3a8a3037f33ced9b54055258c8fa5cfefb902b15", "git_parents": ["b3a4b263ee18b29839214a39f247d530bddc0896"], "node": "ee2e233029d59f5c0ef5841eff332f57e7b890f6", "parents": ["b6b66ba0db4eeff967a45ff761f54ce688518fea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Josef Guenther \u003cjosef@aciragroup.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Enable the remaining anchor positioning properties behind a pref. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis enables the anchor positioning properties that are still\nGecko-only: anchor-name, anchor-scope, position-anchor,\nposition-try-order, position-visibility and the position-try shorthand.\nThey go behind the pref https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/492 already\nuses for position-area and position-try-fallbacks\n(`layout.css.anchor-positioning.enabled`), so the whole feature sits\nbehind one pref, as it does in Gecko.\n\nThey already compile for Servo, so apart from the gates the only change\nis removing a Gecko-only cfg on the position-try shorthand. Nothing\nchanges for Gecko.\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/512\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341406\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/properties/shorthands.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/shorthands.toml"], "git_node": "8a1d81f5a61ba4ff131f30e3e050d61fe91f8419", "git_parents": ["3a8a3037f33ced9b54055258c8fa5cfefb902b15"], "node": "d0169ad35cc3f042395e28e70096c8572121ce50", "parents": ["ee2e233029d59f5c0ef5841eff332f57e7b890f6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Josef Guenther \u003cjosef@aciragroup.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Build resolve_position_try for Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\n@position-try rules already parse in the servo build, but the method\nthat computes a style with a fallback position applied is Gecko-only.\nNothing in it depends on Gecko, so this builds it for Servo too, and an\nembedder that implements position fallbacks can use the same code.\n\nThe change just removes five Gecko-only cfg lines. Nothing changes for\nGecko.\n\nImports https://github.com/servo/stylo/pull/513\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341407\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/stylist.rs"], "git_node": "778ac9d7400362a837ce0674aee7a678e2e34203", "git_parents": ["8a1d81f5a61ba4ff131f30e3e050d61fe91f8419"], "node": "eb5531149157e6051e7982ff0baf50105b30b043", "parents": ["d0169ad35cc3f042395e28e70096c8572121ce50"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Make siphasher optional, restrict it to Gecko. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nD336877 added it as a dependency, but the Servo flavor of Stylo doesn't\nactually use it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341408\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/Cargo.toml"], "git_node": "6324c64abf2ad1acf9a868c9af644c13507e3889", "git_parents": ["778ac9d7400362a837ce0674aee7a678e2e34203"], "node": "361c04e0630a89ec51f099e6276ad0be30f6af0c", "parents": ["eb5531149157e6051e7982ff0baf50105b30b043"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091347 - Fix compile problems for Servo. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nFixes 3 problems:\n- D336673 added a `ParserContext` parameter to `parse_color_keyword()`,\n  and made it private. Switch Servo to use `parse_named_color()` instead.\n- D333055 moved `CssEnvironment`, and added a `VariantNames` derive.\n- D337116 added a `submit_string` field to `Device`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341409\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/device/servo.rs", "servo/components/style/servo/attr.rs", "servo/components/style/substitution/mod.rs"], "git_node": "31287bee57fb2f746fa7036b3881c7e8eec1a84b", "git_parents": ["6324c64abf2ad1acf9a868c9af644c13507e3889"], "node": "16c82530c6ce563763d70339971aaeddef1864bc", "parents": ["361c04e0630a89ec51f099e6276ad0be30f6af0c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089755 - Update the message handling of the remote decoder actor. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340126\n", "files": ["dom/media/ipc/RemoteAudioDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/ipc/RemoteDecoderParent.cpp", "dom/media/ipc/RemoteDecoderParent.h", "dom/media/ipc/RemoteVideoDecoder.cpp"], "git_node": "2e72a0c07f36877bdf9ba5e44d1cee9a3fcdb774", "git_parents": ["31287bee57fb2f746fa7036b3881c7e8eec1a84b"], "node": "70b3a4c0082eb59a8f2c46afab61d4c9901710bb", "parents": ["16c82530c6ce563763d70339971aaeddef1864bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Osmond Arnesto \u003coarnesto@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2005078 - Replace button.footer with moz-button in browser/base/content/ r=places-reviewers,akulyk\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326797\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/appmenu-viewcache.inc.xhtml", "browser/base/content/browser-places.js", "browser/base/content/main-popupset.inc.xhtml", "browser/base/content/main-popupset.js", "browser/components/privatebrowsing/ResetPBMPanel.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "e1dca9e03afd9550fc0708cd80053eab80525954", "git_parents": ["2e72a0c07f36877bdf9ba5e44d1cee9a3fcdb774"], "node": "bdbc5cf215f3facb446b8666c859a31b993f7386", "parents": ["70b3a4c0082eb59a8f2c46afab61d4c9901710bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Osmond Arnesto \u003coarnesto@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2005078 - Replace button.footer with moz-button in browser/components/customizableui/ r=desktop-theme-reviewers,akulyk\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326812\n", "files": ["browser/components/customizableui/CustomizeMode.sys.mjs", "browser/components/customizableui/content/customizeMode.inc.xhtml", "browser/components/customizableui/test/browser_customize_telemetry.js", "browser/themes/shared/customizableui/customizeMode.css"], "git_node": "3e25cf80e85528612c2df7dcf5f80235d0c95d3f", "git_parents": ["e1dca9e03afd9550fc0708cd80053eab80525954"], "node": "92769bde2d3799ed71b792cc977bf444435f056b", "parents": ["bdbc5cf215f3facb446b8666c859a31b993f7386"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Osmond Arnesto \u003coarnesto@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2005078 - Replace button.footer with moz-button in browser/components/downloads/ r=akulyk\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327247\n", "files": ["browser/components/downloads/content/downloads.js", "browser/components/downloads/content/downloadsPanel.inc.xhtml", "browser/components/downloads/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/downloads/test/browser/browser_private_downloads_subview.js"], "git_node": "8473ec210feb