/157bdfb63c.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/6870f3a8aa.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/9d738557a2.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/d86ac8ab5e.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0002.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0003.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0004.patch"], "git_node": "a4a6508c4fffd10cbc1f148b0178ed077053d546", "git_parents": ["e8401047e4c248b83a98c13ea7442b9c1a34572a"], "node": "92e1a3729408d2f001d0f424ea547034023c78f0", "parents": ["e8f582e6614cb7e90a1f46d92870901b3b5578bf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from f86da14f33\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/f86da14f33d7a115949a5adc3c1cf84de36e5456\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-10-13T04:06:05).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: Idcb2c116d8213378d42b8f18af59d9fb943d6634\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508760\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48873}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "118d84a0aa2f32bbb23bd240d7d9d1adac92f75d", "git_parents": ["a4a6508c4fffd10cbc1f148b0178ed077053d546"], "node": "5a55e72372a1d11a7283dbdf604239c7131e202a", "parents": ["92e1a3729408d2f001d0f424ea547034023c78f0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 9639bc0eec\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/9639bc0eecccaae35eeb43f16c3ce3118262a7e0\n    Remove unused parameters from BasicIceController\n\n    CompareCandidatePairNetworks() took a `network_preference` argument that\n    was never read: the body has always used config_.network_preference,\n    which is also the only value callers passed.\n    HandleInitialSelectDampening() took an IceSwitchReason that has been\n    unused since the controller was split out of P2PTransportChannel. Both\n    were only commented out by the -Wunused-parameter cleanup.\n\n    No behavior change.\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I61c36360e9452226f0bdcbc05d301db2d0a0cfdb\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508680\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jonas Oreland \u003cjonaso@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48874}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/basic_ice_controller.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/basic_ice_controller.h"], "git_node": "8b3a0fe52c1d8d91a1f06caeda905887c1ac967b", "git_parents": ["118d84a0aa2f32bbb23bd240d7d9d1adac92f75d"], "node": "d9aed3a732cddd741655a7880964520daf38d67c", "parents": ["5a55e72372a1d11a7283dbdf604239c7131e202a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 7dee88c266\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/7dee88c266b7dbf67874a59bb56a98cbf0efab2a\n    Set CQP via cq_level with bounded QP range in AV1 v2 encoder.\n\n    Previously, CQP mode (AOM_Q) pinned min_quantizer and max_quantizer to\n    the target quantizer. In libaom, this caused best_quality ==\n    worst_quality == base_qindex, which suppressed cyclic refresh delta-Q\n    segments (AV1E_SET_AQ_MODE = 3) and prevented dynamic loop-filter/CDEF\n    disabling (av1_cyclic_refresh_disable_lf_cdef, which requires qindex \u003c\n    rc.worst_quality).\n\n    Configure CQP using cfg_.use_fixed_qp_offsets = 2 and AOME_SET_CQ_LEVEL\n    (tracked via cq_level_ to avoid redundant av1_change_config calls), and\n    constrain min_quantizer / max_quantizer to +/- 4 quantizer units (+/- 16\n    q_index steps) around the target quantizer (or 0 when lossless target_qp\n    == 0 is requested). This keeps the frame base_qindex at the requested\n    target while giving cyclic refresh and dynamic loop-filter/CDEF logic\n    room to operate without initializing avg_frame_qindex / worst_quality to\n    255.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:496266459\n    Change-Id: Id5d977742f34f38997cc6a27665651f179230117\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508580\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48875}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/libaom_av1_encoder_v2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/libaom_av1_encoder_v2.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/libaom_av1_encoder_v2_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "1adead6f8475ef0cdb28ca45ec4e5d3b828a4a83", "git_parents": ["8b3a0fe52c1d8d91a1f06caeda905887c1ac967b"], "node": "e9f23095ccc6d2bbded15fd93292937b218368e3", "parents": ["d9aed3a732cddd741655a7880964520daf38d67c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 65217155f7\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/65217155f735a780676d34c073ef2447589a71c1\n    Replace rtc_test by rtc_test_suite\n\n    impacted targets are:\n    * voip_unittests\n    * rtc_p2p_unittests\n    * tools_unittests\n    * rtc_pc_unittests\n    * audio_engine_tests\n\n    verified that the number of tests triggered by each target is the same as before\n\n    Change-Id: I357fd2147d13b8fc5b5efd22b7c9e3d048994584\n    Bug: webrtc:498394143\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508720\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48876}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/voip/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/voip/test/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0034.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0044.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0054.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0081.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0085.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0097.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0099.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0141.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_tools/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_tools/network_tester/BUILD.gn"], "git_node": "812af487c465b2129f4a45774c2b97195c35e7a2", "git_parents": ["1adead6f8475ef0cdb28ca45ec4e5d3b828a4a83"], "node": "07279dce6e3cce9e28ec9d532ed8ac028c0465d5", "parents": ["e9f23095ccc6d2bbded15fd93292937b218368e3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 689d0150f3\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/689d0150f3152dfa4248195f6c3b9e1f323fff33\n    Restrict 32-bit STUN integrity to GOOG_PING and ignore post-MI attrs\n\n    StunMessage::ValidateMessageIntegrity could accept the 4-byte\n    STUN_ATTR_GOOG_MESSAGE_INTEGRITY_32 attribute for any STUN message type\n    whenever the 20-byte STUN_ATTR_MESSAGE_INTEGRITY attribute was absent,\n    allowing a MAC-strength downgrade on standard STUN/TURN responses.\n\n    Additionally, https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/466000\n    inadvertently reverted the post-MESSAGE-INTEGRITY attribute filtering\n    from https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/468540 in\n    StunMessage::Read, allowing attributes appended after MESSAGE-INTEGRITY\n    to be parsed into attrs_.\n\n    - Restrict STUN_ATTR_GOOG_MESSAGE_INTEGRITY_32 validation in\n      StunMessage::ValidateMessageIntegrity to GOOG_PING_REQUEST,\n      GOOG_PING_RESPONSE, and GOOG_PING_ERROR_RESPONSE.\n    - Restore ignoring all attributes following STUN_ATTR_MESSAGE_INTEGRITY\n      or STUN_ATTR_GOOG_MESSAGE_INTEGRITY_32 except STUN_ATTR_FINGERPRINT in\n      StunMessage::Read per RFC 5389 Section 15.4.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:513727324,webrtc:514524506,webrtc:518078308,chromium:504567957\n    Change-Id: I410abcde8441a2075e767f1124f66099be678016\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508780\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48877}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/transport/stun.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/transport/stun_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "bb9641b070e3f453e765ac24bd50cd87791ca870", "git_parents": ["812af487c465b2129f4a45774c2b97195c35e7a2"], "node": "006cf9c9fc701b6b53db664ef57731415f2f3c44", "parents": ["07279dce6e3cce9e28ec9d532ed8ac028c0465d5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 3efe1a3a90\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/3efe1a3a90c14ce339e22c451d48f4f7e831c75b\n    Spanify and thus harden forward error correction code\n\n    Bug: chromium:570927027\n    Change-Id: I36cc3771838fc6e0524a4c8a1e37528eb30d769e\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508300\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48878}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/fec_private_tables_bursty.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/fec_private_tables_bursty.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/fec_private_tables_bursty_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/fec_private_tables_random.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/fec_private_tables_random.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/forward_error_correction.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/forward_error_correction.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/forward_error_correction_internal.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/forward_error_correction_internal.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/test/testFec/test_fec.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0003.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/unsafe_buffers_paths.txt"], "git_node": "f7d67e4003a84aa45ea85d286edece54f5672b58", "git_parents": ["bb9641b070e3f453e765ac24bd50cd87791ca870"], "node": "720279e1b0cd6918914435750c3337dfc237df4c", "parents": ["006cf9c9fc701b6b53db664ef57731415f2f3c44"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 9905ba54a6\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/9905ba54a68c492c280aed48f8c598019a726512\n    Avoid some unnecessary copies in audio channel setup\n\n    Audio channel construction copies some by-value arguments at their last\n    use instead of moving them, which costs a reference count round trip, or\n    a callback clone, per channel. None of the changes is on a per-packet or\n    per-frame path.\n\n    - Move decoder_factory through CreateChannelReceive() and the\n      ChannelReceive constructor, so that it is moved all the way into\n      NetEqFactory::Create(), and move frame_decryptor into its member.\n    - Move decoder_factory into NetEqFactory::Create() in the AudioIngress\n      constructor.\n    - Move send_frame_callback into its member in\n      ChannelSendFrameTransformerDelegate.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:374845009\n    Change-Id: I7a5812af8be74adc018cbdcd02d16b891d3671ae\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/498660\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48879}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/channel_receive.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/channel_send_frame_transformer_delegate.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/voip/audio_ingress.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0035.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0138.patch"], "git_node": "09764c67f111739d527ef8c6614a844756d8dbb1", "git_parents": ["f7d67e4003a84aa45ea85d286edece54f5672b58"], "node": "ad439c4e5dd0aa25787237d4eb9ffba9d476d426", "parents": ["720279e1b0cd6918914435750c3337dfc237df4c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from ec78315ff5\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/ec78315ff58f84cea53baee892c2e1bcbcc2d6cd\n    Cleanup usage and deprecate CopyOnWriteBuffer(ptr, size) constructor\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42225170\n    Change-Id: Id8eb4468f642098ce6cb5d3aedecd9738c07c4f1\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508700\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48880}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/data_channel_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_voice_engine_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtcp_transceiver_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0003.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0054.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0091.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0118.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/dcsctp_socket_network_test.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/test/fake_packet_transport.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/datagram_connection_internal.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_transport_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/copy_on_write_buffer.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/ssl_fingerprint.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/sdk/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/sdk/objc/api/peerconnection/RTCDataChannel.mm", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/network/emulated_turn_server.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/network/fake_network_socket_server.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/network/network_emulation_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "7bc17fa3707019ec0df563903c847f68e6588fdf", "git_parents": ["09764c67f111739d527ef8c6614a844756d8dbb1"], "node": "244b9c8679e9c49b5a068f4614a8632cd491e86a", "parents": ["ad439c4e5dd0aa25787237d4eb9ffba9d476d426"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 51fe478eef\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/51fe478eef826bc0bc2c4f9d2462e1086f834a13\n    Check video receive codecs against decoder formats\n\n    GetChangedReceiverParameters() verified receive codec support against a\n    codec list from GetPayloadTypesAndDefaultCodecs(), rebuilt on every\n    SetReceiverParameters() call. Building that list assigns payload types\n    and adds RTX codecs, which the check discards: it only compares codec\n    names and codec specific parameters.\n\n    SetReceiverParameters() runs for every video channel on every SLD/SRD,\n    so this dominated worker thread CPU when renegotiating many video\n    transceivers. Compare against the supported SdpVideoFormats instead. In\n    a debug build, SetReceiverParameters() becomes 75% cheaper and worker\n    thread CPU in RenegotiateManyVideoTransceiversAndWatchAudioDelay drops\n    by about 40%.\n\n    Fixed: webrtc:573078379\n    Change-Id: I9ece30c0aab68211f706b30f50026ad28a40a1d6\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508841\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48881}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_video_engine.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_video_engine_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0004.patch"], "git_node": "de39e7f77e3cd82fdf0dc3afa8b5addc2328d66b", "git_parents": ["7bc17fa3707019ec0df563903c847f68e6588fdf"], "node": "16541a75b5a63024a55cfc88b96e0b97b3e33523", "parents": ["244b9c8679e9c49b5a068f4614a8632cd491e86a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 4f4904d91a\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/4f4904d91a523ae0eb4e72acf33cb1b05c049a20\n    Clean up temporary directories and files leaked by tests into out/\n\n    Several unit tests and test support utilities left temporary UUID\n    directories and output files behind in the root out/ directory:\n\n    - DefaultArtifactPath() in test_artifacts.cc called\n      OutputPathWithRandomDirectory() during ABSL_FLAG initialization,\n      creating an unremoved out/\u003cuuid\u003e/ directory on every test binary\n      startup. Use OutputPath() instead and generate a unique filename in\n      IsolatedOutputTest.ShouldBeAbleToWriteContent.\n    - Remove directories created via OutputPathWithRandomDirectory() in\n      file_utils_unittest, test_audio_device_unittest, wav_file_unittest,\n      file_wrapper_unittest, and rtc_event_log_output_file_unittest.\n    - Remove temporary files and use TempFilename() in audio_coding tests,\n      test_clip_unittest, video_file_reader_unittest,\n      rtp_file_writer_unittest, and network_tester_unittest.\n    - Remove unused log file creation in video_quality_analysis_unittest\n      and randomSeedLog.txt creation in test_fec.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: Ia8e33715ac0c8de6ab1988f98397941182b6c485\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508820\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48882}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/rtc_event_log_output_file_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/wav_file_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/test/EncodeDecodeTest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/test/EncodeDecodeTest.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/test/PacketLossTest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/test/TestAllCodecs.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/test/TestAllCodecs.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/test/TestRedFec.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/test/TestRedFec.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/test/TestStereo.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/test/TestStereo.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/test/TestVADDTX.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/test/TestVADDTX.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/test/opus_test.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/test/opus_test.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_device/include/test_audio_device_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/test/testFec/test_fec.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/system/file_wrapper_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_tools/frame_analyzer/video_quality_analysis_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_tools/network_tester/network_tester_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_tools/video_file_reader_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/rtp_file_writer_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/testsupport/file_utils_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/testsupport/test_artifacts.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/testsupport/test_artifacts_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/evaluation/test_clip_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "f2172188ff7eb2b1fbbe93c28f5761fe651a7228", "git_parents": ["de39e7f77e3cd82fdf0dc3afa8b5addc2328d66b"], "node": "ce7bcb3a3c8c3f26e3b6d9b5afb7190047629ffd", "parents": ["16541a75b5a63024a55cfc88b96e0b97b3e33523"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 7e6b034eeb\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/7e6b034eeb80f1053a5864244b3326717caa1424\n    Switch owners email address for jleconte\n\n    Change-Id: Idb7d9d179ffe8f3485d37bcacac792204cdb225e\n    No-Try: True\n    Bug: None\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508801\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48883}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/OWNERS_INFRA", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/OWNERS", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/OWNERS", "third_party/libwebrtc/tools_webrtc/OWNERS"], "git_node": "c05b647da92898f26b086b27d7ec354046379328", "git_parents": ["f2172188ff7eb2b1fbbe93c28f5761fe651a7228"], "node": "318b78cdd211313286aa0225e2f00264a0deace1", "parents": ["ce7bcb3a3c8c3f26e3b6d9b5afb7190047629ffd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from ba84c3bc7e\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/ba84c3bc7edaaa4ebdef997fec009dfa116a5ba3\n    Stop reading input_api.tbr in PRESUBMIT.py\n\n    TBR is no longer supported, and depot_tools removed the --tbrs option\n    from git cl upload in https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/4185277.\n\n    Bug: chromium:40767138\n    Change-Id: If27e2f94ef5fd6e20eb9b4d5a5e0b7d9536a0b50\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508840\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48884}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "5c0c04f21a06dc1a58afba825880c9a1b3b67ada", "git_parents": ["c05b647da92898f26b086b27d7ec354046379328"], "node": "784f45be79411e2c5110e9704f3c7644613ac045", "parents": ["318b78cdd211313286aa0225e2f00264a0deace1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 5859cc69f1\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/5859cc69f147336df5356f1b35a695d2bd1cc42a\n    Add SCReAMv2 g3doc overview and update sitemap\n\n    Adds conceptual documentation for the SCReAMv2 congestion controller implementation in modules/congestion_controller/scream/g3doc/index.md and links it in g3doc/sitemap.md.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:447037083\n    Change-Id: I811d6b38cbe23a5b200262771a88d8a63cbcf907\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508781\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48885}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/g3doc/sitemap.md", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/g3doc/index.md"], "git_node": "9af53d7ee0bcb63de46138b1fccc3494f4bc8538", "git_parents": ["5c0c04f21a06dc1a58afba825880c9a1b3b67ada"], "node": "3696e0058a781026e66d671f7367aaaa07e1d81d", "parents": ["784f45be79411e2c5110e9704f3c7644613ac045"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from c9b8314d7b\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/c9b8314d7ba721bdd105bcc077f623833cf06657\n    Discard the ICE candidate pool after gathering for a local answer\n\n    RFC 8829 (JSEP) uses the candidate pool when setLocalDescription is\n    called and discards the remaining pooled candidates once an answer has\n    been applied (sections 3.5.4 and 5.11). The answer path did this in the\n    wrong order since the MaybeStartGathering() call was moved to the end of\n    DoSetLocalDescription(): the pool was discarded first, so the answerer's\n    transports could never take a pooled session. They gathered from\n    scratch, and the pooled STUN/TURN allocations were made for nothing.\n\n    JsepTransportController::MaybeStartGathering() now takes a\n    `discard_candidate_pool` argument. For a local answer, the pool is\n    discarded right after gathering has started, in the same network thread\n    hop. This also removes one blocking call per local answer.\n\n    The discard for a remote answer is unchanged; the offerer started\n    gathering when the local offer was applied.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:572439023, webrtc:42222804\n    Fixed: webrtc:572439023\n    Change-Id: Iea9bb10b9ccc84372d683d508056ab8835068027\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508440\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48886}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_interface_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_offer_answer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/fake_peer_connection_for_stats.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/peer_scenario/scenario_connection.cc"], "git_node": "ff829b8584bb18a19c8b3a262a9d39865db09a1b", "git_parents": ["9af53d7ee0bcb63de46138b1fccc3494f4bc8538"], "node": "005d7810d7c9de038dcb5ceb837d1946a0739abd", "parents": ["3696e0058a781026e66d671f7367aaaa07e1d81d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 0941d258e2\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/0941d258e29ab1214d236d6702d61fdcb86f5d83\n    SCReAM: Scale reference window increase linearly for small RTTs\n\n    In draft-johansson-ccwg-rfc8298bis-screamv2-05 (Section 4.2.2.2, Appendix B.2.4) and draft-ietf-ccwg-rfc8298bis-screamv2-01, the reference window increase scaling for small RTTs (s_rtt \u003c VIRTUAL_RTT) was updated from quadratic (tmp_t * tmp_t) to linear (tmp_t) because one RTT scaling factor is already accounted for by the per-RTT window growth.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:447037083\n    Change-Id: I149e18cdd5092792aaa6e9365db0ac2e2091ff36\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508842\n    Reviewed-by: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48887}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2.cc"], "git_node": "be4f17795b264fccbef483c7fae5ab55aa49aae6", "git_parents": ["ff829b8584bb18a19c8b3a262a9d39865db09a1b"], "node": "29e1c9e28053a86e476be4df4d6f04c71ed82a6a", "parents": ["005d7810d7c9de038dcb5ceb837d1946a0739abd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 999ac32e48\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/999ac32e483e24a1a44db2d94bc1dc41e26f17b4\n    Have a unique test file per rtc_cc_test\n\n    Make vad_unittest.h a standalone header and add it to the vad_unittest rtc_source_set.\n\n    Change-Id: I5eab34504b4469316e2d6ae5b3c88bd60016d16c\n    Bug: webrtc:498394143\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508800\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48888}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/vad/vad_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/vad/vad_unittest.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0034.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0091.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/jitter/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/pc/e2e/analyzer/video/dvqa/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/peer_scenario/bwe_integration_tests/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/peer_scenario/tests/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/scenario/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/time_controller/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/config/BUILD.gn"], "git_node": "8b79c554e9c586019610f491839b9d36e860c575", "git_parents": ["be4f17795b264fccbef483c7fae5ab55aa49aae6"], "node": "292700d8efbd77717911c66bcbc0326e54e5bd7c", "parents": ["29e1c9e28053a86e476be4df4d6f04c71ed82a6a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 926d586b4d\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/926d586b4d6d5b63e394689144e7f5f32416bf3e\n    Fix inverted check in EventLogger::Stop()\n\n    The switch from rtc_base/atomic_ops.h to std::atomic inverted the check\n    in Stop(): CompareAndSwap() returned the previous value, while\n    compare_exchange_strong() returns true on success. Stop() therefore\n    returned early whenever a capture was active. It stopped recording\n    events but did not flush or terminate the output, and only a second\n    Stop(), e.g. from ShutdownInternalTracer(), finished the file. As a\n    result, --trace_event output from test binaries was always truncated,\n    and starting a new capture after StopInternalCapture() blocked forever.\n    The Android and iOS tracing APIs are affected too.\n\n    Fixed: webrtc:573078026\n    Change-Id: Id791c1020b50118465f67a0420ebe2edb28743cc\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508860\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48889}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0043.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0052.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0083.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0085.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0086.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0099.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0134.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/event_tracer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/event_tracer_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "c56242f8107de0740671cf12bf7e981905acd871", "git_parents": ["8b79c554e9c586019610f491839b9d36e860c575"], "node": "0bcb4352441cb0211cb6035bb363409e963a1567", "parents": ["292700d8efbd77717911c66bcbc0326e54e5bd7c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from d7862361c6\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/d7862361c6c3942b5b96c8162ae4fa37666a2ea3\n    Reland \"Add AES-256-CTR-HMAC-SHA512 Sframe cipher suites\"\n\n    This is a reland of commit 0a4e15369bad2a99fdf784ab19f949b30346dfe9\n\n    Original change's description:\n    \u003e Add AES-256-CTR-HMAC-SHA512 Sframe cipher suites\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Expose the three AES-256-CTR-HMAC-SHA512 cipher suites from\n    \u003e draft-barnes-sframe-iana-256 (registry values 6, 7 and 8), already\n    \u003e implemented by third_party/sframe, through SframeCipherSuite and map\n    \u003e them in ToSframeCipherSuite. This brings the WebRTC enum in line with\n    \u003e the eight suites listed in the WebRTC Encoded Transform\n    \u003e SFrameCipherSuite IDL, which gained these suites in\n    \u003e https://github.com/w3c/webrtc-encoded-transform/pull/303.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Bug: webrtc:479862368\n    \u003e Change-Id: Ie5f0bbcccfeee9ea7dd69b253c75c8c47082fbc7\n    \u003e Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/507780\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Commit-Queue: Kacper Wasniowski \u003ckwasniow@cisco.com\u003e\n    \u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48822}\n\n    Bug: webrtc:479862368\n    Change-Id: I9b571035c8cca04eb4c33c751a6bf440dff54e0d\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508083\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Kacper Wasniowski \u003ckwasniow@cisco.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48890}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/sframe/sframe_types.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/sframe/sframe_context_factory.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/sframe/sframe_encryptor_decryptor_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "26a2efafa38e84cfed482f71873c5cf4e22f41ac", "git_parents": ["c56242f8107de0740671cf12bf7e981905acd871"], "node": "a56d4a9cd0b7d02d7e5d161f2ddd4f45461519fd", "parents": ["0bcb4352441cb0211cb6035bb363409e963a1567"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from ac9591c580\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/ac9591c580ac697e7bb604debf8a141b18626204\n    Add RtpPacketizerSframe for per-frame Sframe packetization\n\n    Sframe over RTP prepends a one-byte descriptor (S, E and T bits) to the\n    payload of every RTP packet. Until now this was only possible by calling\n    PacketizeSframeRtpPacketOrError() on each packet after packetization,\n    which moves the payload by one byte and leaves the caller to track the\n    position of the packet in the frame and to reserve room for the\n    descriptor.\n\n    Add RtpPacketizerSframe for per-frame Sframe, where the whole frame is\n    encrypted before packetization. It splits the encrypted frame like raw\n    packetization and writes the descriptor together with each fragment\n    directly into the packet payload, so no data is moved afterwards. The\n    room for the descriptor is taken from the payload size limits, including\n    the first, last and single packet reductions. The S and E bits come from\n    the position of the packet in the frame and the T bit is always clear.\n\n    The marker bit of the last packet is set from is_last_frame_in_picture,\n    passed to the constructor as a single bool as RtpPacketizerAv1 does.\n    This keeps the packetizer codec agnostic: with spatial scalability (VP9,\n    AV1) only the last frame of a picture ends with a marked packet, and for\n    other codecs the value is true by default.\n\n    Per-packet Sframe is not handled here. There the payload is packetized\n    by the codec packetizer and each packet is encrypted afterwards, so the\n    descriptor can be written while the ciphertext is copied back into the\n    packet. That, and using this packetizer from RTPSenderVideo, are planned\n    for a follow-up CL.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:479862368\n    Change-Id: I7339dbbc69c2f8cc0b45ef68967e5784afd5ab4c\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508322\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Kacper Wasniowski \u003ckwasniow@cisco.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48891}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_packetizer_sframe.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_packetizer_sframe.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_packetizer_sframe_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0003.patch"], "git_node": "6ccf29bb57cd68232529ad0e41c9039d6dd25393", "git_parents": ["26a2efafa38e84cfed482f71873c5cf4e22f41ac"], "node": "532455ba8df43345edcd98b70753c4db270dc6f1", "parents": ["a56d4a9cd0b7d02d7e5d161f2ddd4f45461519fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 0d3c711211\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/0d3c711211f7892437df1837388976ef8db4549c\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-10-14T04:06:57).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I8640cf70b88c7b76b1dd35bf557c0cf59a7700d0\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508920\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48892}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "97aced0259a9f0c68747bbaf60055cf4ba9bd678", "git_parents": ["6ccf29bb57cd68232529ad0e41c9039d6dd25393"], "node": "16cfb9af503bc24566c874bc73f9c72f65491cdb", "parents": ["532455ba8df43345edcd98b70753c4db270dc6f1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from eba0caf098\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/eba0caf0983011189fce5ccbed54e3d6a068b4e4\n    Update JsepTransportController tests to use a separate network thread\n\n    JsepTransportControllerTest ran single threaded but the implementation\n    is multi threaded. The fixture now has a network thread as well as a\n    signaling thread that run the test body.\n\n    Many WaitUntil() calls compared a constant with a copy of a member made\n    before waiting, so they never actually waited. Their arguments are now\n    swapped.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42222804\n    Change-Id: I7bed2f8f2e311b55b05b884532790099518dc316\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508460\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48893}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "8d6b2ee9933a9022c7f45bc4481e5abc0094f3ff", "git_parents": ["97aced0259a9f0c68747bbaf60055cf4ba9bd678"], "node": "ab3a2ff84e2b2cae316aca56d4d9aeb229ae0aad", "parents": ["16cfb9af503bc24566c874bc73f9c72f65491cdb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 9ac655aeb4\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/9ac655aeb457a2066cad2f9da7d917e44d5a25b3\n    Plumb receive side ECN marking to RtcTransport\n\n    Adds the ECN marking of each incoming packet to PacketMetadata and\n    passes it to PacketProcessor::ProcessIncomingPacket, where upcoming\n    congestion control feedback will use it.\n\n    Bug: chromium:443019066\n    Change-Id: Id4bead4d06247ce916f2a0a28a9f241c58945cd4\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/506500\n    Commit-Queue: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48894}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/datagram_connection.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/datagram_connection_internal.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/datagram_connection_internal.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/datagram_connection_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/dtls_packet_processor.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/dtls_packet_processor.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/dtls_packet_processor_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/packet_processor.h"], "git_node": "dc085181058152484f4db03403b347b755b157a5", "git_parents": ["8d6b2ee9933a9022c7f45bc4481e5abc0094f3ff"], "node": "f18fa70d9ba4bf91d93afe29dd10f62391201cb8", "parents": ["ab3a2ff84e2b2cae316aca56d4d9aeb229ae0aad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from f618cb3844\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/f618cb3844d60ab158466aaf615331651a1b9073\n    SCReAM: Do not bump l4s_alpha to 0.25 after long uncongested period\n\n    In draft-johansson-ccwg-rfc8298bis-screamv2-05 (Section 4.2.2.1, Appendix B.2.4) and draft-ietf-ccwg-rfc8298bis-screamv2-01, bumping l4s_alpha to 0.25 after \u003e100 uncongested RTTs was removed when the fast-attack/slow-decay EWMA filter for l4s_alpha was introduced.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:447037083\n    Change-Id: I5c804160aca6d56fd60c0d4e63c162797b587cde\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508881\n    Reviewed-by: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48895}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2.cc"], "git_node": "a3e0606288bab454939ca3227fadc9b9bd6ac23e", "git_parents": ["dc085181058152484f4db03403b347b755b157a5"], "node": "3df6af373e5acdcc3c402895bd007500c335c535", "parents": ["f18fa70d9ba4bf91d93afe29dd10f62391201cb8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 8b2e2d5e77\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/8b2e2d5e77e322100a5e2bd474eec5074869138d\n    Move audio_engine_tests and rtc_p2p_unittests to there respective build file\n\n    Also add the audio utils tests to the audio_engine_tests suite (these tests are currently not running anywhere).\n\n    Change-Id: I730e29c950648be7dcb80a014c48fa5b4707b862\n    Bug: webrtc:498394143\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508843\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48896}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/utility/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/specs/client.webrtc.json", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/specs/gn_isolate_map.pyl", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/specs/tryserver.webrtc.json", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0034.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0044.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0054.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0081.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0085.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0097.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0099.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/tools_webrtc/get_landmines.py"], "git_node": "45b19796db51899724be85630e199305bfff9406", "git_parents": ["a3e0606288bab454939ca3227fadc9b9bd6ac23e"], "node": "8eaf90420e7fad8c360fda354f2c52bbf296482d", "parents": ["3df6af373e5acdcc3c402895bd007500c335c535"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 421d35bd3d\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/421d35bd3de31251f1c36ba22aaee2ce1157e2c8\n    Remove hta@webrtc.org from WATCHLISTS\n\n    Bug: none\n    No-Try: true\n    Change-Id: Id41e01ae3af3d9f9990b14b2921550320be4ec2c\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508861\n    Reviewed-by: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48897}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "909379b39d92af64b5e9934591844e16e3dfe83e", "git_parents": ["45b19796db51899724be85630e199305bfff9406"], "node": "92082156bc99518d081ebcfa7da24f200afd4cdc", "parents": ["8eaf90420e7fad8c360fda354f2c52bbf296482d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 546d2fbc9b\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/546d2fbc9be241f810ec81f30fca81cb87aed06d\n    Update SCReAMv2 implementation_diff.md against draft -01\n\n    Bug: webrtc:447037083\n    Change-Id: I786609f5e16a03df644dd2e3a1c2dc0efd05baea\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508880\n    Reviewed-by: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48898}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/g3doc/implementation_diff.md"], "git_node": "e4dabd931cc74f2fb612ed227d1ca97a486d18c3", "git_parents": ["909379b39d92af64b5e9934591844e16e3dfe83e"], "node": "cae0b2aa7a4e123c46550e771ece5c494d821951", "parents": ["92082156bc99518d081ebcfa7da24f200afd4cdc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from c6bb4fb8b9\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/c6bb4fb8b94a3537c72312a839fb6fc78d5a51fa\n    Set the local certificate without blocking\n\n    JsepTransportController::SetLocalCertificate() made a blocking call to\n    the network thread. The certificate is now posted instead, which still\n    applies it before any later description. If the signaling and network\n    threads are the same thread, it's applied right away, as before.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42222804\n    Change-Id: I11a8ce3163e229e9dd44665ad42b8545993896d5\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508144\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48899}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_crypto_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "283efc3cf123a3c192bceac1a56b9e44df42047f", "git_parents": ["e4dabd931cc74f2fb612ed227d1ca97a486d18c3"], "node": "d37678231505a255702d7e8e85bb5d20b6005ce8", "parents": ["cae0b2aa7a4e123c46550e771ece5c494d821951"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 1670ec1deb\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/1670ec1deb4bc18c0b21c6c458a0436eca6fdbb1\n    Avoid CopyOnWriteBuffer copy in dcsctp_socket_network_test\n\n    Move the CopyOnWriteBuffer parameter into the PostTask lambda capture\n    in emulated_socket.SetReceiver to avoid an unnecessary atomic refcount\n    increment/decrement pair per simulated network packet.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:374845009\n    Change-Id: Id29b2afffd34db80f2a9ad353ab71ab0be02fed9\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/499201\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48900}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/dcsctp_socket_network_test.cc"], "git_node": "70ca55369e0ceb9a33c108ace24f222c5481c9e5", "git_parents": ["283efc3cf123a3c192bceac1a56b9e44df42047f"], "node": "3cc7e9712545316b33895e77e672a6d3013c3011", "parents": ["d37678231505a255702d7e8e85bb5d20b6005ce8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 55344d2a9f\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/55344d2a9f7538abba16cc2640dae54031db37b4\n    dcsctp: Limit when chunks are retransmitted\n\n    When a chunk was retransmitted, its NACK counter was reset and every\n    subsequent SACK that newly acknowledged a higher TSN counted as a new\n    miss indication. But the SACKs that the peer generates for packets that\n    were already in flight when the chunk was retransmitted can't reflect\n    whether the retransmission arrived. With N packets in flight, every\n    third such SACK triggered yet another retransmission of the same chunk,\n    so a single lost packet could be sent N/3 times within one RTT. For\n    partially reliable messages this also used up the retransmission budget\n    prematurely.\n\n    RFC 4960 section 7.2.4 says, when the third miss indication is received:\n\n      5) Mark the DATA chunk(s) as being fast retransmitted and thus\n         ineligible for a subsequent Fast Retransmit.\n\n    FreeBSD records the next TSN to be sent when a chunk is marked for\n    retransmission and only strikes it again if the highest newly\n    acknowledged TSN is at or above that value. Linux flags a fast\n    retransmitted chunk and never fast retransmits it again until T3-rtx\n    expires.\n\n    This change follows the FreeBSD approach, as it still allows a lost\n    retransmission to be recovered by fast retransmit rather than only by\n    T3-rtx. Each chunk records next_tsn() when it is (re)transmitted, and a\n    SACK is only a miss indication for a retransmitted chunk if it newly\n    acknowledges a TSN at or above that value, i.e. data sent after the\n    retransmission.\n\n    Two old test had to be migrated to the new behavior.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:572252436\n    Change-Id: I30f7d7fc0a2dac290160aaf09d43b87c03198e12\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508541\n    Commit-Queue: Victor Boivie \u003cboivie@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48901}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/dcsctp_socket_test.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/tx/outstanding_data.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/tx/outstanding_data.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/tx/outstanding_data_test.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/tx/retransmission_queue_test.cc"], "git_node": "c826f147a385fe9e19578d0c76858e862a0ae0fa", "git_parents": ["70ca55369e0ceb9a33c108ace24f222c5481c9e5"], "node": "5e2812b6ae9f766fcbb203ef253229702f23a1c5", "parents": ["3cc7e9712545316b33895e77e672a6d3013c3011"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 38985cc980\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/38985cc98034fbac976e63d89841b73e136993ae\n    Removing undefined left shifts in AudioProcessing\n\n    Same as https://webrtc-review.git.corp.google.com/c/src/+/14800\n\n    Change-Id: I41d696d284cfc370d17a451ea9c19fba91646d25\n    Bug: None\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509000\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48902}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/resample_by_2_internal.c"], "git_node": "29f56c78ffe6fd6fe33839db41c4c27047e61625", "git_parents": ["c826f147a385fe9e19578d0c76858e862a0ae0fa"], "node": "1c273674ae89bc18c3b24ce6eae7e0fe390d8be2", "parents": ["5e2812b6ae9f766fcbb203ef253229702f23a1c5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from e848b240c8\n\nEssentially a no-op since we're going to see this change\nreverted when we vendor in 1aeb0050d4.\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/e848b240c80da1b6fc3ef690046c2958d75527e5\n    Run audio_decoder_unittest, neteq tests and webrtc_opus_fec_test in audio_coding_unittests\n\n    * Add audio_coding_unittests to run on fuchsia (currently only audio_decoder_unittest was running)\n    * frame_size_ms flag is used in 2 neteq files and moved in neteq_quality_test.h\n\n    Time to run audio_coding_unittests is still small after adding these tests.\n\n    Change-Id: Id21aacef29b74bb4153b4aa5bf7f81bec86707d3\n    Bug: webrtc:498394143\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508960\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48903}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/1aeb0050d4.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0002.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0003.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0004.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0005.patch"], "git_node": "ee57636b30a50857a132bdf985192d9faf388a82", "git_parents": ["29f56c78ffe6fd6fe33839db41c4c27047e61625"], "node": "61f83e7bbdbe581f8701cefeea7af380467aef32", "parents": ["1c273674ae89bc18c3b24ce6eae7e0fe390d8be2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 157bdfb63c\n\nWe already cherry-picked this when we vendored c9688bcc73.\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/157bdfb63caa236d7bbdd0889f99ddba96a44fee\n    Avoid reusing released decoders after SetDecoders()\n\n    SetDecoders() only deregistered decoders that were removed or changed,\n    but it also reset the decoder database's active payload type. The next\n    frame then released the active decoder and configured the same instance\n    again. Not all decoders support that: Chromium's hardware decoders fail\n    Configure() after Release() and permanently fall back to software\n    decoding. This happens e.g. when the receiving side creates a new offer,\n    since that typically changes the set of receive codecs.\n\n    Deregister all of the previous decoders instead, so that the factory\n    creates new instances on demand. This matches how decoders were handled\n    before the receive stream stopped being recreated on decoder changes\n    (https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/494540).\n\n    Bug: chromium:572220780\n    Change-Id: Ibe646151c9803aab1e01665b8a70352f09e5c101\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508961\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48904}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/157bdfb63c.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0002.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0003.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0004.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0005.patch"], "git_node": "7e50b624e17be378b815b4f29fe59218eb6f26d1", "git_parents": ["ee57636b30a50857a132bdf985192d9faf388a82"], "node": "2eba70dfb355707648382d798179567db17dbe43", "parents": ["61f83e7bbdbe581f8701cefeea7af380467aef32"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 1aeb0050d4\n\nWe already cherry-picked this when we vendored e848b240c8.\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/1aeb0050d43fd4338f112c9775ee5c3a214c7c24\n    Revert \"Run audio_decoder_unittest, neteq tests and webrtc_opus_fec_test in audio_coding_unittests\"\n\n    This reverts commit e848b240c80da1b6fc3ef690046c2958d75527e5.\n\n    Reason for revert: breaks downstream\n\n    Original change's description:\n    \u003e Run audio_decoder_unittest, neteq tests and webrtc_opus_fec_test in audio_coding_unittests\n    \u003e\n    \u003e * Add audio_coding_unittests to run on fuchsia (currently only audio_decoder_unittest was running)\n    \u003e * frame_size_ms flag is used in 2 neteq files and moved in neteq_quality_test.h\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Time to run audio_coding_unittests is still small after adding these tests.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Change-Id: Id21aacef29b74bb4153b4aa5bf7f81bec86707d3\n    \u003e Bug: webrtc:498394143\n    \u003e Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508960\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    \u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48903}\n\n    Bug: webrtc:498394143\n    No-Presubmit: true\n    No-Tree-Checks: true\n    No-Try: true\n    Change-Id: I68a4e98c940b3e7643a36a66ff1f10dc46ac034b\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508965\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48905}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/1aeb0050d4.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0002.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0003.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0004.patch"], "git_node": "ff31dcca4a4b9eb9407253224959a404a9102ffc", "git_parents": ["7e50b624e17be378b815b4f29fe59218eb6f26d1"], "node": "5412d2aca9764a768cf6893d2cd33b8d600240d0", "parents": ["2eba70dfb355707648382d798179567db17dbe43"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 1926895897\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/1926895897a5b349fe840ea893bdd78e51ad2beb\n    Look up DTLS transports without blocking\n\n    Applying a description made a blocking call to the network thread to\n    look up the DTLS transports of all transceivers. The transport states\n    that JsepTransportController caches on the signaling thread now include\n    the DTLS transport, so the lookup uses those instead.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42222804\n    Change-Id: I3e2da6ca9438892814fa97ef3bf15c49fe336aca\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508143\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48906}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_collection.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_collection.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_offer_answer.cc"], "git_node": "4b0f1edbc949ee99eec74b4f91112baaaf01e8bb", "git_parents": ["ff31dcca4a4b9eb9407253224959a404a9102ffc"], "node": "38ac58401963a0864ebe9d569a45bedd0ba54717", "parents": ["5412d2aca9764a768cf6893d2cd33b8d600240d0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 6870f3a8aa\n\nWe already cherry-picked this when we vendored 4fe3aece79.\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/6870f3a8aa1b1bfdc97f2b8e1dcab9461f533352\n    Keep unchanged video decoders across SetDecoders()\n\n    Updating the receive codecs, e.g. when the receiving side creates a new\n    offer, deregistered all decoders and reset the decoder database. The\n    decoder in use was then recreated and needed a keyframe even if its\n    configuration hadn't changed, and a keyframe was always requested.\n\n    Apply only the difference between the old and new decoders instead.\n    Removed or updated decoders are deregistered, added or updated ones are\n    registered and unchanged decoders, including the one in use, keep\n    running. A keyframe is now only requested if the decoder in use was\n    removed or replaced.\n\n    Fixed: chromium:572220780\n    Change-Id: Ia4e6e4682c8ece42fc175f24d4b406345bd4a81d\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508964\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48907}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/6870f3a8aa.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0002.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0003.patch"], "git_node": "a58a9ffdd572cfc5f6fe0cdfb0b21d0a4557bbb0", "git_parents": ["4b0f1edbc949ee99eec74b4f91112baaaf01e8bb"], "node": "729cfcdb0a3d7ec2e7855b0a457914f5f41c54ed", "parents": ["38ac58401963a0864ebe9d569a45bedd0ba54717"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 1c42989f39\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/1c42989f395b1c916c76879eb35647046c456ed5\n    Split the HasStream parameterization of the legacy stats tests\n\n    StatsCollectorTrackTest ran each test twice: once with the tracks added\n    to the stats collector through a MediaStream, as Plan B does, and once\n    with AddTrack(), as Unified Plan does. The MediaStream mode goes away\n    with Plan B, so the two modes need to be separate.\n\n    - StatsCollectorTrackTest becomes a plain fixture that only uses\n      AddTrack(). LocalAndRemoteTracksWithSameSsrc now adds its remote track\n      with AddTrack() instead of through a MediaStream; both create the same\n      track report.\n    - The new StatsCollectorTrackPlanBTest fixture keeps the MediaStream\n      mode. It sits at the end of the file together with MediaStream copies\n      of the 15 tests that ran in both modes and the 3 Plan B-only tests, so\n      that this section can move to its own file.\n\n    Test mapping, 36 instances become 33 tests:\n\n    - HasStream/StatsCollectorTrackTest.X/0 -\u003e StatsCollectorTrackTest.X and\n      HasStream/StatsCollectorTrackTest.X/1 -\u003e\n      StatsCollectorTrackPlanBTest.X for the 15 tests that ran in both\n      modes.\n    - FilterOutNegativeInitialValues/1 and TwoLocalTracksWithSameSsrc/1 -\u003e\n      StatsCollectorTrackPlanBTest.X. Their /0 instances returned early.\n    - TwoLocalSendersWithSameTrack ignored the parameter, so /0 and /1 were\n      identical -\u003e\n      StatsCollectorTrackPlanBTest.TwoLocalSendersWithSameTrack.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:470300031\n    Change-Id: I8cf31b0830a15e49a5d67f3fa30bc23a5b7696ff\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508480\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Stefan Holmer \u003cstefan@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48908}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/legacy_stats_collector_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "575474e68e3c810734d1cfef227548f483b45597", "git_parents": ["a58a9ffdd572cfc5f6fe0cdfb0b21d0a4557bbb0"], "node": "1ec01915a3b12bec31c65e23b834e0aa6696c784", "parents": ["729cfcdb0a3d7ec2e7855b0a457914f5f41c54ed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from d53e2bf6d8\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/d53e2bf6d8d1c32fd92db069b4e2ac3527eeee53\n    Move the Plan B legacy stats tests to their own file\n\n    The previous change gathered the StatsCollectorTrackPlanBTest fixture\n    and its tests at the end of legacy_stats_collector_unittest.cc. Move\n    that section verbatim to legacy_stats_collector_plan_b_unittest.cc, so\n    that the whole file can be deleted when Plan B is removed.\n\n    Besides the moved code, the new file only has a file header, a TODO to\n    delete it, includes and the namespace. Its test target is part of\n    peerconnection_unittests.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:470300031\n    Change-Id: I3f84d327829d00fa0f470c2459f962a52428d839\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508429\n    Reviewed-by: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48909}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/legacy_stats_collector_plan_b_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/legacy_stats_collector_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "2726efaa6c12fd74cc4baabdc5d51b6f96184b3b", "git_parents": ["575474e68e3c810734d1cfef227548f483b45597"], "node": "bd37458ae357fe44c7eac21709568b573edda07a", "parents": ["1ec01915a3b12bec31c65e23b834e0aa6696c784"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 602d5fc23c\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/602d5fc23caaca7728ad5f3f0e68b92274d1a38a\n    Let FakeMediaEngine take custom fake engines\n\n    FakeMediaEngine always creates a default FakeVoiceEngine and\n    FakeVideoEngine. Add a constructor that takes the engines, so that a\n    test can install subclasses that create their own media channels.\n    FakePeerConnectionForStats will use this to create its channels through\n    RtpTransceiver::CreateChannel(), the way production code does, instead\n    of setting them on the transceiver directly.\n\n    The default constructor delegates to the new one.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:470300031\n    Change-Id: I9f4e44b60644b059e8bcf9fb3097dd2d35791df9\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508430\n    Reviewed-by: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48910}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/fake_media_engine.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/fake_media_engine.h"], "git_node": "0650743537cca84602671521a70a0d1e392289e8", "git_parents": ["2726efaa6c12fd74cc4baabdc5d51b6f96184b3b"], "node": "7c4f7aa7eb7ae66d7fa60868d1859f059ec5d3f4", "parents": ["bd37458ae357fe44c7eac21709568b573edda07a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 36df283620\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/36df2836205c0e115dd9e41b6f4f9dfd4b2846bc\n    Use the matching relay port when using TURN servers as STUN servers\n\n    PortConfiguration::GetRelayServerAddresses() checked whether a relay\n    config had a port with the requested protocol, but then returned the\n    address of the config's first port. For a config listing e.g. a TCP port\n    before a UDP one, STUN binding requests were sent over UDP to the TCP\n    address, so no srflx candidate was gathered from that server and\n    gathering completion was delayed until the requests timed out.\n\n    Return the addresses of all ports that match the protocol instead.\n    RelayServerConfigs created from RTCIceServer URLs have a single port, so\n    only configs built directly through the native API are affected.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:573252240\n    Change-Id: I260c0f0afc3ddf61b3f34163e2b3a5a257b7575d\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508721\n    Commit-Queue: Kacper Wasniowski \u003ckwasniow@cisco.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jonas Oreland \u003cjonaso@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48911}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/client/basic_port_allocator.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/client/basic_port_allocator_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "88eb73fd54ac892cf7ad41a984144ab55195ccb8", "git_parents": ["0650743537cca84602671521a70a0d1e392289e8"], "node": "86d6eb1b2151958b6a57a9e6abdf635aca820ffb", "parents": ["7c4f7aa7eb7ae66d7fa60868d1859f059ec5d3f4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from c3a079cbcb\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/c3a079cbcb548abe6445ffba899165ebaccad89a\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-10-15T04:06:02).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I99963bb9440cf3e07142cb88fbef9e574216e806\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509100\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48912}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "764f3fe9ccb8fb5d3cd687d3bd0327fafe237be3", "git_parents": ["88eb73fd54ac892cf7ad41a984144ab55195ccb8"], "node": "8d089623b36695726d4b64cc514ec716c0d3346c", "parents": ["86d6eb1b2151958b6a57a9e6abdf635aca820ffb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from be0b336fa3\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/be0b336fa368929971b3d01ab0b8eabcee26f5df\n    DualPi2: Set default target_delay=15ms and step_threshold=10ms\n\n    Bug: webrtc:447037083\n    Change-Id: If7f5dbd19ef713876c399f9e8b301baa3d7aff59\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509021\n    Auto-Submit: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48913}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/test/network_emulation/dual_pi2_network_queue.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/test/network_emulation/dual_pi2_network_queue_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/peer_scenario/bwe_integration_tests/scream_test.cc"], "git_node": "e189a052ec4f188b3f6b7fba77b72c3047aa1062", "git_parents": ["764f3fe9ccb8fb5d3cd687d3bd0327fafe237be3"], "node": "4d14688ce75eb676000a1add91793f765eba2b6e", "parents": ["8d089623b36695726d4b64cc514ec716c0d3346c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from c08eb4edb4\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/c08eb4edb4e9a42d70fdf6d75d5df607d93dcb1b\n    Use standard EWMA with g = 1/16 for SCReAMv2 l4s_alpha\n\n    Update ScreamV2::UpdateL4SAlpha to use a single EWMA gain l4s_avg_g = 1/16\n    (scaled by steps_per_rtt) and interpolate toward fraction_marked on both\n    increases and decreases:\n      l4s_alpha_ = g * fraction_marked + (1 - g) * l4s_alpha_\n\n    This aligns with Section 4.2.1.3 of the latest SCReAMv2 editor's draft\n    (draft-ietf-ccwg-rfc8298bis-screamv2-02) and avoids decaying toward 0\n    when 0 \u003c fraction_marked \u003c= l4s_alpha_.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:447037083\n    Change-Id: I23e3a66922fea100714bf0ecc6146b9aec416d64\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509040\n    Auto-Submit: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48914}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/g3doc/implementation_diff.md", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_parameters.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_parameters.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/peer_scenario/bwe_integration_tests/scream_test.cc"], "git_node": "f0ad40cae5c857fa5d7ecdcbe3920fe1226219a5", "git_parents": ["e189a052ec4f188b3f6b7fba77b72c3047aa1062"], "node": "cdf131063d8ecd256e146471d6f8f5e6388380ff", "parents": ["4d14688ce75eb676000a1add91793f765eba2b6e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 0820fe1ffa\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/0820fe1ffae4c0c2f49be252cc8377cbbd38a9a1\n    Add Sframe to RtpPacketizer::Create\n\n    Add PacketizationFormat::kSframe so that RtpPacketizerSframe can be\n    created through RtpPacketizer::Create() like the codec packetizers. The\n    marker bit of the last packet follows\n    RTPVideoHeader::is_last_frame_in_picture. RtpPayloadParams sets it from\n    CodecSpecificInfo::end_of_picture for all codecs.\n\n    This lets RTPSenderVideo pick the Sframe packetizer through the existing\n    packetization format selection when per-frame Sframe encryption is added\n    in a follow-up CL.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:479862368\n    Change-Id: I391e65daf4e13139679feb5ade0f51bb7a23e873\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509041\n    Commit-Queue: Kacper Wasniowski \u003ckwasniow@cisco.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48915}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_format.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_format.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0120.patch"], "git_node": "e829281c6f2a040270a2aa24e5a312f979bd96f0", "git_parents": ["f0ad40cae5c857fa5d7ecdcbe3920fe1226219a5"], "node": "0488dc0c58389a9d386889ced8ae6e4ea148d7e2", "parents": ["cdf131063d8ecd256e146471d6f8f5e6388380ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 9890fd1551\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/9890fd1551dbbe1f985419fb90cf172ef2d78832\n    Replace ReferenceBufferTracker with ReferenceBufferManager\n\n    Adds ReferenceBufferManager to track free, reserved, and populated V2\n    encoder reference buffers, apply buffer-space-type-specific keyframe\n    invalidation, and sort reference buffers by recency.\n\n    FrameEncodeSettings::reference_buffers are now specified in order of\n    preference (most recent first), allowing LibaomAv1EncoderV2 to map them\n    directly to LAST/GOLDEN/ALTREF instead of tracking timestamps with\n    ReferenceBufferTracker.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:496266459\n    Change-Id: I3f27b4d2ead3638492ac0662d3b0bf08d50f9bca\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508603\n    Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48916}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/g3doc/video_encoder_api_v2.md", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/simple_encoder_wrapper.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/libaom_av1_encoder_v2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/libaom_av1_encoder_v2.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/libaom_av1_encoder_v2_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/svc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/svc/reference_buffer_manager.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/svc/reference_buffer_manager.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/svc/reference_buffer_manager_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/utility/reference_buffer_tracker.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/utility/reference_buffer_tracker.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/utility/reference_buffer_tracker_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0092.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0140.patch"], "git_node": "2308e545b47a8f32760282473cb052c415c141b4", "git_parents": ["e829281c6f2a040270a2aa24e5a312f979bd96f0"], "node": "8a46ff5205c1dd5d722b2f1500f6d57943a5233e", "parents": ["0488dc0c58389a9d386889ced8ae6e4ea148d7e2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 9890fd1551 - moz.build file updates\n", "files": ["CLOBBER", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/video_coding_utility_gn/moz.build"], "git_node": "2c9933b67945c307c120c0bbe613ed959b4d71fd", "git_parents": ["2308e545b47a8f32760282473cb052c415c141b4"], "node": "eec771952179323546efc79983f185dfd987b44b", "parents": ["8a46ff5205c1dd5d722b2f1500f6d57943a5233e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 45872db107\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/45872db1076308186e1f256382a12a2f0fd28acd\n    Create FakePeerConnectionForStats channels with CreateChannel()\n\n    FakePeerConnectionForStats built its channels by hand. It installed a\n    BaseChannel subclass that overrode transport_name() with\n    RtpTransceiver::SetChannelForTest(), and then pushed the media channels\n    to the senders and receivers itself.\n\n    Create the channels with RtpTransceiver::CreateChannel() instead, the\n    way SdpOfferAnswerHandler does. The fake now installs\n    FakeVoiceEngineForStats and FakeVideoEngineForStats, which create the\n    *ForStats media channels that the tests configure. Like production code,\n    it runs the worker tasks before the network tasks, since the latter need\n    the channel.\n\n    ChannelForTesting is no longer needed. Its transport_name() override was\n    only read by RtpTransceiver::channel_transport_name(), which has no\n    callers; the stats collectors read the transport name that\n    SetTransport() sets.\n\n    The transceivers are still Plan B transceivers, which CreateChannel()\n    supports, so the tests are unchanged.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:470300031\n    Change-Id: I83dfb8b428bb1789f5f27aba4e2c15a06a4e6a60\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508462\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48917}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/fake_peer_connection_for_stats.h"], "git_node": "4b1587798c5864ad757b944232a1b4d3641ea6d0", "git_parents": ["2c9933b67945c307c120c0bbe613ed959b4d71fd"], "node": "810c19fb21a18831174cf018b93acc7f3a317bf1", "parents": ["eec771952179323546efc79983f185dfd987b44b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 71180d8442\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/71180d84424d81bf957744678b93e7cd01f55fff\n    Fix qualityLimitationReason bug in \"maintain-resolution\" mode.\n\n    When \"maintain-resolution\" is used, QP scaler is disabled. If this is\n    singlecast and we are bitrate limited, we are neither triggering the\n    traditional \"adapt down\" logic or have simulcast layers to disable. What\n    ends up happening is frames are dropped dynamically by `kEncoder` or\n    `kMediaOptimization` frame dropping logic.\n\n    Before this CL, this kind of frame rate limitation due to BW did not\n    result in qualityLimitationReason \"bandwidth\" (it incorrectly reported\n    \"none\").\n\n    This CL fixes that bug by introducing a\n    `dropped_due_to_bandwidth_rate_tracker_` tracker (configured with the\n    same bucket size and count as `encoded_frame_rate_tracker_` for\n    consistency), and if the frame drop ratio in the last ~second is at or\n    above 20%, we report \"bandwidth\" limited.\n\n    Drive-by: made `fps` more explicit for the helper fake track method.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:565275187\n    Change-Id: I1f568a34557c28286f3594cd0a6817bb99799956\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509020\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48918}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_encodings_integrationtest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/peer_connection_test_wrapper.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/peer_connection_test_wrapper.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/send_statistics_proxy.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/send_statistics_proxy.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/send_statistics_proxy_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "ad07bc6eb23a96c47e257c79b3ab8d22ae432a6a", "git_parents": ["4b1587798c5864ad757b944232a1b4d3641ea6d0"], "node": "3db88e2b02fd56152118501be7c1842b6ea4c3c4", "parents": ["810c19fb21a18831174cf018b93acc7f3a317bf1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 81075eb836\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/81075eb8361a2b702cfa6b32ef82b815e2371b64\n    Add qualityLimitationReason test for \"maintain-framerate\".\n\n    For completeness, add the same type of test as was added in [1] but for\n    \"maintain-framerate\" instead of \"maintain-resolution\".\n\n    [1] https://webrtc-review.git.corp.google.com/c/src/+/509020\n\n    Bug: webrtc:565275187\n    Change-Id: Iee719f69bbaef5a2851f52ed7b4a81843a834495\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509140\n    Commit-Queue: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48919}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_encodings_integrationtest.cc"], "git_node": "f449bd95bc3afaa282c50056e2ae98a1c1edb177", "git_parents": ["ad07bc6eb23a96c47e257c79b3ab8d22ae432a6a"], "node": "a29470b051652090ddc6d3f62bf2346c945692ac", "parents": ["3db88e2b02fd56152118501be7c1842b6ea4c3c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from c5f0fa143c\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/c5f0fa143cfe267cce355bcf436ab58992626ca3\n    Run audio_decoder_unittest and webrtc_opus_fec_test in audio_coding_unittests\n\n    Add audio_coding_unittests to run on fuchsia (currently only audio_decoder_unittest was running)\n\n    Change-Id: Idde915c439939c08abcaee47217043a04465e301\n    Bug: webrtc:498394143\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509220\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48920}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/specs/client.webrtc.json", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/specs/gn_isolate_map.pyl", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/specs/test_suites.pyl", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/specs/tryserver.webrtc.json", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0091.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/tools_webrtc/get_landmines.py"], "git_node": "e5b8fd209d29ea844e97391beb4b2c7903ac3ec3", "git_parents": ["f449bd95bc3afaa282c50056e2ae98a1c1edb177"], "node": "888d031ae9cd3a14deee2148ba8fd06ca848d044", "parents": ["a29470b051652090ddc6d3f62bf2346c945692ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from be2b87be35\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/be2b87be352f0c6c37671d7e21a2f49f6aabf6ea\n    dtls-in-stun: improve test coverage of Connection\n\n    drive-by: use more common `Buffer` instead of `BufferT\u003cuint8_t\u003e`\n\n    Bug: webrtc:367395350\n    Change-Id: I6ac339721935a5e2b2a6483e7ec76370eb878dd4\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/497320\n    Reviewed-by: Jonas Oreland \u003cjonaso@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48921}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/connection_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/test/test_port.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/test/test_port.h"], "git_node": "2c7bc3ebed89229522269254b5ade0d348dc5493", "git_parents": ["e5b8fd209d29ea844e97391beb4b2c7903ac3ec3"], "node": "0864490782d985ce0eac046545f97b1c1349860c", "parents": ["888d031ae9cd3a14deee2148ba8fd06ca848d044"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 52da778c18\n\nEssentially a no-op since we're going to see this change\nreverted when we vendor in b67a9ce02b.\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/52da778c185a17fe953ead983af213aa447e773e\n    Allow combining AV1 SVC frames without dependency descriptor.\n\n    Although using scalability features with without Dependency Descriptors\n    isn't a supported use case (falls outside the RTP Profile for AV1), it\n    would help in some cases where the full stream is received (no sequence\n    number gaps) and frames are otherwise detectable as complete (e.g. using\n    the marker bit), to allow decoding SVC frames without knowing the actual\n    spatial index.\n\n    When receiving AV1 SVC without a dependency descriptor, PacketBuffer\n    emits one RtpFrameObject per spatial layer and RtpSeqNumOnlyRefFinder\n    verifies sequence number continuity across the temporal unit.\n    RtpSeqNumOnlyRefFinder previously stamped SpatialIndex(0) onto every\n    subframe, causing CombineAndDeleteFrames to reject multi-layer temporal\n    units as having duplicate spatial indices.\n\n    Leave SpatialIndex unset (std::nullopt) in RtpSeqNumOnlyRefFinder and\n    only populate SpatialIndex and SpatialLayerFrameSize in\n    CombineAndDeleteFrames when spatial indices are present. Also replace\n    raw pointer arithmetic and memcpy in CombineAndDeleteFrames with\n    std::span and std::ranges::copy.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:560293075, chromium:569667447\n    Change-Id: I504fa458ebc1c6f902b39593de9680faa43f2d2a\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508962\n    Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48922}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/b67a9ce02b.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0002.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0003.patch"], "git_node": "f536f5864c87d320a7021663dc0b33af9d24e179", "git_parents": ["2c7bc3ebed89229522269254b5ade0d348dc5493"], "node": "5a0b8cf7774866fcf158f50bd0fcc32e338036a8", "parents": ["0864490782d985ce0eac046545f97b1c1349860c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from b6cbf8bb73\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/b6cbf8bb73ac34cd0d546dc5310f728212a76068\n    Start gathering and discard the candidate pool without blocking\n\n    Applying a description made blocking calls to the network thread to\n    start gathering and to discard the ICE candidate pool. Both now post a\n    task instead. The pooled ICE credentials that SdpOfferAnswerHandler\n    caches are updated with a reply from the network thread.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42222804\n    Change-Id: I2575ba0e3723decd51afe26f7b705ae311d0c03e\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508145\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48923}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_ice_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_offer_answer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_offer_answer.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/fake_peer_connection_for_stats.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/peer_scenario/scenario_connection.cc"], "git_node": "c486a427264062126fbd663b8825754692f466a7", "git_parents": ["f536f5864c87d320a7021663dc0b33af9d24e179"], "node": "a3ea6acf057348f8d15065c2162746007c6b8125", "parents": ["5a0b8cf7774866fcf158f50bd0fcc32e338036a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from ee18f345bc\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/ee18f345bc4a05732fc64f804b96458cc4c3e27c\n    Remove redundant CopyOnWriteBuffer constructor\n\n    Implicitly switch callers to the constructor that takes std::span as 1st\n    argument (see line #62).\n\n    This also drops support for using this constructor with a container of\n    'char's rather than a container of 'uint8_t's.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42226010\n    Change-Id: Ic01c83095c7353566f5285b0685a032d4abb3eb6\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508602\n    Auto-Submit: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48924}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/copy_on_write_buffer.h"], "git_node": "3fb37d967f9c984a8f8a9bd0f62a4f77f264e5c1", "git_parents": ["c486a427264062126fbd663b8825754692f466a7"], "node": "84352ea9b304748291f0ec4a24867b47c3e3eed4", "parents": ["a3ea6acf057348f8d15065c2162746007c6b8125"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 2f2246127c\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/2f2246127ce24cdd6c3a1090021424b5bfd67b94\n    Roll back transports without a separate blocking call\n\n    SdpOfferAnswerHandler::Rollback() rolled back the transports with a\n    separate blocking call to the network thread. The transports are now\n    rolled back in Rollback()'s existing network batch, after the channels\n    have been detached from them.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42222804\n    Change-Id: I570893871ba065fb81d3bbfad4da3788a37b0c06\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508461\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48925}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_jsep_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_offer_answer.cc"], "git_node": "cc228bd2fc720207dd0496e615c6be8804645e31", "git_parents": ["3fb37d967f9c984a8f8a9bd0f62a4f77f264e5c1"], "node": "cbec1c812db31431866b435f876ea7826e8025c5", "parents": ["84352ea9b304748291f0ec4a24867b47c3e3eed4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 9a49bcc60f\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/9a49bcc60f4b22293dc9451bdbc679c18e5b3a9e\n    Make GetPacketizationFormat a member of RTPSenderVideo\n\n    The packetization format depends on the codec of the frame and on the\n    sender configuration. Read the configuration from the member instead of\n    passing it as a bool next to the codec type, so that the call site only\n    passes what changes per frame. A follow-up adds Sframe, which also\n    depends on the configuration.\n\n    No functional change.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:479862368\n    Change-Id: I755bda7d5073289acfd9a5fbad073368b8d50c8a\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509222\n    Commit-Queue: Kacper Wasniowski \u003ckwasniow@cisco.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48926}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_sender_video.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_sender_video.h"], "git_node": "ef7121ab64d3355f11a5deb1410661ab75a2c612", "git_parents": ["cc228bd2fc720207dd0496e615c6be8804645e31"], "node": "2ca1f6de8fc0c10591e2d52bdad709dfefbbc6cd", "parents": ["cbec1c812db31431866b435f876ea7826e8025c5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from c81ada6ff4\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/c81ada6ff4b322b52d641401ad42a656ac9f3497\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-10-16T04:06:39).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I600fe0586955d6b544af901193b81eb60f47ae29\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509320\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48927}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "42fb0474a286f5c45c1de91075ba74e6adb5fc22", "git_parents": ["ef7121ab64d3355f11a5deb1410661ab75a2c612"], "node": "fc551a1903439f461768a05b76b46649463c7f78", "parents": ["2ca1f6de8fc0c10591e2d52bdad709dfefbbc6cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 7b923bff80\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/7b923bff80cdd2e86afae32750f61b8f29ceb7e6\n    Avoid integer-overflow in WebRtcSpl_FilterMAFastQ12\n\n    Use int64_t instead of int32_t for the accumulator, matching the fix\n    for the sibling AR filter landed in\n    https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/26580\n\n    The sum of int16_t coefficient/sample products can exceed the int32_t\n    range, including with LPC coefficients generated for NetEq. Signed\n    overflow is undefined behavior and would make the output saturate to\n    the wrong sign in rare cases.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:574106925\n    Change-Id: Ibfb475bf4dbbb9989f0fd12ccb44ba6d6bf731f1\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509300\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Lundin \u003chenrik.lundin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Henrik Lundin \u003chenrik.lundin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jakob Ivarsson\u200e \u003cjakobi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48928}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/filter_ma_fast_q12.c", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/signal_processing_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "5a2061e1e86926d16b82b11c754c8290256a7155", "git_parents": ["42fb0474a286f5c45c1de91075ba74e6adb5fc22"], "node": "538a6aafb7d8e1c0401714b1d9ad1730890ba95c", "parents": ["fc551a1903439f461768a05b76b46649463c7f78"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 43e7485b86\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/43e7485b866e8431b5a8bf892bef8566589bbd1d\n    Add gMock guidance to the pre-reviewer skill\n\n    Document two conventions for test code.\n\n    - Add using-declarations for ::testing symbols instead of spelling out\n      the ::testing:: prefix at each call site.\n    - Check containers with matchers such as SizeIs() and IsEmpty() instead\n      of comparing the result of size() or empty().\n\n    Bug: none\n    No-try: true\n    Change-Id: I4da7cdd2bb9120502f8f4542cca5e329cc7a79e9\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509200\n    Auto-Submit: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48929}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/agents/skills/pre-reviewer/SKILL.md"], "git_node": "024aa80e9fccdc3d3bc59c814c8881856067ab91", "git_parents": ["5a2061e1e86926d16b82b11c754c8290256a7155"], "node": "1cfd34e5bfed72f3f141e576460e3a36646486fd", "parents": ["538a6aafb7d8e1c0401714b1d9ad1730890ba95c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 9b1c953a8d\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/9b1c953a8d3de288781c058f548d4757740677b7\n    Deflake RTCStatsIntegrationTest.GetStatsFromCaller.\n\n    # No need to re-run all the tests, the latest PS just changed a comment\n    NOTRY=True\n\n    Bug: webrtc:574304820\n    Change-Id: I3b717f68b99a1fbd64ed53a8f8fd2be7b40b3c0f\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509380\n    Reviewed-by: Guido Urdaneta \u003cguidou@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48930}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtc_stats_integrationtest.cc"], "git_node": "18a41ad19ee250a0ca94977f3dca2d1e63246fe3", "git_parents": ["024aa80e9fccdc3d3bc59c814c8881856067ab91"], "node": "051769247909b55d602cd46ac91cceba1a01b412", "parents": ["1cfd34e5bfed72f3f141e576460e3a36646486fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 04db1a1523\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/04db1a152381fe4694a2d532d3d1c6c481c09221\n    ScreamV2: Add parameter for minimum max_data_in_flight in MSS.\n\n    In WebRTC, min_ref_window defaults to 1000 bytes (compared to 3000 bytes\n    in the IETF SCReAMv2 draft) so target_rate can reach low bitrates on\n    short-RTT links. However, with ref_window_overhead_min = 1.5, this\n    allowed max_data_in_flight() to drop to 1500 bytes (1.17 MSS), causing\n    premature congestion window pauses and ACK starvation at low bitrates.\n\n    Add min_max_data_in_flight_mss (field trial key \"MinMaxDataInFlightMss\",\n    default 4) to floor max_data_in_flight() at 4 MSS (5120 bytes by\n    default), matching the ~4.5 MSS minimum send window in the IETF draft\n    while allowing ref_window_ and target_rate to go lower.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:447037083\n    Change-Id: Idf623eee848e9a674bbe28f36f94d944545540ad\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509261\n    Auto-Submit: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48931}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_parameters.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_parameters.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "d94978595c6d742574a2c19eb212d04a105f43df", "git_parents": ["18a41ad19ee250a0ca94977f3dca2d1e63246fe3"], "node": "15362c5da060cdecf87232d75aaf18c0a7583c28", "parents": ["051769247909b55d602cd46ac91cceba1a01b412"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from e741d2dda6\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/e741d2dda61ececf040503855fc7d3b7cd86d15a\n    dcsctp: Rate limit duplicate FORWARD-TSN chunks\n\n    In commit 0ca62e3752149ad37f73bf074db0a5f8fcaf6585, rate limiting of\n    FORWARD-TSNs were added to at most one per min(200ms, srtt),\n    regardless of whether it advanced the cumulative TSN or not. RFC 3758\n    section 3.5 (C3) says that a FORWARD-TSN MUST be sent when the\n    Advanced.Peer.Ack.Point advances and the implementation note about\n    waiting an RTT only applies to duplicate FORWARD-TSN chunks. This was\n    not considered at that time.\n\n    If there is frequent packet loss, and messages were sent with limited\n    reliability, this delayed every FORWARD-TSN that followed another one\n    within the interval, and each such delay blocked the receiver from\n    delivering messages on ordered streams for up to 200ms. This aligns with\n    how FreeBSD handles rate limiting of FORWARD-TSN.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:572239331\n    Change-Id: I73f2a5e8ffc2ddb1eadcbee641cc19a4bcc4a7f2\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508542\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Victor Boivie \u003cboivie@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48932}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/dcsctp_socket_test.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/transmission_control_block.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/transmission_control_block.h"], "git_node": "73ea6aae7d42086a6324a68b476410ccbc65a910", "git_parents": ["d94978595c6d742574a2c19eb212d04a105f43df"], "node": "4191d6a7dacb284d3e6cef5ee462766ea93b421d", "parents": ["15362c5da060cdecf87232d75aaf18c0a7583c28"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from b1fb16d6b3\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/b1fb16d6b3d47675146187ca8dc590a548c97e27\n    Lazily allocate SctpDataChannel::ObserverAdapter\n\n    SctpDataChannel::CreateProxy unconditionally allocated an adapter even\n    when the registered observer opted into network thread callbacks, or\n    when no observer was registered.\n\n    - Instantiate ObserverAdapter when required in RegisterObserver().\n    - Initialize the observer delegate in ObserverAdapter's constructor\n      and remove SetDelegate().\n    - Reset observer_adapter_ in UnregisterObserver() and avoid posting a\n      deletion task from ~SctpDataChannel().\n    - Remove a redundant scoped_refptr\u003cSctpDataChannel\u003e self-reference.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:510487699\n    Change-Id: I215844a6d73cb6da5e93b778ed0b9fbecd8b83e7\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509060\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48933}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0118.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sctp_data_channel.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sctp_data_channel.h"], "git_node": "619501089f3975ccc8436cc44eadc9448ac9e1fd", "git_parents": ["73ea6aae7d42086a6324a68b476410ccbc65a910"], "node": "09427ab22d7e6ed45b110af1652cd368853344f4", "parents": ["4191d6a7dacb284d3e6cef5ee462766ea93b421d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from b67a9ce02b\n\nWe already cherry-picked this when we vendored 52da778c18.\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/b67a9ce02b9921a822b1cbbc1c7b560c05a23797\n    Revert \"Allow combining AV1 SVC frames without dependency descriptor.\"\n\n    This reverts commit 52da778c185a17fe953ead983af213aa447e773e.\n\n    Reason for revert: Breaks downstream test\n\n    Failure Link: \u003cLINK TO FAILURE\u003e\n\n    Original change's description:\n    \u003e Allow combining AV1 SVC frames without dependency descriptor.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Although using scalability features with without Dependency Descriptors\n    \u003e isn't a supported use case (falls outside the RTP Profile for AV1), it\n    \u003e would help in some cases where the full stream is received (no sequence\n    \u003e number gaps) and frames are otherwise detectable as complete (e.g. using\n    \u003e the marker bit), to allow decoding SVC frames without knowing the actual\n    \u003e spatial index.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e When receiving AV1 SVC without a dependency descriptor, PacketBuffer\n    \u003e emits one RtpFrameObject per spatial layer and RtpSeqNumOnlyRefFinder\n    \u003e verifies sequence number continuity across the temporal unit.\n    \u003e RtpSeqNumOnlyRefFinder previously stamped SpatialIndex(0) onto every\n    \u003e subframe, causing CombineAndDeleteFrames to reject multi-layer temporal\n    \u003e units as having duplicate spatial indices.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Leave SpatialIndex unset (std::nullopt) in RtpSeqNumOnlyRefFinder and\n    \u003e only populate SpatialIndex and SpatialLayerFrameSize in\n    \u003e CombineAndDeleteFrames when spatial indices are present. Also replace\n    \u003e raw pointer arithmetic and memcpy in CombineAndDeleteFrames with\n    \u003e std::span and std::ranges::copy.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Bug: webrtc:560293075, chromium:569667447\n    \u003e Change-Id: I504fa458ebc1c6f902b39593de9680faa43f2d2a\n    \u003e Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508962\n    \u003e Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    \u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48922}\n\n    Bug: webrtc:560293075, chromium:569667447\n    No-Presubmit: true\n    No-Tree-Checks: true\n    No-Try: true\n    Change-Id: Ic16301fde155db2eef2275568c9286b317d755ab\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509420\n    Bot-Commit: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48934}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/b67a9ce02b.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0002.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0003.patch"], "git_node": "5f460f1f3cbe2d0d84b0a66f7c477f18b42aa6ee", "git_parents": ["619501089f3975ccc8436cc44eadc9448ac9e1fd"], "node": "21b2751180354ea4403aafa7ba08b64ea96e00c5", "parents": ["09427ab22d7e6ed45b110af1652cd368853344f4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 541ce6db55\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/541ce6db5597b8d0b97981fec53382a53435e176\n    Implement adaptation in FakePeriodicVideoSource (apply sink wants).\n\n    The impact of this is that if CPU or BW adaptation says we are limited,\n    the resolution and/or frame rate actually gets limited at the source\n    level. This is needed for resolution downscaling due to adaptation\n    in singlecast, unless `scale_resolution_down_to` is used.\n\n    The \"scaleTo\" workaround can now be removed from the test\n    \"QualityLimitationReasonReportsBandwidthInMaintainFrameRate\".\n\n    Bug: webrtc:573828148\n    Change-Id: I1bef322aceeea4f193c7db2724f71e70a39e45da\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509160\n    Auto-Submit: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48935}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_encodings_integrationtest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/fake_periodic_video_source.h"], "git_node": "ab9fa6c7639a19d77330d62ef9bc2529217ef73b", "git_parents": ["5f460f1f3cbe2d0d84b0a66f7c477f18b42aa6ee"], "node": "53d95d1c7550d6456223b7b942742e4de95c7218", "parents": ["21b2751180354ea4403aafa7ba08b64ea96e00c5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from bef233bc69\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/bef233bc69712a4976442f980b1355b990c1107b\n    Cleanup StunByteStringAttribute constructors\n\n    Delete deprecated constructor as unused.\n    Relax constructor that takes reference to vector to accept any span\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: Ice3c1d7c1927b8098edbc0fc68465d971dcea802\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509281\n    Auto-Submit: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48936}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/transport/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/transport/stun.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/transport/stun.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch"], "git_node": "5a988f9f2e2293b7254accedb80b95645fe6a617", "git_parents": ["ab9fa6c7639a19d77330d62ef9bc2529217ef73b"], "node": "5fb6dbf5e79c70a38a5f0d4b11fffbcbf283eb3b", "parents": ["53d95d1c7550d6456223b7b942742e4de95c7218"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from b308828a29\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/b308828a29ed1e897fdcb603da01587cdcac0f35\n    Fix flaky ScaleToIsOrientationAgnostic parameterized test.\n\n    NOTRY=True\n\n    Bug: webrtc:573828148\n    Change-Id: I94db917ecffcf65caecbb134a36cc2ab700bd6ee\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509440\n    Auto-Submit: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48937}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_encodings_integrationtest.cc"], "git_node": "1618f277c7d2729514d39a6e78819bda13a8a19f", "git_parents": ["5a988f9f2e2293b7254accedb80b95645fe6a617"], "node": "0ab9bfb243c9c9a4f3d7b826683a7dbe9dbe6b59", "parents": ["5fb6dbf5e79c70a38a5f0d4b11fffbcbf283eb3b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 65b585ae24\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/65b585ae24587b5b9ccf8c80b9c868b7d013ae17\n    dcsctp: Fast retransmit while in fast recovery\n\n    When a chunk reached three miss indications while the endpoint was\n    already in fast recovery, it was only marked for normal retransmission\n    and had to wait until the congestion window allowed it to be sent. As\n    cwnd was just halved when entering fast recovery, this typically meant\n    waiting until about half of the window had been acknowledged, adding up\n    to half an RTT of recovery latency for every loss but the first one in\n    a window. With bursty loss, several losses per window is the common\n    case.\n\n    RFC 4960 section 7.2.4 step 3 (retransmit the chunks in a single packet,\n    ignoring cwnd) is not conditional on step 2 (entering fast recovery);\n    only the cwnd and ssthresh adjustments are skipped while in fast\n    recovery. Both FreeBSD and Linux fast retransmit every chunk that\n    reaches the threshold.\n\n    Chunks that reach the threshold are now always scheduled for fast\n    retransmission. Losses detected by T3-rtx expiry are unaffected. The\n    cwnd is still only reduced once per fast recovery period.\n\n    Two existing tests had to be migrated to the new behavior.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:572224226\n    Change-Id: Ib459aa9897825f677985aa9dfd6aa49f8a8876b8\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508544\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Victor Boivie \u003cboivie@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48938}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/tx/outstanding_data.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/tx/outstanding_data.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/tx/outstanding_data_test.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/tx/retransmission_queue_test.cc"], "git_node": "5c3065ad74d871fe88feb2ae91072c78f9642111", "git_parents": ["1618f277c7d2729514d39a6e78819bda13a8a19f"], "node": "0f0742d276d66d5e3ec966812a112bc256c55666", "parents": ["0ab9bfb243c9c9a4f3d7b826683a7dbe9dbe6b59"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 524dd5292a\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/524dd5292a7134b7d1a68aff3bc11642c8184ed7\n    Add fallback for WGC window capturer\n\n    Wrap the WGC window capturer in a FallbackDesktopCapturerWrapper with\n    the Cropping/GDI window capturer as fallback. Record each SelectSource()\n    outcome of both capturers to\n    WebRTC.DesktopCapture.Win.WgcWindowFallbackSelectSource.\n\n    The only thing to consider with this change is that SelectSource() now\n    can fails if GDI rejects a window that WGC accepted. However, this is\n    not expected to happen, as both capturers run the same visibility check;\n    still I've added a histogram to check this.\n\n    This change is behind a kill switch.\n\n    Bug: chromium:567859840\n    Change-Id: Icf262b9eeead3c810b3a024070976ddc9d42fe40\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/507500\n    Reviewed-by: Johannes Kron \u003ckron@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Palak Agarwal \u003cagpalak@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48939}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/desktop_capture/desktop_capture_options.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/desktop_capture/desktop_capturer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/desktop_capture/fallback_desktop_capturer_wrapper.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/desktop_capture/fallback_desktop_capturer_wrapper.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/desktop_capture/fallback_desktop_capturer_wrapper_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/desktop_capture/win/wgc_capturer_win_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0134.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0137.patch"], "git_node": "893547edfc00de12a8ce6e042eeef5acff351e5d", "git_parents": ["5c3065ad74d871fe88feb2ae91072c78f9642111"], "node": "0f01fc68aaf6c4d8eaa1a34933c88a0bae08036f", "parents": ["0f0742d276d66d5e3ec966812a112bc256c55666"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from ec0c50db25\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/ec0c50db2550e193ed620b599b25fa7c537df874\n    Mark Buffer-\u003estring_view conversion explicit\n\n    Implicit conversions are generally disallowed by style guide.\n\n    This particular one creates ambiguity when CopyOnWriteBuffer is created\n    from Buffer as Buffer is implicitly convertible both to string_view and\n    to span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e. Marking string_view conversion explicit resolve\n    ambiguity in favor of span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42226010\n    Change-Id: I3b190573f613c7bf36a3ce13e62f1235721e4977\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509081\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48940}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtcp_transceiver_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/buffer.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/buffer_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/openssl_stream_adapter.cc"], "git_node": "7ee3a0d0241af52f8706382e296a88a16bee1d16", "git_parents": ["893547edfc00de12a8ce6e042eeef5acff351e5d"], "node": "bbe7013608542461753b73e0a66f318afe7208cc", "parents": ["0f01fc68aaf6c4d8eaa1a34933c88a0bae08036f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from ff1c351065\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/ff1c351065505980baff04323980bcd8740b3ede\n    Fix flaky ScaleToMaintainsAspectRatio.\n\n    NOTRY=True\n\n    Bug: webrtc:573828148\n    Change-Id: Ie5516febe8f7971e59d9889acc27e32be951da5d\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509520\n    Commit-Queue: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48941}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_encodings_integrationtest.cc"], "git_node": "6c483a9efdec0f9c1190ba42f31418d411a796d0", "git_parents": ["7ee3a0d0241af52f8706382e296a88a16bee1d16"], "node": "77c7412e29ce4669c0ae37a2d44799a704d220cf", "parents": ["bbe7013608542461753b73e0a66f318afe7208cc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from ad255b4e05\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/ad255b4e05288681bb95e861788dc63722c0112e\n    Handle failed I420 conversion in VideoFrameSampler::Create\n\n    Return nullptr from VideoFrameSampler::Create when the underlying\n    frame buffer accessor or ToI420ForInspection() returns nullptr, and\n    check ToI420ForInspection() before allocating the scaled buffer in\n    GetSampleValuesForFrame.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:574312303\n    Change-Id: I1654cba6437269b1627c7a532a6245228d4e6b9b\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509480\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48942}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/halton_frame_sampler.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/halton_frame_sampler_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/video_frame_sampler.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/video_frame_sampler_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "48cb7de5bdf03566cc351d4ad2b2a973de35b49c", "git_parents": ["6c483a9efdec0f9c1190ba42f31418d411a796d0"], "node": "96a5f78c7301925ee0e09c21d979cc50d96daab0", "parents": ["77c7412e29ce4669c0ae37a2d44799a704d220cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 3cdeaaaff3\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/3cdeaaaff3ad6dd1a23f6eacc8daacbc1fe14226\n    Enforce kMaxFrameSidePixels on decoded video frames\n\n    Check that decoded frame width and height do not exceed\n    kMaxFrameSidePixels in Dav1dDecoder, LibvpxVp9Decoder, and\n    H264DecoderImpl.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:574312303\n    Change-Id: I4bf8ecbca92aa44be0ba479bd8f1bd27c95fc41a\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509262\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48943}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/dav1d_decoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/dav1d_decoder_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/h264/h264_decoder_impl.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/vp9/libvpx_vp9_decoder.cc"], "git_node": "97da3f33297e3095212ebd7b29071a0de321c0a0", "git_parents": ["48cb7de5bdf03566cc351d4ad2b2a973de35b49c"], "node": "f8b221055d91f0cac941dafa4a2955dc206e6c05", "parents": ["96a5f78c7301925ee0e09c21d979cc50d96daab0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from f7126d621e\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/f7126d621eb47305291a912939d064f9cacdc4fa\n    Check libyuv return values in VideoFrameBuffer conversions\n\n    Return nullptr from ToI420() and CropAndScale() when the underlying\n    libyuv conversion fails, as documented on VideoFrameBuffer::ToI420(),\n    and use RTC_CHECK_EQ on libyuv copy, rotation, and scaling helpers.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:574312303\n    Change-Id: Ie236328267f1cd1a2e526f0f2d51b0770f0bf9fe\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509461\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48944}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/i010_buffer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/i210_buffer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/i410_buffer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/i420_buffer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/i422_buffer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/i444_buffer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/nv12_buffer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/test/i422_buffer_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/test/i444_buffer_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/video_frame_buffer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_video/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_video/video_frame_buffer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_video/video_frame_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0145.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0147.patch"], "git_node": "253a453643a48c8cb60b61bdff1010d2d6007ee4", "git_parents": ["97da3f33297e3095212ebd7b29071a0de321c0a0"], "node": "f8ec62fa6bb582499431e470e94110fab52e8950", "parents": ["f8b221055d91f0cac941dafa4a2955dc206e6c05"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 225793c2c0\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/225793c2c02d80b988a9e43629127dfb1766eabd\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-10-17T04:07:04).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: If19a74ab598e04db649717aa77446f0be3a53ad9\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509600\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48945}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "c9cf93ebd370a09b80130548d65dc2883a4f9695", "git_parents": ["253a453643a48c8cb60b61bdff1010d2d6007ee4"], "node": "e41bf5538c256e4a296167938e8979c63bd7d037", "parents": ["f8ec62fa6bb582499431e470e94110fab52e8950"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 4fdd50a57b\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/4fdd50a57b79826ea87cc5170be78b6444d9cdf9\n    Use accessor functions instead of direct access to ASN1_STRING fields\n\n    ASN1_STRING is going to be opaque to all BoringSSL users.\n    Upstream OpenSSL has made this switch, we should follow so that we can\n    keep all uses of ASN1 data slices safe.\n\n    Bug: chromium:443769299,chromium:476131577\n    Signed-off-by: xfding \u003cxfding@google.com\u003e\n    Change-Id: Iaed07b1426965af1cfe60e4da94269ae6a6a6964\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509561\n    Reviewed-by: Jonas Oreland \u003cjonaso@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48946}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/openssl_certificate.cc"], "git_node": "1e07b9d3ba317f024e6de8cd0a2f1c7c3adcd9fc", "git_parents": ["c9cf93ebd370a09b80130548d65dc2883a4f9695"], "node": "b93e91ab4128ebb47cc297c24326d791b085e384", "parents": ["e41bf5538c256e4a296167938e8979c63bd7d037"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 35de85922d\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/35de85922d5bd2bd0a6d8b935a8f5717c6d1906d\n    Pass Port callbacks and tiebreaker in constructor\n\n    Extend Port::PortParametersRef and CreateRelayPortArgs with\n    ice_tiebreaker and a Port::Callbacks struct so ports can be initialized\n    with their tiebreaker and event callbacks during construction rather\n    than via post-construction setters and Subscribe* calls.\n\n    Retain const-ref RelayPortFactoryInterface::Create overloads and\n    empty-copy support on Port::Callbacks for downstream compatibility.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42224914, webrtc:42222117\n    Change-Id: Ib01079a8e478b0c7c86eb212d1d4442645696487\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/467840\n    Reviewed-by: Jonas Oreland \u003cjonaso@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48947}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/connection_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/local_network_access_port_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/port.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/port.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/port_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/stun_port.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/stun_port.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/stun_port_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/tcp_port.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/tcp_port.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/turn_port.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/turn_port.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/turn_port_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/client/basic_port_allocator.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/client/basic_port_allocator.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/client/relay_port_factory_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/client/turn_port_factory.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/client/turn_port_factory.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/test/fake_port_allocator.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/test/test_port.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/test/test_port.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/test/turn_server.h"], "git_node": "d1bfd93e0a2a419fc367e182b3cd3850119d0ecb", "git_parents": ["1e07b9d3ba317f024e6de8cd0a2f1c7c3adcd9fc"], "node": "6d2b2326e7849e963f174ec80c29364549d3251e", "parents": ["b93e91ab4128ebb47cc297c24326d791b085e384"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from f30a911f67\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/f30a911f678645a72c09bb319922f73ee0035411\n    Zero-initialize 10-bit buffers in VideoFrameBufferPool\n\n    Add InitializeData() to I010Buffer and I210Buffer, and invoke\n    InitializeData() in VideoFrameBufferPool when zero_initialize_ is\n    enabled for I010, I210, and I410 buffers.\n\n    Fixed: chromium:504552032\n    Change-Id: I36ce748c3da44e4f119332de5c180f80eca93cc9\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509582\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48948}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/i010_buffer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/i010_buffer.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/i210_buffer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/i210_buffer.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_video/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_video/video_frame_buffer_pool.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_video/video_frame_buffer_pool_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0149.patch"], "git_node": "61a756bce622b99844669aad783c250396b8722e", "git_parents": ["d1bfd93e0a2a419fc367e182b3cd3850119d0ecb"], "node": "a4d2d4bf5829ff7b9e4c7d184067eaee04e3efb4", "parents": ["6d2b2326e7849e963f174ec80c29364549d3251e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 64525537e2\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/64525537e27d4530928a3d1be4204d253819b279\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-10-18T04:09:13).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: Ief2ea81942daa92bf55702bdc4e155a370c36420\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509640\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48949}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "2312aa31f67f903a12f16272c7f8e12eb0d1a0ef", "git_parents": ["61a756bce622b99844669aad783c250396b8722e"], "node": "415ee3b079083fce908d464c1ca01f9fbd6b3698", "parents": ["a4d2d4bf5829ff7b9e4c7d184067eaee04e3efb4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 1f37cf15bb\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/1f37cf15bb7fe1b19f422021b28480921ba1fd83\n    Delete CopyOnWriteBuffer implicit constructor from c-array\n\n    Removing this constructor switches users to explicit constructors from\n    `span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e` and from `string_view` delegating type erasure to\n    these 2 view types.\n\n    Implicit constructors are generally disallowed. Additionally this\n    constructor conflicts with the constructor from string_view\n    - it provides a different result when a raw string literal is passed\n    because it counts an extra 0-terminator that absl::string_view\n    constructor doesn't.\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: Ie083d12b612a2b8055049d11697a4208983694ad\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508980\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48950}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/packet_buffer_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/copy_on_write_buffer.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/network/network_emulation_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/rtp_video_stream_receiver2_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "b15c82c0eb855f6b6048ce8a33e11f18de401527", "git_parents": ["2312aa31f67f903a12f16272c7f8e12eb0d1a0ef"], "node": "35d16480e6928ed8ec729ecbcaf7a5051f7da896", "parents": ["415ee3b079083fce908d464c1ca01f9fbd6b3698"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from a306485b7f\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/a306485b7fc0fe38dd2651420e383f92f196cd77\n    Remove deprecated CreatePeerConnectionFactory overload\n\n    Support for a worker thread that is distinct from the network thread is\n    being removed, and the CreatePeerConnectionFactory overload that accepts\n    a worker_thread argument was deprecated as part of that.\n\n    Remove the deprecated overload and fold the shared implementation back\n    into the remaining one.\n\n    Background: https://groups.google.com/g/discuss-webrtc/c/Fs_Hd5XNJh0\n    Bug: webrtc:558821261\n    Change-Id: Icbb8730cbcf0ba614329e7a6e0a004b620a4fdc7\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508545\n    Auto-Submit: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48951}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/create_peerconnection_factory.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/create_peerconnection_factory.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch"], "git_node": "0e02ffeba1e11aaf25b9a3d74629ebf3e5c62575", "git_parents": ["b15c82c0eb855f6b6048ce8a33e11f18de401527"], "node": "eeb2a5b9a0a0a9414d8b8796f919c888d15ef677", "parents": ["35d16480e6928ed8ec729ecbcaf7a5051f7da896"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 454ceb5e24\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/454ceb5e242aaae5ace6b3fdf217290aaea88e4b\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-10-19T04:05:40).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I772a766e7a55780d9d7801b88ae28ead4643b40f\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509860\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48952}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "ba97615749b88655f7d9fab44929dbbe12b1e916", "git_parents": ["0e02ffeba1e11aaf25b9a3d74629ebf3e5c62575"], "node": "c26f0468131375de9a17fdc2dcf3426bff5c6bc0", "parents": ["eeb2a5b9a0a0a9414d8b8796f919c888d15ef677"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from d2b0fd5236\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/d2b0fd523642260d445c236bf87c65718f6c72d9\n    Let ScopedOperationsBatcher tasks return an error and a finalizer\n\n    Replace RTCErrorOr\u003cFinalizerTask\u003e with BatchTaskResult as the return\n    type of BatchTaskWithFinalizer. A returned finalizer now also runs when\n    the task returns an error. No behavior change for existing tasks.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42222804\n    Change-Id: I0fb29a44d0168ea33a73214c1681917b250db6a5\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509660\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48953}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_transceiver.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/scoped_operations_batcher.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/scoped_operations_batcher.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/scoped_operations_batcher_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "ab5df35724c86940fccfaff5d58b9f008be47688", "git_parents": ["ba97615749b88655f7d9fab44929dbbe12b1e916"], "node": "bda75ff053bc8929c5168b87c286ea401b500318", "parents": ["c26f0468131375de9a17fdc2dcf3426bff5c6bc0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from f1503264a3\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/f1503264a31932a9301e33aaf4e610e817e3df49\n    Return the transport rollback error from the batch task\n\n    A batch task's finalizer now also runs when the task returns an error,\n    so MakeRollbackTask() no longer needs an RTCError out-parameter.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42222804\n    Change-Id: I2db35220a1e6a43fdd87b936af6098647d1fc236\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509663\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48954}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_offer_answer.cc"], "git_node": "959ffae512abc8a3e8317e925ed22f80e141b71a", "git_parents": ["ab5df35724c86940fccfaff5d58b9f008be47688"], "node": "1960ad85181957616b78b855236cac35e7b01f0b", "parents": ["bda75ff053bc8929c5168b87c286ea401b500318"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 16de0369cb\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/16de0369cbde30bea3225f7804d5d039d075b06c\n    Remove remote ICE candidates without blocking\n\n    PeerConnection::RemoveIceCandidate() made a blocking call to the network\n    thread and ignored the result. The removal is now posted, as adding\n    candidates already is, so additions and removals still run in order.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42222804\n    Change-Id: I8ee44caa6efa281a1f5bb28087eeeaf2c8d338f1\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508146\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48955}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_controller_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_offer_answer.cc"], "git_node": "fd9589d764bc363c0572ba9218b80edbf35836c8", "git_parents": ["959ffae512abc8a3e8317e925ed22f80e141b71a"], "node": "5447d57c4c33e1c7d15b786b3c0bc6e0fdc85d95", "parents": ["1960ad85181957616b78b855236cac35e7b01f0b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 652992d375\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/652992d375e1ce1d1bcc568d4d45482e32aff257\n    Roll chromium_revision d7aeebe574..4cdeb6cfef (1704344:1710075)\n\n    Change log: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+log/d7aeebe574..4cdeb6cfef\n    Full diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/d7aeebe574..4cdeb6cfef\n\n    Changed dependencies\n    * fuchsia_version: version:33.20260922.5.1..version:33.20260927.4.1\n    * siso_version: git_revision:22353054fea20f637c8fa302a90daf9e2cc10497..git_revision:c574896b272b40aac6e44c228ee0b471ea7e3d7d\n    * src/build: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/build/+log/8f4d213ca2..78170c8ee4\n    * src/buildtools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/buildtools/+log/61df5d8b18..59a37766f1\n    * src/buildtools/linux64: git_revision:56c22442ee369ddc6f44c2ff5e0664d47a3c6b0e..git_revision:9fe99e262126467c4cb2f44cf941767d29fb33d8\n    * src/buildtools/mac: git_revision:56c22442ee369