guIcmwK2BrNjsMYC..P7Pq70iaBKGCBVqKGS1XPUFyG7yWFSBWVy7yOBsghLcC\n    * src/third_party/requests/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/kennethreitz/requests.git/+log/c7e0fc087c..c2b307dbef\n    * src/third_party/rust-toolchain: Linux_x64/rust-toolchain-1edd55dcfcd573872c727fa3e086369a71661ee0-2-llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b.tar.xz,Mac/rust-toolchain-1edd55dcfcd573872c727fa3e086369a71661ee0-2-llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b.tar.xz,Mac_arm64/rust-toolchain-1edd55dcfcd573872c727fa3e086369a71661ee0-2-llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b.tar.xz,Win/rust-toolchain-1edd55dcfcd573872c727fa3e086369a71661ee0-2-llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b.tar.xz..Linux_x64/rust-toolchain-1edd55dcfcd573872c727fa3e086369a71661ee0-1120-llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b.tar.xz,Mac/rust-toolchain-1edd55dcfcd573872c727fa3e086369a71661ee0-1120-llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b.tar.xz,Mac_arm64/rust-toolchain-1edd55dcfcd573872c727fa3e086369a71661ee0-1120-llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b.tar.xz,Win/rust-toolchain-1edd55dcfcd573872c727fa3e086369a71661ee0-1120-llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b.tar.xz\n    * src/third_party/siso/cipd: git_revision:22353054fea20f637c8fa302a90daf9e2cc10497..git_revision:c574896b272b40aac6e44c228ee0b471ea7e3d7d\n    * src/third_party/tflite/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow.git/+log/9edd58f895..385ce38a2a\n    * src/third_party/turbine/cipd: rqbGMhci4trzUCXgMBzoRMpTKADs_F5sWUKJXxsu6BYC..lLSvuXDQIBq-skHpEV38DETcvq3t2lL9rc2VpxEj-h4C\n    * src/third_party/xnnpack/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/google/XNNPACK.git/+log/b6d54fe945..e1881fc977\n    * src/tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/tools/+log/0d9c7e8905..2541180093\n    DEPS diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/d7aeebe574..4cdeb6cfef/DEPS\n\n    BUG=None\n\n    Change-Id: Ifefaa83fda4e6dbe2244eba103158db55235ba5a\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509460\n    Reviewed-by: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48956}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "1e95d7471e5ad620c92ffc1b6f22eaaa05f67bcc", "git_parents": ["fd9589d764bc363c0572ba9218b80edbf35836c8"], "node": "5a90934ede1ba6843e40164461dbd777a7aa5e0d", "parents": ["5447d57c4c33e1c7d15b786b3c0bc6e0fdc85d95"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 60765deeff\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/60765deeff7d252ef8ae27f70732b58119b747d7\n    Remove stale RTX SSRC mapping when overwriting stream\n\n    If the `rtx_ssrc` changes for the same `ssrc`, we should remove the old\n    demuxing mapping.\n\n    Bug: b/423646186\n    Change-Id: I73dcf82eaf6de79b56a104ca03bc3ad5ed6de0d1\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509880\n    Reviewed-by: \u00c5sa Persson \u003casapersson@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48957}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/timing/simulator/rtc_event_log_driver.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/timing/simulator/rtc_event_log_driver_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "68b5fc22c70c1a22e56259d7e297cfd9d6e2ff8f", "git_parents": ["1e95d7471e5ad620c92ffc1b6f22eaaa05f67bcc"], "node": "cdd28cb643aac8f987f900d33787516c7b852aaf", "parents": ["5a90934ede1ba6843e40164461dbd777a7aa5e0d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 9158489bba\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/9158489bbaa70c60636c690c2bacaf6b129bec99\n    Disable dynamic encoder speed in video codec tests by default\n\n    EncoderSpeedController adjusts encoder speed based on wall-clock encode\n    time, which introduces run-to-run metric variance in video codec tests.\n    Set WebRTC-EncoderSpeed/dynamic_speed:false/ in video_codec_tests.cc.\n\n    Bug: b/467294375\n    Change-Id: If895a7801433f3400b389bb5d35d6f6d53288333\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509280\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48958}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/test/video_codec_test.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0092.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0140.patch"], "git_node": "a996fe245fe9cb20403539241d7718f6b4d99524", "git_parents": ["68b5fc22c70c1a22e56259d7e297cfd9d6e2ff8f"], "node": "cc0fce5e88bf72dfb2e9ce0c6e395791e760f4e6", "parents": ["cdd28cb643aac8f987f900d33787516c7b852aaf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 129c39fa34\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/129c39fa34a29dbcb005cbd0876c2bbdbd990732\n    Remove unused field trial registrations\n\n    Remove 10 field trials from ACTIVE_FIELD_TRIALS and\n    POLICY_EXEMPT_FIELD_TRIALS that are no longer read anywhere in WebRTC\n    production code:\n    - WebRTC-Aec3EchoSaturationDetectionKillSwitch\n    - WebRTC-Aec3HighPassFilterEchoReference\n    - WebRTC-Audio-GainController2\n    - WebRTC-Audio-NetEqDecisionLogicConfig\n    - WebRTC-Audio-NetEqNackTrackerConfig\n    - WebRTC-FakeNetworkReceiveConfig\n    - WebRTC-FakeNetworkSendConfig\n    - WebRTC-ForceDtls13\n    - WebRTC-H264HighProfile\n    - WebRTC-TransientSuppressorForcedOff\n\n    Also remove leftover test variants for WebRTC-ForceDtls13 and the unused\n    Objective-C kRTCFieldTrialH264HighProfileKey constant.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42232605, webrtc:383141571, webrtc:42221578, webrtc:42222401, webrtc:42223518, webrtc:42220211, webrtc:42224493, webrtc:41481030, webrtc:40172597\n    Change-Id: I3feb21b08bc9b4898147abb64f31efe7e26558b9\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509441\n    Reviewed-by: Peter Hanspers \u003cpeterhanspers@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48959}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/experiments/field_trials.py", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/data_channel_integrationtest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_callsetup_perf_tests.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/sdk/objc/api/peerconnection/RTCFieldTrials.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/sdk/objc/api/peerconnection/RTCFieldTrials.mm"], "git_node": "a9968f4997dc80b378bc4b3874fdd002ea7172a7", "git_parents": ["a996fe245fe9cb20403539241d7718f6b4d99524"], "node": "d6ff7646b66ab95a8dff68bedb2b3ef397a6d70f", "parents": ["cc0fce5e88bf72dfb2e9ce0c6e395791e760f4e6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from d86ac8ab5e\n\nWe already cherry-picked this when we vendored 69d262980d.\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/d86ac8ab5e04c7efb8f474985e1bec1f82443a34\n    Fail EncodeFec when packets are passed radically out of order\n\n    Bug: chromium:570927027\n    Change-Id: I9fd8d548e9e7935a4862dc95cb65548eba3b4c5f\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509462\n    Reviewed-by: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48960}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/d86ac8ab5e.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0002.patch"], "git_node": "fb7eb6719a332e8d5f7468204c6798669235ffc1", "git_parents": ["a9968f4997dc80b378bc4b3874fdd002ea7172a7"], "node": "eb7161f2a089fd5fad9ace33d54469b0d9582f8a", "parents": ["d6ff7646b66ab95a8dff68bedb2b3ef397a6d70f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from e8e1b9c43b\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/e8e1b9c43b66a4a406f15687f869e1fc05ea93d6\n    Cache id in SctpDataChannel::CachedState and bypass proxy for id()\n\n    Calling DataChannelInterface::id() on the signaling thread while inside\n    an ObserverAdapter callback previously executed a synchronous\n    BlockingCall to the network thread via DataChannelProxy.\n\n    - Bypass DataChannelProxy for id() just like state() and error().\n    - Include id in SctpDataChannel::CachedState so signaling thread\n      observer callbacks can query id() without blocking on the network\n      thread.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:510487699\n    Change-Id: Ie7805ccf0422eafdb76daaf7f999360e26e396e2\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508967\n    Reviewed-by: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48961}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0118.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sctp_data_channel.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sctp_data_channel_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "124cca84b76ed9a0074242877a33fd343458bb8a", "git_parents": ["fb7eb6719a332e8d5f7468204c6798669235ffc1"], "node": "160937cc91b4195b29b714dcf34f4d2802de24bf", "parents": ["eb7161f2a089fd5fad9ace33d54469b0d9582f8a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 818b01e753\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/818b01e753bc124bb33bdd5df42ecb94c3bf181a\n    Increase Siso remote_jobs to 500 on chromium_try_builder\n\n    Chromium trybots (such as webrtc_linux_chromium,\n    linux_chromium_compile_dbg, and android_chromium_compile) execute\n    ~35,000-57,000 remote compilation steps on 8-core VMs, where Siso\n    defaults to remoteexec/200 and spends over 5 minutes per build waiting\n    on the local remoteexec semaphore. Set jobs = 500 on\n    chromium_try_builder to match the CI Chromium builders.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: I61033491ee21790394ac42ba0525a631ead711a7\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509901\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48962}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/config/builders.star", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/config/generated/luci/cr-buildbucket.cfg"], "git_node": "df097471df6c9d2287b00ae0e31c06721b1a5dfd", "git_parents": ["124cca84b76ed9a0074242877a33fd343458bb8a"], "node": "049f9ffde94d28cb92bbcf135a7b0b8a3d10f727", "parents": ["160937cc91b4195b29b714dcf34f4d2802de24bf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 2b4123c336\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/2b4123c33675ca329c5fad7ef7144aebba265674\n    Export Port::Callbacks\n\n    RTC_EXPORT on Port does not apply to nested classes on Windows, so the\n    out-of-line special members of Port::Callbacks were not exported from\n    the WebRTC DLL. This broke linking blink_platform_unittests in\n    Chromium's Windows component builds and blocks the WebRTC roll.\n\n    Using no-try for low risk CL to unlock the chromium roll.\n\n    No-try: true\n    Bug: webrtc:42224914\n    Change-Id: Ibbe6c59d278d3008d941c7f9b3dde3f732a69759\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509960\n    Auto-Submit: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48963}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/port.h"], "git_node": "3f3fe850c3ecd870d5100c7f8dcf36ac48d58173", "git_parents": ["df097471df6c9d2287b00ae0e31c06721b1a5dfd"], "node": "18661e2373ed5cfd91340a979844f55804fe88d6", "parents": ["049f9ffde94d28cb92bbcf135a7b0b8a3d10f727"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 716e0f36f7\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/716e0f36f7960136222f56b050a74006010d2f94\n    Remove 4 redundant compile-only builders from CQ\n\n    Remove android_compile_arm_dbg, ios_compile_arm64_dbg,\n    win_compile_x64_clang_dbg, and win_compile_x64_clang_rel from default CQ\n    verification (cq = None). Each of these compile-only trybots builds the\n    exact same MB config and 'all' target as a test trybot already in CQ\n    (android_arm_dbg, ios_dbg_simulator, win_x64_clang_dbg, and\n    win_x64_clang_rel respectively), duplicating VM and RBE capacity on\n    every CQ run.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: Ibe60627186436446da7c58e1fa809c784d5ea706\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509443\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48964}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/config/builders.star", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/config/generated/luci/commit-queue.cfg"], "git_node": "655662d69e3da18bd284adf8d98f5e1a63b7c62f", "git_parents": ["3f3fe850c3ecd870d5100c7f8dcf36ac48d58173"], "node": "c4eddd0f7d1aaf68e73722eef69c6204c8a6c14e", "parents": ["18661e2373ed5cfd91340a979844f55804fe88d6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 17508bb874\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/17508bb874d1e34c7bd5c6da2b219d2558a425cf\n    Add a skill to fix the Chromium roll into WebRTC\n\n    Change-Id: I6c3c9c88811d94f695f606e63a40523a6dbafc29\n    Bug: None\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509881\n    Reviewed-by: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48965}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/agents/skills/chromium-roll/SKILL.md", "third_party/libwebrtc/agents/skills/chromium-roll/scripts/manual_roll.py", "third_party/libwebrtc/agents/skills/chromium-roll/scripts/manual_roll_test.py"], "git_node": "7cc0d4a2923ba7828eca8620d3bcf42d029aecec", "git_parents": ["655662d69e3da18bd284adf8d98f5e1a63b7c62f"], "node": "eb8c2b1b5ba71e818d5cdffe327e2a1eb14dac6c", "parents": ["c4eddd0f7d1aaf68e73722eef69c6204c8a6c14e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from f00ee0bdfc\n\n(skip-generation)\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/f00ee0bdfc9f41b8ead8be131e6d1a8e78be33f7\n    Use hermetic Python interpreter in .gn for Siso remote rules\n\n    Chromium switched build/config/siso/platform.star to match commands\n    starting with //third_party/cpython3/host/bin/python3 in\n    https://crrev.com/c/8160801. Update .gn's script_executable to match so\n    Siso remote execution rules (such as clang-coverage/cxx, android/*,\n    nasm, proto, and rust) match again instead of falling back to local\n    execution.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: I8b01693039f7b06600030d202bcb1e6cfac21959\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509900\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48966}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0088.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0092.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0106.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0139.patch"], "git_node": "38f010857ae3f70b0dfd7d15927193299c0ba5de", "git_parents": ["7cc0d4a2923ba7828eca8620d3bcf42d029aecec"], "node": "9b1eefef7f2e667d402cac68662d13f9fb122dfe", "parents": ["eb8c2b1b5ba71e818d5cdffe327e2a1eb14dac6c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - (fix-f00ee0bdfc) Revert f00ee0bdfc, which introduced a dependency on an in-tree python executable.\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0150.patch"], "git_node": "09ca97ce4b083b74540fa46b0e904e7606d47619", "git_parents": ["38f010857ae3f70b0dfd7d15927193299c0ba5de"], "node": "b7ba8bee3ea85086cc8e81bde6ba13cffe02ae1f", "parents": ["9b1eefef7f2e667d402cac68662d13f9fb122dfe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from e48a1c8d47\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/e48a1c8d47d982bf15ce643327b9e13c238f2a5f\n    Init quality convergence after InitEncode.\n\n    In LibvpxVp8Encoder [1] and LibvpxVp9Encoder [2], min_qp is\n    content-specific (set only for screensharing) and is therefore only\n    known after InitEncode(), unlike LibaomAv1Encoder where min_qp is static\n    and always populated [3]. Additionally, SimulcastEncoderAdapter did not\n    propagate min_qp across sub-encoders in multi-stream simulcast mode [4].\n\n    Move QualityConvergenceController::Initialize() after\n    encoder_-\u003eInitEncode() in VideoStreamEncoder::ReconfigureEncoder() and\n    report min_qp in SimulcastEncoderAdapter::GetEncoderInfo() when all\n    sub-encoders report the same value.\n\n    [1] https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/webrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/vp8/libvpx_vp8_encoder.cc;l=1428-1430\n    [2] https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/webrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/vp9/libvpx_vp9_encoder.cc;l=1941-1943\n    [3] https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/webrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/libaom_av1_encoder.cc;l=1278\n    [4] https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/webrtc/media/engine/simulcast_encoder_adapter.cc;l=1184-1254\n\n    Bug: chromium:328598314\n    Change-Id: Idb4957b7b19cfe492cb13aadf041f3a399adf5e1\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509800\n    Reviewed-by: Johannes Kron \u003ckron@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48967}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/simulcast_encoder_adapter.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/simulcast_encoder_adapter_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0067.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0101.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0130.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "56159014cb6179992ffd39f61c5b544604466b1f", "git_parents": ["09ca97ce4b083b74540fa46b0e904e7606d47619"], "node": "cb39ff9baf826b07c91f5f15ea7ebad2fc252a30", "parents": ["b7ba8bee3ea85086cc8e81bde6ba13cffe02ae1f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from b1cf37fb21\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/b1cf37fb21dfea3663c0464403b6108ba5bb5183\n    Only build sdk/android:libwebrtc once in build_aar.py\n\n    CollectCommon() only packages classes.jar\n    (lib.java/sdk/android/libwebrtc.jar, built by sdk/android:libwebrtc)\n    from the first architecture in archs, while Collect() only packages\n    libjingle_peerconnection_so.so from each architecture. Avoid building\n    sdk/android:libwebrtc for subsequent architectures in BuildAar() so ~300\n    Java/Turbine/ijar/JNI targets are not compiled 3 redundant times.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: Ic8029a36e1971fb2c0ea26e5a3e477817eb4a468\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509920\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48968}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/tools_webrtc/android/build_aar.py"], "git_node": "bda0172a2a4764f8508226e82bd08ae623f5a1fc", "git_parents": ["56159014cb6179992ffd39f61c5b544604466b1f"], "node": "ef2f9035faf45feb123adfb6af522f8ccd6d0ba7", "parents": ["cb39ff9baf826b07c91f5f15ea7ebad2fc252a30"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 9be5c73ad9\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/9be5c73ad9cd1eb2df04d6f931b4cb1e0c6e5395\n    Spanify CompareHeaderExtensions test helper\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42225170, webrtc:42226010\n    Change-Id: I279a2cdead736048617b557ef0ae1a69dbb3c93c\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509500\n    Reviewed-by: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48969}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/fake_rtp.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/fake_rtp.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/dtls_srtp_transport_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/srtp_transport_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "f61dd818c8ed1d3a263a5f6be2e71b86a2d586a5", "git_parents": ["bda0172a2a4764f8508226e82bd08ae623f5a1fc"], "node": "913bff02ea1d1d8fce72f7a5f1393182163c66b7", "parents": ["ef2f9035faf45feb123adfb6af522f8ccd6d0ba7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 82dd1ebf2e\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/82dd1ebf2efeeb8d5943c080a061fa100a06f5de\n    Update quality convergence only on base temporal layer frames.\n\n    When temporal layering is used, VideoStreamEncoder::OnEncodedImage()\n    passes the QP of every encoded frame (T0, T1, T2) to\n    QualityConvergenceController::AddSampleAndCheckTargetQuality() and\n    FrameCadenceAdapterInterface::UpdateLayerQualityConvergence() [1].\n    Non-reference T\u003e0 frames do not update the T0 reference buffer, so a T\u003e0\n    frame reaching static_qp_threshold [2] prematurely halts ZeroHertz\n    convergence repeats before the T0 reference buffer converges, and\n    interleaving T0 and T\u003e0 QPs skews the 12-sample dynamic QP window [3].\n\n    Gate quality convergence updates in VideoStreamEncoder::OnEncodedImage()\n    on TemporalIndex().value_or(0) == 0. Guard this by the\n    enabled-by-default WebRTC-QCM-IgnoreEnhancementTemporalLayers\n    kill-switch.\n\n    [1]\n    https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/webrtc/video/video_stream_encoder.cc;l=2317-2325\n    [2]\n    https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/webrtc/video/quality_convergence_monitor.cc;l=146-150\n    [3]\n    https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/webrtc/video/quality_convergence_monitor.cc;l=166-193\n\n    Bug: chromium:328598314\n    Change-Id: I383b5e2aa69463513e474861151788681e7a6ff5\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509742\n    Reviewed-by: Johannes Kron \u003ckron@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48970}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/experiments/field_trials.py", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0067.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0101.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0130.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "5985c0c9943195b35800f4c0be16db600e740129", "git_parents": ["f61dd818c8ed1d3a263a5f6be2e71b86a2d586a5"], "node": "99f7b2de206813874e1899c6b82ea0cc86b5734c", "parents": ["913bff02ea1d1d8fce72f7a5f1393182163c66b7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 01a4fa5f6f\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/01a4fa5f6f6d121beda52632d9d27ca6d06ec148\n    Keep RtpSender parameter cache in sync with the media channel\n\n    - SetParametersAsync() completion: Only populate the cache if no other\n      operation updated or invalidated it in the meantime (generation\n      counter).\n    - RtpTransceiver::SetChannelContent(): Update the senders' cache also\n      when applying the content fails.\n    - SetParametersInternalWithAllLayers(): Update the cache also when the\n      media channel rejects the parameters.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42222804\n    Change-Id: I4b4e45ca9f89abcfb4af6e239ad1170437370e71\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509661\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48971}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender_receiver_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_transceiver.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_transceiver_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "6e2ac981822e6e7d1800b3c989878dab6852d8b1", "git_parents": ["5985c0c9943195b35800f4c0be16db600e740129"], "node": "e63b33ad596ee801aeff45e1cf38fd426712bd0b", "parents": ["99f7b2de206813874e1899c6b82ea0cc86b5734c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from fa060dcb12\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/fa060dcb1222cc67e0469da3c2fb94dbc80513dd\n    Add StringBuilder::Reserve()\n\n    Allows pre-allocating the buffer when the final size can be estimated,\n    to avoid repeated reallocations while appending. RTC_LOG will use it.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: I80c1892a74c18b19d7fa16a80ab93b2fdc6fdffd\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509820\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48972}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/strings/string_builder.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/strings/string_builder_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "1d7c82feae4041054e037295ae33cc92f5cc7a01", "git_parents": ["6e2ac981822e6e7d1800b3c989878dab6852d8b1"], "node": "d277b59c8fbb5fa9029a0f6e68d093e5d3be47c0", "parents": ["e63b33ad596ee801aeff45e1cf38fd426712bd0b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 0df45ee396\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/0df45ee396bb2fa47955af3001eb34203ed50759\n    Add Unified Plan SDP performance benchmarks\n\n    Add BM_SdpDeserializeSmallUnifiedPlan, BM_SdpSerializeSmallUnifiedPlan\n    (3 media sections: 1 audio, 1 video, 1 data channel),\n    BM_SdpDeserializeLargeUnifiedPlan, and BM_SdpSerializeLargeUnifiedPlan\n    (50 media sections: 25 audio and 25 video with simulcast, RIDs, codecs,\n    header extensions, and candidates) using Google Benchmark in\n    api:webrtc_sdp_benchmark (linked into //:benchmarks).\n\n    Baseline metrics (Release with dcheck_always_on=false, 5-run median):\n    - BM_SdpDeserializeSmallUnifiedPlan: 85.9 us\n    - BM_SdpSerializeSmallUnifiedPlan: 20.8 us\n    - BM_SdpDeserializeLargeUnifiedPlan: 2167 us\n    - BM_SdpSerializeLargeUnifiedPlan: 518 us\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: I04ff95763997d8f71d31932e7ae8aabc4537dcdc\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509720\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48973}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/webrtc_sdp_benchmark.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0034.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0044.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0054.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0081.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0085.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0097.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0099.patch"], "git_node": "6d26eeefa3d706a8fd66d5cd1279e9261bd68656", "git_parents": ["1d7c82feae4041054e037295ae33cc92f5cc7a01"], "node": "70936be95e1ecb220b26f8f25457fa45b9625f18", "parents": ["d277b59c8fbb5fa9029a0f6e68d093e5d3be47c0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from d8b3c75a5b\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/d8b3c75a5be1286af11f5873c18aa4c56fd78736\n    Add a benchmark for RTC_LOG\n\n    Measures RTC_LOG with one sink that receives the default log line, for\n    literals and numbers, mixed string types and SDPs of different sizes. It\n    is the baseline for reducing the heap allocations in RTC_LOG.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: If06c9caf549f762dd0e24e0bbb08b4dc9ab1420c\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509961\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48974}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0034.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0044.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0052.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0054.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0081.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0083.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0085.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0086.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0097.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0099.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/logging_benchmark.cc"], "git_node": "4024a2aabd43f5f10a1f3df0eff05822d5eceb6d", "git_parents": ["6d26eeefa3d706a8fd66d5cd1279e9261bd68656"], "node": "971b3bc456118cfa8c56edfae3b6710cb7877173", "parents": ["70936be95e1ecb220b26f8f25457fa45b9625f18"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 1de8adc742\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/1de8adc742fba191c589aa4e2fa44f8e50da5b23\n    Fix problem that surface when rtc_cc_test is used as a test binary.\n\n    On CQ/CI bots, the rtc_cc_test targets are used as cc libraries. The actual test binary is the rtc_test_suite target. Some problem surface when trying to directly run rtc_cc_test targets on bots.\n\n    * Fix missing data in test target.\n    * Remove unused multi_stream_tests dependency in transport_feedback_tests.\n    * scenario_unittest_resources_bundle_data is renamed to scenario_unittest_bundle_data to avoid collision with the generated internal ios targets for bundle that has the same name.\n    * Widen the visibility lists naming rtc_cc_test targets. On Android, iOS\n      and Fuchsia, test() compiles the test sources in an internal target\n      (e.g. \u003cname\u003e__library on Android and \u003cname\u003e__exec on Fuchsia), so a\n      visibility entry naming a test target only works while rtc_cc_test\n      defines a library with that name.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:498394143\n    Change-Id: I059ec057f3f9f0289eb8168e212b444af72deeda\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510020\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48975}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/logging/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/agc2/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0052.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0083.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0085.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0086.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0091.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0092.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0099.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0140.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/memory/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/synchronization/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/scenario/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/BUILD.gn"], "git_node": "169038745cb4f81d2e8d0994ccfc8da31357db69", "git_parents": ["4024a2aabd43f5f10a1f3df0eff05822d5eceb6d"], "node": "bc152d5febbb6f754ba11b95fd823c45a1616c33", "parents": ["971b3bc456118cfa8c56edfae3b6710cb7877173"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 29ecea7e21\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/29ecea7e21dd233a7c9d1a822c3ea884d0cacbec\n    Remove deprecated Port setters and make Port state const\n\n    Now that downstream callers have migrated to the rvalue\n    RelayPortFactoryInterface::Create overloads and constructor-time\n    Port::Callbacks:\n\n    - Remove legacy const-ref RelayPortFactoryInterface::Create overloads\n      and make Port::Callbacks a move-only aggregate.\n    - Pass component, generation, and send_retransmit_count_attribute via\n      Port::PortParametersRef and CreateRelayPortArgs instead of post-\n      construction setters.\n    - Remove Port::set_component, Port::set_generation,\n      Port::set_send_retransmit_count_attribute,\n      SubscribeCandidateReadyCallback, SubscribeCandidateError,\n      SubscribePortComplete, SubscribePortError, and\n      TurnPort::SetTurnLoggingId.\n    - Replace Port's single-subscriber CallbackLists with absl::AnyInvocable\n      members and make immutable members const across Port, UDPPort,\n      TurnPort, TCPPort, BasicPortAllocator, BasicPortAllocatorSession,\n      AllocationSequence, and FakePortAllocatorSession.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42224914, webrtc:42222117\n    Change-Id: I1949215efeedaa4261a2cf6f66f20639d24924c4\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509620\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jonas Oreland \u003cjonaso@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48976}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/port.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/port.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/port_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/port_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/stun_port.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/stun_port.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/tcp_port.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/turn_port.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/turn_port.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/turn_port_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/client/basic_port_allocator.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/client/basic_port_allocator.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/client/relay_port_factory_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/client/turn_port_factory.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/client/turn_port_factory.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/test/fake_port_allocator.h"], "git_node": "9b83a2074e505dc0495d788f1c44151eac42a441", "git_parents": ["169038745cb4f81d2e8d0994ccfc8da31357db69"], "node": "3ccf1d70e1f191e1ff350f4748d693186b30cdf7", "parents": ["bc152d5febbb6f754ba11b95fd823c45a1616c33"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from c9ee253547\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/c9ee2535470f049507b2a2c6ebf91cb34b65ca46\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-10-20T04:12:04).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: Ic8c867ddbdbd1cbf907b71eb7974e0a0c440b184\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510140\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48977}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "3f48310d40c127d5ff19aead94b5edf299f6cadd", "git_parents": ["9b83a2074e505dc0495d788f1c44151eac42a441"], "node": "12771cea28ac564adc846def4e9aae614b950b1c", "parents": ["3ccf1d70e1f191e1ff350f4748d693186b30cdf7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 6153082ce4\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/6153082ce46ffa3412188198083d117578d7086b\n    Reland \"Allow combining AV1 SVC frames without dependency descriptor.\"\n\n    This is a reland of commit 52da778c185a17fe953ead983af213aa447e773e\n\n    The downstream test that caused the revert has been fixed.\n\n    Original change's description:\n    \u003e Allow combining AV1 SVC frames without dependency descriptor.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Although using scalability features with without Dependency Descriptors\n    \u003e isn't a supported use case (falls outside the RTP Profile for AV1), it\n    \u003e would help in some cases where the full stream is received (no sequence\n    \u003e number gaps) and frames are otherwise detectable as complete (e.g. using\n    \u003e the marker bit), to allow decoding SVC frames without knowing the actual\n    \u003e spatial index.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e When receiving AV1 SVC without a dependency descriptor, PacketBuffer\n    \u003e emits one RtpFrameObject per spatial layer and RtpSeqNumOnlyRefFinder\n    \u003e verifies sequence number continuity across the temporal unit.\n    \u003e RtpSeqNumOnlyRefFinder previously stamped SpatialIndex(0) onto every\n    \u003e subframe, causing CombineAndDeleteFrames to reject multi-layer temporal\n    \u003e units as having duplicate spatial indices.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Leave SpatialIndex unset (std::nullopt) in RtpSeqNumOnlyRefFinder and\n    \u003e only populate SpatialIndex and SpatialLayerFrameSize in\n    \u003e CombineAndDeleteFrames when spatial indices are present. Also replace\n    \u003e raw pointer arithmetic and memcpy in CombineAndDeleteFrames with\n    \u003e std::span and std::ranges::copy.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Bug: webrtc:560293075, chromium:569667447\n    \u003e Change-Id: I504fa458ebc1c6f902b39593de9680faa43f2d2a\n    \u003e Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508962\n    \u003e Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    \u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48922}\n\n    Bug: webrtc:560293075, chromium:569667447\n    Change-Id: I0dc437b7a3b710d8edb8923b191b870d8cab03da\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510061\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48978}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/experiments/field_trials.py", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/frame_helpers.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/frame_helpers_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/rtp_frame_reference_finder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/rtp_frame_reference_finder.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/rtp_frame_reference_finder_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/rtp_seq_num_only_ref_finder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/rtp_seq_num_only_ref_finder.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0030.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0035.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0037.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0041.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0056.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0057.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0058.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0059.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0092.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0138.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0140.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/unsafe_buffers_paths.txt", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/end_to_end_tests/codec_tests.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/rtp_video_stream_receiver2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_buffer_controller_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "c81c047bede60916aee7f7be6e2f87c51e4f10d1", "git_parents": ["3f48310d40c127d5ff19aead94b5edf299f6cadd"], "node": "983930f80d46f0162795649f95b11738f2dd8987", "parents": ["12771cea28ac564adc846def4e9aae614b950b1c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from d2070f4989\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/d2070f4989854f34548dfd7b6cfb0e778287a6a1\n    AbslStringify support for Connection, Port, Network, SocketAddress\n\n    Connection::ToString() is part of many ICE log lines, assembled from\n    strings from Port, Network and SocketAddress, which together took\n    multiple allocations per call.\n\n    - Add AbslStringify support to IPAddress (plus IPAddress::Sensitive)\n    - Add AbslStringify for Network.\n    - Reserve capacity in the ToString() methods of Network, Port,\n      Connection and Candidate.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: I2a8bea4d5cd1731996c816157c6d381ced9f0665\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509841\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48979}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/candidate.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0052.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0083.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0085.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0086.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0099.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/connection.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/port.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/port_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/ip_address.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/ip_address.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/ip_address_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/network.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/network.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/network_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/socket_address.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/socket_address.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/socket_address_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "55c61b6030bc2cc9a170dc07c8db28625c4ea5fe", "git_parents": ["c81c047bede60916aee7f7be6e2f87c51e4f10d1"], "node": "22355dddbb66cd3ef74cbc2afa03cfa35c2eb72e", "parents": ["983930f80d46f0162795649f95b11738f2dd8987"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 50b81200d1\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/50b81200d1c457bd39d598b0de9674aa386446da\n    Reduce send resolution in l4s_test to 320x180\n\n    Reduce the video send resolution to 320x180 to speed up test execution.\n\n    Bug: b/575637037\n    Change-Id: Ic640ab00b902ae6e2630df90b5cb07b61e47c31f\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510160\n    Reviewed-by: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48980}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/peer_scenario/bwe_integration_tests/l4s_test.cc"], "git_node": "435fb0dce4210fce5d99f03ec58fa64f1a7c39be", "git_parents": ["55c61b6030bc2cc9a170dc07c8db28625c4ea5fe"], "node": "b95d8507f2fa92ca9968693fca338beee19acb3a", "parents": ["22355dddbb66cd3ef74cbc2afa03cfa35c2eb72e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 1529ffb89a\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/1529ffb89af6619c382c034b69048e45d3269376\n    Remove RTCP handling from FakeMediaEngine as unused\n\n    Instead of spanifying it.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42225170\n    Change-Id: Iceb7a40953b903c85dec64534be04c0e03a72cca\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510044\n    Commit-Queue: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48981}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/fake_media_engine.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/fake_media_engine.h"], "git_node": "127df507bd210a794a13663dfea4cc06c79ed31e", "git_parents": ["435fb0dce4210fce5d99f03ec58fa64f1a7c39be"], "node": "932be55a7c91f25e9dc81a0bf083393de3e0f820", "parents": ["b95d8507f2fa92ca9968693fca338beee19acb3a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 0b6ee38516\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/0b6ee38516214b5268454bbf7cacc632aa3fb7e7\n    Use no_symbols on release_bot to match Chromium's trybot config\n\n    release bots inherited default_symbol_level from compiler.gni: 0 on\n    Linux/Fuchsia, 1 on Android, but 2 (full debug info) on Windows, Mac and\n    iOS; win_asan forced 2 via full_symbols. No bot needs full debug info,\n    it only slows down linking and isolate uploads.\n\n    Chromium's release_try_builder is release + dcheck_always_on +\n    no_symbols, the same shape as our release_bot, so add no_symbols to\n    release_bot and drop full_symbols from win_asan. All release bots now\n    build with symbol_level=0, sanitizer bots keep their default of 1\n    (needed by the src: patterns in tools_webrtc/sanitizers/*), and debug\n    bots stay at 1, matching Chromium's debug_builder.\n\n    pure_release_bot is left untouched so the sanitizer and Linux binary\n    size bots keep their defaults; its two non-sanitizer users on Windows\n    and Mac get no_symbols explicitly.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: I4edcaa585de0b9528c02e5298b3d014abd502d5f\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510060\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48982}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/tools_webrtc/mb/mb_config.pyl"], "git_node": "11671af830221f207e427af84b32b7a9c4b3ac36", "git_parents": ["127df507bd210a794a13663dfea4cc06c79ed31e"], "node": "14584fd70d9b82616ba75b919304b4feeb4315de", "parents": ["932be55a7c91f25e9dc81a0bf083393de3e0f820"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 48324e0261\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/48324e026146b084704d2595a04fbd83e01e0fc8\n    Update codecs in-place during SDP parsing\n\n    Previously, every codec attribute line (a=rtpmap, a=fmtp, a=rtcp-fb,\n    a=packetization, a=ptime, a=maxptime) copied the entire\n    std::vector\u003cCodec\u003e from MediaContentDescription, modified or replaced a\n    Codec copy, and wrote the vector back via set_codecs(). For a typical\n    video m= section with ~10 codecs and ~60 codec attribute lines, this\n    resulted in hundreds of unnecessary Codec deep-copies (each containing a\n    CodecParameterMap and FeedbackParams vector).\n\n    - Add mutable_codecs() to MediaContentDescription and mutate Codec\n      entries in-place via GetOrAddCodecWithPayloadType().\n    - Sort and backfill codecs in-place in ParseContentDescription() using a\n      stack-allocated preference lookup array instead of std::unordered_map.\n    - Iterate over media_desc-\u003ecodecs() by const reference in BuildRtpmap()\n      instead of copying each Codec by value.\n\n    Benchmark results (Release with dcheck_always_on=false, 5-run median):\n    - BM_SdpDeserializeSmallUnifiedPlan: 85.9 us -\u003e 50.9 us (-40.7%)\n    - BM_SdpSerializeSmallUnifiedPlan: 20.8 us -\u003e 19.7 us (-5.3%)\n    - BM_SdpDeserializeLargeUnifiedPlan: 2167 us -\u003e 1344 us (-38.0%)\n    - BM_SdpSerializeLargeUnifiedPlan: 518 us -\u003e 492 us (-5.0%)\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: I97480524b0a2abfe24820075ded7f9feadc56893\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509721\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48983}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/webrtc_sdp.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/session_description.h"], "git_node": "be3f36d7b397383654ba4c5a9d69b647746e1902", "git_parents": ["11671af830221f207e427af84b32b7a9c4b3ac36"], "node": "78e69f4977c8495b36adb907ccbf891f30131dd8", "parents": ["14584fd70d9b82616ba75b919304b4feeb4315de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 563d53c0b3\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/563d53c0b31ed91ef1e185ac9a55ae097d416bf3\n    Make rtc_cc_test target names match their test file\n\n    Each rtc_cc_test now has its test file named \u003ctarget_name\u003e.cc.\n\n    * When no other rtc_cc_test uses the file name, the target is renamed\n      to match the file (e.g. environment_unittests -\u003e environment_unittest,\n      speech_level_estimator_unittest_test -\u003e speech_level_estimator_unittest).\n    * Otherwise the file is renamed to match the target (e.g.\n      api/audio_codecs/opus/audio_decoder_opus_unittest.cc -\u003e\n      audio_decoder_opus_api_unittest.cc). rtc_cc_test names must be unique\n      in the whole tree because test() names some outputs after the target\n      name instead of output_name (e.g. bin/run_\u003ctarget\u003e_bin).\n\n    Renamed files keep their unsafe_buffers_paths.txt entries and have their\n    includes regrouped, since the tested header no longer matches the file\n    name.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:498394143\n    Change-Id: I938912f8c6329fe2004720dbbb45a7ea129a7d4a\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510180\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48984}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/audio/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/audio/audio_processing_api_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/audio/audio_processing_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/audio_codecs/opus/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/audio_codecs/opus/audio_decoder_opus_api_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/audio_codecs/opus/audio_decoder_opus_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/environment/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/numerics/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/peer_connection_interface_api_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/peer_connection_interface_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/task_queue/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/voip/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/voip/test/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/common_audio_ring_buffer_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/ring_buffer_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_video/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_video/libyuv/libyuv_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_video/libyuv/webrtc_libyuv_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/aec_dump/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/agc2/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/agc2/rnn_vad/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/agc2/rnn_vad/rnn_vector_math_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_processing/agc2/rnn_vad/vector_math_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/pcc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/pcc/bitrate_controller_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/pcc/pcc_bitrate_controller_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/test/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/decoder_database_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/histogram_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/packet_buffer_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/video_decoder_database_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/video_histogram_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/video_packet_buffer_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0034.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0044.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0052.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0054.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0081.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0083.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0085.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0086.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0091.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0092.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0097.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0099.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0140.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0141.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/dtls/dtls_transport_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/dtls/p2p_dtls_transport_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/system/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/task_utils/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/units/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_tools/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_tools/network_tester/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/sdk/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/network/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/unsafe_buffers_paths.txt", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/evaluation/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/evaluation/corruption_qp_parser_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/evaluation/corruption_utils_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/evaluation/qp_parser_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/evaluation/utils_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "b4f36dce0300914a8b7977b0f0b0e08b1a2d886c", "git_parents": ["be3f36d7b397383654ba4c5a9d69b647746e1902"], "node": "f3171f3e6e304af291ae15e4ba13761551db6fe6", "parents": ["78e69f4977c8495b36adb907ccbf891f30131dd8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from f8e10f94f6\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/f8e10f94f6b69e9afe5ae56cb4ed7335aa457513\n    Cleanup and spanify RtpSendChannelHelper in FakeMediaEngine\n\n    Spanify function sending RTP packets.\n\n    Remove functions for watching received RTP packets - `rtp_packets_` is\n    never populated by the test helper, so validating it is empty doesn't\n    validate any production logic.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42225170\n    Change-Id: I5b1662485e3976898f2314da7970cbcbb98c0dff\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510182\n    Reviewed-by: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48985}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/fake_media_engine.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/channel_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "ced4d30b871fe74c71f1486a150c218af3c5133d", "git_parents": ["b4f36dce0300914a8b7977b0f0b0e08b1a2d886c"], "node": "55056d8ce04b7af2014b85e290a2412e7f11156f", "parents": ["f3171f3e6e304af291ae15e4ba13761551db6fe6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 63a0557ee5\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/63a0557ee526b8b3c6e83b5261d834aeee951679\n    Keep unsafe_buffers_paths.txt sorted\n\n    Also remove allocation_counter rtc_cc_test because it does not test any WebRTC related code anymore (see comments).\n\n    This is a follow up to address comments from\n    https://webrtc-review.git.corp.google.com/c/src/+/510180\n\n    Change-Id: I332edfb4e04db6320b9a166ce03edd3de800a4d5\n    Bug: webrtc:498394143\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510183\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48986}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/allocation_counter.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/allocation_counter.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0034.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/unsafe_buffers_paths.txt"], "git_node": "57eb86bbfaba46265a44899e0c5e8480ff5c4ffa", "git_parents": ["ced4d30b871fe74c71f1486a150c218af3c5133d"], "node": "e60558772c098799bf49ab370d8b4c0cb3561cea", "parents": ["55056d8ce04b7af2014b85e290a2412e7f11156f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 9d738557a2\n\nWe already cherry-picked this when we vendored 95554e4a0c.\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/9d738557a2492104bcea32a183a7106aa2fbd547\n    ApplyEncoderSwitch() must not modify negotiated codecs list.\n\n    Modifying the negotiated list was an easy way to keep track of which\n    codecs remain that have not been attempted yet. Unfortunately, this\n    causes setParameters() to fail when the application is asking to\n    reconfigure the same codec again (which is perfectly valid to try since\n    it is still negotiated). The app should be allowed to try again and a\n    simple get+setParameters() that doesn't change anything should never\n    fail.\n\n    The fix is to introduce `available_negotiated_codecs_`, which is\n    simply a copy of `negotiated_codecs_` that ApplyEncoderSwitch() is\n    able to modify.\n\n    Bug: chromium:575782118, b/486823390\n    Change-Id: I437d7ebee4ae7bda0d0619e601de5ac0bc78ff9e\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510220\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Guido Urdaneta \u003cguidou@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48987}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/9d738557a2.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0001.patch"], "git_node": "7cfd510ae3faee55d213014f32aafe9f56cd7292", "git_parents": ["57eb86bbfaba46265a44899e0c5e8480ff5c4ffa"], "node": "541c03afbbb7002cec6e5d2d029816c8b17539a9", "parents": ["e60558772c098799bf49ab370d8b4c0cb3561cea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 0fdde698c5\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/0fdde698c5c6e22af917de153cd94a3a0a270e85\n    Roll chromium_revision 4cdeb6cfef..1cb7357a22 (1710075:1721831)\n\n    Change log: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+log/4cdeb6cfef..1cb7357a22\n    Full diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/4cdeb6cfef..1cb7357a22\n\n    Changed dependencies\n    * fuchsia_version: version:33.20260927.4.1..version:33.20261003.1.1\n    * siso_version: git_revision:c574896b272b40aac6e44c228ee0b471ea7e3d7d..git_revision:7ab4814901b3c7afc2dddf2ed1a6ff238a0d85c5\n    * src/build: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/build/+log/78170c8ee4..16c326db38\n    * src/buildtools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/buildtools/+log/59a37766f1..54989aa948\n    * src/buildtools/linux64: git_revision:9fe99e262126467c4cb2f44cf941767d29fb33d8..git_revision:f90c3d9df882a9da4a66457f47dd3d99b3df3dd5\n    * src/buildtools/mac: git_revision:9fe99e262126467c4cb2f44cf941767d29fb33d8..git_revision:f90c3d9df882a9da4a66457f47dd3d99b3df3dd5\n    * src/buildtools/win: git_revision:9fe99e262126467c4cb2f44cf941767d29fb33d8..git_revision:f90c3d9df882a9da4a66457f47dd3d99b3df3dd5\n    * src/ios: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/ios/+log/d0685c246e..84410098da\n    * src