4cfea1384c71720c9242c0d5d13\n    * src/tools/luci-go: git_revision:b5ab8c6e7688d99a5702022cfaa95e9f8ce464f2..git_revision:1c4a8b1d449124cfea1384c71720c9242c0d5d13\n    DEPS diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/4cdeb6cfef..1cb7357a22/DEPS\n\n    BUG=None\n\n    Change-Id: I84873d19da417c851a6afe4bfc9daffdf300a58a\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509763\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Zo\u00e9 Lepaul \u003czlep@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Zo\u00e9 Lepaul \u003czlep@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48988}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/specs/client.webrtc.json", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/specs/mixins.pyl", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/specs/test_suites.pyl", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/specs/tryserver.webrtc.json"], "git_node": "801d3cc3c4b08427fa971eba4fc94c5bbee34133", "git_parents": ["7cfd510ae3faee55d213014f32aafe9f56cd7292"], "node": "567d871ec542bce04425f0b60fab5daf57ac1210", "parents": ["541c03afbbb7002cec6e5d2d029816c8b17539a9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from ac1a2f1d3e\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/ac1a2f1d3e91e7e03b1e2fa695be8be6cd681d6e\n    Fix generate_sslroots.py style and emit #include \u003ccstddef\u003e\n\n    Reformat to PEP-8 and snake_case so the script passes pylint,\n    without functional changes besides emitting #include \u003ccstddef\u003e.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42221823\n    Change-Id: I46e3bf6a30ce38854ed211d4e7d60764a46de348\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510260\n    Reviewed-by: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48989}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/tools_webrtc/sslroots/generate_sslroots.py"], "git_node": "3cb802401b32ebdf8b9b8aea046f5f370ea899b0", "git_parents": ["801d3cc3c4b08427fa971eba4fc94c5bbee34133"], "node": "dc08119988998f28cbfa55f2a579571668fbc4a1", "parents": ["567d871ec542bce04425f0b60fab5daf57ac1210"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 10ddc06b44\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/10ddc06b44bb71d067dac92a25ff38743d4312ab\n    Update ssl_roots.h\n\n    Refreshed from the script per comment in the file.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: Id7d9d5991f271a9e7033c918db5e76a91dc2451d\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510080\n    Reviewed-by: Jonas Oreland \u003cjonaso@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: David Benjamin \u003cdavidben@google.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jonas Oreland \u003cjonaso@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48990}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/ssl_roots.h"], "git_node": "8c7c6addbd3f4368bc83702dc397f313fe4e14f0", "git_parents": ["3cb802401b32ebdf8b9b8aea046f5f370ea899b0"], "node": "f4ec3aa4f73cc0ee9c55fca8cfe0e21e92d93357", "parents": ["dc08119988998f28cbfa55f2a579571668fbc4a1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from eedc809397\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/eedc8093976b236d825ecf9187e45a610cc4a5a7\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-10-21T04:09:54).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I736a1a4d2c0a0a58178b7a8621e42614f057c9ea\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510460\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48991}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "377eef184752e9c69db218ea335d2b8bd569c787", "git_parents": ["8c7c6addbd3f4368bc83702dc397f313fe4e14f0"], "node": "da897faa206d8e3dff7f4299c8cbf11de525bfd2", "parents": ["f4ec3aa4f73cc0ee9c55fca8cfe0e21e92d93357"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from faf326f00a\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/faf326f00aacb443609d34f579a9f17007a3d4d2\n    SCReAMv2: Replace non-linear backoff scaling with spec backoff\n\n    Replace the stateful UseNonLinearBackoffScale state machine in\n    ScreamV2::ScaleBackoff with the congestion backoff mechanisms from\n    draft-ietf-ccwg-rfc8298bis-screamv2-02 (controlled via UseSpecBackoff,\n    enabled by default):\n\n    1. Inhibit delay-based backoff (is_virtual_ce) when queue_delay_avg is\n       decreasing relative to queue_delay_avg_prev_ (updated once per\n       min(rtt, ReactionInterval())), and only set is_virtual_ce at a\n       reaction interval when !is_loss && !is_ce.\n    2. Attenuate backoff by BackoffScaleLowTargetRate (0.25) when\n       target_rate_ \u003c AckedBitrateMargin (0.8) * received_rate_ to prevent\n       reference window undershoot when RTT spikes (Section 4.5.3).\n    3. Scale backoff linearly across reactions per RTT via\n       max(1.0, rtt / ReactionInterval()).\n\n    Bug: webrtc:447037083\n    Change-Id: I029fe66442db4be35e86400ac9a52639122237ad\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510185\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48992}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/g3doc/implementation_diff.md", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_parameters.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_parameters.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/peer_scenario/bwe_integration_tests/scream_test.cc"], "git_node": "d8756cb13dc402af06d64be01f8679a971186178", "git_parents": ["377eef184752e9c69db218ea335d2b8bd569c787"], "node": "bf27839f477e923c2a0a44367a93f08e349ca6e4", "parents": ["da897faa206d8e3dff7f4299c8cbf11de525bfd2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 (MOZ) - Remove Empty.java from this script, as it has been removed from upstream. r?mjf\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/third_party_build/vendor-libwebrtc.py"], "git_node": "41d9b9da9aea34cdf89b9330be0c397543d0fa33", "git_parents": ["d8756cb13dc402af06d64be01f8679a971186178"], "node": "10f0cc0046d607112ebbe947c65b0f25efd01026", "parents": ["bf27839f477e923c2a0a44367a93f08e349ca6e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 3ae2dd12c1\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/3ae2dd12c1612c9787ecc74f4af4866ef5971e76\n    Remove the deprecated libjingle_peerconnection_java target\n\n    Replace libjingle_peerconnection_java by the underlying targets.\n\n    Change-Id: I3a60a488356f11ddee959c7ca8f3b03af6185494\n    Bug: webrtc:463418937\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509240\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48993}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/examples/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0092.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0140.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/sdk/android/src/java/org/webrtc/Empty.java"], "git_node": "42aac84d974fc48f5b537670f68daac339f6d572", "git_parents": ["41d9b9da9aea34cdf89b9330be0c397543d0fa33"], "node": "bf5582463982fb8ab39c677d0df20b8c5ee0f23e", "parents": ["10f0cc0046d607112ebbe947c65b0f25efd01026"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 60479dd833\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/60479dd8333861cb47ddc1bf00036c0c7cbf67a9\n    Align ScreamV2 ref_window_i and scl_t with draft -02\n\n    Update WebRTC's ScreamV2 reference window update logic to match the updated draft-ietf-ccwg-rfc8298bis-screamv2-02 (Sections 4.2.2.1 and 4.2.2.2):\n\n    - Remove the duplicate ref_window_scale_factor_close_to_ref_window_i() multiplier from multiplicative_scale in UpdateRefWindow() so scl_t scales window growth only once via std::max(0.25, ref_window_scale_factor_close_to_ref_window_i()).\n    - Gate ref_window_i_ updates on reference window decreases so ref_window_i_ is updated only when previous_ref_window \u003e ref_window_lowest_ * 1.05 or ref_window_i_update_max_hold_rtts (default 50 RTTs) has elapsed since last_ref_window_i_update_time_, preventing ref_window_i_ from stepping down during a congestion episode.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:447037083\n    Change-Id: I5dd94ab29ef4a04c200f777e6cecd4d2aaba5dcb\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510240\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48994}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/g3doc/implementation_diff.md", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_parameters.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_parameters.h"], "git_node": "d84b428c54d68217a0ad368c902003b11af19db7", "git_parents": ["42aac84d974fc48f5b537670f68daac339f6d572"], "node": "c9c404b521f6d83690af13d7ca74f1d962ac85aa", "parents": ["bf5582463982fb8ab39c677d0df20b8c5ee0f23e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from b8a5790f74\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/b8a5790f74228445ce81712038c9079bb3344744\n    Remove rtc_cc_test that don't reference any test file\n\n    Keep a unique test_support_unittests_resources for all the tests in the test_support_unittests rtc_test_suite. This is to avoid ios bundle_data resource file collision when multiple resources in a rtc_test_suite reference the same file.\n\n    Change-Id: I84290b901012ad5da9ea3c2b61cd80bfe2ceb2d1\n    Bug: webrtc:498394143\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510100\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48995}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0091.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/resources/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/pc/e2e/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/pc/e2e/analyzer/video/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/scenario/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/tools_webrtc/get_landmines.py", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/evaluation/BUILD.gn"], "git_node": "2e966b484fc876a846d7f1761c140634af9eb7f1", "git_parents": ["d84b428c54d68217a0ad368c902003b11af19db7"], "node": "33d0310969fd1af20c9b997451f6e8d3efa41216", "parents": ["c9c404b521f6d83690af13d7ca74f1d962ac85aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 145b9bf62e\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/145b9bf62e59f3611c17dc22facfb22411c27835\n    Add VideoEncoder::SetComplexity and map to reference encoders\n\n    Adds SetComplexity(std::span\u003cconst VideoCodecComplexity\u003e) to the legacy\n    VideoEncoder interface to allow dynamically updating complexity per\n    spatial or simulcast layer on a best-effort basis.\n\n    Forwards complexity settings through SimulcastEncoderAdapter,\n    VideoEncoderSoftwareFallbackWrapper, and FrameDumpingEncoder, and maps\n    the presets to the OpenH264, libvpx VP8/VP9, and libaom AV1 software\n    encoders.\n\n    This functionality is intended to map to\n    https://github.com/w3c/webrtc-extensions/issues/191\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42223911\n    Change-Id: I91e1ff4b1194fb7c67eca6920ffdce274f15a04c\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509260\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48996}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/test/mock_video_encoder.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/test/video_encoder_software_fallback_wrapper_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/video_encoder.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/video_encoder_software_fallback_wrapper.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/simulcast_encoder_adapter.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/simulcast_encoder_adapter.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/simulcast_encoder_adapter_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/libaom_av1_encoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/libaom_av1_encoder_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/h264/h264_encoder_impl.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/h264/h264_encoder_impl.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/h264/h264_encoder_impl_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/vp8/libvpx_vp8_encoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/vp8/libvpx_vp8_encoder.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/vp8/test/vp8_impl_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/vp9/libvpx_vp9_encoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/vp9/libvpx_vp9_encoder.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/vp9/test/vp9_impl_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0018.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0096.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0123.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0124.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0125.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0126.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0127.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0128.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0129.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0130.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0131.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0132.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0133.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0134.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0135.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0136.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0137.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0138.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0139.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0140.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0141.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0142.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0143.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0144.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0145.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0146.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0147.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0148.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0149.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0150.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/video_encoder_proxy_factory.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/frame_dumping_encoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/frame_dumping_encoder_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "fbaf8f0aea4ed22a0da87d22062ae4fd47e70392", "git_parents": ["2e966b484fc876a846d7f1761c140634af9eb7f1"], "node": "a3a916b97f6268c6cd58a51b43bc81da3fd77609", "parents": ["33d0310969fd1af20c9b997451f6e8d3efa41216"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 4bd72e8da0\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/4bd72e8da00052bdc961bbc12822a283896b0419\n    SCReAMv2: Inhibit backoff when target rate is low and data in flight decreases\n\n    Per Section 4.5.3 of draft-ietf-ccwg-rfc8298bis-screamv2, when\n    target_rate \u003c acked_bitrate_margin * received_rate, set backoff to 0 if\n    data_in_flight \u003c data_in_flight_prev (gated by field trial parameter\n    InhibitBackoffIfDataInFlightDecreases, enabled by default), and scale\n    by backoff_scale_low_target_rate otherwise.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:447037083\n    Change-Id: Ibe18aafbdeb3f855e303e318ed6dcc7851ae30d0\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510186\n    Reviewed-by: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48997}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/g3doc/implementation_diff.md", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_parameters.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_parameters.h"], "git_node": "0f07b65bd2f18c78536600411043894353d508c5", "git_parents": ["fbaf8f0aea4ed22a0da87d22062ae4fd47e70392"], "node": "8afd439c22474cc6b38645d1c218583a2a6fbbe9", "parents": ["a3a916b97f6268c6cd58a51b43bc81da3fd77609"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 8bff2e3f8b\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/8bff2e3f8b5fd6d21bb488bd54e3b539bdee3016\n    Reserve the log line in DefaultLogLine()\n\n    LogLineRef::DefaultLogLine() grew its buffer step by step while\n    appending the prefix, timestamp, thread, file, line and message. Reserve\n    the estimated size of the line up front instead.\n\n    Median time and heap allocations per call, with one sink:\n\n      BM_RtcLogLiteralsAndNumbers  294 ns -\u003e 276 ns, 4 -\u003e 3\n      BM_RtcLogMixedStrings        289 ns -\u003e 280 ns, 5 -\u003e 4\n      BM_RtcLogSdp/1  (1.4 KB)     330 ns -\u003e 310 ns, 5 -\u003e 4\n      BM_RtcLogSdp/16 (20.6 KB)    904 ns -\u003e 865 ns, 5 -\u003e 4\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: If160a2987ee92a97c62a82e0ea6a5cc3f7f8b3cd\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509762\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48998}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/logging.cc"], "git_node": "ebd7a01b524e9810e3a8c86bc8f5dd04654d9134", "git_parents": ["0f07b65bd2f18c78536600411043894353d508c5"], "node": "6b3e047777ae8dde7c3b354e3b7c3f4200bcd407", "parents": ["8afd439c22474cc6b38645d1c218583a2a6fbbe9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 96270440dc\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/96270440dc37560b2de2ee3dc82c13be610e6ace\n    Fail AddTransceiver with INVALID_STATE when closed\n\n    AddTransceiver() had no closed-state check, so after Close() the new\n    transceiver created its media channels with the already destroyed Call.\n    Return INVALID_STATE instead, as AddTrack() does and the spec requires.\n\n    Fixed: webrtc:576148431\n    Change-Id: Ia75a4dd971825cf6ced81fa4ab89689aa7e50dbc\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510500\n    Reviewed-by: Guido Urdaneta \u003cguidou@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Guido Urdaneta \u003cguidou@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48999}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/peer_connection_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_rtp_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "bbff43590242b31b9c230fd7826747a4a359468e", "git_parents": ["ebd7a01b524e9810e3a8c86bc8f5dd04654d9134"], "node": "17893e0909a0fe2ac9ecd48b29843d68d359c1f4", "parents": ["6b3e047777ae8dde7c3b354e3b7c3f4200bcd407"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 79bb12ff58\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/79bb12ff589454bcc00322e774189729a14f5c4d\n    Let OS pick ephemeral port for server in NetworkTesterTest.ServerClient\n\n    Selecting a single random port in [49152, 65535] for the server causes\n    EADDRINUSE failures when that port is already bound by another process\n    or by the client's ephemeral socket.\n\n    Bind the server socket with port range (0, 0) so the OS assigns an\n    available ephemeral port, and expose TestController::local_port() for\n    the client to connect to.\n\n    Example failure:\n    https://ci.chromium.org/ui/p/webrtc/builders/ci/Mac%20Asan/40576/overview\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42232538\n    Change-Id: I15ee54510ec15890400b8127e957a7ec9c1404ab\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508722\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49000}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0140.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_tools/network_tester/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_tools/network_tester/network_tester_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_tools/network_tester/test_controller.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_tools/network_tester/test_controller.h"], "git_node": "5b917f75a69060a68a38a4321bc868f162335990", "git_parents": ["bbff43590242b31b9c230fd7826747a4a359468e"], "node": "11365c5162dc6e49e066b3cc273b87a661bd5d49", "parents": ["17893e0909a0fe2ac9ecd48b29843d68d359c1f4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from d7880e9c1f\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/d7880e9c1f5a0f4a4c3ee582dce1145d4392daab\n    Delete deprecated CopyOnWriteBuffer(ptr, size) constructor as unused\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42225170\n    Change-Id: Ib72eb32bdcf6a799da12694d96f00ef7833daa38\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509621\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49001}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/copy_on_write_buffer.h"], "git_node": "96590005682de259a6b4a5a672148b7ec9d60a18", "git_parents": ["5b917f75a69060a68a38a4321bc868f162335990"], "node": "d1de76b2ce743a97a40a0199e7d23def37322e00", "parents": ["11365c5162dc6e49e066b3cc273b87a661bd5d49"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 (MOZ) - Use std::span with CopyOnWriteBuffer. r?mjf\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/transportbridge/MediaPipeline.cpp"], "git_node": "8885dca4ded70a374779d244fa83d6787613de66", "git_parents": ["96590005682de259a6b4a5a672148b7ec9d60a18"], "node": "a1bd5d4f2e9f1eaaa71aa68c5b6b10bc9d7a0f6b", "parents": ["d1de76b2ce743a97a40a0199e7d23def37322e00"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 090c4c87c4\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/090c4c87c40977261d017e96e9b98c165bacf12c\n    dcsctp: Do not reset T2-shutdown timer when retransmitting SHUTDOWN ACK\n\n    When the t2-shutdown timer expires in State::kShutdownAckSent, Timer::Trigger() increments expiration_count_ and schedules the next exponentially backed-off timeout before invoking DcSctpSocket::OnShutdownTimerExpiry(). Because OnShutdownTimerExpiry() calls SendShutdownAck(), which unconditionally called t2_shutdown_-\u003eStart(), each timer expiration reset expiration_count_ back to 0 and restarted the timer at the base RTO. As a result, a socket in SHUTDOWN-ACK-SENT whose peer's SHUTDOWN_COMPLETE was lost retransmitted SHUTDOWN_ACK at the base RTO indefinitely without backing off or aborting after max_retransmissions.\n\n    * Make SendShutdownAck() symmetric with SendShutdown() by only transmitting the SHUTDOWN_ACK chunk without starting t2_shutdown_.\n    * Start or restart t2_shutdown_ explicitly at the state transition and incoming SHUTDOWN handling call sites (MaybeSendShutdownOrAck() when transitioning from kShutdownReceived to kShutdownAckSent, and HandleShutdown() when receiving a SHUTDOWN in kShutdownSent or kShutdownAckSent), preserving RFC 4960 Section 9.2 timer restart semantics on incoming SHUTDOWN chunks while letting Timer::Trigger() manage backoff and max_retransmissions on timer expiry.\n    * When an INIT is received or the shutdown timer expires, just resend the SHUTDOWN_ACK without touching the timer. In the former case, this indicates the peer is trying to recreate the association after sending a SHUTDOWN_COMPLETE that was lost. In the latter, it potentially indicates the peer is already gone.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:575841526\n    Change-Id: I4443624816066cb38605d1a1eb15cacf3c1da44b\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510280\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49002}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/dcsctp_socket.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/net/dcsctp/socket/dcsctp_socket_test.cc"], "git_node": "0797715a5e787a998d29e92f6ba1c5810b092490", "git_parents": ["8885dca4ded70a374779d244fa83d6787613de66"], "node": "739598661cc23b1c1c54384896ece4284c07caf8", "parents": ["a1bd5d4f2e9f1eaaa71aa68c5b6b10bc9d7a0f6b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 26b29af875\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/26b29af875140dc5900c034b37ea6e9e817f6e73\n    Remove extra CopyOnWriteBuffer single parameter constructor\n\n    Instead rely on constructors from std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e and from\n    absl::string_view. Thus delegate type erasure to these two view types\n    instead of reimplementing it in CopyOnWriteBuffer.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42226010\n    Change-Id: I85b9c1a76e2be5fb9a9cf54c66192e98a0b5c501\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508660\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49003}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/copy_on_write_buffer.h"], "git_node": "384472ca3a4d2fc335c9a9957e908af2aa69261d", "git_parents": ["0797715a5e787a998d29e92f6ba1c5810b092490"], "node": "3e2e8ee874371e5c6f0663d6d955ba4c517305a0", "parents": ["739598661cc23b1c1c54384896ece4284c07caf8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from bebb00381e\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/bebb00381ebefe874d8f638e77588fdd20e873c2\n    Bump CBR test expectation limits that are too close to failing.\n\n    Some test cases were within 0.1% of failing. Make sure we have about\n    one percent leeway for all those tests.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:575916157, webrtc:496266459\n    Change-Id: I148c80e9b082372a451019ee0dfba4a59a35d4ec\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510560\n    Commit-Queue: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49004}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video_codecs/test/video_encoder_rate_control_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "1017a9cf4b9ee4f99c8a5ab3052286a411db25e5", "git_parents": ["384472ca3a4d2fc335c9a9957e908af2aa69261d"], "node": "69f20b433a12a7740959c414a0cd31032c7b67c6", "parents": ["3e2e8ee874371e5c6f0663d6d955ba4c517305a0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from fe34cbded9\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/fe34cbded9be5c87019e316987129310199e1519\n    Deflake RunLoopTest.RunForQuitsEarly* tests\n\n    The tests expected a quit task, posted with a 10 ms delay, to end the\n    loop within 11 ms of wall-clock time. That leaves 1-2 ms of slack, which\n    scheduling delays on loaded test machines can exceed.\n\n    - RunForQuitsEarlyIfQuitCalled: Use a 10 s max wait duration and expect\n      the loop to quit well before it.\n    - RunForQuitsEarlyAndCancelsQuitCalls: Check that a task posted after\n      RunFor() returns gets to run, instead of measuring elapsed time. A\n      stale RunFor() quit task is due earlier and would always run first,\n      regardless of load.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: Iaf1fabe0add0c8677f4eb33ffe1fceb0d43ccbd7\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510189\n    Auto-Submit: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49005}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/run_loop_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "cc3e6e2cf88eb88cef35548226bcc9ad9c2795ba", "git_parents": ["1017a9cf4b9ee4f99c8a5ab3052286a411db25e5"], "node": "04717677c56949ae13e7b09e123f15237e63f7b8", "parents": ["69f20b433a12a7740959c414a0cd31032c7b67c6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 7102b2679d\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/7102b2679dbd004038bbca96f87010220964d3c7\n    Introduce JavaByteArrayRef to replace JavaToNativeByteArray\n\n    The new helper can expose the buffer as span of uint8 which is preferred\n    way to represent raw buffers in WebRTC.\n\n    Additionally new helper allows to avoid extra memory copy by returning\n    reference to the buffer rather than a copy.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42226010\n    Change-Id: Ibf0ad32d1fba6a28916db67c343ab9e29b5ffacd\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509761\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Zo\u00e9 Lepaul \u003czlep@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49006}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "87bf1d169f7290256be1a3d48528a7943d9a4d93", "git_parents": ["cc3e6e2cf88eb88cef35548226bcc9ad9c2795ba"], "node": "1309b7f5ef373932426f413cb72bc491f0d16fd9", "parents": ["04717677c56949ae13e7b09e123f15237e63f7b8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 239857357a\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/239857357a4feb4bb9c2223a864c76b51318d7dd\n    Re-enable SVC and TickTimer unit tests dropped from test suites.\n\n    Commit https://webrtc-review.git.corp.google.com/c/src/+/491600 (\"Have\n    one rtc_library per test under modules subdirectories\") removed\n    svc:scalability_structure_tests, svc:svc_rate_allocator_tests and\n    svc:simulcast_to_svc_converter_tests from video_coding_unittests and\n    api/neteq:tick_timer_unittest from audio_coding_unittests without adding\n    them back as rtc_cc_test targets. Since then no test binary references\n    these targets, so the ScalabilityStructure*, SvcRateAllocator*,\n    SimulcastToSvcConverter* and TickTimer* tests have not been compiled or\n    run.\n\n    Convert the affected rtc_library targets to rtc_cc_test, remove the\n    scalability_structure_tests aggregate, and list the tests in\n    video_coding_unittests and audio_coding_unittests.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:498394143\n    Change-Id: I5c82f08f61431249f281d58353c53a84e9a5ed8b\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510580\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49007}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/neteq/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/audio_coding/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/svc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0091.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0092.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0139.patch"], "git_node": "ec5cdb6829c7dd80f0b4406ac866cea3a76c418d", "git_parents": ["87bf1d169f7290256be1a3d48528a7943d9a4d93"], "node": "80514431fd79434619322ea479c56d0d185fbd3d", "parents": ["1309b7f5ef373932426f413cb72bc491f0d16fd9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from bf4d8fefc1\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/bf4d8fefc1e2e8e48eb51f96b365e72169cacce3\n    Refactor pc tests from CopyOnWriteBuffer constructor taking raw ptr\n\n    Instead rely on constructor that takes span and capacity as two parameters.\n    Remove intermediate Buffers and c-array as not needed.\n    Rely on on CopyOnWriteBuffer::operator== instead of memcmp when comparing buffers for equality in tests.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42225170\n    Change-Id: Ie6cf0475fd9762c8407f2376536c3c33bd6f6a24\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510582\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49008}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/dtls_srtp_transport_integrationtest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/dtls_srtp_transport_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/srtp_transport_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "81853ae86758bbcb5943fb8a386a0fa4159ac8fc", "git_parents": ["ec5cdb6829c7dd80f0b4406ac866cea3a76c418d"], "node": "8c9f182cbb43dac5911664ed2845f12cd1ee69db", "parents": ["80514431fd79434619322ea479c56d0d185fbd3d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 43bc20bd85\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/43bc20bd85b27e37cdbfd97b564f2bfe95b01b4b\n    Add a fuzzer for STUN response handling\n\n    The three existing STUN/TURN fuzzers are stateless: stun_parser_fuzzer\n    reads a standalone StunMessage and validates it against an empty\n    password, stun_validator_fuzzer calls the static fingerprint and\n    integrity validators on raw bytes, and turn_unwrap_fuzzer calls\n    UnwrapTurnPacket. None of them constructs a StunRequestManager, so\n    none of them reaches response handling at all:\n\n      RequestMap::iterator iter = requests_.find(msg-\u003etransaction_id());\n      if (iter == requests_.end())\n        return false;\n\n    is the third line of CheckResponse, and a fuzzer that never sent a\n    request always returns there. No target in test/fuzzers/BUILD.gn\n    depends on p2p, so everything downstream of that lookup is currently\n    unfuzzed: the integrity decision that depends on the request's\n    AuthenticationRequired state, the comprehension-required attribute\n    check, the success/error branch split, and the OnResponse /\n    OnErrorResponse dispatch.\n\n    This target sends credentialed ALLOCATE requests first, then builds\n    responses for them.\n\n    The response is built with the StunMessage builder instead of being\n    handed over as mutated bytes. Three filters sit in front of the state\n    machine: the transaction id has to match a pending request, the\n    message type has to equal GetStunSuccessResponseType or\n    GetStunErrorResponseType for that request, and on the success branch\n    IntegrityOk() has to hold, which needs a valid HMAC-SHA1 over the\n    message. The last one is not just unlikely to be guessed, it cannot\n    be, so a mutating target can never execute OnResponse. Building the\n    message spends the input on the parts that carry attacker data -- which\n    attributes are present, their lengths and contents, the error code,\n    whether integrity is valid, and the order in which responses arrive\n    relative to each other and to simulated time. Malformed wire input is\n    left to stun_parser_fuzzer rather than duplicated here.\n\n    The request is a TurnMessage rather than a StunMessage. CheckResponse\n    parses the response with iter-\u003esecond-\u003emsg_-\u003eCreateNew(), so the\n    request's class is what decides which attribute types count as\n    comprehended. With a plain StunMessage every TURN attribute (LIFETIME,\n    DATA, XOR-RELAYED-ADDRESS) is unknown, and since they all sit in the\n    comprehension-required range the response is discarded before the\n    branch split is reached.\n\n    The callbacks act on the manager. The base class ones are empty, so a\n    target that sends a plain StunRequest reaches the dispatch and then\n    executes nothing, and CheckResponse states that a callback may modify\n    the StunRequestManager any way it sees fit. Each action mirrors a real\n    one: sending another request, as OnAuthChallenge and OnTryAlternate\n    both do from inside OnErrorResponse; clearing the manager, as TurnPort\n    does when an allocation fails; and deferring that clear with PostTask,\n    as the ALLOCATION_MISMATCH path does. Re-entrancy is depth-capped,\n    since production bounds its retries and an uncapped target would only\n    find its own recursion.\n\n    Simulated time advances between deliveries in steps large enough to\n    reach all eight retransmissions and the timeout.\n\n    Coverage over the seed corpus, four workers for seven minutes:\n    CheckResponse(StunMessage*) 36 of 80 edges, OnResponse 188 hits,\n    OnErrorResponse 220, OnTimeout 83, RevalidateMessageIntegrity 169,\n    GetErrorCodeValue 111. No crashes so far.\n\n    The seed corpus holds one file per branch, each named for the branch it\n    reaches. The byte-level STUN dictionary is deliberately not used here:\n    the input is a command stream, so STUN byte patterns are noise in it.\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I166a130385591ceaf888f8485b39ed8380bfea93\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510380\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    SLSA-Policy-Verified: SLSA Policy Verification Service \u003cdevtools-gerritcodereview-exitgate@google.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49009}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/AUTHORS", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/corpora/stun-response-corpus/error_300_try_alternate", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/corpora/stun-response-corpus/error_300_try_alternate_ipv6", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/corpora/stun-response-corpus/error_401_resends_from_callback", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/corpora/stun-response-corpus/error_437_deferred_teardown", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/corpora/stun-response-corpus/error_438_clears_manager_from_callback", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/corpora/stun-response-corpus/four_pending_out_of_order", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/corpora/stun-response-corpus/many_attributes", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/corpora/stun-response-corpus/non_comprehended_attribute_discards", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/corpora/stun-response-corpus/prevalidated_other_password_revalidates", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/corpora/stun-response-corpus/prevalidated_same_password", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/corpora/stun-response-corpus/success_bad_integrity", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/corpora/stun-response-corpus/success_no_integrity", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/corpora/stun-response-corpus/success_valid_integrity", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/corpora/stun-response-corpus/timeout_after_retransmits", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/corpora/stun-response-corpus/unauthenticated_error_400_rejected", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/corpora/stun-response-corpus/unauthenticated_success_discarded", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/corpora/stun-response-corpus/unmatched_transaction_id", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/corpora/stun-response-corpus/wrong_response_type", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/fuzzers/stun_request_response_fuzzer.cc"], "git_node": "22036dc37af607ce74ffc22bb008b5f9efca2194", "git_parents": ["81853ae86758bbcb5943fb8a386a0fa4159ac8fc"], "node": "89dc273528075aa75c72c4f2728ea8e673dc3db8", "parents": ["8c9f182cbb43dac5911664ed2845f12cd1ee69db"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from a68a53e42a\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/a68a53e42a4dc3c2e2212858a0ae137260497973\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-10-22T04:09:51).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: Idb4bf6f1955fcd11f542d5f4823d249a45579ea9\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510700\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49010}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "49b6100b58697eae2370e542d195c9630b95c551", "git_parents": ["22036dc37af607ce74ffc22bb008b5f9efca2194"], "node": "b2c46ab0d9f3dafbb21e6c39f42ff119a9b8dc5b", "parents": ["89dc273528075aa75c72c4f2728ea8e673dc3db8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from c17eaefae6\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/c17eaefae6c3b9700da02a1923e5daad19f55ab9\n    SCReAMv2: Use min of delay scale factors\n\n    Previously, the reference window increase scale factor multiplied\n    ref_window_scale_factor_due_to_avg_min_delay() (in [0.1, 1.0]) and\n    ref_window_scale_factor_due_to_latency_difference() (in [0.1, 1.0]),\n    compounding the penalty down to 0.01 (100x slower increase) when both\n    metrics observed delay or jitter simultaneously.\n\n    Taking std::min of the two scale factors preserves the intended [0.1, 1.0]\n    floor while keeping both complementary signals active (latency difference\n    for multi-packet burst queueing, and average min delay for standing queues\n    at low packet rates).\n\n    Controlled by the UseMinDelayScaleOnIncrease parameter in the\n    WebRTC-Bwe-ScreamV2 field trial (enabled by default).\n\n    Bug: webrtc:447037083\n    Change-Id: I8393c6d51ba5bb97afece483f95ce6d9b676491a\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510581\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49011}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_parameters.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_parameters.h"], "git_node": "8a11f6146ece172af432458fce0783c429f74f1e", "git_parents": ["49b6100b58697eae2370e542d195c9630b95c551"], "node": "4927b4df63eba7d5e44b4ec8912dd729c2aa582c", "parents": ["b2c46ab0d9f3dafbb21e6c39f42ff119a9b8dc5b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 4f576e6cbd\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/4f576e6cbdd401c3fbbb4b50c1a1f25ed4598d3a\n    stats: fix svc target bitrate\n\n    which underreports only the base spatial layer.\n    This is visible e.g. on\n      https://webrtc.github.io/samples/src/content/extensions/svc\n    with VP9 L2T3. In chrome://webrtc-internals produced bitrate and\n    target bitrate differ considerably (700kbps vs 160kbps).\n\n    Bug: webrtc:571267464\n    Change-Id: Ica3d24704b88362f3df458261012d858f64bd461\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510184\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49012}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/send_statistics_proxy.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/send_statistics_proxy_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "5a5efb798ef51f16c329865b07849b723e50a1d9", "git_parents": ["8a11f6146ece172af432458fce0783c429f74f1e"], "node": "b9d46ca724286aa185357a110b62d08916645097", "parents": ["4927b4df63eba7d5e44b4ec8912dd729c2aa582c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 973b847ae1\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/973b847ae1aabe072c405341dbd566c62bd44a0a\n    Destroy SctpDataChannel on signaling thread\n\n    SctpDataChannel could get deleted on the network thread, since the\n    controller and posted tasks held references to it there.\n\n    - When a channel closes, the controller hands its reference over to the\n      signaling thread.\n    - Network thread tasks use a PendingTaskSafetyFlag, which replaces\n      connected_to_transport_, instead of holding a reference.\n    - Don't touch a channel after it has closed, since it may then get\n      deleted at any time.\n    - SendAsync() always invokes on_complete, with INVALID_STATE if the\n      channel isn't connected or has closed.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:510487699\n    Change-Id: I80a81cb470252ec33092834d296536b6ae95f9b8\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509061\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49013}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0118.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/data_channel_controller.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/data_channel_controller.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/data_channel_controller_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sctp_data_channel.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sctp_data_channel.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sctp_data_channel_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/fake_data_channel_controller.h"], "git_node": "2eac75047acc1a71b56a4871bb05af1f56909a90", "git_parents": ["5a5efb798ef51f16c329865b07849b723e50a1d9"], "node": "f52cb34e246714c76990ba21ebe82af291cab44d", "parents": ["b9d46ca724286aa185357a110b62d08916645097"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from b38573bb56\n\nEssentially a no-op since we're going to see this change\nreverted when we vendor in 1363664fa8.\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/b38573bb56e571405b318c761c23a5b247d24716\n    Batch SDP candidates and O(1) TransportInfo lookup\n\n    SdpDeserialize added candidates one at a time with AddCandidate(), which\n    looks up the m= section, copies the candidate and recomputes the\n    connection address on every call. SdpSerialize copied the candidates of\n    each m= section and looked up its TransportInfo by name.\n\n    Now the parser fills one IceCandidateCollection per m= section and\n    passes them to SessionDescriptionInterface::Create(), which updates each\n    section's connection address once. The serializer reads the candidate\n    collections directly and tries the TransportInfo at the same index\n    before falling back to a lookup by name.\n\n    BM_Sdp* benchmarks (release build, median of 5 runs):\n    - Deserialize: -2.9% (small), -4.6% (large)\n    - Serialize: -3.7% (small), -12.2% (large)\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: I04eae8cab5870cf60708cea9668cc147807ba176\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509664\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49014}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/1363664fa8.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0001.patch"], "git_node": "8d1f6e0250fc1616f12def8bae2f5029173a2f32", "git_parents": ["2eac75047acc1a71b56a4871bb05af1f56909a90"], "node": "613d68d986a39ef748e3e585d1d0ae76cf590afe", "parents": ["f52cb34e246714c76990ba21ebe82af291cab44d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 3f046fd355\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/3f046fd35579dae0f030dccfb4a5079a625a9818\n    Remove Android JVM init from pc and SDP tests\n\n    On Android, the peer connection unit tests and webrtc_sdp_unittest call\n    InitializeAndroidObjects(), which crashes unless a JVM is present. These\n    tests can therefore only run as APKs started by the JNI test launcher.\n\n    The initialization is not needed: the tests use fake audio devices and\n    fake media engines, SSL is already initialized by the test main, and\n    none of the code they exercise uses webrtc::JVM. Removing the calls, and\n    the android_black_magic target that provided them, allows these tests to\n    run as plain native executables on Android, which are much cheaper to\n    build than APKs.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:498394143\n    Change-Id: I5e6b1ce3ad3a03869c8cca93b7ad0dcfe35f45db\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510780\n    Reviewed-by: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49015}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/webrtc_sdp_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_bundle_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_crypto_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_data_channel_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_end_to_end_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_factory_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_field_trial_tests.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_ice_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_interface_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_jsep_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_media_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_signaling_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/android_test_initializer.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/android_test_initializer.h"], "git_node": "893994053a5e59c63ed42968075563095c62e902", "git_parents": ["8d1f6e0250fc1616f12def8bae2f5029173a2f32"], "node": "6a943ad978153fa377330c3e1e76d0e93711d3bc", "parents": ["613d68d986a39ef748e3e585d1d0ae76cf590afe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 888470bad6\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/888470bad6ff92625c73b03a7775ed7213d72d51\n    Ignore stale OpenSSL errors when parsing PEM certificate chains\n\n    CreateFromPEMChainStrings() detects the end of the input by checking\n    that PEM reading failed with PEM_R_NO_START_LINE. It inspected that\n    error with ERR_peek_error(), which returns the oldest error in the\n    thread's error queue rather than the one just added by the failed read.\n    If an earlier operation on the same thread, such as a failed TLS\n    handshake, had left an error in the queue, parsing a valid chain failed.\n\n    Check the most recent error instead, and clear the queue once the end of\n    the input has been reached. Same fix for the BoringSSL and the OpenSSL\n    implementation.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:576525998\n    Change-Id: I70998cdd3dd0d64749fb951c1cd5a8380757da28\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510760\n    Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49016}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/boringssl_identity.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/openssl_identity.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/ssl_identity_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "aa0da9aaf42ddaf0f316436d97eaf8520d25763b", "git_parents": ["893994053a5e59c63ed42968075563095c62e902"], "node": "435182b195cb5014f5b9b9076f2d13717f31558f", "parents": ["6a943ad978153fa377330c3e1e76d0e93711d3bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 7796203a9c\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/7796203a9c9af392411ced60b976f8bc3e2a564a\n    Distrust compromised eMudhra intermediate CA keys\n\n    The private keys of eight eMudhra intermediate CAs (EM {DV,OV,EV} TLS CA\n    and EM OV CS CA, G3B and G3C) are compromised. Removing the \"AAA\n    Certificate Services\" root, which cross-signed them, from ssl_roots.h\n    only protects clients that use the built-in trust store. Embedders with\n    a custom SSLCertificateVerifier or their own trust store, which may\n    still trust that root or the eMudhra roots, remain exposed, and the\n    library does no revocation checking.\n\n    Reject TLS certificate chains in which any certificate has a\n    SubjectPublicKeyInfo whose SHA-256 matches a fixed list, as Go's\n    crypto/x509 does. Matching on the public key also covers the\n    cross-signed and any reissued certificates. The check runs after the\n    built-in trust store and the custom verifier have accepted the chain, in\n    both the X509 and the CRYPTO_BUFFER code path, so neither can override\n    it. Only SetIgnoreBadCert(true), used for\n    TLS_CERT_POLICY_INSECURE_NO_CHECK, bypasses it.\n\n    A custom verifier that completes the path itself, e.g. via AIA fetching,\n    may use certificates that are never checked. Conversely, a distrusted\n    certificate that is presented but not needed for the path still causes\n    the chain to be rejected. Certificates that cannot be parsed are treated\n    as distrusted, so that a lenient custom verifier cannot be handed a BER\n    re-encoding that this parser rejects.\n\n    Based on https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510400 by\n    Byoungchan Lee, with the review comments addressed.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42221823\n    Change-Id: I3e3103e7565d74fed321319ddb7f507da78640db\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510761\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49017}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0052.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0083.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0085.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0086.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0099.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/distrusted_certificates_for_testing.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/openssl_adapter.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/openssl_utility.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/openssl_utility.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/openssl_utility_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/ssl_adapter.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/ssl_adapter_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/ssl_certificate.h"], "git_node": "ae517592b049d47fbdbd26a6e93120da0f55a025", "git_parents": ["aa0da9aaf42ddaf0f316436d97eaf8520d25763b"], "node": "0e580c60e491931dfc97cdaa86d9d5307626b835", "parents": ["435182b195cb5014f5b9b9076f2d13717f31558f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 1f8124c03a\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/1f8124c03a21c29182335aacbefc547f11cbdb3a\n    Delete CopyOnWriteBuffer constructor that takes raw pointer\n\n    Update all usages of that constructor to the constructor that takes span\n    + capacity.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42226010\n    Change-Id: I7c07fd6801c50c5b4239631920ee041987f9e1c2\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508240\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49018}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/datagram_connection_internal.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/srtp_session_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/copy_on_write_buffer.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/copy_on_write_buffer_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/peer_scenario/scenario_connection.cc"], "git_node": "6e898d28192ce41087fcae9add0dea14f426eea4", "git_parents": ["ae517592b049d47fbdbd26a6e93120da0f55a025"], "node": "42ba543e7e8449b010b4809d9d67e820bfc578c5", "parents": ["0e580c60e491931dfc97cdaa86d9d5307626b835"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 326fd06bb4\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/326fd06bb4d93900ed6947205b94cefd2413afca\n    Keep SRTP sessions when activating RTCP mux\n\n    JsepTransport::ActivateRtcpMux() cleared the RTCP DTLS transport before\n    RTCP mux was enabled on the RtpTransport. DtlsSrtpTransport then didn't\n    recognize the removal as part of activating RTCP mux, reset the active\n    SRTP sessions and set them up again from the RTP DTLS transport,\n    discarding their state.\n\n    Enable RTCP mux on the RtpTransport before clearing the RTCP transport,\n    so that DtlsSrtpTransport keeps the sessions.\n\n    Fixed: chromium:513198336\n    Change-Id: I85d81d572ffe38770650d07531ce3af4d0e83647\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510781\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49019}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_transport_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "a9aef1aa9547adcbe09291d941688cfb71fbf3b9", "git_parents": ["6e898d28192ce41087fcae9add0dea14f426eea4"], "node": "2a02e2ef60cb092ce32be6c54fb842a7af298ac0", "parents": ["42ba543e7e8449b010b4809d9d67e820bfc578c5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 60868a628a\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/60868a628a8664a1c90dbe2a0ef0978f823d03dd\n    Wait for ICE gathering before stopping transceiver in integration test.\n\n    In PeerConnectionIntegrationTestUnifiedPlan.StopTransceiverRemovesDtlsTransports, the initial offer/answer exchange only waited for the signaling state to reach kStable before stopping the sole transceiver and renegotiating. Because trickle ICE candidate gathering runs asynchronously on the network thread, tearing down the transceiver's JsepTransport immediately after signaling stabilizes can race with candidate allocation and transition the ICE gathering state directly from kIceGatheringGathering to kIceGatheringNew, skipping kIceGatheringComplete and flaking on the state history assertion.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42222804\n    Change-Id: I58ccf6d6620c98dd302c20efd51543bf6f142c77\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510521\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Darin Peetz \u003cdarinpeetz@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49020}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_integrationtest.cc"], "git_node": "a17b93b43140f9746b16a5c4add681fc88f004c1", "git_parents": ["a9aef1aa9547adcbe09291d941688cfb71fbf3b9"], "node": "c302d40dd2d83fed18a55bd9bd0f4976ee72f12b", "parents": ["2a02e2ef60cb092ce32be6c54fb842a7af298ac0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from dabf75478c\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/dabf75478cb115e1a2f2880e40261b49a281415c\n    Improve setParameters() error messages.\n\n    The message should say which codec and scalability mode was attempted\n    and distinguish between the issue being lack of codec support or lack of\n    scalability mode for the given codec.\n\n    Bug: chromium:576554678\n    Change-Id: I44df64b1b85a6f6958c0807d7ee07ae9fc8a1982\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510800\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49021}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/media_engine.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/media_engine_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_video_engine.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_video_engine_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0092.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0099.patch"], "git_node": "e8d737dd8dbd9f1d5ca78bec7108d007e309013e", "git_parents": ["a17b93b43140f9746b16a5c4add681fc88f004c1"], "node": "740351eed79f49bf5e28c453465ff409efedf8d2", "parents": ["c302d40dd2d83fed18a55bd9bd0f4976ee72f12b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from e518f9925c\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/e518f9925cee60e2f393cbe99aa74b65572be615\n    Do not reorder codecs in GetRtpSendParameters.\n\n    Previously, WebRtcVideoSendChannel::GetRtpSendParameters() moved the\n    active send_codec() to the front of rtp_params.codecs, introduced in\n    [1], causing `getParameters().codecs` to dynamically change order\n    based on current send codec.\n\n    This is a spec-compliance issue as `getParameters().codecs` is supposed\n    to be a readonly fixed list representing the last negotiated codecs, in\n    negotiated order. This is part of the effort to make\n    `setParameters(getParameters())` more robust in case of badly timed\n    codec switches. Without it, `setParameters()` rejects thinking you've\n    modified the readonly parameter `codecs`.\n\n    (It still rejects for other reasons on a different layer, but this\n    fixes the problem on the webrtc_video_engine.cc layer.)\n\n    [1] https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/246500\n\n    Bug: chromium:576126155\n    Change-Id: I72d2e40c2b2396836a183c07a7f2a81020f1aec7\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510763\n    Reviewed-by: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49022}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_video_engine.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_video_engine_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "c36bd56e7c4681f3c914168571a58841a8f144c7", "git_parents": ["e8d737dd8dbd9f1d5ca78bec7108d007e309013e"], "node": "5dfe5260246623f05e6bff66144eed9f3e6c2982", "parents": ["740351eed79f49bf5e28c453465ff409efedf8d2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 5d27ce25e2\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/5d27ce25e244b90d09de3429dd3e702fd70f400b\n    Fix receiver SSRC tracking for unsignaled streams\n\n    Since https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/499601,\n    RTCRtpReceiver.getStats() filters the report by the SSRC that the\n    receiver tracks on the signaling thread, ssrc_s(). For unsignaled\n    streams, that SSRC could get out of sync with the worker thread's view:\n\n    - Renegotiating without signaled SSRCs reset it to nullopt. If the media\n      channel kept the unsignaled stream, no new first packet notification\n      followed and the receiver stayed unbound, so getStats() returned no\n      inbound-rtp and the receiver's sources stopped updating.\n    - A first packet notification for a new unsignaled SSRC, e.g. when the\n      remote endpoint changed the SSRC, was ignored since the receiver was\n      already bound to the previous SSRC.\n\n    Track the signaled SSRC and the most recent unsignaled SSRC separately\n    on the signaling thread, mirroring RtpReceiverBase::ssrc() on the worker\n    thread. Setting up the receiver only updates the signaled SSRC, and a\n    first packet for a new unsignaled stream rebinds the first receiver that\n    doesn't have a signaled SSRC.\n\n    Bug: b:575939917\n    Change-Id: I1dff1ad7ce686322bd0dd60c1fee3557e7a7907e\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510881\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49023}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/audio_rtp_receiver.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/audio_rtp_receiver_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_integrationtest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_receiver.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_receiver.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_transceiver.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/integration_test_helpers.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/integration_test_helpers.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/mock_rtp_receiver_internal.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/video_rtp_receiver.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/video_rtp_receiver_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "659947beebd77ddfbddcf3e11d66285a116ef4fa", "git_parents": ["c36bd56e7c4681f3c914168571a58841a8f144c7"], "node": "d703936eed484520eb7c2d65322c32c67bdf8d9f", "parents": ["5dfe5260246623f05e6bff66144eed9f3e6c2982"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 1363664fa8\n\nWe already cherry-picked this when we vendored b38573bb56.\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/1363664fa800213504a2daa6175e9442210d2bc0\n    Revert \"Batch SDP candidates and O(1) TransportInfo lookup\"\n\n    This reverts commit b38573bb56e571405b318c761c23a5b247d24716.\n\n    Reason for revert: Broke the chromium roll\n\n    Failure Link: https://chromium-review.git.corp.google.com/c/chromium/src/+/8622522?tab=checks\n\n    Original change's description:\n    \u003e Batch SDP candidates and O(1) TransportInfo lookup\n    \u003e\n    \u003e SdpDeserialize added candidates one at a time with AddCandidate(), which\n    \u003e looks up the m= section, copies the candidate and recomputes the\n    \u003e connection address on every call. SdpSerialize copied the candidates of\n    \u003e each m= section and looked up its TransportInfo by name.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Now the parser fills one IceCandidateCollection per m= section and\n    \u003e passes them to SessionDescriptionInterface::Create(), which updates each\n    \u003e section's connection address once. The serializer reads the candidate\n    \u003e collections directly and tries the TransportInfo at the same index\n    \u003e before falling back to a lookup by name.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e BM_Sdp* benchmarks (release build, median of 5 runs):\n    \u003e - Deserialize: -2.9% (small), -4.6% (large)\n    \u003e - Serialize: -3.7% (small), -12.2% (large)\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Bug: none\n    \u003e Change-Id: I04eae8cab5870cf60708cea9668cc147807ba176\n    \u003e Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509664\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49014}\n\n    Bug: none\n    No-Presubmit: true\n    No-Tree-Checks: true\n    No-Try: true\n    Change-Id: I361a5616f1d51402b270f8a3d180453b610293d2\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510940\n    Bot-Commit: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49024}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/1363664fa8.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/p0001.patch"], "git_node": "6839a068160110cc713136185695597bd6b208c9", "git_parents": ["659947beebd77ddfbddcf3e11d66285a116ef4fa"], "node": "6da9b0a2e6d609ad1bfbe4d270ef887cd243bd54", "parents": ["d703936eed484520eb7c2d65322c32c67bdf8d9f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 99716070be\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/99716070beb37c6c87462015dc8c76f221bb022c\n    Serve RtpSender::GetParameters() from the parameter cache\n\n    - Use the cache in GetParameters() instead of a blocking call to the\n      worker thread.\n    - Remove the temporary DCHECK that compared the cache with the worker\n      thread state.\n    - Compare GetParameters() with the media channel's parameters in the\n      tests that relied on that DCHECK.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42222804\n    Change-Id: Icc196dc5ab8ba71ceb0af7efb8771b3724ff983a\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509662\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49025}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_rtp_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender.cc"], "git_node": "668cefca67d59047a609f83aacaf5e5576474736", "git_parents": ["6839a068160110cc713136185695597bd6b208c9"], "node": "6896450a5777774aaf38a8d63815b99e5ec6bda2", "parents": ["6da9b0a2e6d609ad1bfbe4d270ef887cd243bd54"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from c8bca1867e\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/c8bca1867efcbc5f52adf58ad4463088ed257aa0\n    Move SeqNumUnwrapper to api/numerics/\n\n    Move SeqNumUnwrapper and its unit tests from rtc_base/numerics/ to\n    api/numerics/sequence_number_unwrapper.h, leaving a forwarding header in\n    rtc_base/numerics/sequence_number_unwrapper.h until downstream callers\n    are migrated.\n\n    Bug: chromium:576594392\n    Change-Id: I127274d298ea5dadccb2853579c87aef3145c1ac\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510880\n    Commit-Queue: Johannes Kron \u003ckron@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49026}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/numerics/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/numerics/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/numerics/sequence_number_unwrapper.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/numerics/sequence_number_unwrapper_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/logging/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0034.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0044.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0052.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0054.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0081.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0083.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0085.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0086.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0092.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0097.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0099.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0139.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/numerics/sequence_number_unwrapper.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/numerics/sequence_number_unwrapper_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/BUILD.gn"], "git_node": "077d582aa41063fa6b26668fcf118b137eb62760", "git_parents": ["668cefca67d59047a609f83aacaf5e5576474736"], "node": "1cf915c5393388ae9dd2e8c4c138d3274fb17cef", "parents": ["6896450a5777774aaf38a8d63815b99e5ec6bda2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from c8bca1867e - moz.build file updates\n", "files": ["CLOBBER", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/numerics/sequence_number_unwrapper_gn/moz.build", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz.build", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/sequence_number_util_gn/moz.build"], "git_node": "3536e1455364e77510ac471b61caa0df43c164bc", "git_parents": ["077d582aa41063fa6b26668fcf118b137eb62760"], "node": "73d47b6ad583f846515028b727b0a50d0e01f19a", "parents": ["1cf915c5393388ae9dd2e8c4c138d3274fb17cef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from a2a51e5e80\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/a2a51e5e80514511f6cd6760e1785c5b171942cb\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-10-23T04:07:06).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I73e2b2eb275c562774ff0a014da3bd9f29dcb443\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/511020\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49027}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "145a8044e64a3f22fb1f5e21be03ded7e9b981d0", "git_parents": ["3536e1455364e77510ac471b61caa0df43c164bc"], "node": "6ab921f7c88b72d7f4ff19dd19e0596438a04ceb", "parents": ["73d47b6ad583f846515028b727b0a50d0e01f19a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 5b8be32bd6\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/5b8be32bd6011d4f7afc39daeee623283638505a\n    Deflake FrameSelector unittest\n\n    SelectsAboutHalfInMiddleOfSpan expects 40-60 of 100 frames to be\n    selected, where each frame is selected with a probability of 50%. Since\n    FrameSelector seeds its random number generator with the current time,\n    the count varies between runs and falls outside that range in about 1 in\n    28 runs, which turns bots that don't retry failed tests red. Example\n    failure:\n    https://ci.chromium.org/ui/p/webrtc/builders/ci/Fuchsia%20Release/10290/overview\n\n    Use a simulated clock for a fixed seed, and 1000 frames so that the same\n    40-60% range holds for practically any seed.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: Ie5c9ca19b2451cf21570fa9916aa30c5940204a1\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/511040\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49028}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/corruption_detection/frame_selector_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "8b0178e31fa4b318760be149f3ce495554cec120", "git_parents": ["145a8044e64a3f22fb1f5e21be03ded7e9b981d0"], "node": "2d3880e5a2700948018d0cb527a4d8e111a52422", "parents": ["6ab921f7c88b72d7f4ff19dd19e0596438a04ceb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from ed7d57f1e2\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/ed7d57f1e2747ac7528e8d30421d840b4ff6a976\n    Remove PeerConnectionFactoryDependencies::worker_thread\n\n    Support for a worker thread that is distinct from the network thread is\n    being removed. The worker_thread member is deprecated and a distinct\n    worker thread logs a deprecation error, but affected integrations keep\n    running until support is gone. Removing the member, rather than making\n    such configurations a fatal error at runtime, makes remaining users fail\n    at compile time instead of crashing in production.\n\n    ConnectionContext now always uses the network thread as the worker\n    thread. The fallback that used a socket-capable worker thread as the\n    network thread when network_thread was not set is removed, as is the\n    deprecation log.\n\n    Downstream migration:\n    - Remove assignments to\n      PeerConnectionFactoryDependencies::worker_thread.\n    - Integrations that set worker_thread but not network_thread, relying on\n      the worker thread being used as the network thread, should assign that\n      thread to network_thread instead.\n\n    See PSA: https://groups.google.com/g/discuss-webrtc/c/Fs_Hd5XNJh0\n\n    Bug: webrtc:558821261\n    Change-Id: Iebb46c3d25ae66f6cd7b22b5d4802c82732520bb\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510120\n    Reviewed-by: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49029}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/peer_connection_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/connection_context.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_factory_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "e73ba33db838506f3143cc8958e7d60c481c974c", "git_parents": ["8b0178e31fa4b318760be149f3ce495554cec120"], "node": "4cd3591689728cc84e366064e0e4c44dfd044aa8", "parents": ["2d3880e5a2700948018d0cb527a4d8e111a52422"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from c48dfce372\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/c48dfce372a005c22c345fc96e488430c1ffaa07\n    Add WebRTC.Video.PlayoutDelayMode histogram on the receiver\n\n    Logs a 4-bit bitmask at the end of a video receive stream session\n    indicating which playout-delay RTP header extension modes\n    (default/unset, 0/0, 0/X, X/Y) were used during the session.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: I5cb4dcccdc3b5d6a37fb5549dc4ff70f4839e534\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510480\n    Reviewed-by: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Johannes Kron \u003ckron@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49030}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0037.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0041.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0056.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0057.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0058.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/receive_statistics_proxy.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/receive_statistics_proxy.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/receive_statistics_proxy_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_receive_stream2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_receive_stream2_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "a1b1c0d7282c03d6ac5553987514a1806fb05d19", "git_parents": ["e73ba33db838506f3143cc8958e7d60c481c974c"], "node": "24d1a3ff9ad3028042e6e537dfc1e8df1132ac65", "parents": ["4cd3591689728cc84e366064e0e4c44dfd044aa8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 0881849e28\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/0881849e284d4de8a6cb981dbd0355e8537b91b3\n    Implemented synchronized sframe encryptor\n\n    The public key-management proxy dispatches key updates to the worker\n    thread, but the video send path calls the shared encryptor directly from\n    a different execution context (encoder queue or transformer queue). The\n    proxy therefore does not serialize key rotation against media\n    encryption. Both operations access the same mutable encryption state, so\n    enabling video encryption requires synchronization across these paths\n    rather than single-sequence affinity. A sequence checker alone neither\n    permits this cross-thread use nor prevents concurrent access.\n\n    Add SynchronizedSframeEncryptor, a mutex-protected wrapper around\n    SframeEncryptor, and use it in\n    RtpSenderBase::CreateSframeEncryptorOrError. The key-management proxy\n    and the media pipeline then share a single encryptor, with key\n    installation and encryption serialized by the mutex.\n    GetMaxCiphertextByteSize() does not take the lock: it depends only on\n    the frame size and a constant, and does not touch mutable state.\n\n    Replace the underlying SframeEncryptor's sequence checker with a race\n    checker to permit calls from different threads while still requiring\n    serialized access.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:479862368\n    Change-Id: Icceeb698249d724d2ae52de32223d9692ca05b08\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508380\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Kacper Wasniowski \u003ckwasniow@cisco.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49031}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/sframe/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/sframe/sframe_encryptor.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/sframe/sframe_encryptor.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/sframe/synchronized_sframe_encryptor.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/sframe/synchronized_sframe_encryptor.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/sframe/synchronized_sframe_encryptor_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender_receiver_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "12eae02494a8ad9cec1f080531e8e58101f7720e", "git_parents": ["a1b1c0d7282c03d6ac5553987514a1806fb05d19"], "node": "bbee792a484eb6c7b53e2a35c0e0ad1b67c078f2", "parents": ["24d1a3ff9ad3028042e6e537dfc1e8df1132ac65"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 6300440aee\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/6300440aeeb87d712d1e490587f15851f71237e1\n    Drain OpenSSL error queue in OpenSSLAdapter\n\n    OpenSSLAdapter::ContinueSSL did not call LogSslError on SSL_ERROR_SSL,\n    unlike DoSslWrite and Recv, leaving handshake errors in the thread's\n    OpenSSL error queue. In addition, LogSslError broke out of its loop\n    after logging the first ERR_LIB_SSL entry, leaving any subsequent queued\n    errors behind.\n\n    Call LogSslError from ContinueSSL on SSL_ERROR_SSL and drain the entire\n    error queue in LogSslError.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:576525998\n    Change-Id: I3a1ab14426be5ca2efde2e7a2430f9c3a92d17c7\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510841\n    Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49032}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/openssl_adapter.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/ssl_adapter_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "a8906b0e959e194b84d77c8dae1a648d43768b0e", "git_parents": ["12eae02494a8ad9cec1f080531e8e58101f7720e"], "node": "e89fe5de76c3a547517ac7fdbb6db8bdeec9a2fa", "parents": ["bbee792a484eb6c7b53e2a35c0e0ad1b67c078f2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 8cb3d509a1\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/8cb3d509a138ef2a3413f4b0d6a9344084eba116\n    Disable builtin SSL root certificates when building with Chromium\n\n    Chromium handles TLS-TURN in the network service and verifies\n    certificates there, so the root store linked in via\n    BasicPacketSocketFactory is never used. This saves ~20kb.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42221823\n    Change-Id: I079fa4feada4323af7033a6b09ec6d8f1c4ad6d3\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510920\n    Reviewed-by: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49033}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0034.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0044.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0068.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0092.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0093.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0095.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0099.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0105.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0140.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/webrtc.gni"], "git_node": "12c71032c2c89cce360c9a29298288eb6cf56227", "git_parents": ["a8906b0e959e194b84d77c8dae1a648d43768b0e"], "node": "e4bf638793dc072dc4f14ed56c08e08c3a6f3af0", "parents": ["e89fe5de76c3a547517ac7fdbb6db8bdeec9a2fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 2174976414\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/21749764142ff39fbea8814a9b25ac129955f99f\n    Use 100 source frames in LibaomAv1EncoderComplexityTest\n\n    SetComplexityIncreasesQuality previously loaded only 10 frames of\n    foreman_cif and looped them 10 times in variable complexity mode,\n    introducing a jump-cut every 10 frames. After libaom's SVC ref-frame\n    refresh fix (b7cd5ffb57a8), 1-pass CBR rate-control variance across\n    those cuts caused kComplexityNormal to dip 0.06 dB below kComplexityLow.\n\n    Read 100 distinct frames from foreman_cif and encode 100 frames in both\n    modes so average PSNR increases monotonically across all presets.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:496266459, webrtc:42223911\n    Change-Id: I01b72e1657bf1a941f54828b5a154f4929addcef\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510900\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49034}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/codecs/av1/libaom_av1_encoder_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "a58bccff210cd2532f4498eeec25443c43335e8f", "git_parents": ["12c71032c2c89cce360c9a29298288eb6cf56227"], "node": "36e93353efbda137a00b47911d41edba9e0930df", "parents": ["e4bf638793dc072dc4f14ed56c08e08c3a6f3af0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 202acee882\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/202acee882062f7ca632472e4810f25938828f6a\n    Add per-frame Sframe encryption to the video send path\n\n    When negotiation requires Sframe, RTPSenderVideo dropped every encoded\n    frame unconditionally. Encrypt the frame instead when a per-frame Sframe\n    encryptor is configured.\n\n    In per-frame mode the whole encoded frame is encrypted with the\n    configured encryptor before packetization. The ciphertext is packetized\n    with RtpPacketizerSframe, selected through GetPacketizationFormat() as\n    PacketizationFormat::kSframe. It splits the ciphertext like raw\n    packetization, writes the Sframe descriptor into every packet and sets\n    the marker bit of the last packet from is_last_frame_in_picture, which\n    keeps the VP9 and AV1 end-of-picture semantics.\n\n    Frames are still dropped when Sframe is required but no encryptor is\n    configured, when the encryptor is configured for per-packet mode, which\n    is not supported yet, or when encryption fails. The check is done both\n    in SendEncodedImage() and in SendVideoFrame(), since frames can reach\n    SendVideoFrame() without SendEncodedImage(), e.g. from an encoded frame\n    transform. An encryptor configured before negotiation requires Sframe\n    stays unused.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:479862368\n    Change-Id: I04588be499555eca69cd668b77abff08c6c18f1e\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508080\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Kacper Wasniowski \u003ckwasniow@cisco.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49035}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_sender_video.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_sender_video.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_sender_video_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/sframe/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/sframe/mock_sframe_media_encryptor.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch"], "git_node": "a9bc62234174aae1aa85a93fb0b42c7dd43ecd19", "git_parents": ["a58bccff210cd2532f4498eeec25443c43335e8f"], "node": "f3b90fdaea40c47a0289dfe90fcac4da1edc35de", "parents": ["36e93353efbda137a00b47911d41edba9e0930df"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 165fc4c85a\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/165fc4c85aaaf2ee18084eda940577b07c0f720b\n    Roll chromium_revision 1cb7357a22..b1ff7dbb45 (1721831:1724627)\n\n    Change log: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+log/1cb7357a22..b1ff7dbb45\n    Full diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/1cb7357a22..b1ff7dbb45\n\n    Changed dependencies\n    * src/build: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/build/+log/16c326db38..6c397581be\n    * src/buildtools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/buildtools/+log/54989aa948..de083582f3\n    * src/ios: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/ios/+log/84410098da..16b1bdb304\n    * src/testing: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/testing/+