n/llvm-code-coverage-llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b-67.tar.xz,Win/llvmobjdump-llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b-67.tar.xz..Linux_x64/clang-android-runtime-library-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Linux_x64/clang-linux-runtime-library-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Linux_x64/clang-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Linux_x64/clang-tidy-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Linux_x64/clangd-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Linux_x64/llvm-code-coverage-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Linux_x64/llvmobjdump-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Mac/clang-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Mac/clang-mac-runtime-library-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Mac/clang-tidy-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Mac/clangd-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Mac/llvm-code-coverage-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Mac/llvmobjdump-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Mac_arm64/clang-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Mac_arm64/clang-tidy-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Mac_arm64/clangd-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Mac_arm64/llvm-code-coverage-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Mac_arm64/llvmobjdump-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Win/clang-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Win/clang-tidy-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Win/clang-win-runtime-library-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Win/clangd-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Win/llvm-code-coverage-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz,Win/llvmobjdump-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79-1.tar.xz\n    * src/third_party/llvm-libc/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/llvm/llvm-project/libc.git/+log/74407cd399..ebba81a8e2\n    * src/third_party/openh264/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/cisco/openh264/+log/9547f96ea5..1bca62311e\n    * src/third_party/perfetto: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/google/perfetto.git/+log/594af1c30f..0ffe7d1e13\n    * src/third_party/r8/cipd: P7Pq70iaBKGCBVqKGS1XPUFyG7yWFSBWVy7yOBsghLcC..3J6GXbaAOLdywagRZSV4xGbqfUQccHCDuQsWU941ObsC\n    * src/third_party/rust-toolchain: Linux_x64/rust-toolchain-1edd55dcfcd573872c727fa3e086369a71661ee0-1125-llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b.tar.xz,Mac/rust-toolchain-1edd55dcfcd573872c727fa3e086369a71661ee0-1125-llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b.tar.xz,Mac_arm64/rust-toolchain-1edd55dcfcd573872c727fa3e086369a71661ee0-1125-llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b.tar.xz,Win/rust-toolchain-1edd55dcfcd573872c727fa3e086369a71661ee0-1125-llvmorg-24-init-7747-g62397f8b.tar.xz..Linux_x64/rust-toolchain-8a9dd7abdf013ec10cfeaaa3685feba18ef1c90c-1-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79.tar.xz,Mac/rust-toolchain-8a9dd7abdf013ec10cfeaaa3685feba18ef1c90c-1-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79.tar.xz,Mac_arm64/rust-toolchain-8a9dd7abdf013ec10cfeaaa3685feba18ef1c90c-1-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79.tar.xz,Win/rust-toolchain-8a9dd7abdf013ec10cfeaaa3685feba18ef1c90c-1-llvmorg-24-init-14453-ge063be79.tar.xz\n    * src/third_party/tflite/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow.git/+log/35746aec16..201e0b2f5e\n    * src/third_party/turbine/cipd: PpirAriY9g7xvoA-fAEt4KU9CpbuQIBVgRha8lY_N3IC..dUkwEFWxZhv6ER7jQDD8KlEtrh2sfMlIZzlP2TdVYVkC\n    * src/third_party/xnnpack/src: https://chromium.googlesource.com/external/github.com/google/XNNPACK.git/+log/5d067b8f52..49ac6bffa2\n    * src/tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/tools/+log/950096b4af..7e44902fdf\n    DEPS diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/1cb7357a22..b1ff7dbb45/DEPS\n\n    BUG=None\n\n    Change-Id: Idb3c3a2d3ed536f3776421e7ef8abaf21a484bf7\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510840\n    Auto-Submit: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Ilya Nikolaevskiy \u003cilnik@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49036}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "3fbd367846286c8ed54c902a356e8287a7790a0b", "git_parents": ["a9bc62234174aae1aa85a93fb0b42c7dd43ecd19"], "node": "3772a81fadc3ccb7345dd82cb1fdfad6ecbd0722", "parents": ["f3b90fdaea40c47a0289dfe90fcac4da1edc35de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 1f05919e94\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/1f05919e949e0472732c1403a66f7ae0b2c49538\n    Reland \"Batch SDP candidates and O(1) TransportInfo lookup\"\n\n    This is a reland of commit b38573bb56e571405b318c761c23a5b247d24716\n\n    The key change for the reland is the addition of a call to\n    `RelinquishThreadOwnership` which was needed for the the chromium code.\n    A btw change is also to use by-ref instead of by-pointer for passing the\n    ice candidate collection in a few places.\n\n    Original change's description:\n    \u003e Batch SDP candidates and O(1) TransportInfo lookup\n    \u003e\n    \u003e SdpDeserialize added candidates one at a time with AddCandidate(), which\n    \u003e looks up the m= section, copies the candidate and recomputes the\n    \u003e connection address on every call. SdpSerialize copied the candidates of\n    \u003e each m= section and looked up its TransportInfo by name.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Now the parser fills one IceCandidateCollection per m= section and\n    \u003e passes them to SessionDescriptionInterface::Create(), which updates each\n    \u003e section's connection address once. The serializer reads the candidate\n    \u003e collections directly and tries the TransportInfo at the same index\n    \u003e before falling back to a lookup by name.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e BM_Sdp* benchmarks (release build, median of 5 runs):\n    \u003e - Deserialize: -2.9% (small), -4.6% (large)\n    \u003e - Serialize: -3.7% (small), -12.2% (large)\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Bug: none\n    \u003e Change-Id: I04eae8cab5870cf60708cea9668cc147807ba176\n    \u003e Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509664\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49014}\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: I3cd9eafe705695ae438509e38e26c0c1ab755351\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510960\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49037}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/jsep.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/jsep.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/webrtc_sdp.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/webrtc_sdp_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/jsep_session_description_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "27cedfba7be95ad6a6c7038f8fa0ea1fd58da68e", "git_parents": ["3fbd367846286c8ed54c902a356e8287a7790a0b"], "node": "a350d1cd5bd6f9504ed492283dd3e8b6ce01ebd7", "parents": ["3772a81fadc3ccb7345dd82cb1fdfad6ecbd0722"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 0346b7660a\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/0346b7660aa456879871f0bdcb5f4036bd462b29\n    Clean up distrusted certificate helpers\n\n    Follow-up to https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510761:\n\n    - Move the ContainsDistrustedCertificate overloads from\n      openssl_adapter.cc into webrtc::openssl in openssl_utility, alongside\n      IsDistrustedCertificate, and add unit tests.\n    - Fold the EVP_Digest call in GetSpkiSha256 into the\n      OPENSSL_IS_BORINGSSL preprocessor branches so that the non-BoringSSL\n      spki_data buffer is allocated and freed within the same block.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:576525998\n    Change-Id: Ib233d61cbd63ef31c194a1e6f07e4e545293370c\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510901\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49038}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/openssl_adapter.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/openssl_utility.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/openssl_utility.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/openssl_utility_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "20dc59cb15e8cd655f4b9bffdcd75b3b8d0af76c", "git_parents": ["27cedfba7be95ad6a6c7038f8fa0ea1fd58da68e"], "node": "b3514d3fdd7ad8be8330e0b47abe9acca39731c4", "parents": ["a350d1cd5bd6f9504ed492283dd3e8b6ce01ebd7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from d2ddb03481\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/d2ddb034812732cad978e40a06a80240cc0fc02e\n    Fix dangling queue_factory pointer in scream_test\n\n    In CreateNetworkPathWithVaryingCapacity, queue_factory was declared inside the if (use_ecn) block, causing SchedulableNetworkNodeBuilder::Build() to dereference a dangling pointer after the block scope ended.\n\n    Bug: b/574966174\n    Change-Id: Ibed158cad07261d6e036f90d2e08e4f3a85f5bba\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510941\n    Auto-Submit: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49039}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/peer_scenario/bwe_integration_tests/scream_test.cc"], "git_node": "14d0e6f57754da7c1b58a5329822f9da8f852c81", "git_parents": ["20dc59cb15e8cd655f4b9bffdcd75b3b8d0af76c"], "node": "99457ff7265049b9c475e8b398a75d0ecae53e1f", "parents": ["b3514d3fdd7ad8be8330e0b47abe9acca39731c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 443994f307\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/443994f307caf34450e93f300b0a7bd8ed9dcd87\n    pc: keep offering mandatory header extensions after negotiation\n\n    With header extension negotiation memory, a remote answer or offer\n    that did not negotiate MID marked it as stopped in\n      GetHeaderExtensionsToNegotiate().\n\n    A subsequent\n      SetHeaderExtensionsToNegotiate()\n    then rejected the unmodified result of the getter, and new transceivers\n    inherited the stopped state.\n\n    MID is mandatory to implement per RFC 8834 section 5.2.4 so keep it as\n    sendrecv in the extensions to negotiate. GetNegotiatedHeaderExtensions()\n    still reports it as stopped.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:576082210\n    Change-Id: I841d1d445ae2d730640248d890656ccd95fc4571\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510620\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Markus Handell \u003chandellm@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49040}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_header_extension_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_transceiver.cc"], "git_node": "56ecb3feef076141163efcfb4ab2ec961d1d0302", "git_parents": ["14d0e6f57754da7c1b58a5329822f9da8f852c81"], "node": "a114e1eab1034950a3a9f8a4276c3f8159ea19a8", "parents": ["99457ff7265049b9c475e8b398a75d0ecae53e1f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 67ec81eed3\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/67ec81eed3226988cacb266001426da6806a2acb\n    Increase svc_tests shards from 4 to 8 on desktop and Fuchsia\n\n    svc_tests already runs on 8 shards in android_tests and\n    ios_simulator_tests, but was still configured with 4 shards in\n    desktop_tests and fuchsia_compatible_tests. With AV1 and H.264 SVC\n    test additions, total shard runtime has grown to ~70m on linux_tsan2\n    (18.6m per shard), ~55m on linux_msan (14.7m per shard), and ~46m on\n    fuchsia_rel (12.9m per shard), making svc_tests the critical-path test\n    suite on those bots.\n\n    Doubling the shard count to 8 matches mobile and cuts the per-shard\n    wall time in half.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:575920311\n    Change-Id: Id20731ad54360e48cae5047ae1ed783b729e3424\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/511060\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49041}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/specs/client.webrtc.json", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/specs/test_suites.pyl", "third_party/libwebrtc/infra/specs/tryserver.webrtc.json"], "git_node": "bb3985f81b11327c96190adad8c173132ab21fc3", "git_parents": ["56ecb3feef076141163efcfb4ab2ec961d1d0302"], "node": "8f9f892e26e6f5a1d06be96b9ecc46a60d890190", "parents": ["a114e1eab1034950a3a9f8a4276c3f8159ea19a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 47e0e0a16f\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/47e0e0a16fe101e47d2ef393ecc3dcd36ded3311\n    Support high precision in TaskQueueGcd delayed tasks\n\n    TaskQueueGcd previously ignored PostDelayedTaskTraits::high_precision\n    and scheduled all delayed tasks with dispatch_after_f(), which is\n    subject to OS timer coalescing (up to 100 ms under background policy).\n\n    Schedule high-precision delayed tasks using a one-shot\n    DISPATCH_TIMER_STRICT timer source with leeway capped at 1 ms. Low-\n    precision tasks continue to use dispatch_after_f().\n\n    Bug: webrtc:470337728\n    Change-Id: Iafd6b1296d6bcd2446c3fade1f624907128e684a\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510942\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Markus Handell \u003chandellm@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49042}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/task_queue/task_queue_test.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0052.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0083.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0085.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0086.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0099.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/task_queue_gcd.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/task_queue_gcd_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "8697214d116c6164cdacc679310c8e92498af62e", "git_parents": ["bb3985f81b11327c96190adad8c173132ab21fc3"], "node": "16da17fa73e4a8845788aa77658965a57e69e497", "parents": ["8f9f892e26e6f5a1d06be96b9ecc46a60d890190"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from ab1f920f50\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/ab1f920f500914252276b0d4f04b0e49aa5e3986\n    Migrate LogTest to LoggingConfig\n\n    InitializeLogging() succeeds only once per process, so the logging\n    initialization tests ran as EXPECT_EXIT death tests and relied on a\n    WEBRTC_TEST_SKIP_LOGGING_INIT environment variable in\n    TestMainImpl::Init(). The other LogTest tests used legacy static setters\n    such as AddLogToStream(), SetLogQueueNames() and the deprecated\n    LogThreads().\n\n    - Add ResetLoggingForTesting(). It swaps the active LoggingConfig for a\n      default one and lets the next InitializeLogging() call succeed, or\n      restores a previously saved config. The test-only state is only read\n      by InitializeLogging(), so the per-message logging path is unchanged.\n    - Convert LogTest to a fixture that saves and restores the config set up\n      by TestMainImpl::Init() and logs through LoggingConfig sinks. Remove\n      the death tests, the environment variable, a duplicate queue name test\n      and ImplicitInitialization, which cannot run in-process and whose\n      death-test version passed regardless.\n    - Filter LoggingConfig sinks by LoggingConfig::min_severity(). They were\n      filtered by LogSink::min_severity_, which only AddLogToStream() sets,\n      so config sinks always used LS_INFO and kept the global threshold at\n      LS_INFO or lower.\n    - Log the --verbose warning in TestMainImpl::Init() after\n      InitializeLogging(). Logging it first triggered implicit\n      initialization in debug builds, so the logging flags were ignored.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42234107\n    Change-Id: Icd992a3e1d0e252df09ccf52609ff91106eecd97\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510041\n    Reviewed-by: Fredrik Solenberg \u003csolenberg@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49043}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0052.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0083.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0085.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0086.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0099.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/logging.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/logging.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/logging_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/test_main_lib.cc"], "git_node": "a42dee35ecb08ca1a64cd7a89013dca3475b5f27", "git_parents": ["8697214d116c6164cdacc679310c8e92498af62e"], "node": "e6206a331fc7b34f4cef02ba3d0b72c92a4bdf31", "parents": ["16da17fa73e4a8845788aa77658965a57e69e497"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 3dec7d0537\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/3dec7d05377fb690e84f503db865edde982ab2a5\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-10-24T04:07:00).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: Ie7791ca2c3a6264bc09137d356c29738ea74cad9\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/511120\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49044}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "2e89b798c082717813a77688a5cb87c379e869cb", "git_parents": ["a42dee35ecb08ca1a64cd7a89013dca3475b5f27"], "node": "5294d26ee1bb88707d9ac4d202bb09ce54899851", "parents": ["e6206a331fc7b34f4cef02ba3d0b72c92a4bdf31"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 659d2c5204\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/659d2c520432d033769a0f0472e89234260a824d\n    Remove SequenceChecker from IceCandidateCollection\n\n    IceCandidateCollection is a plain container owned by\n    SessionDescriptionInterface, which already guards the collections with\n    its own sequence checker. The per-collection checker is redundant, and\n    it forces every collection to be detached from the thread that filled it\n    before a description can be used on another thread, e.g. when Chromium\n    parses SDP on the main thread and uses the description on the signaling\n    thread. SessionDescriptionInterface no longer has to do that in its\n    constructor and in RelinquishThreadOwnership().\n\n    IceCandidateCollection::RelinquishThreadOwnership() is now a deprecated\n    no-op. There are no known callers outside of WebRTC, but it's kept for\n    now so that downstream code keeps compiling. Callers can simply drop the\n    call.\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: I815f97ed45afb3abaebfb16870531ead72fa4a9d\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/511180\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49045}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/jsep.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/jsep.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/jsep_ice_candidate.cc"], "git_node": "e350bad0619ab32502ad72c4027f8c08a1f9feff", "git_parents": ["2e89b798c082717813a77688a5cb87c379e869cb"], "node": "83e29e9bc71b7431a99c582096c8ccce5a1c4f3b", "parents": ["5294d26ee1bb88707d9ac4d202bb09ce54899851"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 83de8057df\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/83de8057df74f225a85c045413aae01398b65c06\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-10-25T04:03:18).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: Ib9e560445bf988f5c427489f4ca300fbfe241f93\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/511200\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49046}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "97edfc0d61b2887270c8820c55463dc80e4c4b24", "git_parents": ["e350bad0619ab32502ad72c4027f8c08a1f9feff"], "node": "145d77d994056a4b6d3cba68dc5b321b70458983", "parents": ["83e29e9bc71b7431a99c582096c8ccce5a1c4f3b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from b675bf63d3\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/b675bf63d3a0164affbf932a19cb1867d0611074\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-10-26T04:06:31).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I6f0064b6e21a94e072deb899932eaa90490e2423\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/511240\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49047}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "25e19dababc9f6258315338523a3c4c10be00d6a", "git_parents": ["97edfc0d61b2887270c8820c55463dc80e4c4b24"], "node": "faf476897824e9d64496b7e79738c20a8fe76820", "parents": ["145d77d994056a4b6d3cba68dc5b321b70458983"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from d18a4f7621\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/d18a4f7621dd4fdae6314084aa541d4f19cbb90a\n    Add per-packet Sframe encryption to the video send path\n\n    Support Sframe per-packet mode in RTPSenderVideo, which so far dropped\n    frames when the Sframe encryptor was configured for it.\n\n    In per-packet mode the frame is packetized by the codec packetizer as\n    usual and the payload of every packet is encrypted on its own. The\n    packetizer limits are reduced by the Sframe descriptor and by the\n    encryption overhead (Sframe header and authentication tag), so the\n    encrypted payload fits into the packet. Each packet's payload is\n    replaced by the Sframe ciphertext and PacketizeSframeRtpPacketOrError()\n    prepends the descriptor with the T bit set; the S and E bits come from\n    the packet's position in the frame. The marker bit is still set by the\n    codec packetizer. Encryption happens before RED encapsulation and FEC,\n    which therefore protect the encrypted payload.\n\n    Packets are only enqueued after the whole frame has been processed, so\n    an encryption failure on any packet drops the entire frame.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:479862368\n    Change-Id: I14e2fca6a419dc4c234d0a960d5bc80dea5a69ba\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509360\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Kacper Wasniowski \u003ckwasniow@cisco.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49048}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_sender_video.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_sender_video.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_sender_video_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "d0c3de2c1409a59e773392dfc797e70d52c5b27d", "git_parents": ["25e19dababc9f6258315338523a3c4c10be00d6a"], "node": "1a77e0f9a2f594e8cb7fec09ef550ff396ca63eb", "parents": ["faf476897824e9d64496b7e79738c20a8fe76820"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from f670aa3e96\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/f670aa3e9649c18a1a7118e93ed280cd723cb224\n    Propagate Sframe requirement to the audio RTP send path\n\n    Carries the Sframe send options recorded on the voice send channel down\n    to the audio send stream and into ChannelSend, so that a channel marked\n    as requiring Sframe drops audio frames until an Sframe encryptor is\n    wired up. This is the audio counterpart of the equivalent video CL.\n\n    Flow:\n    - WebRtcVoiceSendChannel::EnableSframe() now fans sframe_options_ out to\n      every send stream (previously a TODO placeholder), and returns early\n      when the requirement is already set.\n    - WebRtcVoiceSendChannel::AddSendStream() seeds newly created streams\n      with the current sframe_options_, so streams added after negotiation\n      also observe the requirement.\n    - WebRtcAudioSendStream::UpdateSframeOptions() stores the options in the\n      stream config and reconfigures the stream.\n    - AudioSendStream::ConfigureStream() forwards changed options to\n      ChannelSend::SetSframeOptions().\n    - ChannelSend::SendRtpAudio() fails closed on a required-but-unwired\n      stream.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:479862368\n    Change-Id: I51f01c9e60be16b725756062831bdf07e3efcb18\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/507541\n    Commit-Queue: Kacper Wasniowski \u003ckwasniow@cisco.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49049}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/audio_send_stream.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/audio_send_stream_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/channel_send.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/channel_send.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/channel_send_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/audio/mock_voe_channel_proxy.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/audio_send_stream.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/audio_send_stream.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/sframe_options.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_voice_engine.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/webrtc_voice_engine_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/sframe/sframe_encryption_config.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0029.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0069.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch"], "git_node": "82fd0012441eb2104dd30c96e323e03a11f25c8b", "git_parents": ["d0c3de2c1409a59e773392dfc797e70d52c5b27d"], "node": "3f90ba75523bd567f2107be6a95bb2a5fe8a728d", "parents": ["1a77e0f9a2f594e8cb7fec09ef550ff396ca63eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 04a9c30194\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/04a9c30194cb39c93120b974547ed25b73d116d0\n    Remove the may_use_cache parameter of GetParametersInternal()\n\n    All callers use the cache since GetParameters() does.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42222804\n    Change-Id: Iad90962598c4262b3599141b4de6c69cddc91df5\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509680\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49050}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtc_stats_collector.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtc_stats_collector_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_transceiver.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_transceiver_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/mock_rtp_sender_internal.h"], "git_node": "2cf2f0b0c9a4e438f1f0f626590ead63e30b0b7f", "git_parents": ["82fd0012441eb2104dd30c96e323e03a11f25c8b"], "node": "316efae3468112b77df4b96d0ef389679ed7d19a", "parents": ["3f90ba75523bd567f2107be6a95bb2a5fe8a728d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 95cc77e5bd\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/95cc77e5bd439f16611880947bbf8f09133fc4fd\n    Call DataChannel test observers on network thread\n\n    Make the SctpDataChannel tests and the PeerConnection integration tests\n    exercise network thread callbacks, the path Chrome uses. Delivery on the\n    signaling thread via ObserverAdapter keeps dedicated test coverage.\n    MockDataChannelObserver's test callbacks still run on the signaling\n    thread.\n\n    Also fix MaxMessageSizePropagated, which waited on the wrong observer.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:510487699\n    Change-Id: I26640799fba481d86bbcacac010ccc4261e90d50\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509062\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49051}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_end_to_end_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sctp_data_channel_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/integration_test_helpers.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/mock_peer_connection_observers.h"], "git_node": "756fa97deee32505106762c263edafe3312df008", "git_parents": ["2cf2f0b0c9a4e438f1f0f626590ead63e30b0b7f"], "node": "e9d003f2b2daed77fb001f569ffba470d6004a3c", "parents": ["316efae3468112b77df4b96d0ef389679ed7d19a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 28807683a6\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/28807683a65c9cc38ccf4b211e259c003ac113ea\n    Keep the RtpSender parameter cache populated after SetSend()\n\n    Read the parameters back after SetAudioSend()/SetVideoSend() and when\n    the sender is attached to a send stream, instead of leaving the cache\n    empty until the next GetParameters() call fills it with a blocking call.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:42222804\n    Change-Id: Icdb71e2a275dcd9eca13dfd856a369721102e550\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/509700\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49052}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtp_sender_receiver_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "369c1362b644ab93e89075fc390a4ba6dd85bd9d", "git_parents": ["756fa97deee32505106762c263edafe3312df008"], "node": "64c3797f7305cffe271c6de420ccfb496e5b0dc4", "parents": ["e9d003f2b2daed77fb001f569ffba470d6004a3c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 0b58cbb30c\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/0b58cbb30c3fcb48c623670b026d94476b052405\n    Give the Plan B legacy stats tests their own Plan B fake\n\n    The Plan B legacy stats tests depend on the Plan B methods of\n    FakePeerConnectionForStats: AddSender() and AddReceiver() put any number\n    of senders and receivers on one transceiver per media type. Before the\n    shared fake moves to Unified Plan transceivers, the Plan B test file\n    needs a fake of its own, so that no Plan B code has to stay in the\n    shared one.\n\n    Add FakePlanBPeerConnectionForStats to\n    legacy_stats_collector_plan_b_unittest.cc. It creates Plan B\n    transceivers and implements AddSender(), RemoveSender() and\n    AddReceiver() with the *PlanB methods of RtpTransceiver. Its\n    AddVoiceChannel() and AddVideoChannel() make sure that the channel goes\n    on that transceiver, GetSenders() and GetReceivers() list senders and\n    receivers the Plan B way, and IsUnifiedPlan() returns false.\n    FakePeerConnectionForStats gets protected hooks for this.\n\n    StatsCollectorTrackPlanBTest::CreatePeerConnection() returns the new\n    fake, so the test bodies are unchanged.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:470300031\n    Change-Id: Ia8ce6848db660d9d4f6826812e49fa8fe01a7c12\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/508431\n    Reviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49053}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/legacy_stats_collector_plan_b_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/test/fake_peer_connection_for_stats.h"], "git_node": "3127efb6d165ff08b88811745368b02b893b5cff", "git_parents": ["369c1362b644ab93e89075fc390a4ba6dd85bd9d"], "node": "9343be7b327b970f0ffc691af944ec74c6c71122", "parents": ["64c3797f7305cffe271c6de420ccfb496e5b0dc4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from 3af9f8e985\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/3af9f8e98535968eda6b141718c0e505d24667e2\n    Fix IPv4 ECN reception on macOS/iOS in PhysicalSocket\n\n    When IP_RECVTOS is enabled on an IPv4 socket, Linux delivers the\n    ancillary header in recvmsg() with cmsg_type == IP_TOS, whereas\n    macOS/iOS uses cmsg_type == IP_RECVTOS. Check IP_RECVTOS on macOS/iOS\n    and IP_TOS on other POSIX platforms when parsing IPPROTO_IP ancillary\n    messages, and enable PhysicalSocketTest.TestSocketSendRecvWithEcnIPv4 on\n    macOS/iOS.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:15368\n    Change-Id: I6d52b399eba0a8878fa93ef8ee3459a853c4232c\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/511280\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49054}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0009.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0010.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/physical_socket_server.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/physical_socket_server_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "dafcbe0e952fc77e67cda833109276a7e5f2fdcc", "git_parents": ["3127efb6d165ff08b88811745368b02b893b5cff"], "node": "9a9911cdaf90e17ea293aa1be4d65b101fe14035", "parents": ["9343be7b327b970f0ffc691af944ec74c6c71122"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086269 - Vendor libwebrtc from bd3d2d3150. IGNORE BAD COMMIT MESSAGES\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/bd3d2d31501d3acabd9bd54a7bb1f615f6e1345b\n    Reserve the RTC_LOG message buffer up front\n\n    Formatting an RTC_LOG message grew the buffer step by step as the\n    arguments were appended, reallocating several times for long arguments\n    such as SDPs.\n\n    - Store a compile-time estimate of the message size in the first element\n      of the LogArgType array that LogStreamer passes to Log(): the exact\n      length of string literals plus estimates for numbers and pointers.\n    - Log() adds the sizes of std::string and string view arguments and\n      reserves the buffer through the new LogMessage::ReserveStream().\n    - Select the MakeVal() overload for string arguments with ranked\n      overloads (https://abseil.io/tips/229), so that string literals\n      provide their exact length.\n\n    Median time and heap allocations per call, with one sink:\n\n      BM_RtcLogLiteralsAndNumbers  276 ns -\u003e 257 ns, 3 -\u003e 2\n      BM_RtcLogMixedStrings        280 ns -\u003e 245 ns, 4 -\u003e 2\n      BM_RtcLogSdp/1  (1.4 KB)     310 ns -\u003e 284 ns, 4 -\u003e 2\n      BM_RtcLogSdp/16 (20.6 KB)    865 ns -\u003e 851 ns, 4 -\u003e 2\n\n    Bug: none\n    Change-Id: I62dbb2d56545aad8803d17c942b1d75abe8f1d77\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/510000\n    Commit-Queue: Tomas Gunnarsson \u003ctommi@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#49055}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0001.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/logging.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/logging.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/logging_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "a9a644f66adb0cbb132f042bb7df24032f56346a", "git_parents": ["dafcbe0e952fc77e67cda833109276a7e5f2fdcc"], "node": "3b0e7a18530e47dba0c56e2440d8f1fc4d5847fa", "parents": ["9a9911cdaf90e17ea293aa1be4d65b101fe14035"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794445450, "git_changesets": ["e8401047e4c248b83a98c13ea7442b9c1a34572a", "a4a6508c4fffd10cbc1f148b0178ed077053d546", "118d84a0aa2f32bbb23bd240d7d9d1adac92f75d", "8b3a0fe52c1d8d91a1f06caeda905887c1ac967b", "1adead6f8475ef0cdb28ca45ec4e5d3b828a4a83", "812af487c465b2129f4a45774c2b97195c35e7a2", "bb9641b070e3f453e765ac24bd50cd87791ca870", "f7d67e4003a84aa45ea85d286edece54f5672b58", "09764c67f111739d527ef8c6614a844756d8dbb1", "7bc17fa3707019ec0df563903c847f68e6588fdf", "de39e7f77e3