35161dcdc76ee3240b93\nml -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nmr -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nms -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nmy -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nnb-NO -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nne-NP -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nnl -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nnn-NO -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\noc -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\npa-IN -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\npl -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\npt-BR -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\npt-PT -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nrm -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nro -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nru -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nsk -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nsl -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nson -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nsq -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nsr -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nsv-SE -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nta -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nte -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nth -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\ntl -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\ntr -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\ntrs -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nuk -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nur -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nuz -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nvi -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nwo -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nxh -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nzam -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nzh-CN -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\nzh-TW -\u003e 8486a0949983ae20a44335161dcdc76ee3240b93\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "2741a0aa2b89543edc27871d9136252b0c1551a8", "git_parents": ["dfbdcca977929284e9bcab7742ec87d16c53dd61"], "node": "9ed7177715b7d5cfe5f9df225656e6cd5d3fffd1", "parents": ["df48eab485ea91d73c5594167d75f0c0bea56ed9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mayank Bansal \u003cmayankleoboy1@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092174 - Track Http3Session slow-consumer queue membership with a flag. r=necko-reviewers,jesup\n\nConnectSlowConsumer could queue a stream more than once, while\nRemoveStreamFromQueues only removed its first entry, so a closed stream could\nstay queued and be read again. An IsInRxQueue() flag now dedupes the queue and\nlets RemoveStreamFromQueues skip scanning it for streams that are not queued.\nThe queue becomes a deque so ProcessSlowConsumers pops in constant time.\n\nA stream that asks to be read several times before it is processed is now read\nonce, as in Http2Session.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342245\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/Http3Session.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3Session.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3StreamBase.h"], "git_node": "62778d6ec116fe8df13d65f78c08897c3e3be0c0", "git_parents": ["2741a0aa2b89543edc27871d9136252b0c1551a8"], "node": "c82c1fb35d67d6c42d9cfaf0dbaa89f7b6030de6", "parents": ["9ed7177715b7d5cfe5f9df225656e6cd5d3fffd1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daisuke Akatsuka \u003cdaisuke@birchill.co.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090808 - Fix a11y-checks failures when opening the urlbar result context menu in test r=urlbar-reviewers,daleharvey\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342161\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-editing/browser_urlbar_contextmenu.js"], "git_node": "630cef3c53aae859f6f593b4e978e78135cce185", "git_parents": ["62778d6ec116fe8df13d65f78c08897c3e3be0c0"], "node": "0d8ff3f82099db009ebc66ede0c51b93cc8802cc", "parents": ["c82c1fb35d67d6c42d9cfaf0dbaa89f7b6030de6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073932 [Linux] Don't listen on org.freedesktop.UPower when dom.battery.enabled if off r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341382\n", "files": ["hal/linux/UPowerClient.cpp"], "git_node": "804fcbed8fd6ff7389441f61fc5a110f58656afd", "git_parents": ["630cef3c53aae859f6f593b4e978e78135cce185"], "node": "da6ef6bd5d3c33e16be9d875bde914cdc6aa4f3e", "parents": ["0d8ff3f82099db009ebc66ede0c51b93cc8802cc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "AndiAJ \u003candiaj@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092099 - Create a new search downloads related regression UI tests r=aaronmt,android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nThe UI test successfully passed 25x on Firebase \u2705\nAll UI tests successfully passed 1x on Firebase \u2705\n\n\u2757 The test tag addition will need to be reviewed by someone from the development team\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342156\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/DownloadsSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/DownloadTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/downloads/listscreen/DownloadsListTestTag.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/downloads/listscreen/ui/DownloadSearchField.kt"], "git_node": "d0e6d385f9fa468e85927a87ca866c0605df3d2f", "git_parents": ["804fcbed8fd6ff7389441f61fc5a110f58656afd"], "node": "eaf9b135e34621073a70feb73232085bd78b2f0c", "parents": ["da6ef6bd5d3c33e16be9d875bde914cdc6aa4f3e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092029 - Clean up dom.element.popoverhint.enabled flag r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342101\n", "files": ["accessible/tests/browser/caching_granularity/browser.toml", "accessible/tests/browser/relations/browser.toml", "dom/html/nsGenericHTMLElement.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/popovers/__dir__.ini"], "git_node": "9559f3eef34ae16de11b7c8503ef922ba9a077b3", "git_parents": ["d0e6d385f9fa468e85927a87ca866c0605df3d2f"], "node": "f3aa8b299e96de66b2cffdde950b0df5e4eafe2a", "parents": ["eaf9b135e34621073a70feb73232085bd78b2f0c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092025 - Clean up dom.element.dialog.request_close.enabled flag r=webidl,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342098\n", "files": ["dom/webidl/HTMLDialogElement.webidl", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/interactive-elements/the-dialog-element/dialog-requestclose.html.ini"], "git_node": "70cf0319a989f305a784469b7c9f9f3fc27f1294", "git_parents": ["9559f3eef34ae16de11b7c8503ef922ba9a077b3"], "node": "21277a8610db9f586500ba9b6abcb1f93d72a772", "parents": ["f3aa8b299e96de66b2cffdde950b0df5e4eafe2a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092259 - Move the native cursor away from the selection menu after the native click in browser_chat_shortcuts.js, r=mlucks.\n\nOtherwise, on Windows, test_selection_callout_link_opens_more_actions can lose\nits synthesized hover on the callout link when the file runs a second time in\nthe same browser.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342337\n", "files": ["browser/components/genai/tests/browser/browser_chat_shortcuts.js"], "git_node": "c185a546ab3d09dcc39fd6c9c1f931bd3e09ab7c", "git_parents": ["70cf0319a989f305a784469b7c9f9f3fc27f1294"], "node": "e080aea929f46e6fc250241b4e9f90e44eaf69cd", "parents": ["21277a8610db9f586500ba9b6abcb1f93d72a772"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092068 - Reset the server state of the bug 1716290 charset tests once the forced detection reload is served, r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug.\n\nThe .sjs state survived the test, so a second run served the post-detection response on its first load. The verify-standalone skip-if (bug 1995208) failed the same way.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342141\n", "files": ["docshell/test/browser/browser.toml", "docshell/test/browser/file_bug1716290-1.sjs", "docshell/test/browser/file_bug1716290-2.sjs", "docshell/test/browser/file_bug1716290-3.sjs", "docshell/test/browser/file_bug1716290-4.sjs"], "git_node": "1fbf48e6158c8d4b86e9340a9b0f9d6039610dea", "git_parents": ["c185a546ab3d09dcc39fd6c9c1f931bd3e09ab7c"], "node": "e5f28fb5b65cd4fff184d92505ab3224abf1b87c", "parents": ["e080aea929f46e6fc250241b4e9f90e44eaf69cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092071 - Clear history after browser_bug420605.js and browser_bug503832.js so they pass when run again, r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug.\n\nBoth tests assert that their pages are not in history yet, but left the visits they recorded behind, so a second run in the same profile failed. This also lets them run in verify-standalone again.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342143\n", "files": ["docshell/test/browser/browser.toml", "docshell/test/browser/browser_bug420605.js", "docshell/test/browser/browser_bug503832.js"], "git_node": "fc496e6612c5206083b7143dc5b9685e1a932efb", "git_parents": ["1fbf48e6158c8d4b86e9340a9b0f9d6039610dea"], "node": "1eea795633b39b79296eb3088bd1c3c3ba55bfeb", "parents": ["e5f28fb5b65cd4fff184d92505ab3224abf1b87c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092283 - Clean up the installed manifest in browser_Manifest_install.js, r=daleharvey.\n\nThe test left its manifest installed: the cached Manifest object, its file in the profile, and its scope entry. The first Manifest object also still had a pending deferred save, which rewrote the file after the test ended, so finalize it instead of only saving it. This makes the test pass when run twice in the same browser and under verify-standalone, so remove the verify-standalone annotation from bug 1995208.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342345\n", "files": ["dom/manifest/test/browser.toml", "dom/manifest/test/browser_Manifest_install.js"], "git_node": "d8851dadbf5679da07fa0c4ec8334ebafa3ba8c5", "git_parents": ["fc496e6612c5206083b7143dc5b9685e1a932efb"], "node": "081fb065cf499e3429fd858fc6e6affce11633f3", "parents": ["1eea795633b39b79296eb3088bd1c3c3ba55bfeb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan Varga \u003cjvarga@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086032 - Fix the length of the base64 value Substring() in the CSP parser; r=tschuster\n\nnonceSource() and hashSource() take the base64 value after the dash with a\nlength of `expr.Length() - dashIndex + 1`, which is 2 too long and only worked\nbecause Substring() clamps it. Take it up to the end of the expression instead.\n\nNo functional change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341304\n", "files": ["dom/security/nsCSPParser.cpp"], "git_node": "cd15f179243b435a1d46bd379ed34a4c963ef1f2", "git_parents": ["d8851dadbf5679da07fa0c4ec8334ebafa3ba8c5"], "node": "3cb4e521856eb709e4b2537690f53be2ff4e317e", "parents": ["081fb065cf499e3429fd858fc6e6affce11633f3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090042 - Add `./mach theme` to run the token, contrast and pixel-diff tools. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,mach-reviewers,tgiles,ahochheiden\n\n`tokens` passes its arguments through because token names start with `--`; the other subcommands parse with the script's own parser, so `--help` lists its flags. contrast's and pairs' `--context` becomes `--realm`, the skills' word for chrome versus content, because mach passes its own `context` to every handler. pixel-diff's exception handler moved into run() so an error under mach still exits 2 rather than 1, which means the captures differ.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340511\n", "files": ["python/mach/mach/command_util.py", "toolkit/themes/tools/contrast.py", "toolkit/themes/tools/mach_commands.py", "toolkit/themes/tools/pair_walk.py", "toolkit/themes/tools/pixel_diff.py", "toolkit/themes/tools/screen-grab.py", "toolkit/themes/tools/token_resolve.py"], "git_node": "b379684cef5dbc43a4b2fedaa9880d6c7bc6c917", "git_parents": ["cd15f179243b435a1d46bd379ed34a4c963ef1f2"], "node": "ec0ea19774b4399fc9e301aa823d5919a8c43be8", "parents": ["3cb4e521856eb709e4b2537690f53be2ff4e317e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090042 - Point the desktop-theme skills at `./mach theme`. r=tgiles\n\nfirefox-probe.py's `--context` becomes `--realm` too, to match contrast and pairs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340512\n", "files": [".agents/skills/desktop-theme-colors/SKILL.md", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-colors/references/forced-color-filter.md", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-colors/references/system-color-pairs.md", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-layout/references/environment-sweep.md", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-probing/SKILL.md", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-probing/references/measuring-pixels.md", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-probing/references/probe-recipes.md", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-probing/references/probe-runner.md", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-probing/scripts/firefox-probe.py", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-probing/scripts/marker-probe.py", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-screenshots/SKILL.md", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-screenshots/scripts/capture-pair.sh", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-screenshots/scripts/capture.js", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-screenshots/scripts/zoom-pair.py", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-tokens/SKILL.md", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-tokens/references/nova-overrides.md", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-tokens/references/rem-roots.md", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-tokens/references/token-history.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-colors/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-colors/references/forced-color-filter.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-colors/references/system-color-pairs.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-layout/references/environment-sweep.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-probing/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-probing/references/measuring-pixels.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-probing/references/probe-recipes.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-probing/references/probe-runner.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-probing/scripts/firefox-probe.py", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-probing/scripts/marker-probe.py", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-screenshots/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-screenshots/scripts/capture-pair.sh", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-screenshots/scripts/capture.js", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-screenshots/scripts/zoom-pair.py", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-tokens/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-tokens/references/nova-overrides.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-tokens/references/rem-roots.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-tokens/references/token-history.md"], "git_node": "617af0daa85e81ad011f8ba5965761d5295ccd0c", "git_parents": ["b379684cef5dbc43a4b2fedaa9880d6c7bc6c917"], "node": "1cac99acfe53d0e9881593be3decf0cd1d5ff75c", "parents": ["ec0ea19774b4399fc9e301aa823d5919a8c43be8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090260 - Let desktop-theme-colors measure contrast without a build and over an OS-painted backdrop. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340487\n", "files": [".agents/skills/desktop-theme-colors/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-colors/SKILL.md", "toolkit/themes/tools/contrast.py"], "git_node": "5b335b0ed807414a4f81b8db6cc386f5c443826c", "git_parents": ["617af0daa85e81ad011f8ba5965761d5295ccd0c"], "node": "9b8b97ba30a77d1f0bc5e8e6eb99289e89665b8a", "parents": ["1cac99acfe53d0e9881593be3decf0cd1d5ff75c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090260 - Let desktop-theme-probing load test helpers in a probe, and fill its other setup gaps. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340489\n", "files": [".agents/skills/desktop-theme-probing/SKILL.md", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-probing/references/measuring-pixels.md", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-probing/references/platform-linux.md", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-probing/references/probe-recipes.md", ".agents/skills/desktop-theme-probing/references/probe-runner.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-probing/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-probing/references/measuring-pixels.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-probing/references/platform-linux.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-probing/references/probe-recipes.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-probing/references/probe-runner.md", "toolkit/themes/tools/probelib.py"], "git_node": "12b2fa15605de912b10c60e9c4e3ad1cc6979c73", "git_parents": ["5b335b0ed807414a4f81b8db6cc386f5c443826c"], "node": "d8f3a0a9c72c1b0d36723f720aa4a0a6182aff07", "parents": ["9b8b97ba30a77d1f0bc5e8e6eb99289e89665b8a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090260 - State `./mach theme pixel-diff`'s exit codes where desktop-theme-screenshots runs it. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340490\n", "files": [".agents/skills/desktop-theme-screenshots/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-screenshots/SKILL.md"], "git_node": "8faaa1d0404e0dbba8e3b54cae7a2adbef9c998c", "git_parents": ["12b2fa15605de912b10c60e9c4e3ad1cc6979c73"], "node": "14b43e2665684cb2a7ea2bc9fef4dadfee7b6981", "parents": ["d8f3a0a9c72c1b0d36723f720aa4a0a6182aff07"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonatan Wallmander \u003cjonatan.wallmander@kdab.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2025390 - WebGL: Refactor/add checks for attribute count r=nical\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339090\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLContext.cpp", "dom/canvas/WebGLContext.h", "dom/canvas/WebGLProgram.cpp", "dom/canvas/WebGLProgram.h", "dom/canvas/WebGLShader.cpp", "dom/canvas/WebGLShader.h"], "git_node": "1cbe250928427fdc3f3715c09117de8ea9d6b708", "git_parents": ["8faaa1d0404e0dbba8e3b54cae7a2adbef9c998c"], "node": "0ec2b7a8864371cbdef8e40c7dc5482da1da4da8", "parents": ["14b43e2665684cb2a7ea2bc9fef4dadfee7b6981"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080349 - Fix intermittent test_proxy_doesnt_respond timeout on Windows. r=necko-reviewers,jesup\n\nThe test set a 1s websocket open timeout, but on Windows a refused\nconnection to a closed localhost port can take longer than that to be\nreported, so the timeout fired first. It also guessed a closed port as\nproxy.port() + 1, which the websocket server could end up using.\nUse the default timeout and a port that was bound and then closed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341824\n", "files": ["netwerk/test/unit/test_websocket_fails.js"], "git_node": "909f91b01835bf6d8895c2ba07d0466c4557ac32", "git_parents": ["1cbe250928427fdc3f3715c09117de8ea9d6b708"], "node": "5ae23b9ace084d51160c56b1cae31d6f93c73d4d", "parents": ["0ec2b7a8864371cbdef8e40c7dc5482da1da4da8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ignat Remizov \u003cignat@ignatremizov.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053470 - Bound synthesized X11 startup times to the server clock. r=stransky,gtk-reviewers\n\nQuery the X server clock through GDK's existing group-leader window, normalize future window user times against that timestamp, and select the latest time using wrapping ages relative to that reference. Preserve zero as the no-user-time sentinel and restore the group leader's event mask after the query.\n\nKeep the production changes in WidgetUtilsGtk and add GTK/X11 regression tests to Firefox's existing GTest build, including timestamps around wraparound.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341828\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/WidgetUtilsGtk.cpp", "widget/gtk/WidgetUtilsGtk.h", "widget/tests/gtest/TestX11UserTime.cpp", "widget/tests/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "77e6f4ebc5b55fb0d6306b16608099a83d0ac161", "git_parents": ["909f91b01835bf6d8895c2ba07d0466c4557ac32"], "node": "45e7535306c342f85224a82e7713b1b8fa4b36fa", "parents": ["5ae23b9ace084d51160c56b1cae31d6f93c73d4d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Corentin Bect \u003ccbect@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092124 - Enable the pairing sign-in prompt by default on Nightly and Beta r=twhite\n\nPull request: https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/pull/444\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/nimbus.fml.yaml"], "git_node": "5716b3af951664d0c065111ed0bbb778da644767", "git_parents": ["77e6f4ebc5b55fb0d6306b16608099a83d0ac161"], "node": "1865ce95be243d1588210c25908f83a2b84ed218", "parents": ["45e7535306c342f85224a82e7713b1b8fa4b36fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2025390 - WebGL: Refactor/add checks for attribute count r=nical\" for causing webgl failures\n\nThis reverts commit 1cbe250928427fdc3f3715c09117de8ea9d6b708.\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLContext.cpp", "dom/canvas/WebGLContext.h", "dom/canvas/WebGLProgram.cpp", "dom/canvas/WebGLProgram.h", "dom/canvas/WebGLShader.cpp", "dom/canvas/WebGLShader.h"], "git_node": "57f8509487b793d69739a7e33c5bfad6baf3efa4", "git_parents": ["5716b3af951664d0c065111ed0bbb778da644767"], "node": "51227c406cb16c9d349700a0a02faa8aaac71e10", "parents": ["1865ce95be243d1588210c25908f83a2b84ed218"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052054 - Remove EARLY_BETA_OR_EARLIER. r=perftest-reviewers,necko-reviewers,mozperftest-reviewers,firefox-build-system-reviewers,spidermonkey-reviewers,linter-reviewers,ahal,ahochheiden,aglavic,valentin,jonco\n\nIt has been an alias for NIGHTLY_BUILD since bug 2052050 and no code reads it anymore. This also removes the\ndeprecated early-beta and late-beta --as-milestone aliases and adds a rejected-words lint to keep new uses\nfrom appearing.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342336\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/init.configure", "build/rust/mozbuild/generate_buildconfig.py", "docs/code-quality/lint/linters/test-manifest-toml.md", "docs/setup/configuring_build_options.md", "js/src/doc/feature_checklist.md", "js/src/frontend/ParseNodeVerify.h", "js/src/tests/jstests.py", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http2Session.cpp", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/mozinfo.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/configure/test_toolkit_moz_configure.py", "python/mozperftest/mozperftest/tests/data/mozinfo.json", "taskcluster/kinds/source-test/mozlint.yml", "testing/mozbase/manifestparser/manifestparser/token.py", "testing/perfdocs/generated/perf-sheriffing.md", "testing/performance/perf-sheriffing/perfdocs/index.md", "testing/web-platform/meta/wasm/jsapi/memory/constructor.any.js.ini", "toolkit/modules/AppConstants.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/moz.build", "tools/@types/subs/AppConstants.sys.d.mts", "tools/lint/rejected-words.yml"], "git_node": "2d34d593da83179cbc9c29ca04b2d79b03dc59be", "git_parents": ["57f8509487b793d69739a7e33c5bfad6baf3efa4"], "node": "0699e49d0efd653c23e1ed293462f21f0ed63a06", "parents": ["51227c406cb16c9d349700a0a02faa8aaac71e10"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anthony Frehner \u003cfrehner@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1988232 - Delegate focus from display: contents shadow hosts. r=edgar\n\nA display: contents shadow host has no frame, so GetTheFocusableArea and the mousedown focus loop gave up before reaching the delegatesFocus step. This broke focus(), label activation, form validation and clicks on shadow or slotted content.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340515\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsFocusManager.cpp", "dom/events/EventStateManager.cpp", "dom/tests/browser/browser_form_associated_custom_elements_validity.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/shadow-dom/focus/focus-delegatesFocus-display-contents.html"], "git_node": "dd2263d4d0dabf23c486bf7f8536d5e0f2cb08e7", "git_parents": ["2d34d593da83179cbc9c29ca04b2d79b03dc59be"], "node": "43bce9dd415f0519a31516f73704d9fdad8dd4ee", "parents": ["0699e49d0efd653c23e1ed293462f21f0ed63a06"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090279 - Don't trigger notifications during GC callback r=mccr8\n\nThe assertion added in bug 2076890 is failing because we're running script in\nan interrupted realm. The flow is as follows:\n\n 1. Allocation triggers GC\n 2. GC callback causes CC to finish ongoing CC\n 3. CC destroys some white objects\n 4. Destructors trigger notifications\n 5. Notification observers run script\n\nI should probably have realized that this could happen because allocation\ntriggering GC is a normal thing to happen, so any script run during the GC\ncallback will trigger this.\n\nThe patch aims to fix this by deferring notifications that happen during the\ndestruction of cycle collected objects. If there are other routes to running JS\nthen this will not be complete fix.\n\nThe patch adds a second way for notifications to be blocked in addition to\nscript blockers. (It is not possible to use a script blocker here because their\nscope would need to extend beyond the end of the GC.) Then notifications that\ncan be triggered from destructors are migrated to use NotifyWhenScriptSafe.\nWhen called during the GC callback this queues a runnable to trigger the\nnotification later.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341450\n", "files": ["docshell/base/BrowsingContext.cpp", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/nsJSEnvironment.cpp", "dom/events/EventStateManager.cpp", "dom/media/autoplay/GVAutoplayPermissionRequest.cpp", "dom/media/webaudio/AudioNode.cpp", "js/xpconnect/src/XPCJSRuntime.cpp", "toolkit/components/windowwatcher/nsWindowWatcher.cpp", "xpcom/base/CycleCollectedJSRuntime.cpp", "xpcom/base/CycleCollectedJSRuntime.h", "xpcom/base/nsCycleCollector.cpp", "xpcom/base/nsCycleCollector.h", "xpcom/components/nsComponentManager.cpp", "xpcom/ds/nsObserverService.cpp", "xpcom/ds/nsObserverService.h"], "git_node": "c0c9acf51e692551fd8bfb14f4b8624517458e23", "git_parents": ["dd2263d4d0dabf23c486bf7f8536d5e0f2cb08e7"], "node": "7f5d9baf39e298abbd89a5c64db52cba16a09a35", "parents": ["43bce9dd415f0519a31516f73704d9fdad8dd4ee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090260 - Make desktop-theme probes stop a stale build that never starts a Marionette session. r=ai4dev-reviewers,suhaib\n\nThe watch starts only after the Marionette constructor returns, so it never reads the previous run's log and never times the port wait; it also leaves a started session alone.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341173\n", "files": [".agents/skills/desktop-theme-probing/references/build-freshness.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-probing/references/build-freshness.md", "toolkit/themes/tools/probelib.py"], "git_node": "ee837bab9d5cdad7bd4a76a347facccfafe20ac3", "git_parents": ["c0c9acf51e692551fd8bfb14f4b8624517458e23"], "node": "4da163fd037061f58014c54a2fef4ebd948c3e9b", "parents": ["7f5d9baf39e298abbd89a5c64db52cba16a09a35"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andy Wingo \u003cwingo@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091678 - Use stack/malloc scratch space for BigInt division, bis r=mgaudet\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341735\n", "files": ["js/src/vm/BigIntType.cpp", "js/src/vm/BigIntType.h"], "git_node": "bd5bf972f0aaa2da249cf428c454516f6a60b4ba", "git_parents": ["ee837bab9d5cdad7bd4a76a347facccfafe20ac3"], "node": "56b924f5a03263d9fbfe927a86f94affe53e9e0e", "parents": ["4da163fd037061f58014c54a2fef4ebd948c3e9b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lars Eggert \u003clars@eggert.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092000 - Pass origin attributes and socket provider flags to TLSTransportLayer. r=necko-reviewers,jesup\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342115\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/TLSTransportLayer.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/TLSTransportLayer.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpConnection.cpp"], "git_node": "808ff50bb59476a15584f7684913ba754670fe02", "git_parents": ["bd5bf972f0aaa2da249cf428c454516f6a60b4ba"], "node": "c7486be8e5d888653fe0b7167ec988dfc1946c27", "parents": ["56b924f5a03263d9fbfe927a86f94affe53e9e0e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085128 - swipe-to-nav on touchscreen: Extract TouchSwipeState into separate files. r=hiro\n\nNo behavior change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340753\n", "files": ["widget/TouchSwipeState.cpp", "widget/TouchSwipeState.h", "widget/moz.build", "widget/nsIWidget.h"], "git_node": "cab176a72691b4eb0cbbc2cbd1a85e7e4f28b132", "git_parents": ["808ff50bb59476a15584f7684913ba754670fe02"], "node": "5348b74d809482cf50c4c320f18ee1cab83d85ec", "parents": ["c7486be8e5d888653fe0b7167ec988dfc1946c27"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085128 - swipe-to-nav on touchscreen: Split HandleTouchInputForSwipe out of DispatchTouchInput. r=hiro\n\nNo behavior change. The part of DispatchTouchInput that updates the\ntouch swipe state with an input APZ has handled moves to\nHandleTouchInputForSwipe().\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340754\n", "files": ["widget/nsIWidget.cpp", "widget/nsIWidget.h"], "git_node": "f2b976ee16a968258119e6bea4e0e2bbe16bf94f", "git_parents": ["cab176a72691b4eb0cbbc2cbd1a85e7e4f28b132"], "node": "07487bac6f807cb806249c70e4d56bb97ee55565", "parents": ["5348b74d809482cf50c4c320f18ee1cab83d85ec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085128 - swipe-to-nav on touchscreen: Add a path for APZ to notify the widget of the swipable directions later. r=hiro\n\nWhen APZ cannot tell the swipable directions synchronously on touchstart,\nit will need to tell the widget once it can. This adds\nGeckoContentController::NotifyTouchSwipeResult and a callback that\nInputQueue can call to reach it on the root controller. In the GPU\nprocess, RemoteContentController forwards it to the parent process over\nPAPZBridge, where ChromeProcessController receives it on the UI thread.\n\nNothing calls it yet, and ChromeProcessController does not pass it to the\nwidget yet.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340755\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/public/GeckoContentController.h", "gfx/layers/apz/src/APZCTreeManager.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/InputBlockState.h", "gfx/layers/apz/src/InputQueue.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/InputQueue.h", "gfx/layers/apz/util/ChromeProcessController.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/util/ChromeProcessController.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/APZBridgeChild.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/APZBridgeChild.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/PAPZBridge.ipdl", "gfx/layers/ipc/RemoteContentController.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/RemoteContentController.h"], "git_node": "bbc22a0617642c8981502635f91dd779bae65ba3", "git_parents": ["f2b976ee16a968258119e6bea4e0e2bbe16bf94f"], "node": "a54f53688d3a6358ce0ef9c1f9f71b471af43823", "parents": ["07487bac6f807cb806249c70e4d56bb97ee55565"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085128 - swipe-to-nav on touchscreen: Wait for APZ when the target is not confirmed on touchstart. r=hiro\n\nIf the target APZC is not confirmed on touchstart, for example when the\ntouch is in an irregular area that needs a hit test on the main thread,\nAPZ cannot compute the swipable directions. Instead of using the\ntentative target, APZ now asks the widget to wait, and notifies it once\nthe target is confirmed.\n\nWhile waiting, the widget passes inputs to APZ as usual, queues them, and\nreplays them when the result arrives. A new touch block starting during\nWaitingForAPZ phase discards the queue. If that is a new touch gesture,\na new swipe gesture starts, and, if that is an added finger, the ongoing\nswipe is rejected.\n\nNote that timeout mechanics are added in subsequent patches.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340756\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/public/APZBridge.h", "gfx/layers/apz/src/InputBlockState.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/InputBlockState.h", "gfx/layers/apz/src/InputQueue.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/util/ChromeProcessController.cpp", "widget/TouchSwipeInfo.h", "widget/TouchSwipeState.cpp", "widget/TouchSwipeState.h", "widget/moz.build", "widget/nsIWidget.cpp", "widget/nsIWidget.h", "widget/tests/browser/browser.toml", "widget/tests/browser/browser_test_touchscreen_swipe_gesture_while_waiting.js", "widget/tests/browser/browser_test_touchscreen_swipe_gesture_with_irregular_area.js", "widget/tests/browser/helper_touchscreen_swipe_irregular_scrollers.html", "widget/tests/browser/helper_touchscreen_swipe_navigation.html"], "git_node": "1eab978bc5776e4568b9586894d9b5c2632149b8", "git_parents": ["bbc22a0617642c8981502635f91dd779bae65ba3"], "node": "7a86a3cd2ed408deea382facf6bd2f3d12f21797", "parents": ["a54f53688d3a6358ce0ef9c1f9f71b471af43823"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085128 - swipe-to-nav on touchscreen: Wait for APZ when touch-action is not known on touchstart. r=hiro\n\nSwipe also depends on touch-action. Treat it like the target, i.e., the\nwidget waits until both are known, and APZ notifies it when the last of\nthem arrives.\n\nIn practice, content sends touch-action before it confirms the target.\n(https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/fa1e90ea670c4234c61b65a05dc02032b9bcde03/dom/ipc/BrowserChild.cpp#1979,1983-1985)\nThat means APZ knows touch-action when it gets to know the target.\nSo, strictly speaking, touch-action is handled properly even without\nthis patch.\n\nNote that timeout mechanics are added in subsequent patches.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340757\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/src/InputBlockState.cpp", "widget/tests/browser/browser.toml", "widget/tests/browser/browser_test_touchscreen_swipe_gesture_with_irregular_area.js", "widget/tests/browser/helper_touchscreen_swipe_irregular_area.html"], "git_node": "1ee79b6e595107aef421796c6f358909535502fc", "git_parents": ["1eab978bc5776e4568b9586894d9b5c2632149b8"], "node": "eb65533efa8c4bedaa1099416da76aa8390aa357", "parents": ["7a86a3cd2ed408deea382facf6bd2f3d12f21797"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085128 - swipe-to-nav on touchscreen: Wait for APZ when APZ starts to wait for a content response on touchstart. r=hiro\n\nIf there is a non-passive touchstart or touchmove listener when APZ\nhandles the touchstart, the widget waits for the response from APZ.\nAPZ will send the result to the widget when it receives the content\nreponse. APZ prevents swipe if the event is preventDefault-ed, by\nsending SideBits::eNone.\n\nNote that the wait on touchstart also covers the touchmove listener,\nbecause...\n- APZ considers touchmove listeners as well when APZ processes the\n  touchstart event.\n  (https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/fa1e90ea670c4234c61b65a05dc02032b9bcde03/dom/events/EventListenerManager.cpp#2271,2281-2284)\n- Content holds its response about preventDefault until the first\n  touchmove, when the touchstart is not prevented.\n  (https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/fa1e90ea670c4234c61b65a05dc02032b9bcde03/gfx/layers/apz/util/APZEventState.cpp#297,299,303,329,341)\n\nAPZ can also start waiting for a content response on the first\ntouchmove. That case is handled in a later patch.\n\nNote that timeout mechanics are added in the next patch.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340758\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/src/InputBlockState.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/InputBlockState.h", "gfx/layers/apz/src/InputQueue.cpp", "widget/tests/browser/browser.toml", "widget/tests/browser/browser_test_touchscreen_swipe_gesture_with_dispatch_to_content.js"], "git_node": "16d74a02f4d47bc65e7e756e799e05d4bee0b58c", "git_parents": ["1ee79b6e595107aef421796c6f358909535502fc"], "node": "87514bc8282763a38d150108429707b1109a2728", "parents": ["eb65533efa8c4bedaa1099416da76aa8390aa357"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085128 - swipe-to-nav on touchscreen: Stop waiting and reject swipe when the main thread does not respond in time. r=hiro\n\nIf the target, touch-action or the content response does not arrive\nbefore APZ's content response timeout, notify the widget at that point\nso that it stops waiting. In that case, swipe is rejected, while APZ\ngoes ahead with its own guess. Unlike scrolling, swipe navigates away\nfrom the current page, so it should not be triggered based on a guess.\n\nNote that TouchBlockState::TimeoutContentResponse doesn't tweak\nmWaitingForBrowserGestureResponse as\nPanGestureBlockState::TimeoutContentResponse does, because\nthe widget will give a reply about browser gesture response\nwhen it processes the queue.\n\nRegarding timer for browser gesture response, it is considered\nunnecessary. This is because APZ will tell the widget swipable directions\nregardless of whether APZ receives the content response or not, and\ntherefore the widget will always send the browser gesture response\nto APZ. There might be room for optimization, but this patch doesn't\ndo that.\n\nNote about a long tap: while the touch stays in slop, content holds its\nresponse, so the content response always times out (possibly forced by\nInputQueue::MaybeLongTapTimeout()) before a long tap happens, and swipe\nis rejected whether or not a context menu opens.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340759\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/src/InputBlockState.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/InputBlockState.h", "widget/tests/browser/browser.toml", "widget/tests/browser/browser_test_touchscreen_swipe_gesture_with_content_response_timeout.js"], "git_node": "37dd6e73cc41f73cd1e0139ab6cc8383e4c3d8e8", "git_parents": ["16d74a02f4d47bc65e7e756e799e05d4bee0b58c"], "node": "57a06eb59bbaa4651d1ba10b6f89819b8da0b96b", "parents": ["87514bc8282763a38d150108429707b1109a2728"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085128 - swipe-to-nav on touchscreen: Wait when APZ starts waiting for a content response on the first touchmove. r=hiro\n\nAPZ can start waiting for a content response about preventDefault on\nthe first touchmove out of slop.\nIn this case, the widget has to wait on that touchmove too, even if\nit already knows the swipable directions, because preventDefault on\nthe touchmove can prevent swipe.\n\nThis case happens when a non-passive touchmove listener is not in APZ's\nhit-test information yet, e.g. it is added in a touchstart passive listener.\nAPZ checks such listeners on the first touchmove (i.e., fast path).\n\nAfter the content response timeout, the widget does not wait on the\ntouchmove, because APZ has stopped waiting for the content response.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340760\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/src/InputBlockState.h", "gfx/layers/apz/src/InputQueue.cpp", "widget/TouchSwipeState.cpp", "widget/TouchSwipeState.h", "widget/nsIWidget.cpp", "widget/tests/browser/browser_test_touchscreen_swipe_gesture_with_dispatch_to_content.js"], "git_node": "6d0af1fde20e7efd4ee44e0c6db3f3544f110b75", "git_parents": ["37dd6e73cc41f73cd1e0139ab6cc8383e4c3d8e8"], "node": "47803bb27822bcc0f13d2a3bb40754f547597c73", "parents": ["57a06eb59bbaa4651d1ba10b6f89819b8da0b96b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085128 - swipe-to-nav on touchscreen: Handle a touchmove that starts a new wait while a result is in flight. r=hiro\n\nIt's possible that APZ sends the result for a block and then, before it\nreaches the widget, starts a new wait for the same block on its first\ntouchmove. When the widget replays its queue for the first result, it\nreaches that touchmove and starts waiting again.\n\nAn example flow is like this:\n- the widget receives the touchstart and passes it to APZ\n- APZ can't confirm touch-action, so it sets this touchstart's\n  mTouchSwipeNeedsToWait as true\n- the widget receives the result and starts to wait\n- APZ receives touch-action from content and send swipable directions\n  to the widget -- *1\n- (the swipable directions are now in flight)\n- a new touchmove non-passive listener is set -- *2\n- the widget receives the touchmove and passes it to APZ\n- APZ now has an APZ-aware listener (*2), so it starts to wait for\n  content response. And it has no mTouchSwipeResultCallback (*1).\n  So APZ sets this touchmove's mTouchSwipeNeedsToWait as true\n- the widget receives the result and queues it\n- finally, the widget receives the swipable directions for the\n  touchstart. So it starts to process the queue\n- while processing the queue, the queued touchmove changes the phase\n  to WaitingForAPZ\n\nThis race is not likely to happen, but in this case, the remaining queued\ninputs have to be moved to the new queue instead of processing them.\n\nCouldn't write a test case to reproduce this race reliably.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340761\n", "files": ["widget/nsIWidget.cpp"], "git_node": "e38e2d02702769175862b7824309081312767094", "git_parents": ["6d0af1fde20e7efd4ee44e0c6db3f3544f110b75"], "node": "ab5eaf433784ca62a7791797b44dbb25ed996f35", "parents": ["47803bb27822bcc0f13d2a3bb40754f547597c73"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hubert B Manilla \u003chmanilla@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092096 - [devtools] Test reloading the debugger with and without stylesheet support r=devtools-reviewers,jdescottes\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342247\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-reloading.js"], "git_node": "272d8c36c5a6a4c95761d075cbdcfbc40326627a", "git_parents": ["e38e2d02702769175862b7824309081312767094"], "node": "3a2a00786a3ef8bdc352d27aa5fcd0b75d0e5d42", "parents": ["ab5eaf433784ca62a7791797b44dbb25ed996f35"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092252 - Record build times when mach build forwards to a parent resource monitor. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nSince mach build stopped writing profile_build_resources.json when forwarding,\nmozharness had nothing to report the \"build times\" suite from. mach build now\nwrites a summary of its duration and phases to the objdir for mozharness to\nread.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342501\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/controller/building.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/controller/test_build_times.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/python.toml", "testing/mozharness/mozharness/mozilla/building/buildbase.py", "testing/mozharness/test/test_mozilla_building_buildbase.py"], "git_node": "ab4715d1435d24d00f9ea7a4a2bfa427515fd854", "git_parents": ["272d8c36c5a6a4c95761d075cbdcfbc40326627a"], "node": "8a77c5b2cd570132746c9c3dbf47471e5f26ac7c", "parents": ["3a2a00786a3ef8bdc352d27aa5fcd0b75d0e5d42"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091780 - Part 1: Fold MLexicalCheck for non-magic values. r=iain\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342048\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/MIR.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR.h"], "git_node": "d98de373bd9686a901da26356cd3483326076d50", "git_parents": ["ab4715d1435d24d00f9ea7a4a2bfa427515fd854"], "node": "5d0ebf3fe8ff0c436ca41f790f9dcf9cad9023df", "parents": ["8a77c5b2cd570132746c9c3dbf47471e5f26ac7c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091780 - Part 2: Bake in module const bindings in Warp. r=iain\n\nModule code runs with a single, known environment object so when loading an\nimmutable (eg `const` or `using`) binding we can snapshot the value and bake\nit in.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342049\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/modules/ion-constant-bindings.js", "js/src/jit/CacheIR.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpBuilder.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpBuilder.h", "js/src/jit/WarpOracle.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpOracle.h", "js/src/jit/WarpSnapshot.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpSnapshot.h", "js/src/vm/Scope.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "c62db2d20f0a93a9df89eb634b216c42fcbeccb5", "git_parents": ["d98de373bd9686a901da26356cd3483326076d50"], "node": "5df91fd1953006150de084899dff4a1c36604264", "parents": ["5d0ebf3fe8ff0c436ca41f790f9dcf9cad9023df"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091780 - Part 3: Bake in initialized const imports in Warp. r=iain\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342050\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/modules/constant-bindings-cycle-a.js", "js/src/jit-test/modules/constant-bindings-cycle-b.js", "js/src/jit-test/modules/constant-bindings-exports.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/modules/ion-constant-imports.js", "js/src/jit/WarpBuilder.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpOracle.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpSnapshot.h"], "git_node": "673d8f693a6f27f0240fc6c4779c4c3f7911f312", "git_parents": ["c62db2d20f0a93a9df89eb634b216c42fcbeccb5"], "node": "37e48ea7c4e2dffa8f54c34dce1d02062f735f3b", "parents": ["5df91fd1953006150de084899dff4a1c36604264"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091780 - Part 4: Bake in const bindings captured by inlined functions with a known callee in Warp. r=iain\n\nIf we're inlining and use `GuardSpecificFunction`, we can get that function's\nenvironment object in WarpOracle and apply the same `const` binding optimizations.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342051\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/warp/inlined-constant-bindings.js", "js/src/jit/TrialInlining.cpp", "js/src/jit/TrialInlining.h", "js/src/jit/WarpOracle.cpp"], "git_node": "12626f6a90dbced32a9ad9976a49e75b37248da5", "git_parents": ["673d8f693a6f27f0240fc6c4779c4c3f7911f312"], "node": "549c45cf0a93adbe8cc71d58d891b8eeee6a6e97", "parents": ["37e48ea7c4e2dffa8f54c34dce1d02062f735f3b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091780 - Part 5: Bake in known target environment objects for aliased var ops in Warp. r=iain\n\nIf we know the target environment object, we can bake it in to avoid having to\nload and walk the function's environment chain.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342052\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/modules/ion-known-environment.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/warp/known-environment-slots.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/warp/known-environment-stores.js", "js/src/jit/WarpBuilder.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpBuilder.h", "js/src/jit/WarpOracle.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpSnapshot.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpSnapshot.h"], "git_node": "9c2da5ec165aa5f7576096631ff00f4a5ed3374c", "git_parents": ["12626f6a90dbced32a9ad9976a49e75b37248da5"], "node": "f1c784243cac54dc2dc8fa1a9a3d642929eb70d7", "parents": ["549c45cf0a93adbe8cc71d58d891b8eeee6a6e97"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091780 - Part 6: Initialize class body environment bindings as uninitialized lexicals. r=iain\n\nClass body environment slots used to start out as `undefined`. This patch\nchanges that to the uninitialized lexical magic value, similar to block lexical\nenvironments.\n\nPrivate methods are stored after code for computed property keys runs, but\nthe initial `undefined` value (and now uninitialized lexical) wasn't observable\nto JS due to the private brand check. This change prevents us from baking in\nthis initial `undefined` value as constant in Warp in a later patch.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342053\n", "files": ["js/src/frontend/BytecodeEmitter.cpp", "js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.cpp", "js/src/jit/TemplateObject-inl.h", "js/src/jit/TemplateObject.h", "js/src/vm/EnvironmentObject.cpp"], "git_node": "1b504ab1206aeacba28435fc391e6a21a7a0509e", "git_parents": ["9c2da5ec165aa5f7576096631ff00f4a5ed3374c"], "node": "b3bee0e5da7cbb5bb4453221dd39f5793e67371b", "parents": ["f1c784243cac54dc2dc8fa1a9a3d642929eb70d7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091780 - Part 7: Move .staticInitializers and .staticFieldKeys to the class's lexical scope. r=iain,mgaudet\n\nClasses have an inner scope (an ordinary lexical scope) that contains the\nclass's body scope. Unlike the body scope bindings, `.staticInitializers` and\n`.staticFieldKeys` are mutable: they are set to `undefined` after the static\nfields have been initialized.\n\nThis patch moves these two bindings from the body scope to the class's lexical\nscope as Let bindings. This lets us mark all `Synthetic` and `PrivateMethod`\nbindings in the body scope as immutable in the next patch, which allows Warp\nto bake in their values.\n\nThe alternative of having both mutable and immutable bindings in the class body\nscope is complicated for multiple reasons. `.privateBrand` must be the first\nbinding (see `privateBrandSlot`) but it's immutable so it would have to be moved\nafter these mutable bindings. We would also need to add a third binding range\nto `ClassBodyScope` just for these two bindings.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342054\n", "files": ["js/src/frontend/NameOpEmitter.cpp", "js/src/frontend/Parser.cpp", "js/src/vm/BindingKind.h", "js/src/vm/Scope.h"], "git_node": "f6405c29ec1e08d2ce5d7b69074740918c716894", "git_parents": ["1b504ab1206aeacba28435fc391e6a21a7a0509e"], "node": "b842becd598d95f81d5cafaf8fbed7900c7d76bb", "parents": ["b3bee0e5da7cbb5bb4453221dd39f5793e67371b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091780 - Part 8: Make class body environment bindings non-writable. r=iain\n\nClass body bindings (private names, the private brand, private methods and the\nother synthetic bindings used to implement classes) are initialized once when\nthe class is defined, and can't be mutated by script or the debugger. Making\nthem non-writable in the environment shape lets Warp bake them in like const\nbindings when the environment is known at compile time.\n\nThis helps code using private fields and methods, for example JetStream 3's\nraytrace-private-class-fields gets ~25-40% faster.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342055\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/warp/inlined-private-methods.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/warp/inlined-private-names.js", "js/src/vm/Scope.cpp"], "git_node": "b6a5d81f648a52094a9fcfe7efe1e7fd13603ca1", "git_parents": ["f6405c29ec1e08d2ce5d7b69074740918c716894"], "node": "f50ecb4602696efbe826bc91fe55f0ab4870a701", "parents": ["b842becd598d95f81d5cafaf8fbed7900c7d76bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vincent Hilla \u003cvhilla@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091545 - Update top-level about:blank history length synchronously. r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341897\n", "files": ["docshell/base/BrowsingContext.cpp", "docshell/base/BrowsingContext.h", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/navigating-across-documents/initial-empty-document/window-open-history-length.html.ini"], "git_node": "9eb16d66cb213456f2726fbc943327efcf0354d0", "git_parents": ["b6a5d81f648a52094a9fcfe7efe1e7fd13603ca1"], "node": "5f5c68c6c3e740f5df3bc9ca2c3a8eb95afa6fc5", "parents": ["f50ecb4602696efbe826bc91fe55f0ab4870a701"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshi Cheng-Hao Huang \u003callstars.chh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092485 - Reset preloaded module graphs before cancelling preloads when registering an import map. r=jonco\n\nThis fixes the intermittent failure of test_dynamic_importMap_with_external_script.html.\n\nOriginally cancelling a preload that is still fetching its dependencies\nclears its module script, so ResetPreloadedModuleGraph bailed out early\nand the wrong module record was kept in the module map.\n\nCall ResetPreloadedModuleGraph first to make sure the preloaded module graph\nis cleared.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342504\n", "files": ["dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp"], "git_node": "83e2536e7fac5a77def77f0161859a43ab7ef8bd", "git_parents": ["9eb16d66cb213456f2726fbc943327efcf0354d0"], "node": "87142c0f445500d8958a21db728a3baabd6daa1b", "parents": ["5f5c68c6c3e740f5df3bc9ca2c3a8eb95afa6fc5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshi Cheng-Hao Huang \u003callstars.chh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2021012 - Skip the single import map rejection tests on Nightly. r=jonco\n\ndom.multiple_import_maps.enabled is enabled on Nightly, where\ntest_reject_multiple_importMaps.html, test_module_script_reject_importMap.html,\ntest_dynamic_import_reject_importMap.html and\ntest_inline_module_reject_importMap.html no longer apply. They still cover Beta\nand Release until the pref ships there, and will be removed then.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342505\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/jsmodules/importmaps/chrome.toml"], "git_node": "46bf28e8699cc56b5a90f3e917a67fdba32a5706", "git_parents": ["83e2536e7fac5a77def77f0161859a43ab7ef8bd"], "node": "1dabe5a8698163e20e5ff49f72ed9388b4e7c7e3", "parents": ["87142c0f445500d8958a21db728a3baabd6daa1b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshi Cheng-Hao Huang \u003callstars.chh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2021012 : Enable multiple import maps in Nightly build. r=jonco\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342190\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "92e849b91d2ed45abe6817a03ffcba6042804998", "git_parents": ["46bf28e8699cc56b5a90f3e917a67fdba32a5706"], "node": "229f27b81ffdc833b55cf3072033102dbc324e42", "parents": ["1dabe5a8698163e20e5ff49f72ed9388b4e7c7e3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092331 - Add a bit of extra fuzz to text-shadow test. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342499\n", "files": ["layout/reftests/svg/text/reftest.list"], "git_node": "adbfd3d688899d5026f4fbad8c0bb6ba26617f1e", "git_parents": ["92e849b91d2ed45abe6817a03ffcba6042804998"], "node": "aac3d4e8959b87bcb8ceaa3700549edd272b4627", "parents": ["229f27b81ffdc833b55cf3072033102dbc324e42"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim Huang \u003ctihuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091711 - Normalize hostnames in ContentClassifierRequest before matching. r=bvandersloot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342104\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/content-classifier/content_classifier_engine/ContentClassifierEngine.cpp", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/test/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/test/browser/browser_content_classifier_normalization.js", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/test/browser/browser_content_classifier_subdomain_rules.js", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "d8c03f626270a746bc2105d3026b2c3566513559", "git_parents": ["adbfd3d688899d5026f4fbad8c0bb6ba26617f1e"], "node": "dd974c78254fab68d70171b1570f7946338f4e01", "parents": ["aac3d4e8959b87bcb8ceaa3700549edd272b4627"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Niklas Jaeschke \u003cjjaschke@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090900 - Stop setting up a document viewer once another one has replaced the old one. r=smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342108\n", "files": ["docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp"], "git_node": "708f54ffef79e9f29042f0a54ebb4cc5b76710ac", "git_parents": ["d8c03f626270a746bc2105d3026b2c3566513559"], "node": "6371fd8154bf4d2c070eec81396968a6946c591b", "parents": ["dd974c78254fab68d70171b1570f7946338f4e01"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kershaw Chang \u003ckershaw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084553 - Fail the WebTransport request when no session is established, r=necko-reviewers,jesup\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342094\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpTransaction.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_webtransport_https_rr_no_h3.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "32ad7ce0739464168e0b5844ca262441d77fca09", "git_parents": ["708f54ffef79e9f29042f0a54ebb4cc5b76710ac"], "node": "121e18ebeb9cb9475718c94af40273527cbe5824", "parents": ["6371fd8154bf4d2c070eec81396968a6946c591b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kershaw Chang \u003ckershaw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084553 - Only accept WebTransport sessions over HTTP/3 unless network.webtransport.http2.enabled is set, r=necko-reviewers,jesup\n\nDepends on D342094\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342095\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpConnectionMgr.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpTransaction.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/webtransport/WebTransportSessionProxy.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_webtransport_https_rr_no_h3.js", "netwerk/test/unit/test_webtransport_simple.js"], "git_node": "541bba92fbe398a1a6edf960da73b9e584f8ecb5", "git_parents": ["32ad7ce0739464168e0b5844ca262441d77fca09"], "node": "f7e3538133d20ffd9df9b9f92333d9cb5dd021dd", "parents": ["121e18ebeb9cb9475718c94af40273527cbe5824"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081261 - Apply and restore every draw buffer's color mask around WebGL resource clears. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333257\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLContext.cpp", "dom/canvas/WebGLContext.h", "dom/canvas/WebGLContextFramebufferOperations.cpp", "dom/canvas/WebGLContextState.cpp"], "git_node": "105fac7457a06ef2fd1d51a66ec93ad55244beb2", "git_parents": ["541bba92fbe398a1a6edf960da73b9e584f8ecb5"], "node": "252098f85e42b7f857e3607aff0fd599bc8a9fc5", "parents": ["f7e3538133d20ffd9df9b9f92333d9cb5dd021dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Chopin \u003cschopin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091337 - Wait for the CDM to report its termination in the CDMCrashMinidump gtest. r=aosmond,media-playback-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342236\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestCDMStorage.cpp"], "git_node": "b5fb32d30020572a646029164cec051ac210c3c1", "git_parents": ["105fac7457a06ef2fd1d51a66ec93ad55244beb2"], "node": "a97aa934e9cc533ef72b07c66681dd8f31501cd2", "parents": ["252098f85e42b7f857e3607aff0fd599bc8a9fc5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092365 - Keep rendering blocked when a navigation aborts a render-blocking script load. r=farre\n\nWhen a navigation away from a document cancels the document's loads, a\nrender-blocking script load failed like any other load. That unblocked\nrendering, so the old page could be revealed before the new page. Per spec,\naborting the document discards the fetch, so the script never completes.\n\nThis is a spot fix for skip-outbound-vt-before-reveal.html. It does not try to\nfix request stopping during page unload in general.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342412\n", "files": ["dom/script/ScriptElement.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoadContext.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoadContext.h", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-view-transitions/navigation/skip-outbound-vt-before-reveal.html.ini"], "git_node": "33bc299defa60ae0cf519c6d787882b56eb85888", "git_parents": ["b5fb32d30020572a646029164cec051ac210c3c1"], "node": "fdd53933057949069f5b6f6359751316c82e32f5", "parents": ["a97aa934e9cc533ef72b07c66681dd8f31501cd2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kershaw Chang \u003ckershaw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091707 - Add the proxy type to the pageload event, r=necko-reviewers,acreskey,jesup\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341806\n", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/test/browser_page_load_event_telemetry.js", "dom/metrics.yaml", "netwerk/ipc/NeckoMessageUtils.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3Session.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3StreamTunnel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpBaseChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpBaseChannel.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpChannelChild.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpChannelParams.ipdlh", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpChannelParent.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpConnectionBase.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpTransactionShell.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttp.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttp.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpTransaction.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpTransaction.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsIHttpChannelInternal.idl", "netwerk/test/unit/http3_proxy_common.js", "tools/performance/PageloadEvent.h"], "git_node": "72575ad073b1dad53d221e40bba13ec6a90eac73", "git_parents": ["33bc299defa60ae0cf519c6d787882b56eb85888"], "node": "318233088647defdb99ba85f099039b3a66b9bc0", "parents": ["fdd53933057949069f5b6f6359751316c82e32f5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069243 - Move Container Storage Layer into A-S - part 1 - Add migration tests r=timhuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329039\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_migratedFile.js"], "git_node": "a9e671c6d0610b60ca863c08d0d500291e375b1d", "git_parents": ["72575ad073b1dad53d221e40bba13ec6a90eac73"], "node": "5acc961806c040f845797ce0ec3aabc84fb4d10d", "parents": ["318233088647defdb99ba85f099039b3a66b9bc0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069243 - Move Container Storage Layer into A-S - part 2 - ContextualIdentityService r=timhuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329040\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/contextualidentity/ContextualIdentityService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_basic.js", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_containersStore.js", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_corruptedFile.js", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_migratedFile.js", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_siteAssociations.js", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/xpcshell.toml", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ext_contextual_identities.js"], "git_node": "d399140d596e0a337185f3fac5b1f912a025e98e", "git_parents": ["a9e671c6d0610b60ca863c08d0d500291e375b1d"], "node": "641005d2174f34e38b67200d72498ab9292d0c64", "parents": ["5acc961806c040f845797ce0ec3aabc84fb4d10d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092215 - Update freetype2 to dbb00e529e69a2be629a9ef98498e4f9b188aab1 r=jfkthame\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342279\n", "files": ["modules/freetype2/moz.yaml", "modules/freetype2/src/cff/cffparse.c", "modules/freetype2/src/truetype/ttgxvar.c", "modules/freetype2/src/truetype/ttvarc.c"], "git_node": "31773d075e214698acf367109b2e39e6628ce1d8", "git_parents": ["d399140d596e0a337185f3fac5b1f912a025e98e"], "node": "c078184594b7d09952190989807ca26d0d60a67c", "parents": ["641005d2174f34e38b67200d72498ab9292d0c64"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jamie Nicol \u003cjnicol@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091692 - Make file_generate_wrapper.py use cwd relative to topobjdir. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre,sergesanspaille\n\nfile_generate_wrapper.py's `action()` resolves the script's working\ndirectory by joining the provided `target_dir` onto `Path.cwd()`. The\ntarget_dir provided by gn_processor.py is expressed relative to the\ngenerated project's build root, so this is only correct if `Path.cwd()`\nis the top-level objdir.\n\nThat assumption was previously true for all GeneratedFiles emitted by\ngn_processor.py, as they all produced files that land in the \"export\"\ntier and therefore the top-level backend.mk file.\n\nWhen vendoring ANGLE's Vulkan backend, however, we now encounter\nGeneratedFiles that output \".inc\" files, which currently land in the\n\"pre-compile\" tier instead, and therefore a nested target-specific\nbackend.mk. This results in the action being executed with an incorrect\ncwd, resulting in failures.\n\nMake action() instead join the provided `target_dir` to\n`buildconfig.topobjdir`, ensuring the correct working directory is used.\n\nNote that these files do in fact belong in the \"export\" tier, which will\nbe addressed in the following patch, making this moot. But we take this\nopportunity to fix this bug, hopefully saving somebody a headache in the\nfuture.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341759\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/action/file_generate_wrapper.py"], "git_node": "18b88f6c31770f5f59459c8ba228e9a8f1f6d726", "git_parents": ["31773d075e214698acf367109b2e39e6628ce1d8"], "node": "c8e69eb6fd7b836af5629601f15c5b060bac20a2", "parents": ["c078184594b7d09952190989807ca26d0d60a67c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jamie Nicol \u003cjnicol@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091692 - Treat .inc files as required before compile. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nANGLE's Vulkan backend generates several .inc files at build time, which\nwe must ensure are generated before any code which tries to include them\nis compiled.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341760\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/data.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/xpi-stage-compile-output/staged/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/test_xpi_archive.py"], "git_node": "3105e2d706c1adb6d99b1e41a932683873f13ca8", "git_parents": ["18b88f6c31770f5f59459c8ba228e9a8f1f6d726"], "node": "71ab0b3ae19b0db771e9bff81534bdf2ef20819b", "parents": ["c8e69eb6fd7b836af5629601f15c5b060bac20a2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jamie Nicol \u003cjnicol@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091692 - Escape commas when formatting generated file flags. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nVendoring ANGLE's Vulkan backend introduces GeneratedFiles with flags\nsuch as `--extinst=,\u003cpath\u003e`, i.e. containing a literal comma.\n\nWe shell-escape flags before writing them into $(call py_action, ...),\nso each flag reaches the script as a single shell argument. But `$(call\n...)` itself splits on unescaped commas in its own argument list before\nthe shell is ever involved, so a flag containing a comma is mistaken for\na boundary between py_action's own arguments.\n\nFix by escaping commas embedded within flags as `$(comma)`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341761\n", "files": ["config/makefiles/functions.mk", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/make.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/generated-files/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/test_recursivemake.py"], "git_node": "4e69d41a692b475cb7b3f161e95b7c04fd0c42ff", "git_parents": ["3105e2d706c1adb6d99b1e41a932683873f13ca8"], "node": "957d1108d577e4bfe0c9a66e2f459dc4d49ba06c", "parents": ["71ab0b3ae19b0db771e9bff81534bdf2ef20819b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jamie Nicol \u003cjnicol@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091692 - gn_processor.py: Include subdirs of root gen dir in LOCAL_INCLUDES. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\ngn_processor.py has existing logic for ensuring the root `gen_path`\ndirectory is added to LOCAL_INCLUDES when required. However, some\ntargets may require a subdirectory of `gen_path` as an include dir. This\nensures that subdirectories of `gen_path` are also rebased correctly and\nadded to LOCAL_INCLUDES.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341762\n", "files": ["build/gn_processor.py"], "git_node": "fe07acd355f092e667d4acbf7bf26c6c5f11133b", "git_parents": ["4e69d41a692b475cb7b3f161e95b7c04fd0c42ff"], "node": "88a3d07c2d3fbe3fa7e867cbf89f1479600d26ec", "parents": ["957d1108d577e4bfe0c9a66e2f459dc4d49ba06c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1991278 - Use a NodeHTTP2Server in test_bug1940663.js r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nThe moz-http2 handler reset the stream on a timer after writing the response,\nso the reset could reach the client before the data. The new handler only\nresets the stream once the data has been written. The handler and resetLater\nare removed from moz-http2.js, since nothing else uses them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342503\n", "files": ["netwerk/test/unit/test_bug1940663.js", "testing/xpcshell/moz-http2/moz-http2.js"], "git_node": "e6116d32baba569ae881d3cf73973e65417b3584", "git_parents": ["fe07acd355f092e667d4acbf7bf26c6c5f11133b"], "node": "255864f115afc89c9683492a53ff9dfc90bbe136", "parents": ["88a3d07c2d3fbe3fa7e867cbf89f1479600d26ec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092176 - Use a keep-alive server in test_plaintext_sniff.js r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nhttpd.js closes the connection after every response, so each of the ~850\nrequests made by the test left a client port in TIME_WAIT. Test-verify runs\nthe test 20 times in quick succession, which exhausted the ephemeral ports on\nWindows and made every later test in the job that connects to localhost fail.\n\nServe the responses from a NodeHTTPServer instead, so connections are kept\nalive and reused, and read each response to the end instead of cancelling the\nrequest, which would close the connection.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342507\n", "files": ["netwerk/test/unit/test_plaintext_sniff.js"], "git_node": "78a444b9c8a64e2370bde59077cf66349470a949", "git_parents": ["e6116d32baba569ae881d3cf73973e65417b3584"], "node": "e1757c57dbc1132ffc0502e7706a3286130b2ec4", "parents": ["255864f115afc89c9683492a53ff9dfc90bbe136"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1994039 - Fix debug assertion in CacheStorageService.cpp r=necko-reviewers,jesup\n\nCacheFileMetadata and memory-only CacheFileChunk objects report their memory\nusage to CacheStorageService, but only CacheEntry kept the service alive. At\nshutdown a CacheFile can outlive its last CacheEntry, for example when a closed\noutput stream or an in-flight NetUtil.asyncCopy still references it. Dropping\nthat entry then destroyed the service while the file's memory was still\ncounted, which tripped the \"memory consumption is not at 0\" assertion in\n~MemoryPool. The file's later reports were skipped, or could race with the\nservice's destruction on another thread.\n\nEach reporting CacheMemoryConsumer now holds a strong reference to the service,\nso the service is destroyed only after every consumer has reported a size of 0.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341821\n", "files": ["netwerk/cache2/CacheStorageService.cpp", "netwerk/cache2/CacheStorageService.h", "netwerk/test/unit/test_cache2-46-output-stream-outlives-entry.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "d309c64608759684de0fa7b14400685ec271482c", "git_parents": ["78a444b9c8a64e2370bde59077cf66349470a949"], "node": "e2bfc32069a75c11037b1bede0e086ff06a8b9b4", "parents": ["e1757c57dbc1132ffc0502e7706a3286130b2ec4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "iulian moraru \u003cimoraru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2069243 - Move Container Storage Layer into A-S - part 2 - ContextualIdentityService r=timhuang\" for causing xpcshell failures on test_siteAssociations.js.\n\nThis reverts commit d399140d596e0a337185f3fac5b1f912a025e98e.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2069243 - Move Container Storage Layer into A-S - part 1 - Add migration tests r=timhuang\"\n\nThis reverts commit a9e671c6d0610b60ca863c08d0d500291e375b1d.\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/contextualidentity/ContextualIdentityService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_basic.js", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_containersStore.js", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_corruptedFile.js", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_migratedFile.js", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_siteAssociations.js", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/xpcshell.toml", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ext_contextual_identities.js"], "git_node": "d6455fc075b6d5135b30f272b6208a5f0461cc2b", "git_parents": ["d309c64608759684de0fa7b14400685ec271482c"], "node": "15119fd883080503ceff83edb372e30ca734fe24", "parents": ["e2bfc32069a75c11037b1bede0e086ff06a8b9b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089298 [wpt PR 64356] - Remove inline margin trimming from comment., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRemove inline margin trimming from comment.\n\nFollow-up to crrev.com/c/8256869\n\nBug: 40886857\nChange-Id: I6c5c275c939c8cd460fbf38a8f7ad4b4fc1a74dd\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8274791\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1730670}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ab32d02795620cccec712dd3fddc4dcdaa478016\nwpt-pr: 64356\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-box/parsing/margin-trim.html"], "git_node": "211abd218ee41622712579b3419ce028d77265ae", "git_parents": ["d6455fc075b6d5135b30f272b6208a5f0461cc2b"], "node": "db3ed994c1e5d887fcc3c9ec3ecf5173c0919641", "parents": ["15119fd883080503ceff83edb372e30ca734fe24"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hoch Hochkeppel \u003cmhochk@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089300 [wpt PR 64355] - [Masonry] Apply track-reverse to OOF items, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Masonry] Apply track-reverse to OOF items\n\nPer CSSWG resolution [1], out-of-flow (OOF) items in grid-lanes should\nfollow the precedent of `flexbox` and reverse their placement when\n`fill-reverse` or `track-reverse` is applied. This was largely\nimplemented by crrev.com/c/7808903, and this change adds the last piece\nto respect `track-reverse` appropriately.\n\n[1] https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13931\n\nBug: 343257585\nChange-Id: If0dc1939e80df78c30e6f927171a61db9b78911d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8675818\nReviewed-by: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Hoch Hochkeppel \u003cmhochk@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1730693}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f5d40ab96dcf1c80df3398ce74088da9576fea61\nwpt-pr: 64355\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-rtl-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-rtl-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-rtl-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-rtl-001.html"], "git_node": "193a8ebd5a18dd30216ed5624320d824d2e5d132", "git_parents": ["211abd218ee41622712579b3419ce028d77265ae"], "node": "cf597f8d06d02d4502b262c34b1105da9b0dd1a6", "parents": ["db3ed994c1e5d887fcc3c9ec3ecf5173c0919641"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089300 [wpt PR 64355] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64355\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/column-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-rtl-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/abspos/row-grid-lanes-oof-track-reverse-rtl-001.html.ini"], "git_node": "f48338a2862d9ad90a52e635f7f6b51766cf8f53", "git_parents": ["193a8ebd5a18dd30216ed5624320d824d2e5d132"], "node": "b9402640abd0ee80dd3f76760c8a3087ea4600c3", "parents": ["cf597f8d06d02d4502b262c34b1105da9b0dd1a6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089301 [wpt PR 64363] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327897, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Flex] A stretched item in a column-reverse wrap flex container ignores its main-axis auto margin\n\nThe flex formatting context read the items' margins off their renderers, where item layouts overwrite them from style with auto as 0.\nSo a stretched item in a column-reverse wrap container lost its main-axis auto margin in its stretch relayout, before computeFlexItemRects read it to flip the item.\nFlexLayoutItem now carries the margins, resolved from the item's used style, so its own zoom applies, and updated with the auto margins the algorithm resolves.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327897\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324398@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: cbe8f54eafbbcd55e6188005d6c74ffe512ea2b5\nwpt-pr: 64363\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/column-reverse-wrap-auto-margins-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/flex-item-margin.html"], "git_node": "3abdafd1af8f5170326f134e165c3b8cf05eba68", "git_parents": ["f48338a2862d9ad90a52e635f7f6b51766cf8f53"], "node": "fa1faa7a6acddbc13664c900be2f49bb086945b4", "parents": ["b9402640abd0ee80dd3f76760c8a3087ea4600c3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matt Woodrow \u003cmattwoodrow@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089303 [wpt PR 64362] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328543, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nREGRESSION(313316@main): Filtered layers with composited ancestor clips allocate oversized filter buffers\n\n313316@main changed setupFilters() to call calculateLayerBounds() with empty flags so that descendant\nlayers would use the default flags, which include IncludeSelfTransform. The defaults also include\nUseLocalClipRectIfPossible, which makes each descendant report its ancestor clip rect (relative to the\npainting root) as its bounds. On MotionMark Map Zoomer, each 50x66 drop-shadow placard now produced a\n400x320 filter buffer, the size of the map's overflow clip.\n\nAdd IncludeDescendantTransforms, which adds IncludeSelfTransform to the descendant flags, and use it with\nPreserveAncestorFlags in setupFilters(). Descendant transforms are honored without the local clip rect\nshortcut, and the filtered layer's own transform is still excluded.\n\nViewTransition::captureOverflowRect() had the same problem: PreserveAncestorFlags without\nIncludeSelfTransform ignored descendant transforms, so transformed descendants were clipped out of the\ncaptured image. Use IncludeDescendantTransforms there too.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328543\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324517@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 16ab045792758846d125e97e77e978a426a79980\nwpt-pr: 64362\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/content-with-transformed-child-old-image.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/content-with-transformed-child-ref.html"], "git_node": "730b6e5aeddeed9fca4648908c857a624dcc55f9", "git_parents": ["3abdafd1af8f5170326f134e165c3b8cf05eba68"], "node": "2de6c40ce6936450c2a9be299524b06377ba71e3", "parents": ["fa1faa7a6acddbc13664c900be2f49bb086945b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089304 [wpt PR 64364] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327867, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nQuote marks from open-quote and close-quote don't take the ::first-line style\n\n  \u003cstyle\u003e\n    div::first-line { color: green }\n    span::before { content: open-quote }\n  \u003c/style\u003e\n  \u003cdiv\u003e\u003cspan\u003equoted\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\nThe quote mark should be green like the rest of the first line. Instead it was black.\n\nEach open-quote/close-quote was an anonymous RenderQuote inline box around a text\nrenderer. The box added nothing to layout (its style only inherits from the\npseudo-element), but that style also never got the ::first-line style, so the\ntext under it fell back to the plain style. The box only existed to hold the\nquote's type and depth and to survive ::first-letter replacing its text.\n\nRemove RenderQuote. A quote is now a RenderTextFragment tagged with its QuoteType,\ndirectly under the pseudo-element like a 'content' string. ::first-letter hands\nthe tag to the remaining text, and the quote depth walk carries the depth itself.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327867\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324380@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 706286c0794324d6d60e5c5b7bceb39146520f40\nwpt-pr: 64364\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/first-line-with-quote-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/first-line-with-quote.html"], "git_node": "9cfb352fffcf843d89e308a85b6f783bd5e808c2", "git_parents": ["730b6e5aeddeed9fca4648908c857a624dcc55f9"], "node": "c068f59ba0ff160e6b5e814fba787228e2d43057", "parents": ["2de6c40ce6936450c2a9be299524b06377ba71e3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Elika Etemad \u003cfantasai.bugs@inkedblade.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089305 [wpt PR 64365] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327212, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nREGRESSION(321159@main): Creating a \u003cselect\u003e triggers a CSP style-src violation\n\nThe button slot in the \u003cselect\u003e UA shadow tree received `text-overflow: inherit`\nvia a style attribute, set before the slot was inserted into the shadow root, so\nit was subject to the document's CSP. Style it from the UA style sheet instead,\nvia a new internal UA part.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327212\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324283@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 364f64847e5bce33fbb6673071a014de4e485184\nwpt-pr: 64365\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/select-csp-style-src-attr.html"], "git_node": "2bbd884bc89460f1cdf9aab7129becc3642e2495", "git_parents": ["9cfb352fffcf843d89e308a85b6f783bd5e808c2"], "node": "f49e4de49c1a09cc2d4f299bf360e4fc9246ed7e", "parents": ["c068f59ba0ff160e6b5e814fba787228e2d43057"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sammy Gill \u003csammy.gill@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089307 [wpt PR 64366] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326939, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-grid] Grid item with a non-auto min-block-size overflows the grid when the grid shrinks and its content wraps\n\nWhen a grid item in an auto row has a min-block-size other than auto, its minimum\ncontribution is computed by GridTrackSizingAlgorithmStrategy::minLogicalSizeForGridItem()\ninstead of going through the min-content contribution. This function ends up setting the\ngrid item's grid area content logical width and calls layout on it. The problem is that\nRenderGrid keeps track of the grid item's intrinsic logical height for each item so that\nit can reuse it in subsequent layouts and in this case we were getting back a stale\nvalue. The min/max-content contribution paths already invalidated this cache when\nwe recompute the height of the grid item with a different containing block size but\nthis path for the minimum contribution did not.\n\nWhat happens is basically:\n1.) Run one pass of grid layout at some width -\u003e when computing the minimum\ncontribution run layout on the item with the computed grid area width when we\nsized the columns -\u003e compute the max-content height of the grid item and cache the\nvalue\n\n2.) Run subsequent pass of grid layout with different set of constraints due to the\nwidth change -\u003e when computing the minimum contribution update the grid area\ncontent width (note this does not invalidate the cache) -\u003e when recomputing\nthe max-content height see that there is an entry in the cache and use it\n\nSince we update the grid area for the item when we are computing the minimum\ncontribution but do not invalidate the cache we have no way of knowing that\nwe need to invalidate the entry by the time we need to compute the max-content\nheight since we think it did not end up changing.\n\nMove the cache invalidation into updateOverridingContainingBlockContentSizeForGridItem()\nso that it happens whenever that function changes the override size, instead of being\nrepeated by each contribution path. This removes the two existing copies in the\nmin-content and max-content contribution paths.\n\nThe test lays out a grid containing an item with min-block-size: 0, shrinks the grid's\ncontaining block so that the item's text wraps, and checks that the grid's height grew.\nIt fails without this change.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326939\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324127@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c059bc3a4cabd0a12150453bef34ce8bc2db11b5\nwpt-pr: 64366\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-items/grid-item-min-block-size-dynamic-container-shrink-001.html"], "git_node": "9605bf1d122ace6aa2119c33267bdef57c122477", "git_parents": ["2bbd884bc89460f1cdf9aab7129becc3642e2495"], "node": "d65d86bf3c297a79ae7dcb9b49138da6d6cc7934", "parents": ["f49e4de49c1a09cc2d4f299bf360e4fc9246ed7e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Taher Ali \u003ctaher_ali@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089308 [wpt PR 64369] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=258225, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSupport external and data: URL filter references on SVG elements\n\nAn SVG element's filter can now reference a \u003cfilter\u003e in another document \u2014\nfilter=\"url(effects.svg#blur)\" or a data: URL instead of only a same-document\n`#id` reference.\n\nThis covers the filter presentation attribute on SVG elements only. External references from\nthe CSS filter property on HTML elements are a separate follow-up.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=258225\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/317538@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d76185a3594cf89a5b2cf352d40ba6d36b03faa2\nwpt-pr: 64369\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/svg-data-uri-filter-resource.html"], "git_node": "b8984ab0a4cfa815adbe36bb54ba3b41f4dcf7bb", "git_parents": ["9605bf1d122ace6aa2119c33267bdef57c122477"], "node": "2479b20f7845568da3eb043bfef9d9064fb905f1", "parents": ["d65d86bf3c297a79ae7dcb9b49138da6d6cc7934"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089308 [wpt PR 64369] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64369\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/filter-effects/svg-data-uri-filter-resource.html.ini"], "git_node": "cbec93189ff51a6e6cfb7e99b49afc03b314ebb2", "git_parents": ["b8984ab0a4cfa815adbe36bb54ba3b41f4dcf7bb"], "node": "51eb34f0691c3912e7367fd73b74579ceb0bd2fb", "parents": ["2479b20f7845568da3eb043bfef9d9064fb905f1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003cahmad.saleem792+github@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089309 [wpt PR 64370] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=318325, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nfeConvolveMatrix: removing an invalid order attribute leaves the filter permanently disabled\n\nWhen feConvolveMatrix parses an invalid order (e.g. order=\"0\"), it sets\nm_hasInvalidOrderAttribute so createFilterEffect() bails out and the filtered\nelement is not displayed. Removing the order attribute produces an empty value,\nwhich parseNumberOptionalNumber() rejects, so the code took the parse-failure\npath and kept m_hasInvalidOrderAttribute set. The filter therefore stayed\ndisabled even though a missing order attribute is valid and defaults to 3x3.\n\nTreat an empty/absent order value as the valid 3x3 default: reset orderX/orderY\nto the initial value and clear m_hasInvalidOrderAttribute, distinct from a\npresent-but-malformed value which continues to invalidate the primitive.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=318325\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/317005@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 69a023fe42f541f30b95092120ca3e2a90e8af53\nwpt-pr: 64370\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/feconvolvematrix-order-removal.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/reference/feconvolvematrix-order-removal-ref.html"], "git_node": "8265e4185bf3c1edfcbfa6fe9bb906eefb1b4c1f", "git_parents": ["cbec93189ff51a6e6cfb7e99b49afc03b314ebb2"], "node": "d2cc048af3fc1aec534edd18e64777d35c278588", "parents": ["51eb34f0691c3912e7367fd73b74579ceb0bd2fb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Taher Ali \u003ctaher_ali@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089310 [wpt PR 64367] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=104442, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSupport external and data: URL clip-path references on SVG elements\n\nclip-path on an SVG element now resolves a \u003cclipPath\u003e referenced by an\nexternal file or a data: URL.\n\nclip-path on HTML elements goes through a separate path and is a follow-up.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=104442\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/317649@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9cf683faef8aaab66b31d1ede61c9e301e849375\nwpt-pr: 64367\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-url-reference-data-uri-svg-element.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-url-reference-external-svg-element.html"], "git_node": "b6c9218860cd5168a144b636bfe8ce931dbb5cc7", "git_parents": ["8265e4185bf3c1edfcbfa6fe9bb906eefb1b4c1f"], "node": "464b0014c8ee120963e9602d37d9d1ceb2a8cc6c", "parents": ["d2cc048af3fc1aec534edd18e64777d35c278588"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Taher Ali \u003ctaher_ali@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089312 [wpt PR 64368] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=44144, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSupport external and data: URL marker references on SVG elements\n\nmarker-start, marker-mid, and marker-end now resolve \u003cmarker\u003e elements\nreferenced by an external file or a data: URL.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=44144\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/317614@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b7683dacd913c0eec7fccd09b9fd017d6efb2ab1\nwpt-pr: 64368\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/painting/reftests/marker-data-uri-reference.svg"], "git_node": "ceeb3a765b6a18c650e575b48cf1d2a6c441ffc0", "git_parents": ["b6c9218860cd5168a144b636bfe8ce931dbb5cc7"], "node": "80368b6d5dffac661547f41cad11c2d7a9f1fff2", "parents": ["464b0014c8ee120963e9602d37d9d1ceb2a8cc6c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Fraser \u003csimon.fraser@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089313 [wpt PR 64371] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=318756, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Scroll anchoring] nfl.com scroll position jumps when hovering the top bar (changing scroll-padding)\n\nThe scroll anchoring code re-used `computeScrollerRelativeRects()` for both anchor selection, and\nscroll anchoring adjustment. However, only anchor selection should respect `scroll-padding`; this caused\nan erroneous scroll anchoring adjustment on nfl.com when the page changes `scroll-padding` on the root\nwhen the top bar is hovered.\n\nFix by passing in a flag to say whether `scroll-padding` should be respected; off for anchor adjustment,\nand on for anchor selection.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=318756\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/316662@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1a54955ca46236a54eb489452effdfc6bd2d9279\nwpt-pr: 64371\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-anchoring/scroll-padding-change.html"], "git_node": "76b60fc774415ef8177c4d209fd26b16e33973b3", "git_parents": ["ceeb3a765b6a18c650e575b48cf1d2a6c441ffc0"], "node": "eb5c6806658768c810d9e25928a8c94f93410c8f", "parents": ["80368b6d5dffac661547f41cad11c2d7a9f1fff2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089313 [wpt PR 64371] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64371\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-anchoring/table-col-and-dead-row-group-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "8902f23b9227f0c166f5560fa364b8ad4f2c7821", "git_parents": ["76b60fc774415ef8177c4d209fd26b16e33973b3"], "node": "fa3e8cdaaad05bf746d7da05b1bf8d1bb4467238", "parents": ["eb5c6806658768c810d9e25928a8c94f93410c8f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089314 [wpt PR 64321] - script: Remove the `\u003cinput type=file\u003e` button activation workaround, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nscript: Remove the `\u003cinput type=file\u003e` button activation workaround\n\nThis workaround was causing a panic when clicking on a disabled file\ninput. Instead of manually triggering the activation behavior on the\n`\u003cinput\u003e` when the button is clicked, mark the shadow tree button\nnon-activable. This causes the activation to happen on an ancestor. In\naddition, bring a couple of these methods closer to the specification\ntext.\n\nThis fixes a panic when clicking on a disabled `\u003cinput type=file\u003e`.\n\nSigned-off-by: Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ac2b73f31dac7448aa9b415d70251006fad39e43\nwpt-pr: 64321\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-input-element/disabled-file-input-click-crash.html"], "git_node": "5e2e5e7d38c8ccdb3ac999b2d3774d90dc7ae1c7", "git_parents": ["8902f23b9227f0c166f5560fa364b8ad4f2c7821"], "node": "7d317ec8275f7d5f71f2e10b11efe60df859ba09", "parents": ["fa3e8cdaaad05bf746d7da05b1bf8d1bb4467238"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mahesh Kannan \u003ckmaheshb@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089316 [wpt PR 64335] - [WebAudio] Fire processorerror instead of error at AudioWorkletNode, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebAudio] Fire processorerror instead of error at AudioWorkletNode\n\nEnsure addEventListener(\"processorerror\") works on AudioWorkletNode as\nprescribed by the WebAudio spec. Previously, AudioWorkletNode\ndispatched an ErrorEvent with type \"error\" and bound onprocessorerror\nto \"error\", so addEventListener(\"processorerror\") never fired.\n\nRe-add \"processorerror\" to event_type_names.json5 and gate switching\nboth onprocessorerror and the dispatched ErrorEvent type behind the\nstable AudioWorkletProcessorErrorEventType flag.\n\nBug: 573625316\nTest: audioworkletnode-onerror.https.html\nChange-Id: I1029c29ac629cc4885da63194202651ef56649ce\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8665592\nReviewed-by: Michael Wilson \u003cmjwilson@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Mahesh Kannan \u003ckmaheshb@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1729803}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1c72cdbad806aa69c4b3b56da9009663cf12daf4\nwpt-pr: 64335\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audioworklet-interface/audioworkletnode-onerror.https.html"], "git_node": "adc59309bd22089048a63e7ad995e5a3fc9130e5", "git_parents": ["5e2e5e7d38c8ccdb3ac999b2d3774d90dc7ae1c7"], "node": "09625a36dae3a3c50bf6a21b5d9dc544ab49bb62", "parents": ["7d317ec8275f7d5f71f2e10b11efe60df859ba09"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Guohui Deng \u003cguohuideng@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089318 [wpt PR 64338] - [WPT] Fixes in /wpt/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WPT] Fixes in /wpt/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url\n\nThese are mostly style changes, with a few minor fixes that do not\nchange what the tests check. Some test titles and subtest names were\ncorrected.\n\nBug: 40919714\nChange-Id: I873e44f23de55e512765397f056bc8b8117222cf\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8663690\nCommit-Queue: Guohui Deng \u003cguohuideng@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Guohui Deng \u003cguohuideng@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Scott Haseley \u003cshaseley@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1729838}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9c169dd73b5be5d1eb3c46afbc13c02ef76c5a5f\nwpt-pr: 64338\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/resources/message-handler-in-shared-worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/resources/message-handler-in-worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/resources/test-initiator.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/dedicated-worker-script.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/direct.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/event-handler-overwritten.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/event-handler.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/external-script-in-posted-task.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/external-script.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/iframe-post-message.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/inline-document-write.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/inline-script.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/module-script-from-document.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/module-script-from-dynamic-importer.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/module-script-from-static-importer.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/module-script-from-worker.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/post-message-shared-worker.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/post-message-worker.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/post-task.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/post-task.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/promise.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/promise.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/queue-microtask.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/queue-microtask.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/request-animation-frame.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/request-idle-callback.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/set-interval.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/set-interval.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/set-timeout.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/set-timeout.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/static-resource.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/stylesheet-dynamic.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/stylesheet-static.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/xml-http-request.html"], "git_node": "9bdbba4219a90062e8df3e4bc8dc5de098f8b9d7", "git_parents": ["adc59309bd22089048a63e7ad995e5a3fc9130e5"], "node": "da1c29c3f18ba8743d46b64206afc3f67a42bdce", "parents": ["09625a36dae3a3c50bf6a21b5d9dc544ab49bb62"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089318 [wpt PR 64338] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64338\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/promise.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/request-idle-callback.html.ini"], "git_node": "9b306a00e1b8359566a9b31475d32073ad926fd0", "git_parents": ["9bdbba4219a90062e8df3e4bc8dc5de098f8b9d7"], "node": "6611cf7bc904d922ffdd877c9e1a528c046527ba", "parents": ["da1c29c3f18ba8743d46b64206afc3f67a42bdce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Guohui Deng \u003cguohuideng@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089319 [wpt PR 64337] - Prevent cross-origin information leak by LoAF userTimingEntries, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nPrevent cross-origin information leak by LoAF userTimingEntries\n\nUser timing entries are now checked against the origin of the document\nthat reads them, both when they are accessed directly and when a\nconditional measure resolves a mark, so they are no longer leaked\ncross-origin.\n\nBug: 557288873\nChange-Id: I4c1fe3837283c3a2df257ec11478816c7e2c9d5f\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8434022\nReviewed-by: Scott Haseley \u003cshaseley@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Guohui Deng \u003cguohuideng@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Guohui Deng \u003cguohuideng@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1729853}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 93c3ac81c84673924557a71d485ffd4b589f1d59\nwpt-pr: 64337\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/conditional-measure-iframe-time-origin.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/conditional-user-timing-basic.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/conditional-user-timing-cross-origin-measure.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/conditional-user-timing-cross-origin-measure.tentative.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/conditional-user-timing-cross-origin.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/conditional-user-timing-cross-origin.tentative.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/conditional-user-timing-detached-window.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/conditional-user-timing-same-origin.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/resources/conditional-user-timing-iframe.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/resources/conditional-user-timing-iframe.html.headers"], "git_node": "1334ee7d709a61852fae12053a71f815c75b44b4", "git_parents": ["9b306a00e1b8359566a9b31475d32073ad926fd0"], "node": "142818a63b9c495644bb6732c654049f4e821171", "parents": ["6611cf7bc904d922ffdd877c9e1a528c046527ba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brandon Jones \u003cbajones@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089320 [wpt PR 64331] - Mark Opaque XR framebuffers as incomplete on session end, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMark Opaque XR framebuffers as incomplete on session end\n\nEnsures that Opaque framebuffers created by WebXR are always marked\nas incomplete at the end of an XR frame, even if the session ended\nduring the frame.\n\nAs an additional guard against accessing orphaned shared image\ntexture handles via an opaque framebuffer, ensure that the color\ntextures are detached from the framebuffer when the frame ends.\n\nFixed: 578670966\nChange-Id: I67525e51b7eaf7cac5703ba2f2c9bd604aa53b38\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8665766\nReviewed-by: Brian Sheedy \u003cbsheedy@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Brandon Jones \u003cbajones@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1729896}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b719612f963a05ece9c89a7dd7598c1c59618874\nwpt-pr: 64331\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webxr/xrWebGLLayer_opaque_framebuffer.https.html"], "git_node": "407be60f851fb787cf113ab670fd7b941120e62f", "git_parents": ["1334ee7d709a61852fae12053a71f815c75b44b4"], "node": "6d8a001cd9e2e8c8fe81589eeb9fdd3c2c5a82f1", "parents": ["142818a63b9c495644bb6732c654049f4e821171"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tannal \u003cmtan@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085317 [wpt PR 63978] - [Sanitizer] Add WPT coverage for all default safe MathML elements and attributes, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Sanitizer] Add WPT coverage for all default safe MathML elements and attributes\n\nAdd WPT for Sanitizer API covering all default safe MathML elements and\ntheir allowed attributes.\n\nAdd end to end tests to ensure that clicking sanitized 'a' elements\n(HTML, SVG, and MathML) cannot trigger unsafe navigations/executions.\n\nSpec change in sanitizer api for MathML a element:\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12592\n\nAlso update the default configuration in `sanitizer-default-config.html`\n\nBug: 510487697\nChange-Id: I1fddafd008713c454a0cb3c0061e817d5f42d338\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8212842\nReviewed-by: Daniel Vogelheim \u003cvogelheim@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1729970}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 198cc91d4e5d24def16a19b8e2ec027fa5e5135d\nwpt-pr: 63978\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-a-navigation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-default-config.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-mathml-elements.html"], "git_node": "f5a0e978c7fc822482a856a5a7b38d5f2d4b774a", "git_parents": ["407be60f851fb787cf113ab670fd7b941120e62f"], "node": "89fa70d35d287480c52612eaa60e84b24614708f", "parents": ["6d8a001cd9e2e8c8fe81589eeb9fdd3c2c5a82f1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085317 [wpt PR 63978] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63978\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-a-navigation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-default-config.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-mathml-elements.html.ini"], "git_node": "9741dce9b18c796aeef35aa6381e4c99e819fd0d", "git_parents": ["f5a0e978c7fc822482a856a5a7b38d5f2d4b774a"], "node": "3000a8f9f8569b87eb6b32e8ed7a8608c546dd33", "parents": ["89fa70d35d287480c52612eaa60e84b24614708f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jose Dapena Paz \u003cjdapena@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089321 [wpt PR 64373] - ContainerTiming WPT: move tests to promise_test, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nContainerTiming WPT: move tests to promise_test\n\nThe tests chained observer callbacks, step_func wrappers and t.done()\ncalls. Rewrite them as promise_test with await, so each test reads top\nto bottom, using new helpers:\n- getContainerEntries() waits for a minimum number of entries, with a\n  timeout, and then for every other pending paint, so the tests now\n  check the full list of entries and catch extra or late ones.\n- waitForPendingPaints() replaces waitAfterTest(). It waits for the\n  entry of an image that is its own container root, instead of an\n  element timing entry with a two-second timeout fallback, so the tests\n  no longer depend on Element Timing.\n- waitWithoutObserving() and getContainerEntriesWithin() wait with a\n  timeout, for the tests that must not observe container entries while\n  painting.\n\nThis also:\n- Asserts an empty entry list in the tests expecting no entries, instead\n  of calling assert_unreached() from observer callbacks that were not\n  wrapped in step_func, where a failure was reported as a harness error.\n- Removes the script-scope beforeRender and img globals.\n- Uses type: 'container' for every observer, instead of a mix with\n  entryTypes.\n\nThe image added by waitForPendingPaints() is fixed in the viewport and\nremoved once reported: otherwise, in\ncontainertiming-body-with-child-img.html, the whitespace next to it\npainted as text inside the \u003cbody\u003e container root.\n\nChange-Id: Ic1bb998bae278b8d86566bfce9e781f40964ee68\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8629364\nCommit-Queue: Jos\u00e9 Dapena Paz \u003cjdapena@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Scott Haseley \u003cshaseley@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1731251}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7fd42b513e653557b7aaec963ba3e0da6a1f1b7f\nwpt-pr: 64373\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/resources/container-timing-helpers.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-and-ignore-on-img-itself.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-and-ignore-on-text-itself.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-body-with-child-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-img-already-loaded.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-img-itself.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-largest-painted-element-own-area.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-largest-painted-element.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-observe-after-paint-with-buffering.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-observe-after-paint-without-buffering.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-observe-no-paint.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-text-itself.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-two-overlapping-imgs.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-with-child-ignore-and-child-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-with-child-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-with-child-text.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-with-ignore-and-child-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/iframe-isolation-cross-origin.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/iframe-isolation-same-origin.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/ignore-with-containertiming-and-child-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/img-not-child-of-container-timing.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-and-ignore-on-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-and-ignore-on-text.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-child-img-with-ignore.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-child-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-on-img-without-ignore.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-with-ignore.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/pseudo-background-image-before-in-container-timing.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/pseudo-with-image-content-in-container-timing.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/pseudo-with-text-content-in-container-timing.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/resources/iframe-isolation-subframe.html"], "git_node": "e2d30fe3c5658b47edc6a23a9fb2f564f6f357d2", "git_parents": ["9741dce9b18c796aeef35aa6381e4c99e819fd0d"], "node": "243386c80bf57e404edeeb857a17c8da00e87103", "parents": ["3000a8f9f8569b87eb6b32e8ed7a8608c546dd33"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089321 [wpt PR 64373] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64373\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-and-ignore-on-img-itself.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-and-ignore-on-text-itself.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-attribute-reflection.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-body-with-child-img.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-clips-to-viewport.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-html-elements-only.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-img-already-loaded.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-img-itself.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-large-container-size.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-largest-painted-element-own-area.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-largest-painted-element.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-last-painted-element.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-movebefore-preserves-region.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-observe-after-paint-with-buffering.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-observe-after-paint-without-buffering.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-observe-no-paint.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-reconnect-empties-region.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-repaint.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-shadow-tree-excluded.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-text-itself.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-two-overlapping-imgs.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-with-child-canvas.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-with-child-ignore-and-child-img.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-with-child-img.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-with-child-text.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-with-child-video.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-with-ignore-and-child-img.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/iframe-isolation-cross-origin.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/iframe-isolation-same-origin.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/ignore-with-containertiming-and-child-img.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/img-not-child-of-container-timing.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-and-ignore-on-img.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-and-ignore-on-text.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-child-img-with-ignore.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-child-img.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-on-img-without-ignore.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-with-ignore.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/pseudo-background-image-before-in-container-timing.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/pseudo-with-image-content-in-container-timing.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/pseudo-with-text-content-in-container-timing.html.ini"], "git_node": "c2aeb1c646acee67e48208175058ee2239746f5f", "git_parents": ["e2d30fe3c5658b47edc6a23a9fb2f564f6f357d2"], "node": "beb50f1613dce4500c280658ad7eb3e8815981dc", "parents": ["243386c80bf57e404edeeb857a17c8da00e87103"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Domenic Denicola \u003cd@domenic.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078031 [wpt PR 63244] - Let the stash manager allocate its own TCP port, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nLet the stash manager allocate its own TCP port\n\nWhen binding the stash to the configured server host, wpt serve first probes for an available port and closes the probe socket before starting the manager. Another listener can claim that port in between, causing the manager to fail with EADDRINUSE and abort server startup.\n\nPass port 0 directly to the manager instead. Its existing startup protocol returns the bound address, which StashServer already publishes to workers through WPT_STASH_CONFIG.\n\nCo-authored-by: codex \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7120511adae8edcd71f947c11afe13277a922aa6\nwpt-pr: 63244\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/tools/serve/serve.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/serve/test_serve.py"], "git_node": "41109ebbba6d79eefc4f583a489d34fe5ef0cb0e", "git_parents": ["c2aeb1c646acee67e48208175058ee2239746f5f"], "node": "9e6f2149bfc190224797461dc931e835080b3582", "parents": ["beb50f1613dce4500c280658ad7eb3e8815981dc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stalgia Grigg \u003cstalgiag@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089322 [wpt PR 63425] - Re-enable generic-sensor screen referenceFrame test, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRe-enable generic-sensor screen referenceFrame test (#63425)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7e1243dd51da4162ea4a0b0e539b40db0144b22c\nwpt-pr: 63425\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/generic-sensor/generic-sensor-tests.js"], "git_node": "d11bc97fbd018bd3052924bb84f20786bdb756d1", "git_parents": ["41109ebbba6d79eefc4f583a489d34fe5ef0cb0e"], "node": "e4761ff8298b6d1b76705ed2d0292037880eaa76", "parents": ["9e6f2149bfc190224797461dc931e835080b3582"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089323 [wpt PR 64347] - wpt: Add tests for resolved inset for relpos inline and block-in-inline, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd tests for resolved inset for relpos inline and block-in-inline\n\nSigned-off-by: Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2d5191b69aaa11f91720c5cc0891af704ef885f3\nwpt-pr: 64347\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom/getComputedStyle-insets-relpos-block-in-inline.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom/getComputedStyle-insets-relpos-inline-002.html"], "git_node": "20d25f2faa2b5b0932c12162495601415fe461e1", "git_parents": ["d11bc97fbd018bd3052924bb84f20786bdb756d1"], "node": "93f007860b8e2c1ab8169b448d50a84c8fe9f658", "parents": ["e4761ff8298b6d1b76705ed2d0292037880eaa76"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stalgia Grigg \u003cstalgiag@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089324 [wpt PR 64350] - Cookie Store API: Stop cookieStore_set_path from leaking a cookie, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nStop cookieStore_set_path from leaking a cookie (#64350)\n\nThe first subtest of cookieStore_set_path.https.window.js cleans up with cookieStore.delete(), which misses the cookie in Chrome (crbug 402779102). When the directory runs in one session, the leftover cookie fails httponly_cookies and serviceworker_cookieStore_cross_origin. This cleans up over HTTP instead (following after the set and delete argument tests) and registers the first httponly_cookies cleanup earlier so one failure doesn't leak into subsequent subtests.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e444a63c5f2e41d92620dc0cd2d2d89335ca9b22\nwpt-pr: 64350\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/cookiestore/cookieStore_set_path.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/cookiestore/httponly_cookies.https.window.js"], "git_node": "54daa9006224b8a572c82add5f9e12273154c1b4", "git_parents": ["20d25f2faa2b5b0932c12162495601415fe461e1"], "node": "824f133d3d262990a43833032d6aa1c9efdfe2ed", "parents": ["93f007860b8e2c1ab8169b448d50a84c8fe9f658"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matt Hargett \u003cplaztiksyke@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085259 [wpt PR 63970] - WebNN: cover int8 gather tables followed by cast, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebNN: cover int8 gather tables followed by cast (#63970)\n\n* test(webnn): cover int8 gather tables followed by cast\n\nCover a signed 8-bit table read by gather and widened by cast, including negative entries, repeated indices and index values at the table edges. The expected values are exact. Chrome Canary 158.0.8112.0 (macOS) passes all cases on the cpu, gpu and npu variants. Found while lowering quantized embedding tables, where a backend narrowed the table to unsigned bytes before the cast.\n\n* test(webnn): add runtime int8 tables to the gather/cast cases\n\nFeed the int8 table as a runtime input to gather -\u003e cast and to\ncast -\u003e gather. The cast tests widen only non-negative runtime int8\nvalues, so these are the cases where a runtime int8 operand read as\nunsigned shows. On A12 devices with Core ML's CPU and Neural Engine\ncompute units, RustNN's CoreML backend reads the runtime int8 value\n-124 as 132 in the dequantizeLinear broadcast case.\n\nValidation: expected values recomputed from the table; WPT lint; Chrome\nCanary 158.0.8112.0 on M4 Max (macOS 27.2) passes all eight tests on\nthe cpu, gpu and npu variants, and a control copy that delivers the\ntable as uint8 fails all eight on each variant.\n\n* Update webnn/conformance_tests/gather-cast-int8-table.https.any.js\n\nCo-authored-by: Dwayne Robinson \u003cfdwr@hotmail.com\u003e\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dwayne Robinson \u003cfdwr@hotmail.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1448e6a1c945fb1ae777b2f5ea4f41670613c212\nwpt-pr: 63970\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/conformance_tests/gather-cast-int8-table.https.any.js"], "git_node": "73f5b8d1a2d8cda0f88009769684671aa1163a24", "git_parents": ["54daa9006224b8a572c82add5f9e12273154c1b4"], "node": "35a22013623cc8338dd002187e73976737ba0d1c", "parents": ["824f133d3d262990a43833032d6aa1c9efdfe2ed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089325 [wpt PR 64343] - Make printing/mask-and-opacity-offset-print.html pass in Blink., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMake printing/mask-and-opacity-offset-print.html pass in Blink.\n\nSet a page width large enough not to trigger Blink's scale-to-fit\nmechanism, since that causes sub-pixel differences.\n\nThe default page box size is 5in by 3in, with 0.5in of margins on each\nside.\n\nBug: 579038778\nChange-Id: I12bd5ae3bb45eb5d0e3232cbb47ce0eae86a9a25\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8678459\nCommit-Queue: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1730125}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: cf149160927047ce8b8a8deb9408664db0ef643b\nwpt-pr: 64343\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/printing/mask-and-opacity-offset-print-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/printing/mask-and-opacity-offset-print.html"], "git_node": "c78f649362661b97223e9089cbc4696fe5972e30", "git_parents": ["73f5b8d1a2d8cda0f88009769684671aa1163a24"], "node": "c7bb869ccf5cf237898e534dc3a1f0d2be153c26", "parents": ["35a22013623cc8338dd002187e73976737ba0d1c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089325 [wpt PR 64343] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64343\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/printing/mask-and-opacity-offset-print.html.ini"], "git_node": "cfd262a43c732947d2baa011c1cc609f527df1e2", "git_parents": ["c78f649362661b97223e9089cbc4696fe5972e30"], "node": "e5f7b5f1c0bf0e4afcc87494db4eb3237bf29f1d", "parents": ["c7bb869ccf5cf237898e534dc3a1f0d2be153c26"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eldar Pulatov \u003cepulatov.dev@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089326 [wpt PR 64374] - [css] Enable Georgian uppercase text-transforms, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css] Enable Georgian uppercase text-transforms\n\nSo CSS text-transform: uppercase leaves Mkhedruli unchanged and even\nlowercases existing Mtavruli capitals. The workaround in\nhttps://crrev.com/c/1205712 reversed ICU's mappings to avoid missing\nglyphs after Unicode 11 introduced Mtavruli in 2018.\n\nAuthors should be able to request Georgian all-caps text through CSS\nwithout replacing the underlying text. Font support has improved a lot\nsince 2018.\n\nUse ICU's mappings by default and add tests.\n\nKeep the legacy mapping behind the GeorgianUppercase kill switch so we\ncan restore it if font regressions are reported in the field. Remove the\nflag, legacy mapping, and flag-specific test two milestones after the\nStable launch if rollback is no longer needed.\n\nThe unicase WPT uses Georgian U+10D0 as an uncased character, but it has\nmapped to U+1C90 under uppercase since Unicode 11. Use uncased Han\nU+4E00 in both the test and reference to preserve the original\nassertion.\n\n- W3C gap analysis:\nhttps://www.w3.org/TR/geor-gap/#transforms\n- Font coverage:\nhttps://www.w3.org/TR/geor-gap/#fonts\n\nBug: 40127672, 40219793\nChange-Id: Ief04450fb9cda0628a034b13d9916ecfc610771d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8618004\nReviewed-by: Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Eldar Pulatov \u003cepulatov.dev@gmail.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1731294}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2f0c5ce2d43d0451c9ad670ed3b90559891f13ff\nwpt-pr: 64374\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/CSS2/text/text-transform-unicase-001-ref.xht", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/CSS2/text/text-transform-unicase-001.xht", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/text-transform/text-transform-georgian.html"], "git_node": "d975da4548e1fb0f0bef0f99809a5f3ce76caf93", "git_parents": ["cfd262a43c732947d2baa011c1cc609f527df1e2"], "node": "4a900a1bd87b0cd3e121d5ac587fb75bdc4742c4", "parents": ["e5f7b5f1c0bf0e4afcc87494db4eb3237bf29f1d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089326 [wpt PR 64374] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64374\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/text/text-transform-unicase-001.xht.ini"], "git_node": "37ab776452c60101acdefb26ad4522960642de10", "git_parents": ["d975da4548e1fb0f0bef0f99809a5f3ce76caf93"], "node": "b3311facfeaa4ff89ebac256e17c770c48814f94", "parents": ["4a900a1bd87b0cd3e121d5ac587fb75bdc4742c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cameron McCormack \u003cheycam@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089328 [wpt PR 64390] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=221124, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRemove the 1ms minimum for setTimeout\n\nLayoutTests/imported/w3c:\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=221124\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/248952@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4f9d9261cbf065866b966a82965d2ba8cd7d1005\nwpt-pr: 64390\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/webappapis/timers/zero-settimeout.any.js"], "git_node": "0d7fd66420d3e06d85a3c1f408ae43c535439f98", "git_parents": ["37ab776452c60101acdefb26ad4522960642de10"], "node": "12b5aa3cf193a86e536489d17b67585eee1e6cc5", "parents": ["b3311facfeaa4ff89ebac256e17c770c48814f94"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alicia Boya Garcia \u003caboya@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089330 [wpt PR 64389] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=248683, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[MSE][GStreamer] Workaround basesink's lack of support for position queries between a non-resetting flush and a pre-roll\n\nWorkaround for upstream GStreamer patch projected to land in GStreamer\n1.24.0: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer/-/merge_requests/3471\nbasesink: Support position queries after non-resetting flushes\n\nBriefly explained, before the fix GStreamer sinks will fail to answer\nposition queries after a FLUSH_STOP(reset_time=FALSE) until they receive\na new segment, even though the sinks in this situation will preserve the\nprevious segment.\n\nThis is particularly a problem for streams with quality changes, such as\nMSE, but potentially also native adaptive streaming implementations, as\nthe currentTime will suddenly reset to zero, and unlike seeks, quality\nchange flushes generally occur automatically without user intervention.\n\nThe bug means that currentTime can reset to zero seemingly randomly when\na stream is flushed for reason other than a seek, notably in MSE, and\nmost notably after https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/3966 finally\ngets landed. This has been seen in failures for the test\nmedia/media-source/media-source-seek-unbuffered.html -- although that\ntest has several simultaneous unrelated issues that need work on.\n\nTo demonstrate the issue in a more isolated case, a new test case has\nbeen added:\n\nmedia-source/mediasource-remove-preserves-currentTime.html\n\nAs of writing there are no plans currently for the patch to be\nofficially backported into the GStreamer 1.22.x series due to concerns\nover making changes on critical paths of critical elements.\n\nTherefore, in order to not suffer this problem in WebKit with any\ncurrently released versions of GStreamer, we need a workaround.\n\nThis is a difficult bug to work around: you can add probes that capture\nqueries flowing through a pipeline, but you cannot add a probe that\ncaptures a query that is sent directly to an element without going\nthrough any pads (e.g. with gst_element_query_position()). Unfortunately\nthis is more often than not how position queries are made.\n\nSince we cannot monkey-patch or probe the position queries for basesink\ndirectly, the workaround is instead based on analysis and manipulation\nof the basesink internals so that gst_base_sink_get_position() won't\nfail in the desired case, by tweaking basesink-\u003ehave_newsegment inside a\nprobe for the FLUSH_STOP event.\n\nI went through lots of different approaches for this workaround over\nweeks, and the workaround method proposed was the final one that was\nable to fix the issue without introducing any regressions in\nLayoutTests.\n\nThis is the second workaround for an issue in GStreamer sinks that takes\nadvantage of re-registering elements. To keep things clean, both\nworkarounds have been grouped in a new file\nGStreamerSinksWorkarounds.cpp, and refactored into classes with similar\ninterfaces.\n\nAlso, now the workarounds can be enabled and disabled independently with\nnew environment variables:\n\n* WEBKIT_GST_WORKAROUND_APP_SINK_FLUSH_CAPS\n* WEBKIT_GST_WORKAROUND_BASE_SINK_POSITION_FLUSH\n\nAllowed values are: ForceEnable, ForceDisabled and UseIfNeeded\n(case-insensitive). The latter enables each workaround only for\nGStreamer versions known to need it.\n\nUseIfNeeded is the default value for both workarounds, but this can be\nchanged at build time if desired by setting the following macros:\n\n* WEBKIT_GST_WORKAROUND_APP_SINK_FLUSH_CAPS_DEFAULT_MODE\n* WEBKIT_GST_WORKAROUND_BASE_SINK_POSITION_FLUSH_DEFAULT_MODE\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=248683\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/264476@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ed0ba7ac1e669ae9dd5fc246b2d900031bcf02ba\nwpt-pr: 64389\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/media-source/mediasource-remove-preserves-currentTime.html"], "git_node": "2c2ee6b6e08772df41bfbec5ac9b6170f359f9ff", "git_parents": ["0d7fd66420d3e06d85a3c1f408ae43c535439f98"], "node": "662de906cb9fb7e7b4a796b3eda239df59746a3d", "parents": ["12b5aa3cf193a86e536489d17b67585eee1e6cc5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "rogerkorantenng \u003crogerkorantenng@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089331 [wpt PR 64121] - script: Use create_a_potential_cors_request_with_claim in htmlmediaelement.rs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nscript: Use create_a_potential_cors_request_with_claim in htmlmediaelement.rs\n\nSigned-off-by: rogerkorantenng \u003crogerkorantenng@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: dee08ed764d2df968e3d1bf9d8dda1b485b01a79\nwpt-pr: 64121\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/loading-the-media-resource/media-blob-url-revoked.window.js"], "git_node": "1ba81819694b2da86cd7bed7625f60c2027df2a4", "git_parents": ["2c2ee6b6e08772df41bfbec5ac9b6170f359f9ff"], "node": "38ede4d353aed94e2cd4885ed3b5e3d1330c3e04", "parents": ["662de906cb9fb7e7b4a796b3eda239df59746a3d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089331 [wpt PR 64121] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64121\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/loading-the-media-resource/media-blob-url-revoked.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "6320480caec7ae1bceee35bbc7ae6d0451f1ee7d", "git_parents": ["1ba81819694b2da86cd7bed7625f60c2027df2a4"], "node": "6237e3b36ddac97e3827349de07010acd2cd0f21", "parents": ["38ede4d353aed94e2cd4885ed3b5e3d1330c3e04"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jose Dapena Paz \u003cjdapena@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089332 [wpt PR 64388] - ContainerTiming WPT: add helpers to build the test content, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nContainerTiming WPT: add helpers to build the test content\n\nMost tests created their container roots, images and text with the same\ncreateElement(), setAttribute() and appendChild() sequence. Add\naddElement(), addContainerRoot(), addSquare100Image() and addText() to\ncontainer-timing-helpers.js and use them, dropping the comments that\nonly described that sequence. Attributes are still set before the\nelement is inserted.\n\nChange-Id: Id25e27c0d0cb53de7746aeed3179a1f6cfd40e48\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8629366\nCommit-Queue: Jos\u00e9 Dapena Paz \u003cjdapena@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Scott Haseley \u003cshaseley@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1731265}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5e2867066f8431e3c29e34863258d6c79ac8c6c2\nwpt-pr: 64388\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/resources/container-timing-helpers.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-and-ignore-on-img-itself.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-and-ignore-on-text-itself.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-body-with-child-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-img-already-loaded.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-img-itself.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-largest-painted-element-own-area.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-largest-painted-element.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-observe-after-paint-with-buffering.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-observe-after-paint-without-buffering.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-observe-no-paint.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-text-itself.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-two-overlapping-imgs.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-with-child-ignore-and-child-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-with-child-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-with-child-text.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-with-ignore-and-child-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/ignore-with-containertiming-and-child-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/img-not-child-of-container-timing.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-and-ignore-on-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-and-ignore-on-text.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-child-img-with-ignore.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-child-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-on-img-without-ignore.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-with-ignore.html"], "git_node": "40e08b496c164ff8348e1eead40eda0d40a7aa07", "git_parents": ["6320480caec7ae1bceee35bbc7ae6d0451f1ee7d"], "node": "07fe29d6a1611b2f6bdc4105a9e98b812ee5f175", "parents": ["6237e3b36ddac97e3827349de07010acd2cd0f21"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089333 [wpt PR 64386] - [FragmentedOofInCb] Resume fragmented OOFs in table layout., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[FragmentedOofInCb] Resume fragmented OOFs in table layout.\n\nIf the table is the containing block of out-of-flow positioned\ndescendants, out-of-flow break tokens may now found directly under the\ntable (and that's not unlawful at all).\n\nThe test coverage for this was low, so added a test that would have\nfailed without this.\n\nBug: 40267498\nChange-Id: Ic86c8c281007af147f7c6c4f9bf26f9c8afd2e1d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8690927\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1731396}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 99d45d53e39441fb7fe6828cc46e7b9da02f0337\nwpt-pr: 64386\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/table/oof-static-pos-percentage-height.html"], "git_node": "33b529084169f5c617d059bf0a80315c436a5fb6", "git_parents": ["40e08b496c164ff8348e1eead40eda0d40a7aa07"], "node": "4c89fa44f6495556c4d5e9a23b18c85ae249a98b", "parents": ["07fe29d6a1611b2f6bdc4105a9e98b812ee5f175"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089333 [wpt PR 64386] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64386\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/table/oof-static-pos-percentage-height.html.ini"], "git_node": "5152634e1f6cb38c2347825b66482832792914b7", "git_parents": ["33b529084169f5c617d059bf0a80315c436a5fb6"], "node": "883d8107286d1a8ee746c25d1a2b07436af2fb8e", "parents": ["4c89fa44f6495556c4d5e9a23b18c85ae249a98b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Luke Warlow \u003clwarlow@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089334 [wpt PR 64376] - script: Fix failing close watcher assertion in dialog element., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nscript: Fix failing close watcher assertion in dialog element.\n\nFixes: #49428\n\nSigned-off-by: Luke Warlow \u003clwarlow@igalia.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 543264c4d119b2b4269ebce17ee7426e5331e5bd\nwpt-pr: 64376\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interactive-elements/the-dialog-element/dialog-set-open-twice-crash.html"], "git_node": "dfdc6e7180d3cf43ffb4783ffdc2c7b25014bd8b", "git_parents": ["5152634e1f6cb38c2347825b66482832792914b7"], "node": "268214d958c91171d8eef22960544c6f1a7a01b1", "parents": ["883d8107286d1a8ee746c25d1a2b07436af2fb8e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Narfinger \u003cNarfinger@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089335 [wpt PR 64372] - wpt: Fix missed edits on readable-byte-stream crashtest tee-from-scroll-crash, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nfix test\n\nSigned-off-by: Narfinger \u003cNarfinger@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n\n--\nUpdate tests/wpt/tests/streams/readable-byte-streams/crashtests/tee-from-scroll-crash.html\n\nCo-authored-by: Tim van der Lippe \u003cTimvdLippe@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\nSigned-off-by: Narfinger \u003cNarfinger@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f73b53ae3d2ccb2263871794204aaf1ae5dff460, 882d8ca86e6fd88edcf2991ebe67f918365e6779\nwpt-pr: 64372\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/streams/readable-byte-streams/crashtests/tee-from-scroll-crash.html"], "git_node": "e443a76ecf38426d343df6a8aefe5cf2b32b32d3", "git_parents": ["dfdc6e7180d3cf43ffb4783ffdc2c7b25014bd8b"], "node": "ff0d5a1f09f1b8939b717517e27a624eeedb0c9a", "parents": ["268214d958c91171d8eef22960544c6f1a7a01b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089335 [wpt PR 64372] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64372\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/streams/readable-byte-streams/crashtests/from-cross-realm-error.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/streams/readable-byte-streams/crashtests/from-cross-realm.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/streams/readable-byte-streams/crashtests/tee-from-scroll-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/streams/readable-byte-streams/crashtests/tee-locked-stream.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "1752857f51d07a8fc284d6810d060d7aa8796d58", "git_parents": ["e443a76ecf38426d343df6a8aefe5cf2b32b32d3"], "node": "43d2414e0d784f688a1bcad6c21b0e394ed664c7", "parents": ["ff0d5a1f09f1b8939b717517e27a624eeedb0c9a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089336 [wpt PR 64320] - script: No longer rely on the incumbent global when getting JSON attributes, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nscript: No longer rely on the incumbent global when getting JSON attributes\n\nThe included test case panicked because it triggered an unhandled\npromise rejection. The stringifier would run as part of that code path\nwithout an incumbent global. This change fixes that in two places:\n\n1. Stringification in this case is wrapped in `run_a_script` so that the\n   settings stack is never empty. Stringification can run code, so this\n   is important.\n2. Instead of getting the incumbent global for `CollectJSONAttributes`,\n   the global is fetched from the object using the SpiderMonkey\n   API. This more closely matches Firefox.\n\nSigned-off-by: Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e1833d20dd6cbf889fc8f4a5e9e75af69e23cb97\nwpt-pr: 64320\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/webappapis/scripting/processing-model-2/unhandled-promise-rejections/promise-rejection-during-parsing-crash.html"], "git_node": "0510c341f72914d4e84809c48b7822f44538f6ee", "git_parents": ["1752857f51d07a8fc284d6810d060d7aa8796d58"], "node": "bcf54d1a5bd418316b85173280e09cb24b5da4bb", "parents": ["43d2414e0d784f688a1bcad6c21b0e394ed664c7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sabb \u003csarafaabbas@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089337 [wpt PR 64326] - net: Cap natural_size fallback by MAX_SVG_PIXMAP_DIMENSION, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nnet: Cap natural_size fallback by MAX_SVG_PIXMAP_DIMENSION in SVG rasterization\n\nSigned-off-by: Sabb \u003csarafaabbas@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 31da0cccec15d2ba07c74c2b7879694204a02e1c\nwpt-pr: 64326\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/crashtests/svg-zero-width-img-crash.html"], "git_node": "df761dd894bb852f33c3577025fc41326cd7a2aa", "git_parents": ["0510c341f72914d4e84809c48b7822f44538f6ee"], "node": "450e34bb7ca7fdc7d8f0e033142284aa9b61d581", "parents": ["bcf54d1a5bd418316b85173280e09cb24b5da4bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vitor Roriz \u003cvitor.roriz@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089338 [wpt PR 64385] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=304530, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\noutlook.com: Microsoft OWA: ETS:Font Mingliu renders malpositioned numbers in Safari\n\nCoreText returns reserved font names like \".Times Fallback\" when\nresolving generic families for certain locales (e.g., lang=\"en-US\"\nwith font-family: serif). Font names starting with '.' are reserved\nfor system use and must be created via CTFontCreateUIFontForLanguage(),\nnot standard font lookup.\n\nWebKit cannot look up these reserved names, causing the generic family\nto fail and the cascade to continue. This resulted in incorrect font\nselection where text would fall through to emoji fonts.\n\nFix by rejecting font names starting with '.' in platformResolveGenericFamily()\nand using settings-based resolution instead.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=304530\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/304809@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2051edd5c14da7f7af76888453563fc5e50d286b\nwpt-pr: 64385\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/generic-family-lang-attr-cascade-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/generic-family-lang-attr-cascade.html"], "git_node": "1cbeef698e8f87d612059a4e3eb582ef47d24bd4", "git_parents": ["df761dd894bb852f33c3577025fc41326cd7a2aa"], "node": "f5e7278c0e57df3501169df07d51453d320f7bef", "parents": ["450e34bb7ca7fdc7d8f0e033142284aa9b61d581"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089338 [wpt PR 64385] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64385\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-fonts/generic-family-lang-attr-cascade.html.ini"], "git_node": "b9d738e833bab52d2a851495881da6418779494f", "git_parents": ["1cbeef698e8f87d612059a4e3eb582ef47d24bd4"], "node": "5a60cd73ff7ae0f8aea202c721c6845a7bec043e", "parents": ["f5e7278c0e57df3501169df07d51453d320f7bef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Taher Ali \u003ctaher_ali@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089339 [wpt PR 64384] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=309281, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSVG elements with unresolved filter references are not rendered\n\nWhen an SVG element references a filter ID that doesn't exist in the\ndocument, the element should still render without any filter applied.\n\nUser impact: On youtube.com in fullscreen mode, the arrow button in the\ncontrols area that navigates to \"More videos\" is invisible because its\nSVG markup references a filter ID that doesn't exist in the document.\nOther browsers display the button correctly.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=309281\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/308809@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4d065ab8a428ba5021c5f89871f2ea28494ab7b0\nwpt-pr: 64384\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/render/reftests/svg-filter-unresolved-reference-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/render/reftests/svg-filter-unresolved-reference.html"], "git_node": "4dca7b5fbffa9c99fdf74c980688be3d6dad196a", "git_parents": ["b9d738e833bab52d2a851495881da6418779494f"], "node": "a9272ed22540f6714173ffd63f105fd4b284840c", "parents": ["5a60cd73ff7ae0f8aea202c721c6845a7bec043e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089340 [wpt PR 64379] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=313879, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[block-in-inline] mercedes-benz.com: `arrow` next to text in menu drop-down is not on same baseline\n\nWhen a block container has align-content: center, WebKit shifts all line\npositions down so content appears centered vertically. This works by calling\nshiftLinesByInBlockDirection, which moves line boxes and also updates the\nactual render position of atomic inline boxes (like images or inline-blocks).\n\nBut it did not update block-level boxes that appear inside inline elements\n(the \"block-in-inline\" case, like \u003cspan\u003e\u003cdiv\u003eX\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/span\u003e). The display\nbox position in the inline content tree was shifted correctly, but the\nRenderBox position -- which is what painting uses -- stayed at (0,0). So the\ncontent appeared at the top instead of centered.\n\nThe fix adds block-level boxes to the same condition that already handles\natomic inline boxes, so their renderer position gets shifted too.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=313879\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/312514@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ba4bb6aa5dc0a855264db7c568cf046c12df0d19\nwpt-pr: 64379\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/blocks/align-content-block-in-inline-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/blocks/align-content-block-in-inline-001.html"], "git_node": "f413091c1b3240bd2c919b4ece8a26a91d1e1968", "git_parents": ["4dca7b5fbffa9c99fdf74c980688be3d6dad196a"], "node": "a03de347ebb966fedfbc5f406d0144bcaff55a0a", "parents": ["a9272ed22540f6714173ffd63f105fd4b284840c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089341 [wpt PR 64377] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=317310, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[replaced] min-width is not honored over max-width when sizing a shrink-to-fit container around a replaced element\n\nWhen a box's used min-width is larger than its max-width, min-width wins: per CSS 2.1\n10.4, max-width is floored to min-width (equivalently, the used width is\nmax(min-width, min(width, max-width))).\n\nRenderReplaced got this right for the used width (see\ncomputeReplacedLogicalWidthRespectingMinMaxWidth(), which clamps as\nmax(min, min(width, max))), but not for the min/max-content contributions computed in\ncomputeIntrinsicLogicalWidthContributions(). There, the explicit fixed min/max-width\nconstraints were applied in the wrong order - min-width first, then max-width - so a\nsmaller max-width clamped the contribution back down and won. As a result a shrink-to-fit\nancestor (e.g. an inline-block) sized to max-width instead of min-width.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=317310\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/315396@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3691d5e2fe5543b4c71d7825bbb43d9dbf78d784\nwpt-pr: 64377\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/replaced-min-width-greater-than-max-width.html"], "git_node": "53dd4d697d8d2e05c390204127495a8e0c2978c7", "git_parents": ["f413091c1b3240bd2c919b4ece8a26a91d1e1968"], "node": "8f621fcc645c811c275734b130f419168f3304be", "parents": ["a03de347ebb966fedfbc5f406d0144bcaff55a0a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089342 [wpt PR 64378] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=316601, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nUnderline is drawn twice on a \u003csup\u003e\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"text-decoration: underline green\"\u003e\n    A\u003cspan style=\"text-decoration: overline green; vertical-align: top\"\u003eB\u003c/span\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\nThe underline should be one line under both \"A\" and the superscript \"B\".\nInstead \"B\" got a second underline at its raised position, so the line\nlooked broken in two.\n\nEach text box paints its slice of the decorations from its decorating-box\nancestors. The span counts as a decorating box for its own overline, but the\nset of lines it painted came from text-decoration-line-in-effect, which also\nincludes the underline propagated from the div. So the raised \"B\" painted that\nunderline again at its own offset, on top of the one the root inline box\nalready draws at the baseline.\n\nA non-root decorating box now keeps only the decorations it originates (its own\ntext-decoration-line); a propagated underline or overline it does not originate\nis dropped, unless a marked text genuinely overrides it. The root inline box\nand \u003ca\u003e/\u003cfont\u003e keep the in-effect decorations. Per css-text-decor a\nvertical-align'd inline takes its parent's underline position.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=316601\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/315220@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c5a905c2d5a96653a601d1f00edd2bbc113aba7d\nwpt-pr: 64378\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/reference/text-decoration-decorating-box-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-decorating-box-002.html"], "git_node": "7fa5f1002aee9fb34425c81067f8f8ea524549da", "git_parents": ["53dd4d697d8d2e05c390204127495a8e0c2978c7"], "node": "5f544bd63f7d124a7f6e8b1aa29aed07b353c97f", "parents": ["8f621fcc645c811c275734b130f419168f3304be"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brent Fulgham \u003cbfulgham@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089343 [wpt PR 64383] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=120499, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFont-faces with different styles should not be mixed in a CSSSegmentedFontFace\n\nThis patch is inspired by a Blink change: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/blink/+/7823ceba809d5c05bffeeb9e732e92fe76fab7e9\n\nBefore this patch, when a glyph for the character to be rendered is not\nin the matched @font-face, glyph from other @font-face (with different\nstyle) in the family or system font with the same name were used as fallback.\nThis behavior does not follow the font matching algorithm\n(http://www.w3.org/TR/css3-fonts/#font-matching-algorithm):\n\n\"6. If no matching face exists or the matched face does not contain a glyph\n    for the character to be rendered, the next family name is selected and\n    the previous three steps repeated. Glyphs from other faces in the family\n    are not considered.\"\n\nPreviously, CSSFontFaceSet::fontFace() was sorting all candidate faces by distance and\nadding all of them to the CSSSegmentedFontFace. This allowed faces with worse-matching\ntraits to supply glyphs for characters covered by their unicode-range, violating the spec.\n\nThe fix uses FontSelectionAlgorithm's filter to eliminate \"non-best\" candidates before\npopulating the segmented face. Only faces that tie at the best distance for all three\nproperties (width, style, weight) are eligible to supply glyphs.\n\nThis work also revealed that the test expectation for fast/text/font-weight-download-3.html\nwas wrong. The previous expected file showed \"Ahem.otf\" being downloaded, which was\nincorrect because it had a font-weight of 900 (while the test restricts weight to 100).\n\nA similar issue needed to be corrected it fast/text/font-weight-fallback.html. The test\nreferences two fonts, one that matches the requested weight, the other having the\ncharacters needed to render the content. Neither font should be used, according to the\nspec, and it should fall back to a system font (which is what Firefox and Chrome do).\nThis test was revised to confirm this behavior works according to spec.\n\nBecause of GTK's installed fonts (at least on the bots) the test results had to be\nrebaselined because the corrected font fallback logic resulted in a slightly different\noutput (Courier is not a viable choice since is not a good match to the required weight\n700) so it resolves to a system font.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=120499\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/309121@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 72b5eb1bc92894547c2d4a41daa3a80c7c7bd472\nwpt-pr: 64383\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/font-face-unicode-range-stretch-isolation-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/font-face-unicode-range-stretch-isolation.html"], "git_node": "609c9467863c19add10a924f8bad324f8ed7330f", "git_parents": ["7fa5f1002aee9fb34425c81067f8f8ea524549da"], "node": "0dbcdd81810eed07045c67185a15cf7fa762129f", "parents": ["5f544bd63f7d124a7f6e8b1aa29aed07b353c97f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089344 [wpt PR 64381] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=313094, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix css/css-writing-modes/margin-collapse-vrl-022.xht\n\nWhen an absolutely positioned element has auto inset (top/left/right/bottom),\nwe compute a \"static position\" - where the element would have been if it\nweren't absolutely positioned. This works fine in most cases, but breaks when the\nparent has an orthogonal writing mode with a flipped axis (vs. the real containing block).\n\nFor example, in vertical-rl the block axis runs right-to-left (flipped compared to\nhorizontal-tb's top-to-bottom). When an absolutely positioned child inside vertical-rl\nuses static position, three things go wrong:\n\n1. The static position is placed at the min edge (left), but it should be at the max\n   edge (right) because vertical-rl's block axis starts from the right.\n\n2. Margins are applied in the wrong direction - margin-right should push the element\n   away from the right edge, but it's treated as a before-margin on the wrong side.\n\n3. After computing the position, there's an adjustment that subtracts the element's\n   height (to convert from bottom-edge to top-edge positioning). This adjustment is\n   wrong when we've already corrected the static position to come from the right edge.\n\nThe fix adds isOrthogonalWithParentFlippedAxis() which detects when the parent's axis\nruns in the reverse direction. When it does: place the static position at the max edge,\nswap the before/after margins, and skip the height adjustment.\n\nThe same logic handles direction:rtl (inline-flipped) with orthogonal children.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=313094\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/311868@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ca49a8372c4e4191d70eeff6bbfe7aff8350188f\nwpt-pr: 64381\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/orthogonal-static-position-margin-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/orthogonal-static-position-margin.html"], "git_node": "972fe75eeeed7eb36a18b691841fe9f57f78804c", "git_parents": ["609c9467863c19add10a924f8bad324f8ed7330f"], "node": "7d99671bc64f6cee2cefda3eddfba72decfa6131", "parents": ["0dbcdd81810eed07045c67185a15cf7fa762129f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sammy Gill \u003csammy.gill@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089345 [wpt PR 64380] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=313028, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nmarketwatch.com: Tapping the \u201cshare\u201d button causes the media controls to shift to the top of the video.\n\nWhen an element goes from display: none to some other display we need to\nfind a spot in the render tree to insert it. This is done by taking said\nelement and its rendering parent and finding its next sibling in the\nrender tree. One of the things that happens is we create an iterator to\ngo over the composed tree in order to find this spot.\n\nHowever, one problem that can arise, which seems to be the source of the\nbug on MarketWatch, is when the element we are creating a renderer for is\npart of some slotted content that is a descendant of elements with\ndisplay: contents.\n\nWhen we try to initialize the context stack, we walk up from the target\nnode to the root. Initially currentContext is set to the targeted node\nand gets updated as we cross different boundaries. However, one thing to\nnote is that if we hit a parent/ancestor that has display: contents we\ndo not update contextCurrent. Then by the time we hit a boundary\nand need to create a Context for the slotted content we use the targeted\nnode to compute the iterator's start and end.\n\nFor the case of the MarketWatch bug the iterator points to the targeted\nnode and the end iterator points to its sibling which is the source of\nthe bug. When we try to traverse the iterator we reach the end (the\nsibling) and that gives us an incorrect insertion point. What should\ninstead happen is that the end should point to the end of the slotted\ncontent, which is the end of the display: contents subtree.\n\nTo fix this we can:\n1.) Detect this case if the node and the current context is not the\nsame *and* the node has display: contents.\n2.) Create a dedicated constructor that will take in a separate node to\ncompute the iterator's end from alongside the current context and root.\nThis can replace the existing one and we can just pass in the same node\nwhich is what we were doing before.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=313028\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/312003@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3a459437419d3f638a81025ffe6ed4f150dd4b21\nwpt-pr: 64380\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/shadow-dom/slot-display-contents-display-toggle-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/shadow-dom/slot-display-contents-display-toggle.html"], "git_node": "44b622be8e802e68afbe57886cf49b6958a59259", "git_parents": ["972fe75eeeed7eb36a18b691841fe9f57f78804c"], "node": "49b81e6e2af4b53e9efe7b9d63e18a3c7778f718", "parents": ["7d99671bc64f6cee2cefda3eddfba72decfa6131"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julio Piubello \u003cjulio@gitstart.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086610 [wpt PR 64206] - [WebDriver BiDi] Test huge-document screenshot clipping at multiple DPRs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebDriver BiDi] Test huge-document screenshot clipping at multiple DPRs\n\nExercise huge-element browsingContext.captureScreenshot clipping with\nan explicit 250x300 CSS viewport at DPR 1 and 3. Hide scrollbars while\nverifying that the 32768x32768 element still expands the document, then\ncompare PNG dimensions with the physical viewport using the existing\nrounding tolerance.\n\nApply the viewport before navigation to avoid laying out the huge\ndocument twice. This adds coverage to the imported WPT test.\n\nBug: 561642182\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.linux:Linux Tests|webdriver_wpt_tests\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.android:android-16-x64-rel|android_webdriver_wpt_tests\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.fyi:linux-surface-embed-rel|surface_embed_chrome_wpt_tests\nCq-Include-Trybots: luci.chromium.try\u200b:android-15-chrome-blink-rel,android-16-x64-rel,linux-surface-embed-rel\nChange-Id: I50e14c9b6a9d4903f045aa5ddf184aeda4af16f7\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8407226\nCommit-Queue: Julio Piubello \u003cjulio@gitstart.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Danil Somsikov \u003cdsv@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1728805}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 44f96522920e7b36e540badac32c5a4561ffeb94\nwpt-pr: 64206\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/capture_screenshot/capture_screenshot.py"], "git_node": "31a9c08a55b5b2f3b455e2679c333e3a04d37cfa", "git_parents": ["44b622be8e802e68afbe57886cf49b6958a59259"], "node": "d3f75e681911e59fbf5ccbb3745c99cb92bc56ac", "parents": ["49b81e6e2af4b53e9efe7b9d63e18a3c7778f718"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086610 [wpt PR 64206] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64206\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/capture_screenshot/capture_screenshot.py.ini"], "git_node": "36f95ef88039bc06e039e45991f0a8b1bd63d05e", "git_parents": ["31a9c08a55b5b2f3b455e2679c333e3a04d37cfa"], "node": "85657b797cad13319d001c0876b0a400f352b69e", "parents": ["d3f75e681911e59fbf5ccbb3745c99cb92bc56ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olga Gerchikov \u003cgerchiko@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089346 [wpt PR 64392] - [VT] Fix hit-test overlays outside scope overflow clips, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[VT] Fix hit-test overlays outside scope overflow clips\n\nScoped view transition overlays can paint outside the scope's overflow\nclip, but hit testing incorrectly rejects hits in that visible area.\n\nAvoid this restriction when the scope has a laid-out ::view-transition\npseudo.\n\nSpec: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-view-transitions-2/#scoped-view-transition-layout\nBug: 577165354\nChange-Id: I289fa9a2ec856b60f54eaab39d70f4dd5bea8380\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8646353\nCommit-Queue: Olga Gerchikov \u003cgerchiko@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1731564}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: bdfb775118d5854a29db24edb2d146655053faa3\nwpt-pr: 64392\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/scoped/hit-test-overflow-clipped-scope.html"], "git_node": "cc87cd26423597e976dd8ff2508bba36ec62201b", "git_parents": ["36f95ef88039bc06e039e45991f0a8b1bd63d05e"], "node": "25e8fb67e2c3dc7fd3ae6f1170aa16982a4d7042", "parents": ["85657b797cad13319d001c0876b0a400f352b69e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089346 [wpt PR 64392] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64392\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-view-transitions/scoped/hit-test-overflow-clipped-scope.html.ini"], "git_node": "000cac9b64faa90416c15a68695da00036ca9700", "git_parents": ["cc87cd26423597e976dd8ff2508bba36ec62201b"], "node": "41614c30c50a2838e265678d458c482a6da9ca04", "parents": ["25e8fb67e2c3dc7fd3ae6f1170aa16982a4d7042"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080559 [wpt PR 63513] - Deflake WPT preload/subresource-integrity.html, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDeflake WPT preload/subresource-integrity.html\n\nSRIPreloadTest in resources/sriharness.js synchronously calls\nverifyNumberOfResourceTimingEntries() inside the subresource's\nonload/onerror handler. In Blink, PerformanceResourceTiming entries for\nmemory-cached resources are queued asynchronously on a one-shot timer in\nResourceFetcher::DidLoadResourceFromMemoryCache(), which can fire\nslightly after onload/onerror. Wait up to 300ms if the expected number\nof ResourceTiming entries has not yet been recorded, matching other\npreload WPT tests (e.g. preload-resource-match.https.html).\n\nAlso add \u003cmeta name=\"timeout\" content=\"long\"\u003e since the test runs 77\npreload+subresource subtests (~97 network requests), and remove the test\nfrom TestExpectations.\n\nBug: 552768634\nChange-Id: Ib7ba8c4981512ec6a046bc7ddfd8e7b5ab9f6d8d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8548814\nCommit-Queue: Ari Chivukula \u003carichiv@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ari Chivukula \u003carichiv@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Mike Taylor \u003cmiketaylr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1715964}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b0e523078380c0653ca64b6a8fda2c1292608463\nwpt-pr: 63513\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/preload/subresource-integrity.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resources/sriharness.js"], "git_node": "181670394829418b4bab5688da1f97b5c3df1098", "git_parents": ["000cac9b64faa90416c15a68695da00036ca9700"], "node": "38f3bcb87557cf923369ee5d46a340ed50d4b393", "parents": ["41614c30c50a2838e265678d458c482a6da9ca04"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089347 [wpt PR 64329] - Prevent dirty slot assignments during layout and frame rect updates, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nPrevent dirty slot assignments during layout and frame rect updates\n\nFlatTreeTraversal::TraverseParent calls Node::AssignedSlot, which\ntriggers SlotAssignment::RecalcAssignment if a shadow root still has\nNeedsSlotAssignmentRecalc() set. During RecalcAssignment,\nHTMLSlotElement::DetachDisplayLockedAssignedNodesLayoutTreeIfNeeded\nsynchronously detaches the layout tree of display-locked assigned\nnodes. If a shadow root remains dirty into layout (e.g.\nBlockNode::AttachScrollMarkers) or frame rect propagation\n(LocalFrameView::PropagateFrameRectsRecursively), detaching the layout\ntree mutates vectors being iterated on the stack, such as\nColumnPseudoElementsVector or LocalFrameView::plugins_.\n\nA slottable Node stores two slot pointers on FlatTreeNodeData:\nassigned_slot_ (the \u003cslot\u003e it is currently slotted into in the flat\ntree as a direct child of that slot's host) and manually_assigned_slot_\n(the candidate \u003cslot\u003e imperatively assigned via\nHTMLSlotElement.prototype.assign(), which the DOM spec requires\npreserving even while the node is outside the shadow host). However,\nBlink also uses SlotAssignmentMode::kManual internally for User-Agent\nshadow roots on \u003cdetails\u003e, \u003cselect\u003e, and \u003coptgroup\u003e, which run\nElement::ManuallyAssignSlots() during\nSlotAssignment::RecalcAssignment() and call ua_slot-\u003eAssign() on their\ncurrent children.\n\nShadow roots could remain dirty past\nSlotAssignmentEngine::RecalcSlotAssignments() for two reasons:\n\n1. HTMLSlotElement::Assign() treated UA slots identically to author\n   slots and shared Node::ManuallyAssignedSlot() for both. When a node\n   previously passed to an author slot's assign() was moved into a\n   \u003cdetails\u003e element, \u003cdetails\u003e's UA slot assignment ran\n   ManuallyAssignSlots() -\u003e content_slot_-\u003eAssign() inside\n   RecalcAssignment(), saw previous_slot = node-\u003eManuallyAssignedSlot()\n   pointing to the author \u003cslot\u003e, erased the node from the author\n   slot's manually_assigned_nodes_, overwrote\n   node-\u003eSetManuallyAssignedSlot(content_slot_), and called\n   DidSlotChange() -\u003e SetNeedsAssignmentRecalc() on the author shadow\n   root mid-recalc. Because\n   SlotAssignmentEngine::RecalcSlotAssignments() performs a single pass\n   over a snapshot of shadow_roots_needing_recalc_, the newly dirtied\n   author shadow root remained dirty after RecalcSlotAssignments()\n   returned. Sharing Node::ManuallyAssignedSlot() also violated the DOM\n   spec by destroying the node's author slot.assign() association when\n   moved into \u003cdetails\u003e (and conversely allowed\n   author_slot.assign(details_child) to steal a child from \u003cdetails\u003e's\n   UA slot).\n\n2. SlotAssignment::DidRemoveSlot() for manual slotting cleared\n   candidate nodes without calling SetNeedsAssignmentRecalc().\n\nThis patch fixes these issues by construction:\n\n- In HTMLSlotElement::Assign(), only read or modify\n  Node::ManuallyAssignedSlot() and previous_slot when\n  !IsInUserAgentShadowRoot(). UA slots only update their own\n  manually_assigned_nodes_ set without touching\n  Node::ManuallyAssignedSlot() or dirtying author shadow roots. In\n  SlotAssignment::FindSlotInManualSlotting(), check the UA slots'\n  ManuallyAssignedNodes() when owner_-\u003eIsUserAgent() is true.\n- Call SetNeedsAssignmentRecalc() in SlotAssignment::DidRemoveSlot()\n  when a removed manual slot had candidate assigned nodes.\n- Add SlotAssignmentRecalcForbiddenScope in\n  LocalFrameView::PerformLayout() and\n  LocalFrameView::PropagateFrameRectsRecursively() to enforce via\n  DCHECK that slot assignment recalculation is never triggered in those\n  phases.\n\nFixed: 576736463, 575533210\nChange-Id: Ib359a4b0ce88d60d6f90fdf5964979c0fdd23878\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8652233\nReviewed-by: Daniel Cheng \u003cdcheng@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Daniel Cheng \u003cdcheng@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1729487}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e6d2f5926d221813d3e1ea7475d805420b81cecc\nwpt-pr: 64329\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scroll-markers/column-scroll-marker-manual-slot-recalc-crash.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/shadow-dom/manual-slot-assignment-with-details.html"], "git_node": "54a0d95b565ee13a7da1df3f280834e6172a8308", "git_parents": ["181670394829418b4bab5688da1f97b5c3df1098"], "node": "9fc71cbe3149315efcbad412f53151d8db2f1e8c", "parents": ["38f3bcb87557cf923369ee5d46a340ed50d4b393"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089348 [wpt PR 64306] - [flex] Remove item_indices vector in FlexLine, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[flex] Remove item_indices vector in FlexLine\n\nitem_indices is not actually necessary in FlexLine, as at the point it\nis created, all flex items are sequential. It is replaced with two\nwtf_size_t's (item count and first index, respectively). Individual item\nindices are then computed on-the-fly.\n\nThis saves overall memory and reduces allocation overhead. Benchmarks\ndemonstrate this:\n\nSpeedometer3: 0.1%\n\nflexbox_with_list_item: 1%\n\nflexbox-deeply-nested-with-ortho-flow: 3.4%\n\nflexbox-nested-rows-and-columns-auto-overflow: 4%\n\nChange-Id: Ib9394a672991e2971e54130f63d15e9ca624a1a2\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8625835\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1728398}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1d50a11e6a0f1e4f2890544d42a77bd92d8fb094\nwpt-pr: 64306\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/shadow-dom/focus-navigation/reading-flow/flex-flow.html"], "git_node": "e47346f35327e90e3facb989ff704b9ca19cacea", "git_parents": ["54a0d95b565ee13a7da1df3f280834e6172a8308"], "node": "8bf9f8e2ba12dba79efd96deb07697797af88c49", "parents": ["9fc71cbe3149315efcbad412f53151d8db2f1e8c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089348 [wpt PR 64306] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64306\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/shadow-dom/focus-navigation/reading-flow/flex-flow.html.ini"], "git_node": "28ff51c95d96a8745637c45a16d4722623aad543", "git_parents": ["e47346f35327e90e3facb989ff704b9ca19cacea"], "node": "85ab8c7c16734983bb5d7cc26d39a6099d352d84", "parents": ["8bf9f8e2ba12dba79efd96deb07697797af88c49"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eriko Kurimoto \u003celkurin@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087047 [wpt PR 64293] - [bfcache] Reland WPT test for WebLocks grant to a worker in BFCache, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[bfcache] Reland WPT test for WebLocks grant to a worker in BFCache\n\nhttps://crrev.com/c/7894097 added a WPT test verifying that a WebLock\ngranted to a dedicated worker in BFCache has its callback deferred\nuntil the page is restored from BFCache, and was later reverted in\nhttps://crrev.com/c/8274931 due to an Android WebView regression.\n\nNow that https://crrev.com/c/8526329 routes TaskType::kWebLocks to the\npausable task queue on frames and workers, reland the WPT test to\nprovide end-to-end BFCache coverage for dedicated workers.\n\nBug: 511277457\nChange-Id: I5112774570000000000000000000000000000001\n\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8667767\nCommit-Queue: Eriko Kurimoto \u003celkurin@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ming-Ying Chung \u003cmych@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1728843}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6f880aaacf5071b9dad909e7cf1b608089328b29\nwpt-pr: 64293\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/back-forward-cache/weblocks-worker.https.window.js"], "git_node": "04ef6749361f37224af16917fcf266c93c035ffc", "git_parents": ["28ff51c95d96a8745637c45a16d4722623aad543"], "node": "362bcde6a99d3353b094a4af6218226827ac33da", "parents": ["85ab8c7c16734983bb5d7cc26d39a6099d352d84"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087047 [wpt PR 64293] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64293\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/back-forward-cache/weblocks-worker.https.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "d16073a9f04b5e15c22335df186b257ae49e2a0a", "git_parents": ["04ef6749361f37224af16917fcf266c93c035ffc"], "node": "8e8e32ebcdd3f1cc4a7ba4f2f43fe5bd04df0df6", "parents": ["362bcde6a99d3353b094a4af6218226827ac33da"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089349 [wpt PR 64305] - Pass OldStyle() to animation updates, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nPass OldStyle() to animation updates\n\nMulti-pass styling such as OOF updates for anchored elements need to\npass the old style stored for the first style update and not use some\nintermediate ComputedStyle from the previous pass.\n\nFixes CHECK() failure trying to set a nullptr ComputedStyle on an\nexisting LayoutObject in RecalcOwnStyle().\n\nAlso, do not start CSS animations when base display remains none.\n\nWhen an element's base style has display:none,\nCSSAnimations::CalculateAnimationUpdate checks\nold_style-\u003eDisplay() != EDisplay::kNone so that already-running CSS\nanimations can continue while display is animated to a non-none value.\n\nHowever, if a Web Animation animated display to a non-none value while\nthe base style was already display:none, a subsequent style recalc (such\nas an animation style change) sees\nold_style-\u003eDisplay() != EDisplay::kNone and attempts to start new CSS\nanimations that did not start during the initial style recalc, failing\nDCHECK(!is_animation_style_change).\n\nOnly start new CSS animations when\nstyle_builder.Display() != EDisplay::kNone or\nold_style-\u003eGetBaseComputedStyleOrThis()-\u003eDisplay() != EDisplay::kNone.\n\nBug: 576322434\nChange-Id: I89dc828bb3e32747611ca23dbd61d859d16a50e7\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8662682\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kevin Ellis \u003ckevers@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1728905}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d227eee27ee68ff64b468ccdeafa9701d1246554\nwpt-pr: 64305\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-animations/crashtests/chrome-bug-576322434.html"], "git_node": "58e3af280650d6cc79035465f358f4d0444ad269", "git_parents": ["d16073a9f04b5e15c22335df186b257ae49e2a0a"], "node": "c673538022acaa0d4e0ff8b7e9932a374af26078", "parents": ["8e8e32ebcdd3f1cc4a7ba4f2f43fe5bd04df0df6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089351 [wpt PR 64304] - webrtc: wire up \"disable\" RtpHeaderEncryptionPolicy, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nwebrtc: wire up \"disable\" RtpHeaderEncryptionPolicy\n\ndefined in\n  https://github.com/w3c/webrtc-extensions/pull/256\n\nBug: webrtc:455813732\nChange-Id: I30bb39cf45f6edc0b22d4bfa1544e235d1ed3de4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8652762\nReviewed-by: Henrik Bostr\u00f6m \u003chbos@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1728909}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3700e2a1a3548ae654c2ccdbc5916577b1f2e78a\nwpt-pr: 64304\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webrtc-extensions/RTCConfiguration-rtpHeaderEncryptionPolicy.html"], "git_node": "f904e155068d37611b90863eb967620fc1da9571", "git_parents": ["58e3af280650d6cc79035465f358f4d0444ad269"], "node": "b4b69b3a12771ccd1e6220d47533a7b7d226c03f", "parents": ["c673538022acaa0d4e0ff8b7e9932a374af26078"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089351 [wpt PR 64304] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64304\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc-extensions/RTCConfiguration-rtpHeaderEncryptionPolicy.html.ini"], "git_node": "e79c3444f635a87e9656637577986c74e4795cbe", "git_parents": ["f904e155068d37611b90863eb967620fc1da9571"], "node": "ce269600e2243f2183c166a956dc2cb25e5d69a6", "parents": ["b4b69b3a12771ccd1e6220d47533a7b7d226c03f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089352 [wpt PR 64318] - Don't clamp line-height percentages to int, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDon't clamp line-height percentages to int\n\nThis was a really old behavior in Blink. Safari behaves similarly, but\nFirefox does not clamp.\n\nBug: 577459422\nChange-Id: Id5954dca4cc1e34751788aaff3b296c05d9f85a4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8667164\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1729133}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c337617bc995ecb57b5e8563c56d6d0b83656305\nwpt-pr: 64318\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/parsing/line-height-computed.html"], "git_node": "e7493e5cc7704247c5485982c7a69f46475417a6", "git_parents": ["e79c3444f635a87e9656637577986c74e4795cbe"], "node": "ac56f7a64b9fb6edd0ba53a19ba3e4faa373dca5", "parents": ["ce269600e2243f2183c166a956dc2cb25e5d69a6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Javier Contreras Tenorio \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089353 [wpt PR 64307] - [gap-decorations] Fix flex rule with space-between, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[gap-decorations] Fix flex rule with space-between\n\nFlex gap decorations place each column rule at the midpoint of the\neffective gap, which is the `gap` plus the space that `justify-content`\ninserts between items.\n\nFor `space-around` and `space-evenly`, these values are equal, so the\nrule was correct. However, I found a bug for `space-between` where with\nexactly two items in a line, there is no space after the last item, so\nthe effective gap was only the `gap` value. As a result, the rule was\npainted next to the second item instead of at the center of the gap.\n\nThis CL records the effective gap size from the space after the first\nitem, which is the space between the first two items.\n\nThis CL adds flex-gap-decorations-070 to cover the three distribution\nvalues.\n\nChange-Id: Ia6fa3aeaf6e39f5ffb1f7a71aa8d5f2b8c2759ab\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8670887\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1729153}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d98de7deabcc3d3d11ee9736afb94107c108cc42\nwpt-pr: 64307\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/flex/flex-gap-decorations-070-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/flex/flex-gap-decorations-070.html"], "git_node": "b72410eb74523a69522bfbdcf0e56f512d0f5009", "git_parents": ["e7493e5cc7704247c5485982c7a69f46475417a6"], "node": "57f72d0257e51f42dd02d272c774c7fbec5ef710", "parents": ["ac56f7a64b9fb6edd0ba53a19ba3e4faa373dca5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089353 [wpt PR 64307] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64307\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/flex/flex-gap-decorations-026-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/flex/flex-gap-decorations-070.html.ini"], "git_node": "c188bce3cbb217fa43c225775bb75d77f52772b1", "git_parents": ["b72410eb74523a69522bfbdcf0e56f512d0f5009"], "node": "31586192695e8eb49db848c248b3a47aff52316c", "parents": ["57f72d0257e51f42dd02d272c774c7fbec5ef710"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089354 [wpt PR 64309] - [masonry] Update visibility to be computed before rule-break, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[masonry] Update visibility to be computed before rule-break\n\nIn line with recent edits to the css-gaps spec, we are updating the\n`rule-visibility` states for grid lanes to be computed pre `rule-break`\nrather than post `rule-break`. The change that introduced\n`rule-visibility` for `grid-lanes` was under the impression that the\nspec would change to apply them post `rule-break`, however after\ndiscussion that turned out to not be the case.\n\nWith this CL, we now compute the visibility state for every lane (gap)\nby checking whether each segment in the gap has a \"empty\" window\nadjacent to it.\n\nThe methods were moved to GapGeometry now since it makes more sense for\nthe utils to be there rather than in the painter.\n\nThe overall complexity class of the gap decorations painter does not\nchange.\n\nSome edits were needed to two WPTs that tested the wrong behavior\nassumed by the previous CL.\n\nhttps://drafts.csswg.org/css-gaps-1/#visibility\n\nChange-Id: I3b14782613df4a8a79dcb504d4b31202fa1c2e78\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8654933\nReviewed-by: Kurt Catti-Schmidt \u003ckschmi@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1729190}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 62d2c3bba44ab44e628ac86cf1ff4904cd90ed21\nwpt-pr: 64309\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-015-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-015.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-016-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-016.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-018-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-018.html"], "git_node": "5bd7d647e0bb7c8ed20d4de78fbcc095c21e7cee", "git_parents": ["c188bce3cbb217fa43c225775bb75d77f52772b1"], "node": "6d3e3a1edbe172b60042f69bf37a36eafec64d41", "parents": ["31586192695e8eb49db848c248b3a47aff52316c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089354 [wpt PR 64309] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64309\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-rule-visibility-items-between-018.html.ini"], "git_node": "07da687adbe188d1d8beaae4e18f783cdd3dafd6", "git_parents": ["5bd7d647e0bb7c8ed20d4de78fbcc095c21e7cee"], "node": "60a427205d931890e1cf525890f2f03557b6a00b", "parents": ["6d3e3a1edbe172b60042f69bf37a36eafec64d41"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kevin Ellis \u003ckevers@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089355 [wpt PR 64317] - [sda] Make ViewTimelineOptions and subject mandatory, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[sda] Make ViewTimelineOptions and subject mandatory\n\nCSSWG issue with resolution:\nhttps://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13959\n\nA ViewTimeline is not useful without a subject, since the subject\nmember is readonly. You essentially have a timeline that is forever\ninactive.  The CSSWG resolved to make ViewTimelineOptions mandatory\nin the constructor, and the subject mandatory within the options.\n\nThis path resolves the remaining interop failure for scroll-\nanimations.\n\nBug: 507395681\nChange-Id: I7dcbcfb68f896f69d87f31a26c253cc0e3c0f83b\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8581323\nReviewed-by: David A \u003cawogbemila@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Kevin Ellis \u003ckevers@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1729196}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 435fdd8fed34335fdac18c4479ff356aebda60af\nwpt-pr: 64317\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/web-animations/interfaces/TimelineTrigger/constructor.html"], "git_node": "9e4a967eaaef9cdd07b0681ae9036c1408148dcc", "git_parents": ["07da687adbe188d1d8beaae4e18f783cdd3dafd6"], "node": "53701ddc8fd2a80d1225274f09d9b4c32469ea5e", "parents": ["60a427205d931890e1cf525890f2f03557b6a00b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089356 [wpt PR 64325] - [HiC] Fix CanvasTransform with CSS object-fit, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[HiC] Fix CanvasTransform with CSS object-fit\n\nWhen CSS object-fit is used the canvas bitmap may not fill the canvas\nelement's layout box or may be clipped or may be rescaled. Previously,\nthis was not accounted for in the CanvasTransform resulting in\nincorrectly positioned elements for hit testing and selection.\n\nFix the issue by keeping the offset for the bitmap in the canvas child\npaint state and then applying it to the canvas transform.\n\nFixed: 567607176\nChange-Id: If19ce2b7dc79db040171a1a89ea0d48ccc28a9ff\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8510719\nCommit-Queue: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1729310}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: fa98b2572d8713316226572d112c2ee8a31b653a\nwpt-pr: 64325\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint-object-fit-contain-tall.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint-object-fit-contain-wide.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint-object-fit-cover-tall.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint-object-fit-cover-wide.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint-object-fit-fill-tall.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint-object-fit-fill-wide.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint-object-fit-none-tall.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint-object-fit-none-wide.tentative.html"], "git_node": "ca25980e2317b38aebb0058218f32e73792885ae", "git_parents": ["9e4a967eaaef9cdd07b0681ae9036c1408148dcc"], "node": "d14518a150bee6d86df8a039285ce73d19e26196", "parents": ["53701ddc8fd2a80d1225274f09d9b4c32469ea5e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089356 [wpt PR 64325] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64325\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint-object-fit-contain-tall.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint-object-fit-contain-wide.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint-object-fit-cover-tall.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint-object-fit-cover-wide.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint-object-fit-fill-tall.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint-object-fit-fill-wide.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint-object-fit-none-tall.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/elementsFromPoint-object-fit-none-wide.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "348a6a4651dbd103ed47e62118c55f4d1d31fcc5", "git_parents": ["ca25980e2317b38aebb0058218f32e73792885ae"], "node": "0ccd598c069a64d4021f8443cbbd698c14577395", "parents": ["d14518a150bee6d86df8a039285ce73d19e26196"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreu Botella \u003cabotella@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089359 [wpt PR 64398] - [line-clamp] Floats shouldn't grow the height of line-clamp containers, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[line-clamp] Floats shouldn't grow the height of line-clamp containers\n\nWhen a line-clamp container clamps, floats before the clamp point\ndon't grow the container past the clamp point. Instead, they get\nclipped to the container's block-end content edge. But when the\ncontainer doesn't clamp, floats can make the container grow beyond the\npoint at which it'd clamp by height. This is our current behavior in\nChromium.\n\nAs per https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/pull/14569, the CSSWG\nresolved that if the line-clamp container doesn't clamp, floats would\nalso not grow the container, and they would also be clipped at the\nblock-end content edge. This CL implements this.\n\nBug: 40336192\nChange-Id: I95375b9b1503ec591c35f9d6f0355f45f97b52cb\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8687857\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Andreu Botella \u003cabotella@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1731607}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 69e8afc1279dc86fede7501d0f2a008f30922ec6\nwpt-pr: 64398\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-floats-016.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-floats-017.html"], "git_node": "0afdb0c7804e71a0ccc06a360d0dce4008741ca5", "git_parents": ["348a6a4651dbd103ed47e62118c55f4d1d31fcc5"], "node": "6d8193c76ca473897866118b61959e0630765984", "parents": ["0ccd598c069a64d4021f8443cbbd698c14577395"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089359 [wpt PR 64398] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64398\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-floats-016.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-floats-017.html.ini"], "git_node": "7fcaab3eaf738c58452e410c343d3bcd4f0622bd", "git_parents": ["0afdb0c7804e71a0ccc06a360d0dce4008741ca5"], "node": "9aa2d7f032af644806bdcd65374430ffa3c29d17", "parents": ["6d8193c76ca473897866118b61959e0630765984"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jessica Cheung \u003cjcheung23@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089360 [wpt PR 64328] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328386, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nOn dentaistudy.com, entry field does not return to initial position after dismissing keyboard\n\nOn dentaistudy.com, which uses `interactive-widget=resizes-content`, the\ntext input moves up when the virtual keyboard appears but does not move\nback down after the keyboard is dismissed. This is a grid layout bug,\nnot an interactive-widget bug: `resizes-content` just makes it easy to\nreproduce, because the keyboard shrinks the page's height: 100dvh grid\nand dismissing it grows the grid back.\n\nThe input sits below an auto row whose grid item has min-height: 0.\nWhen the grid gets shorter, that row correctly shrinks to fit the\nremaining space, and the item is stretched to the smaller row. When the\ngrid gets taller again, the row should grow back to the item's content\nheight, but it stays small, so the input stays where the keyboard moved\nit.\n\nGridTrackSizingAlgorithmStrategy::logicalHeightForGridItem() measures an\nitem by calling layoutIfNeeded() and reading its logicalHeight(). If the\nitem isn't marked for layout, nothing is recomputed, so the row gets the\nitem's old stretched height. This can happen when the grid's intrinsic\nlogical height cache has no value for the item.\n\nclearGridItemOverridingSizesBeforeLayout() removes each item's\noverriding size without marking the item for layout. Now, it flags items\nthat had a block-axis overriding size with\nNeedsLayoutForIntrinsicLogicalHeight.\n\nWhen logicalHeightForGridItem() measures a flagged item that has no\ncached value, it marks the item for layout, so its real content height\nis used. The flag is then cleared, so each item is relaid out at most\nonce per grid layout.\n\nAdd a layout test that exercises replicates this use case with the keyboard.\nAdd a WPT test that exercises this grid layout issue.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328386\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324575@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 38eae4c4e954a51b333baa4fe9f2c2f5e6f4a9da\nwpt-pr: 64328\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/layout-algorithm/grid-auto-row-regrows-after-container-height-shrinks-001.html"], "git_node": "6162e17d9624ffe8101139d6aa3c0a1bbd2a1f91", "git_parents": ["7fcaab3eaf738c58452e410c343d3bcd4f0622bd"], "node": "e5aec0f1b11d15d63d0bb8349b9e6e709e352105", "parents": ["9aa2d7f032af644806bdcd65374430ffa3c29d17"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089361 [wpt PR 64402] - [FragmentedOofInCb] Resume fragmented OOFs in table section., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[FragmentedOofInCb] Resume fragmented OOFs in table section.\n\nIf a table section is the containing block of out-of-flow positioned\ndescendants, out-of-flow break tokens may now found directly under the\nsection.\n\nUpdate BlockChildIterator to skip child tracking for resumed OOFs. Child\ntracking is only used by table section and table row layout, and\nsections/rows cannot have direct OOF children.\n\nThe test coverage for this was non-existent, so add a test that would\nhave failed without this fix.\n\nBug: 40267498\nChange-Id: I2d93dcb4c2391c2bfeb3aa8c52f7a8b841fc3948\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8692448\nCommit-Queue: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1731651}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7895077b7e97e43d4ea09859a3b9040067aff5e1\nwpt-pr: 64402\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/table/oof-static-pos-percentage-height-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/table/oof-static-pos-percentage-height-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/table/oof-static-pos-percentage-height.html"], "git_node": "dce73cf5b7dad2df6faa411a37e59a6fcd91e44f", "git_parents": ["6162e17d9624ffe8101139d6aa3c0a1bbd2a1f91"], "node": "01a1beabce0632fdc1d9aed3b30edc1e93826fd9", "parents": ["e5aec0f1b11d15d63d0bb8349b9e6e709e352105"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089361 [wpt PR 64402] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64402\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/table/oof-static-pos-percentage-height-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/table/oof-static-pos-percentage-height-002.html.ini"], "git_node": "9b56f8821a6ab14c6621febbb37c169f1dfb27e4", "git_parents": ["dce73cf5b7dad2df6faa411a37e59a6fcd91e44f"], "node": "973d8c397da9d6b9dd30cd6cd376c6125575ed45", "parents": ["01a1beabce0632fdc1d9aed3b30edc1e93826fd9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086351 [wpt PR 64288] - Remove \u003c/img\u003e and \u003c/embed\u003e from css-images WPTs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRemove \u003c/img\u003e and \u003c/embed\u003e from css-images WPTs\n\nimg and embed have no end tag. Writing \u003c/img\u003e or \u003c/embed\u003e anyway is a\nparse error, and the parser drops the tag, so the source suggests a\nstructure the document never had. Remove these void end tags from\ncss-images WPTs.\n\nThis CL doesn't introduce any behavioral changes.\n\nBug: 542686202\nChange-Id: Ibfc3556989498439fc6f17a7d451d2cf1b020315\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8221906\nCommit-Queue: Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1728626}\n\n--\nOmit void `\u003c/img\u003e` closing tag in `object-view-box` test generator\n\nThe original PR only touched some generated tests. Need to correct the\ngenerator.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 38ac6cd2214520c511b418b243ce03fb2e0de23d, 6498bfe43015f425496a4c3b870f20391bacd122\nwpt-pr: 64288\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/animation/object-view-box-interpolation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/image-orientation/image-orientation-from-image-content-images.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/image-orientation/image-orientation-none-content-images.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/image-orientation/image-orientation-none-cross-origin-svg.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/image-orientation/reference/image-orientation-from-image-content-images-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/image-orientation/reference/image-orientation-none-content-images-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-fit-containcontainintrinsicsize-png-001e.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-fit-containsize-png-001e.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-contain-intrinsic-size-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-contain-intrinsic-size.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-empty-bounds-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-empty-bounds.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-fit-contain-img-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-fit-contain-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-fit-contain-svg-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-fit-contain-svg.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-fit-cover-img-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-fit-cover-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-fit-cover-svg-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-fit-cover-svg.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-fit-fill-img-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-fit-fill-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-fit-fill-svg-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-fit-fill-svg.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-fit-none-img-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-fit-none-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-fit-none-svg-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-fit-none-svg.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-writing-mode-img-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-writing-mode-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-writing-mode-svg-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-writing-mode-svg.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/tools/generate_object_view_box_tests.py"], "git_node": "36a39c3c723ce359fe84eb08f996efe997b6f8b6", "git_parents": ["9b56f8821a6ab14c6621febbb37c169f1dfb27e4"], "node": "8b01035712d5657da4d53d04cf911b216624c3a3", "parents": ["973d8c397da9d6b9dd30cd6cd376c6125575ed45"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Elika Etemad \u003cfantasai.bugs@inkedblade.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089363 [wpt PR 64387] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=285351, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nConvert (bidi) inline content coordinates for writing-mode: sideways-lr\n\nUpdates the bidi codepath in inline layout to also support sideways-lr output.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=285351\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/288447@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9fc900cfca98718f710174beb121745254589a96\nwpt-pr: 64387\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/sideways-inline-004-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/sideways-inline-004.html"], "git_node": "f92ad95f8f5372c4da9de9acb882c4a08bf0af42", "git_parents": ["36a39c3c723ce359fe84eb08f996efe997b6f8b6"], "node": "167bb28a0727abf6e0f1febb674d85fc03b6337b", "parents": ["8b01035712d5657da4d53d04cf911b216624c3a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089363 [wpt PR 64387] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64387\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-writing-modes/sideways-inline-004.html.ini"], "git_node": "513d8bfb2013774500df41136e312a9ff2122c9b", "git_parents": ["f92ad95f8f5372c4da9de9acb882c4a08bf0af42"], "node": "cac197620a93225bdc04374d0c9a190f787ff9ac", "parents": ["167bb28a0727abf6e0f1febb674d85fc03b6337b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olga Gerchikov \u003cgerchiko@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089364 [wpt PR 64403] - [VT] Skip scoped transitions when scope becomes document root, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[VT] Skip scoped transitions when scope becomes document root\n\nA scoped view transition's element can become the document element after\nthe transition is created. This invalidates an assumption in\nUnsupportedCapture() and triggers a CHECK failure.\n\nTreat this case as an unsupported capture and skip the transition.\n\nChange-Id: I98e05e084e7e34400e37d5010459f642dbd8a4c4\nBug: 578581694\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8672240\nReviewed-by: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Olga Gerchikov \u003cgerchiko@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1731681}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: fb8f9a563e5e709d3e91f080025288bec7eb7f04\nwpt-pr: 64403\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/scoped/scope-becomes-document-element.html"], "git_node": "071c639fa00ec865f36dd7ba0d26f5db6b7e9fb3", "git_parents": ["513d8bfb2013774500df41136e312a9ff2122c9b"], "node": "7d04db727ba591f06120397bf11637c0873a11a3", "parents": ["cac197620a93225bdc04374d0c9a190f787ff9ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089364 [wpt PR 64403] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64403\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-view-transitions/scoped/scope-becomes-document-element.html.ini"], "git_node": "94e9670e686d44068385c0242f74a441698e7ac3", "git_parents": ["071c639fa00ec865f36dd7ba0d26f5db6b7e9fb3"], "node": "b662b9a3678e06312edc594409431c1cbde47689", "parents": ["7d04db727ba591f06120397bf11637c0873a11a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Blink WPT Bot \u003cblink-w3c-test-autoroller@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078477 [wpt PR 63287] - text-detection: Add EnsureReady() and TextDetector.create() API, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\ntext-detection: Add EnsureReady() and TextDetector.create() API (#63287)\n\nAdds EnsureReady() to shape_detection.mojom.TextDetection so callers can\nasynchronously verify text detection backend readiness before performing\ndetection.\n\nIn Blink, exposes the static Promise\u003cTextDetector\u003e TextDetector.create()\nmethod on TextDetector (with UseCounter kTextDetectorCreate) and adds\nWPT tests.\n\nBug: 556760835\nIntent-to-Prototype: https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/P2dn1LHygIU\nChange-Id: I18af6a0bb9e22bb470921421c6372ce2d9f7cdf3\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8384498\nReviewed-by: Tom Sepez \u003ctsepez@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Alvin Ji \u003calvinji@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rob Pitkin \u003crobpitkin@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1711546}\n\nCo-authored-by: Alvin Ji \u003calvinji@chromium.org\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 13f665b1e0a53ca6cbd552ff9507cd8217bbe9fa\nwpt-pr: 63287\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/resources/chromium/mock-textdetection.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/shape-detection/text-detector-create.https.html"], "git_node": "a431ee7e658c1490422f498fc1b68f5e6c03a735", "git_parents": ["94e9670e686d44068385c0242f74a441698e7ac3"], "node": "ee0f2440e6252009935a84481b8e7dee15895c56", "parents": ["b662b9a3678e06312edc594409431c1cbde47689"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vitor Roriz \u003cvitor.roriz@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089365 [wpt PR 64382] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=283538, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nfont downloaded despite no document characters contained within its unicode-range\n\nFonts were being downloaded even when no document characters matched their\nunicode-range. The root cause was primaryFont() using rangeAt(0) as an\nunconditional fallback, which bypasses unicode-range and triggers a download\nfor the font at that range regardless of whether it's needed.\n\nCSS Fonts 4 \u00a75.2 defines the \"first available font\" as the first font whose\nunicode-range includes U+0020 \u2014 whether the font actually contains a space\nglyph doesn't matter, only the CSS descriptor.\n\nApply upstream WPT fix for font-unicode-presented-as-emoji-outline.html\n(add U+0020 to unicode-range so the test font acts as first available font).\n\nRename primary-font-interstitial test to font-face-unicode-range-failing-source-no-effect\nsince it tests that a failing @font-face source with non-matching unicode-range\ndoesn't affect rendering.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=283538\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/309360@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5f46bdb8dc4e1ce02f7879f55db0fa0554191faf\nwpt-pr: 64382\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/font-face-unicode-range-no-match-no-download.html"], "git_node": "19de7cbaea9f7af57301e21b9039b6418211b298", "git_parents": ["a431ee7e658c1490422f498fc1b68f5e6c03a735"], "node": "693d08bccdfd6b0ba6b02ded24120c408d8aeeb5", "parents": ["ee0f2440e6252009935a84481b8e7dee15895c56"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Blink WPT Bot \u003cblink-w3c-test-autoroller@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082338 [wpt PR 63647] - [wdspec] Scale fixed BiDi WPT waits by the timeout multiplier, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[wdspec] Scale fixed BiDi WPT waits by the timeout multiplier (#63647)\n\n- Make BiDi WebDriver WPTs with fixed 1-2 second waits stop timing out\n  and flaking on slow (Debug) builds, and make Web Bluetooth tests fail\n  fast with the real error instead of timing out when requestDevice is\n  rejected without a prompt.\n- setup_blocked_request gave up after 2 seconds and never released\n  requests blocked later, which kept navigations pending until the\n  whole file timed out. The CSP, history traversal and navigation\n  input tests had the same fixed waits, while other helpers already\n  scale waits by timeout_multiplier.\n\nBug: 565712857\nCq-Include-Trybots: luci.chromium.try\u200b:linux-blink-rel\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.linux:Linux Tests|webdriver_wpt_tests\nChange-Id: I11a9359458d05cb3093979efdef8daf19b95366a\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8575200\nCommit-Queue: Nikolay Vitkov \u003cnvitkov@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Nikolay Vitkov \u003cnvitkov@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1718535}\n\nCo-authored-by: Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9a8f2372ba5db2e227d2455e750342abeef66256\nwpt-pr: 63647\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/traverse_history/conftest.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/external/bluetooth/__init__.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/input/perform_actions/navigation.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/script/call_function/csp_tentative.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/script/evaluate/csp_tentative.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/support/bidi/fixtures.py"], "git_node": "b994911ebae4ad13da7eaf006cd6f6ea161fccb7", "git_parents": ["19de7cbaea9f7af57301e21b9039b6418211b298"], "node": "8aae1f980e8405b3964e82e9f0e4a951f677b248", "parents": ["693d08bccdfd6b0ba6b02ded24120c408d8aeeb5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Blink WPT Bot \u003cblink-w3c-test-autoroller@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086271 [wpt PR 64267] - [WebAudio] Guard chunk rendering state during promise resolution, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebAudio] Guard chunk rendering state during promise resolution (#64267)\n\nWhen an incremental render chunk completes, OnChunkRendered() removes\nthe target buffer from pending_render_targets_ before resolving the\nchunk promise. Resolving a promise with an AudioBuffer synchronously\ninvokes any 'then' getter on its prototype chain, allowing re-entrant\nstartRendering() calls to observe an empty queue and start a duplicate\nrender pass for the next chunk.\n\nChanges:\n- Keep the completed target in pending_render_targets_ until Resolve()\n  finishes so re-entrant startRendering() calls only enqueue targets.\n- Re-check IsContextCleared() and kClosed after resolving the chunk\n  promise in OnChunkRendered() before popping the target or starting\n  the next chunk.\n- Stop the offline render thread in CloseInternal() before finishing\n  tail processing or transitioning the context state to kClosed.\n- Promote queue and duplicate-start invariants in OfflineAudioContext\n  and SetSharedRenderTarget() to CHECKs.\n- Add unit tests and WPTs covering re-entrant startRendering() and\n  close() calls from a synchronous thenable getter.\n\nFixed: 577366760\nTest: blink_unittests --gtest_filter=OfflineAudioContextTest.*\nTest: wpt/webaudio/.../offlineaudiocontext-incremental-rendering.html\nChange-Id: I142eff32cf01b18161c7e7ce32cd7cfc97971f60\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8661658\nReviewed-by: Mahesh Kannan \u003ckmaheshb@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Gabriel Brito \u003cgabrielbrito@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Hongchan Choi \u003chongchan@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1728540}\n\nCo-authored-by: Hongchan Choi \u003chongchan@google.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d8b6cb09e2d02145debb53188c98546c719ad423\nwpt-pr: 64267\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-offlineaudiocontext-interface/offlineaudiocontext-incremental-rendering.html"], "git_node": "bd2440d98d68d036c066aa2d5385554a71e65588", "git_parents": ["b994911ebae4ad13da7eaf006cd6f6ea161fccb7"], "node": "5f085962c5b98ab265dae6a61c8bfc7b590143ec", "parents": ["8aae1f980e8405b3964e82e9f0e4a951f677b248"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086271 [wpt PR 64267] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64267\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-offlineaudiocontext-interface/offlineaudiocontext-incremental-rendering.html.ini"], "git_node": "044d0dfd80d6c2df2648fd9d28441d8c9a9656e3", "git_parents": ["bd2440d98d68d036c066aa2d5385554a71e65588"], "node": "225b7d3b01512e05ebce727475dca1acc8884de3", "parents": ["5f085962c5b98ab265dae6a61c8bfc7b590143ec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Blink WPT Bot \u003cblink-w3c-test-autoroller@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089367 [wpt PR 64327] - Remove \u003c/img\u003e from css-images WPTs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRemove \u003c/img\u003e from css-images WPTs (#64327)\n\nimg elements have no end tag. Writing \u003c/img\u003e anyway is a parse error,\nand the parser drops the tag, so the source suggests a structure the\ndocument never had. Remove these void end tags from css-images WPT\ntests.\n\nThis CL doesn't introduce any behavioral changes.\n\nBug: 542686202\nChange-Id: I9816502aaefef1e8e900f535f0d116d2a0130a9f\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8222563\nAuto-Submit: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Andres Regalado Rosas \u003candresrega@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Andres Regalado Rosas \u003candresrega@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1729549}\n\nCo-authored-by: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 73c67a5a84679c5e94fefc6a19d6be0b671abba9\nwpt-pr: 64327\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-negative-bounds-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-negative-bounds.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-property-changed-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-property-changed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-rect-auto-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-rect-auto.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-rect-percentage-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-rect-percentage.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-rect-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-rect.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-same-size-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-same-size.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-size-containment-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-size-containment.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-svg-img-no-size-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-svg-img-no-size.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-xywh-percentage-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-xywh-percentage.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-xywh-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-xywh.html"], "git_node": "eac038f96144c17f18a979ac5f3b1be3afb18a8b", "git_parents": ["044d0dfd80d6c2df2648fd9d28441d8c9a9656e3"], "node": "6d4cdbb129f9743eafbd2efd859832af8b77cb67", "parents": ["225b7d3b01512e05ebce727475dca1acc8884de3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089368 [wpt PR 64345] - script: Cancel and do not run tasks for replaced documents, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nscript: Cancel and do not run tasks for replaced documents\n\nThis change does three things:\n\n1. Reworks the `ScriptThread` message handling logic to be more\n   readable.\n2. Ensures that tasks for closed pipelines are never run.\n3. Cancels tasks when a `Document` is being replaced in a `Window`.\n   This is supposed to happen via \"unload,\" but that does not yet\n   call \"destroy\" on the `Document`.\n\nThis fixes a crash where a promise rejection handler was queued for a\nreplaced `Document` and it was run without a global.\n\nSigned-off-by: Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8fe482cfdfa0938da6864ec6767e09e3cf91ba54\nwpt-pr: 64345\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/navigating-across-documents/initial-empty-document/promise-rejection-after-replacement-crash.html"], "git_node": "412404ba57c25aaa57c8789cc1131700f63fcc30", "git_parents": ["eac038f96144c17f18a979ac5f3b1be3afb18a8b"], "node": "f0e8636883bbc0cd3c91b2718d14ecd7c8f6911d", "parents": ["6d4cdbb129f9743eafbd2efd859832af8b77cb67"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matt Menke \u003cmmenke@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089369 [wpt PR 64409] - Prevent net/ from requesting invalid hostnames., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nPrevent net/ from requesting invalid hostnames.\n\nThe URL spec allows invalid hostnames to appear in URLs. When a webpage\nrequests such a URL, they're passed to net/. net/ will typically fail\nsuch requests as the DNS layer, but if the requests end up not going\nover DNS (e.g., in the case of proxies), we can end up actually trying\nto send an over-the-wire request.\n\nHSTS considers, e.g., http://a!b.c.com not to be a child of\nhttp://c.com, but the cookie code does, which is problematic. While\nsites should be using secure cookies, and not relying on HSTS to protect\ncookies (which has its own lifetimes, max database size, and expiration\ntimes), sites could even then use this to write cookies. So the current\nlogic is not very safe.\n\nThis CL fixes the issue by checking for hostname validity in\nURLRequestHttpJob, and failing requests with ERR_INVALID_URL if the host\nis not valid. This does mean that some domain names that once may have\nworked in niche conditions (like proxies that do weird things) will now\nfail, so this change is guarded by an enabled-by-default base::Feature.\n\nIt looks to me like the cookie spec says domain matching should fail on\nthese domains, so we should additionally change that, but rejecting\ninvalid HTTP URLs, instead of sending them to proxies that might not\nknow how to deal with URLs with invalid hostnames, is also a good idea,\nand is a much simpler fix.\n\nThis CL also updates a couple of tests that now have failing navigations\nas a result of this change.\n\nFixed: 579450551\nChange-Id: I155448b3522625df7b869e225b260429fcb938a7\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8680296\nReviewed-by: Tom Sepez \u003ctsepez@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Adam Rice \u003cricea@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: mmenke \u003cmmenke@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1731887}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 20ba58c70e600862041666a656f5c3a8ad972407\nwpt-pr: 64409\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/origin/relaxing-the-same-origin-restriction/document_domain_setter.html"], "git_node": "cf5671c7557236782c9ffeecfa269e81e3786cac", "git_parents": ["412404ba57c25aaa57c8789cc1131700f63fcc30"], "node": "fc967c832c0be1523865f815b24cc1ae9391f7cb", "parents": ["f0e8636883bbc0cd3c91b2718d14ecd7c8f6911d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089370 [wpt PR 64406] - [HiC] Add rendering tests for canvases with CSS object-fit, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[HiC] Add rendering tests for canvases with CSS object-fit\n\nDrawing into a canvas with CSS object-fit active is non-obvious\ndue to the canvas being resized in CSS coordinates by object-fit.\n\nAdd tests to set the expectations for other vendors implementing\nHTML-in-Canvas, and possibly spark discussion about more intuitive\nbehavior (if such a thing exists).\n\nBug: 567607176\nChange-Id: I5970568fea1b55a3a81feddd3c9567dff149a92d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8664840\nAuto-Submit: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1731948}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b05966edb580b08aea921cff5d5670333e42c7b5\nwpt-pr: 64406\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-object-fit-contain-tall-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-object-fit-contain-tall.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-object-fit-contain-wide-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-object-fit-contain-wide.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-object-fit-cover-tall-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-object-fit-cover-tall.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-object-fit-cover-wide-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-object-fit-cover-wide.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-object-fit-fill-tall-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-object-fit-fill-tall.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-object-fit-fill-wide-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-object-fit-fill-wide.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-object-fit-none-tall-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-object-fit-none-tall.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-object-fit-none-wide-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/css-object-fit-none-wide.tentative.html"], "git_node": "de016d2fc4ff9273be93d6cef96d98644f28ca2e", "git_parents": ["cf5671c7557236782c9ffeecfa269e81e3786cac"], "node": "11f0d74e8beebf6f679853d497a9af0f1687d9be", "parents": ["fc967c832c0be1523865f815b24cc1ae9391f7cb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Felipe Piubello \u003cpiubellofelipe97@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089371 [wpt PR 64340] - Propagate emulated screen info to remote frames, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nPropagate emulated screen info to remote frames\n\nUse effective screen information when initializing and updating remote\nframes so screen emulation reaches cross-origin iframes. Compare previous\nand current effective values for local Screen and ScreenDetails updates,\nchange events and color-gamut invalidation. Keep the original screen\nsnapshot for physical device-scale popup handling.\n\nCover local Screen and ScreenDetails events during apply/reset, and extend\nthe WebDriver BiDi orientation test to cover updates and reset. Remove the\nstale expected failure.\n\nBug: 565674536\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.linux:Linux Tests|webdriver_wpt_tests\nCq-Include-Trybots: luci.chromium.try\u200b:linux-webdriver-bidi-rel,android-15-chrome-blink-rel\nChange-Id: I6cbc174b96fcdec713990acfac2d78d0728f95cf\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8459645\nCommit-Queue: Julio Piubello \u003cjulio@gitstart.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: David Bokan \u003cbokan@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Daniel Cheng \u003cdcheng@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1731998}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d399fdd9635a7f1f76b96967dd8723c0926dcc2f\nwpt-pr: 64340\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/emulation/set_screen_orientation_override/contexts.py"], "git_node": "82696a5138358dbb26b25fa382520a76ba898c1a", "git_parents": ["de016d2fc4ff9273be93d6cef96d98644f28ca2e"], "node": "88c4c60f4c61b54c3aa39cfea997b4db5f4fd7e3", "parents": ["11f0d74e8beebf6f679853d497a9af0f1687d9be"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Euclid Ye \u003cyezhizhenjiakang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089372 [wpt PR 64358] - script: Implement readEntries() state machine + Chromium style batching, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd `FileSystemDirectoryReader` automated tests and helper\n\nSigned-off-by: Euclid Ye \u003cyezhizhenjiakang@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 69b548eb5b89801773133fda4221e589c12c4976\nwpt-pr: 64358\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/entries-api/automated-support.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/entries-api/filesystemdirectoryreader.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/entries-api/filesystementry-getParent.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/entries-api/webkitGetAsEntry.html"], "git_node": "821d6bd6520155e50be01e3761ae520a4d72c46e", "git_parents": ["82696a5138358dbb26b25fa382520a76ba898c1a"], "node": "b224acdcecaa76ad9f15b0ce8992ba8359433ee6", "parents": ["88c4c60f4c61b54c3aa39cfea997b4db5f4fd7e3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089372 [wpt PR 64358] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64358\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/entries-api/filesystemdirectoryreader.html.ini"], "git_node": "607dabbb30a01877f1c74a6a2c8d1ea23993dd0d", "git_parents": ["821d6bd6520155e50be01e3761ae520a4d72c46e"], "node": "60556de65ebcedc189d1f938e288d9c0d4f1d8a5", "parents": ["b224acdcecaa76ad9f15b0ce8992ba8359433ee6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "luci-bisection@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003cluci-bisection@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089373 [wpt PR 64412] - Revert \"Prevent net/ from requesting invalid hostnames.\", a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRevert \"Prevent net/ from requesting invalid hostnames.\"\n\nThis reverts commit 370a8766e850dec28a81f5f0aacc13f1c86eae98.\n\nReason for revert:\nLUCI Bisection has identified this change as the cause of a test failure. See the analysis: https://ci.chromium.org/ui/p/chromium/bisection/test-analysis/b/5706821961515008\n\nSample build with failed test: https://ci.chromium.org/b/8666480168227937233\nAffected test(s):\n[://\\:chrome_wpt_tests!webtest::external/wpt/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/navigate#invalid.py](https://ci.chromium.org/ui/test/chromium/:%2F%2F%5C:chrome_wpt_tests%21webtest::external%2Fwpt%2Fwebdriver%2Ftests%2Fbidi%2Fbrowsing_context%2Fnavigate%23invalid.py?q=VHash%3A0bc243e3f1e70338)\n\nIf this is a false positive, please report it at http://b.corp.google.com/createIssue?component=1199205&description=Analysis%3A+https%3A%2F%2Fci.chromium.org%2Fui%2Fp%2Fchromium%2Fbisection%2Ftest-analysis%2Fb%2F5706821961515008&format=PLAIN&priority=P3&title=Wrongly+blamed+https%3A%2F%2Fchromium-review.googlesource.com%2Fc%2Fchromium%2Fsrc%2F%2B%2F8680296&type=BUG\n\nOriginal change's description:\n\u003e Prevent net/ from requesting invalid hostnames.\n\u003e\n\u003e The URL spec allows invalid hostnames to appear in URLs. When a webpage\n\u003e requests such a URL, they're passed to net/. net/ will typically fail\n\u003e such requests as the DNS layer, but if the requests end up not going\n\u003e over DNS (e.g., in the case of proxies), we can end up actually trying\n\u003e to send an over-the-wire request.\n\u003e\n\u003e HSTS considers, e.g., http://a!b.c.com not to be a child of\n\u003e http://c.com, but the cookie code does, which is problematic. While\n\u003e sites should be using secure cookies, and not relying on HSTS to protect\n\u003e cookies (which has its own lifetimes, max database size, and expiration\n\u003e times), sites could even then use this to write cookies. So the current\n\u003e logic is not very safe.\n\u003e\n\u003e This CL fixes the issue by checking for hostname validity in\n\u003e URLRequestHttpJob, and failing requests with ERR_INVALID_URL if the host\n\u003e is not valid. This does mean that some domain names that once may have\n\u003e worked in niche conditions (like proxies that do weird things) will now\n\u003e fail, so this change is guarded by an enabled-by-default base::Feature.\n\u003e\n\u003e It looks to me like the cookie spec says domain matching should fail on\n\u003e these domains, so we should additionally change that, but rejecting\n\u003e invalid HTTP URLs, instead of sending them to proxies that might not\n\u003e know how to deal with URLs with invalid hostnames, is also a good idea,\n\u003e and is a much simpler fix.\n\u003e\n\u003e This CL also updates a couple of tests that now have failing navigations\n\u003e as a result of this change.\n\u003e\n\u003e Fixed: 579450551\n\u003e Change-Id: I155448b3522625df7b869e225b260429fcb938a7\n\u003e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8680296\n\u003e Reviewed-by: Tom Sepez \u003ctsepez@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Reviewed-by: Adam Rice \u003cricea@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Commit-Queue: mmenke \u003cmmenke@chromium.org\u003e\n\u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1731887}\n\u003e\n\nNo-Presubmit: true\nNo-Tree-Checks: true\nNo-Try: true\nChange-Id: If9f6bbff2180dfb04d5568253996d3c1ad344637\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8692792\nCommit-Queue: Syed AbuTalib \u003clowkey@google.com\u003e\nOwners-Override: Syed AbuTalib \u003clowkey@google.com\u003e\nBot-Commit: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Syed AbuTalib \u003clowkey@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1732059}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4fa34c721570cad34ee7283bf531811eafed6010\nwpt-pr: 64412\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/origin/relaxing-the-same-origin-restriction/document_domain_setter.html"], "git_node": "51ab0f7223bd1e9fad4ac4a3f9407c729a1f691c", "git_parents": ["607dabbb30a01877f1c74a6a2c8d1ea23993dd0d"], "node": "08d6a7c593775908e5ed49a2cea814db9b9cd037", "parents": ["60556de65ebcedc189d1f938e288d9c0d4f1d8a5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Weinig \u003csam@webkit.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089374 [wpt PR 64414] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326836, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n\u003csvg:image\u003e should cause referenced SVG images to treat their own root preserveAspectRatio as none\n\nSVG2 says:\n\n  \"For \u2018image\u2019 elements embedding an SVG image, the \u2018preserveAspectRatio\u2019 attribute on the root element in the\n   referenced SVG image must be ignored, and instead treated as if it had a value of none.\"\n\n    - https://w3c.github.io/svgwg/svg2-draft/embedded.html#ImageElement\n\nTo implement this, we now pass a new flag IgnoreRootPreserveAspectRatio when painting \u003csvg:image\u003e elements\n(both RenderSVGImage and LegacyRenderSVGImage) and implement the rest of the placement sizing via new helpers.\n\nIn the follow on changes we can add support for `object-fit` and `object-position` in this shared placement code.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326836\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/323568@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a16b8f51293a83137fa89af99a203d88f066a133\nwpt-pr: 64414\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-fit-fill-svg-with-natural-size-and-viewbox-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-fit-fill-svg-with-natural-size-and-viewbox.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-does-not-affect-img-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-does-not-affect-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-ignores-svg-root-viewbox-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-ignores-svg-root-viewbox.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-meet-svg-viewbox-only-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-meet-svg-viewbox-only.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-meet-svg-with-size-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-meet-svg-with-size.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-none-animated-viewbox-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-none-animated-viewbox.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-none-shared-document-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-none-shared-document.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-none-svg-viewbox-only-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-none-svg-viewbox-only.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-overrides-svg-root-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-overrides-svg-root.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-slice-svg-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-slice-svg.html"], "git_node": "09f16d51db7e62c12337ba4c9d935155d2966e78", "git_parents": ["51ab0f7223bd1e9fad4ac4a3f9407c729a1f691c"], "node": "f46c52fc0c305cd373da78cc8681d1c7fe776820", "parents": ["08d6a7c593775908e5ed49a2cea814db9b9cd037"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089374 [wpt PR 64414] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64414\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-ignores-svg-root-viewbox.html.ini"], "git_node": "3db9803022da30bcfd00599e8677ae3296c02cb2", "git_parents": ["09f16d51db7e62c12337ba4c9d935155d2966e78"], "node": "ff2eb70e49db61f650f4bf3d43ec602fe6adb4d9", "parents": ["f46c52fc0c305cd373da78cc8681d1c7fe776820"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Domenic Denicola \u003cd@domenic.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078032 [wpt PR 63245] - Use the server process context for the stash, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nUse the server process context for the stash\n\nwpt serve selects a multiprocessing context for its server processes, defaulting to spawn, but starts the stash manager with the platform default instead. On Linux before Python 3.14 that default is fork, so the stash inherits unrelated open sockets and can keep their ports occupied after the parent closes them.\n\nPass the selected context to StashServer as well, so the stash follows the caller's process-start policy along with the HTTP and WebSocket servers.\n\nCo-authored-by: codex \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2d8c2306fa4c8eed2d26fa9161e200a57aaf839f\nwpt-pr: 63245\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/tools/serve/serve.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/tools/serve/test_serve.py"], "git_node": "1816cec235303e8dc49548510c724961023e3841", "git_parents": ["3db9803022da30bcfd00599e8677ae3296c02cb2"], "node": "48d9b31fa4c9f9b4affe0d41ffbb8b379488502d", "parents": ["ff2eb70e49db61f650f4bf3d43ec602fe6adb4d9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sabb \u003csarafaabbas@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089375 [wpt PR 64198] - script: Use encoding_parse_a_url in handle_stylesheet_url, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nscript: Use encoding_parse_a_url in handle_stylesheet_url\n\nSigned-off-by: Sabb \u003csarafaabbas@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: cb6cc97ada2772b2afe668b9fd5cb39a576a5347\nwpt-pr: 64198\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/document-metadata/the-link-element/stylesheet-encoding-parse.html"], "git_node": "3d6c58104aa04d00fbd1e1e0c527186e2472176b", "git_parents": ["1816cec235303e8dc49548510c724961023e3841"], "node": "54908b014f5097c1121a8dcbe02e23c178959b34", "parents": ["48d9b31fa4c9f9b4affe0d41ffbb8b379488502d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Martinez \u003camartinez55@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089376 [wpt PR 64413] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328038, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix the links to svgwg.org to the right url  w3c.github.io/svgwg/\n\nUpdate all https://svgwg.org/* to https://w3c.github.io/svgwg/*\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328038\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324641@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 15b31607c5102637a3401608427e6a05aaaf3849\nwpt-pr: 64413\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-display/display-on-svg-text-content-element.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-fit-fill-svg-with-natural-size-and-viewbox.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/animations/animate-path-additive-sum-both-empty-over-base.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/animations/animate-path-by-animation-empty-base.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/animations/animate-path-from-by-animation-both-empty.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/animations/animate-path-from-by-animation-empty-by.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/animations/animate-path-from-by-animation-empty-from.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/animations/animate-path-from-to-accumulate-sum-empty-base.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/animations/animate-path-from-to-animation-both-empty.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/animations/animate-path-from-to-animation-empty-from.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/animations/animate-path-from-to-animation-empty-to.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/animations/animate-path-to-animation-empty-base.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/animations/animateMotion-path-moveto-only.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/animations/animateMotion-path-zero-length-subpaths.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/animations/scripted/smil-values-empty-segments.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/animations/smil-detach-releases-animated-presentation-attribute.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/animations/smil-values-trailing-semicolon.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/animations/svglengthlist-animation-percentage.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/as-image/sprite-sheet-fractional-size.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-does-not-affect-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-ignores-svg-root-viewbox.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-meet-svg-viewbox-only.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-meet-svg-with-size.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-none-animated-viewbox.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-none-shared-document.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-none-svg-viewbox-only.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-overrides-svg-root.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/embedded/image-preserveaspectratio-slice-svg.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/geometry/svg-length-convert-to-percentage-precision.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/interact/scripted/pointer-events-fill-stroke-hittest.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/interact/scripted/pointer-events-getBoundingClientRect.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/media-fragment-spatial-decimal-values.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/media-fragment-spatial-img-element.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/media-fragment-spatial-invalid-negative-width.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/media-fragment-spatial-invalid-zero-height.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/media-fragment-spatial-invalid-zero-width.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/media-fragment-spatial-last-wins.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/media-fragment-spatial-overflow-clamped-nonzero-origin.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/media-fragment-spatial-overflow-clamped.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/media-fragment-spatial-percent-full.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/media-fragment-spatial-percent-img-element.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/media-fragment-spatial-percent-no-natural-size.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/media-fragment-spatial-percent-nonsquare.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/media-fragment-spatial-percent-viewbox-no-size.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/media-fragment-spatial-percent-zero-size.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/media-fragment-spatial-percent.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/media-fragment-spatial-pixel-explicit.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/media-fragment-spatial-pixel-implicit.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/media-fragment-spatial-viewbox-only.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/media-fragment-spatial-viewbox-width.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/svgview-and-xywh.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/scripted/a.target-dynamic-update.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/path/interfaces/getPathData-css-d-vs-attribute.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/path/interfaces/getPathData-detached-element.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/path/interfaces/getPathData-during-smil-animation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/path/interfaces/getPathData-during-web-animation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/path/interfaces/getPathData-empty-or-missing-d.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/path/interfaces/getPathData-malformed-d.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/path/interfaces/getPathData-normalize.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/path/interfaces/getPathData-segments.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/path/interfaces/setPathData-css-d.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/path/interfaces/setPathData-during-animation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/path/interfaces/setPathData-malformed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/path/interfaces/setPathData-mutation-observer.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/path/interfaces/setPathData-overrides-d.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/path/interfaces/setPathData-plain-object.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/path/interfaces/setPathData-segment-types.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/resources/svg-transform-equals.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/struct/reftests/use-image-href-mutating.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/struct/reftests/use-symbol-inline-css-003.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/attr-style-media-dynamic.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/attr-style-type-dynamic.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/text/reftests/textLength-list-x-spacingAndGlyphs.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/text/reftests/textLength-list-y-spacing.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/text/reftests/textLength-list-y-spacingAndGlyphs.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/text/scripted/getstartpositionofchar-dominant-baseline-shift.html"], "git_node": "5067bbb83301508a516c22965fe10b39bc8166d0", "git_parents": ["3d6c58104aa04d00fbd1e1e0c527186e2472176b"], "node": "ea0711b05593426347e6621cdbb6bc85aaff9a4d", "parents": ["54908b014f5097c1121a8dcbe02e23c178959b34"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089376 [wpt PR 64413] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64413\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/svg/animations/animated-classname-crash.svg.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/linking/reftests/media-fragment-spatial-percent-zero-size.html.ini"], "git_node": "a50c71b694201150f92028e5be4fa7b47b85564d", "git_parents": ["5067bbb83301508a516c22965fe10b39bc8166d0"], "node": "c2be84abcf06c2d333fb183d8dc46b06a977eed5", "parents": ["ea0711b05593426347e6621cdbb6bc85aaff9a4d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Youenn Fablet \u003cyouenn@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089377 [wpt PR 64417] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=305564, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nImplement https://w3c.github.io/webrtc-extensions/#target-latency\n\nWe add RTCConfiguration.targetLatency and compute whether enabling service class accordingly.\nWe remove some no longer needed code.\nWe add an internal API to  query whether service class is enabled for a given peer connection and use that in a test to validate that passing the parameter works fine.\n\nCovered by added tests.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=305564\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/306062@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 06fe5d3288a55bd290c0bd6de7674b224263f874\nwpt-pr: 64417\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webrtc-extensions/targetLatency.html"], "git_node": "451c7cefe811c592d6dcc51171c325978b11b6c9", "git_parents": ["a50c71b694201150f92028e5be4fa7b47b85564d"], "node": "4c768c69b66a1ddb8b69c19df61f632c0613c6e6", "parents": ["c2be84abcf06c2d333fb183d8dc46b06a977eed5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089377 [wpt PR 64417] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64417\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc-extensions/targetLatency.html.ini"], "git_node": "e9fa0471dde198493d69e23ea17b615bb5fbf84d", "git_parents": ["451c7cefe811c592d6dcc51171c325978b11b6c9"], "node": "6ff0ec2fa1b35fa20ba22b70a2a00a682d679fa9", "parents": ["4c768c69b66a1ddb8b69c19df61f632c0613c6e6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fujii Hironori \u003cfujii@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089378 [wpt PR 64418] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=303954, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebXR Hit Test] Distinguish gripSpace of an input source to targetRaySpace\n\nWebXRInputSpace method nativeOriginInformation() always returned\nPlatformXR::InputSourceSpaceType::TargetRay even for gripSpace. It should\nreturn PlatformXR::InputSourceSpaceType::Grip for it.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=303954\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/305117@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6d752d8d354fa74051299849e8ea18528e2aa6ab\nwpt-pr: 64418\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webxr/hit-test/ar_hittest_subscription_inputSources_gripSpace.https.html"], "git_node": "25973a979552b6c1172861974533a8b36d7513f2", "git_parents": ["e9fa0471dde198493d69e23ea17b615bb5fbf84d"], "node": "ea2c57e97fcf4e593f2d5954b42660a0cfb388aa", "parents": ["6ff0ec2fa1b35fa20ba22b70a2a00a682d679fa9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089378 [wpt PR 64418] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64418\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webxr/hit-test/ar_hittest_subscription_inputSources_gripSpace.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "3d36b981038e5dae4d96d6884fa22bc347574ba6", "git_parents": ["25973a979552b6c1172861974533a8b36d7513f2"], "node": "e4582a2c94678e0fc03228419fbf07931e16878c", "parents": ["ea2c57e97fcf4e593f2d5954b42660a0cfb388aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoav Weiss \u003cyoav.weiss@shopify.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089379 [wpt PR 64416] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=306860, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSpeculation Rules: ensure that non-visible anchors with visible descendants get prefetched\n\nAnchor elements with `display: contents` may not be visible but could have visible descendants.\nThe current speculation rules logic doesn't account for that, and prevents prefetches on such elements from working.\nThis fixes that by looking at their descendants and seeing if they are rendered.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=306860\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/306730@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9ffd58b0dd837aa252163151c33d7968b87b9402\nwpt-pr: 64416\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prefetch/document-rules-visibility.https.html"], "git_node": "41ee71daf9cfd48af79f4c9c033da2becc792907", "git_parents": ["3d36b981038e5dae4d96d6884fa22bc347574ba6"], "node": "7d5a9c4bf00a020670cbe6913d9d3d8c10d8a2a6", "parents": ["e4582a2c94678e0fc03228419fbf07931e16878c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089379 [wpt PR 64416] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64416\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prefetch/document-rules-visibility.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "bfd46c87f73af41e59d57cd1722964dfdd231f0b", "git_parents": ["41ee71daf9cfd48af79f4c9c033da2becc792907"], "node": "c734161c193b5bbed527131600e89122f9290cb5", "parents": ["7d5a9c4bf00a020670cbe6913d9d3d8c10d8a2a6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Franco Vieira de Souza \u003cfranco_vieira@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089380 [wpt PR 64419] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=299211, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nImplement EventCounts as maplike\n\nImplements the EventCounts interface as a maplike, which\nprovides methods such as .forEach(), keys(), etc.\n\nEventCounts cannot use the previous maplike implementation\nbecause it would get out of sync after the backing map is\ninitialized. To solve this, we use the trait\nshouldAlwaysInitializeMapLike to decide if the backing map\nshould be reloaded on every access through the wrapper. The trait\nsimply checks for the presence of a marker\n(shouldAlwaysInitializeMapLikeMarker).\n\nThis implementation isn't perfect: although the backing map\nwill be kept up-to-date when accessed through the wrapper,\nit won't be updated if accessed through an iterator generated\nfrom that map. This is documented by the failing test\nevent-timing/event-counts-maplike-iterators-always-updated.html.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=299211\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/300830@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5af2d084f6f31dc6f3aaf36aa1b328c8e48bc202\nwpt-pr: 64419\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/event-timing/event-counts-maplike-iterators-always-updated.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/event-timing/event-counts-maplike-validate-iterators.html"], "git_node": "8ebb303770982b9e6c191ce94e6419d856bac89f", "git_parents": ["bfd46c87f73af41e59d57cd1722964dfdd231f0b"], "node": "cdd65e9f1e2e57773083dcbe9ebee126c53f0a5f", "parents": ["c734161c193b5bbed527131600e89122f9290cb5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Elika Etemad \u003cfantasai.bugs@inkedblade.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089381 [wpt PR 64420] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=285276, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nConvert coordinates properly for floats in writing-mode: sideways-lr\n\nUpdates preparePlacedFloats to convert external floats to logical coordinates,\nand toMarginAndBorderBoxVisualRect to convert logical coordinates out to\nRenderBox coordinates in sideways-lr mode.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=285276\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/288382@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f1760e03b9e459bc09595ee935ddb2b6f970a7f2\nwpt-pr: 64420\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/sideways-inline-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/sideways-inline-003.html"], "git_node": "4447c27f93b8cbd1b223d256b0fbd5a5b062e7d4", "git_parents": ["8ebb303770982b9e6c191ce94e6419d856bac89f"], "node": "8aa5f13a86f4b38b4716515f1cdb3e154c9d41af", "parents": ["cdd65e9f1e2e57773083dcbe9ebee126c53f0a5f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Weinig \u003csam@webkit.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089382 [wpt PR 64421] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328228, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Image Redux] Place and draw an \u003cfeImage\u003e's image like an SVG \u003cimage\u003e\n\nThe filter effects states:\n\n  \"If the href references a stand-alone image resource such as a JPEG, PNG or SVG file, then the image resource is\n   rendered according to the behavior of the image element\"\n    - https://drafts.csswg.org/filter-effects/#feImageElement.\n\nLuckily for us, we have been refactoring all the code to size SVG images, but unluckily for us, it requires having\na real RenderObject to work. So, RenderSVGResourceFEImage and LegacyRenderSVGResourceFEImage are born, and like the\nother image render objects, each hold a RenderImageResource with a Style::Image in it.\n\nWith these additional image renderers, it made sense to further factor out some logic from RenderSVGImage and\nLegacyRenderSVGImage to calculate the drawing options via calculateSVGImageDrawingOptions().\n\nAn \u003cfeImage\u003e with nothing to show, such as one without a renderer in a display: none subtree, now produces transparent\nblack rather than failing the whole filter, matching Firefox. The spec does not specify what do with the display: none,\nbut this seems like a good default choice.\n\nAlso, the subregion, filter region, and scale are now needed when an effect is created, so they get passed from SVGFilterRenderer\nin a new FilterEffectPlacement struct.\n\nA few test results show an \"image-size\" attribute no longer being present on an feImage. This is due to how the legacy\nSVG renderer's dumping work for filters, where it gives it a zero sized dummy region. Now that we are correctly sizing\nthe images, the dummy region causes use to make the images zero size. This is only an artifact of dumping, as all the\ntests that actual invoke the filters have a non-zero sized region.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328228\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324592@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 150eb03b6be9d65e50c18f4b92fd4420d01da5a0\nwpt-pr: 64421\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/feimage-huge-subregion.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/feimage-subregion-beyond-filter-region.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/feimage-svg-fragment.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/feimage-svg-preserveaspectratio-slice.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/feimage-svg-resolution.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/feimage-svg-root-preserveaspectratio.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-feimage-dynamic.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-feimage-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-feimage-resolution.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-feimage-subregion-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-feimage-subregion.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-feimage.html"], "git_node": "a9282e5de5f4072913fcb39c1f4de5b16d440728", "git_parents": ["4447c27f93b8cbd1b223d256b0fbd5a5b062e7d4"], "node": "75d514b133cf4d20bcad123135e5f8dcfcaf024a", "parents": ["8aa5f13a86f4b38b4716515f1cdb3e154c9d41af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089382 [wpt PR 64421] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64421\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/filter-effects/feimage-svg-resolution.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/filter-effects/feimage-svg-root-preserveaspectratio.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-feimage-dynamic.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-feimage-resolution.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-feimage-subregion.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-feimage.html.ini"], "git_node": "3be585ac0f65d40b9939be7697d42d852cc73f4a", "git_parents": ["a9282e5de5f4072913fcb39c1f4de5b16d440728"], "node": "0a7e6ee4968ea0d25b24ccb3217ea222f085f141", "parents": ["75d514b133cf4d20bcad123135e5f8dcfcaf024a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sammy Gill \u003csammy.gill@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089383 [wpt PR 64422] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327723, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[GFC][Integration] Allow grids with auto-fit tracks\n\nStop rejecting auto-fit repeats in hasUnsupportedGridTrackListEntry(). The tracks inside an\nauto-fit repeat are still subject to the same restrictions as those inside an auto-fill repeat.\n\nAdd tests for the core auto-fit behavior which reach GFC: collapsing of leading and middle\nempty tracks along with their gutters, a repeat range that is entirely empty, flexible tracks\nstretching into the space freed by collapsed tracks, leading implicit tracks and spanning items,\nand the intrinsic width of a container with collapsed tracks and gaps.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327723\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/323996@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 54c066ac148065ba24af6622d8bc7e5935fb0392\nwpt-pr: 64422\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-definition/grid-auto-fit-collapsed-gutters-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-definition/grid-auto-fit-collapsed-gutters-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-definition/grid-auto-fit-collapsed-rows-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-definition/grid-auto-fit-collapsed-rows-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-definition/grid-auto-fit-empty-repeat-range-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-definition/grid-auto-fit-empty-repeat-range-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-definition/grid-auto-fit-fewer-items-than-tracks-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-definition/grid-auto-fit-fewer-items-than-tracks-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-definition/grid-auto-fit-implicit-and-spanning-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-definition/grid-auto-fit-implicit-and-spanning-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-definition/grid-auto-fit-intrinsic-collapsed-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-definition/grid-auto-fit-intrinsic-collapsed-001.html"], "git_node": "49ae185062f7b88f1bfba1b1bb9bd14346360b99", "git_parents": ["3be585ac0f65d40b9939be7697d42d852cc73f4a"], "node": "389831355cb7c6cc014ea29c4b16cfe9359fd7a5", "parents": ["0a7e6ee4968ea0d25b24ccb3217ea222f085f141"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Weinig \u003csam@webkit.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089385 [wpt PR 64423] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327540, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Image Redux] Unify rules for sizing SVG images with 0 width or height\n\nPreviously, RenderImage and RenderEmbeddedObject each overrode shouldRespectZeroIntrinsicWidth()/Height() with their own rule for\nwhen a natural width or height of 0 is respected. Instead, we now have a single implementation in RenderReplaced using the virtual\nnatural dimensions accessor. To make that accessor meaningful for every replaced element, RenderReplaced::zoomedNaturalDimensions()\nis now pure virtual and each subclass has to declare its own natural dimensions.\n\nAdditionally, an SVG's natural dimensions took its aspect ratio from the width and height even when one of them is 0. That ratio is\nconsidered degenerate, so it now falls back to the viewBox as the CSS WG resolved in https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/6286.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327540\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/323884@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5b11a9b4169aba2d11f33d787c88222bf9f017c3\nwpt-pr: 64423\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-fit-contain-svg-zero-height-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-fit-contain-svg-zero-height.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/support/svg-width-100-height-0-viewBox-2-1-green.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/support/svg-width-0-height-0-viewBox-1-1.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/support/svg-width-0-height-100-viewBox-1-1.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/support/svg-width-0-height-100.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/support/svg-width-100-height-0-viewBox-1-1.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/support/svg-width-100-height-0-viewBox-2-1.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/support/svg-width-100-height-0.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/svg-intrinsic-size-zero-img-and-object.html"], "git_node": "e4051471bd4aa3088c184324d033ed9f53eecc7c", "git_parents": ["49ae185062f7b88f1bfba1b1bb9bd14346360b99"], "node": "364026a098744758c885352e8ccb03f1bba55030", "parents": ["389831355cb7c6cc014ea29c4b16cfe9359fd7a5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089385 [wpt PR 64423] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64423\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-images/object-fit-contain-svg-zero-height.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-sizing/svg-intrinsic-size-zero-img-and-object.html.ini"], "git_node": "882b68e2a696df291b99175ecb7cdea693070d08", "git_parents": ["e4051471bd4aa3088c184324d033ed9f53eecc7c"], "node": "7f01d3cbfcdf85e424ed387e341f724410561644", "parents": ["364026a098744758c885352e8ccb03f1bba55030"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Weinig \u003csam@webkit.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089387 [wpt PR 64424] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327417, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Image Redux] Add support for 'object-fit', 'object-position' and 'object-view-box` for SVG documents in \u003cembed\u003e and \u003cobject\u003e\n\nAdds support for 'object-fit', 'object-position' and 'object-view-box` for SVG documents in \u003cembed\u003e and \u003cobject\u003e\nusing the recently added natural dimensions infrastructure.\n\nMoved RenderImage::imagePaintRect() down to RenderReplaced and renamed to RenderReplaced::replacedContentPaintRect(),\nso that it can be used with RenderWidget as well.\n\nHit testing, repaints and coordinate conversions for the child frame now use RenderWidget::widgetContentLocation()\nwhich accounts for 'object-fit' and 'object-position'.\n\nRemoves 66 tests from TestExpectations and adds a few more that I wrote to make sure content changes worked correctly.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327417\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/323822@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9ecb1d9bf91338da93f65a709669a921c269dd9c\nwpt-pr: 64424\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-fit-embedded-svg-dynamic-change-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-fit-embedded-svg-dynamic-change.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-fit-embedded-svg-root-will-change-dynamic-change-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-fit-embedded-svg-root-will-change-dynamic-change.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-fit-embedded-svg-root-will-change-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-fit-embedded-svg-root-will-change.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-fit-embedded-svg-will-change-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-fit-embedded-svg-will-change.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-embedded-svg-dynamic-change-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/object-view-box-embedded-svg-dynamic-change.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/support/colors-16x8-will-change.svg"], "git_node": "b3952fdb79be9728304fdeaaf4ff2c40e4db0b79", "git_parents": ["882b68e2a696df291b99175ecb7cdea693070d08"], "node": "6bf3fb24587c8ee8cac1e260d4a577720d40703b", "parents": ["7f01d3cbfcdf85e424ed387e341f724410561644"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089387 [wpt PR 64424] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64424\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-images/object-view-box-embedded-svg-dynamic-change.html.ini"], "git_node": "779ec860674b651911d0d06eb23f67e1f3d10f32", "git_parents": ["b3952fdb79be9728304fdeaaf4ff2c40e4db0b79"], "node": "3a6f7d4eb9277d6f8a76d81d698ba73b1fc9a332", "parents": ["6bf3fb24587c8ee8cac1e260d4a577720d40703b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brent Fulgham \u003cbfulgham@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089388 [wpt PR 64425] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=303066, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSelect fallback fonts and glyphs by canonical equivalence\n\nFontCascade::fontForCombiningCharacterSequence on Cocoa and Skia accepts a\nfont for a combining character cluster only when the font's cmap has every\ncode point in the cluster. That is the first rule in step 1 of CSS Fonts 4\ncluster matching. Neither port implemented the second, canonical-equivalence\nrule, so a font missing only a combining mark's glyph was rejected even when\nit had the precomposed letter, and the whole cluster fell back to a system\nfont with a different weight.\n\nThe canonical-equivalence check runs before moving on to the next font family,\nso a cluster still comes from a single font, as intended by\nhttps://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=68287.\n\nThe new check keeps the cmap-based coverage test from\nhttps://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=185933, and uses the same test for\nthe precomposed character.\n\nOn Cocoa, choosing the font is not enough, because CoreText does not compose a\ndecomposed cluster into the precomposed glyph.\nfontForCombiningCharacterSequence now reports the precomposed character it\nmatched, and ComplexTextController::collectComplexTextRuns builds the text to\nshape from it while it walks the clusters, the same way it builds\nm_smallCapsBuffer. ComplexTextRun maps the shaped indices back to the original\ntext. With synthesized small caps, a matched cluster is shaped from its\ncapitalized cluster's precomposed character when the font has one, and\notherwise is not shaped as small caps, because the font has none of the\ncluster's combining marks.\n\nOn Skia, HarfBuzz already composes the cluster when it shapes, so the shaping\ntext is not needed. Font selection still reports the precomposed character it\nmatched, so the synthesized small caps decision above is the same as on Cocoa.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=303066\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/323560@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 78840745e581428a0b3310eebebc425743119db5\nwpt-pr: 64425\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/cluster-matching-canonical-equivalence-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/cluster-matching-canonical-equivalence-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/cluster-matching-canonical-equivalence-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/cluster-matching-canonical-equivalence-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/cluster-matching-canonical-equivalence-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/cluster-matching-canonical-equivalence-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/support/fonts/no-combining-marks.ttf"], "git_node": "41312426276880902f5918f04dbfc631dc55bfe3", "git_parents": ["779ec860674b651911d0d06eb23f67e1f3d10f32"], "node": "277a1640e614d489739727bc8c0a0ffb27a704ef", "parents": ["3a6f7d4eb9277d6f8a76d81d698ba73b1fc9a332"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089388 [wpt PR 64425] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64425\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-fonts/cluster-matching-canonical-equivalence-002.html.ini"], "git_node": "b1e7f08156611ca3f3a235f2627d246c56911c1d", "git_parents": ["41312426276880902f5918f04dbfc631dc55bfe3"], "node": "bf9a10bdf1903936a1df4ada366dc96786343c20", "parents": ["277a1640e614d489739727bc8c0a0ffb27a704ef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cameron McCormack \u003cheycam@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089390 [wpt PR 64428] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324610, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Site Isolation] Make noopener windows eligible for the bfcache\n\nWith Site Isolation enabled, noopener windows are not eligible for the\nbfcache, but they should be.\n\nA window opened with noopener has openedByDOM() set, so\nProvisionalPageProxy reuses its main frame across a process swap. Since\n321195@main, suspendCurrentPageIfPossible declines to suspend a page\nwhen the provisional page is committing into that page's main frame.\nSuch a window is therefore never suspended, and a cross-site navigation\ndoes not use the bfcache.\n\nReusing the main frame keeps a window reference held in another process\nvalid across the swap. Only a page in the same browsing context group\ncan hold such a reference, so condition the reuse on the group holding\nmore than one page. openedByDOM() was the wrong check, since it stays\nset whether or not anything can still reach the window. The new\ncondition mirrors the browsing context group check in\nsuspendCurrentPageIfPossible.\n\nA noopener window opened at a same-site URL was getting the opener's\nbrowsing context group because createNewPage set relatedPage on its\nconfiguration, and preferredBrowsingContextGroup returns the related\npage's group. relatedPage was set there so that the window would load in\nthe process of the window that opened it. Sharing a process and sharing\na browsing context group are separate concerns, so createNewPage records\nthe opener's process on the configuration instead, and createWebPage\nuses that process when the two pages are able to share a process.\n_setRelatedWebView: still sets relatedPage, so the behavior added in\n306438@main is unchanged.\n\ncreateNewPage copies the opening page's configuration, so it clears any\nprocess recorded there before deciding whether to record one for the new\nwindow. Otherwise a window opened from a window that was itself opened\nsame-site with noopener would inherit a process from further up the\nchain, which placed a cross-site noopener window in the wrong process,\nand without Site Isolation placed a window opened with an opener outside\nits opener's process.\n\nprocessForNavigationInternal decided whether to keep a noopener window\nin the opener's process by comparing the navigation target against the\nrelated page's current URL. It now compares the target against the site\nthe window was opened at.\n\ncanShareProcessWithOpener declines the opener's process when that\nprocess is the browsing context group's shared process. A shared process\nonly hosts subframes, and creating a FrameProcess for it in a group that\ndoes not have one would dedicate it to a single site. A window opened\nfrom a frame in the shared process therefore loads in a process of its\nown. CrossSiteIframeOpenWindowWithBlobURL expected such a window to\nshare the shared process with the frame that opened it, and now expects\nthree distinct processes.\n\nTo test these changes, we use the historical agent cluster key map.\nThe browsing context group a noopener window lands in is observable with\nor without Site Isolation: before these changes, a same-origin noopener\nwindow was inheriting the opener's origin-keying decision rather than\nmaking its own. noopener-opener-no-openee-yes-same.https.html is added\nto test this, modeled on other tests in its directory.\n\nwindow-noopener-failure.https.html and window-opener-success.https.html\ntest the agent cluster requirement for SharedArrayBuffer, which we were\nalready correctly doing before these changes (but were written during\npatch development and seemed worth keeping).\n\nhasPageOpenedByMainFrame() had no other callers and is removed.\n\nThe http/wpt copy of old_vt_promises_bfcache.html, whose failure\nprompted this investigation, is removed. It existed so that\nUsesBackForwardCache could be applied to it, and 300920@main turned the\nbfcache on by default in WebKitTestRunner and deleted other similar\ncopies, but missed this one. Because http/wpt tests are served from\nlocalhost rather than the WPT server's browser_host, its\noriginSameOrigin put pageB on another site, which is why it was failing.\nThe imported test under\nruns and has been passing with and without Site Isolation.\n\nThe two SharedArrayBuffer tests are skipped on GLib, which skips the\nother window-* tests in that directory too.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324610\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/321634@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5e8c056075ac95a9dfdab2405e0c946ece18b121\nwpt-pr: 64428\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/origin/origin-keyed-agent-clusters/popups/noopener-opener-no-openee-yes-same.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/origin/origin-keyed-agent-clusters/resources/oac-broadcast-popup.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/origin/origin-keyed-agent-clusters/resources/oac-broadcast-popup.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/infrastructure/safe-passing-of-structured-data/shared-array-buffers/resources/broadcastchannel-popup.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/infrastructure/safe-passing-of-structured-data/shared-array-buffers/resources/broadcastchannel-popup.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/infrastructure/safe-passing-of-structured-data/shared-array-buffers/window-noopener-failure.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/infrastructure/safe-passing-of-structured-data/shared-array-buffers/window-noopener-failure.https.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/infrastructure/safe-passing-of-structured-data/shared-array-buffers/window-opener-success.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/infrastructure/safe-passing-of-structured-data/shared-array-buffers/window-opener-success.https.html.headers"], "git_node": "826008953200c5c0018d50ac8b8fbdca9b01e0f8", "git_parents": ["b1e7f08156611ca3f3a235f2627d246c56911c1d"], "node": "5bbdafa389712815fe10c959a60e28bef116cd41", "parents": ["bf9a10bdf1903936a1df4ada366dc96786343c20"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Fraser \u003csimon.fraser@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089391 [wpt PR 64429] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323558, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[corner-shape] Outlines with negative offset look ugly\n\nBevel, notch and square corners are adjusted for insets (e.g. for an outline with\nnegative inset) by offsetting the border-box corner at constant thickness rather than by\nscaling their radius (rebuildOffsetCornersFromReference). There were three issues for a\nnegative (inset) offset:\n\nThe rebuilt corner follows the border-box curve, so it extends past the edges of the\nrect it is being offset relative to. The inner contour already trimmed to that rect, but\nthe outer one did not, resulting in uneven thickness of inset outlines on bevel corners.\n\nWhen the inset outline becomes empty, we now detect that we should draw nothing.\n\nFix a rendering issue when the inset is larger than the notch size.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323558\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/321259@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4e8e0db353b903fc57938c3ab7257fdf1712bff0\nwpt-pr: 64429\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-negative-offset-bevel-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-negative-offset-bevel.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-negative-offset-notch001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-negative-offset-notch001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-negative-offset-notch002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-negative-offset-notch002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-negative-offset-notch003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-negative-offset-notch003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-negative-offset-square-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-negative-offset-square.html"], "git_node": "10517e66ba34b7e8517b1f9f12965fe026c618a1", "git_parents": ["826008953200c5c0018d50ac8b8fbdca9b01e0f8"], "node": "531a7731187d5a8c67e27d7ec63bbd3abbbd42b0", "parents": ["5bbdafa389712815fe10c959a60e28bef116cd41"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089391 [wpt PR 64429] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64429\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-negative-offset-bevel.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-negative-offset-notch001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-negative-offset-notch002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-negative-offset-notch003.html.ini"], "git_node": "9a7d767d306c4500dd5bc879c757a6eea10454a3", "git_parents": ["10517e66ba34b7e8517b1f9f12965fe026c618a1"], "node": "a251785309578f82a3d3f1b2c84f1125054a6be6", "parents": ["531a7731187d5a8c67e27d7ec63bbd3abbbd42b0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Weinig \u003csam@webkit.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089393 [wpt PR 64426] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326824, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nsvgView() fragment with an invalid or zero-size viewBox draws the SVG unscaled\n\nAn svgView() fragment's viewBox was previously parsed without validation, so missing numbers became 0 and a negative\nwidth or height was accepted.\n\nAdditionally we now check whichever viewBox is in effect in viewBoxDisablesPainting() to ensure fragments can disable\nthe painting when they are active.\n\nWhile in the area, I update the warning and error text to include the invalid string being parsed as well as the issue\nat hand.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326824\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/323217@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8709c6534dc533c4928fc052a1188825397ee5d9\nwpt-pr: 64426\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/support/green-viewbox-25x25.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/support/red-viewbox-25x25.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/support/view-invalid-viewbox.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/svgview-viewbox-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/svgview-viewbox-zero.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/linking/reftests/view-viewbox-invalid-fallback.html"], "git_node": "55cea10f823d66bd9d9bc4d7de93002c7af2e5f7", "git_parents": ["9a7d767d306c4500dd5bc879c757a6eea10454a3"], "node": "42fb1a4ece2af54b55a0ca27a9a937a2c1ece86a", "parents": ["a251785309578f82a3d3f1b2c84f1125054a6be6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Fraser \u003csimon.fraser@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089394 [wpt PR 64431] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323566, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[corner-shape] Add some more shape-outside/corner-shape tests\n\nAdd more shape-outside/corner-shape tests (which test the code landed in 320552@main).\n\nBased on work by Lilly Le (@cupidsity).\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323566\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/320633@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c3e25a01bfadaea1193a780675467e52d75bcba7\nwpt-pr: 64431\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outside-content-box.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outside-corners.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outside-margin-box.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outside-padding-box.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outside-shape-margin.html"], "git_node": "eb75417af186fe19e3dd3f8b084fd14027fe2f8d", "git_parents": ["55cea10f823d66bd9d9bc4d7de93002c7af2e5f7"], "node": "16f06fb8190357b31bef539eb6635025c39b1d3d", "parents": ["42fb1a4ece2af54b55a0ca27a9a937a2c1ece86a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089394 [wpt PR 64431] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64431\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outside-content-box.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outside-corners.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outside-margin-box.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outside-padding-box.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outside-shape-margin.html.ini"], "git_node": "bd33988c17075540b6601f4829810827e5c99d7c", "git_parents": ["eb75417af186fe19e3dd3f8b084fd14027fe2f8d"], "node": "9e54e0cd420dbb57415a0e8d76e821932e08d664", "parents": ["16f06fb8190357b31bef539eb6635025c39b1d3d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089395 [wpt PR 64430] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323710, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[SVG] Mutating a display: contents tspan inside SVG text crashes with anonymous inline wrapper\n\nRenderTreeUpdater::createTextRenderer wraps a text renderer in an anonymous RenderInline to carry a display: contents style.\nInside SVG text that wrapper has to be a RenderSVGInline, because everything walking SVG text looks for one:\n\n1. RenderSVGText::subtreeChildWasAdded/subtreeChildWillBeRemoved skip it, so the layout attributes\ncache goes stale and checkLayoutAttributesConsistency asserts on removal, on text insertion and on a display change.\n2. SVGTextLayoutAttributesBuilder and SVGTextMetricsBuilder do not descend into it, so its text is never measured and getStartPositionOfChar() hangs.\n\nCreate it as an anonymous RenderSVGInline instead.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323710\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/320865@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a53d5e6d69a146e9ac7218192d031241cfe942db\nwpt-pr: 64430\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-display/display-contents-svg-tspan-child-character-positions.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-display/display-contents-svg-tspan-child-display-changed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-display/display-contents-svg-tspan-child-removed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-display/display-contents-svg-tspan-child-text-inserted.html"], "git_node": "97478c6edb22cacd702383da48e1ab5c377473ae", "git_parents": ["bd33988c17075540b6601f4829810827e5c99d7c"], "node": "aae5ae862938fecf82e2ec47a16a0ecacc4216ff", "parents": ["9e54e0cd420dbb57415a0e8d76e821932e08d664"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089396 [wpt PR 64432] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321802, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[list-marker] Position every outside list marker after layout, not just the ones whose first formatted line is in a descendant block\n\nAn outside marker was excluded from in-flow layout only when its list item had block level children. Exclude every\noutside marker and position them all after layout.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321802\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/320561@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 834caf76772de4b5a52f77bd72465b2e5fb405e1\nwpt-pr: 64432\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-lists/inside-marker-with-block-in-inline-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-lists/inside-marker-with-block-in-inline.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-lists/outside-marker-position-with-cached-line-content-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-lists/outside-marker-position-with-cached-line-content.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-lists/outside-marker-taller-than-content-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-lists/outside-marker-taller-than-content.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-lists/outside-marker-with-block-in-nested-inline-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-lists/outside-marker-with-block-in-nested-inline.html"], "git_node": "60f0e19e6a2fd32190dc9b089452848f50a001c9", "git_parents": ["97478c6edb22cacd702383da48e1ab5c377473ae"], "node": "e8cdd2ae2a7105814f3db6bf7609e1c9a2017c47", "parents": ["aae5ae862938fecf82e2ec47a16a0ecacc4216ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089396 [wpt PR 64432] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64432\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-lists/outside-marker-taller-than-content.html.ini"], "git_node": "4d469d1c516b8a17ce62f6dec0988632aaac4027", "git_parents": ["60f0e19e6a2fd32190dc9b089452848f50a001c9"], "node": "7a622f8d045bdf63b1bd5da11eab528f57f71fcb", "parents": ["e8cdd2ae2a7105814f3db6bf7609e1c9a2017c47"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089397 [wpt PR 64433] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323064, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n`shape-outside` renders incorrectly when the float has margins\n\nIFC integration codepath builds that geometry out of FloatingObject::frameRect(), which is the margin box.\nHowever shape's coordinates are relative to the float's border box.\nAny margin on the float is dropped from the shape's position: the line is constrained as if the\nshape sat at the float's margin box origin.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323064\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/320417@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9c4f26b9e1de185fc4ad1883855f9abc0abe1ce5\nwpt-pr: 64433\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-shapes/shape-outside/shape-box/reference/shape-outside-border-box-shape-margin-with-margin-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-shapes/shape-outside/shape-box/reference/shape-outside-border-box-with-block-start-margin-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-shapes/shape-outside/shape-box/reference/shape-outside-border-box-with-margin-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-shapes/shape-outside/shape-box/reference/shape-outside-border-box-with-margin-right-float-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-shapes/shape-outside/shape-box/reference/shape-outside-content-box-with-margin-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-shapes/shape-outside/shape-box/reference/shape-outside-padding-box-with-margin-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-shapes/shape-outside/shape-box/shape-outside-border-box-shape-margin-with-margin.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-shapes/shape-outside/shape-box/shape-outside-border-box-with-block-start-margin.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-shapes/shape-outside/shape-box/shape-outside-border-box-with-margin-right-float.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-shapes/shape-outside/shape-box/shape-outside-border-box-with-margin.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-shapes/shape-outside/shape-box/shape-outside-content-box-with-margin.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-shapes/shape-outside/shape-box/shape-outside-padding-box-with-margin.html"], "git_node": "94f1abb280c8292a2cad5452d92bc9507d8c549a", "git_parents": ["4d469d1c516b8a17ce62f6dec0988632aaac4027"], "node": "32947f571ea02c949d76df6e2748502b71dc8ff1", "parents": ["7a622f8d045bdf63b1bd5da11eab528f57f71fcb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "lilly \u003c173393835+cupidsity@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089398 [wpt PR 64435] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321604, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\ncorner-shape: Implement oppositeCornerScaleFactor\n\nImplements https://drafts.csswg.org/css-borders-4/#corner-shape-constrain-radii with\nalgorithm adaption from https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/pull/14142\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321604\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/319157@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 39c04517bbc3c8d187924e17282c905cb0e40469\nwpt-pr: 64435\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-opposite-scale-convex-inert-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-opposite-scale-convex-inert.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-opposite-scale-elliptical-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-opposite-scale-elliptical.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-opposite-scale-mixed-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-opposite-scale-mixed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-opposite-scale-notch-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-opposite-scale-notch.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-opposite-scale-scoop-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-opposite-scale-scoop.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-opposite-scale-superellipse-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-opposite-scale-superellipse.html"], "git_node": "e57b0bbbccf2869514bf4a102738a83a2f6c9317", "git_parents": ["94f1abb280c8292a2cad5452d92bc9507d8c549a"], "node": "0737e3ce2c481ca750f79c95423c8c70506908e8", "parents": ["32947f571ea02c949d76df6e2748502b71dc8ff1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089398 [wpt PR 64435] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64435\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-opposite-scale-convex-inert.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-opposite-scale-elliptical.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-opposite-scale-mixed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-opposite-scale-notch.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-opposite-scale-scoop.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-opposite-scale-superellipse.html.ini"], "git_node": "86b64c8c05a60d957bcb4ba2f7386bcaae6ec123", "git_parents": ["e57b0bbbccf2869514bf4a102738a83a2f6c9317"], "node": "db1ec22b0bb4e4bb1b03abfc42f3f8fed961ec19", "parents": ["0737e3ce2c481ca750f79c95423c8c70506908e8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089399 [wpt PR 64436] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321398, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[block-in-inline] A block level box on a line does not start a new paragraph for unicode-bidi: plaintext or text-indent: each-line\n\nTwo properties ask whether the previous line ended a paragraph, and PreviousLine answered with nothing but\nendsWithLineBreak.\n\nunicode-bidi: plaintext gives each unicode paragraph the base direction of its own first strong character.\nbuildBidiParagraph already counts a block level box as a paragraph separator, alongside a hard line break,\nso the runs come back from ICU in the right order. The line's own base direction is decided separately in\ninlineBaseDirectionForLineContent, where a line carrying a block level box does not count, so the line after\nit takes the direction of the paragraph before the box rather than computing its own.\n\ntext-indent with the each-line modifier indents the first line of the block and every line after a paragraph\nend. computedTextIndent takes the same flag, so the line after a block level box is not indented either.\n\nAn anonymous block hid both. One block per chunk meant each chunk was its own formatting context, resolving\nits own direction from its own content and indenting its own first line. Firefox indents the line after a\nblock level box in both shapes, with and without an inline box around the box, which is what this matches.\n\nFold the two questions into one: PreviousLine::endsParagraph, true for a forced line break and for a block\nlevel box on a line, both of which are paragraph separators. computedTextIndent's parameter is named for\nwhat it now takes.\n\nThe text-wrap: balance path keeps its own per line record of forced breaks and is left alone here.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=321398\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/318886@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3775829468bef72c6628efa3dfd81fb2e2576934\nwpt-pr: 64436\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/text-indent/text-indent-each-line-after-block-level-box-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/text-indent/text-indent-each-line-after-block-level-box.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/block-plaintext-paragraph-after-block-level-box-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/block-plaintext-paragraph-after-block-level-box.html"], "git_node": "15774e67ec7b919ab658b70c85b04129e9dbf703", "git_parents": ["86b64c8c05a60d957bcb4ba2f7386bcaae6ec123"], "node": "3abd882136c85eee64a5e0c64f1a25cc3da76da1", "parents": ["db1ec22b0bb4e4bb1b03abfc42f3f8fed961ec19"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Basuke Suzuki \u003cbasuke@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089400 [wpt PR 64427] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=325553, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Navigation API] preventDefault() does not cancel a cross-site navigation.navigate() that swaps processes\n\nnavigation.navigate() used a synchronous navigation policy check (288106@main), whose reply falls\nback to Use before the UI process decides on a process swap. The source process then loaded the\ndestination as well as the process the UI process chose, so preventDefault() could not cancel it,\nand under Site Isolation the source process was killed or committed a cross-site document in the\nembedder's process (rdar://188750371).\n\nCross-document navigation.navigate() now uses the asynchronous policy check like other\ncross-document navigations. FrameLoader::shouldCheckNavigationPolicyAfterDispatchingEvents()\nfirst fires the events navigate() needs, the navigate event and then beforeunload, which is the\norder the HTML spec uses for push, replace and reload navigations, and then tells whether the\nnavigation should still go on to the policy check. A navigate() whose navigate event is\nintercepted therefore no longer fires beforeunload. The events run after the load being replaced\nis stopped and after scheduled navigations are cancelled, as they did when they ran after the\nsynchronous policy decision.\n\nSince these events already ran, the rest of the navigation treats them as done:\n- continueLoadAfterNavigationPolicy() does not dispatch beforeunload again.\n- If the policy check denies the navigation, the navigate event is aborted (navigateerror and\n  AbortError). The abort is queued and only applies while that event is still the ongoing one,\n  because a newer navigation cancels this policy check as it starts and aborts the event itself.\n  To recognize it, every NavigateEvent now has a NavigateEventIdentifier, which\n  NavigateEventDispatchResult carries back to the navigation that fired it.\n- LoadWillContinueInAnotherProcess does not abort it, since the navigation carries on elsewhere.\n\nWhen the other process commits the navigation, the old frame or page is torn down through\nFrameLoader::detachFromParent(). Its closeURL() unloads the document without aborting the\nNavigation API, but the stopAllLoaders() that followed aborted the ongoing navigation whenever\nthe document was still loading, so the document got navigateerror for a navigation that had\ncommitted. navigate() now leaves that navigation ongoing until then, which made this reachable.\ndetachFromParent() no longer aborts after unloading; removing an iframe still aborts, through\nFrameLoader::frameDetached(), as the spec requires for a destroyed child navigable.\n\nThe asynchronous check also lets a client that decides late deny navigate(); before, its answer\narrived after the synchronous fallback had already allowed the load.\n\nTwo tentative deferPageSwap tests call navigate() while their popup is still parsing. The load\nused to start inside that script and stop the parser, so pagehide never fired and they timed out.\nThey now reach their assertions: one passes and the other fails because WebKit does not\nimplement deferPageSwap.\n\nfast/canvas/offscreen-webgl-transfer-after-navigation-crash.html relied on\nnavigation.navigate(\"about:blank\") committing before its next line ran, which tore down the\ndocument and lost the WebGL context. It now navigates an iframe that owns the canvas and calls\ntransferToImageBitmap() once the iframe has loaded; without the fix from 309187@main it still\ncrashes.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=325553\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/322591@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5395057e7ce29345ac49ce5c7c91842f5838b445\nwpt-pr: 64427\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/navigate-event/intercept-no-beforeunload.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/navigate-event/intercept-stops-ongoing-cross-document-navigation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/navigate-event/navigate-navigation-navigate-cross-site-preventDefault.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/navigate-event/resources/navigate-cross-site-preventDefault-helper.html"], "git_node": "409c164fe610dd8eb73e342aa0f12209842026e5", "git_parents": ["15774e67ec7b919ab658b70c85b04129e9dbf703"], "node": "130a3875ea1945439416f69949474820649143e1", "parents": ["3abd882136c85eee64a5e0c64f1a25cc3da76da1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089400 [wpt PR 64427] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64427\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/navigation-api/navigate-event/intercept-stops-ongoing-cross-document-navigation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/navigation-api/navigate-event/signal-abort-replaceState-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "4753c4d37b0702f1751cba202cce2d6ac1a4d765", "git_parents": ["409c164fe610dd8eb73e342aa0f12209842026e5"], "node": "4abae47a64936f71b8eba74a079c58e039cbc73d", "parents": ["130a3875ea1945439416f69949474820649143e1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089402 [wpt PR 64434] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322214, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nInset box-shadow with a large spread paints outside the box on an inline box\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"width: 200px\"\u003e\n    before\n    \u003cspan style=\"box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 400px blue\"\u003e\n      first \u003cbr\u003e\n      second\n    \u003c/span\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\nThe blue _inset_ shadow should stop at the end of each line's fragment. Instead it ran 400px past it to the containing block.\nWhen an inline box is split across lines, the incoming edge value (where it breaks) is \"open\" and the box keeps growing to the next line.\n(Note inset shadows are clipped to the padding box)\n\n  paintRect                      expansion = blur extent + spread\n  +--------------------------+- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -+\n  |##########################|                                 |\n  |###+----------------------+- - - - - - - - - - - - - - -+   |\n  |###|  hole, reaching the break edge                     |   |\n  |###+----------------------+- - - - - - - - - - - - - - -+   |\n  |##########################|                                 |\n  +--------------------------+- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -+\n  |\u003c--- clip: padding box --\u003e|  everything past here is clipped\n\nOn trunk we call shapeForInnerHole.fillOuterShape() when shapeForInnerHole is empty (i.e. inset shadow covers the box).\nWith no hole left, we just call fill on the \"grown\" rect before any clip is applied.\n\n  +-----------+- - - - - - - - - - - - - -+\n  |###########|###########################|\n  +-----------+- - - - - - - - - - - - - -+\n   fragment     spread carries it 400px\n                past the line break\n\nbut what we should do instead is this:\n\n  +-----------+\n  |###########|\n  +-----------+\n    fragment\n\nSo let's call borderShape.fillInnerShape() instead. borderShape is the box itself, not the \"grown\" rect, and its inner shape is the padding box.\n\nIt also fixes blocks: on trunk a block with a transparent border paints the shadow under the border (the outer shape is the border box),\nnow it stops at the padding box.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322214\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/320150@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 79816e2994281d693a78c5406a7a27ec9503ff1d\nwpt-pr: 64434\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-backgrounds/box-shadow/inset-shadow-large-spread-clipped-to-padding-box-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-backgrounds/box-shadow/inset-shadow-large-spread-clipped-to-padding-box.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-backgrounds/box-shadow/inset-shadow-large-spread-cloned-inline-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-backgrounds/box-shadow/inset-shadow-large-spread-cloned-inline.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-backgrounds/box-shadow/inset-shadow-large-spread-fragmented-inline-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-backgrounds/box-shadow/inset-shadow-large-spread-fragmented-inline.html"], "git_node": "d666020f5b2d6ba64771a4fcbf865453999f0367", "git_parents": ["4753c4d37b0702f1751cba202cce2d6ac1a4d765"], "node": "6e78f222d481ff0756c6788e045821d29613886a", "parents": ["4abae47a64936f71b8eba74a079c58e039cbc73d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089402 [wpt PR 64434] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64434\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-backgrounds/box-shadow/inset-shadow-large-spread-fragmented-inline.html.ini"], "git_node": "d4557344c5abd8271f8502a473ed47e960065613", "git_parents": ["d666020f5b2d6ba64771a4fcbf865453999f0367"], "node": "bd0b126182b53501ad272dd39cfd6bfd131bf338", "parents": ["6e78f222d481ff0756c6788e045821d29613886a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andy Estes \u003caestes@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089404 [wpt PR 64438] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=320588, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Site Isolation] Embedded YouTube videos on yahoo.com fail to render\n\nAs of 311380@main we gate accelerated video rendering on the video element intersecting the\nviewport (by using an IntersectionObserver). If the observer never reports the video as\nintersecting, a video layer is never attached and decoded frames are dropped, so the video plays\naudio but shows no frames.\n\nFor a video in a cross-origin iframe with Site Isolation enabled, the observer computes\nintersection from geometry sent over by the parent frame's process. That geometry was wrong on some\nyahoo.com pages, so the video was reported as never intersecting even while fully within the\nviewport.\n\nThe process that contains the iframe computes the frame's visible rect in\nLocalFrameView::visibleRectOfChild by passing the iframe's rect to computeVisibleRectsInContainer.\nThat function expects a rect in the iframe's own coordinate space, but we were passing it a rect in\nits container's coordinate space. This resulted in the iframe's offset position being applied\ntwice, resulting in an IntersectionObserver believing that elements within the iframe were too far\ndown to intersect the viewport.\n\nResolved this by passing borderBoxRect() (i.e. a rect in the element's own coordinate space) to\ncomputeVisibleRectsInContainer, matching other call sites.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=320588\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/318254@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4e1f07d13e0af1c1985db971fdd7e4b9317d977a\nwpt-pr: 64438\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/intersection-observer/offset-iframe-cross-origin.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/intersection-observer/offset-iframe-same-origin.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/intersection-observer/resources/offset-iframe-subframe.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/intersection-observer/resources/offset-iframe.js"], "git_node": "2e16c2f5f6f8058d93dc9c0115cb5dc0d3f0ead1", "git_parents": ["d4557344c5abd8271f8502a473ed47e960065613"], "node": "923559cacc7c553c25b0c2b347a3b06df1174e4f", "parents": ["bd0b126182b53501ad272dd39cfd6bfd131bf338"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089405 [wpt PR 64439] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319534, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-align] Support justify-self for out-of-flow boxes at the static position\n\n    \u003cdiv style=\"position: relative; width: 500px\"\u003e\n        \u003cdiv style=\"position: absolute; justify-self: center\"\u003ehi\u003c/div\u003e\n    \u003c/div\u003e\n\nThe absolutely-positioned inner block has auto insets, so it is placed at its\nstatic position and should be centered within the 500px containing block. Instead\njustify-self was ignored: the box stayed pinned to the inline-start edge.\n\nWhen both inline-axis insets are auto, an out-of-flow box is placed at its static\nposition. Per css-align-3, justify-self then aligns its margin box within the box's\nstatic-position rectangle, resolving against the containing block's writing mode; a\njustify-self of auto resolves to the parent's justify-items. (See\nhttps://drafts.csswg.org/css-align-3/#justify-abspos and Appendix A.)\n\nAlign the box within the remaining inline space at the static position when\njustify-self asks for it, gating the behavior with\nshouldAlignStaticPositionInInlineAxis() so it applies only where it is both correct\nand covered by tests:\n\n  - the box's own inline axis (non-orthogonal); orthogonal / block-axis static\n    positioning keeps the existing static-position path,\n  - justify-self resolves (against the parent) to something other than normal;\n    normal / auto-resolving-to-normal keeps the box at its static position,\n  - the static-position containing block is a plain block container -- flex and grid\n    containers place their abspos children with their own alignment rules, and\n    alignment does not apply to out-of-flow children of inline boxes.\n\nEverything else falls back to the existing static-position placement, which already\nresolves the correct edge for every writing-mode / direction / orthogonal\ncombination via the parent-relative static inset. This gating matters because the\nexisting path anchors to that parent-relative edge while resolveAlignmentShift()\nreasons in the containing block's writing mode; the two diverge whenever the\nparent's inline direction differs from the containing block's, so aligning\nunconditionally mispositioned ordinary (justify-self: auto) abspos boxes. The\nblock-axis / align-self behavior is unchanged.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319534\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/317349@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 90bc0f78b4a2a19cc4dde503ec7166deae87bed5\nwpt-pr: 64439\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/abspos/justify-self-static-position-htb-ltr-htb.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/abspos/justify-self-static-position-htb-rtl-htb.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/abspos/justify-self-static-position-vlr-ltr-vlr.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-align/abspos/justify-self-static-position-vrl-ltr-vrl.html"], "git_node": "b4e646e085966077198a99843ebec13bd39f83b0", "git_parents": ["2e16c2f5f6f8058d93dc9c0115cb5dc0d3f0ead1"], "node": "6f4453e6c534d8ae14edeb87ca7a525317b33b5e", "parents": ["923559cacc7c553c25b0c2b347a3b06df1174e4f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089405 [wpt PR 64439] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64439\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/abspos/justify-self-static-position-htb-ltr-htb.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/abspos/justify-self-static-position-htb-rtl-htb.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/abspos/justify-self-static-position-vlr-ltr-vlr.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-align/abspos/justify-self-static-position-vrl-ltr-vrl.html.ini"], "git_node": "b0045f263b5b68195ced426d019a0e6a6e7838ee", "git_parents": ["b4e646e085966077198a99843ebec13bd39f83b0"], "node": "13ba474321fae58d0a31420a51c5a6da466df6cf", "parents": ["6f4453e6c534d8ae14edeb87ca7a525317b33b5e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089406 [wpt PR 64442] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=315324, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[block-in-inline] inline-block baseline should fall back to bottom margin edge when content inside is block-in-inline only\n\n\u003cspan\u003etext\n  \u003cdiv style=\"display: inline-block; width: 320px; height: 100px;\"\u003e\n    \u003cspan\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"display: block; width: 320px; height: 100px;\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\n\nThe \"text\" should sit at the bottom of the inline-block. The inline-block's\nbaseline should be its bottom margin edge per CSS 2.1 10.8.1 (and CSS Inline 3\natomic-inline baseline synthesis), since the only content is block-in-inline\nand there are no in-flow line boxes with a baseline. Instead the \"text\" sat\nat the top of the inline-block.\n\nIn LayoutIntegrationBoxGeometryUpdater::baselineForBox, the RenderBlockFlow\npath called LineLayout::lastLineBaseline() which correctly returns nullopt\nwhen no line contributes a baseline (e.g. when the only content is a\nblock-in-inline whose inner block is empty). The integration was substituting\n0 via .value_or(0_lu) and reporting the inline-block's top edge as its\nbaseline.\n\nDrop the .value_or(0_lu) so the nullopt propagates: setIntegrationBaseline's\nexisting fallback then synthesizes margin-box-bottom for atomic inlines (per\ncss-inline-3 A.3), and lastInflowBoxBaseline's sibling walk skips the\nnon-contributing child and continues to the previous in-flow block-level\nsibling (per css-align-3 \u00a711.5).\n\nLineLayout::lastLineBaseline already recurses into block-in-inline via\nblockLevelBoxForLine, so when the inner block does contribute a last baseline\nthe inline-block aligns to it (covered by css/css-lists/list-and-block-in-inline.html)\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=315324\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/313769@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: fc64a83038182a4f11b581656c70588b62743817\nwpt-pr: 64442\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/inline-block-baseline-with-block-in-inline-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/inline-block-baseline-with-block-in-inline.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/inline-block-last-baseline-skips-non-contributing-block-in-inline-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/inline-block-last-baseline-skips-non-contributing-block-in-inline.html"], "git_node": "2a5cd81f884b629e2c7b9f358e9ea0180c41aded", "git_parents": ["b0045f263b5b68195ced426d019a0e6a6e7838ee"], "node": "99ad750eb4617dee6b57be3895004317f70c0dc7", "parents": ["13ba474321fae58d0a31420a51c5a6da466df6cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089408 [wpt PR 64440] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=257992, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nText decoration is too thin over a descendant block\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-thickness: 5px; text-decoration-color: red\"\u003e\n    before\u003cdiv\u003einside\u003c/div\u003eafter\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\nThe underline under \"inside\" should be 5px thick, the same as under \"before\" and\n\"after\". Instead it was a thin auto line: the nested block painted the underline\nwith its own text-decoration-thickness rather than the div that set the underline.\n\nLine decorations propagate down the render tree, but at paint time the thickness was\nread from the box the line was drawn over - here the nested block, whose\ntext-decoration-thickness is auto - not from the box that originated the\ndecoration. The color was already resolved from the originating box, which is why\nonly the thickness came out wrong.\n\nThe thickness is now resolved next to the color in collectStylesForRenderer, taken\nfrom the box that originated each decoration, and the painter reads that per-line\nthickness instead of the decorating box's style. This also corrects overline and\nline-through propagated across block boundaries.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=257992\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/314502@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3fb420db51842ed7569a2104d429427f20239409\nwpt-pr: 64440\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-thickness-linethrough-block-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-thickness-linethrough-block-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-thickness-overline-block-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-thickness-overline-block-001.html"], "git_node": "97bfcd721c9de9a30861ae7501ddfca9fe2615e1", "git_parents": ["2a5cd81f884b629e2c7b9f358e9ea0180c41aded"], "node": "90c65acc03bc3ec5c2f5978937719bcc2ce798d7", "parents": ["99ad750eb4617dee6b57be3895004317f70c0dc7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089409 [wpt PR 64443] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=240128, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nBFC with margin-start overlaps adjacent float\n\ncomputedClearDeltaForChild checked only the border-box width against the\navailable space, but the border box is positioned at the margin offset. When\nthe margin placed the border box into the float's margin box, the overlap\nwent undetected and the BFC was not moved below the float.\n\nThe fix computes where the border box will actually land -\nmax(marginStart, positionToAvoidFloats) - and checks whether it fits from\nthere. The margin only consumes available space to the extent it exceeds\npositionToAvoidFloats (the space already occupied by a start-side float).\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=240128\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/312082@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c9a26d388678db3b7ffcc94603ae5190d7acd84a\nwpt-pr: 64443\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/CSS2/floats/float-avoids-float-with-margin-004-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/CSS2/floats/float-avoids-float-with-margin-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/CSS2/floats/float-avoids-float-with-margin-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/CSS2/floats/float-avoids-float-with-margin-012-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/CSS2/floats/float-avoids-float-with-margin-012.html"], "git_node": "8c1ee13ae19d6972c4a16fdf887eb7575ef1fe92", "git_parents": ["97bfcd721c9de9a30861ae7501ddfca9fe2615e1"], "node": "424f167441e92928afba0f1f285026ea259babe0", "parents": ["90c65acc03bc3ec5c2f5978937719bcc2ce798d7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoav Weiss \u003cyoav.weiss@shopify.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089410 [wpt PR 64444] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=312252, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSpeculation Rules - Fix race conditions with non-OK responses\n\nWhile the speculation rules implementation properly handled non-2XX status responses that came to completion,\nit failed to handle responses that were not done before the navigation request for them was triggered.\nThis PR fixes that by:\n* Ensuring that a failed response gets evicted from the memory cache even before it's done.\n* Avoiding to commit and retrying a navigation request if its prefetch response has failed.\n* Properly clearing prefetched resources when the DocumentPrefetcher gets destructed. (lack of that cleanup caused issues in some of the new test scenarios)\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=312252\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/311445@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6ccf56925653dcf4eab0d9307fabe5acc27dc289\nwpt-pr: 64444\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prefetch/no-http-cache-interference-inflight.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prefetch/no-http-cache-interference-slow-error.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prefetch/prefetch-inflight-success.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prefetch/resources/delayed-conditional-status.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prefetch/resources/slow-body-conditional-status.py"], "git_node": "3eb455fc21e2b6244fc9480b0129e18aac3bb631", "git_parents": ["8c1ee13ae19d6972c4a16fdf887eb7575ef1fe92"], "node": "6efeed5cbe174e0b8c0f88d7785494bd3db9d2dc", "parents": ["424f167441e92928afba0f1f285026ea259babe0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089411 [wpt PR 64441] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=316108, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nLine-through is too thin over a descendant inline box\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"text-decoration: line-through; text-decoration-thickness: 30px\"\u003e\n    1\u003cspan\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e3\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\nThe line-through should be 30px thick across 1, 2 and 3. Instead the segment\nover the \u003cspan\u003e (2) was a thin line: its thickness came from the span, whose\ntext-decoration-thickness is auto, rather than from the div that set the\nline-through.\n\nWhen painting a line-through, paintForegroundDecorations took the thickness,\nposition and color from the text's direct parent inline box. For text inside an\ninline box that does not itself set the decoration that parent is the wrong box,\nsince the decoration was established by an ancestor.\n\npaintForegroundDecorations now collects the decorating boxes by walking the\ninline box ancestors and paints the line-through using the style of the box that\nestablished it, one per decorating box. This mirrors what the background\n(underline/overline) path already does, which is why those were unaffected.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=316108\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/314391@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 394ad5bab62c014fdf8c68ecc00006bb83497bca\nwpt-pr: 64441\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-thickness-linethrough-descendant-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-thickness-linethrough-descendant-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-thickness-linethrough-descendant-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-thickness-linethrough-descendant-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-thickness-linethrough-descendant-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-thickness-linethrough-descendant-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-thickness-linethrough-descendant-004-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-thickness-linethrough-descendant-004.html"], "git_node": "f2559b3c1ebecbb7a200ff982aebd21ba9ff5cf2", "git_parents": ["3eb455fc21e2b6244fc9480b0129e18aac3bb631"], "node": "f83f473fa7cb4ebab7d4f35b04c46fa6fa7b3336", "parents": ["6efeed5cbe174e0b8c0f88d7785494bd3db9d2dc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089412 [wpt PR 64445] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=47815, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nfirst-letter not updated when ::before pseudo-element is dynamically added\n\nWhen you have a block with ::first-letter styling and then dynamically add\na ::before pseudo-element to an element inside it, the ::before content\nshould become the new first letter.\n\nIn the render tree, the ::before renderer gets placed after the existing\nfirst-letter wrapper (which already occupies the first-child slot):\n\n  first-letter wrapper -\u003e \"1\"\n  ::before -\u003e \"A\"\n  remaining text -\u003e \"23\"\n\nAfter detecting staleness, the existing rebuild logic handles the rest:\nit resets the remaining text (which tears down the old wrapper), re-walks\nthe tree to find the new first letter (\"A\" from ::before), and creates\nthe split.\n\nNote that when the first letter were already from ::before\ncontent, the wrapper would be inside the ::before renderer (as its\ndescendant), not beside it as a sibling.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=47815\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/310774@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 203232b38e45d462ffdfe18ff68b75f32b74a42e\nwpt-pr: 64445\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/first-letter-before-dynamic-multi-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/first-letter-before-dynamic-multi.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/first-letter-before-dynamic-on-block-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/first-letter-before-dynamic-on-block.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/first-letter-before-dynamic-punctuation-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/first-letter-before-dynamic-punctuation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/first-letter-before-dynamic-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/first-letter-before-dynamic.html"], "git_node": "e4fcd9c031861ca8dad8bfc642edeb6a97cc3c78", "git_parents": ["f2559b3c1ebecbb7a200ff982aebd21ba9ff5cf2"], "node": "5bb7692c68bd27d26d88deaa7e7c0bb38dd4e05a", "parents": ["f83f473fa7cb4ebab7d4f35b04c46fa6fa7b3336"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089413 [wpt PR 64437] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=320944, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[block-in-inline] text-align:justify shouldn't justify the last line\n\n  \u003cdiv style=\"text-align: justify; width: 200px\"\u003e\n    \u003cspan\u003exx xx xx xx xx xx\u003cdiv\u003eitem\u003c/div\u003eyy yy\u003c/span\u003e\n  \u003c/div\u003e\n\nThe line right before the \u003cdiv\u003e should be start aligned. Instead it was justified, stretched out to the full 200px.\n\nA block level box inside an inline box starts a block, and CSS Text 3 counts\nthe start of a block as a forced line break, so the line before it is the last\nline before a forced line break and follows text-align-last.\n\nThe justify check now treats ForcedLineBreakByBlockContent as a forced line break too, mirroring layoutInlineContent.\nThis also lets text-align-last: justify justify the line before the block, which it used to skip.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=320944\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/318562@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 16cc3039191861e50cb55b9d3a97f0b2b883c36f\nwpt-pr: 64437\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/text-align/reference/text-align-justify-block-in-inline-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/text-align/reference/text-align-last-justify-block-in-inline-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/text-align/text-align-justify-block-in-inline.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/text-align/text-align-last-justify-block-in-inline.html"], "git_node": "77cb4a70f7838a3c72032c411625e20f9e4ad1ef", "git_parents": ["e4fcd9c031861ca8dad8bfc642edeb6a97cc3c78"], "node": "27bae162e8948c5ea2e5687c4bf31e203bf1f904", "parents": ["5bb7692c68bd27d26d88deaa7e7c0bb38dd4e05a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089413 [wpt PR 64437] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64437\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-text/text-align/text-align-inline-end-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "54b9c436ef93b728ea3b4e9b1a9dd49fd7a85090", "git_parents": ["77cb4a70f7838a3c72032c411625e20f9e4ad1ef"], "node": "31b8cdb3336f1cb7e36907078ac5243d1347e0c2", "parents": ["27bae162e8948c5ea2e5687c4bf31e203bf1f904"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nikolas Zimmermann \u003cnzimmermann@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089414 [wpt PR 64446] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328003, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nREGRESSION(324026@main): [Legacy SVG] ASSERTION FAILED: isDescendantOf(&view()) in RenderObject::repaint() for a marker that references its own resource container\n\nSince 324026@main, which registered CSS clients for mask references in the\nlegacy SVG engine, svg/painting/marker-with-mask-cycle-crash.html\ntriggers an assertion. The test constructs a reference cycle: a \u003cmarker\u003e\nreferences a \u003cmask\u003e, whose content contains a \u003cpath\u003e that in turn\nreferences the \u003cmarker\u003e.\n\nThe assertion results from the following actions during creation of the\n\u003cmarker\u003e renderer:\n\n1. RenderElement::initializeStyle() invokes styleDidChange() on the newly\n   created renderer, before it has been inserted into the render tree.\n\n2. During styleDidChange(), the \u003cmarker\u003e renderer registers itself as a\n   client of the referenced \u003cmask\u003e element.\n\n3. The resource container registers itself with its tree scope. Since the\n   \u003cpath\u003e within the \u003cmask\u003e holds a pending reference to the \u003cmarker\u003e,\n   registration resolves that reference and updates the cached resources\n   of the \u003cpath\u003e, which in turn invalidates the \u003cmask\u003e and notifies all of its clients.\n\n4. The notified clients include the \u003cmarker\u003e renderer itself. The legacy\n   engine tries to repaints it, yet the renderer is still not attached to\n   the render tree and RenderObject::repaint() asserts.\n\nA \u003cclipPath\u003e instead of the \u003cmask\u003e leads to the same assertion. That\nvariant is not a regression from 324026@main: the legacy engine already\nregistered CSS clients for clip-path (and filter) references before it,\nso it asserted before as well.\n\nResolve this by deferring resource registration from styleDidChange() to\ninsertedIntoTree(). The resource container is then part of the render\ntree by the time its pending clients are resolved, and any resulting\nrepaint operates on an attached renderer.\n\nLBSE registers its resource containers in the same way. It didn't assert\nonly because of its invalidation path returns early for renderers that\nstill require layout, which is always the case for a newly created renderer.\nFor consistency, LBSE now defers registration to insertedIntoTree() as well,\nand CSSSVGResourceElementClient::resourceChanged() asserts, for both engines,\nthat the client renderer has a parent.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328003\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324619@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: afe38435cbc4b18c0fb7a210478c8bd269f43b66\nwpt-pr: 64446\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/painting/marker-with-clip-path-cycle-crash.html"], "git_node": "66ec0bec49cc50a9afb94f03842c4b462d17aa67", "git_parents": ["54b9c436ef93b728ea3b4e9b1a9dd49fd7a85090"], "node": "6f0f827963958eceed4e21e6ab8c4afb9179afad", "parents": ["31b8cdb3336f1cb7e36907078ac5243d1347e0c2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Elika Etemad \u003cfantasai.bugs@inkedblade.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089415 [wpt PR 64451] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=285222, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nTest inline layout in writing-mode: sideways-lr\n\nThese tests come from two WebKit changes, exported together because the second one edits a test the first one adds:\n- Convert (non-bidi) inline content coordinates for writing-mode: sideways-lr (https://commits.webkit.org/288381@main)\n- Switch border/background fragmentation to accommodate sideways-lr (https://commits.webkit.org/288383@main)\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=285222\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=285285\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: efa59d198328f41c6b5f9067d7c46ad79ccd6ea6\nwpt-pr: 64451\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/sideways-inline-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/sideways-inline-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/sideways-inline-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/sideways-inline-002.html"], "git_node": "3d1ecb83813a0dfd815e52fa38a62edf16b66116", "git_parents": ["66ec0bec49cc50a9afb94f03842c4b462d17aa67"], "node": "20e8ac525bb28d7d05498b02548627a240df88f6", "parents": ["6f0f827963958eceed4e21e6ab8c4afb9179afad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089415 [wpt PR 64451] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64451\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-writing-modes/sideways-inline-002.html.ini"], "git_node": "f589db8286d3d94a2c757b92ee5cec4b767c7395", "git_parents": ["3d1ecb83813a0dfd815e52fa38a62edf16b66116"], "node": "81b06ea4fc726a8e22b99b960caa6b7c9cdb7ef8", "parents": ["20e8ac525bb28d7d05498b02548627a240df88f6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vitor Roriz \u003cvitor.roriz@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089416 [wpt PR 64450] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=287423, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd a text-autospace crash test with ruby\n\nThis test comes from two WebKit changes, exported together because the second one edits the test the first one adds:\n- Adding `text-autospace: normal` causes some pages to crash (https://commits.webkit.org/290211@main)\n- Crash WPT text-autospace-ruby-crash takes no reference (https://commits.webkit.org/290224@main)\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=287423\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=287488\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 10da42f2471fd734e33bac946eb977b21d7fe5e4\nwpt-pr: 64450\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/text-autospace/crashtests/text-autospace-ruby-crash.html"], "git_node": "7a8f5dfe3fea263e3f24b50f52321adb5d0fc382", "git_parents": ["f589db8286d3d94a2c757b92ee5cec4b767c7395"], "node": "35d7a149d835afab28b8815096fb660d559bba7c", "parents": ["81b06ea4fc726a8e22b99b960caa6b7c9cdb7ef8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ian Gower \u003ci_gower@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089417 [wpt PR 64447] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=257369, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-counter-styles] Support the extended range for the longhand East Asian counter styles\n\nThe nine longhand East Asian counter styles stopped at -9999 to 9999, so a list numbered\npast 9999 dropped to cjk-decimal partway down. Chrome and Firefox already number the\nChinese and Korean styles over the extended range.\n\ncounterForSystemCJK only implemented the Chinese form of the algorithm, and the Japanese\nand Korean styles were built out of additive-symbols, which cannot reach past one group of\nfour digits. Therefore the algorithm now takes the language and the formality, and the\nJapanese and Korean styles get internal systems like the Chinese ones already have. The\nnegative sign now comes from the negative descriptor, because the Japanese and Korean signs\nare four characters long and every other system already works that way. The output buffer\nhas room for two characters per abstract character, because the simplified Chinese fourth\ngroup marker is spelled with two and the old one held a single character of each.\n\nResync the nine reference files corrected by web-platform-tests/wpt#54469. WebKit imported\nthis directory on 2025-08-21, twelve days before that landed, so the copies here still\nexpect the informal \"drop ones\" rule in the formal styles and spell the Korean styles with\ncharacters from the Chinese and hangul ones.\n\nCover the range with reference tests in css/css-counter-styles, one per style, rather than a\nlayout test. Section 7.1.2 is optional, so they carry the .optional filename flag, and they\ngo upstream next. The values stay inside what a counter value can hold, so the rows are all\ndefined by the algorithm rather than by where an engine truncates.\n\nA counter value is an int, so the reachable part of the new range stops at 2147483647.\nReaching the rest of it needs a wider counter value, which is separate work.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=257369\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/320887@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1657914be1f348d9d59c1c31930c2f5c08c194f0\nwpt-pr: 64447\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/cjk-ideographic/counter-cjk-ideographic-extended-range-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/cjk-ideographic/counter-cjk-ideographic-extended-range.optional.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/japanese-formal/counter-japanese-formal-extended-range-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/japanese-formal/counter-japanese-formal-extended-range.optional.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/japanese-informal/counter-japanese-informal-extended-range-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/japanese-informal/counter-japanese-informal-extended-range.optional.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/korean-hangul-formal/counter-korean-hangul-formal-extended-range-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/korean-hangul-formal/counter-korean-hangul-formal-extended-range.optional.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/korean-hanja-formal/counter-korean-hanja-formal-extended-range-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/korean-hanja-formal/counter-korean-hanja-formal-extended-range.optional.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/korean-hanja-informal/counter-korean-hanja-informal-extended-range-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/korean-hanja-informal/counter-korean-hanja-informal-extended-range.optional.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/simp-chinese-formal/counter-simp-chinese-formal-extended-range-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/simp-chinese-formal/counter-simp-chinese-formal-extended-range.optional.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/simp-chinese-informal/counter-simp-chinese-informal-extended-range-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/simp-chinese-informal/counter-simp-chinese-informal-extended-range.optional.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/trad-chinese-formal/counter-trad-chinese-formal-extended-range-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/trad-chinese-formal/counter-trad-chinese-formal-extended-range.optional.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/trad-chinese-informal/counter-trad-chinese-informal-extended-range-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/trad-chinese-informal/counter-trad-chinese-informal-extended-range.optional.html"], "git_node": "52784dafa37040f46be79fff786dbbfe79c5bd88", "git_parents": ["7a8f5dfe3fea263e3f24b50f52321adb5d0fc382"], "node": "c59cceed57868ca0a30f641fb0f184f66ca1f839", "parents": ["35d7a149d835afab28b8815096fb660d559bba7c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089417 [wpt PR 64447] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64447\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-counter-styles/cjk-ideographic/counter-cjk-ideographic-extended-range.optional.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-counter-styles/japanese-formal/counter-japanese-formal-extended-range.optional.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-counter-styles/japanese-informal/co