e6917a2f6e51e94e86c12dba6f6f3772", "parents": ["6781c83cd91e70587af11b713182805973e54160"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091798 - Emit a move or nothing for computeEffectiveAddress with a zero offset on x86. r=jandem\n\nlea with a bare base register is a register copy, and a no-op when the\nbase is the destination, as in the pre-barrier paths. Emitting mov or\nnothing instead saves the address-generation work and, in the no-op case,\nthe instruction. On JetStream 3 this removes about 3.4K no-op LEAs and\nturns about 19K more into moves, mostly in Ion.\n\nFound via x86lint.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341901\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/x86-shared/MacroAssembler-x86-shared.h", "js/src/jit/x86/MacroAssembler-x86.h"], "git_node": "9d9644d11cd91fdb193e3ec29acf78c523b385d3", "git_parents": ["0d3e5817ecdcb3be8a1d61b8fd65cffd3576de04"], "node": "5caf6971e9c88678648a21a5d14ae5e6234ca45d", "parents": ["0ff52925e6917a2f6e51e94e86c12dba6f6f3772"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Johannes Salas Schmidt \u003cjoschmidt@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088428 - Reject logins containing lone surrogate pairs  r=markh,dimi\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338735\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/passwordmgr/LoginHelper.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/passwordmgr/test/unit/test_logins_change.js"], "git_node": "3c18802502f6e579105f29cfa36782f7b83493d6", "git_parents": ["9d9644d11cd91fdb193e3ec29acf78c523b385d3"], "node": "397e912a8905a81fe50c312039d5f402d52f7adc", "parents": ["5caf6971e9c88678648a21a5d14ae5e6234ca45d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089680. r=gfx-reviewers,wsmind\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342536\n", "files": ["image/VectorImage.cpp"], "git_node": "99264c48ab0630977891fc2733fb5751f5344637", "git_parents": ["3c18802502f6e579105f29cfa36782f7b83493d6"], "node": "771a19d3230991db6ebdca4ae69f0c57e31a93bb", "parents": ["397e912a8905a81fe50c312039d5f402d52f7adc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harshit Sohaney \u003chsohaney@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078939 - Update icons and strings for Mini Window's and the overlay entrypoint. r=fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,kcochrane,bolsson,niklas\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342181\n", "files": ["browser/components/miniwindow/assets/full-page-20.svg", "browser/components/miniwindow/assets/part-of-page-20.svg", "browser/components/miniwindow/assets/put-tab-back-16.svg", "browser/components/miniwindow/jar.mn", "browser/components/screenshots/screenshots-buttons.css", "browser/components/screenshots/screenshots-buttons.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/miniWindow.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/toolbarbutton-icons.css"], "git_node": "22612fb57a8ab68b17c4a66b89f29c7fb6a9c40c", "git_parents": ["99264c48ab0630977891fc2733fb5751f5344637"], "node": "f4377c4bec503eb453fe3612a4d433dae65bf7c4", "parents": ["771a19d3230991db6ebdca4ae69f0c57e31a93bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Moyin \u003cmadeyemi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092509 - Add Listen to Page to Secret Settings in Beta r=android-reviewers,ltokhtamuradova\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342540\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/SecretSettingsFragment.kt"], "git_node": "fc7af1e5426cfd0f6ff3d7ee5727a9b99c8f3bf3", "git_parents": ["22612fb57a8ab68b17c4a66b89f29c7fb6a9c40c"], "node": "5cccf882f5baaee83c2ec6b3138ec5b3bc1e952c", "parents": ["f4377c4bec503eb453fe3612a4d433dae65bf7c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Friedberger \u003csimon@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088051 - Keep inherited state when setting a header permissions policy. r=ahedri\n\nSetDeclaredHeaderPolicy called ResetDeclaredPolicy, which also cleared the\nsource origin and the ancestor chain that InheritPolicy had copied from the\ncontainer.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339510\n", "files": ["dom/security/permissionspolicy/PermissionsPolicy.cpp", "dom/security/permissionspolicy/test/browser/browser.toml", "dom/security/permissionspolicy/test/browser/browser_header_combines_inherited_policy.js", "dom/security/permissionspolicy/test/browser/file_header_policy.sjs"], "git_node": "305814fdef420c1211ea2429fcb91ad59e73fe06", "git_parents": ["fc7af1e5426cfd0f6ff3d7ee5727a9b99c8f3bf3"], "node": "bee73310dfbb4b863bab7b42feb48f77ec89a49f", "parents": ["5cccf882f5baaee83c2ec6b3138ec5b3bc1e952c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Menzel \u003cpmenzel@molgen.mpg.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092225 - Sync with the X server when destroying a WebRender compositor on X11. r=stransky,gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nWith the GPU process, the parent destroys the window on its own X\nconnection right after WillClose has removed the renderer. The X server\ndoes not order requests across clients, so it can process DestroyWindow\nbefore the GPU process\u2019s last request that names the window, and GDK\u2019s\nerror handler crashes the GPU process at quit:\n\n    (xfwm4) The error was 'BadWindow (invalid Window parameter)'.\n    (Details: serial 1258 error_code 3 request_code 147 (unknown) minor_code 1)\n\nRequest 147 minor 1 is Present.PresentPixmap from RenderCompositorEGL.\nSoftware WebRender has the same gap: RenderCompositorSWGL blits through\nnsShmImage::Put, which flushes but only waits for the round trip on the\nnext frame, or through the cairo-xlib XPutImage fallback, which does not\nflush explicitly. RenderCompositorOGLSWGL and the GLX RenderCompositorOGL\nalso present to the window.\n\nSo do the round trip in the RenderCompositor base destructor, which runs\nafter every subclass has released its window resources.\n\nAssisted-by: claude-opus-5.5 (Claude Code)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342297\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderCompositor.cpp"], "git_node": "39b4131c61b95566fbb793f8b0f4b1b08a7734ba", "git_parents": ["305814fdef420c1211ea2429fcb91ad59e73fe06"], "node": "a8da231a426647ed4ca41f30cc45efc4b26c13ce", "parents": ["bee73310dfbb4b863bab7b42feb48f77ec89a49f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mitar \u003cmitar.git@tnode.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090791 - [Linux] Launch local handler applications through GIO r=stransky,gtk-reviewers\n\nAn executable chosen as the handler of a MIME type or URI scheme, or named\nby a mailcap file, was run with nsIProcess, while applications from\ndesktop entries are launched through GIO. Such a handler received no\nactivation token on Wayland, inherited MOZ_APP_LAUNCHER, which the GIO\nlaunch context unsets for third-party handlers (bug 1494436), and stayed\nin Firefox's cgroup, where GLib cannot give it a systemd scope of its own.\n\nnsIGIOService::CreateAppFromExecutable() describes the executable as a\ndesktop entry whose Exec key passes the URI unchanged (%u with\nX-GIO-NoFuse) or the path of the local file (%f). The path is quoted,\nand % is doubled. We fall back to nsIProcess when GLib refuses the\nexecutable: when it is no executable file, so that the error is still\nreported, and when its path contains %, as GLib checks the Exec\nkey before it turns %% back into %. OpenBSD keeps nsIProcess.\n\nOn Wayland the launch waits for the activation token, as for other GIO\nhandlers, so errors after the executable check are logged instead of\nreturned, and GLib spawns the handler through gio-launch-desktop, so it is\nno longer a direct child of Firefox.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340772\n", "files": ["toolkit/system/gnome/nsGIOService.cpp", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.xpcom.d.ts", "uriloader/exthandler/nsLocalHandlerApp.cpp", "uriloader/exthandler/nsMIMEInfoImpl.cpp", "uriloader/exthandler/nsMIMEInfoImpl.h", "uriloader/exthandler/tests/unit/test_launch_local_handler.js", "uriloader/exthandler/tests/unit/xpcshell.toml", "widget/gtk/GRefPtr.h", "xpcom/system/nsIGIOService.idl"], "git_node": "cb24fc0b765df47312f72125ee2fff8db3e47a84", "git_parents": ["39b4131c61b95566fbb793f8b0f4b1b08a7734ba"], "node": "78759f77f307cbc6dc6394dbe57cdbe45086c806", "parents": ["a8da231a426647ed4ca41f30cc45efc4b26c13ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Louis-Philippe \u003clpmanette@omnicesoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089552 - [Wayland][HDR] Harden parameter validation for HDR metadata to prevent protocol errors. r=stransky,gtk-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340497\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/NativeLayerWayland.cpp", "widget/gtk/WaylandSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/WaylandSurface.h"], "git_node": "51ffb1b70cb218bb9e44afec9433f33307b3adea", "git_parents": ["cb24fc0b765df47312f72125ee2fff8db3e47a84"], "node": "bdbd57d4dd483d4f2774175083b68b63c5d0048c", "parents": ["78759f77f307cbc6dc6394dbe57cdbe45086c806"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Calixte Denizet \u003ccalixte.denizet@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092533 - Update PDF.js to new version 5430213a11db643b2645ba3ae02ed761d1b46623 r=pdfjs-reviewers,marco\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342567\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/PdfJsVersion.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.renderer.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.scripting.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/build/pdf.worker.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/cmaps/78-EUC-H.bcmap", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/cmaps/78-EUC-H.bcmap.br", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/cmaps/78-EUC-V.bcmap", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/cmaps/78-EUC-V.bcmap.br", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/web/cmaps/78-H.bcmap", "too