150e758df6\npl -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\npt-BR -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\npt-PT -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\nrm -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\nro -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\nru -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\nsk -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\nsl -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\nson -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\nsq -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\nsr -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\nsv-SE -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\nta -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\nte -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\nth -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\ntl -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\ntr -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\ntrs -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\nuk -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\nur -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\nuz -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\nvi -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\nwo -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\nxh -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\nzam -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\nzh-CN -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\nzh-TW -\u003e 0a728ef4d40f56a36dc7bc97f1a780150e758df6\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "fbbf4f32f4b1c03286597dd73c05e89fad3bc73b", "git_parents": ["0ce97a5b02eeeb605a012214e55250db8492f5d0"], "node": "b0d80a463f1b4efb391b49ae2875148a1c2b7746", "parents": ["faedd60ec4bc6c05358ec71d767435ab46756f59"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Niklas Jaeschke \u003cjjaschke@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092636 - Skip frame destruction bookkeeping that has nothing to remove. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nRemoving a frame from the overflow tracker, the approximately visible list and\nthe retained display list data each did a lookup (or an ancestor walk) even\nwhen there was nothing to remove.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342705\n", "files": ["layout/base/OverflowChangedTracker.h", "layout/base/PresShell.cpp", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "aa26cef6e7cfd122eb9c8b15f576af72bab2b30b", "git_parents": ["fbbf4f32f4b1c03286597dd73c05e89fad3bc73b"], "node": "6600e416403ce8338af4af1afce8dedd1d3c6903", "parents": ["b0d80a463f1b4efb391b49ae2875148a1c2b7746"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alastor0325 \u003calastor0325@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1731727 - Part 1: Read the constant IV of a protected seig sample group entry. r=media-playback-reviewers,aosmond\n\nRead the constant IV of a CENC sample group entry when the entry is protected\nand has a per-sample IV size of 0, which is the usual cbcs layout, and reject\nan unprotected entry that declares a per-sample IV size.\n\nThis follows the syntax of the sample group entry in ISO/IEC 23001-7:2023\nsection 6, where the constant IV size and the constant IV follow the key ID\nonly when the per-sample IV size is 0, whatever the protection state is. A\nprotected entry uses this to give all of its samples one constant IV. An\nunprotected entry also has a per-sample IV size of 0 (section 7.2.3), but its\nsamples are not decrypted, so no IV is read for it.\n\nThe parser only read a constant IV for unprotected entries and rejected the\nprotected ones, so the whole sample group description was dropped and the\nsamples fell back to the track default key ID and IV. Key rotation through a\nfragment-level seig sample group was therefore ignored for cbcs, and the\nrotated samples were decrypted with the previous key.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340131\n", "files": ["dom/media/mp4/MoofParser.cpp"], "git_node": "6960d38d9730dda627a5304a0fd094c4893079d4", "git_parents": ["aa26cef6e7cfd122eb9c8b15f576af72bab2b30b"], "node": "9d3bf9147562debdadc0c8cf6a338b2db186f073", "parents": ["6600e416403ce8338af4af1afce8dedd1d3c6903"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alastor0325 \u003calastor0325@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1731727 - Part 2: Support cbcs samples in the WMF ClearKey decryptor. r=media-playback-reviewers,aosmond\n\nPass the protection scheme and the encryption pattern that the media engine\nsets on each sample to the ClearKey decryption, instead of always treating the\nsample as cenc.\n\nTests use the WMF ClearKey CDM in place of real Media Foundation CDMs, and it\ncould not decrypt cbcs content before.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340132\n", "files": ["media/wmf-clearkey/WMFClearKeyDecryptor.cpp"], "git_node": "5e4f5f22cc95089ce7d460005678ad6da8ddeded", "git_parents": ["6960d38d9730dda627a5304a0fd094c4893079d4"], "node": "6f261ae319ba92160d3c893132360c70a9992137", "parents": ["9d3bf9147562debdadc0c8cf6a338b2db186f073"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alastor0325 \u003calastor0325@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1731727 - Part 3: Test seig key rotation in the MP4 demuxer. r=media-playback-reviewers,aosmond\n\nAdd cenc and cbcs fixtures whose last two fragments switch to a second key\nthrough a fragment-level seig sample group, and check that the demuxed samples\ncarry the rotated key ID and, for cbcs, the constant IV of the sample group\nentry.\n\nEach fixture is a 4 second, 320x180, 30 fps H.264 test pattern from ffmpeg,\npackaged twice by Shaka Packager with a raw key, no clear lead and 1 second\nfragments: once with key A and once with key B. The file keeps the init\nsegment and the first two fragments of the key A packaging, and takes the last\ntwo fragments from the key B packaging. A seig sample group description with\nkey ID B, and a mapping of every sample to it, is appended to each track\nfragment of those two fragments, with the sample data offset moved to match.\nThe pssh box in the movie box is a Common System one that lists both key IDs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340133\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestMP4Demuxer.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/moz.build", "dom/media/test/seig-key-rotation-cbcs.mp4", "dom/media/test/seig-key-rotation-cenc.mp4"], "git_node": "3522edf8d573853d7044febb2c09fec886722130", "git_parents": ["5e4f5f22cc95089ce7d460005678ad6da8ddeded"], "node": "3c8ddf5997d1aa1fa2dc53f8fd186bb70cf5a663", "parents": ["6f261ae319ba92160d3c893132360c70a9992137"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alastor0325 \u003calastor0325@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1731727 - Part 4: Test the per-sample encryption parameters in the WMF ClearKey decryptor. r=media-playback-reviewers,aosmond\n\nCheck that the decryptor passes the protection scheme, the encryption pattern\nand the IV of each sample to the ClearKey decryption, for cenc samples, for\ncbcs samples with a pattern and for cbcs samples without one. The session\nmanager mock moves to a shared header so that both test files use one\ndefinition of it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340134\n", "files": ["media/wmf-clearkey/gtest/MockSessionManagerWrapper.h", "media/wmf-clearkey/gtest/TestWMFClearKeyDecryptor.cpp", "media/wmf-clearkey/gtest/TestWMFClearKeySession.cpp", "media/wmf-clearkey/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "96f96d32ee63dadeaa1cf9ef623c0be7d5aa414e", "git_parents": ["3522edf8d573853d7044febb2c09fec886722130"], "node": "2e7e46672f38f34d7b6743a6d67bc038a20e61eb", "parents": ["3c8ddf5997d1aa1fa2dc53f8fd186bb70cf5a663"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alastor0325 \u003calastor0325@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1731727 - Part 5: Test seig key rotation playback with GMP ClearKey. r=media-playback-reviewers,aosmond\n\nPlay the cenc and cbcs rotation fixtures with both keys provisioned, and with\nthe rotated key withheld. Playback must reach the end in the first case. In\nthe second case it must stall with waitingforkey before the rotation point and\nresume to the end once the rotated key is provided, which shows that the\nrotated key ID is used.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340135\n", "files": ["dom/media/test/mochitest_eme.toml", "dom/media/test/seig-key-rotation-cbcs.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/test/seig-key-rotation-cenc.mp4^headers^", "dom/media/test/seig_key_rotation.js", "dom/media/test/test_eme_seig_key_rotation.html"], "git_node": "435a7158833e45a68f12d581ebd81cb40401c0cf", "git_parents": ["96f96d32ee63dadeaa1cf9ef623c0be7d5aa414e"], "node": "75a780f3fb3de771ed528d8dc522e8e2e0537c7a", "parents": ["2e7e46672f38f34d7b6743a6d67bc038a20e61eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alastor0325 \u003calastor0325@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1731727 - Part 6: Test seig key rotation playback with WMF ClearKey. r=media-playback-reviewers,aosmond\n\nPlay the cenc and cbcs rotation fixtures on the media engine with WMF ClearKey,\nwith the rotated key withheld and with both keys provisioned. Without the\nrotated key, playback must stop before the rotation point. With both keys,\nplayback must reach the end.\n\nOn the media engine, a key that goes missing in the middle of a stream does not\nlead to waitingforkey. The media engine reports waitingforkey only while the\nCDM keeps content enabling pending, and PlayReady does not do that for a\nsample whose key is missing: playback fails with a decode error instead of\nrunning the Wait for Key algorithm that EME requires. WMF ClearKey behaves the\nsame way, because it enables content at once and then fails to decrypt such a\nsample.\n\nSo unlike the GMP test, this test does not wait for the rotated key and then\nprovide it to resume playback, because there is no stall to resume from. It\naccepts either an error or waitingforkey, and only requires that playback does\nnot pass the rotation point, which is what shows that the rotated key ID is\nused.\n\nThe ClearKey CDM keeps every key it receives for the lifetime of its process,\nso the cases without the rotated key run first.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340136\n", "files": ["dom/media/test/mochitest_media_engine.toml", "dom/media/test/test_eme_wmfclearkey_seig_key_rotation.html"], "git_node": "4234740037e3e9329e672e04298237f1f4a22d92", "git_parents": ["435a7158833e45a68f12d581ebd81cb40401c0cf"], "node": "553da2dc623b8fe096cc80251e5d0dd040693ead", "parents": ["75a780f3fb3de771ed528d8dc522e8e2e0537c7a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dre Grant \u003cdgrant@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087660 - Move widget source values into one shared list in WidgetsRegistry.mjs r=maxx\n\nMost widgets repeat \"context_menu\" and \"widget\" in their recordUserAction calls, and shared menu components use the same values for widget_source. This puts them in WIDGET_SOURCES beside WIDGET_USER_ACTIONS in WidgetsRegistry.mjs. Widget-specific sources like \"row\" stay local, and Glean receives the same values.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338944\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/common/WidgetsRegistry.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Clocks/Clocks.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Crossword/Crossword.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/FocusTimer/FocusTimer.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/FramedWidgetCard.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Horoscopes/Horoscopes.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Lists/Lists.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/MoveSubmenu.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/MozWidgetCard.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/PictureOfTheDay/PictureOfTheDay.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Privacy/Privacy.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/RecentSearches/RecentSearches.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Solitaire/Solitaire.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Travel/Travel.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Weather/Weather.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/WidgetMenuFooter.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/WidgetMenuPoweredBy.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/WidgetPlacement.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Widgets.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/useWidgetTelemetry.jsx"], "git_node": "8195c77e14f4537b72f586ef197a6f9ad8946846", "git_parents": ["4234740037e3e9329e672e04298237f1f4a22d92"], "node": "2609a208f95dfb955a2c49e45cf2eb30e313d8cd", "parents": ["553da2dc623b8fe096cc80251e5d0dd040693ead"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091101 - Part 1: Parse fragments up to the seek target before the keyframe lookup. r=media-playback-reviewers,aosmond\n\nA fragmented MP4 that plays with a media element can have fragments that are\nnot parsed yet. A video seek to a time after the last parsed fragment landed\non the last known keyframe, not on the keyframe before the target.\n\nBefore the keyframe lookup, the seek now parses the next fragments until one\nends after the target, or until there are no more fragments.\n\nThe keyframe lookup knows only the keyframes of the parsed fragments. Before\nbug 2080453, the seek read fragments forward until it reached the target.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341545\n", "files": ["dom/media/mp4/SampleIterator.cpp"], "git_node": "3fa697643b4bf5c17b0879dbe39951d463bd9c17", "git_parents": ["8195c77e14f4537b72f586ef197a6f9ad8946846"], "node": "3062263e12721d0eb89bee97d1c49c3fa1e84e04", "parents": ["2609a208f95dfb955a2c49e45cf2eb30e313d8cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091101 - Part 2: Count skipped samples correctly at the end of a fragmented stream and inside one fragment. r=media-playback-reviewers,aosmond\n\nWhen a skip to the next keyframe read to the end of a fragmented stream, the\nsample count asserted in debug and fuzzing builds, and gave 0 in release\nbuilds. When the start and the end were in the same fragment, the count also\nincluded the samples to the end of that fragment.\n\nThe count now accepts the position after the last sample, and it counts only\nthe samples between the two positions when they are in the same fragment.\n\nThe iterator stops at the position after the last sample when it reaches the\nend of the stream. The media player adds the skipped count to the dropped\nframes, so an incorrect count gives incorrect playback quality data.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341546\n", "files": ["dom/media/mp4/SampleIterator.cpp"], "git_node": "67dab7364ac43d0584384aa7b611e1fe20d3b23a", "git_parents": ["3fa697643b4bf5c17b0879dbe39951d463bd9c17"], "node": "5bc12c64fd5cf831abd5f5f8a3535a5777fb7f71", "parents": ["3062263e12721d0eb89bee97d1c49c3fa1e84e04"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091101 - Part 3: Test fragmented MP4 seek and skip counts. r=media-playback-reviewers,aosmond\n\nAdd tests for a fragmented MP4 that has fragments that are not parsed yet.\nA seek must land on the keyframe before the target, a skip that reads to the\nend of the stream must fail with the correct count, and the sample count must\nbe correct inside one fragment and at the end of the stream.\n\nAdd a fixture with several keyframes in each fragment, so that a seek and a\nskip inside one fragment are tested through the demuxer.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341547\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestMP4Demuxer.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/frag_multi_gop.mp4", "dom/media/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "30ac121fcc8e0c83e2ccb5182257df80c9143b15", "git_parents": ["67dab7364ac43d0584384aa7b611e1fe20d3b23a"], "node": "a05145e48701d1e9f3a7d30b123cf699f3d006c5", "parents": ["5bc12c64fd5cf831abd5f5f8a3535a5777fb7f71"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794604532, "git_changesets": ["0d3e5817ecdcb3be8a1d61b8fd65cffd3576de04", "9d9644d11cd91fdb193e3ec29acf78c523b385d3", "3c18802502f6e579105f29cfa36782f7b83493d6", "99264c48ab0630977891fc2733fb5751f5344637", "22612fb57a8ab68b17c4a66b89f29c7fb6a9c40c", "fc7af1e5426cfd0f6ff3d7ee5727a9b99c8f3bf3", "305814fdef420c1211ea2429fcb91ad59e73fe06", "39b4131c61b95566fbb793f8b0f4b1b08a7734ba", "cb24fc0b765df47312f72125ee2fff8db3e47a84", "51ffb1b70cb218bb9e44afec9433f33307b3adea", "7882638c86fb41499d485bfeddb9f70406bed761", "312b0658d4fbae1b1bb57532e2205c96fbe01757", "475df73106cb9e1f67764b5e0ec3b0a79cd76532", "6f3e5c023e68adbade792a987a152d7d930e57c9", "e72acd40afdf6572ee4f358f8df9b5b6df85baa9", "b0255bea113df03a1ab8e5fcb04e3038364c59a7", "0dda077b856c21cb0a4ecf442693d5bbdfd69011", "a3e3bc6e2a03ff38fe9a2ca1b5bae7ab8b1d8a8b", "72019fc8615109dc33b0e4730a56ec0c12e72f59", "98e526109ac55aa4371831206d63a5a021cc5b89", "aa3813e889bd5239fad51cc08f982149ed3bbc99", "fb3376a2a8545d18437dc885e708f0a623d304f6", "e813a1545089e443d6e9170ea97d2bdd225f4a4d", "fefbae596f5a5a024b98d212b589c38af2ebfc4f", "a5368422625abded5e6393964c8c7788606a265d", "c5b23792ba288308c26f2f2536b14ff0163d0943", "91989a949e778589a15aed9408775c3913f3aaff", "e1da14d64fab840c3193e1a02a8cf317972ab280", "73521f95b2e8466959ddb7a4bd599f9d2ea2408e", "079fa6f4ae3e253be4d742351a250471f0f0e5e2", "61cba4943c9e4df99298bdcb2064c5539c3bd0c6", "81ab73f807b916a450afa29bfaf09c15d14e225d", "a64aebb49bc5f523a8c53caddcb6b4690e01c738", "a50ac0d83e98218086668e198244ad882b9c8a90", "a7ac55c3646a5f24ff56ba135833a0a0715e4915", "50de4adde523f8c1181d97f48e389a2a73a86d1c", "8341cfa1f58d9f63daccd7d24f118c33d55e1058", "a80876a1a0289d90662329fb6c05127ef4f19095", "6b50b61de91f678fd8d7aeaa5d0e985612b8e9e0", "38851d434c3749fb0612de499856dbfce370ca5e", "66ddb60fdb2dc331e1379f079ded91dce40358cd", "a693792dc629cc786aa9aede90396eac7daaaa1c", "48bcce5ab5abb69099731a9a96d0735d240b68a8", "ad8ff0b2c93b921fb4777579b61ded2454317aba", "dda77d3e170d11e0ee7f2db165eb3f4d1430e3e5", "2577e1ffd7c48a9b88223d850e10f1fe57a9f36f", "d7170bc4cc670e6816b2173f4e2bdc6068cf3028", "f520abc1d74d8767c2e27922a1075d59f70c074f", "cf7dc8682f1c9a8eb9446be758437fcecf547828", "90e1e0804aafce810a9ce361d32b71a37cee0cc5", "bf3a37933374f8a0cc635d51d76ba09f06e9294e", "a1e9e06a819cf9dbf51c0806be7b3ff55e07afd4", "7c82c0685a5669155e789b2fe188378d4861e401", "e0fab0bc175b5217dd62e95e6fffc0473d19166c", "7d92295174c6cbbd84ae6b6c0ca13ee79d75a7ce", "64bf0be265f7dbd36c0b171b2eee5d81662bac50", "1b3e377ada22a323b0b47a12159424b9b23a6d61", "a03572be3551eba3e0c271c7ea8f7c22ee19c2e0", "dcd6a8da3ca976600d018816d84bf0b96334acac", "25dd0458572ce41df4a8a32edebe70d93a40e338", "e2c254f4b79aff891c284d22a1589ed92333ffa5", "4341c31075592bfc96506b757297156fcfc4d896", "68062ebfdc4df509913f2e1251f7657e3b7170c6", "6886202f8bb7d9f0d4afc674128327659c45a816", "e78f3dbf173e4b17664199d6fee91331ad8072f4", "ee7dcb94e7c7637a61ff58036223369ce87bb968", "fcd0da65a6d447da330870bed8d067ff21ad24c4", "29f1fb674a93fdbc351b8a6bbc99b422c6902ba1", "36ff9bdcd33d243d35e1136bb030e9cda941c314", "34ee244c4f1f0f3b962b492f14ce8f757955606b", "e2d56589eb3c71eadf2e10adf80fe74389659f27", "a86262f06ede3514f349fe426f1baf06eace3fed", "d58842133df9c6bb0103f8f3b014a6647565baf8", "67c79f8599e129e8d85cc9e53b0edcf7f7bea6ed", "e0ebd3dc5a40eb8b364c5b3681ec5bcb2c268f5a", "ea800026502e5731719d30c6fc1c542d988cc6d4", "0d62bc1ba73ba1f93b6d5328f2b49e0ba6f99e6a", "bff489c8aa740b819cd4cca9586307c8268f66f6", "25345c2472928a1eab72a17b3ff178eb42d1b55b", "4f7a38d818e6ac1bca38ec5233135ce6fb0a28fd", "2ff3850524492fb92ac246b5ac92d728312256d0", "bfcb341d3e2ea447329a7f4c6e9e1b1d99216394", "89021a79cf23666170979c46dcea1389c72e4d29", "bbe0dbe21f1548de22322e78b092b8c7ba713caf", "f97045ec8fa8783a47c1e640dd1a0dc412b0b854", "574dab78b78680f01623cd3b12ca4f1109ba1f73", "bd70cbdde2568e62ab1377a49d0fb747524d6658", "2de94fa60a5cd7f5acd782adf835840ae6eff12b", "ca700f27d8cfa1ef03ea9837cc8ec1a8b525f54b", "748ec1fc1801f986349cf3a20371a3063c0bb6b8", "b99e2e43264c15ebef6923841367489aa90dcf6f", "d3ff08a16272d4134aafc63cf9e213964f2f157b", "e85782bce171483995a83c21fa613e08d464b5bf", "f76d73479944a0eb8655aedfff81e1241a729408", "988dc5e5440d1661121c6abb951e65105829b9e4", "b1c58d9fb09efb26ea73aef0bf97c8dfae66ec44", "30ff60f17e02db1b4dc81b02c295fe1ec474b183", "ee72d17814107464372d303f38b4d84586da54e3", "827b4fce11c0380d4fdc00d80cdb6ad48cb66fde", "fac5a4479e9ef140262b3f7cd5c8d91199bf0c9f", "0ce97a5b02eeeb605a012214e55250db8492f5d0", "fbbf4f32f4b1c03286597dd73c05e89fad3bc73b", "aa26cef6e7cfd122eb9c8b15f576af72bab2b30b", "6960d38d9730dda627a5304a0fd094c4893079d4", "5e4f5f22cc95089ce7d460005678ad6da8ddeded", "3522edf8d573853d7044febb2c09fec886722130", "96f96d32ee63dadeaa1cf9ef623c0be7d5aa414e", "435a7158833e45a68f12d581ebd81cb40401c0cf", "4234740037e3e9329e672e04298237f1f4a22d92", "8195c77e14f4537b72f586ef197a6f9ad8946846", "3fa697643b4bf5c17b0879dbe39951d463bd9c17", "67dab7364ac43d0584384aa7b611e1fe20d3b23a", "30ac121fcc8e0c83e2ccb5182257df80c9143b15"], "user": "ctuns@mozilla.com"}, "45783": {"changesets": [{"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Automatic newtab version bump NO BUG a=release CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/manifest.json"], "git_node": "6beeccd5eef3aa453b1a9bd267f6410b0f38121e", "git_parents": ["30ac121fcc8e0c83e2ccb5182257df80c9143b15"], "node": "fb0bcf4048ae0bb353f0a22fed8a5e70420de8ac", "parents": ["a05145e48701d1e9f3a7d30b123cf699f3d006c5"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794604655, "git_changesets": ["6beeccd5eef3aa453b1a9bd267f6410b0f38121e"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45784": {"changesets": [{"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079061 - Add a crashtest. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333030\n", "files": ["dom/media/webvtt/test/crashtests/2079061.html", "dom/media/webvtt/test/crashtests/crashtests.list"], "git_node": "e0fe5dfe3e91c724c623850eb61f6e014a88d37c", "git_parents": ["30ac121fcc8e0c83e2ccb5182257df80c9143b15"], "node": "dfa70e658864306134585e3f76b7afedcc9f0aac", "parents": ["a05145e48701d1e9f3a7d30b123cf699f3d006c5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087617: Allow caching evals containing inner objects r=mgaudet\n\nThere are two cases where the existing restriction actually matters: JSOp::Object, and JSOp::CallSiteObj. Both cases return an object from the script's data. JSOp::Object avoids reuse by only being usable in run-once context. JSOp::CallSiteObj is used to implement template literals, and is required by the spec to always return the same object for a given parse node. (See [the MDN article on template literals](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Template_literals#:~:text=exact%20same%20literal%20array).)\n\nThis patch addresses the JSOp::Object case by not marking eval scripts as runOnce. The JSOp::Object optimization is the only effect of that flag, so the only thing we lose is slightly slower initialization of large top-level object literals in evals. In exchange, we can cache significantly more evals (in particular including evals with inner functions).\n\nIn the CallSiteObj case, the spec effectively requires us to store the CallSiteObj on the script, meaning that we can't share scripts that use template literals, including in inner functions. To handle this case, we simply disable caching for eval statements that include template literals, which shouldn't be that common.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340548\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/Eval.cpp", "js/src/frontend/BytecodeCompiler.cpp", "js/src/frontend/BytecodeCompiler.h", "js/src/jit-test/tests/basic/eval-object-identity.js", "js/src/vm/JSScript.h"], "git_node": "b8db280dd433022964f0cabe100117881a99e61a", "git_parents": ["e0fe5dfe3e91c724c623850eb61f6e014a88d37c"], "node": "d5c5d66cc2341352d0b0c70596f4716863a00c0a", "parents": ["dfa70e658864306134585e3f76b7afedcc9f0aac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087617: Put eval scripts in the cache immediately r=mgaudet\n\nBecause eval scripts were runOnce, we did a complicated dance to remove them from the cache while running, then put them back afterwards. Now that they're no longer runOnce, we can simplify this code. Note that this also means that we can cache reentrant eval scripts and eval scripts that throw exceptions.\n\nWe also no longer need EvalCacheLookup::trace, because we've shortened the lifetime of its uses.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340549\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/Eval.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/tests/basic/eval-reentrant.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/basic/eval-throws.js", "js/src/vm/Caches.h"], "git_node": "e7229e8f8b287061eb23cda97eaedd594bc95df8", "git_parents": ["b8db280dd433022964f0cabe100117881a99e61a"], "node": "5004ea49b6fd133326236dbf4d2f386c0d6a406f", "parents": ["d5c5d66cc2341352d0b0c70596f4716863a00c0a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087617: Hoist EvalType into Caches.h as an enum class r=mgaudet\n\nThe next patch will start using EvalType in EvalCacheEntry/EvalCacheLookup. To avoid defining bare DIRECT_EVAL / INDIRECT_EVAL in a larger scope, I'm also turning it into an enum class.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340550\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/Eval.cpp", "js/src/vm/Caches.h"], "git_node": "bd95670a0ebb9d59665b4ce781d8abccb14b1897", "git_parents": ["e7229e8f8b287061eb23cda97eaedd594bc95df8"], "node": "965c9b38100e0560c005a062495ac8435bdfb93a", "parents": ["5004ea49b6fd133326236dbf4d2f386c0d6a406f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087617: Cache indirect and top-level evals r=mgaudet\n\nThe existing EvalCacheLookup does not store enough information to cache all evals correctly. In particular:\n\n1. We have to be careful to ensure that we only reuse an eval script if it will appear the same in a backtrace, so we need the introducerScript and introducerPc to be the same.\n2. An indirect eval can call `g.eval(s)` with two different globals for g1 and g2, so we need to compare the current global to the global of the cached script to ensure that they match.\n3. It is technically possible to have a direct and indirect eval at the same site if `eval` is replaced with a bound copy of itself.\n\nI also changed pc from a pointer to an offset, which means that at least on 64-bit, the size of an EvalCacheEntry is unchanged.\n\nWith this patch, we can now cache any eval unless a) it is called directly from Wasm, or b) it contains a JSOp::CallSiteObj. The former could be fixed if we really wanted; the latter is more or less mandatory because of the semantics of tagged template literals.\n\nA couple of existing debugger tests had to be updated because they did not expect script reuse.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340551\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/Eval.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/lib/debuggerNXHelper.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/basic/eval-cache-indirect.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/debug/Script-gc-01.js", "js/src/vm/Caches.h"], "git_node": "d6508e8617277aa654966bdcca350833d3cbb564", "git_parents": ["bd95670a0ebb9d59665b4ce781d8abccb14b1897"], "node": "e851960a73bf7e671bc535dbae09e31660e12c1f", "parents": ["965c9b38100e0560c005a062495ac8435bdfb93a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087617: Speed up hashing for long eval strings r=mgaudet\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340552\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/Eval.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/tests/basic/eval-cache-hash.js"], "git_node": "7c62e7813e68540ac838878097deeb43cb94920c", "git_parents": ["d6508e8617277aa654966bdcca350833d3cbb564"], "node": "63edb368ad6ca52bafdec3ae2d232ece6e9b4d3a", "parents": ["e851960a73bf7e671bc535dbae09e31660e12c1f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087617: Limit eval caching for non-syntactic scopes r=mgaudet\n\nWhile reviewing this stack, Claude consistently leaves comments along the lines of \"this design always does the right thing for non-syntactic scopes, but the reasoning is subtle\".\n\n(Concrete example: \"An unwritten assumption is now more exposed. Compilation reads env through ScopeContext::determineEffectiveScope, which walks a non-syntactic env chain looking for a CallObject. Caching by script+pc is only sound if that walk always gives the same result for a given script+pc. For function-frame direct evals that held trivially: the frame's own CallObject is first on the chain. With top-level direct evals now cached, a non-syntactic global script can run the same JSScript under different env chains; Gecko frame scripts do this. As far as I can tell, no such chain can contain a CallObject, and Debugger.Frame.eval compiles a fresh script each call, so this is fine today. A short comment on the cache key saying it's valid because compilation doesn't depend on env beyond the scope would help keep it that way.\")\n\nScopeContext::determineEffectiveScope looks for a surrounding CallObject and uses its scope. The only concerning case is if there's somehow a CallObject in the non-syntactic scope chain. That seems like a profoundly silly thing to do, but it's not trivial to assert without adding a bunch of code. The simplest way to nip this all in the bud is to just avoid caching direct eval in non-syntactic scopes. Indirect eval always uses the global lexical as the env, so non-syntactic scopes aren't an issue there.\n\n(The more precise version of this would allow direct eval to be cached if the caller frame is a function frame with its own CallObject, because in that case the ScopeContext::determineEffectiveScope walk will always find the immediately surrounding scope, but since we're already being conservative here, it seems better to keep it simple.)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340553\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/Eval.cpp"], "git_node": "7e42543463dae571b64e588d0843021f9b2d6347", "git_parents": ["7c62e7813e68540ac838878097deeb43cb94920c"], "node": "890e99179d1120985c7611d155f4a58da8284c95", "parents": ["63edb368ad6ca52bafdec3ae2d232ece6e9b4d3a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087617: Update xpconnect tests for eval cache changes r=mgaudet\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341616\n", "files": ["js/xpconnect/tests/chrome/test_bug732665.xhtml", "js/xpconnect/tests/chrome/test_bug732665_meta.js"], "git_node": "d789bb6b7fad9edf56b8a90f7aee6c2a748e347a", "git_parents": ["7e42543463dae571b64e588d0843021f9b2d6347"], "node": "284418513464d0cc7f370e149e3ae75038138b53", "parents": ["890e99179d1120985c7611d155f4a58da8284c95"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087617: Update devtools tests for eval cache changes r=devtools-reviewers,bomsy\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341617\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/examples/sourcemaps-reload-compressed/v1/test-functions.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/examples/sourcemaps-reload-uncompressed/v1/test-functions.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/integration/browser_dbg-features-tabs.js"], "git_node": "0a7c83fc1f68e36c4555186c3cf9e79445125d48", "git_parents": ["d789bb6b7fad9edf56b8a90f7aee6c2a748e347a"], "node": "5cedbfe7fca9d55de8897f6c306f435194018662", "parents": ["284418513464d0cc7f370e149e3ae75038138b53"], "tags": []}, {"author": "unifolia \u003cjlewis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088206 - Fix Smart Page UX QA layout issues. r=omarg\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339561\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-base.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-header/aitab-header.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-page.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/A2UI.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_A2UI.js"], "git_node": "cc1dfe99e2f9e5648846a882c440fe747bfc39a4", "git_parents": ["0a7c83fc1f68e36c4555186c3cf9e79445125d48"], "node": "b5f9aa0fb354d56db0e85c1d4ce2eecc275b3c71", "parents": ["5cedbfe7fca9d55de8897f6c306f435194018662"], "tags": []}, {"author": "unifolia \u003cjlewis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085208 - Show untitled Smart Page highlights statements as a list. r=omarg\n\nA Highlights block whose statements all lack titles rendered an empty statement column beside each body. A2UI hydration now turns several untitled statements under a titled Highlights block into a List of their bodies, matching the titles-only conversion from bug 2088206.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339722\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-highlights/aitab-highlights.stories.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/A2UI.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_A2UI.js"], "git_node": "6534e7e890afe6a6e321c7c7bbbd38f95f8473b0", "git_parents": ["cc1dfe99e2f9e5648846a882c440fe747bfc39a4"], "node": "abb00d8c441fd69a30fcb0ed9f2a5b21bdc0a005", "parents": ["b5f9aa0fb354d56db0e85c1d4ce2eecc275b3c71"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sarah Clements \u003csclements@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092168 - Point new contributors to the guide to contributing code at the end of mach bootstrap. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342248\n", "files": ["python/mozboot/mozboot/bootstrap.py", "python/mozboot/mozboot/test/test_bootstrap.py"], "git_node": "0f81af79c9359661c3c7a51107f462a971388028", "git_parents": ["6534e7e890afe6a6e321c7c7bbbd38f95f8473b0"], "node": "3e589c9f528b648fdaf14bc4f880640cec7bfaf1", "parents": ["abb00d8c441fd69a30fcb0ed9f2a5b21bdc0a005"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073171 - Part 1: Handling X1/X2 button presses in EventStateManager. r=masayuki\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334577\n", "files": ["browser/actors/ClickHandlerChild.sys.mjs", "dom/events/EventStateManager.cpp", "dom/events/EventStateManager.h", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "5ca033f9cbf83a8e28594edc370696aa73c3a975", "git_parents": ["0f81af79c9359661c3c7a51107f462a971388028"], "node": "d61d97da77ac3a4bcd4af61a6d969190b984eac9", "parents": ["3e589c9f528b648fdaf14bc4f880640cec7bfaf1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073171 - Part 2: Do the default action for X1/X2 press if not prevented. r=masayuki,webidl,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334578\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp", "dom/base/nsContentUtils.h", "dom/base/nsDOMWindowUtils.cpp", "dom/events/EventStateManager.cpp", "dom/events/test/browser.toml", "dom/events/test/browser_mouse_x_buttons.js", "dom/events/test/file_mouse_x_buttons.html", "dom/ipc/BrowserChild.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserChild.h", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.h", "dom/ipc/CoalescedMouseData.cpp", "dom/ipc/CoalescedMouseData.h", "dom/ipc/PBrowser.ipdl", "dom/webidl/Window.webidl", "widget/MouseEvents.h", "widget/WidgetEventImpl.cpp"], "git_node": "70379ffecc995c5d99021d29b27a8c9f3ad28c1c", "git_parents": ["5ca033f9cbf83a8e28594edc370696aa73c3a975"], "node": "9e6f422d9e5707bc928f918f5a9305d38765158b", "parents": ["d61d97da77ac3a4bcd4af61a6d969190b984eac9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073171 - Part 3: GTK handling of X1/X2 button presses. r=masayuki,gtk-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334579\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsWindow.cpp"], "git_node": "aa03fc8fd27628f6edb4be0bd57697fa3897ffcd", "git_parents": ["70379ffecc995c5d99021d29b27a8c9f3ad28c1c"], "node": "cedcd4688b9d799475f87f7a8660fcc6d404e229", "parents": ["9e6f422d9e5707bc928f918f5a9305d38765158b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073171 - Part 4: Windows handling of X1/X2 button presses. r=masayuki,win-reviewers,gstoll\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335357\n", "files": ["widget/windows/KeyboardLayout.cpp", "widget/windows/KeyboardLayout.h", "widget/windows/WinMessages.h", "widget/windows/WinPointerEvents.cpp", "widget/windows/nsWindow.cpp", "widget/windows/nsWindow.h"], "git_node": "46e16767a441e9c145128f847bd4c26eb74e07b3", "git_parents": ["aa03fc8fd27628f6edb4be0bd57697fa3897ffcd"], "node": "20bfa03ce3faff00e25f2786034907cc2e735e99", "parents": ["cedcd4688b9d799475f87f7a8660fcc6d404e229"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073171 - Part 5: macOS handling of X1/X2 button presses. r=masayuki,spohl\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335694\n", "files": ["widget/cocoa/nsCocoaWindow.mm"], "git_node": "48438ae3207e834ead82317201d8324f07bcfccc", "git_parents": ["46e16767a441e9c145128f847bd4c26eb74e07b3"], "node": "7e63dc30cebfe2feeea0b8b3cc438ce42148bfe4", "parents": ["20bfa03ce3faff00e25f2786034907cc2e735e99"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jack Brown \u003cjbrown@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2010048 - Record Merino stories feed failures and what New Tab shows instead in the newtab-content ping. r=thecount\n\nStories feed failures only reached console.error, so we couldn't tell how often Merino requests fail or what users see instead.\n\n`stories_feed_result` counts requests by result (success or an error type). Failing clients retry every 5 minutes instead of every 30, so it overstates how many users are affected. `stories_feed_state` records what the stories section shows (stories, cache, placeholder or off) with every ping, so it measures the share of New Tab sessions without stories.\n\nBoth go in the private newtab-content ping, and only when that ping is enabled. The stories request can carry the inferred interest vector over OHTTP, and reporting its failure alongside a `client_id` could let someone match the two by time.\n\nA stories response with the wrong shape now falls back like a failed fetch, and `fetchFromEndpoint` resolves to null on invalid JSON instead of rejecting.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339691\n", "files": ["browser/components/newtab/metrics.yaml", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/DiscoveryStreamFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/DiscoveryStreamFeed.test.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_NewTabContentPing.js"], "git_node": "3bd46a59369131f07d0c058aa3f775c141076835", "git_parents": ["48438ae3207e834ead82317201d8324f07bcfccc"], "node": "d9b640caa173fdb32e7a415d74ef23d2109de233", "parents": ["7e63dc30cebfe2feeea0b8b3cc438ce42148bfe4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Foster \u003csfoster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087372 - Improve speculative connect on tab hover. r=sessionstore-reviewers,jswinarton,necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338969\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "1290aa03838f25350f49bad85203036abf20c6f1", "git_parents": ["3bd46a59369131f07d0c058aa3f775c141076835"], "node": "662ca25a07b740614bf9aa7f15418e4e356a5a5f", "parents": ["d9b640caa173fdb32e7a415d74ef23d2109de233"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088015 - Prevent textarea autofill from causing overflow. r=layout-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342088\n", "files": ["layout/reftests/forms/textarea/autofill-preview-multiline-ref.html", "layout/reftests/forms/textarea/autofill-preview-multiline.html", "layout/reftests/forms/textarea/reftest.list", "layout/style/res/forms.css"], "git_node": "87a1e4215a2a610342130111a58c29e53ef76b60", "git_parents": ["1290aa03838f25350f49bad85203036abf20c6f1"], "node": "e76e0682c94ea9e44e8174ce77d6fc1135a80d2c", "parents": ["662ca25a07b740614bf9aa7f15418e4e356a5a5f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sebastian Hengst \u003caryx.github@gmx-topmail.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092632 - disable two NTLM tests which fail after Windows update\n\nThe November 2026 update for Windows 11 contained KB 5135557 which caused the\ntest failures. Temporarily disable them until they are fixed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342756\n", "files": ["netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "cc2b16c31d9917adf4252b0939e11fed515ddffc", "git_parents": ["87a1e4215a2a610342130111a58c29e53ef76b60"], "node": "5266aadb27b2a614c929196a40d0496595349a1a", "parents": ["e76e0682c94ea9e44e8174ce77d6fc1135a80d2c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nhadji \u003cnhadji@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074022 - Run the Fenix instrumented build, baseline profile, macrobenchmark and UI test kinds on git-backed pushes, r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nDrop `run-on-repo-type: [hg]` and `clone-with: hg` from instrumented-build-apk,\ngenerate-baseline-profile-firebase, instrumented-build-macrobenchmark-apk,\nrun-macrobenchmark-firebase and ui-test-apk, so these Fenix tasks schedule on\ngit-backed pushes and check out the GitHub mirror (run-task-git, shallow\nclone).\n\nVerified on try with the whole chain cloning from Git, all green:\ninstrumented-build-apk-fenix, generate-baseline-profile-firebase-fenix,\ninstrumented-build-macrobenchmark-apk-fenix, run-macrobenchmark-firebase-fenix\nand the ui-test-apk-fenix-arm-debug-smoke run, including the two tasks that\ntalk to Firebase Test Lab.\nhttps://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&revision=c2b24335f065e2d63c7fa56eebf2d0f7375c3f97\n\nWith the guard gone, the baseline profile task and the four ui-test-apk tasks\nwithout a `run-on-projects` are offered to every project through the implicit\ndefault, enterprise-firefox included. Which of them run there is for the\nenterprise target task method to decide, not for these kinds.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340897\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/generate-baseline-profile-firebase/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/instrumented-build-apk/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/instrumented-build-macrobenchmark-apk/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/run-macrobenchmark-firebase/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/ui-test-apk/kind.yml"], "git_node": "86f978c14bdd392b7773c0f8cd2ad5308e0808d3", "git_parents": ["cc2b16c31d9917adf4252b0939e11fed515ddffc"], "node": "3a9e17784b98c60eed9e211da300c40e28dfd7e0", "parents": ["5266aadb27b2a614c929196a40d0496595349a1a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091537 - Push the concept of animation-only restyles further down. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-reviewers,boris\n\nThey only serve the purpose of not triggering transitions on inherited\nthings. Move this to before_change_style and process_transitions.\n\nWe need to clear ForCSSRuleChanges because otherwise we'd run\nupdate_animations() twice incorrectly when that flag is set.\n\nThis is the least ugly / more self-contained I could make this, I think\nit's nicer than both the old animation traversal and bug 2019782, but\ndefinitely subtle...\n\nIt does fix some correctness issues where right now we don't trigger\nanimation changes in response to inheritance.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341621\n", "files": ["layout/style/ServoStyleSet.cpp", "servo/components/style/data.rs", "servo/components/style/matching.rs", "servo/components/style/traversal.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/web-animations/responsive/background-position-responsive.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/web-animations/responsive/box-shadow-responsive.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/web-animations/responsive/offsetDistance.html.ini"], "git_node": "92b52c5a87330e79744c12e25716d031323f53fa", "git_parents": ["86f978c14bdd392b7773c0f8cd2ad5308e0808d3"], "node": "fb79d12a4d90eded0d9503030b71f9cccf9a2add", "parents": ["3a9e17784b98c60eed9e211da300c40e28dfd7e0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Heitor Neiva \u003chneiva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092611 - fix mach try with bookmarked changes r=ahochheiden\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342655\n", "files": ["python/mozversioncontrol/mozversioncontrol/repo/jj.py", "python/mozversioncontrol/test/test_branch.py", "python/mozversioncontrol/test/test_push_to_try.py", "python/mozversioncontrol/test/test_try_commit.py"], "git_node": "1218b287d4924d9885c7cfe6dc1876ab352c2447", "git_parents": ["92b52c5a87330e79744c12e25716d031323f53fa"], "node": "7f7b070253d240205ec53de5a2bde560197147fe", "parents": ["fb79d12a4d90eded0d9503030b71f9cccf9a2add"], "tags": []}, {"author": "az \u003cazebrowski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088644 - Recheck ChannelMediaDecoder state after notifying the owner of download progress. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342636\n", "files": ["dom/media/ChannelMediaDecoder.cpp"], "git_node": "a63cf7d5e22d41064da730ecae7d8fb759c19fe5", "git_parents": ["1218b287d4924d9885c7cfe6dc1876ab352c2447"], "node": "2cade6214d115727062de820110c2045540dab3b", "parents": ["7f7b070253d240205ec53de5a2bde560197147fe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julie De Lorenzo \u003cjdelorenzo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063470 - Make tab groups menu secret setting visible in nightly r=android-reviewers,calu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342651\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/SecretSettingsFragment.kt"], "git_node": "9aaa6f195f270afa55a810a3904c8ee5b135706b", "git_parents": ["a63cf7d5e22d41064da730ecae7d8fb759c19fe5"], "node": "8603d5c364018e39b7a51173dd70cbd19c7ae596", "parents": ["2cade6214d115727062de820110c2045540dab3b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maxx Crawford \u003cmcrawford@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087930 - Open the Solitaire widget in a modal dialog while a game is played r=fluent-reviewers,flod,ini\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341634\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Weather/_Weather.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Solitaire/Solitaire.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Solitaire/_Solitaire.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/Solitaire.test.jsx", "browser/locales-preview/newtabPreview.ftl"], "git_node": "981db9220a72b5dd143efcae629787d9a3e39337", "git_parents": ["9aaa6f195f270afa55a810a3904c8ee5b135706b"], "node": "bcc7df82cd9e49af50de1f2ff29725fd4518b3b5", "parents": ["8603d5c364018e39b7a51173dd70cbd19c7ae596"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yubin Jamora \u003cyjamora@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060609 - Add a comment that watch and Monitor refer to the same agent task command r=flozia\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342219\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AgentCommands.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AgentUI.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "a146f913fec1790f9e4b6fad59b0498dd132c4dd", "git_parents": ["981db9220a72b5dd143efcae629787d9a3e39337"], "node": "69f037b41ecdb3489996dd252eeacc79d9e57b1b", "parents": ["bcc7df82cd9e49af50de1f2ff29725fd4518b3b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rebecca King \u003crking@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088234 - Add Set to Default promo to locations subview - r=ip-protection-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,flod,mcleinman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341133\n", "files": ["browser/components/ipprotection/IPProtectionPanel.sys.mjs", "browser/components/ipprotection/assets/location-pin.svg", "browser/components/ipprotection/content/ipprotection-constants.mjs", "browser/components/ipprotection/content/ipprotection-locations.mjs", "browser/components/ipprotection/content/locations-subview.css", "browser/components/ipprotection/tests/browser/browser_ipprotection_location_selector_telemetry.js", "browser/components/ipprotection/tests/browser/browser_ipprotection_locations_keyboard_navigation.js", "browser/components/ipprotection/tests/browser/browser_ipprotection_locations_list.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/ipProtection.ftl"], "git_node": "726ecb120c25828f199696869f06db6c81ee0232", "git_parents": ["a146f913fec1790f9e4b6fad59b0498dd132c4dd"], "node": "f39a96f0bf2924fadfdeed6da2e70153f33bc3c2", "parents": ["69f037b41ecdb3489996dd252eeacc79d9e57b1b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rebecca King \u003crking@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088236 - Add Set to Default promo to built-in VPN settings - r=ip-protection-reviewers,settings-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles,mcleinman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341439\n", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/DefaultBrowserHelper.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/config/privacy.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/tests/privacy/browser_privacy_ipprotection.js"], "git_node": "4bc40525afcb499e7494dbda010e217e8d8f66e0", "git_parents": ["726ecb120c25828f199696869f06db6c81ee0232"], "node": "4fd0012e4f4a836b27035607e315e2f1edba2212", "parents": ["f39a96f0bf2924fadfdeed6da2e70153f33bc3c2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rebecca King \u003crking@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091150 - Refactor handleEvent in IPProtectionPanel to reduce complexity - r=ip-protection-reviewers,mcleinman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341517\n", "files": ["browser/components/ipprotection/IPProtectionPanel.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "e8b02842d1854a9e46a28a9e10e8c9c8ed5c237a", "git_parents": ["4bc40525afcb499e7494dbda010e217e8d8f66e0"], "node": "acb6e88b42ee1b85f05e1ec5c6b130cf1081be02", "parents": ["4fd0012e4f4a836b27035607e315e2f1edba2212"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Minor \u003cdminor@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059792 - Ship Regular Expression Boundaries; r=spidermonkey-reviewers,mgaudet\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338094\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/JitContext.cpp", "js/src/shell/js.cpp", "js/src/tests/jstests.list", "js/src/tests/test262-update.py", "js/src/tests/test262/prs/4975/annexB/built-ins/RegExp/buffer-boundaries/not-supported-outside-unicode-modes.js", "js/src/tests/test262/prs/4975/built-ins/RegExp/buffer-boundaries/slash-lower-case-z-matches-end-of-buffer-u-mode.js", "js/src/tests/test262/prs/4975/built-ins/RegExp/buffer-boundaries/slash-lower-case-z-matches-end-of-buffer-v-mode.js", "js/src/tests/test262/prs/4975/built-ins/RegExp/buffer-boundaries/slash-upper-case-a-matches-start-of-buffer-u-mode.js", "js/src/tests/test262/prs/4975/built-ins/RegExp/buffer-boundaries/slash-upper-case-a-matches-start-of-buffer-v-mode.js", "js/src/tests/test262/prs/4975/built-ins/RegExp/buffer-boundaries/slash-upper-case-z-matches-lineterminatorsequence-end-of-buffer-u-mode.js", "js/src/tests/test262/prs/4975/built-ins/RegExp/buffer-boundaries/slash-upper-case-z-matches-lineterminatorsequence-end-of-buffer-v-mode.js", "js/src/tests/test262/prs/4975/built-ins/RegExp/buffer-boundaries/syntax/u-mode.js", "js/src/tests/test262/prs/4975/built-ins/RegExp/buffer-boundaries/syntax/v-mode.js", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "82791f0109ef3b83d43ff6be7e8b37e5f4d77768", "git_parents": ["e8b02842d1854a9e46a28a9e10e8c9c8ed5c237a"], "node": "cc0033612ebb8c40b520204f3323490675250546", "parents": ["acb6e88b42ee1b85f05e1ec5c6b130cf1081be02"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092596 - Skip regexp/bug2072420.js in non-Intl builds. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,mgaudet\n\nUnicode case-insensitive backreference matching depends on ICU (V8_INTL_SUPPORT). Builds configured with --without-intl-api aren't supported for this, so skip the test there. It uses the same `skip-if: typeof Intl === 'undefined'` directive as the other Intl-dependent regexp tests (e.g. non-unicode-case-folding.js).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342747\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/regexp/bug2072420.js"], "git_node": "a8d9b2455f47cfc4ec80bed530491c4e8f071947", "git_parents": ["82791f0109ef3b83d43ff6be7e8b37e5f4d77768"], "node": "1bed5fa63b16e95710f87c21bbf1b79f1d4c243d", "parents": ["cc0033612ebb8c40b520204f3323490675250546"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089816: Check JIT_ARGS_LENGTH_MAX for non-spread native/bound calls r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nWe already impose this restriction in most places. (See bug 2010945.) After this patch, each JIT_ARGS_LENGTH_MAX check in CacheIR.cpp is independent of spread vs non-spread.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342383\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/cacheir/bug2089816.js", "js/src/jit/CacheIR.cpp"], "git_node": "fe51dd174a21d55885da5ce0e413b1b6503cf689", "git_parents": ["a8d9b2455f47cfc4ec80bed530491c4e8f071947"], "node": "5d61e6493e694793a70808953cad85a36571f482", "parents": ["1bed5fa63b16e95710f87c21bbf1b79f1d4c243d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089584: Check for overrecursion in OSR r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342408\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/Ion.cpp"], "git_node": "58458b5f56ca0eba683eed4234f8031bdfc18e0a", "git_parents": ["fe51dd174a21d55885da5ce0e413b1b6503cf689"], "node": "c7f78ebd2b9edc66195deb9b0531952c7f695171", "parents": ["5d61e6493e694793a70808953cad85a36571f482"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089584: Add test r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342409\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/ion/bug2089584.js"], "git_node": "4f25b53aaaafa02fce47cf81fd4c8947913b0580", "git_parents": ["58458b5f56ca0eba683eed4234f8031bdfc18e0a"], "node": "317d6d2c72ffad499f39ff1ab995364f5f97545b", "parents": ["c7f78ebd2b9edc66195deb9b0531952c7f695171"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1883561 - Remove pending auth prompts from the bucket they were added to, r=credential-management-reviewers,mtigley.\n\nWhen the prompter's browser changed while a prompt was pending, the prompt was\nnever removed from its original bucket, and every later prompt with the same\nkey got merged into it without ever being shown.\n\nThis also removes the verify-standalone skip-if added in bug 1995208, which\nwas this failure on repeated runs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342586\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/passwordmgr/LoginManagerAuthPrompter.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/passwordmgr/test/browser/browser.toml"], "git_node": "31491360fd6e30103576a2b8f63e4320a7b4f631", "git_parents": ["4f25b53aaaafa02fce47cf81fd4c8947913b0580"], "node": "1ff19ef2abeeb6fc02567dd521511bf34bcfb9c2", "parents": ["317d6d2c72ffad499f39ff1ab995364f5f97545b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092559 - Use emulated fullscreen in test_MozDomFullscreen_event.xhtml, r=dom-core-reviewers,edgar.\n\nThe test closes its window right after MozDOMFullscreen:Exited, which on macOS\nfires at the start of the native fullscreen exit animation. When the test runs\nagain right away, its new window's native fullscreen request fails, the window\nleaves fullscreen 10ms after entering it, and the test times out.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342608\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/fullscreen/test_MozDomFullscreen_event.xhtml"], "git_node": "b457811df98e39b9e775b66c3e71f35e5aff19c0", "git_parents": ["31491360fd6e30103576a2b8f63e4320a7b4f631"], "node": "abdd320ed02391cffa5666530ba6fcfaa8d634c0", "parents": ["1ff19ef2abeeb6fc02567dd521511bf34bcfb9c2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Seva Alipov \u003csalipov@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086787 Part 1: Rename and update comments for flags that determine whether line-clamp should apply. r=layout-reviewers,AlaskanEmily\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342231\n", "files": ["layout/generic/BlockReflowState.h", "layout/generic/ReflowInput.h", "layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "58aa74a97c68e8f46fe639bc2f362a3dc1393c7c", "git_parents": ["b457811df98e39b9e775b66c3e71f35e5aff19c0"], "node": "b55b556b9b7252398e26bafba94aff6278094913", "parents": ["abdd320ed02391cffa5666530ba6fcfaa8d634c0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Seva Alipov \u003csalipov@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086787 Part 2: Move IsBEndMarginRoot() out of LineClampLineIterator, and declare its getters as const. r=layout-reviewers,AlaskanEmily\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342232\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "d3002b8424676c9efee779470e1104c3510f9e3c", "git_parents": ["58aa74a97c68e8f46fe639bc2f362a3dc1393c7c"], "node": "14f02f5a441ec7b9f26d14375c15afe62f302e7d", "parents": ["b55b556b9b7252398e26bafba94aff6278094913"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Seva Alipov \u003csalipov@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086787 Part 3: Separate LineClampLineIterator::mConsumedSize into its block start and block end border and padding components. r=layout-reviewers,AlaskanEmily\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342233\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "9ca3238e6293b1144c649a152c7e53f0eb22ea29", "git_parents": ["d3002b8424676c9efee779470e1104c3510f9e3c"], "node": "5258e0443c87edf7c6517306a423fab62d4235b1", "parents": ["14f02f5a441ec7b9f26d14375c15afe62f302e7d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Seva Alipov \u003csalipov@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086787 Part 4: Refactoring around LineClampLineIterator::Boundary. r=layout-reviewers,AlaskanEmily\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342234\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "0b08b35e602a70d07772accc6be4767a906dc231", "git_parents": ["9ca3238e6293b1144c649a152c7e53f0eb22ea29"], "node": "d53f2bca2964fc91dfbb1cf3d32ba7bf4b3e4032", "parents": ["5258e0443c87edf7c6517306a423fab62d4235b1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Seva Alipov \u003csalipov@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086787 Part 5: Correct handling of collapsing margins in non-auto line-clamp conatainers. r=layout-reviewers,AlaskanEmily\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338441\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-023.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-024.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-025.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-auto-alt-writingmode-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-auto-alt-writingmode-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-auto-alt-writingmode-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-auto-alt-writingmode-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/line-clamp-auto-alt-writingmode-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/line-clamp-auto-alt-writingmode-002-ref.html"], "git_node": "6cc8a8d875166d036ae6dce63e19812e8a697a26", "git_parents": ["0b08b35e602a70d07772accc6be4767a906dc231"], "node": "8d4bb08585a976e113e7c4a969fae90603b9572c", "parents": ["d53f2bca2964fc91dfbb1cf3d32ba7bf4b3e4032"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2091150, Bug 2088236, Bug 2088234 - Refactor handleEvent in IPProtectionPanel to reduce complexity - r=ip-protection-reviewers,mcleinman\" for causing Linting failures.\n\nThis reverts commit e8b02842d1854a9e46a28a9e10e8c9c8ed5c237a.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2088236 - Add Set to Default promo to built-in VPN settings - r=ip-protection-reviewers,settings-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles,mcleinman\"\n\nThis reverts commit 4bc40525afcb499e7494dbda010e217e8d8f66e0.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2088234 - Add Set to Default promo to locations subview - r=ip-protection-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,flod,mcleinman\"\n\nThis reverts commit 726ecb120c25828f199696869f06db6c81ee0232.\n", "files": ["browser/components/ipprotection/IPProtectionPanel.sys.mjs", "browser/components/ipprotection/assets/location-pin.svg", "browser/components/ipprotection/content/ipprotection-constants.mjs", "browser/components/ipprotection/content/ipprotection-locations.mjs", "browser/components/ipprotection/content/locations-subview.css", "browser/components/ipprotection/tests/browser/browser_ipprotection_location_selector_telemetry.js", "browser/components/ipprotection/tests/browser/browser_ipprotection_locations_keyboard_navigation.js", "browser/components/ipprotection/tests/browser/browser_ipprotection_locations_list.js", "browser/components/preferences/DefaultBrowserHelper.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/config/privacy.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/tests/privacy/browser_privacy_ipprotection.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/ipProtection.ftl"], "git_node": "07ca6580cfb8b426cb4ae5a0bd21151a6bba2321", "git_parents": ["6cc8a8d875166d036ae6dce63e19812e8a697a26"], "node": "bc939c3330dadd9a31ede16c99c5206f48e23eb8", "parents": ["8d4bb08585a976e113e7c4a969fae90603b9572c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2089584: Add test r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\" for causing SM bustages at bug2089584.js.\n\nThis reverts commit 4f25b53aaaafa02fce47cf81fd4c8947913b0580.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2089584: Check for overrecursion in OSR r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\"\n\nThis reverts commit 58458b5f56ca0eba683eed4234f8031bdfc18e0a.\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/ion/bug2089584.js", "js/src/jit/Ion.cpp"], "git_node": "6a8b271cc2b6bbfff7d035ca80ec57f14deae75a", "git_parents": ["07ca6580cfb8b426cb4ae5a0bd21151a6bba2321"], "node": "f6ee7616a7b85503deff11021b4b5536a136a12a", "parents": ["bc939c3330dadd9a31ede16c99c5206f48e23eb8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2083894 - Fix origin bounds in PushDB forEachOrigin. r=saschanaz\" for causing failures at test_pushsubscriptionchange_origin_prefix.html.\n\nThis reverts commit a03572be3551eba3e0c271c7ea8f7c22ee19c2e0.\n", "files": ["build/pgo/certs/cert9.db", "build/pgo/certs/key4.db", "build/pgo/certs/mochitest.client", "build/pgo/server-locations.txt", "dom/push/PushDB.sys.mjs", "dom/push/PushServiceWebSocket.sys.mjs", "dom/push/test/file_pushsubscriptionchange_origin_prefix.html", "dom/push/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/push/test/test_pushsubscriptionchange_origin_prefix.html", "dom/push/test/worker.js"], "git_node": "4863c707611cf3961ee9e7e56e72df9aa60137bb", "git_parents": ["6a8b271cc2b6bbfff7d035ca80ec57f14deae75a"], "node": "a01edb88140499540378fb4f0fee85360089bc32", "parents": ["f6ee7616a7b85503deff11021b4b5536a136a12a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "andyh \u003candhuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091058 - Removed privacy notice infobar for TOS. r=omc-reviewers,mimi,sachung.\n\nWe'll be launching a new privacy notice on Dec 15 that should replace this in-tree one.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341686\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/modules/OnboardingMessageProvider.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/browser/browser_asrouter_infobar.js"], "git_node": "9d3889c08681b1ebcc2ec57cc1957614701fd2c5", "git_parents": ["4863c707611cf3961ee9e7e56e72df9aa60137bb"], "node": "b168a92f18e57ff8e614cea6458effed1ce50445", "parents": ["a01edb88140499540378fb4f0fee85360089bc32"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092579 - Stop overriding LD_LIBRARY_PATH in the clang-tidy source-test tasks. r=sergesanspaille\n\nLD_LIBRARY_PATH made clang-tidy load the libclang-cpp and libLLVM of the\nclang toolchain instead of its own, which are a different build with the\nsame soname, making modernize-loop-convert crash. clang does not need it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342620\n", "files": ["taskcluster/scripts/misc/source-test-clang-setup.sh"], "git_node": "a53e48a1e711edcff88763b012c791af3222ab9b", "git_parents": ["9d3889c08681b1ebcc2ec57cc1957614701fd2c5"], "node": "ad90f98a47718df05baa4b86723b022bcc0e51a2", "parents": ["b168a92f18e57ff8e614cea6458effed1ce50445"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Taimur Hasan \u003cthasan@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074080 - Give static embeddings their own engineId r=ai-platform-reviewers,ai-security-reviewers,cdipersio,valentinp\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336313\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/Tools.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/content/nlp/EmbeddingsGenerator.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_static_embeddings.js"], "git_node": "adb85ab1555bb9693a0753353ee6c67c48fa1cd9", "git_parents": ["a53e48a1e711edcff88763b012c791af3222ab9b"], "node": "1f80322070b360cd6887ca5de5bf4c4aaedc9881", "parents": ["ad90f98a47718df05baa4b86723b022bcc0e51a2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Taimur Hasan \u003cthasan@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090291 - Keep ML engines usable after the inference process shuts them down for being idle r=ai-platform-reviewers,valentinp\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340521\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/ml/actors/MLEngineChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/actors/MLEngineParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/componen