-\u003e 220587b09555a88ebe4a44e3364cd65aaba56fa5\nxh -\u003e 220587b09555a88ebe4a44e3364cd65aaba56fa5\nzam -\u003e 220587b09555a88ebe4a44e3364cd65aaba56fa5\nzh-CN -\u003e 220587b09555a88ebe4a44e3364cd65aaba56fa5\nzh-TW -\u003e 220587b09555a88ebe4a44e3364cd65aaba56fa5\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "b5053bad4339a3e911639371392868a31296d4e4", "git_parents": ["99b8f116a696a437226bf2739720d20def934190"], "node": "50b018e7f3213e4e42453b107f6c734a1177c49d", "parents": ["4b245c262e593acfa208c54d0d225c2b510d9bf1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-central repo-update remote-settings tld-suffixes mobile-experiments ct-logs r=release-managers,RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342981\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/raw/initial_experiments.json", "netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/ct/CTKnownLogs.h", "security/manager/tools/log_list.json", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/ai-window-prompts.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": "9bbf3ea8f7b6a50bea8148d20c0b132613f21ff6", "git_parents": ["b5053bad4339a3e911639371392868a31296d4e4"], "node": "95c7eb9a4d9d316d759df73797b257aa01d239e6", "parents": ["50b018e7f3213e4e42453b107f6c734a1177c49d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092576 - Remove Mercurial instructions and hg.mozilla.org links from the build system docs. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden DONTBUILD\n\nThe local Mercurial sparse checkout walkthrough goes; sparse profiles are still used by automation through robustcheckout.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342678\n", "files": ["build/docs/sccache-dist.md", "build/docs/sparse.md", "build/docs/test_manifests.md", "python/mach/docs/windows-usage-outside-mozillabuild.md", "python/mozboot/README.md"], "git_node": "9abb7f9d6bd6eaa86f480f72b499ee56fa8b1f8a", "git_parents": ["9bbf3ea8f7b6a50bea8148d20c0b132613f21ff6"], "node": "9e1be32c9d3f928d24b54f1b0e17891556ca9f40", "parents": ["95c7eb9a4d9d316d759df73797b257aa01d239e6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nina Pypchenko \u003cnpypchenko@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087970 - Refine dragging widgets on New Tab r=fchasen\n\nA widget still starts dragging once the pointer moves from a spot that\nisn't a control. An iframe widget drags by its header and the padding\naround the frame, since the frame keeps its own pointer events.\n\nThe grab cursor shows on the header row and the padding of each card,\nso the rest of the widget keeps the usual cursor. The padding has no\nelement of its own, so the cursor is set on the card element and also\nshows wherever that element is uncovered.\n\nA dragged widget now scales up slightly. The drag offset has moved from\n`transform` to `translate`, which the scale doesn't apply to, so the\nwidget stays under the cursor.\n\nA drag also ends when the button is released outside the window or\nover an iframe, and the click that follows a drop no longer activates\nthe link or button under the cursor.\n\nStopping iframe widgets from reloading after a drop has moved to\nbug 2090258.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338939\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/_Widgets.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/lib/usePointerReorder.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/Widgets.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/useWidgetDnD.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/lib/usePointerReorder.test.jsx"], "git_node": "c75997a72087b7e14c52374ffff181a0ee90af21", "git_parents": ["9abb7f9d6bd6eaa86f480f72b499ee56fa8b1f8a"], "node": "a4d1573e7c0325fd129f12b3697e7df0c6e65f65", "parents": ["9e1be32c9d3f928d24b54f1b0e17891556ca9f40"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085901: Fix the role of rows and cells inside a thead/tbody/tfoot with role=\"rowgroup\". r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,morgan\n\nIf a containing `\u003ctable\u003e` has a non-table role, we expose a generic role on its rows and cells, as rows and cells aren't valid outside of a semantic table.\nPreviously, this code didn't account for the possibility of an intervening role=\"rowgroup\", which broke row and cell roles in this case.\nTo fix this, we now explicitly check for role=\"rowgroup\", using the parent as the containing table in that case.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342455\n", "files": ["accessible/base/nsAccessibilityService.cpp", "accessible/tests/browser/tree/browser.toml", "accessible/tests/browser/tree/browser_table.js"], "git_node": "6a33653ac73fd93bb14e67359c35514735434c3f", "git_parents": ["c75997a72087b7e14c52374ffff181a0ee90af21"], "node": "127fd72dc0da3d996cab0286340fa8d6e2c5d258", "parents": ["a4d1573e7c0325fd129f12b3697e7df0c6e65f65"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Harvey \u003cdale@arandomurl.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092012 - Use moz-src for toolkit/components/content-classifier r=timhuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342069\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/content-classifier/components.conf", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/moz.build", "toolkit/components/content-classifier/test/unit/test_rs_client_shutdown.js", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.modules.d.ts", "tools/@types/generated/tspaths.json", "tools/lint/extra-js-modules/allowlist.txt"], "git_node": "d370ee046fe31c40f262a5a1f9dd41e2b46a0a03", "git_parents": ["6a33653ac73fd93bb14e67359c35514735434c3f"], "node": "bf89a2f80804490e000953430673b02f27c93d5d", "parents": ["127fd72dc0da3d996cab0286340fa8d6e2c5d258"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1732284 part 1: Move valuetext object attribute exposure into ATK code. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\n\nOther platforms have dedicated methods to retrieve a textual value, so this was only ever needed for ATK.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342490\n", "files": ["accessible/atk/AccessibleWrap.cpp", "accessible/generic/LocalAccessible.cpp", "accessible/ipc/RemoteAccessible.cpp", "accessible/tests/browser/atk/browser.toml", "accessible/tests/browser/atk/browser_valuetext.js", "accessible/tests/browser/e10s/browser_caching_attributes.js"], "git_node": "3954aadc4e0a75307e0a9db30547fd68211a43ab", "git_parents": ["d370ee046fe31c40f262a5a1f9dd41e2b46a0a03"], "node": "c9bc4a46f991dc9cec6885c2f21748d2667274fd", "parents": ["bf89a2f80804490e000953430673b02f27c93d5d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1732284 part 2: Expose valuetext object attribute for non-editable comboboxes in ATK. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\n\nATK has no other way to expose the value of a combobox.\nSince bug 2050939, collapsed select elements no longer have children which clients could use instead.\nEditable comboboxes are excluded because their value is already exposed via AtkText.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342491\n", "files": ["accessible/atk/AccessibleWrap.cpp", "accessible/tests/browser/atk/browser_valuetext.js"], "git_node": "e03db2c450113944d3fd16233a11fc1521c1b5dd", "git_parents": ["3954aadc4e0a75307e0a9db30547fd68211a43ab"], "node": "05740656555872a57aad0ce2104e81ffd671680b", "parents": ["c9bc4a46f991dc9cec6885c2f21748d2667274fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093090 - Part 1. Don't wait for remote texture owners that have been unregistered. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nRemoteTextureMap could not tell an owner that had not been registered yet\nfrom one that had already been unregistered, so a texture arriving after\nits owner went away waited for the full timeout on the compositor thread.\nRemember whether each owner named by a live RemoteTextureHostWrapper was\nregistered, which bounds the state by the wrappers, and don't wait for\ntextures that no wrapper can use any more.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342949\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/RemoteTextureMap.cpp", "gfx/layers/RemoteTextureMap.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/ImageBridgeParent.cpp"], "git_node": "f2ba912aa5d715bd4db9a94b2af4f6e82720303a", "git_parents": ["e03db2c450113944d3fd16233a11fc1521c1b5dd"], "node": "d8bf3df5dd6e24c11b873f6e4bb20b67c6cd3a03", "parents": ["05740656555872a57aad0ce2104e81ffd671680b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093090 - Part 2. Wake remote texture ready checks when a texture owner will not push again. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nReady checks waiting for a texture from an owner whose context was lost,\nor whose unregistration was deferred until its last transaction, were\nleft waiting until the owner was unregistered or the check timed out,\neven though no more textures were coming.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342950\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/RemoteTextureMap.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderImageHost.cpp"], "git_node": "cc4febe78ddc082336c823d8299deb13133a6bdd", "git_parents": ["f2ba912aa5d715bd4db9a94b2af4f6e82720303a"], "node": "8de6bbf913a6e20f17ed557b5401ded9b81aa90b", "parents": ["d8bf3df5dd6e24c11b873f6e4bb20b67c6cd3a03"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093090 - Part 3. Add RemoteTextureMap gtests for owners that are gone or will not push again. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342951\n", "files": ["gfx/tests/gtest/TestRemoteTextureMap.cpp", "gfx/tests/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "0fe6b50df37589969e79719db00754b5670be4ad", "git_parents": ["cc4febe78ddc082336c823d8299deb13133a6bdd"], "node": "2a8201a4437d067085e708fca41f9b90c638402e", "parents": ["8de6bbf913a6e20f17ed557b5401ded9b81aa90b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093133 - Flush pending ImageBridge updates in nsDOMWindowUtils::UpdateLayerTree. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nFrames presented through ImageBridge, such as those of an OffscreenCanvas or a\nvideo, are not part of the layer transaction, so a compositor snapshot taken\nafter updateLayerTree could miss them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342986\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsDOMWindowUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "dd6386ed022ef898ee596a14adb1efd953c82f03", "git_parents": ["0fe6b50df37589969e79719db00754b5670be4ad"], "node": "e6d245159cb83945cf5821fe456d99405e1d539a", "parents": ["2a8201a4437d067085e708fca41f9b90c638402e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "pstanciu \u003cpstanciu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2093090 - Part 3. Add RemoteTextureMap gtests for owners that are gone or will not push again. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\" for causing build bustages @ TestRemoteTextureMap.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit 0fe6b50df37589969e79719db00754b5670be4ad.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2093090 - Part 2. Wake remote texture ready checks when a texture owner will not push again. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\"\n\nThis reverts commit cc4febe78ddc082336c823d8299deb13133a6bdd.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2093090 - Part 1. Don't wait for remote texture owners that have been unregistered. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\"\n\nThis reverts commit f2ba912aa5d715bd4db9a94b2af4f6e82720303a.\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/RemoteTextureMap.cpp", "gfx/layers/RemoteTextureMap.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/ImageBridgeParent.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderImageHost.cpp", "gfx/tests/gtest/TestRemoteTextureMap.cpp", "gfx/tests/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "3ed7043dd351521a26be686ba3aa61671afa2904", "git_parents": ["dd6386ed022ef898ee596a14adb1efd953c82f03"], "node": "db64d3cf88f033a2aa07d6ddb77939bb64a0d592", "parents": ["e6d245159cb83945cf5821fe456d99405e1d539a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Import translations from https://github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n CLOSED TREE\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-sl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-oc/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/addons/src/main/res/values-bqi/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/addons/src/main/res/values-fi/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/addons/src/main/res/values-lv/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/addons/src/main/res/values-sl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/autofill/src/main/res/values-lv/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/importer/src/main/res/values-fi/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/importer/src/main/res/values-sl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-oc/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/res/values-lv/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-bqi/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-fi/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-lv/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-nn-rNO/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-oc/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-sl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-tr/strings.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/values-sl/strings.xml"], "git_node": "cf6a69d1fe08766da5bc342d219d180a9e8c3405", "git_parents": ["3ed7043dd351521a26be686ba3aa61671afa2904"], "node": "ae967e3f962f97b34d23cb7bec922e77214fcc72", "parents": ["db64d3cf88f033a2aa07d6ddb77939bb64a0d592"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Botond Ballo \u003cbotond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092397 - Migrate Mac to use DefaultNativePanHandler as well. r=mac-reviewers,mstange\n\nThis involves implementing nsIWidget::SynthesizeNativeTouchpadPan on\nMac. The refactor preserves the existing behaviour (the implementation\nforwards to SynthesizeNativeMouseScrollEvent, which is what the\nMac-specific pan handler ended up calling).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342441\n", "files": ["dom/interfaces/base/nsIDOMWindowUtils.idl", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/apz_test_native_event_utils.js", "widget/cocoa/nsCocoaWindow.h", "widget/cocoa/nsCocoaWindow.mm"], "git_node": "db3b51d4fbe47dc98942ff9ae105793e07b8eb35", "git_parents": ["cf6a69d1fe08766da5bc342d219d180a9e8c3405"], "node": "87505300822924d8a98f0109753285ff3a2471ec", "parents": ["ae967e3f962f97b34d23cb7bec922e77214fcc72"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Logan Rosen \u003cloganrosen@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090438 - Don't replace a DOM translation with one from an older request. r=emilio\n\nEach TranslateElements call formats its elements in a separate async task,\nand those tasks can resolve out of order. ApplyTranslations only checked that\nthe element still had a data-l10n-id, so an older request for the same\nelement could overwrite a newer one. This happens when L10nMutations flushes\nthe same element twice, or when a locale change re-translates the roots\nwhile an earlier request is still pending.\n\nEach TranslateElements call now gets an increasing request id. While any\nrequest for an element is in flight, a static map in DOMLocalization tracks\nthe id of the latest request applied to it, and ApplyTranslations skips\nresults from older requests. Entries are removed once an element has no\nrequests left, so nothing persists on elements.\n\nThis makes the wait added to browser_file_close_tabs.js in bug 2090437\nunnecessary.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340625\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/browser-menubar/browser_file_close_tabs.js", "dom/l10n/DOMLocalization.cpp", "dom/l10n/DOMLocalization.h", "dom/l10n/tests/mochitest/chrome.toml", "dom/l10n/tests/mochitest/dom_localization/file_translateElements_held.sjs", "dom/l10n/tests/mochitest/dom_localization/test_translateElements_superseded.html"], "git_node": "404aeb35caeb9b97506371fae641b59caede7cbf", "git_parents": ["db3b51d4fbe47dc98942ff9ae105793e07b8eb35"], "node": "9744c14ac850aa820aa27f3df501e3c75a45db3a", "parents": ["87505300822924d8a98f0109753285ff3a2471ec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093103 - Preserve CPU access usage flags for WebGL AHardwareBuffers on Android emulators r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nUse AndroidHardwareBuffer::kDefaultUsage for WebGL shared surfaces when the GL renderer is GLRenderer::AndroidEmulator, restoring the CPU read and write usage flags removed in bug 2092364. This is intended to avoid the EGLImage texture binding crash reported on the Android emulator.\n\nKeep GPU-only usage flags for other renderers.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343005\n", "files": ["gfx/gl/SharedSurfaceAndroidHardwareBuffer.cpp"], "git_node": "582ade133ea3cb63038f563d00b9e7697ee04cfc", "git_parents": ["404aeb35caeb9b97506371fae641b59caede7cbf"], "node": "a73953ad298a9604cc86bd5331e311cd58fcabd3", "parents": ["9744c14ac850aa820aa27f3df501e3c75a45db3a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2035780 - Make `IMContextWrapper::ResetIME` stop calling `gtk_im_context_reset` if it's called by `OnSelectionChange` recursively r=m_kato\n\nWhile `gtk_im_context_reset` is calling, anything could happen. In the\nreported case, selection change in the content is caused recursively.\nTherefore, we should stop calling it if we've already called it for\na selection change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341960\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/IMContextWrapper.cpp", "widget/gtk/IMContextWrapper.h"], "git_node": "a1c15750ac931e142d313ba651283178f9fcf0de", "git_parents": ["582ade133ea3cb63038f563d00b9e7697ee04cfc"], "node": "f9ed1d1e4be249f04fafafbc10955a85496b087d", "parents": ["a73953ad298a9604cc86bd5331e311cd58fcabd3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Makoto Kato \u003cm_kato@ga2.so-net.ne.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086001 - Update WPT meta data for GeckoView with isolated process. r=geckoview-reviewers,owlish\n\nIsolated process tests runs after turning on NDK codecs, so we should\nupdate meta data of WPT even if some tests of WebRTC are still failed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336997\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/content-security-policy/media-src/media-src-7_2.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/content-security-policy/media-src/media-src-redir-bug.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-contain/contain-inline-size-replaced.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-contain/contain-size-replaced-003a.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-contain/contain-size-replaced-003b.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-contain/contain-size-replaced-003c.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-scaled-video.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/custom-elements/reactions/customized-builtins/HTMLMediaElement.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/custom-elements/reactions/customized-builtins/HTMLSourceElement.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/element-timing/observe-video-poster.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/metadata/redirect/multiple-redirect-https-downgrade-upgrade.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/metadata/redirect/redirect-http-upgrade.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/metadata/redirect/redirect-https-downgrade.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/metadata/track.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/orb/tentative/hls.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/security/dangling-markup/media.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/cross-origin-opener-policy/resource-popup.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/bfcache/embedded-mp4.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/loading-the-media-resource/autoplay-overrides-preload.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/track/track-element/track-api-texttracks.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/track/track-element/track-cue-inline.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-embed-element/embed-change-src.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element/video_size_preserved_after_ended.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/largest-contentful-paint/video-poster.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/largest-contentful-paint/web-font-styled-text-resize-block.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/largest-contentful-paint/web-font-styled-text-resize-swap-after-interaction.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/SourceBuffer-appendWindowEnd-rounding.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/SourceBuffer-short-frame-endOfStream.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/last-frame-dimensions.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-activesourcebuffers.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-append-buffer.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-appendwindow.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-buffered.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-changetype-play-negative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-changetype-play.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-changetype.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-config-change-mp4-a-bitrate.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-config-change-mp4-av-framesize.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-config-change-mp4-av-video-bitrate.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-config-change-mp4-v-bitrate.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-config-change-mp4-v-framerate.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-config-change-mp4-v-framesize.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-detach.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-h264-play-starved.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-play-then-seek-back.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-play.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-remove.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-seek-beyond-duration.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-seek-during-pending-seek.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-sequencemode-append-buffer.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-timestamp-offset.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/waiting-for-audio.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mediacapture-fromelement/capture-muted.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mediacapture-fromelement/capture.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mediacapture-fromelement/creation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mediacapture-fromelement/ended.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mediacapture-fromelement/restart-after-ended.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mediacapture-fromelement/src-reset.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mixed-content/tentative/autoupgrades/mixed-content-cors.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mixed-content/tentative/autoupgrades/video-upgrade.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/navigation-timing/dom-interactive-media-document.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/preload/link-header-preload-non-html.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/resource-timing/initiator-type/audio.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/resource-timing/initiator-type/video.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/service-workers/cache-storage/cache-add.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCDataChannel-close.html.ini"], "git_node": "60b5578faf368724dc0ff87bdfb778a4d0b1a1f1", "git_parents": ["a1c15750ac931e142d313ba651283178f9fcf0de"], "node": "302511e86060a2fa700a829ec8ecb15127e761d1", "parents": ["f9ed1d1e4be249f04fafafbc10955a85496b087d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093090 - Part 1. Don't wait for remote texture owners that have been unregistered. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nRemoteTextureMap could not tell an owner that had not been registered yet\nfrom one that had already been unregistered, so a texture arriving after\nits owner went away waited for the full timeout on the compositor thread.\nRemember whether each owner named by a live RemoteTextureHostWrapper was\nregistered, which bounds the state by the wrappers, and don't wait for\ntextures that no wrapper can use any more.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342949\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/RemoteTextureMap.cpp", "gfx/layers/RemoteTextureMap.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/ImageBridgeParent.cpp"], "git_node": "340c6c79ba2b0b54d3c255bdf3ef8be6cd2c9b30", "git_parents": ["60b5578faf368724dc0ff87bdfb778a4d0b1a1f1"], "node": "94762f2e800e82815fbca898b843485ed7edeece", "parents": ["302511e86060a2fa700a829ec8ecb15127e761d1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093090 - Part 2. Wake remote texture ready checks when a texture owner will not push again. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nReady checks waiting for a texture from an owner whose context was lost,\nor whose unregistration was deferred until its last transaction, were\nleft waiting until the owner was unregistered or the check timed out,\neven though no more textures were coming.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342950\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/RemoteTextureMap.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderImageHost.cpp"], "git_node": "4d222f0c59ba80f16a1d568ea07b6ba7ea71a8c2", "git_parents": ["340c6c79ba2b0b54d3c255bdf3ef8be6cd2c9b30"], "node": "88f9895fb075a222993b1fc4fa44e47cc891d2d5", "parents": ["94762f2e800e82815fbca898b843485ed7edeece"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093090 - Part 3. Add RemoteTextureMap gtests for owners that are gone or will not push again. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342951\n", "files": ["gfx/tests/gtest/TestRemoteTextureMap.cpp", "gfx/tests/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "d7161e35da7704cff60e48ee86fb7747ffcc93c7", "git_parents": ["4d222f0c59ba80f16a1d568ea07b6ba7ea71a8c2"], "node": "4211a1ce1da294805573e629e591118237a5e55b", "parents": ["88f9895fb075a222993b1fc4fa44e47cc891d2d5"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794822310, "git_changesets": ["f1c5a5211f474e01c9ca65ff32f2e3d7a67a46ad", "3855545701c691ce652ea2b1a5daf4ac046894f6", "ccb0d7ceefadd63886879ffd05c62d7920808afd", "2b0ad18ca032a411ffe9f599d49f47aefa243