: ["27728dd7c25b7cfaa0ec7682af85208d3b762bb4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Corentin Bect \u003ccbect@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092151 - Advance onboarding only when a pairing QR code is scanned r=twhite\n\nSelecting \"Scan pairing code\" on the the onboarding pairing sync card opened `PairFragment` and also called `scrollToNextPageOrDismiss()` immediately. This ran `OnboardingFragment.onFinish` while the scanner was still open and pairing was not complete. Onboarding was marked as complete and telemetry was recorded, but the navigation to home was skipped because `PairFragment` was the current destination. As soon as the account was connected, the sign in `LaunchedEffect` in `OnboardingScreen` called `OnboardingFragment.onFinish` another time, resulting in a duplicate event and a delayed navigation to the home screen.\n\nThis patch adds `OnboardingSyncFlowResult`, an object that lets sync flows started from onboarding report flow completion. The result is stored in the `SavedStateHandle` of the previous back stack entry so that only the destination that started the flow is notified. `PairFragment` reports completion when a QR code is scanned and `SyncFlowCompletedEffect` moves to the next page once and consumes the result.\n\nAlso `OnboardingFragment.onFinish` now returns early if the current destination is not the onboarding. This avoids unexpected side effects when another screen is the current destination.\n\nPull request: https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/pull/447\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/OnboardingFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/OnboardingSyncFlowResult.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/view/OnboardingScreen.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/PairFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/OnboardingSyncFlowResultTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/view/OnboardingScreenTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/view/SyncFlowCompletedEffectTest.kt"], "git_node": "a3b629a58cd01520bb547ecbf4721760b8133bdb", "git_parents": ["7520cc3fc3a1c17c468aa7d5651a5a1334545925"], "node": "4f7b9aeb39f1ea7a01cc3376f170a2b37e990981", "parents": ["3e6a629f99c615fdf3c81ba251c1e8a0edcf029b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093088 - Wait for ImageBridge tasks before handing off the last remote texture transaction of an OffscreenCanvas WebGL context. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nAn OffscreenCanvas's compositable updates are sent from the ImageBridge\nthread, which is also where FwdTransactionTracker is updated. Destroying\nthe context could read the tracker before the last update was sent, so the\nowner was unregistered before the compositor saw its last texture, as was\nfixed for WebGPU in bug 2060449.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342948\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/ClientWebGLContext.cpp"], "git_node": "f8eb10a7536a2b9af124ffdff4f8939955737a97", "git_parents": ["a3b629a58cd01520bb547ecbf4721760b8133bdb"], "node": "ad309f069e3d80208a742dcfdb794cdc85d20b09", "parents": ["4f7b9aeb39f1ea7a01cc3376f170a2b37e990981"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093219 - Don't create a main_raw.log file for local JS test runs. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jonco\n\njit-test and jstests with `--format=automation` wrote a stray `main_raw.log`\nfile into the source tree when `MOZ_UPLOAD_DIR` wasn't set. Automation jobs set\n`MOZ_UPLOAD_DIR`, and the test results are also printed to stdout, so only write\nthe raw JSON log when that environment variable is set.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343029\n", "files": ["js/src/tests/lib/structuredlog.py"], "git_node": "992d7c9ed962cdda228192c40821b2a7d05081d4", "git_parents": ["f8eb10a7536a2b9af124ffdff4f8939955737a97"], "node": "4a768332e3e96c2fd88ed7ac149e90a5034188f5", "parents": ["ad309f069e3d80208a742dcfdb794cdc85d20b09"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093219 - Print test summary for jit-test and jstests when the progress bar is hidden. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jonco\n\nThe test harness only printed PASS (for jstests) or PASSED ALL (for jit-tests) when\nredirecting output to a file, so Claude often ran tests with `--format=automation`\nto get more information.\n\nWith this patch we print a summary at the end when the progress bar is hidden:\n```\nResults: PASS: 3035, FAIL: 0, TIMEOUT: 0, SKIP: 6 | 6.2s\nPASSED ALL\n```\n\njstests with `--format=automation` now also calls the progress bar's `update()`\nfor every test, not just skipped ones.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343039\n", "files": ["js/src/tests/lib/progressbar.py", "js/src/tests/lib/results.py"], "git_node": "4dff698ff78a57268308e8f06992cb1dd402872f", "git_parents": ["992d7c9ed962cdda228192c40821b2a7d05081d4"], "node": "8ce4a400da3095307d09d68794e36b841f8044ef", "parents": ["4a768332e3e96c2fd88ed7ac149e90a5034188f5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nhadji \u003cnhadji@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083656 - Run the fuzzing build kind on git-backed pushes and clone it with Git, r=taskgraph-reviewers,ahal\n\nDrop `run-on-repo-type: [hg]` and the per-task `clone-with: hg` lines from\nthe fuzzing kind, so its tasks schedule on git-backed pushes and check out\nthe GitHub mirror (run-task-git, shallow clone).\n\nVerified on try cloning from Git:\nhttps://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&revision=2d5c01eb8bed4a22cb8f80aa35e1134450c62a1d\nThe fuzzing builds and fuzzing-simple are green. The three grizzly tasks\nfail at start with \"No module named 'pkg_resources'\" inside the grizzly\nvirtualenv; the same three tasks fail identically on an unmodified main\nwith the Mercurial checkout\n(https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&revision=87425d1206fac3304a2e73388653bfccf42ff962),\nso that breakage predates this change and is unrelated to the clone\n(bug 2084054).\n\nWith the guard gone, the simple task and the three Linux grizzly tasks,\nwhich have no `run-on-projects`, are offered to every project through the\nimplicit default, enterprise-firefox included. Which of them run there is\nfor the enterprise target task method to decide, not for this kind.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335510\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/fuzzing/kind.yml"], "git_node": "035b2c356c1c9ee92db2ffb89295619b1efdc671", "git_parents": ["4dff698ff78a57268308e8f06992cb1dd402872f"], "node": "3ce72c368d0cf8928fdd85997b3e9b4a56bf643d", "parents": ["8ce4a400da3095307d09d68794e36b841f8044ef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092700 - Update Robolectric to 4.18. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\n4.18 reports the runtime permission state of the test package on SDK 37 (robolectric#11518), so the denial\ntest in `LensCameraActivityTest` no longer needs to run on SDK 36. It also no longer reaches into JDK\n`FileDescriptor` internals, so the test JVMs no longer need\n`--add-exports=java.base/jdk.internal.access=ALL-UNNAMED`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342918\n", "files": ["gradle/libs.versions.toml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/lens/LensCameraActivityTest.kt", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/conventions/src/main/java/org/mozilla/conventions/ProjectPlugin.kt"], "git_node": "1f30a6f7304a1dd1d11d9d117caa1b30f64264b7", "git_parents": ["035b2c356c1c9ee92db2ffb89295619b1efdc671"], "node": "03da608cf5d4420a834ed66ef86e96fcf2962e2e", "parents": ["3ce72c368d0cf8928fdd85997b3e9b4a56bf643d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090260 - Have desktop-theme-colors check that a changed background keeps its text counterpart. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341174\n", "files": [".agents/skills/desktop-theme-colors/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/desktop-theme-colors/SKILL.md"], "git_node": "a7672a7ae52f8c177b78b073eedbb125034cb7c6", "git_parents": ["1f30a6f7304a1dd1d11d9d117caa1b30f64264b7"], "node": "9c4ca4e203157f8fce1b135cadee57242c8ba784", "parents": ["03da608cf5d4420a834ed66ef86e96fcf2962e2e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Younes SERRAJ \u003cyounes.serraj@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062777 - Return the available locales of L10nRegistry in a stable order. r=eemeli,extension-reviewers,mconley,robwu\n\nL10nRegistry::get_available_locales collected the locales into a HashSet,\nwhose iteration order is randomized per instance. LocaleService::\nSetAvailableLocales compares the list as an ordered array, so most source\nmutations looked like a change of the available locales, and the\nnegotiation then reordered the region-range matches of the requested\nlocale (en-CA, en-GB, ... for en-US) and fired intl:app-locales-changed\nalthough nothing had changed.\n\nEach langpack update removes and re-registers its sources. Updating the 98\nlangpacks that the Snap package installs fired the topic about 100 times,\neach one retranslating every open document and running the observers of\nthe topic, and made the parent process run out of memory.\n\nCollecting into a BTreeSet returns the same list for the same set of\nlocales. Source mutations are still not batched: updating the langpack of\na negotiated app locale still changes the app locales twice.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339501\n", "files": ["browser/components/newtab/AboutNewTabResourceMapping.sys.mjs", "intl/l10n/rust/l10nregistry-rs/src/registry/mod.rs", "intl/l10n/test/test_l10nregistry_observer.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_webextension_langpack_update_locales.js", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "8cd8db20376b90d2e4c9b385064ee3283bc35f61", "git_parents": ["a7672a7ae52f8c177b78b073eedbb125034cb7c6"], "node": "e4052f89ce7e9e28bb64b5fa13a9da45b8cb051c", "parents": ["9c4ca4e203157f8fce1b135cadee57242c8ba784"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nhadji \u003cnhadji@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081108 - Clone the partials, partner repack, eme-free repack, attribution and update test kinds with Git, r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nDeletes the `clone-with: hg` lines of partials-zucchini, partials-zucchini-l10n,\nrelease-partner-repack, release-eme-free-repack, release-partner-attribution,\nupdate-test and test-update-integrity, so their tasks clone the Git\nrepository on pushes that carry one, like the rest of the tree. The\nscheduling guard of these kinds went away in bug 2081108 already.\n\nVerified with a staging release on try (Ship-it staging, Firefox 160.0b8\nbuild 1, revision 6aaf02b85428): in its promotion graph every checkout of\nthese kinds is a Git clone of the git-backing mirror. release-partner-repack\n37/37, release-eme-free-repack 28/28, release-partner-attribution 4/4 and\npartials-zucchini 36/36 tasks passed. update-test passed 35/42; the 7\nfailures are one background-update variant per platform that needs\ncandidate builds of the staged version and a linux XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\nenvironment issue, both independent of the checkout, which completed in\nevery task. test-update-integrity ran its checkout and setup in all 36 tasks\nand then failed on staging data: the staging archive lacks the previous\nreleases it downloads and the MAR applications it did attempt failed, the\nsame way with or without a Git checkout, which no earlier try staging\nrelease exercised. One macOS 10.15 worker refused the Git checkout because\nits command line tools ship a git too old for that macOS; the other five\n10.15 update tests cloned fine, so that is a single worker image to refresh.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336497\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/partials-zucchini-l10n/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/partials-zucchini/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-eme-free-repack/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-partner-attribution/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/release-partner-repack/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/test-update-integrity/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/update-test/kind.yml"], "git_node": "a93b444a89e56e5cc94d88e9089cd95bf8d5aeb5", "git_parents": ["8cd8db20376b90d2e4c9b385064ee3283bc35f61"], "node": "fe629a40fc05fb2e779fd2933e5b262287535308", "parents": ["e4052f89ce7e9e28bb64b5fa13a9da45b8cb051c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093110 - Binary search for the OSI index of a return address. r=iain\n\nIonScript::getOsiIndex scanned the OSI indices linearly, calling the\nout-of-line OsiIndex::returnPointDisplacement for each one, and a stack walk\nlooks up the OSI index of every Ion frame it visits. CodeGeneratorShared's\nmarkOsiPoint records the indices in code order, and ensureOsiSpace keeps each\nOSI point at least a near call past the previous one, so they are sorted by\ndisplacement and can be binary searched. A debug check in copyOsiIndices\nasserts the order.\n\nThe JS shell captures async stacks for all code, and on an Apple M4 Max the\nscan took 11.0% of JetStream 3's doxbee-async, 1.8% with this change. Over ten\nrounds of the three async tests, each running this change and its parent in\ntwo code layouts, doxbee-async's score improves 6.1% (95% confidence interval\n4.8% to 7.4%), async-fs 3.4% (2.5% to 4.3%) and doxbee-promise 1.2% (0.4% to\n1.9%).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342964\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/Ion.cpp"], "git_node": "d3024c5f931ad5f93c4c139a7f5f4434df820807", "git_parents": ["a93b444a89e56e5cc94d88e9089cd95bf8d5aeb5"], "node": "a8da4c0ac7b2b18d3991611a86051fe6254c0ec0", "parents": ["fe629a40fc05fb2e779fd2933e5b262287535308"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091345 - Don't cache initial shapes that can be replaced by SharedShape::insertInitialShape. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,iain\n\nFor some classes we replace the initial empty-shape entry in the table with the\nshape that has builtin properties added to it. Future lookups then get the final\nshape instead of the empty shape.\n\nThis complicates the `ShapeCachePtr` `ShapeWithProto` optimization because it's\nbased on matching the shape in the table. The easiest fix is to not use that\noptimization for those replaceable empty shapes. This patch adds a shape flag\nto make that cheap.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342641\n", "files": ["js/src/vm/Shape.cpp", "js/src/vm/Shape.h"], "git_node": "d131d8bca66626b76adde000ec9d4abe78b5af45", "git_parents": ["d3024c5f931ad5f93c4c139a7f5f4434df820807"], "node": "b8f18c4e6513f06890516af38fda879025ec15eb", "parents": ["a8da4c0ac7b2b18d3991611a86051fe6254c0ec0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexander Schmitz \u003carschmitz@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090781 - Skip off-thread compilation for text modules. r=eemeli\n\nExclude text modules from off-thread JavaScript compilation, matching JSON\nand CSS modules. This preserves the source for CreateTextModule.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340750\n", "files": ["dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/text-module/large-import.window.js"], "git_node": "ed7f0a9ad4f0741870b20856153fdb85970bb497", "git_parents": ["d131d8bca66626b76adde000ec9d4abe78b5af45"], "node": "ec48970dca2070987d9a3124e21a2d3e35d385cb", "parents": ["b8f18c4e6513f06890516af38fda879025ec15eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082867 - Preserve SPS and PPS NAL units in AVC encoder configuration records. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nThe serializer originated in 2018 in bug 1409664 to build synthetic\nSPS/PPS for decoder capability probing, so adding NAL headers was\nintentional and fine.\n\nBug 1570337 extracted it as `WriteExtraData` in 2019, but its\nAndroid caller passed complete NAL units, Windows and FFmpeg later\nadopted the same code and that's how we're here.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334650\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestMediaDataEncoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/agnostic/bytestreams/H264.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/agnostic/bytestreams/H264.h", "dom/media/platforms/agnostic/bytestreams/gtest/TestByteStreams.cpp"], "git_node": "99b4e60e120244064d99195571c6dee38d201936", "git_parents": ["ed7f0a9ad4f0741870b20856153fdb85970bb497"], "node": "b915807399a82aaba2bade799c280895925d2e5d", "parents": ["ec48970dca2070987d9a3124e21a2d3e35d385cb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 873618 - Add a --start-maximized command line option. r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,mossop\n\nMatches Chrome's switch of the same name. Persisting the sizemode before the\nfirst window opens lets the platform's restore path apply it during initial\nlayout, so the window is never shown unmaximized; popups are unaffected\nbecause they are created with CHROME_NO_PERSISTENCE.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340458\n", "files": ["browser/components/BrowserContentHandler.sys.mjs", "browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs", "browser/docs/CommandLineParameters.md", "toolkit/xre/test/marionette/test_cli_window_size.py"], "git_node": "2fd8b88bdcaf60f6ca62957de5f60dc529a87487", "git_parents": ["99b4e60e120244064d99195571c6dee38d201936"], "node": "f20d41df353633fc1c6e659ccbc342c278895f18", "parents": ["b915807399a82aaba2bade799c280895925d2e5d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089358 - Update the audio configuration check in decoder creation. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339792\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/PDMFactory.cpp"], "git_node": "6223b7e1e3deb2cdced6b75d6f4996acc0871cee", "git_parents": ["2fd8b88bdcaf60f6ca62957de5f60dc529a87487"], "node": "f13c98b664d756abb1104b3e900db2cd39e6a35c", "parents": ["f20d41df353633fc1c6e659ccbc342c278895f18"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089358 - Add a gtest for decoder creation with audio configurations. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339793\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestMediaDataDecoder.cpp"], "git_node": "ee0e38f501ed6f1ca6f1e8039f72121c5542d117", "git_parents": ["6223b7e1e3deb2cdced6b75d6f4996acc0871cee"], "node": "50ac4ced913cf1e726f541cfa4ba40110bf9b3d1", "parents": ["f13c98b664d756abb1104b3e900db2cd39e6a35c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Gaul \u003candrew@gaul.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092456 - Raise the arm64 constant pool range from 1 KiB to 16 KiB. r=jandem\n\nBufferMaxPoolOffset has been 1024 since VIXL was imported, the limit that\nbug 1026919 gave ARM32 for VLDR, although LDR (literal) reaches 1 MiB on arm64.\nMost pools therefore go in the middle of the code behind a guard branch, and\nloads of the same value share a pool entry only within 1 KiB.\n\n16 KiB keeps the pool data within half the reach of TBZ, so that a TBZ just\nbefore a pool still reaches a veneer after the data. In a JetStream 3 run this\nmakes Baseline and Ion code 1.7% smaller, mostly because more loads share an\nentry, and takes most pools out of straight-line code.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342473\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/arm64/vixl/MozBaseAssembler-vixl.h"], "git_node": "8f0e841b4d82b10a27bf41fddbb927a3035f15ae", "git_parents": ["ee0e38f501ed6f1ca6f1e8039f72121c5542d117"], "node": "859868810c37860be56d1c7bec2c058417701c65", "parents": ["50ac4ced913cf1e726f541cfa4ba40110bf9b3d1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092626 - Apply uniform rounded rect clips directly in the quad shaders. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nRounded rect clips always went through an intermediate render task where the\npattern is drawn and then masked. When the only clip that needs a mask is a\nrounded rect with the same circular radius in all corners, and both the\nprimitive and the clip map to device space with a scale and offset, the\ntextured, gradient and repeat quad shaders now apply the clip directly.\nLarge primitives keep the nine-patch split and draw their corners directly.\n\nWith this patch, solid rounded rects are no longer rendered using border\nprimitives. The justification for that was to avoid an extra render task,\nbut that hack came with other issues.\n\nMost but not all quad shaders now can apply a uniform rounded rect clip.\nThis is controlled by the presence of a WR_QUAD_ROUNDED_CLIP define in the\nshader. SWGL span shaders don't support this so for now this fast path is\ndisabled with SWGL (otherwise it would prevent the span shaders which would\ndo more harm than the good we get from the fast path).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342693\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/WebRenderAPI.cpp", "gfx/wr/webrender/res/ps_quad.glsl", "gfx/wr/webrender/res/ps_quad_gradient.glsl", "gfx/wr/webrender/res/ps_quad_repeat.glsl", "gfx/wr/webrender/res/ps_quad_textured.glsl", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/command_buffer.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/gpu_types.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_item.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/rounded-clip-direct-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/rounded-clip-direct.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/compositor-surface/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/compositor/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/compositor/rounded-corners-1.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/image/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/mask/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/parse_function.rs", "layout/reftests/bugs/reftest.list", "layout/svg/SVGGeometryFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-masking/clip-path/animations/clip-path-animation-inherit.html.ini"], "git_node": "b380b98063126ed114a0cdf531af89314a87f30c", "git_parents": ["8f0e841b4d82b10a27bf41fddbb927a3035f15ae"], "node": "09d0e7ae6d31dd8e6318f7228379978b5863e73f", "parents": ["859868810c37860be56d1c7bec2c058417701c65"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Goutam Tamvada \u003cgtamvada@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091038 - Remove the oidName field from the EVInfo struct. r=keeler\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342320\n", "files": ["security/certverifier/ExtendedValidation.cpp", "security/manager/tools/ev_cert_info.py"], "git_node": "16866d5f85718bc814d59782145ed5c28c38cd50", "git_parents": ["b380b98063126ed114a0cdf531af89314a87f30c"], "node": "f6cfefa71325b3081c23fa38620a5f09c4f2675e", "parents": ["09d0e7ae6d31dd8e6318f7228379978b5863e73f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092091 - Skip the What's New page startup tests in repeat mode, like in verify mode, r=application-update-reviewers,yjuglaret,omc-reviewers,hanna_a.\n\nThese tests check the pages and update state left by startup, which only exist the first time they run in a browser session.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342127\n", "files": ["browser/components/tests/browser/whats_new_page/browser.toml", "browser/components/tests/browser/whats_new_page/browser_whats_new_page_nimbus.toml", "browser/components/tests/browser/whats_new_page/browser_whats_new_page_nimbus_disable.toml"], "git_node": "a0002459c3ac6058cbc496d126957dc749ff4c82", "git_parents": ["16866d5f85718bc814d59782145ed5c28c38cd50"], "node": "a6affcfc4e69ae8a29e30c2fbbe346ecb9444177", "parents": ["f6cfefa71325b3081c23fa38620a5f09c4f2675e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092091 - Skip browser_suppressTips.js in repeat mode, like in verify mode, r=urlbar-reviewers,Standard8.\n\nThe test checks the pages and update state left by startup, which only exist the first time it runs in a browser session.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342128\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-tips/suppress-tips/browser.toml"], "git_node": "c2089dee2145489c9797035a4569162d0b208ddf", "git_parents": ["a0002459c3ac6058cbc496d126957dc749ff4c82"], "node": "2e41838fea621f6e8e96fcba07114b13f03aa8e9", "parents": ["a6affcfc4e69ae8a29e30c2fbbe346ecb9444177"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jari Jalkanen \u003cjjalkanen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082691 - Improve robustness of error handling in test_sandbox.html. r=dom-storage-reviewers,ArnaudBienner,asuth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342215\n", "files": ["dom/indexedDB/test/mochitest-common.toml", "dom/indexedDB/test/test_sandbox.html"], "git_node": "4d458ef2d78dc7b25504ec77e8d6653049023f02", "git_parents": ["c2089dee2145489c9797035a4569162d0b208ddf"], "node": "c44fda9df246cddd76a126f3cf806f0c2f15af88", "parents": ["2e41838fea621f6e8e96fcba07114b13f03aa8e9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Sudiaman \u003cjsudiaman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091187 - Wait for animations to complete before opening tab context menus. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,kcochrane\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343124\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/head.js"], "git_node": "bb4dc8036386666a258420a29e8926f56238ba62", "git_parents": ["4d458ef2d78dc7b25504ec77e8d6653049023f02"], "node": "da21ac4a364da3a4323ad8b3ef31a46b1b8280e6", "parents": ["c44fda9df246cddd76a126f3cf806f0c2f15af88"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Franchuk \u003cafranchuk@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088350 - Initialize IPC memory reporters reliably r=ipc-reviewers,nika\n\nThis fixes behavior on ccov builds. `CodeCoverageHandler::Init` is\ncalled very early in `XRE_main`, before the memory reporter manager is\ninitialized. It uses a `CrossProcessMutex` (which uses shared memory)\nand this eventually calls `RegisterAllocationMemoryReporter`, which\nfails with no manager.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339298\n", "files": ["ipc/glue/IPCModule.cpp", "ipc/glue/IPCModule.h", "ipc/glue/SharedMemoryHandle.cpp", "ipc/glue/SharedMemoryMapping.cpp", "ipc/glue/moz.build", "ipc/gtest/TestSharedMemory.cpp", "xpcom/components/nsComponentManager.cpp"], "git_node": "df58a313081b624ef81f72de91b3390c000cbb56", "git_parents": ["bb4dc8036386666a258420a29e8926f56238ba62"], "node": "21ed2be56f5ea028a48e3bd0f51eae2e1c5c16ef", "parents": ["da21ac4a364da3a4323ad8b3ef31a46b1b8280e6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Franchuk \u003cafranchuk@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088350 - Remove unused member from nsMemoryReporterManager r=nika\n\n`mThreadPool` is unused; the comment references a method that does not\nexist.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341679\n", "files": ["xpcom/base/nsMemoryReporterManager.cpp", "xpcom/base/nsMemoryReporterManager.h"], "git_node": "f8a1e79c7777c92cc11012e01faf9f1a03a6a8b3", "git_parents": ["df58a313081b624ef81f72de91b3390c000cbb56"], "node": "72dedcf9983a610b4a57bb73e7a47c73546d8342", "parents": ["21ed2be56f5ea028a48e3bd0f51eae2e1c5c16ef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Taimur Hasan \u003cthasan@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074063 - Keep ML engines usable after the inference process crashes r=ai-platform-reviewers,valentinp\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340557\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/ml/actors/MLEngineParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_engine_lifetime.js"], "git_node": "b779e69f014e608e788b0fcf23d597a71482a033", "git_parents": ["f8a1e79c7777c92cc11012e01faf9f1a03a6a8b3"], "node": "119f34727d1a060d2429e978823692bbe5c7b566", "parents": ["72dedcf9983a610b4a57bb73e7a47c73546d8342"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Danielle Graham \u003cdgraham@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1968832 - Use moz-visual-picker for the tab group color swatches. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,reusable-components-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,nsharpley,tgiles\n\nWith VoiceOver you couldn't tell which color was selected when accessing each input directly. The actual radio inputs were hidden off-screen and the labels were the visible swatches, so VO read each label as a \"group\" with no checked state.\n\nRather than adding hidden \"(selected)\" text like the bug suggested, I switched to moz-visual-picker, which the container editor already uses for its color picker. It gives us real radios with a checked state, plus keyboard nav and hover/focus styles, so we don't have to maintain any of that ourselves. Arrow keys still move and select like before.\n\nNo string changes. The existing Fluent messages go on a span inside each picker item, which also gives the item its name.\n\nOne behavior change worth a flag as a result: Enter on a swatch now just selects the color instead of selecting and closing the panel. Enter-to-close came from bug 1926248 as a catch-all, and bug 1953179 later said Enter should activate the focused control here, with only Escape closing the panel. This feels more consistent to me, but happy to change it if needed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339713\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabgroup-menu.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tab_group_menu.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tab_groups_telemetry.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/types/elements.ts", "browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/tabs.css"], "git_node": "e38b62f9042e2209e99b5c06324aefa28796834f", "git_parents": ["b779e69f014e608e788b0fcf23d597a71482a033"], "node": "3d39722f77ffec1398d74d327b5472554918ba1e", "parents": ["119f34727d1a060d2429e978823692bbe5c7b566"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2092617: apply code formatting via Lando\" for causing mda failures @ test_peerConnection_vp9SpatialLayers.html\n\nThis reverts commit 24091d3b38fb6a2a7d6b4ee56f129a0ac8c177f3.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2092617 - Part 4. Add a mochitest for receiving VP9 with spatial layers. r=webrtc-reviewers,pehrsons\"\n\nThis reverts commit 5e9cd4194e59abd743ad8373253fe24ac87408f7.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2092617 - Part 3. Size Java MediaCodec video frames from the codec's output format. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\"\n\nThis reverts commit 4e84d46e08bf8c3fbd98426be800ad568328e599.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2092617 - Part 2. Allow MediaCodec through FFmpeg to decode VP9 in WebRTC on Android. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\"\n\nThis reverts commit 3faf8ae1759e2321881126318ec1b4199a126e77.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2092617 - Part 1. Disable VP9 quality scaling when sending several spatial layers. r=webrtc-reviewers,pehrsons\"\n\nThis reverts commit 930cb2f5737a17ca97966b2c3bbea84399a1d681.\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/android/RemoteDataDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegDecoderModule.h", "dom/media/webrtc/libwebrtcglue/VideoConduit.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/mochitest_peerconnection.toml", "dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/test_peerConnection_vp9SpatialLayers.html", "dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/test_peerConnection_vp9SpatialLayersKeyFrame.html", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/gecko/media/FormatParam.java"], "git_node": "a88f25fc1e468d733e5016e35988448382e179f4", "git_parents": ["e38b62f9042e2209e99b5c06324aefa28796834f"], "node": "245f02506c5f426c498b7d13f6bf5fe92da55488", "parents": ["3d39722f77ffec1398d74d327b5472554918ba1e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nhadji \u003cnhadji@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080077 - Run the python-firefox-ci source-test task from a git checkout on a 64 GB worker, r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDeletes the `clone-with: hg` line of the firefox-ci task, the last\nsource-test python task on a Mercurial clone, and moves it to the\nb-linux-docker-amd pool. The ci subsuite already peaks between 27 and\n30 GB on the 32 GB test workers from a Mercurial checkout; from a Git\ncheckout it reaches the limit and the worker kills it with the tests\npassing. The build docker workers have 64 GB.\n\nTested on try (push 065d0efb58f2): the task ran on b-linux-docker-amd\nfrom a Git clone, all three test files passed (45 tests) in 10 minutes\nwith a peak of 45.07 GiB of the worker's 62.79 (task W5k1f8VLTvSaAZB8vlaBgQ).\nThe other source-test python tasks selected by the same push stayed green.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343135\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/source-test/python.yml"], "git_node": "bcc0f6746924cb213ab9195163f853eb220f0343", "git_parents": ["a88f25fc1e468d733e5016e35988448382e179f4"], "node": "1e9617c9bab5a87c230d03b04539218fd59f5ea5", "parents": ["245f02506c5f426c498b7d13f6bf5fe92da55488"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Zoya \u003czfatima@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087153 - Added new intent to open tts settings r=android-reviewers,android-l10n-reviewers,moyin,flod\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342264\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ui/VoiceSelection.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values/strings.xml"], "git_node": "7547f56a338078b8b1ece2c9f07ac56bf2db30cb", "git_parents": ["bcc0f6746924cb213ab9195163f853eb220f0343"], "node": "1b5d437de1d97d89a0e52f0e1818ec3c6336a1d1", "parents": ["1e9617c9bab5a87c230d03b04539218fd59f5ea5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1935325 - Enable Declarative Web Push on all channels. r=saschanaz\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341034\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "21e472d24ca71dad6e36692a5ea10430f022ac00", "git_parents": ["7547f56a338078b8b1ece2c9f07ac56bf2db30cb"], "node": "f2f4d175b7ad7bc92e412530f26c7a6af6f4d120", "parents": ["1b5d437de1d97d89a0e52f0e1818ec3c6336a1d1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2089358 - Add a gtest for decoder creation with audio configurations. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\" for causing assertion failures @ MFTDecoder.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit ee0e38f501ed6f1ca6f1e8039f72121c5542d117.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2089358 - Update the audio configuration check in decoder creation. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\"\n\nThis reverts commit 6223b7e1e3deb2cdced6b75d6f4996acc0871cee.\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestMediaDataDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/PDMFactory.cpp"], "git_node": "23a3e86354482980f506c445a7b8218fec9813b6", "git_parents": ["21e472d24ca71dad6e36692a5ea10430f022ac00"], "node": "665e5b63c24b68aec672a03ba9ba79b376f2ec4e", "parents": ["f2f4d175b7ad7bc92e412530f26c7a6af6f4d120"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Greg Stoll \u003cgreg@gregstoll.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076769 part 1 - Route copies from alert()/prompt() dialogs through nsBaseClipboard r=dlp-reviewers,handyman\n\nMake these go through nsIClipboard.asyncSetData instead of calling\nContent Analysis directly. This is in preparation for local clipboard\nsupport.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329943\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/contentanalysis/ContentAnalysisUtils.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "66220d4b7a5197bfd7d955eb2a2e1ae0083da85d", "git_parents": ["23a3e86354482980f506c445a7b8218fec9813b6"], "node": "242e6b2ef49446812a05d5087bb1896d8d1677e7", "parents": ["665e5b63c24b68aec672a03ba9ba79b376f2ec4e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Greg Stoll \u003cgreg@gregstoll.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076769 part 2 - Make bypass_for_same_tab_operations require the same page r=dlp-reviewers,handyman\n\nWe will use this new method for local clipboard checks in later changes.\n\nThis actually fixes a bug for paste - previously if\nbypass_For_same_tab_operations was set, you could copy from a page,\nnavigate away in that tab, and paste into that tab as long as the principal\n(i.e. origin) matched. This adds a test for that case.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329944\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/contentanalysis/ContentAnalysis.cpp", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/ContentAnalysis.h", "toolkit/components/contentanalysis/tests/browser/browser_clipboard_copy_content_analysis.js"], "git_node": "1f33f3939557874e45b4b9f5e26b6bda712fc3a2", "git_parents": ["66220d4b7a5197bfd7d955eb2a2e1ae0083da85d"], "node": "fadd3f1a10907fdaeafee1ca9dd41a602c28130e", "parents": ["242e6b2ef49446812a05d5087bb1896d8d1677e7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Greg Stoll \u003cgreg@gregstoll.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076769 part 3 - Let nsBaseClipboard serve reads from a copy kept instead of the native clipboard r=edgar,dlp-reviewers,handyman\n\nThis adds the hooks for Firefox-local clipboard support into nsBaseClipboard.\nFuture work will be done in bug 2074118 for Enterprise-only.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329945\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/contentanalysis/ContentAnalysis.cpp", "widget/ClipboardContentAnalysisParent.cpp", "widget/nsBaseClipboard.cpp", "widget/nsBaseClipboard.h"], "git_node": "9f51ba5ea3f4f5c4e07bf7763b1f40c0c16d0851", "git_parents": ["1f33f3939557874e45b4b9f5e26b6bda712fc3a2"], "node": "cc32d54804b35fa97e2a33c2c20e151f5c6ae977", "parents": ["fadd3f1a10907fdaeafee1ca9dd41a602c28130e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092994 - Update libffi to version 3.8.1. r=sfink\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342929\n", "files": ["js/src/ctypes/libffi/LICENSE", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/moz.yaml", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/aarch64/ffi.c", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/aarch64/internal.h", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/aarch64/sysv.S", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/arm/ffi.c", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/closures.c", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/java_raw_api.c", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/loongarch/ffi.c", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/loongarch/ffitarget.h", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/metag/sysv.S", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/mips/ffi.c", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/mips/n32.S", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/mips/o32.S", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/powerpc/ffi.c", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/powerpc/ffi_linux64.c", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/powerpc/ffi_powerpc.h", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/powerpc/ffi_sysv.c", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/powerpc/ffitarget.h", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/powerpc/linux64_closure.S", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/powerpc/ppc_closure.S", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/powerpc/sysv.S", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/raw_api.c", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/riscv/ffi.c", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/riscv/ffitarget.h", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/s390/ffi.c", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/sparc/ffi64.c", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/sparc/internal.h", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/sparc/v9.S", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/tramp.c", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/wasm/ffi.c", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/x86/ffi.c", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/x86/ffi64.c", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/x86/sysv.S", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/x86/sysv_intel.S", "js/src/ctypes/libffi/src/x86/unix64.S"], "git_node": "a063ab27f3ba572aa0ce6ee3a555f012b494e1f9", "git_parents": ["9f51ba5ea3f4f5c4e07bf7763b1f40c0c16d0851"], "node": "6477e78aa50cfe708527281bb99f94296b7ca284", "parents": ["cc32d54804b35fa97e2a33c2c20e151f5c6ae977"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093148 - Avoid rebuilding the containers menu one item at a time. r=baku\n\nI noticed this in bug 2013119. It's trivial to do something more efficient.\n\nIn the end I fixed the GTK code to cope, but this change seems still worth it.\n\nIdeally it'd be nice to reuse menuitems when possible even?\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342994\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/utilityOverlay.js"], "git_node": "370df731e9ecf0d9caa572b63fda1ae609a61ca0", "git_parents": ["a063ab27f3ba572aa0ce6ee3a555f012b494e1f9"], "node": "953548d3b3fe0dfce42d6b7c4ebc467f6d5856dc", "parents": ["6477e78aa50cfe708527281bb99f94296b7ca284"], "tags": []}, {"author": "hanna.alemu \u003chalemu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081494 - Add a Nimbus switch to turn off the set-to-default startup prompt (legacy or Messaging System version) off-train. r=omc-reviewers,firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,aminomancer,mossop\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342244\n", "files": ["browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tests/browser/browser_default_browser_prompt.js", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/TriggerActionSchemas/TriggerActionSchemas.json", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/TriggerActionSchemas/index.md", "toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml"], "git_node": "ef27a93d61e95041438a9cc955be2a69a7def3df", "git_parents": ["370df731e9ecf0d9caa572b63fda1ae609a61ca0"], "node": "67be15baf836b83be1835b33ea3da6638f4c3cc0", "parents": ["953548d3b3fe0dfce42d6b7c4ebc467f6d5856dc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Zoya \u003czfatima@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060365 - Part 3: Add Context Menu Candidate, order with other tab menu items r=android-reviewers,android-l10n-reviewers,parker,007\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322425\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/contextmenu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/contextmenu/ContextMenuCandidate.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BrowserFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/NativeShareSheetContextMenuCandidate.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/TabGroupContextMenuCandidate.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml"], "git_node": "1cb4816d9b38d37257412609fdd12326ffcc245a", "git_parents": ["ef27a93d61e95041438a9cc955be2a69a7def3df"], "node": "325463534ee8d03f2aec9bd3f14e5c6028ec3cee", "parents": ["67be15baf836b83be1835b33ea3da6638f4c3cc0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Zoya \u003czfatima@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060365 - Part 4: Added Snackbar and telemetry r=android-reviewers,android-l10n-reviewers,parker,007\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323394\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/contextmenu/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/contextmenu/ContextMenuCandidateTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/metrics.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BrowserFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/TabGroupContextMenuCandidate.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/MetricController.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/NativeShareSheetContextMenuCandidateTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/TabGroupContextMenuCandidateTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/MetricControllerTest.kt"], "git_node": "b988c8c4225b8017fe2938c604de7292ea5f11c0", "git_parents": ["1cb4816d9b38d37257412609fdd12326ffcc245a"], "node": "2e731c58b2995cb35c82a02fef05fd5dd6784a7e", "parents": ["325463534ee8d03f2aec9bd3f14e5c6028ec3cee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matheus Guedes \u003c92537312+MatheusGattiGuedes@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092040 - Display COM port numbers in Web Serial API port chooser on Windows. r=webserial-reviewers,gstoll\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343096\n", "files": ["dom/webserial/Win32SerialPlatformService.cpp"], "git_node": "16b8265c0b71b7e52ff3f47275ebcf02ab6d050f", "git_parents": ["b988c8c4225b8017fe2938c604de7292ea5f11c0"], "node": "78186d4de4a1640bfc4f2d327fd3af84becf0e7c", "parents": ["2e731c58b2995cb35c82a02fef05fd5dd6784a7e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sebastian Streich \u003cgit@basti.fyi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067288 - Retry IP Protection proxy pass rotation on wake instead of erroring out r=ip-protection-reviewers,apopov,rking\n\nOn wake the pass is usually expired, so we rotate over a network that is\noften not usable yet.\nHowever we rely on `isOffline` to to be accurate in order to determine wheter we should attempt to retry on a network error.\n\nGiven that we do know network-errors are more likely after wake, let's pass our expectation during rotation.\n-\u003e So after wake, at network error is not a critical failure\n-\u003e After wake, we give more time to rotate.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323324\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/ipprotection/IPPLifecycleHelper.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/IPPProxyManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPPLifecycleHelper.js", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPProxyManager.js"], "git_node": "09b6878b900e49124e3640eb99739d4bfd4d3ec9", "git_parents": ["16b8265c0b71b7e52ff3f47275ebcf02ab6d050f"], "node": "f83561bd68e309612ed5a3a99fd47fc6345f2ad6", "parents": ["78186d4de4a1640bfc4f2d327fd3af84becf0e7c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093335 - Install mozperftest requirements files without pip build isolation r=sparky,mozperftest-reviewers\n\npip 26.3 builds every in tree package from `marionette_requirements.txt`\nin its own isolated environment, which added about 75 seconds to each\nmozperftest mochitest run.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343226\n", "files": ["python/mozperftest/mozperftest/tests/test_utils.py", "python/mozperftest/mozperftest/utils.py"], "git_node": "1e593d86e563650e0fd295b9f91337df12780540", "git_parents": ["09b6878b900e49124e3640eb99739d4bfd4d3ec9"], "node": "29933c84a95de6bc01aa623bf6b2b24dd4c024d4", "parents": ["f83561bd68e309612ed5a3a99fd47fc6345f2ad6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "hlin \u003chlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088276 - Fix AITab surface validation failure caused by bound ListGroup items. r=rrando\n\nSurface validation fails while generating a smart page. Because the models emit List groups whose items is a data-model binding, which does not match with the catalog schema.  Inline the bound array before validation and add description in the schema that ListGroup.items are literal-only in the catalog.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339732\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/aitab/AITab.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/aitab/component_schema.json", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_aitab_validation.js"], "git_node": "b1dcea678e20d1a90221aa625cc7f0528f280160", "git_parents": ["1e593d86e563650e0fd295b9f91337df12780540"], "node": "3512c5be2d3e833e58900b8444523fd09ee78a90", "parents": ["29933c84a95de6bc01aa623bf6b2b24dd4c024d4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083894 - Fix origin bounds in PushDB forEachOrigin. r=saschanaz\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335748\n", "files": ["build/pgo/certs/cert9.db", "build/pgo/certs/key4.db", "build/pgo/certs/mochitest.client", "build/pgo/server-locations.txt", "dom/push/PushDB.sys.mjs", "dom/push/PushServiceWebSocket.sys.mjs", "dom/push/test/file_pushsubscriptionchange_origin_prefix.html", "dom/push/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/push/test/test_pushsubscriptionchange_origin_prefix.html", "dom/push/test/worker.js"], "git_node": "0c19a5a159ecb53e7ca4deaaa0c87b9e5c377ee9", "git_parents": ["b1dcea678e20d1a90221aa625cc7f0528f280160"], "node": "80bad83f3f9a0b9698d9f91f89724b04459179f9", "parents": ["3512c5be2d3e833e58900b8444523fd09ee78a90"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092793 - Ask media tests to name the values they depend on r=ai4dev-reviewers,padenot\n\nWhen a test repeats literals, it hides which values must match a spec, a\nformat or the code under test, and how its values depend on each other, so\nchanging one of them can stop the test from checking what it claims without\nany failure.\n\nAsk that tests name each meaningful value with where it comes from, compute\nthe values that depend on it, and assert the relation where it can break.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342852\n", "files": ["dom/media/AGENTS.md"], "git_node": "b192865d0a8938047af8089cb3e0874e1485a867", "git_parents": ["0c19a5a159ecb53e7ca4deaaa0c87b9e5c377ee9"], "node": "f923b5f45ea821d2ddc6d6e6696a503415f06e92", "parents": ["80bad83f3f9a0b9698d9f91f89724b04459179f9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "hlin-ux \u003chlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091142 - Keep markdown emphasis out of URL tokens in UrlTokenizer.tokenizeText. r=rrando\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341130\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/UrlTokenizer.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_UrlTokenizer.js"], "git_node": "013300427600bf6465e7523254d94539a1847ac6", "git_parents": ["b192865d0a8938047af8089cb3e0874e1485a867"], "node": "62580c366b2c638c76a7a71c0928497309568dd4", "parents": ["f923b5f45ea821d2ddc6d6e6696a503415f06e92"], "tags": []}, {"author": "hlin \u003chlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091131 - Build a Smart Page from raw_content when none of its URLs can be read. r=rrando\n\ngenerate_page failed with pages_unreadable whenever none of the URLs in\nurl_list could be read, even when raw_content already held the content\nto build from. The chat model now sends search-result URLs in url_list\nalongside its answer in raw_content, so search results that all block\nautomated reads made page creation fail, and the retry without the URLs\nproduced a page with no sources.\n\nOnly report pages_unreadable when there is no raw_content. Otherwise\nbuild from raw_content, with the unreadable pages passed on as failed\nreads.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341129\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/aitab/AITab.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_aitab.js"], "git_node": "04706dbcb5c9b4800d9df638d7c26790d8576e53", "git_parents": ["013300427600bf6465e7523254d94539a1847ac6"], "node": "7da39e03a79957d31878c2137f6e99a36114db49", "parents": ["62580c366b2c638c76a7a71c0928497309568dd4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Francesco Lodolo \u003cflod@lodolo.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091097 - Check all variants of brand names in Fluent linter, r=eemeli\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341233\n", "files": ["tools/lint/fluent-lint/__init__.py", "tools/lint/test/files/fluent-lint/brand-names.ftl", "tools/lint/test/files/fluent-lint/test-brands.ftl", "tools/lint/test/test_fluent_lint.py"], "git_node": "7300a0dd9e836877f70d14323d63691743f62b0b", "git_parents": ["04706dbcb5c9b4800d9df638d7c26790d8576e53"], "node": "24304a978d3e8a7421daf1ac04af32a2ba0b26b5", "parents": ["7da39e03a79957d31878c2137f6e99a36114db49"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rebecca King \u003crking@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082582 - Post-Nova CSS Cleanup for Desktop VPN - r=kpatenio,ip-protection-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334325\n", "files": ["browser/components/ipprotection/assets/shield-vpn-exceptions.svg", "browser/components/ipprotection/content/ipprotection-content.css", "browser/components/ipprotection/content/ipprotection-status-box.css", "browser/themes/shared/customizableui/panelUI-shared.css"], "git_node": "b2cf05c7504f09ba222c88c512172643fd01229b", "git_parents": ["7300a0dd9e836877f70d14323d63691743f62b0b"], "node": "0d682767db740eed5ed2c670bee7d457beef97b5", "parents": ["24304a978d3e8a7421daf1ac04af32a2ba0b26b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Reem H \u003c42309026+reemhamz@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086314 - Move hard-coded Crossword strings to the new newtabPreview.ftl file. r=fluent-reviewers,nina-py,flod\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337355\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Crossword/Crossword.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/Crossword.test.jsx", "browser/locales-preview/newtabPreview.ftl", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl"], "git_node": "3d5dcccf91c902e050c816d0823e7e37ff001b5e", "git_parents": ["b2cf05c7504f09ba222c88c512172643fd01229b"], "node": "82df135f1886215778ec0d5568fb73f22714f26a", "parents": ["0d682767db740eed5ed2c670bee7d457beef97b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@intuitionlibrary.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090044 - Reuse the glyph buffer when interning text runs in the display list builder. r=nical,gfx-reviewers\n\nGlyphs are quantized once into a reused buffer that is lent to the key for\nthe lookup, so a run that is already interned no longer allocates.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342980\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_list.rs"], "git_node": "d9b8c7c999077587eb632ae7a4847bce547e68ff", "git_parents": ["3d5dcccf91c902e050c816d0823e7e37ff001b5e"], "node": "b77ecb0b31ab9e9e53a7197d9ab83a8afd8b1866", "parents": ["82df135f1886215778ec0d5568fb73f22714f26a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@intuitionlibrary.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092300 - Round half device pixel shadow offsets up. r=nical,gfx-reviewers\n\nBug 2076646 moved shadow copies by their offset rounded to whole device\npixels with round(), which takes -0.5 to -1. Pixel aligned content snapped\non its own used to land -0.5 at 0, as the glyph pens and positive rect edges\nround ties up, so the lightweight theme text-shadow (0 -0.5px 1.5px white)\nstarted showing above dark chrome text at 100% scale.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342985\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/text_run.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/space.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/2092300-shadow-offset-half-pixel-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/2092300-shadow-offset-half-pixel.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/reftest.list"], "git_node": "4f40e009fa7a38bce3c866b4b7e18b6647eaa184", "git_parents": ["d9b8c7c999077587eb632ae7a4847bce547e68ff"], "node": "fd4d796466576a03868633334d496d95b5bbed05", "parents": ["b77ecb0b31ab9e9e53a7197d9ab83a8afd8b1866"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sebastian Streich \u003csstreich@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078175 - Move an active non-premium connection off a locked location. r=ip-protection-reviewers,rking\n\nOn open the panel rechecks the premium status and shows the location the\nuser may use, but an active connection kept its server. IPPProxyManager now\nexposes the location it routes through, and the panel switches to the shown\none when they differ, in both directions.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339235\n", "files": ["browser/components/ipprotection/IPProtectionPanel.sys.mjs", "browser/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPProtectionPanel.js", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/IPPProxyManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPProxyManager.js"], "git_node": "391e2a565ba8efb11355f2d421ead99682a54461", "git_parents": ["4f40e009fa7a38bce3c866b4b7e18b6647eaa184"], "node": "3ec0956f195fab34dcdf162a17d0ac49706db92c", "parents": ["fd4d796466576a03868633334d496d95b5bbed05"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079683 - Skip parser/bug2076003.js when lcov is enabled. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,mgaudet\n\nThis test compiles a very large switch-heavy function. On code coverage builds it times out, so skip it there.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343233\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/parser/bug2076003.js"], "git_node": "44fb0bcca16dea7a696dbf7b3ccf1f4aa54711d9", "git_parents": ["391e2a565ba8efb11355f2d421ead99682a54461"], "node": "b3d7143a1ae7f25edfbb99ab6986f65db6419d05", "parents": ["3ec0956f195fab34dcdf162a17d0ac49706db92c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092868: Handle OOM in bug1610192.js r=spidermonkey-reviewers,mgaudet\n\nThis is now supported in the eval cache, which appears to run out of memory on 32-bit Windows in CI. I couldn't reproduce locally; it may be machine-specific.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343235\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/basic/bug1610192.js"], "git_node": "6a2e1c7864de7564a17a9869746c907c6805f408", "git_parents": ["44fb0bcca16dea7a696dbf7b3ccf1f4aa54711d9"], "node": "1cdbe0b97640e5590b51913eaa42058f7c831a55", "parents": ["b3d7143a1ae7f25edfbb99ab6986f65db6419d05"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093652 - Use a timer to drop free canvas buffers when dormant. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDOM workers do not support delayed dispatch, which would fail and leak the\nrunnable.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343240\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasChild.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasChild.h"], "git_node": "69e493928ec5bcda1434b97f090f7696be6ccb9c", "git_parents": ["6a2e1c7864de7564a17a9869746c907c6805f408"], "node": "38283737f3aa73104581c95db603a9e4e4f6826f", "parents": ["1cdbe0b97640e5590b51913eaa42058f7c831a55"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Halberstadt \u003cahal@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092851 - Version bump taskcluster-taskgraph to v24.9.0, r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343152\n", "files": ["taskcluster/requirements.in", "taskcluster/requirements.txt"], "git_node": "199d17875edf8bc66026f3a61e0dc77c89a11997", "git_parents": ["69e493928ec5bcda1434b97f090f7696be6ccb9c"], "node": "f0012c73a8441b056719a003a9feb2d828db6af0", "parents": ["38283737f3aa73104581c95db603a9e4e4f6826f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nina Pypchenko \u003cnpypchenko@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085804 - POTD: Remove `widgets.pictureOfTheDay.setAsWallpaper.enabled` pref r=fchasen\n\nThe Picture of the day \"Set wallpaper\" button now shows whenever\nwallpapers and custom wallpapers are turned on, whether or not the\nuser is in a Picture of the day rollout.\n\nBug 2085803 already turned the button on by default. The pref, the two\ntrain-hop settings that could override it and the \"Set as wallpaper\"\ntoggle in the New Tab devtools panel have been removed, so the button\ncan no longer be switched off. Nimbus recipes that still send\n`setAsWallpaperEnabled` are ignored.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342987\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/common/WidgetsRegistry.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamAdmin/DiscoveryStreamAdmin.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/PictureOfTheDay/PictureOfTheDay.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/ActivityStream.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Widgets/PictureOfTheDayFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamAdmin.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/PictureOfTheDay.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/PrefsFeed.test.js"], "git_node": "2494052d6c4404e88b0073020043c52af7f505c9", "git_parents": ["199d17875edf8bc66026f3a61e0dc77c89a11997"], "node": "f36db4c1076d2cc71ee09eea7691b383e320a1f1", "parents": ["f0012c73a8441b056719a003a9feb2d828db6af0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Markus Stange \u003cmstange.moz@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093566 - Rename PersistentBufferProviderAccelerated to PersistentBufferProviderRemote, and add IsRemote(). r=lsalzman\n\nAt the moment, canvas being remote is tied to whether it's accelerated.\nThis doesn't necessarily need to be true; as a first step we can rename\nclasses and methods that are clearly about remoteness as oppossed to acceleration.\n\nFor example, callers that ask IsAccelerated() really want to know whether\nthe canvas is drawn in another process: whether it can be lost, whether\nit needs a refresh, and whether DrawImage can hand it surface descriptors.\nHave them call IsRemote() instead, so that IsAccelerated() can\nlater mean what it says.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343208\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "gfx/layers/PersistentBufferProvider.cpp", "gfx/layers/PersistentBufferProvider.h"], "git_node": "4e087b0961e0fd031fe17b7b175854857b0d1d18", "git_parents": ["2494052d6c4404e88b0073020043c52af7f505c9"], "node": "218fa0f4380d6db0b2d72f8c5b81dc5e72e47bdb", "parents": ["f36db4c1076d2cc71ee09eea7691b383e320a1f1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092544 - Use the toolbar node created by browser_registerArea.js instead of looking it up with CustomizableUI.getWidget(), r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,Gijs.\n\nAn area isn't a widget. getWidget() on the toolbar's id cached a widget wrapper that unregistering the area doesn't drop, so on a second run in the same browser the test got the removed toolbar's wrapper and threw.\n\nThe verify-standalone skip-if added in bug 1995208 is removed: --verify, which reruns the test in one browser, fails locally with the same TypeError without this fix and passes with it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342584\n", "files": ["browser/components/customizableui/test/browser.toml", "browser/components/customizableui/test/browser_registerArea.js"], "git_node": "af3365918c94bb807f26958fcc3a343f160953a5", "git_parents": ["4e087b0961e0fd031fe17b7b175854857b0d1d18"], "node": "650a6f064f1d52de81340ee53f575e757b2f8b5d", "parents": ["218fa0f4380d6db0b2d72f8c5b81dc5e72e47bdb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cosmin Sabou \u003ccsabou@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1935325 - Enable Declarative Web Push on all channels. r=saschanaz\" for causing mochitest failures on test_interfaces_secureContext.\n\nThis reverts commit 21e472d24ca71dad6e36692a5ea10430f022ac00.\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "c3207314427690814451c73249422871d3bb2017", "git_parents": ["af3365918c94bb807f26958fcc3a343f160953a5"], "node": "614c2a97bda617c77c545f45b9ccd408ad7d5a5e", "parents": ["650a6f064f1d52de81340ee53f575e757b2f8b5d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cosmin Sabou \u003ccsabou@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2093566 - Rename PersistentBufferProviderAccelerated to PersistentBufferProviderRemote, and add IsRemote(). r=lsalzman\" for causing fetch failures.\n\nThis reverts commit 4e087b0961e0fd031fe17b7b175854857b0d1d18.\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "gfx/layers/PersistentBufferProvider.cpp", "gfx/layers/PersistentBufferProvider.h"], "git_node": "11b881bd41a134793823b1a238dd717c7d67c4d5", "git_parents": ["c3207314427690814451c73249422871d3bb2017"], "node": "dea440a271c8bd8882dd1d995432e0254a9e2aa8", "parents": ["614c2a97bda617c77c545f45b9ccd408ad7d5a5e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2092626 - Apply uniform rounded rect clips directly in the quad shaders. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\" for causing perma reftest failures\n\nThis reverts commit b380b98063126ed114a0cdf531af89314a87f30c.\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/WebRenderAPI.cpp", "gfx/wr/webrender/res/ps_quad.glsl", "gfx/wr/webrender/res/ps_quad_gradient.glsl", "gfx/wr/webrender/res/ps_quad_repeat.glsl", "gfx/wr/webrender/res/ps_quad_textured.glsl", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/command_buffer.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/gpu_types.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_item.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/rounded-clip-direct-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/rounded-clip-direct.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/compositor-surface/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/compositor/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/compositor/rounded-corners-1.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/image/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/mask/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/parse_function.rs", "layout/reftests/bugs/reftest.list", "layout/svg/SVGGeometryFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-masking/clip-path/animations/clip-path-animation-inherit.html.ini"], "git_node": "1e2122577ba8287c914c23d911fa0aa53a493c78", "git_parents": ["11b881bd41a134793823b1a238dd717c7d67c4d5"], "node": "98e0bc8d5dad35e39265015fe7a49127e855bff7", "parents": ["dea440a271c8bd8882dd1d995432e0254a9e2aa8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Benoit Goupilleau \u003cbenoit.goupilleau@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082559 - Log an error and end the suite when a mochitest run receives SIGTERM r=mozbase-reviewers,ahal\n\nShortly before a task exceeds its maxRunTime, run-task sends SIGTERM to the task's processes, so that they can shut down before the worker kills them. A new mozprocess helper turns it into a KeyboardInterrupt and logs an error. When it arrives while the tests are running, which is where a run spends nearly all of its time, the harness goes through its Ctrl+C cleanup, and mozharness keeps reading the harness's output, so that its summary still makes it into summary.jsonl. When it arrives during the harness's own setup or teardown, the run stops there without that cleanup, as it did when SIGTERM killed the process.\n\nIn CI an interrupted run was followed by a new browser for the tests that did not get to start; runMochitests now stops there. The task's other processes get the signal too, so the cleanup can fail: on Linux pipewire is gone by the time the harness destroys its audio nodes. That failure is now logged rather than raised, and the suite is ended whatever the run raises.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334531\n", "files": ["testing/mochitest/runtests.py", "testing/mochitest/tests/python/files/test_hang.html", "testing/mochitest/tests/python/test_mochitest_integration.py", "testing/mozbase/mozprocess/mozprocess/termination.py", "testing/mozbase/mozprocess/tests/manifest.toml", "testing/mozbase/mozprocess/tests/test_termination.py", "testing/mozharness/mozharness/base/script.py", "testing/mozharness/test/test_base_script.py"], "git_node": "bb75ff642a88bff6b90b50cb31dab4df085523ee", "git_parents": ["1e2122577ba8287c914c23d911fa0aa53a493c78"], "node": "95d03d4eb3a1e512deb8958dbfcf4cda81fc6384", "parents": ["98e0bc8d5dad35e39265015fe7a49127e855bff7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Benoit Goupilleau \u003cbenoit.goupilleau@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082559 - Make run-task send SIGTERM to the task's processes shortly before the task exceeds its maxRunTime r=taskgraph-reviewers,jcristau\n\nWhen a task exceeds its maxRunTime, the worker kills its processes straight away, so test harnesses can't log that they were aborted, and their structured logs just stop.\n\nrun-task now aborts the task itself, 5% of maxRunTime early and at most 60 seconds early: it sends SIGTERM to its own process group, ignores that signal itself, keeps forwarding the output of the running command until it exits, and then exits 1 whatever that command returned, whether the abort hit the checkout, the fetches or the task's command. taskgraph passes maxRunTime in the TASKCLUSTER_MAX_RUN_TIME environment variable.\n\nThe command stays in run-task's process group, since that is what the worker kills on maxRunTime, cancellation and shutdown. The worker's own kill is unchanged, and nothing changes on Windows. Tasks that clone with git run taskgraph's own copy of run-task, which needs the same change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338003\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/test_transforms_task.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/task.py", "taskcluster/scripts/run-task"], "git_node": "a78bb5240525e5b7fe52be44bf544e52ba5f9157", "git_parents": ["bb75ff642a88bff6b90b50cb31dab4df085523ee"], "node": "136add65504a5b15de8a0c134d808b2c8506ec42", "parents": ["95d03d4eb3a1e512deb8958dbfcf4cda81fc6384"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Foster \u003csfoster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1940355 - Call the clean up method in SidebarPermissions when the panel is unloaded. r=Mardak,sidebar-reviewers,jsudiaman\n\n* Switching between sidebar panels doesn't result in a SidebarWillHide event, so we can leak the chat.html document and browser. Adding a unload listener catches that case\n* Also refactor to use handleEvent to avoid some of the bookkeeping around onSidebarHideEvent\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341204\n", "files": ["browser/components/genai/tests/browser/browser_chat_sidebar_permissions.js", "browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-permissions.mjs"], "git_node": "144e8fb51b9b3544884880438889fdec1e77dba2", "git_parents": ["a78bb5240525e5b7fe52be44bf544e52ba5f9157"], "node": "f12d9990a9d34d1f1ec50eefb66071ca94237b8e", "parents": ["136add65504a5b15de8a0c134d808b2c8506ec42"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Luong \u003cgabriel.luong@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092167 - Part 1: Use the Application Services WrexhamClient in MerinoSportsProvider r=android-reviewers,android-build-system-reviewers,npoon\n\n- Fetch the matches with the Uniffi WrexhamClient instead of concept-fetch\n- Keep the kotlinx deserialization since the client returns the raw JSON response\n- Report only MerinoWrexhamApiException.Other to avoid reports of network failures and of Merino having no data to serve\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342933\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/service/merino-sports/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/merino-sports/src/main/java/mozilla/components/service/merino/sports/MerinoSportsProvider.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/merino-sports/src/test/java/mozilla/components/service/merino/sports/MerinoSportsProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/merino-sports/src/test/java/mozilla/components/service/merino/sports/fake/FakeWrexhamClient.kt"], "git_node": "6cc089278aa6fe6f36735dcb115a0417d1ea222c", "git_parents": ["144e8fb51b9b3544884880438889fdec1e77dba2"], "node": "1ce232f58eba81aedfee864706a7e97568da2b04", "parents": ["f12d9990a9d34d1f1ec50eefb66071ca94237b8e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Luong \u003cgabriel.luong@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092167 - Part 2: Align the Merino matches model with the Merino API schema r=android-reviewers,npoon\n\n- Require the team logo URL and the previous, current and upcoming match groups\n- Cap the matches limit at 5, the maximum the Merino service accepts\n- Update the KDoc to match the Merino API schema\n\nMerino API schema: https://merino.services.mozilla.com/docs#/widgets/get_wrexham_matches_api_v1_widgets_wrexham_matches_get\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343017\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/service/merino-sports/src/main/java/mozilla/components/service/merino/sports/MerinoMatches.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/merino-sports/src/main/java/mozilla/components/service/merino/sports/MerinoSportsProvider.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/merino-sports/src/test/java/mozilla/components/service/merino/sports/DataStoreMerinoMatchesStorageTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/merino-sports/src/test/java/mozilla/components/service/merino/sports/MerinoMatchesSerializerTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/merino-sports/src/test/java/mozilla/components/service/merino/sports/MerinoSportsProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/merino-sports/src/test/java/mozilla/components/service/merino/sports/MerinoSportsUpdaterWorkerTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/merino-sports/src/test/java/mozilla/components/service/merino/sports/MerinoSportsUseCasesTest.kt"], "git_node": "0d9ea9faaceb8a80dd7a2d6048602f18e28cb25b", "git_parents": ["6cc089278aa6fe6f36735dcb115a0417d1ea222c"], "node": "0538e6a0dd932c7ab651bb59fd6551ff5f9db7d2", "parents": ["1ce232f58eba81aedfee864706a7e97568da2b04"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ed Lee \u003cedilee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068201 - send smart cursor text to chatbot with annotations r=echa,gregtatum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342780\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-window/ai-window.mjs", "browser/components/genai/GenAI.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "a1532ffdb97a6fcd05fb9832e46a4d516058205d", "git_parents": ["0d9ea9faaceb8a80dd7a2d6048602f18e28cb25b"], "node": "482f4c045f460034040c517d5b6a3ede801ae606", "parents": ["0538e6a0dd932c7ab651bb59fd6551ff5f9db7d2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092749 - Fix the test by preventing the overscroll effect with overscroll-behavior chain. r=hiro\n\nIn test case \"test_second_finger_while_waiting_prevents_swipe\", APZ handles\nthe first gesture once content responds.\nCurrently it overscrolls the page at the left edge. The overscroll effect\nintermittently gets larger. As a result, the scroll caused by the second\nsingle-finger gesture is consumed to restore the page position from that\noverscroll. In this case, the case fails.\nThis patch makes the test steady by preventing the overscroll using\noverscroll-behavior chain.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342824\n", "files": ["widget/tests/browser/browser_test_touchscreen_swipe_gesture_while_waiting.js"], "git_node": "501dd07c241e79590f421c799cd32d3914a79ca8", "git_parents": ["a1532ffdb97a6fcd05fb9832e46a4d516058205d"], "node": "13bdfb09800b524b3df46b5b6d35ac3d076b1f3c", "parents": ["482f4c045f460034040c517d5b6a3ede801ae606"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080285 - Turn the tab bar visibility script into a module that browser.js loads lazily. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,frontend-codestyle-reviewers,niklas\n\nTabBarVisibility now loads on first access, from browser-init.js's onBeforeInitialXULLayout, instead of at startup; this is the first browser-window use of defineESModuleGetters with { global: \"current\" }, and each window gets its own instance.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340033\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-init.js", "browser/base/content/browser-main.js", "browser/base/content/browser.js", "browser/base/content/browser.js.globals", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab-bar-visibility.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab-bar-visibility.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/jar.mn", "tools/@types/browser-window-globals.d.ts", "tools/@types/browser-window.d.ts", "tools/@types/generated/tspaths.json"], "git_node": "85d8890193877ab3179e44c9eb624718b39d8351", "git_parents": ["501dd07c241e79590f421c799cd32d3914a79ca8"], "node": "afb014c94ed631376a0b6d6c5d251b0b21f0b46f", "parents": ["13bdfb09800b524b3df46b5b6d35ac3d076b1f3c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080284 - Turn the status panel script into a module that browser.js loads lazily. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,frontend-codestyle-reviewers,niklas\n\nThe panel and _labelElement getters replace themselves with Object.defineProperty, because tsc rejects deleting and assigning a getter-only property.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340046\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-main.js", "browser/base/content/browser.js", "browser/base/content/browser.js.globals", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/status-panel.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/status-panel.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/jar.mn", "tools/@types/browser-window-globals.d.ts", "tools/@types/browser-window.d.ts", "tools/@types/generated/tspaths.json"], "git_node": "c7ef9706b55d5cbee37ce15dc94ed66ff19b6514", "git_parents": ["85d8890193877ab3179e44c9eb624718b39d8351"], "node": "5e1bc97a77edbc90757153432ca794c9467afc1f", "parents": ["afb014c94ed631376a0b6d6c5d251b0b21f0b46f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nathan Barrett \u003cnbarrett@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092144 - Add new wallpaper category for partner repack r=fluent-reviewers,thecount,flod,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342210\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/WallpaperCategories/WallpaperCategories.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/lib/constants.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Wallpapers/WallpaperFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/locales-preview/newtabPreview.ftl"], "git_node": "8b8b2d67f29f235ca29b7f0b888ddbeb578afe5e", "git_parents": ["c7ef9706b55d5cbee37ce15dc94ed66ff19b6514"], "node": "2b52b9d10c894b97fa4de688c9c273054a30884f", "parents": ["5e1bc97a77edbc90757153432ca794c9467afc1f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andy Wingo \u003cwingo@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093336 - Use a Digits kernel in BigInt mod r=mgaudet\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343144\n", "files": ["js/src/vm/BigIntType.cpp", "js/src/vm/BigIntType.h"], "git_node": "2dfff3092e353fc36ab185d1e2c72e81672bf6e5", "git_parents": ["8b8b2d67f29f235ca29b7f0b888ddbeb578afe5e"], "node": "41f79a54aeee070916f5b995cca554c2f4c1b26a", "parents": ["2b52b9d10c894b97fa4de688c9c273054a30884f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nhadji \u003cnhadji@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058156 - Run the vendor-verify source-test tasks from a git checkout, r=taskgraph-reviewers,ahal\n\nDeletes the `clone-with: hg` line of the vendor-verify kind, so its tasks\nclone the Git repository on pushes that carry one, like the other\nsource-test kinds. The kind was kept on Mercurial because libsoundtouch\nre-vendored cleanly from a Git clone while being annotated as an expected\nfailure, which turned the media group orange; that annotation went away\nin bug 2014269 and the expected-fail list no longer depends on the VCS.\n\nTested on try (push 03c162f5353f): all 11 vendor-verify groups ran from a\nGit clone and passed, the media group included (task MFvk6ILOSeGZohf4mQIxUQ);\nthe longest, sandbox, took 23 minutes of its 35-minute limit\n(fzeWmgb7Q-aDCmEv9R8eiw).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343136\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/source-test/vendor-verify.yml"], "git_node": "19f4be23f11edbc25be14868c71628611befe456", "git_parents": ["2dfff3092e353fc36ab185d1e2c72e81672bf6e5"], "node": "062bfa0e45b233dd6146a301e92b0329a8fa1f91", "parents": ["41f79a54aeee070916f5b995cca554c2f4c1b26a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Wisniewski \u003ctwisniewski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093654 - disable gathering console logs for broken site reports to fix a crash; r=ksenia,webcompat-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343253\n", "files": ["browser/components/reportbrokensite/test/browser/browser_antitracking_data_sent.js", "toolkit/components/reportbrokensite/ReportBrokenSiteChild.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "41db707342feaa6722e4a2076a24ec3d01fe96d2", "git_parents": ["19f4be23f11edbc25be14868c71628611befe456"], "node": "2e616e4a4ae55056aec51edf21e0683eda5a2491", "parents": ["062bfa0e45b233dd6146a301e92b0329a8fa1f91"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794888823, "git_changesets": ["2d75683e18caa194ef4f474ad0461face5ffdcb7", "54e31fc4a93c7982f7e2bbb770eaaba6f1701ba6", "ce4a3b1a42370737aa4439bf3573eff4219a5834", "ec06bd552b9bbd9035b9a7b85c85fc4251d86082", "930cb2f5737a17ca97966b2c3bbea84399a1d681", "3faf8ae1759e2321881126318ec1b4199a126e77", "4e84d46e08bf8c3fbd98426be800ad568328e599", "5e9cd4194e59abd743ad8373253fe24ac87408f7", "24091d3b38fb6a2a7d6b4ee56f129a0ac8c177f3", "d877986b287ffa9e064b615d68fe4e68fbb65b4b", "9f3e05f203635d9478df8bcddaf2fc98624353b3", "7520cc3fc3a1c17c468aa7d5651a5a1334545925", "a3b629a58cd01520bb547ecbf4721760b8133bdb", "f8eb10a7536a2b9af124ffdff4f8939955737a97", "992d7c9ed962cdda228192c40821b2a7d05081d4", "4dff698ff78a57268308e8f06992cb1dd402872f", "035b2c356c1c9ee92db2ffb89295619b1efdc671", "1f30a6f7304a1dd1d11d9d117caa1b30f64264b7", "a7672a7ae52f8c177b78b073eedbb125034cb7c6", "8cd8db20376b90d2e4c9b385064ee3283bc35f61", "a93b444a89e56e5cc94d88e9089cd95bf8d5aeb5", "d3024c5f931ad5f93c4c139a7f5f4434df820807", "d131d8bca66626b76adde000ec9d4abe78b5af45", "ed7f0a9ad4f0741870b20856153fdb85970bb497", "99b4e60e120244064d99195571c6dee38d201936", "2fd8b88bdcaf60f6ca62957de5f60dc529a87487", "6223b7e1e3deb2cdced6b75d6f4996acc0871cee", "ee0e38f501ed6f1ca6f1e8039f72121c5542d117", "8f0e841b4d82b10a27bf41fddbb927a3035f15ae", "b380b98063126ed114a0cdf531af89314a87f30c", "16866d5f85718bc814d59782145ed5c28c38cd50", "a0002459c3ac6058cbc496d126957dc749ff4c82", "c2089dee2145489c9797035a4569162d0b208ddf", "4d458ef2d78dc7b25504ec77e8d6653049023f02", "bb4dc8036386666a258420a29e8926f56238ba62", "df58a313081b624ef81f72de91b3390c000cbb56", "f8a1e79c7777c92cc11012e01faf9f1a03a6a8b3", "b779e69f014e608e788b0fcf23d597a71482a033", "e38b62f9042e2209e99b5c06324aefa28796834f", "a88f25fc1e468d733e5016e35988448382e179f4", "bcc0f6746924cb213ab9195163f853eb220f0343", "7