@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1935325 - Enable Declarative Web Push on all channels. r=saschanaz,webidl,jjaschke\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341034\n", "files": ["dom/tests/mochitest/general/test_interfaces.js", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/push-api/__dir__.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/push-api/idlharness.https.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "37f513bb9561c92d135bb0934e201effadbc781a", "git_parents": ["92c8f1dd633591e0270462d5cba81ef4472ed80d"], "node": "fa8f5013b688624ac792ea1af552b707e8f4f478", "parents": ["18960d84a9fa1c0e14681370968a46afd9d1e989"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083027 - Be more careful about calling DropJSObjects from Unlink. r=smaug\n\nClean up nsJSArgArray which is gross.\n\nIDBObjectStore, IDBIndex and IDBKeyRange all call drop in their\nunlink, but they also actively track whether the object is currently\nholding and make it hold if it needs to, so that's fine. IDBRequest::SetResult\ncalls HoldJSObjects immediately after every write to mResultVal, so that's\nalso okay.\n\nCustomEvent::mDetail is set to null in Unlink to match the constructor,\nwhich is a change in behavior.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342817\n", "files": ["dom/base/TimeoutHandler.cpp", "dom/base/TimeoutHandler.h", "dom/base/nsJSEnvironment.cpp", "dom/base/nsJSEnvironment.h", "dom/events/CustomEvent.cpp", "dom/payments/PaymentMethodChangeEvent.cpp", "dom/performance/PerformanceMainThread.cpp", "dom/performance/PerformanceMark.cpp", "dom/performance/PerformanceMeasure.cpp"], "git_node": "95ef4ee7186c3dc6f9e3b471498ca8e41a79a74d", "git_parents": ["37f513bb9561c92d135bb0934e201effadbc781a"], "node": "3b5727dbc8242b1602ea1836c06570d53099a764", "parents": ["fa8f5013b688624ac792ea1af552b707e8f4f478"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083027 - Add CycleCollectorUnlinkTester for testing use-after-unlink. r=smaug,webidl\n\nWith the unlink hardening in this series, objects like CustomEvent no\nlonger make it easy to observe a use-after-unlink. This pref-gated\ninterface records when it has been unlinked, and can crash on use after\nunlink, so it can be used for standalone test cases and regression tests.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342818\n", "files": ["dom/base/CycleCollectorUnlinkTester.cpp", "dom/base/CycleCollectorUnlinkTester.h", "dom/base/moz.build", "dom/webidl/CycleCollectorUnlinkTester.webidl", "dom/webidl/moz.build", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "ee255ef6398c23a703e2cc89bd3f324fbf777192", "git_parents": ["95ef4ee7186c3dc6f9e3b471498ca8e41a79a74d"], "node": "d8caf1c1bd456354d1220967b15f33ce9f2a6b48", "parents": ["3b5727dbc8242b1602ea1836c06570d53099a764"], "tags": []}, {"author": "owlishDeveloper \u003cbugzeeeeee@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075435 - Add telemetry to ScrollCapture callback implementation r=geckoview-reviewers,kaya\n\nI went with C++ path for this to avoid adding JS/GeckoBundle object overhead, since the feature doesn't use JS. The objective is to measure the failure rate of the feature, as well as to gain isight into the failre causes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336264\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/ScrollCaptureTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/GeckoSession.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/GeckoViewScrollCaptureCallback.java", "mobile/shared/modules/geckoview/metrics.yaml", "widget/android/GeckoViewSupport.h", "widget/android/moz.build", "widget/android/nsWindow.cpp"], "git_node": "9ece3007ac8749ea008e384166c71f97504e3966", "git_parents": ["ee255ef6398c23a703e2cc89bd3f324fbf777192"], "node": "c20d106552d5b74d44234bf1e43357e21412a498", "parents": ["d8caf1c1bd456354d1220967b15f33ce9f2a6b48"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Roger Yang \u003croyang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088958 - Show the VPN \"Paused\" menu badge in the same color as in the Trust Panel. r=android-reviewers,cbect\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342688\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/compose/IPProtectionMenuItem.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ipprotection/VpnMenuItemProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ipprotection/VpnMenuItemProviderTest.kt"], "git_node": "57a74ad6af0c31e5744ebaf5cdbb3a64266f1842", "git_parents": ["9ece3007ac8749ea008e384166c71f97504e3966"], "node": "0bd745fe3050a8165456596777e722c5eac97442", "parents": ["c20d106552d5b74d44234bf1e43357e21412a498"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Poon \u003cnpoon@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085941 - Refresh search engines on focus when a search configuration collection is updated r=android-reviewers,skhan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342327\n", "files": ["mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/focus/FocusApplication.kt", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/focus/FocusApplicationTest.kt"], "git_node": "90fa1f30bc0e154f5d5c90df5e1548e911bd58e2", "git_parents": ["57a74ad6af0c31e5744ebaf5cdbb3a64266f1842"], "node": "cd1f29c83ea338d6f3697f4b156690b76795b5d1", "parents": ["0bd745fe3050a8165456596777e722c5eac97442"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Poon \u003cnpoon@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084415 - Refresh search engines on fenix when search-config-v3 collection is updated r=android-reviewers,skhan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340088\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/FenixApplication.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/FenixApplicationTest.kt"], "git_node": "70482255670611570b7fa0a1450c1418798a0074", "git_parents": ["90fa1f30bc0e154f5d5c90df5e1548e911bd58e2"], "node": "7c31c15bdbfd07e8cbd54a0f40b172a915efb68b", "parents": ["cd1f29c83ea338d6f3697f4b156690b76795b5d1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Pages \u003cjpages@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2029617 - wasm: Move some wasm specific functions from MIR.cpp to MIR-wasm.cpp. r=bvisness\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328920\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/MIR-wasm.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR.cpp"], "git_node": "b135f4dbe1f72f9db2ed407f14aff557c29f5189", "git_parents": ["70482255670611570b7fa0a1450c1418798a0074"], "node": "95570a370e63acdfef593d6d7d48dd0c56d15a5c", "parents": ["7c31c15bdbfd07e8cbd54a0f40b172a915efb68b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Pages \u003cjpages@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2029617 - wasm: Rename keepAlive to wasmObject on MWasmLoadField and MWasmStoreField(Ref). r=bvisness\n\nThe wasmObject operand is the GC object owning the accessed location, and is\nnow the only source of type information for these instructions. Is it now non-optional, the base\noperand is only used as a raw pointer.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338184\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/Lowering.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR-wasm.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR-wasm.h", "js/src/jit/ScalarReplacement.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmIonCompile.cpp"], "git_node": "24ff56f137f34e5ecf507011043115467e46e2f7", "git_parents": ["b135f4dbe1f72f9db2ed407f14aff557c29f5189"], "node": "7811a213d84fc411e354c09e5efadb7af50b39bb", "parents": ["95570a370e63acdfef593d6d7d48dd0c56d15a5c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Pages \u003cjpages@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2029617 - wasm: Add MWasmLoadInternalField for the immutable internal fields of wasm GC objects. r=bvisness\n\nStruct out-of-line data pointers, array data pointers, array lengths and\nexception data pointers are never written by wasm code once the object has been\nallocated, so these loads get their own instruction with no alias set and no\nkeepalive operand.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338185\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/gc/ref-gvn.js", "js/src/jit/Lowering.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR-wasm.h", "js/src/jit/MIROps.yaml", "js/src/jit/WasmBCE.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmIonCompile.cpp"], "git_node": "ab0d503c718c27ea2ece079e058ad9c621644909", "git_parents": ["24ff56f137f34e5ecf507011043115467e46e2f7"], "node": "e5131e6be34b2fd4ad14efee345c90066855ec84", "parents": ["7811a213d84fc411e354c09e5efadb7af50b39bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Pages \u003cjpages@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2029617 - wasm: Support wasm gc struct loads forwarding in GVN. r=bvisness\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D297752\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/gc/ref-gvn.js", "js/src/jit/MIR-wasm.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR-wasm.h"], "git_node": "202736352b268d0bfd526f5f651881ae8fd013bf", "git_parents": ["ab0d503c718c27ea2ece079e058ad9c621644909"], "node": "6add2fe0ff028f6b5c8d2c35c8150061301d3fa2", "parents": ["e5131e6be34b2fd4ad14efee345c90066855ec84"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Pages \u003cjpages@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2029617 - Adding tests for wasm gc load forwarding pass. r=bvisness\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D297753\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/gc/load-forwarding.js"], "git_node": "e379a824cdec3ba5016a1a252d9111d21c00df95", "git_parents": ["202736352b268d0bfd526f5f651881ae8fd013bf"], "node": "2ddd569779e209297714f423a90b5ab378addd08", "parents": ["6add2fe0ff028f6b5c8d2c35c8150061301d3fa2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rebecca King \u003crking@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093664 - Add unlimited bandwidth text to vpn status card - r=ip-protection-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,bolsson,mcleinman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343260\n", "files": ["browser/components/ipprotection/IPProtectionPanel.sys.mjs", "browser/components/ipprotection/content/ipprotection-content.css", "browser/components/ipprotection/content/ipprotection-content.mjs", "browser/components/ipprotection/tests/browser/browser_ipprotection_status_card.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/ipProtection.ftl"], "git_node": "a26849229c64cc26ab321bc9ca5d579eeb5b44eb", "git_parents": ["e379a824cdec3ba5016a1a252d9111d21c00df95"], "node": "98fb026d2cf9f8fb06628e5d32b85291859a0357", "parents": ["2ddd569779e209297714f423a90b5ab378addd08"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081759 - Read credit cards from the Rust store without decrypting them unless a secret is needed r=joschmidt,credential-management-reviewers,NeilDeakin,mtigley,mossop,theidkamp\n\nEvery read from the Rust store decrypted every card, so with a primary\npassword set, listing cards prompted on every page with a card form.\n\nRecords are now built from CreditCardCandidates, which need no key, so\nlisting never prompts. The number and security code are read together\nthrough decryptFields, only to fill, edit, export or compare a card. A\nrecord reports a stored security code as hasSecurityCode.\n\nA submitted card is compared only against saved cards ending in the same\nfour digits, so offering to save a new card does not prompt either.\n\nThese no longer prompt: form detection, the autocomplete dropdown and its\npreview, the manage credit cards dialog, the settings payment methods list,\nthe save doorhanger for a new card, and the saved card counts used by\ntelemetry, ASRouter targeting and the profile deletion page. Filling,\nediting and saving a card still prompt.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334111\n", "files": ["browser/components/profiles/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/profiles/tests/browser/browser_delete_profile_page_locked_cards.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/content/manageDialog.mjs", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser_creditCard_primaryPassword.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_creditCard_capture_cvv.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_creditCard_cvv.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_creditCard_doorhanger_cvv.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_creditCard_fill_cancel_login.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_editCreditCardDialog_cvv.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/head.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_rustStoreShutdown.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_rust_autofill_credit_card_adapter.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_rust_autofill_credit_card_migration.js", "toolkit/components/formautofill/AutofillStorageMigrator.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillPreferences.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillStorageBase.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/ProfileAutoCompleteResult.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/RustAutofillAdapterBase.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/RustAutofillCreditCardStorage.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/RustAutofillStore.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/default/FormAutofillPrompter.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/default/FormAutofillStorage.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/shared/CreditCardRecord.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/shared/FormAutofillSection.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "9c1896744b682f35b545ed3cc094009d0ddf4c04", "git_parents": ["a26849229c64cc26ab321bc9ca5d579eeb5b44eb"], "node": "51cafbd5b3fbc13652b3eb041608b3e8d73c6a14", "parents": ["98fb026d2cf9f8fb06628e5d32b85291859a0357"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093105 - Don't send SetDataSurfaceBuffer after the canvas recorder has failed. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nWhen the recorder fails, its pause events are silently dropped, but\nCanvasChild::EnsureDataSurfaceShmem still sent SetDataSurfaceBuffer. The\ntranslator then received it while not paused. DropFreeBuffers could also\nrevive the invalid buffer, desynchronizing the writer and reader.\n\nAdditionally, stop translation when playing an event deactivated the\ntranslator, so the Failed state is not overwritten.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342963\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/CanvasDrawEventRecorder.cpp", "gfx/layers/CanvasDrawEventRecorder.h", "gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasChild.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/CanvasTranslator.cpp"], "git_node": "bea96966faa4131d2e26af3f2c479698bb8abbe7", "git_parents": ["9c1896744b682f35b545ed3cc094009d0ddf4c04"], "node": "54b0013d4a479a3953af96694d32b30ef154d983", "parents": ["51cafbd5b3fbc13652b3eb041608b3e8d73c6a14"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jason Prickett \u003cjprickett@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091147 - Remove import picker screen from about:welcome flow for linux r=omc-reviewers,yazan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342250\n", "files": ["browser/components/aboutwelcome/modules/AboutWelcomeDefaults.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/tests/browser/browser_aboutwelcome_multistage_mr.js", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/tests/browser/browser_aboutwelcome_screen_targeting.js", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/tests/browser/browser_aboutwelcome_theme_picker.js"], "git_node": "ef77d5e3f081c5924a2a3a6cfbbf778c09e5251e", "git_parents": ["bea96966faa4131d2e26af3f2c479698bb8abbe7"], "node": "d41aa739175fc6c0a2dbc022a942ad28ac104bde", "parents": ["54b0013d4a479a3953af96694d32b30ef154d983"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093690 - Keep EventStateManager's real idle tick away from the opened page dwell time tests, r=fchasen.\n\ntest_opened_page_dwell_time_ends_with_its_window and\ntest_opened_page_dwell_time_follows_the_tab stand in for a user who stays\nactive, but a real user-interaction-inactive-non-synthesized tick landing while\nexample.com loads stops the stopwatch before it starts, so nothing is recorded.\nRe-notifying active after the load would defeat follows_the_tab, which checks\nthat the location change alone starts the measurement.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343255\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_newtab_ping.js"], "git_node": "098e401148638470c144155c7ab464b5f643fefb", "git_parents": ["ef77d5e3f081c5924a2a3a6cfbbf778c09e5251e"], "node": "8f3ac0427ace9747493f7b925ea82204e0b2e590", "parents": ["d41aa739175fc6c0a2dbc022a942ad28ac104bde"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089612 - Wait for the Discovery Stream reload before using a story card in browser_discovery_card.js, r=fchasen.\n\nThe prefs pushed in before() make DiscoveryStreamFeed reset and reload the already open page, which replaces the story cards. When that reload lands after the test has picked a card, the card is detached and the hit test misses it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343256\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_discovery_card.js"], "git_node": "c572a1fb792594fa7458311244f8245b63499969", "git_parents": ["098e401148638470c144155c7ab464b5f643fefb"], "node": "99b16e8f1cbd0210b7f0e01980c6473458647941", "parents": ["8f3ac0427ace9747493f7b925ea82204e0b2e590"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093686 - Check the Stories space by its tab id rather than its localized label in browser_newtab_spaces.js, r=fchasen.\n\nThe tab label is filled in by Fluent asynchronously, so it can still be empty\nwhen the test sees the spaces container. The tab id is set at render.\ntest_spaces_respects_a_toggle_made_while_enrolled gets the same change: its\nnegative check passed whenever the label was still untranslated, so it proved\nnothing.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343257\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_newtab_spaces.js"], "git_node": "1211608405a398d900a2a0c80285b53fb8b639c3", "git_parents": ["c572a1fb792594fa7458311244f8245b63499969"], "node": "d8c91e7e98f9670d529a4702a58108e9a8b3bb5e", "parents": ["99b16e8f1cbd0210b7f0e01980c6473458647941"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093687 - Destroy the WebRenderBridgeParent before erasing its layer tree state in EraseLayerState, r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth.\n\nThis matters when the parent process unmaps a closed tab's layer tree before\nthe content process's Shutdown/ClearCachedResources for its bridge reaches the\ncompositor. WebRenderBridgeParent::ActorDestroy already destroys the bridge\nbefore DisconnectWrBridge erases the state; this makes the parent-initiated\npath match it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343258\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeParent.cpp"], "git_node": "64becaa04e200971a25c8c31781b6b63d86504ab", "git_parents": ["1211608405a398d900a2a0c80285b53fb8b639c3"], "node": "d5741ab15ef4a8b65d84fbb4fc78996ea038d221", "parents": ["d8c91e7e98f9670d529a4702a58108e9a8b3bb5e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093708 - Keep the built-in add-ons override when restarting the add-on manager in the newtab xpcshell head, r=mconley.\n\nBug 1982652 replaced promiseRestartManager() with promiseShutdownManager(), which clears overrides by default, so the built_in_addons.json override limiting the test to newtab was dropped before the restart. Every test using this head then installed and started all built-in add-ons, and startup waits for their background pages. Under chaos mode, the five extra hidden background pages' vsync tasks starve the extension process's sync Extension:GetFrameData message in the parent, so that wait never resolves and head_initialize hangs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343287\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/head.js"], "git_node": "47860762179eb2e351d39ec79d745160af4679d5", "git_parents": ["64becaa04e200971a25c8c31781b6b63d86504ab"], "node": "23c1676f77cb684d0c0acae6317e3b3c63cbe1c7", "parents": ["d5741ab15ef4a8b65d84fbb4fc78996ea038d221"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1966300 - Ignore rejections from onSearchEngineModified listeners in search-detection, r=extension-reviewers,robwu.\n\nWhen the search engine list changes while the extension is shutting down, the background listener can't reply and fire.async() rejects, showing up as an uncaught rejection (e.g. in test_AboutHomeStartupCacheWorker.js, whose search engine is removed during shutdown). Handle it like the other built-in experiment APIs do.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343290\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/search-detection/extension/api.js"], "git_node": "e3c586be408ec97322eaf549e5e5693a2e433d4e", "git_parents": ["47860762179eb2e351d39ec79d745160af4679d5"], "node": "2304be5dc043da332551d2d2ff14eb3be7296a20", "parents": ["23c1676f77cb684d0c0acae6317e3b3c63cbe1c7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093711 - Don't schedule StartupCache writes once profileBeforeChange has started, r=extension-reviewers,robwu.\n\nA late cache update, such as a still-pending scripting.registerContentScripts\ncall from a built-in add-on, rejected from addBlocker() or DeferredTask.arm(),\nand that uncaught rejection failed xpcshell tests.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343291\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/extensions/ExtensionParent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "7c1d99f0380a350db53281bf93834a4e8ed40936", "git_parents": ["e3c586be408ec97322eaf549e5e5693a2e433d4e"], "node": "b905aef8830ea81471c1ac86e17864d5a643f214", "parents": ["2304be5dc043da332551d2d2ff14eb3be7296a20"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081147 - Default the compiler cache directory to the mozbuild state directory r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nConfigure now sets `SCCACHE_DIR`, `CCACHE_DIR` or `BUILDCACHE_DIR` to\n`cache/\u003ctool\u003e` in the state directory, unless the environment already sets it\nor the build runs in automation.\n\n`./mach cargo` and the ccache hit rate report run outside make, so they take\nthe directory from the configured substs. ccache and buildcache look for\ntheir configuration file in the new directory.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333179\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/toolchain.configure", "config/config.mk", "docs/setup/configuring_build_options.md", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/controller/building.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/mach_commands.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/configure/test_toolchain_configure.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/controller/test_ccachestats.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/test_mach_cargo.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/util.py"], "git_node": "97936ba1dca4e5f6896157a239036affcf906658", "git_parents": ["7c1d99f0380a350db53281bf93834a4e8ed40936"], "node": "2797e3a342680613936b93466b71ec4b11e07502", "parents": ["b905aef8830ea81471c1ac86e17864d5a643f214"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nathan Barrett \u003cnbarrett@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087642 - Center backup screens for FRO r=fchasen,omc-reviewers,emcminn\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341550\n", "files": ["browser/components/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.bundle.js", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.css", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/ContentTiles.jsx", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/EmbeddedBackupRestore.jsx", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/styles/_multistage.scss", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.bundle.js", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.css", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/unit/content-src/components/EmbeddedBackupRestore.test.jsx", "browser/components/backup/content/restore-from-backup.css", "browser/components/backup/content/restore-from-backup.mjs", "browser/components/backup/tests/chrome/test_restore_from_backup.html"], "git_node": "cdd67f73e048e13e884c07a0d3886263ea05bc22", "git_parents": ["97936ba1dca4e5f6896157a239036affcf906658"], "node": "14f9a0ceae10bd960c530510ce6bdeed3f502893", "parents": ["2797e3a342680613936b93466b71ec4b11e07502"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091120 part 1: Move the innerHTML retrieval code from sdnAccessible::get_innerHTML into MsaaAccessible::GetInnerHTML. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,morgan\n\nThis will soon be used by UIA too.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343020\n", "files": ["accessible/ipc/RemoteAccessible.h", "accessible/windows/msaa/MsaaAccessible.cpp", "accessible/windows/msaa/MsaaAccessible.h", "accessible/windows/sdn/sdnAccessible.cpp"], "git_node": "53f2454d01b4fa37f6bb39379ebf25fbd47438ab", "git_parents": ["cdd67f73e048e13e884c07a0d3886263ea05bc22"], "node": "b9aa8935875f9188ee945d093f0ff9bee63794cf", "parents": ["14f9a0ceae10bd960c530510ce6bdeed3f502893"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091120 part 2: Expose MathML via the MathML UIA custom property. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,morgan\n\nThis property was originally defined by Microsoft Word and is also supported by Chromium.\nNarrator uses it to support math.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343021\n", "files": ["accessible/tests/browser/windows/a11y_setup.py", "accessible/tests/browser/windows/uia/browser_controlType.js", "accessible/tests/browser/windows/uia/browser_generalProps.js", "accessible/tests/browser/windows/uia/browser_miscCustomProps.js", "accessible/windows/uia/uiaRawElmProvider.cpp", "accessible/windows/uia/uiaRawElmProvider.h"], "git_node": "c70e5403f79d997fcd098f4394614c60db0296a7", "git_parents": ["53f2454d01b4fa37f6bb39379ebf25fbd47438ab"], "node": "5e16596665a2a36f76948698ae363e65cb4d8979", "parents": ["b9aa8935875f9188ee945d093f0ff9bee63794cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089584: Check for overrecursion in OSR r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342408\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/Ion.cpp"], "git_node": "2d9d1f877853218829268e5412ee67c00b4ebe06", "git_parents": ["c70e5403f79d997fcd098f4394614c60db0296a7"], "node": "b857763755c379a852ca6284b4c383ac794aba84", "parents": ["5e16596665a2a36f76948698ae363e65cb4d8979"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nina Pypchenko \u003cnpypchenko@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091617 - Show the sign-in prompt in Widget Studio when no account is signed in r=fchasen,fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,bolsson,tgiles\n\nWidget Studio now shows a sign-in screen to people who aren't signed in\nto a Mozilla account, instead of an empty panel.\n\nThe screen has a heading, a \"Sign in\" button, a \"Learn more\" link and\nKit. The button doesn't do anything yet, because the sign-in flow itself\nis bug 2080367, of which this is the first piece. The link opens the\nexisting widgets support page for now, and bug 2092332 will replace it\nwith a new article. Users who are signed in see the widget composer\ninstead.\n\nIt follows the design in Figma. Where Figma's colours and sizes have no\ndesign token, it uses the nearest one, and in dark mode it matches Nova\nmessages styles.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341712\n", "files": ["browser/components/widgets/content/sidebar-widget-studio.css", "browser/components/widgets/content/sidebar-widget-studio.html", "browser/components/widgets/content/sidebar-widget-studio.mjs", "browser/components/widgets/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/widgets/tests/browser/browser_widget_studio_sign_in.js", "browser/locales-preview/widgets.ftl"], "git_node": "ec7fe5147c267a12d94dabb338e9a44f3ca22ed5", "git_parents": ["2d9d1f877853218829268e5412ee67c00b4ebe06"], "node": "b43e92eb9f07581461a54dafa0f7a31616b680f4", "parents": ["b857763755c379a852ca6284b4c383ac794aba84"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nina Pypchenko \u003cnpypchenko@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080367 - Add a sign-in flow for using widget generation r=fchasen\n\nThe \"Sign in\" button on the Widget Studio sign-in screen now opens the\nMozilla account sign-in page, and is disabled while that page is open.\nOnce someone has signed in, that tab closes and they're back on the page\nthey started from, which is New Tab if that's where they began. The\nsign-in screen is replaced by the widget composer.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342472\n", "files": ["browser/components/widgets/AuthenticationController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/widgets/content/sidebar-widget-studio.mjs", "browser/components/widgets/tests/browser/browser_widget_studio_sign_in.js"], "git_node": "7ba0d5f8573a52ab9f86db3c1568543a8dfc4587", "git_parents": ["ec7fe5147c267a12d94dabb338e9a44f3ca22ed5"], "node": "908fd09deb64291862e7a3ef1158d7d2b8f87edc", "parents": ["b43e92eb9f07581461a54dafa0f7a31616b680f4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Christopher DiPersio \u003ccdipersio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078322 - Implement extended Memories telemetry r=cmurray,pdahiya\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341100\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/Memories.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/MemoriesChatSource.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/MemoriesConstants.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/MemoriesHistorySource.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/MemoriesManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/MemoriesSchedulers.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_MemoriesGenerationRunTelemetry.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_MemoriesManager.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_MemoriesSchedulers.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "aa808ff76d1ab6f2bbf4758174ae34868e96a605", "git_parents": ["7ba0d5f8573a52ab9f86db3c1568543a8dfc4587"], "node": "c9d15ee7455dc8509370249b3e873d35e6e7fa9b", "parents": ["908fd09deb64291862e7a3ef1158d7d2b8f87edc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Christopher DiPersio \u003ccdipersio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091519 - Implement Journeys generation telemetry r=cmurray,pdahiya\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341594\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/Memories.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/MemoriesConstants.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/MemoriesSchedulers.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/journeys/JourneyManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_JourneyManager.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_JourneysGenerationRunTelemetry.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_MemoriesGenerationRunTelemetry.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_MemoriesManager.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_MemoriesSchedulers.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "9e932c6c0c70fe743cf9e0645a71545117b7ea89", "git_parents": ["aa808ff76d1ab6f2bbf4758174ae34868e96a605"], "node": "6bf5e05ca79ebde36f810516410dbbebaf326a31", "parents": ["c9d15ee7455dc8509370249b3e873d35e6e7fa9b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Christopher DiPersio \u003ccdipersio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092619 - Implement Memories and Journeys maintenance telemetry r=cmurray,pdahiya\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342699\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/MemoriesConstants.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/MemoriesManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/MemoriesSchedulers.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/journeys/JourneyManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_JourneyManager.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_MemoriesGenerationRunTelemetry.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_MemoriesMaintenanceRunTelemetry.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_MemoriesSchedulers.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/services/MemoryStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/services/tests/xpcshell/test_MemoryStore.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AIWindow.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "4e6f9b83069797ed81ae0d8eab5ebf7d5c54063e", "git_parents": ["9e932c6c0c70fe743cf9e0645a71545117b7ea89"], "node": "ee2939cd02a78f0a6b6c6099f678742036819fc0", "parents": ["6bf5e05ca79ebde36f810516410dbbebaf326a31"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2029617 - Adding tests for wasm gc load forwarding pass. r=bvisness\" for causing Spidermonkey failures\n\nThis reverts commit e379a824cdec3ba5016a1a252d9111d21c00df95.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2029617 - wasm: Support wasm gc struct loads forwarding in GVN. r=bvisness\"\n\nThis reverts commit 202736352b268d0bfd526f5f651881ae8fd013bf.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2029617 - wasm: Add MWasmLoadInternalField for the immutable internal fields of wasm GC objects. r=bvisness\"\n\nThis reverts commit ab0d503c718c27ea2ece079e058ad9c621644909.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2029617 - wasm: Rename keepAlive to wasmObject on MWasmLoadField and MWasmStoreField(Ref). r=bvisness\"\n\nThis reverts commit 24ff56f137f34e5ecf507011043115467e46e2f7.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2029617 - wasm: Move some wasm specific functions from MIR.cpp to MIR-wasm.cpp. r=bvisness\"\n\nThis reverts commit b135f4dbe1f72f9db2ed407f14aff557c29f5189.\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/gc/load-forwarding.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/gc/ref-gvn.js", "js/src/jit/Lowering.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR-wasm.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR-wasm.h", "js/src/jit/MIR.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIROps.yaml", "js/src/jit/ScalarReplacement.cpp", "js/src/jit/WasmBCE.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmIonCompile.cpp"], "git_node": "2c820c1fae30dbe8494e917c67970d57d92018c2", "git_parents": ["4e6f9b83069797ed81ae0d8eab5ebf7d5c54063e"], "node": "8238d7f928d50de1508c0fe188561feb912253b4", "parents": ["ee2939cd02a78f0a6b6c6099f678742036819fc0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "kpatenio \u003ckpatenio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067725 - adjust bookmark panel expander button to better align chevron icon with the menulist if the button is taller than 32px. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,places-reviewers,hjones,mak\n\nAlso update #bookmarkpropertiesdialog expander buttons to have a 1:1 ratio to keep styles between the panels and dialogs consistent.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340173\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/places/editBookmark.css", "browser/themes/shared/places/editBookmarkPanel.css"], "git_node": "42007de976314c3d0e9387328543a24741435147", "git_parents": ["2c820c1fae30dbe8494e917c67970d57d92018c2"], "node": "47c6c63ea38b8971c6637ccb1554279438f39fb3", "parents": ["8238d7f928d50de1508c0fe188561feb912253b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089251 - Test drawImage, createPattern and copyExternalImageToTexture with ImageBitmaps cropped entirely outside their source. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339750\n", "files": ["dom/webgpu/tests/mochitest/mochitest.toml", "dom/webgpu/tests/mochitest/test_queue_copyExternalImageToTexture_imagebitmap.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/imagebitmap/createImageBitmap-crop-outside-source.html"], "git_node": "feb7e87942adeaf931a245c58d7a577f09610b38", "git_parents": ["42007de976314c3d0e9387328543a24741435147"], "node": "07deadbf8837effad52509a271096e796e973ff0", "parents": ["47c6c63ea38b8971c6637ccb1554279438f39fb3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089251 - Return a transparent surface for an ImageBitmap cropped entirely outside its source. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nPrepareForDrawTarget() returned nothing when the crop rect does not intersect\nthe image, so createPattern() and copyExternalImageToTexture() threw for such\na bitmap. It now returns a transparent black surface of the crop size.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339751\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/ImageBitmap.cpp"], "git_node": "4c84b75fc00a4ea9337735ffea9496ca11cdc238", "git_parents": ["feb7e87942adeaf931a245c58d7a577f09610b38"], "node": "a767cb9f04da6976c8cfe35d1411784aea8763f9", "parents": ["07deadbf8837effad52509a271096e796e973ff0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091373 - Reset FOG in browser_last_window_close_trigger.js before checking the bypass counter, r=omc-reviewers,aminomancer.\n\nThe lastWindowCloseTriggerBypassed counter keeps the value recorded by a previous run of the test in the same browser, so test_second_close_attempt_does_not_redispatch failed when the test was run twice.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341428\n", "files": ["browser/components/tests/browser/browser_last_window_close_trigger.js"], "git_node": "8e2560c28de1eb37084f88f11872b2b3fac4f4fa", "git_parents": ["4c84b75fc00a4ea9337735ffea9496ca11cdc238"], "node": "111c7e63734d5d93f71db0ba2afa758868583575", "parents": ["a767cb9f04da6976c8cfe35d1411784aea8763f9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1775779 - Stop clicking the spammy page in browser_download_spam_protection.js, r=Gijs.\n\nThe page starts its 100 downloads from its load event; the click was not needed.\nLink clicks navigate asynchronously, so when the test's click landed before the\nfirst download's load started, every download carried user activation, none was\nblocked, and the test timed out. A repeated run can only lose this race since\nbug 2078564 removes the automatic-download permission in cleanup.\n\nAlso check that a download a page starts from a timer after a user click is not\ntreated as spam.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342368\n", "files": ["browser/components/downloads/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/downloads/test/browser/browser_download_spam_protection.js", "browser/components/downloads/test/browser/test_user_activated_download_page.html"], "git_node": "770f87accf3a18bc42643e46ed33145c5e34b3d8", "git_parents": ["8e2560c28de1eb37084f88f11872b2b3fac4f4fa"], "node": "bd4a553b18f54edf70c235c2a3ab0e053d26723a", "parents": ["111c7e63734d5d93f71db0ba2afa758868583575"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093632 - Update NSS to 6fb125cd44fa7b9e6267872b4405526f9f4ee1d8. UPGRADE_NSS_RELEASE r=jschanck\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343224\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/RootHashes.inc", "security/nss/cmd/lib/secutil.c", "security/nss/cmd/tstclnt/tstclnt.c", "security/nss/coreconf/WIN32.mk", "security/nss/coreconf/command.mk", "security/nss/coreconf/config.gypi", "security/nss/cpputil/Makefile", "security/nss/gtests/certdb_gtest/decode_certs_unittest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/certdb_gtest/smime_profile_unittest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/common/gtest.mk", "security/nss/gtests/mozpkix_gtest/mozpkix_gtest.gyp", "security/nss/gtests/mozpkix_gtest/pkixcheck_CheckSignatureAlgorithm_tests.cpp", "security/nss/gtests/mozpkix_gtest/pkixder_pki_types_tests.cpp", "security/nss/gtests/mozpkix_gtest/pkixgtest.h", "security/nss/gtests/mozpkix_gtest/pkixmldsa_tests.cpp", "security/nss/gtests/nss_bogo_shim/Makefile", "security/nss/gtests/pk11_gtest/pk11_ecdsa_unittest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/pk11_gtest/pk11_eddsa_unittest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/pk11_gtest/pk11_mldsa_unittest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/pk11_gtest/pk11_rsapkcs1_unittest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/pk11_gtest/pk1