fault", "desc": "Bug 2078654 - Reset the mini window framing on pagehide so its zoom isn't saved into session history. r=mconley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342082\n", "files": ["browser/components/miniwindow/MiniWindowChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/miniwindow/test/browser/browser_cropped_navigation.js"], "git_node": "eb7f8e0212a07f435fbd390095af103955086a89", "git_parents": ["8b99bafe541fb1dded3bbbaa1c56d55cdda1d235"], "node": "f2f6f37cd9853a96b1838150ea110108339e198e", "parents": ["de8605bfc1957f55aa25f1613fad8149102d20fc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091722: Move EventMatchesKeyEquivalent to nsMenuUtilsX. r=mac-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nNo functional changes. This lets a gtest call it in the next patch.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341937\n", "files": ["widget/cocoa/nsMenuBarX.mm", "widget/cocoa/nsMenuUtilsX.h", "widget/cocoa/nsMenuUtilsX.mm"], "git_node": "ccfc796856313ad85a4d79ac6b7ec22cbb919d45", "git_parents": ["eb7f8e0212a07f435fbd390095af103955086a89"], "node": "702655129a662df9a10b6985faa9609e99bee62d", "parents": ["f2f6f37cd9853a96b1838150ea110108339e198e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091722: Match shortcuts assigned in System Settings to function keys, arrows and similar keys. r=mac-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nThe keyboard layout gives these keys a control character, such as 0x10 for every function key, rather than no character, so they were compared against the layout's character and never matched the key equivalent AppKit uses, such as `NSF14FunctionKey`. They are now compared through the event's own character.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341938\n", "files": ["widget/cocoa/TextInputHandler.h", "widget/cocoa/TextInputHandler.mm", "widget/cocoa/nsMenuUtilsX.mm", "widget/tests/gtest/TestCocoaMenuKeyEquivalent.mm", "widget/tests/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "c0013297402742bdc37cd0cf104ae989537dc080", "git_parents": ["ccfc796856313ad85a4d79ac6b7ec22cbb919d45"], "node": "95687ce5ea693d3c2077081aa861eb80e84d9386", "parents": ["702655129a662df9a10b6985faa9609e99bee62d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gela \u003cgmalekpour@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089899 - Part 1: Move the credit card security code changelog entries to 162.0. r=android-reviewers,twhite\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341182\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/docs/changelog.md"], "git_node": "5ed9a51c9dcbf0b4b4952f8f229182bc603f3dbb", "git_parents": ["c0013297402742bdc37cd0cf104ae989537dc080"], "node": "5b59bd6c901c4e0a87859295e24ba51444a95159", "parents": ["95687ce5ea693d3c2077081aa861eb80e84d9386"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gela \u003cgmalekpour@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089899 - Part 2: Stop the save credit card prompt from confirming the security code. r=android-reviewers,Roger,twhite\n\nThe save and dismiss handling moves into onSaveClicked and onDismissClicked, and the check for a new or an already\nsaved card into checkIfCardIsNewOrSaved, so that the security code prompt can reuse them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341183\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/prompts/creditcard/CreditCardSaveDialogFragment.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/prompts/creditcard/CreditCardSaveDialogFragmentTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/docs/changelog.md"], "git_node": "032dffcf6fa30bc850166d992ab82b50fd9a389a", "git_parents": ["5ed9a51c9dcbf0b4b4952f8f229182bc603f3dbb"], "node": "42dfebd98249cc1ff95afcfb7dce324e9c02f279", "parents": ["5b59bd6c901c4e0a87859295e24ba51444a95159"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gela \u003cgmalekpour@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089899 - Part 3: Prompt user to save or update their CVV when they enter their credit card info r=android-reviewers,android-l10n-reviewers,Roger,twhite,flod\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340246\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/prompts/PromptFeature.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/prompts/creditcard/CreditCardDelegate.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/prompts/creditcard/CreditCardSaveDialogContent.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/prompts/creditcard/CreditCardSaveDialogFragment.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/prompts/dialog/PromptDialogFragment.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/res/values/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/prompts/PromptFeatureTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/prompts/creditcard/CreditCardSaveDialogFragmentTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/prompts/dialog/TestPromptFeature.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/docs/changelog.md"], "git_node": "c77d8f248cfeb2e29e29fb0ceb8a317dbe8126cb", "git_parents": ["032dffcf6fa30bc850166d992ab82b50fd9a389a"], "node": "65d6c7559eb31706b3678682ec1a7fb3105de298", "parents": ["42dfebd98249cc1ff95afcfb7dce324e9c02f279"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gela \u003cgmalekpour@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089899 - Part 4: Put the credit card security code prompt behind a Nimbus feature in Fenix. r=android-reviewers,geckoview-reviewers,Roger,tcampbell\n\nFenix passes the feature value to Gecko through the engine settings, so the secret settings toggle and an experiment always change both.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341184\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/engine-gecko/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/engine/gecko/GeckoEngine.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/engine-gecko/src/test/java/mozilla/components/browser/engine/gecko/GeckoEngineTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/engine/src/main/java/mozilla/components/concept/engine/Settings.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/engine/src/test/java/mozilla/components/concept/engine/SettingsTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/docs/changelog.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/nimbus.fml.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BaseBrowserFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Core.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/SecretSettingsFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/Settings.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/preference_keys.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/static_strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/xml/secret_settings_preferences.xml", "mobile/android/geckoview/api.txt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/GeckoRuntimeSettings.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/doc-files/CHANGELOG.md"], "git_node": "7e0a727de72ec9844140dd75d30f7cd9fb631d3c", "git_parents": ["c77d8f248cfeb2e29e29fb0ceb8a317dbe8126cb"], "node": "32238e338aceb47c741658afb922803ec8559a7a", "parents": ["65d6c7559eb31706b3678682ec1a7fb3105de298"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gela \u003cgmalekpour@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089899 - Part 5: Add an edit option on the credit card prompt r=android-reviewers,android-l10n-reviewers,android-build-system-reviewers,Roger,parker\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340247\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/prompts/creditcard/CreditCardEditContent.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/prompts/creditcard/CreditCardSaveDialogContent.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/prompts/creditcard/CreditCardSaveDialogFragment.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/res/values/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/prompts/creditcard/CreditCardEditContentTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/prompts/creditcard/CreditCardSaveDialogFragmentTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/docs/changelog.md"], "git_node": "1cfabaf9e5bb065d4dc71c287149f4d60e453712", "git_parents": ["7e0a727de72ec9844140dd75d30f7cd9fb631d3c"], "node": "af82e2173a565884dd4d66e91d17cc429d7ce47a", "parents": ["32238e338aceb47c741658afb922803ec8559a7a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gela \u003cgmalekpour@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089899 - Part 6: If user changes their CVV after autofill, prompt them to update their card info r=credential-management-reviewers,geckoview-reviewers,tcampbell,mtigley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340249\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/assets/www/cc_form.html", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/AutocompleteTest.kt", "toolkit/components/formautofill/android/FormAutofillStorage.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "714fb24d3169108ce56eb5ca803d8a4b7ab78704", "git_parents": ["1cfabaf9e5bb065d4dc71c287149f4d60e453712"], "node": "ce6df8ced8de08cc5b19e0602e3fc557dd41c125", "parents": ["af82e2173a565884dd4d66e91d17cc429d7ce47a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092815 - Annotate padding as unused. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343399\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLTypes.h"], "git_node": "67435de2a3a11a0d5c5451856ade2bb8d082831d", "git_parents": ["714fb24d3169108ce56eb5ca803d8a4b7ab78704"], "node": "af51d354cf6245091f19458059516c142d78ab9c", "parents": ["ce6df8ced8de08cc5b19e0602e3fc557dd41c125"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Abhishek Sharma \u003cabhishekcs@protonmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087784 - pt1. Introduce a tailJump MASM operation for jumps to call targets r=jandem,rhunt\n\nSome indirect jumps in the JIT transfer control to call targets, leaving the\ncurrent return address in place. Examples include chaining Baseline IC stubs\nand Wasm return calls. The tailJump MASM operation makes these transfers explicit.\n\nThis is needed to support forward-edge CFI, since call target landing pads may\nrestrict how they can be reached. On ARM64 with BTI, an indirect jump to a\ncall landing pad (BTI c) must go through x16 or x17.\n\nAdd a new --enable-js-hardware-indirect-targets option to enable IBT/BTI\nsupport. For now it routes the tailJump through x16/x17 on ARM64.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338531\n", "files": ["js/moz.configure", "js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.h", "js/src/jit/arm/MacroAssembler-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm64/Assembler-arm64.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm64/MacroAssembler-arm64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/mips-shared/MacroAssembler-mips-shared.cpp", "js/src/jit/riscv64/MacroAssembler-riscv64.cpp", "js/src/jit/wasm32/MacroAssembler-wasm32.cpp", "js/src/jit/x86-shared/MacroAssembler-x86-shared.cpp"], "git_node": "5415c199e1e3b268980d196818901ee8130a0f01", "git_parents": ["67435de2a3a11a0d5c5451856ade2bb8d082831d"], "node": "1f42b26922a3d8734b092220d01fc4a7ee8abc4e", "parents": ["af51d354cf6245091f19458059516c142d78ab9c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Abhishek Sharma \u003cabhishekcs@protonmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087784 - pt2. Use the tailJump MASM op across the JS and Wasm JIT r=jandem,rhunt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338532\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/BaselineCodeGen.cpp", "js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/SharedICHelpers-arm-inl.h", "js/src/jit/arm/SharedICHelpers-arm.h", "js/src/jit/arm64/SharedICHelpers-arm64-inl.h", "js/src/jit/arm64/SharedICHelpers-arm64.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/SharedICHelpers-loong64-inl.h", "js/src/jit/loong64/SharedICHelpers-loong64.h", "js/src/jit/mips-shared/SharedICHelpers-mips-shared-inl.h", "js/src/jit/mips-shared/SharedICHelpers-mips-shared.h", "js/src/jit/riscv64/SharedICHelpers-riscv64-inl.h", "js/src/jit/riscv64/SharedICHelpers-riscv64.h", "js/src/jit/x64/SharedICHelpers-x64-inl.h", "js/src/jit/x64/SharedICHelpers-x64.h", "js/src/jit/x86/SharedICHelpers-x86-inl.h", "js/src/jit/x86/SharedICHelpers-x86.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmBaselineCompile.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmStubs.cpp"], "git_node": "248127dfc5e5737e45fffc2f84370760a83455e3", "git_parents": ["5415c199e1e3b268980d196818901ee8130a0f01"], "node": "bc765b5da1cf9ce3369fd181f13cb2482190ae49", "parents": ["1f42b26922a3d8734b092220d01fc4a7ee8abc4e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064828: Hide the browser chrome, the menu bar and the Dock in kiosk mode on macOS. r=mac-reviewers,mossop,bradwerth\n\nKiosk mode has never hidden the toolbars on macOS, because hideNavToolbox() returns early unless browser.fullscreen.autohide is set and that pref is off by default there. A kiosk window offers no way to bring the chrome back, so it now collapses the toolbox whatever the pref says.\n\nHiding the menu bar and the Dock needs more. In macOS native fullscreen, moving the pointer to the top of the screen brings the menu bar back and moving it to the screen edge the Dock sits on brings the Dock back. Only the emulated fullscreen path calls nsCocoaUtils::HideOSChromeOnScreen(), so a locked down kiosk window opts out of native fullscreen. browser.kiosk.lockdown selects how far this goes and defaults to the full lockdown, which also blocks Cmd+Tab and Cmd+H. Quit and force quit are left alone so the machine can always be recovered.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328050\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/base/content/browser-fullScreenAndPointerLock.js", "browser/base/content/browser-init.js", "browser/base/content/test/browser-fullscreen/browser.toml", "browser/base/content/test/browser-fullscreen/browser_fullscreen_kiosk_lockdown.js", "widget/cocoa/nsCocoaUtils.h", "widget/cocoa/nsCocoaUtils.mm", "widget/cocoa/nsCocoaWindow.h", "widget/cocoa/nsCocoaWindow.mm", "widget/nsIWidget.h", "xpfe/appshell/AppWindow.cpp"], "git_node": "83a654a4a3be2d0b065d6ea3ca6e60881d3f1c10", "git_parents": ["248127dfc5e5737e45fffc2f84370760a83455e3"], "node": "3e2f0b6baaa8f5381a87d82896c43386185b2a2e", "parents": ["bc765b5da1cf9ce3369fd181f13cb2482190ae49"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794921400, "git_changesets": ["83a1ef1dd8aad72f7424de6b3e85252884cfa7a0", "40571803ce42521e03de3a7429e41df211fda0a3", "c09596f28056489bbd47a4054d4cb46e5872ec41", "d9de130bfd3b2956d8bdca60665d0655d1d0dcba", "40e7a6c44da0aa343795b62bd85f27d850ca7b1f", "5170b5461731bff4e60f93b58ed329cd3a939a94", "0f9f26fe2ba1e938179394469feb6ffeb77f7390", "aa2b30cbb905dd3a2f4f3c5f980247e0c65bf9d6", "2ffe034397053b84e05543a224ebb438c661abae", "80976b4a8517b3e3281aa055f06f4afd0cf36899", "24937bbd3e7cb89672ec8a0c0b25589363beb9f7", "8b99bafe541fb1dded3bbbaa1c56d55cdda1d235", "eb7f8e0212a07f435fbd390095af103955086a89", "ccfc796856313ad85a4d79ac6b7ec22cbb919d45", "c0013297402742bdc37cd0cf104ae989537dc080", "5ed9a51c9dcbf0b4b4952f8f229182bc603f3dbb", "032dffcf6fa30bc850166d992ab82b50fd9a389a", "c77d8f248cfeb2e29e29fb0ceb8a317dbe8126cb", "7e0a727de72ec9844140dd75d30f7cd9fb631d3c", "1cfabaf9e5bb065d4dc71c287149f4d60e453712", "714fb24d3169108ce56eb5ca803d8a4b7ab78704", "67435de2a3a11a0d5c5451856ade2bb8d082831d", "5415c199e1e3b268980d196818901ee8130a0f01", "248127dfc5e5737e45fffc2f84370760a83455e3", "83a654a4a3be2d0b065d6ea3ca6e60881d3f1c10"], "user": "archaeopteryx@coole-files.de"}, "45802": {"changesets": [{"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2092815 - Annotate padding as unused. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\" for causing build bustages at /WebGLTypes.h\n\nThis reverts commit 67435de2a3a11a0d5c5451856ade2bb8d082831d.\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLTypes.h"], "git_node": "77bdc2893ade1d2e9029d11fc4fe261fc310fe54", "git_parents": ["83a654a4a3be2d0b065d6ea3ca6e60881d3f1c10"], "node": "f685a69cdc831886b3dd8923b1a15e4da2b2ad2e", "parents": ["3e2f0b6baaa8f5381a87d82896c43386185b2a2e"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794921639, "git_changesets": ["77bdc2893ade1d2e9029d11fc4fe261fc310fe54"], "user": "archaeopteryx@coole-files.de"}, "45803": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging b1145b0710192f716be5f59f5b2dfeed650d5294 with FIREFOX_160_0_1_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "9134adbb207fd01830c7d7454e71d0972083bcfc", "git_parents": ["dd164223a80153fd038f855eff97925d389fedba"], "node": "cb67a717152c4206ff92aec3c94c7ff90f4f0d7f", "parents": ["115878f06de784652a2d3bddc3759fe464743e5f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794924419, "git_changesets": ["9134adbb207fd01830c7d7454e71d0972083bcfc"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45804": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mark Banner \u003cstandard8@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091674 - Change the Weave Service to be a class. r=sync-reviewers,markh\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341755\n", "files": ["services/sync/Weave.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "c5b484d61559abebd99a63b9c7563bfb7ba0d965", "git_parents": ["83a654a4a3be2d0b065d6ea3ca6e60881d3f1c10"], "node": "34e917558888fb03b4692ec782754f04a0a3b819", "parents": ["3e2f0b6baaa8f5381a87d82896c43386185b2a2e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Banner \u003cstandard8@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091674 - Change the Weave Service to be a singleton JS module rather than an XPCOM service. r=sync-reviewers,omc-reviewers,urlbar-reviewers,daleharvey,janerik,markh,aminomancer\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341756\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/browser-sync/head.js", "browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/browser/browser_trigger_listeners.js", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderRemoteTabs.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-UrlbarView/browser_resultTypes_display.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-engagementTelemetry/head.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-searchMode/browser_excludeResults.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-tabs/browser_remotetab.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-telemetry/browser_remotetab.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_remote_tabs.js", "services/fxaccounts/FxAccountsWebChannel.sys.mjs", "services/sync/Weave.sys.mjs", "services/sync/components.conf", "services/sync/modules/SyncedTabs.sys.mjs", "services/sync/modules/UIState.sys.mjs", "services/sync/modules/service.sys.mjs", "services/sync/modules/telemetry.sys.mjs", "services/sync/moz.build", "services/sync/tests/unit/test_service_startup.js", "services/sync/tests/unit/test_syncedtabs.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/app/TelemetryEnvironment.sys.mjs", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.modules.d.ts", "tools/lint/extra-js-modules/allowlist.txt"], "git_node": "e581c914fc5291e7a0b9dc0f6299cfde59b68c62", "git_parents": ["c5b484d61559abebd99a63b9c7563bfb7ba0d965"], "node": "5bceb0a213c0edf6ad01e8cf2376fc27c1d531bd", "parents": ["34e917558888fb03b4692ec782754f04a0a3b819"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Banner \u003cstandard8@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088023 - Fix configuration for ESLint jsx-a11y rules so that they are correctly applied. r=frontend-codestyle-reviewers,omc-reviewers,Dre,aminomancer,Gijs\n\nThis changes the rules to warnings for the current failures, with follow-ups filed for future.\n\nThis also centralises the configuration as it makes it easier to update in future patches.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338713\n", "files": ["browser/components/aboutwelcome/.eslintrc.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/.eslintrc.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/.eslintrc.mjs", "eslint-rollouts.config.mjs", "eslint.config.mjs"], "git_node": "b98207cd891bce1b7b1102003c1a919dad99c98b", "git_parents": ["e581c914fc5291e7a0b9dc0f6299cfde59b68c62"], "node": "fc7d3173e3710bcaeeb73f23e9f2e1c743aab325", "parents": ["5bceb0a213c0edf6ad01e8cf2376fc27c1d531bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Banner \u003cstandard8@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088404 - Centralise the eslint-plugin-react configuration into the main config. r=frontend-codestyle-reviewers,devtools-reviewers,omc-reviewers,Dre,nchevobbe,andhuang,mossop\n\nThis applies the rules more consistently across the projects where they are used and makes it easier for future updates.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339458\n", "files": ["browser/components/aboutwelcome/.eslintrc.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/.eslintrc.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/.eslintrc.mjs", "devtools/.eslintrc.mjs", "devtools/client/debugger/src/.eslintrc.mjs", "eslint.config.mjs"], "git_node": "229c7ea9040f3c3f5cc831a6a02d1b55612e20fe", "git_parents": ["b98207cd891bce1b7b1102003c1a919dad99c98b"], "node": "9f9463179cb3be75ddd38817d94e8428550e9e40", "parents": ["fc7d3173e3710bcaeeb73f23e9f2e1c743aab325"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Banner \u003cstandard8@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088404 - Change from eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y to eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y-x. r=frontend-codestyle-reviewers,omc-reviewers,Dre,andhuang,mossop\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339459\n", "files": ["browser/components/aboutwelcome/.eslintrc.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/ContentTiles.jsx", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/LinkParagraph.jsx", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/OnboardingVideo.jsx", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/SingleSelect.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/.eslintrc.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/ContextMenu/ContextMenu.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Spaces/Spaces.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/TopSites/TopSite.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/TopSites/TopSiteFormInput.jsx", "eslint-rollouts.config.mjs", "eslint.config.mjs", "package-lock.json", "package.json"], "git_node": "bb0e62278ab2330a06e65253999a66b32607c162", "git_parents": ["229c7ea9040f3c3f5cc831a6a02d1b55612e20fe"], "node": "ff42d2f284753b5e1b5d7dd9a14c39edf5d763b2", "parents": ["9f9463179cb3be75ddd38817d94e8428550e9e40"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Naz\u0131m Can Alt\u0131nova \u003ccanaltinova@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092491 - Send profiler JS source text through a single shared memory buffer over IPC. r=mstange,profiler-reviewers,ipc-reviewers\n\nThe JS source text and source map URL were written inline in the IPC message\nfor each entry, so profiles with many or large sources, or inline data: source\nmaps, could exceed IPC::Channel::kMaximumMessageSize. Now the source map URL and\nthe source text of all entries are packed into one BigBuffer after their\nmetadata, which goes through shared memory above BigBuffer::kShmemThreshold. If\nthat buffer can't be allocated, the sources are sent without them instead of\nfailing the whole message.\n\nThe shutdown profile size checks no longer count them against the IPC message\nlimit.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343092\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/ContentChild.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPChild.cpp", "ipc/glue/UtilityProcessChild.cpp", "tools/profiler/core/ProfileAdditionalInformation.cpp", "tools/profiler/gecko/ProfilerChild.cpp", "tools/profiler/public/ProfileAdditionalInformation.h", "tools/profiler/tests/browser/browser_test_feature_js_sources_retrieval.js"], "git_node": "51530bb1a2c5f2c67d49eebeaf2266fbb0a1f96c", "git_parents": ["bb0e62278ab2330a06e65253999a66b32607c162"], "node": "7faaeb684e5c0e1d9447bb8809b7a45a201c44b2", "parents": ["ff42d2f284753b5e1b5d7dd9a14c39edf5d763b2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2088404 - Change from eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y to eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y-x. r=frontend-codestyle-reviewers,omc-reviewers,Dre,andhuang,mossop\" for causing ES lint failures at Crossword/Crossword.jsx\n\nThis reverts commit bb0e62278ab2330a06e65253999a66b32607c162.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2088404 - Centralise the eslint-plugin-react configuration into the main config. r=frontend-codestyle-reviewers,devtools-reviewers,omc-reviewers,Dre,nchevobbe,andhuang,mossop\"\n\nThis reverts commit 229c7ea9040f3c3f5cc831a6a02d1b55612e20fe.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2088023 - Fix configuration for ESLint jsx-a11y rules so that they are correctly applied. r=frontend-codestyle-reviewers,omc-reviewers,Dre,aminomancer,Gijs\"\n\nThis reverts commit b98207cd891bce1b7b1102003c1a919dad99c98b.\n", "files": ["browser/components/aboutwelcome/.eslintrc.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/.eslintrc.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/ContentTiles.jsx", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/LinkParagraph.jsx", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/OnboardingVideo.jsx", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/SingleSelect.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/.eslintrc.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/ContextMenu/ContextMenu.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Spaces/Spaces.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/TopSites/TopSite.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/TopSites/TopSiteFormInput.jsx", "devtools/.eslintrc.mjs", "devtools/client/debugger/src/.eslintrc.mjs", "eslint-rollouts.config.mjs", "eslint.config.mjs", "package-lock.json", "package.json"], "git_node": "6407bf1fdb711310072e730d92bb826dd2c0368c", "git_parents": ["51530bb1a2c5f2c67d49eebeaf2266fbb0a1f96c"], "node": "7a5c54f57e785f4d0353862812b3948f3b41504f", "parents": ["7faaeb684e5c0e1d9447bb8809b7a45a201c44b2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092576 - Remove duplicated content from the contribution docs. r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,ahal\n\nThe quick reference, how_to_submit_a_patch, the reviewer checklist and contributing_to_mozilla repeated each other and reviews.md; link to the page that covers each topic instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342674\n", "files": ["docs/contributing/contributing_to_mozilla.md", "docs/contributing/contribution_quickref.md", "docs/contributing/how_to_submit_a_patch.md", "docs/contributing/reviewer_checklist.md", "docs/contributing/reviews.md", "docs/contributing/stack_quickref.md"], "git_node": "530e917e779b5d5d674109f1cc6f2e291a856015", "git_parents": ["6407bf1fdb711310072e730d92bb826dd2c0368c"], "node": "e5fe5e3abb8deb47779e4a34cc992b4e4738fcfe", "parents": ["7a5c54f57e785f4d0353862812b3948f3b41504f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092576 - Point the Android and GeckoView contributor docs to the central contribution docs.\n\nThey still described the GitHub workflow of the standalone repositories and Mercurial setup steps, and repeated the generic test, lint and review steps.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342675\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/README.md", "mobile/android/docs/geckoview/contributor/for-gecko-engineers.md", "mobile/android/docs/geckoview/contributor/geckoview-quick-start.md", "mobile/android/docs/index.md", "mobile/android/docs/shared/android/CONTRIBUTING.md", "mobile/android/docs/shared/android/CONTRIBUTING_code.md", "mobile/android/docs/shared/android/taskcluster_guide.md", "mobile/android/docs/shared/git_guide.md", "mobile/android/fenix/docs/Home.md", "mobile/android/fenix/docs/release-checklist.md"], "git_node": "d9200224ca56bd53474581b4b6460f5dcb88c31d", "git_parents": ["530e917e779b5d5d674109f1cc6f2e291a856015"], "node": "287719e08546902e965c75683e30dac03491e53b", "parents": ["e5fe5e3abb8deb47779e4a34cc992b4e4738fcfe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092576 - Remove the generic and Mercurial setup steps from the Marionette and geckodriver docs. r=webdriver-reviewers,jdescottes\n\nLink to the contributors' quick reference instead, keep a single copy of the Remote Protocol try instructions, and replace the hg.mozilla.org links.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342676\n", "files": ["remote/doc/Testing.md", "remote/doc/marionette/Building.md", "remote/doc/marionette/NewContributors.md", "remote/doc/marionette/Patches.md", "testing/geckodriver/README.md", "testing/geckodriver/doc/ARM.md"], "git_node": "147e7cdb4fb4796c130a2123fea11b92cd3cdd5f", "git_parents": ["d9200224ca56bd53474581b4b6460f5dcb88c31d"], "node": "8e1e090cca11f34da8aabeed985596b08bda0b94", "parents": ["287719e08546902e965c75683e30dac03491e53b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2092815 - Annotate padding as unused. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\" for causing build bustages at /WebGLTypes.h\n\nThis reverts commit 67435de2a3a11a0d5c5451856ade2bb8d082831d.\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLTypes.h"], "git_node": "f6ccf4106cb195443607eaa362ee6376fc7883fc", "git_parents": ["147e7cdb4fb4796c130a2123fea11b92cd3cdd5f"], "node": "53a731f1ba67029b2aadcf22c850d48b2a79b4bd", "parents": ["8e1e090cca11f34da8aabeed985596b08bda0b94"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090983 - Clear the HTTP cache after browser_webconsole_show_subresource_security_errors.js, r=devtools-reviewers,jdescottes.\n\nThis also lets the test run in test-verify again.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340947\n", "files": ["devtools/client/webconsole/test/browser/_webconsole_lz.toml", "devtools/client/webconsole/test/browser/browser_webconsole_show_subresource_security_errors.js"], "git_node": "5c728e15bf6f211b8641ef8933f451239ab90dae", "git_parents": ["f6ccf4106cb195443607eaa362ee6376fc7883fc"], "node": "08f6e91da9f43c6089b71969a515f6e304077c9b", "parents": ["53a731f1ba67029b2aadcf22c850d48b2a79b4bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090987 - Ignore closed windows in the allocation tracker's acceptGlobal, r=devtools-reviewers,bomsy.\n\nWhen an allocation test runs again in the same browser, windows of the\nprevious run's toolbox can still be waiting for GC. Their `top` getter\nthrows NS_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED, which broke `head.js` before the test started.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340948\n", "files": ["devtools/shared/test-helpers/allocation-tracker.js"], "git_node": "5c7092e6bbde04b45888212bfe6e9588e2f18e48", "git_parents": ["5c728e15bf6f211b8641ef8933f451239ab90dae"], "node": "67d322856b5515f5c436123240ecdc357189e009", "parents": ["08f6e91da9f43c6089b71969a515f6e304077c9b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090984 - Add an objects-manager actor to the content process target, r=devtools-reviewers,bomsy.\n\nWithout it, releasing the object grips of a content process target, as clearing the Browser Console does, fails with \"Can't find the actor ID for objects-manager\".\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340949\n", "files": ["devtools/server/actors/targets/content-process.js"], "git_node": "607689c969cc853d8bd0d65f4544a0e7009eff55", "git_parents": ["5c7092e6bbde04b45888212bfe6e9588e2f18e48"], "node": "cc483564d8db6327bed690e25814ca5409761158", "parents": ["67d322856b5515f5c436123240ecdc357189e009"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092274 - Reset the privateWindowRedesign exposure flag in browser_privatebrowsing_redesign_telemetry.js, r=nimbus-reviewers,beth.\n\nThe exposure timeout throws past closeWindow, so a second run also left\nits private window open (\"Found an unexpected browser window\").\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342341\n", "files": ["browser/components/privatebrowsing/test/browser/browser_privatebrowsing_redesign_telemetry.js"], "git_node": "e6e284e2c1f9ab5acf4776c3760408a0e34adace", "git_parents": ["607689c969cc853d8bd0d65f4544a0e7009eff55"], "node": "b4c1b84793c3f453ab4392a6f23f5e1570069aa6", "parents": ["cc483564d8db6327bed690e25814ca5409761158"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kershaw Chang \u003ckershaw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047860 - Compare the embedder policy when matching Early Hints preloads, r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342519\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/EarlyHintPreloader.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/loading/early-hints/coep-early-hints-none-final-require-corp.h2.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "1019e902a44fa85e61c4c8f553e2ecbae2cdd39c", "git_parents": ["e6e284e2c1f9ab5acf4776c3760408a0e34adace"], "node": "2a6daebf9fa85a7d4ca686dbeaae8d1540951d29", "parents": ["b4c1b84793c3f453ab4392a6f23f5e1570069aa6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081759 - Read credit cards from the Rust store without decrypting them unless a secret is needed r=joschmidt,credential-management-reviewers,NeilDeakin,mtigley,mossop,theidkamp\n\nEvery read from the Rust store decrypted every card, so with a primary\npassword set, listing cards prompted on every page with a card form.\n\nRecords are now built from CreditCardCandidates, which need no key, so\nlisting never prompts. The number and security code are read together\nthrough decryptFields, only to fill, edit, export or compare a card. A\nrecord reports a stored security code as hasSecurityCode.\n\nA submitted card is compared only against saved cards ending in the same\nfour digits, so offering to save a new card does not prompt either.\n\nThese no longer prompt: form detection, the autocomplete dropdown and its\npreview, the manage credit cards dialog, the settings payment methods list,\nthe save doorhanger for a new card, and the saved card counts used by\ntelemetry, ASRouter targeting and the profile deletion page. Filling,\nediting and saving a card still prompt.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334111\n", "files": ["browser/components/profiles/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/profiles/tests/browser/browser_delete_profile_page_locked_cards.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/content/manageDialog.mjs", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser_creditCard_primaryPassword.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_creditCard_capture_cvv.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_creditCard_cvv.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_creditCard_doorhanger_cvv.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_creditCard_fill_cancel_login.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_creditCard_telemetry_cvv.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/creditCard/browser_editCreditCardDialog_cvv.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/head.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_rustStoreShutdown.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_rust_autofill_credit_card_adapter.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_rust_autofill_credit_card_migration.js", "toolkit/components/formautofill/AutofillStorageMigrator.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillPreferences.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillStorageBase.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/ProfileAutoCompleteResult.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/RustAutofillAdapterBase.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/RustAutofillCreditCardStorage.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/RustAutofillStore.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/default/FormAutofillPrompter.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/default/FormAutofillStorage.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/shared/CreditCardRecord.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/shared/FormAutofillSection.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "23478a78ae24a81ce8dabd69099e98c6448f55d1", "git_parents": ["1019e902a44fa85e61c4c8f553e2ecbae2cdd39c"], "node": "94f4895b13c7d85b1ff2763babfe7ef63474ef3c", "parents": ["2a6daebf9fa85a7d4ca686dbeaae8d1540951d29"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan Varga \u003cjvarga@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086032 - Update the steps of the CSP script directives pre-request check to the current spec; r=tschuster\n\nThe spec has since moved the integrity check of the script directives\npre-request check into its own algorithm, \u00a76.7.2.4 Does integrity metadata\nmatch source list?, called in step 1.2, so 'strict-dynamic' became step 1.3.\n\nMove the check into DoesIntegrityMetadataMatchSourceList(), like\nDoesNonceMatchSourceList() for \u00a76.7.2.3, and update the step numbers in\nnsCSPDirective::permits(). The integrity expressions are still collected in\nthe existing loop over the source list, so the source list isn't walked again.\n\nNo functional change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341433\n", "files": ["dom/security/nsCSPUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "a6498802389c2b884f800e6341eeb58e124c88bc", "git_parents": ["23478a78ae24a81ce8dabd69099e98c6448f55d1"], "node": "892122da91c685a2861d329f6418f767bc737536", "parents": ["94f4895b13c7d85b1ff2763babfe7ef63474ef3c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dave Vandyke \u003ckzar@kzar.co.uk\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077408 - Fix handling of publicSuffix.getDomain options r=robwu\n\nThe \"allowPlainSuffix\" option should only apply to known eTLDs, so if an unknown\neTLD is passed to getDomain, the \"allowUnknownSuffix\" option should determine\nwhat is returned.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330807\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/extensions/child/ext-publicSuffix.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ext_publicSuffix.js"], "git_node": "60a29a558e37f1ed1cc2b335b4c8599f0c72f523", "git_parents": ["a6498802389c2b884f800e6341eeb58e124c88bc"], "node": "ff2125c49ec81e1a63b68cac69911e88a10ee420", "parents": ["892122da91c685a2861d329f6418f767bc737536"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Johannes Salas Schmidt \u003cjoschmidt@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090276 - Double the timeout of test_rust_autofill_address_migration.js. r=credential-management-reviewers,dimi\n\nThe test needs about 40 seconds in the chaos mode of test-verify, which comes close to the 60 seconds it gets there.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340918\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "abc4b155077ffd45dae96d51f2950f65ebd5a824", "git_parents": ["60a29a558e37f1ed1cc2b335b4c8599f0c72f523"], "node": "20258093d6de58f7b593fd6e2ced4b4390f38ad6", "parents": ["ff2125c49ec81e1a63b68cac69911e88a10ee420"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjfkthame@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1995428 - Reflow orthogonal table cell content after the table's height stretches the rows. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nThe content's inline-size spans the rows, so it must be laid out using the final row sizes\nfor text-align in orthogonal cells to work correctly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342891\n", "files": ["layout/tables/nsTableFrame.cpp", "layout/tables/nsTableRowGroupFrame.cpp", "layout/tables/nsTableRowGroupFrame.h", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/orthogonal-cell-rowspan-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/reference/orthogonal-cell-rowspan-004-ref.html"], "git_node": "3cedc6cfc66fdd95e6673cc5a8434f719d41f24e", "git_parents": ["abc4b155077ffd45dae96d51f2950f65ebd5a824"], "node": "872a287e563a717f3ef04b2f82dddbda56062d13", "parents": ["20258093d6de58f7b593fd6e2ced4b4390f38ad6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093229 - Add missing include to memory/replace/dmd/DMD.h r=emilio\n\nSo that the header becomes self-compilable.\n\nDifferen