e0743 with FIREFOX_153_8_0esr_BUILD1 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "0981d93f93536d90389518d439d77175401282fd", "git_parents": ["9134adbb207fd01830c7d7454e71d0972083bcfc"], "node": "5cd1c94cb57742a419296efca10693a8db32c532", "parents": ["cb67a717152c4206ff92aec3c94c7ff90f4f0d7f"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794951216, "git_changesets": ["0981d93f93536d90389518d439d77175401282fd"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45808": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 220e416288cf99375f47ed595fafa7fbb4166e52 with FIREFOX_115_46_0esr_BUILD1 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "a636d4a02150babf8fc9dc9ee594b327ac73e1ea", "git_parents": ["0981d93f93536d90389518d439d77175401282fd"], "node": "cd2ed85933a2be97fb4f061a131dc3ff02cd2154", "parents": ["5cd1c94cb57742a419296efca10693a8db32c532"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794951344, "git_changesets": ["a636d4a02150babf8fc9dc9ee594b327ac73e1ea"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45809": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging b1145b0710192f716be5f59f5b2dfeed650d5294 with FIREFOX-ANDROID_160_0_1_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "3b604583d0e73352f833a9ed6f43d9d3d4ca4090", "git_parents": ["a636d4a02150babf8fc9dc9ee594b327ac73e1ea"], "node": "eb8d4cd85a1e96a5ba48d7d9f8ebe6aee9ae71a0", "parents": ["cd2ed85933a2be97fb4f061a131dc3ff02cd2154"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794954674, "git_changesets": ["3b604583d0e73352f833a9ed6f43d9d3d4ca4090"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45810": {"changesets": [{"author": "Kyle Jones \u003ckjones@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093869 - Default undefined and 0 counts for tiles and spocs to 1 r=mconley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343388\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/DiscoveryStreamFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TopSitesFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/DiscoveryStreamFeed.test.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_TopSitesFeed.js"], "git_node": "9b6696ac6617e0b8f8df46a0b33fca7380fcb34e", "git_parents": ["cbf384d7d7170a19888a54e368a2a999a60cb754"], "node": "c86580a54bae4fbeb4df19c0018d89f7a91e449e", "parents": ["3d00ec09778a52d764f67e6d29ddca87270e5c7e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kalen Lu \u003cklu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088407 - Cap the autocomplete popup using --size-layout-xlarge and ellipsize long row labels. r=mtigley,desktop-theme-reviewers,credential-management-reviewers,emilio\n\nCap `richlistbox` at `max-width: var(--size-layout-xlarge)`.\nThe popup used to grow indefinitely to fit its widest row.\n\nSet `min-width: 0` on `autocomplete-row-item` and `.labels-container`.\nSo long entries no longer push the row past the popup edge and hide\nthe secondary action button. The `.label` ellipsis gets applied.\n\nGive `.description` the same ellipsis rules as `.label`, skipping\n`.smart-form-fill-sources`, so a long second line stays on one line.\n`.icon` and `.secondary-action` get `flex-shrink: 0` so only the text\nshrinks.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340471\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/autocomplete.css", "toolkit/components/satchel/autocomplete-row-item/autocomplete-row-item.css", "toolkit/components/satchel/test/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/satchel/test/browser/browser_popup_long_entries.js"], "git_node": "915e26f407365a00bf980a64ee4db37c40050bb6", "git_parents": ["9b6696ac6617e0b8f8df46a0b33fca7380fcb34e"], "node": "18ac8c71205b7806af1452642e8f6f70a1afb685", "parents": ["c86580a54bae4fbeb4df19c0018d89f7a91e449e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan Varga \u003cjvarga@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086032 - Use a constant for the CSP nonce-source prefix; r=tschuster\n\n'nonce- is the prefix of the nonce-source grammar, not a keyword-source. Use a\nconstant for it when parsing and serializing nonce-source expressions, rather\nthan its entry in the list of keywords.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342814\n", "files": ["dom/security/nsCSPParser.cpp", "dom/security/nsCSPUtils.cpp", "dom/security/nsCSPUtils.h"], "git_node": "ae6d0a7fd9797c2c0186a7a1e2d5d0a497109d6d", "git_parents": ["915e26f407365a00bf980a64ee4db37c40050bb6"], "node": "fad3aeeac9d09208c8ae85f34780a07b95933da4", "parents": ["18ac8c71205b7806af1452642e8f6f70a1afb685"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090955 - Make static-analysis a tier 1 task r=sylvestre\n\nSo that we no longer regress on those.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341378\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/source-test/clang.yml"], "git_node": "a0cde524c5d6c7ada9e09e6da05759c4aaaf8682", "git_parents": ["ae6d0a7fd9797c2c0186a7a1e2d5d0a497109d6d"], "node": "5beac1ff3e076d6acb26d2e1f6238d2cbe51a06a", "parents": ["fad3aeeac9d09208c8ae85f34780a07b95933da4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1914844 - Only take the IntervalSet::Add append fast path for intervals not starting before the last one. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nIntervalSet keeps its intervals sorted by mStart, with no two neighbours\ntouching within their fuzz.\n\nAdd() first merges aInterval into the last interval if TouchesOnRight(last),\ni.e. last.mStart \u003c= aInterval.mStart and the two touch within their fuzz.\nOtherwise it appended aInterval if RightOf(last), i.e.\nlast.mEnd - last.mFuzz \u003c= aInterval.mStart + aInterval.mFuzz. That only\ncompares against the end of last, so when last is shorter than the combined\nfuzz, an interval starting before last.mStart, possibly touching it, was\nappended after it, leaving the set unsorted and unmerged.\n\nIf last.mStart \u003c= aInterval.mStart and TouchesOnRight() failed, the two\nintervals don't touch. Since aInterval.mEnd \u003e= aInterval.mStart \u003e=\nlast.mStart and fuzz is non-negative, aInterval can't be to the left of last,\nso aInterval.mStart - aInterval.mFuzz \u003e last.mEnd + last.mFuzz, and it is\nalso to the right of every earlier interval. Appending it keeps the set\nnormalized. Intervals starting before last.mStart take the general path,\nwhich merges with Touches(). RightOf() then always holds, so it is now\nasserted.\n\nTrackBuffersManager's mSanitizedBufferedRanges is the only fuzzed set there.\nOnce unsorted, it no longer covered mBufferedRanges, and RemoveFrames built an\ninverted gap interval.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343555\n", "files": ["dom/media/Intervals.h", "dom/media/gtest/TestIntervalSet.cpp"], "git_node": "f505d8a9809137a372d5debcae9ffeed4482bc49", "git_parents": ["a0cde524c5d6c7ada9e09e6da05759c4aaaf8682"], "node": "84e7efc766cdc6efc78856f0890c170a00427e6c", "parents": ["5beac1ff3e076d6acb26d2e1f6238d2cbe51a06a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2094113 - Part 1: Remove VREventObserver::mIs2DView r=webidl,tschuster\n\nIt's never read by anyone, so it's fully redundant now.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343567\n", "files": ["dom/vr/VREventObserver.cpp", "dom/vr/VREventObserver.h"], "git_node": "1fd39f1db9e26899e36bc2627d80478f0df4a814", "git_parents": ["f505d8a9809137a372d5debcae9ffeed4482bc49"], "node": "157f40bc33cc64f1e7fdd5009a4ccbb5389c0596", "parents": ["84e7efc766cdc6efc78856f0890c170a00427e6c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2094113 - Part 2: Remove VRDisplayEvent and its callers r=webidl,tschuster\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343568\n", "files": ["dom/base/Navigator.cpp", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.cpp", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.h", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.cpp", "dom/vr/VRDisplayEvent.cpp", "dom/vr/VRDisplayEvent.h", "dom/vr/VREventObserver.cpp", "dom/vr/VREventObserver.h", "dom/vr/moz.build", "dom/webidl/VRDisplayEvent.webidl"], "git_node": "1c225b674f518f8cca0df7e1e2734d040636292b", "git_parents": ["1fd39f1db9e26899e36bc2627d80478f0df4a814"], "node": "5435495585fe39c313b2da527e17bce188b20811", "parents": ["157f40bc33cc64f1e7fdd5009a4ccbb5389c0596"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2094113 - Part 3: Remove Navigator::RequestVRPresentation r=webidl,tschuster\n\nNot only the parent patch emptied the implementation, turns out no one is using the function at all.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343569\n", "files": ["dom/base/Navigator.cpp", "dom/webidl/Navigator.webidl"], "git_node": "ebdfd8156ae3aa4705d822f0ac44d12a3da85bfc", "git_parents": ["1c225b674f518f8cca0df7e1e2734d040636292b"], "node": "2e3a65063c59df0aeba50e941ad0b7347bffbcf3", "parents": ["5435495585fe39c313b2da527e17bce188b20811"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2094162. r=layout-reviewers,dshin,jfkthame\n\nIn this case we're plain leaking a frame so seems hard to mitigate.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343571\n", "files": ["layout/generic/AbsoluteContainingBlock.cpp"], "git_node": "2f021d9e5fd3427348fda149f0f00a2c87f06b21", "git_parents": ["ebdfd8156ae3aa4705d822f0ac44d12a3da85bfc"], "node": "519705c7d5505e3678a9f30efd4f02f2d9bc13c8", "parents": ["2e3a65063c59df0aeba50e941ad0b7347bffbcf3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088968 - Only include the resource monitor's collection and profile writing in run-task images. r=mozbase-reviewers,taskgraph-reviewers,ahal\n\nrun-task's monitor doesn't interpret logs: monitors in the processes it\nspawns forward the markers they build. Keeping that code out of\nbasemonitor.py avoids rebuilding the docker images for changes to how\ntest logs are turned into markers.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339545\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/__init__.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/decision.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/test_transforms_job.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/job/run_task.py", "taskcluster/scripts/run_task_resource_monitor.py", "testing/mozbase/mozsystemmonitor/mozsystemmonitor/basemonitor.py", "testing/mozbase/mozsystemmonitor/mozsystemmonitor/resourcemonitor.py", "testing/mozbase/mozsystemmonitor/tests/test_resource_monitor.py"], "git_node": "34a70cd2cd3c4d0839d8ae521feab873988d886b", "git_parents": ["2f021d9e5fd3427348fda149f0f00a2c87f06b21"], "node": "8da835cfb0c3e76aad9afd1e82f25ca7922770af", "parents": ["519705c7d5505e3678a9f30efd4f02f2d9bc13c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088968 - Move the tests of BaseResourceMonitor to their own file. r=mozbase-reviewers,ahal\n\nThey now use BaseResourceMonitor rather than SystemResourceMonitor, so\nthat they check it works without the log interpretation.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341346\n", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozsystemmonitor/tests/manifest.toml", "testing/mozbase/mozsystemmonitor/tests/test_basemonitor.py", "testing/mozbase/mozsystemmonitor/tests/test_resource_monitor.py"], "git_node": "8cc938ff101fbec297580b4a8394e2b5043cf346", "git_parents": ["34a70cd2cd3c4d0839d8ae521feab873988d886b"], "node": "36d867d509b0546807aef5167d685afd55202055", "parents": ["8da835cfb0c3e76aad9afd1e82f25ca7922770af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088968 - Forward the marker schemas of the markers resource monitors forward to their parent. r=mozbase-reviewers,ahal\n\nThis lets the schemas of markers built from logs live next to the code\nbuilding them, so that adding one doesn't change basemonitor.py and\nrebuild the run-task docker images.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339546\n", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozsystemmonitor/mozsystemmonitor/basemonitor.py", "testing/mozbase/mozsystemmonitor/mozsystemmonitor/resourcemonitor.py", "testing/mozbase/mozsystemmonitor/tests/test_resource_monitor.py"], "git_node": "9c958ce493f6e0f5b9e81855962621249259928d", "git_parents": ["8cc938ff101fbec297580b4a8394e2b5043cf346"], "node": "97cc0e55ffe4cc00609d15768291a1b4659173b9", "parents": ["36d867d509b0546807aef5167d685afd55202055"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshi Cheng-Hao Huang \u003callstars.chh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092888 - Part 1: Restart normal module loads waiting on a preload fetch cancelled by an import map. r=jonco\n\nWith multiple import maps, a normal load may be waiting on a preload's fetch\nwhen an import map is registered. Restart it instead of cancelling it with the\npreload.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343513\n", "files": ["js/loader/ModuleLoaderBase.cpp"], "git_node": "ef0883bd4412a51e21fd2098ffdfa9d232d9fcac", "git_parents": ["9c958ce493f6e0f5b9e81855962621249259928d"], "node": "8e30d59728f38f07bb8bd7f3651684515c56d34c", "parents": ["97cc0e55ffe4cc00609d15768291a1b4659173b9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshi Cheng-Hao Huang \u003callstars.chh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092888 - Part 2: Test a dynamic import waiting on a modulepreload fetch when an import map is registered. r=jonco\n\nWith multiple import maps, a dynamic import may be waiting on a\n\u003clink rel=modulepreload\u003e's fetch when an import map is registered.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343514\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/jsmodules/importmaps/multiple/mochitest.toml", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/importmaps/multiple/preload_linked_helpers.js", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/importmaps/multiple/test_importMap_with_waiter_on_fetching_preload.html", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/importmaps/multiple/test_preload_linked_normal_deps_not_reset.html"], "git_node": "f7490971b183d7a9489ca0ca36f52e1164fd5d86", "git_parents": ["ef0883bd4412a51e21fd2098ffdfa9d232d9fcac"], "node": "30a6bf1095443be3817e0e8d891548791b0b0fce", "parents": ["8e30d59728f38f07bb8bd7f3651684515c56d34c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshi Cheng-Hao Huang \u003callstars.chh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092888 - Part 3: Test an import map parsed while an inline module waits on a modulepreload fetch. r=jonco\n\nWith multiple import maps, the parser may register an import map while an\ninline module is waiting on a \u003clink rel=modulepreload\u003e's fetch.\n\nThe test is from the website repoted from\nhttps://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2093524.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343515\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/jsmodules/importmaps/multiple/file_importMap_after_module_waiting_on_modulepreload.html", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/importmaps/multiple/mochitest.toml", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/importmaps/multiple/test_importMap_after_module_waiting_on_modulepreload.html"], "git_node": "1538a572fb5209052b1382fcb8d8b3b0f2d79bc0", "git_parents": ["f7490971b183d7a9489ca0ca36f52e1164fd5d86"], "node": "c8e155858294e5b83b50e24b1c120a231091233c", "parents": ["30a6bf1095443be3817e0e8d891548791b0b0fce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072337: Remove support for usrsctp. r=ng,decoder\n\nDoing this now so there's no need to modify this dead code to keep up\nwith the change to DataChannelConnect