 prunes in batches through deletePrunableRecords\n\nthe stores stop wrapping ensureDatabase in a catch that logged again and rethrew, since ensureDatabase already logs each failure\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342875\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/AGENTS.md", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AITabStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AIWindowConstants.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/ChatStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/ConversationStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/SQLiteStoreBase.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "d25e59cbc2245d82d18b0501b6361483b85d157c", "git_parents": ["78b3e1b5a322ba6252f1acc2861c0ab01fe73d03"], "node": "a0f7f7b23cf0d9313d12842da66c5fa8ef3d722c", "parents": ["03110c6d204a51b9469e4d358d3b0137f8c1878e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2080905 - Report the actual date range for imported history. r=jhirsch,migration-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,bolsson,mconley\" for causing failures at test_Safari_history.js.\n\nThis reverts commit 62df8029554b8095f34c82ad7510bd823cb80073.\n", "files": ["browser/components/migration/MigrationUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/migration/MigrationWizardParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/migration/MigratorBase.sys.mjs", "browser/components/migration/tests/unit/test_Chrome_history.js", "browser/components/migration/tests/unit/test_Safari_history.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/migrationWizard.ftl"], "git_node": "30d6d9080408a3d14260466923be0c71ea865216", "git_parents": ["d25e59cbc2245d82d18b0501b6361483b85d157c"], "node": "fd5869dbb1eefbefe8d22f5818d73f3817765f42", "parents": ["a0f7f7b23cf0d9313d12842da66c5fa8ef3d722c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093837 - Add WebRenderImageItemInfo and frame-based image key and push entry points. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nAdd WebRenderImageItemInfo, which carries what the image key and push\nhelpers used to read from a display item (frame, per-frame key, backface\nvisibility). CreateImageKey and PushImage take it instead of the item,\nCreateImageProviderKey takes the frame and per-frame key, and\nPushImageProvider gets a frame-based overload. nsImageRenderer,\nnsCSSRendering and nsCSSRenderingBorders take the info instead of the\nitem. Display items convert to the info implicitly, so behavior is\nunchanged.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343365\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderCommandBuilder.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderCommandBuilder.h", "layout/painting/nsCSSRendering.cpp", "layout/painting/nsCSSRendering.h", "layout/painting/nsCSSRenderingBorders.cpp", "layout/painting/nsCSSRenderingBorders.h", "layout/painting/nsImageRenderer.cpp", "layout/painting/nsImageRenderer.h"], "git_node": "bda12786434add7662ff9d6e0bf1be62aa222973", "git_parents": ["30d6d9080408a3d14260466923be0c71ea865216"], "node": "36fa537dbabbcc0b76e19a8358aa27107ffe267a", "parents": ["fd5869dbb1eefbefe8d22f5818d73f3817765f42"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Luca Greco \u003clgreco@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058271 r=robwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342302\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/extensions/ext-toolkit.json"], "git_node": "6facb2284c410170102e8275e550f4e4fa1f3c85", "git_parents": ["bda12786434add7662ff9d6e0bf1be62aa222973"], "node": "bfec0e614e317a09633fee5c2109b41df07621b7", "parents": ["36fa537dbabbcc0b76e19a8358aa27107ffe267a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ed Lee \u003cedilee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081891 - combine link previews anonymous requests with more attributes r=omarg\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343336\n", "files": ["browser/components/genai/LinkPreviewChild.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "514239dc421516b357485b62ea71802ca0c8ce51", "git_parents": ["6facb2284c410170102e8275e550f4e4fa1f3c85"], "node": "68894879399c6c7d28d2861f027cd65c1ba1b995", "parents": ["bfec0e614e317a09633fee5c2109b41df07621b7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "az \u003cazebrowski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091590 - Part 1: Restrict media decoder cloning. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343317\n", "files": ["dom/media/mediaelement/HTMLMediaElement.cpp"], "git_node": "cd18b112cdfa18c3f831ae675ada41ec514d8a68", "git_parents": ["514239dc421516b357485b62ea71802ca0c8ce51"], "node": "3e593e58bf5d9cc2f515f8ed555d8790dce58b6c", "parents": ["68894879399c6c7d28d2861f027cd65c1ba1b995"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Pages \u003cjpages@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2029617 - wasm: Move some wasm specific functions from MIR.cpp to MIR-wasm.cpp. r=bvisness\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328920\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/MIR-wasm.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR.cpp"], "git_node": "7dbbee460f3d150090b0af03a439a90222941b71", "git_parents": ["cd18b112cdfa18c3f831ae675ada41ec514d8a68"], "node": "1dea162b7cb2c352535b1f78ee0a8ba4755b9b67", "parents": ["3e593e58bf5d9cc2f515f8ed555d8790dce58b6c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Pages \u003cjpages@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2029617 - wasm: Rename keepAlive to wasmObject on MWasmLoadField and MWasmStoreField(Ref). r=bvisness\n\nThe wasmObject operand is the GC object owning the accessed location, and is\nnow the only source of type information for these instructions. Is it now non-optional, the base\noperand is only used as a raw pointer.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338184\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/Lowering.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR-wasm.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR-wasm.h", "js/src/jit/ScalarReplacement.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmIonCompile.cpp"], "git_node": "6caa27a93f7b9a8379d626c2aae020e961042156", "git_parents": ["7dbbee460f3d150090b0af03a439a90222941b71"], "node": "27278ea4e5581337c98aadf2c202656bb58fa741", "parents": ["1dea162b7cb2c352535b1f78ee0a8ba4755b9b67"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Pages \u003cjpages@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2029617 - wasm: Add MWasmLoadInternalField for the immutable internal fields of wasm GC objects. r=bvisness\n\nStruct out-of-line data pointers, array data pointers, array lengths and\nexception data pointers are never written by wasm code once the object has been\nallocated, so these loads get their own instruction with no alias set and no\nkeepalive operand.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338185\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/gc/ref-gvn.js", "js/src/jit/Lowering.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR-wasm.h", "js/src/jit/MIROps.yaml", "js/src/jit/WasmBCE.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmIonCompile.cpp"], "git_node": "ab1572b2b99394feac919777f339d3fc2258b92b", "git_parents": ["6caa27a93f7b9a8379d626c2aae020e961042156"], "node": "d1927d0e8169b65ddcb3dbcc189160e8dd269bda", "parents": ["27278ea4e5581337c98aadf2c202656bb58fa741"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Pages \u003cjpages@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2029617 - wasm: Support wasm gc struct loads forwarding in GVN. r=bvisness\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D297752\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/gc/ref-gvn.js", "js/src/jit/MIR-wasm.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR-wasm.h"], "git_node": "95dd7e6833c0218fc85c7cc77f1f736f3d9204a4", "git_parents": ["ab1572b2b99394feac919777f339d3fc2258b92b"], "node": "e868ea9b1e827b8405ff67d0ff445fe18385c77b", "parents": ["d1927d0e8169b65ddcb3dbcc189160e8dd269bda"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Pages \u003cjpages@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2029617 - Adding tests for wasm gc load forwarding pass. r=bvisness\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D297753\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/gc/load-forwarding.js"], "git_node": "e9e551b5ac83fa7cbb9f365ac96d95c3836a8dc4", "git_parents": ["95dd7e6833c0218fc85c7cc77f1f736f3d9204a4"], "node": "2d53cc342d879e739ea195c50b27470642e889f3", "parents": ["e868ea9b1e827b8405ff67d0ff445fe18385c77b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maxx Crawford \u003cmcrawford@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093279 - Keep chrome://global/skin/media/ alongside resource://content-accessible/media/ in the play/pause icons of New Tab r=mconley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343724\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamComponents/CardCarousel/CardCarousel.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/FocusTimer/FocusTimer.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/PrefsFeed.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "b06ca9f08bab306c697741ef958e79bec69325ef", "git_parents": ["e9e551b5ac83fa7cbb9f365ac96d95c3836a8dc4"], "node": "4d2071a08c2802d1ccc08f849a6bfdc0b9656a5f", "parents": ["2d53cc342d879e739ea195c50b27470642e889f3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088016 - Split large non-axis-aligned quads and skip oversized render tasks. r=gw\n\nNon-axis-aligned quads that need a mask always used the indirect strategy, which draws the whole primitive into a single render task. When the clipped surface rect exceeds the maximum render task size this panics in render_task_sanity_check.\n\nUse the tiled strategy for such primitives when they exceed the maximum task size, and skip any individual render task that is still too large.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343123\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs"], "git_node": "26fe610cb10b9fedfab0767747c51facb5274eac", "git_parents": ["b06ca9f08bab306c697741ef958e79bec69325ef"], "node": "042d88094cf6667877e846ba710b639b48ee6ad4", "parents": ["4d2071a08c2802d1ccc08f849a6bfdc0b9656a5f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093095 - Have `./mach buildtokens` regenerate the use-design-tokens checked-properties docs page. r=hjones,reusable-components-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342961\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/widgets/mach_commands.py"], "git_node": "5bddf5b7e8159460d0f61331c5b845145fb08e23", "git_parents": ["26fe610cb10b9fedfab0767747c51facb5274eac"], "node": "a55cc7391d2fc6e690b193dc920a9b86a472cc46", "parents": ["042d88094cf6667877e846ba710b639b48ee6ad4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092626 - Apply uniform rounded rect clips directly in the quad shaders. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nRounded rect clips always went through an intermediate render task where the\npattern is drawn and then masked. When the only clip that needs a mask is a\nrounded rect with the same circular radius in all corners, and both the\nprimitive and the clip map to device space with a scale and offset, the\ntextured, gradient and repeat quad shaders now apply the clip directly.\nLarge primitives keep the nine-patch split and draw their corners directly.\n\nWith this patch, solid rounded rects are no longer rendered using border\nprimitives. The justification for that was to avoid an extra render task,\nbut that hack came with other issues.\n\nMost but not all quad shaders now can apply a uniform rounded rect clip.\nThis is controlled by the presence of a WR_QUAD_ROUNDED_CLIP define in the\nshader. SWGL span shaders don't support this so for now this fast path is\ndisabled with SWGL (otherwise it would prevent the span shaders which would\ndo more harm than the good we get from the fast path).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342693\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/WebRenderAPI.cpp", "gfx/wr/webrender/res/ps_quad.glsl", "gfx/wr/webrender/res/ps_quad_gradient.glsl", "gfx/wr/webrender/res/ps_quad_repeat.glsl", "gfx/wr/webrender/res/ps_quad_textured.glsl", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/command_buffer.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/gpu_types.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/pattern/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_item.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/rounded-clip-direct-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/rounded-clip-direct.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/compositor-surface/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/compositor/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/compositor/rounded-corners-1.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/image/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/mask/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/parse_function.rs", "layout/reftests/bugs/reftest.list", "layout/svg/SVGGeometryFrame.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-masking/clip-path/animations/clip-path-animation-inherit.html.ini"], "git_node": "a05d304ff5bc0d1f106771f794e7b2ac6d35acf2", "git_parents": ["5bddf5b7e8159460d0f61331c5b845145fb08e23"], "node": "58f7f868b1c4817ac6e91180d8fca40c684afad6", "parents": ["a55cc7391d2fc6e690b193dc920a9b86a472cc46"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 962029 - Merge test_bug746272-1.html and test_bug746272-2.html into one self-contained test, r=dom-storage-reviewers,asuth.\n\ntest_bug746272-2.html read the items test_bug746272-1.html stored, so it failed whenever it didn't run right after it in the same browser (standalone jobs, skipped since bug 2026600). Do the removeItem on a fresh Storage object from an iframe instead of in a second test.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337701\n", "files": ["dom/tests/mochitest/localstorage/mochitest.toml", "dom/tests/mochitest/localstorage/test_bug746272-1.html", "dom/tests/mochitest/localstorage/test_bug746272-2.html", "dom/tests/mochitest/localstorage/test_bug746272.html"], "git_node": "f048ce1ecd8dbd7b20742372aa7db3f2a5cd70ca", "git_parents": ["a05d304ff5bc0d1f106771f794e7b2ac6d35acf2"], "node": "8f2decb4d57b95bc530853ab4d73ea059c6180eb", "parents": ["58f7f868b1c4817ac6e91180d8fca40c684afad6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Wisniewski \u003ctwisniewski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084993 - add a webcompat intervention for www.uol.com.br; r=ksenia,webcompat-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343733\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/data/interventions/2084993-uol.com.br.json", "browser/extensions/webcompat/injections/js/bug2084993-uol.com.br-fix-volume-slider.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/manifest.json", "testing/webcompat/interventions/tests/test_2084993_uol_com_br.py"], "git_node": "29f3f9f040566620f2e2e8fb3cef532c14725715", "git_parents": ["f048ce1ecd8dbd7b20742372aa7db3f2a5cd70ca"], "node": "b992d90c06ee1b769a08adaefab9cbf5a049a923", "parents": ["8f2decb4d57b95bc530853ab4d73ea059c6180eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Wisniewski \u003ctwisniewski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1878024 - remove our webcompat intervention for g1.globo.com account icons; r=ksenia,webcompat-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343734\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/data/interventions/1878024-g1.globo.com.json", "browser/extensions/webcompat/injections/js/bug1878024-g1.globo.com-fix-account-icon.js", "testing/webcompat/interventions/tests/test_1878024_g1_globo_com.py"], "git_node": "cc6a0cf0b752b36fa40810a58e915160ec90b5c8", "git_parents": ["29f3f9f040566620f2e2e8fb3cef532c14725715"], "node": "0959fe55ded342d840d0a47ee0a376b49869a1cf", "parents": ["b992d90c06ee1b769a08adaefab9cbf5a049a923"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Wisniewski \u003ctwisniewski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2074120 - improve console debug-logging for webcompat intervention startup messages on the Android remote-debugger; r=ksenia,webcompat-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343735\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/lib/logging.js"], "git_node": "8a29d00a6a20f80b81aa5d031cafc85061909488", "git_parents": ["cc6a0cf0b752b36fa40810a58e915160ec90b5c8"], "node": "90ae848447af2bdcac9cdfd9aa14278c9a3a1e9c", "parents": ["0959fe55ded342d840d0a47ee0a376b49869a1cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Thomas Wisniewski \u003ctwisniewski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1875540 - add a webcompat intervention for allstate.com; r=ksenia,webcompat-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343736\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/data/interventions/1875540-allstate.com.json", "browser/extensions/webcompat/preprocessed_intervention_files.mozbuild", "testing/webcompat/interventions/tests/test_1875540_allstate_com.py"], "git_node": "15be12047d539e3adf2be373ef0a89b0b6da9bff", "git_parents": ["8a29d00a6a20f80b81aa5d031cafc85061909488"], "node": "3fb3e3ee617ef5cc511e6397acb4964ac67225d8", "parents": ["90ae848447af2bdcac9cdfd9aa14278c9a3a1e9c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091496: Open a link from the About dialog in one window when no browser window is open. r=Gijs\n\nWith no browser window open, the handle-xul-text-link observer opens a new window asynchronously, but the caller checks linkHandled.data before that finishes and opens the link again in its own window. The observer now claims the link before it waits for the new window.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341549\n", "files": ["browser/components/BrowserGlue.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/tests/browser/browser_text_link_without_browser_window.js"], "git_node": "f15e15e14fdb9880df94ab4171f124c3664f3e63", "git_parents": ["15be12047d539e3adf2be373ef0a89b0b6da9bff"], "node": "3486ce2e201187f5261dda89a951d7a39f3f7216", "parents": ["3fb3e3ee617ef5cc511e6397acb4964ac67225d8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Tu \u003candrewtu335@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089979 - Give DecoderDoctorDiagnostics::mEvent a default initializer. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342439\n", "files": ["dom/media/doctor/DecoderDoctorDiagnostics.h"], "git_node": "be29768a0fd7793942bea00fd34373061ca845f8", "git_parents": ["f15e15e14fdb9880df94ab4171f124c3664f3e63"], "node": "b1a62859c570eea75589f5c691f3a8bbbc5eb00d", "parents": ["3486ce2e201187f5261dda89a951d7a39f3f7216"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2091590 - Part 1: Restrict media decoder cloning. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\" for causing failures at test_bug2079058.html.\n\nThis reverts commit cd18b112cdfa18c3f831ae675ada41ec514d8a68.\n", "files": ["dom/media/mediaelement/HTMLMediaElement.cpp"], "git_node": "73e9eaf502df1577af5134ec9052e93fc4d512a8", "git_parents": ["be29768a0fd7793942bea00fd34373061ca845f8"], "node": "824c3dcced6c9881646074d1daf13670553f5517", "parents": ["b1a62859c570eea75589f5c691f3a8bbbc5eb00d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Import translations from https://github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n CLOSED TREE\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-ro/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/addons/src/main/res/values-lv/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/addons/src/main/res/values-ro/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/importer/src/main/res/values-da/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/importer/src/main/res/values-ka/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/importer/src/main/res/values-ro/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/res/values-ro/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ar/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-co/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-da/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-fy-rNL/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-hy-rAM/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ka/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ro/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-sq/strings.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/values-lo/strings.xml"], "git_node": "b86afab148b7b6c32181ccf346bf071675b22e5b", "git_parents": ["73e9eaf502df1577af5134ec9052e93fc4d512a8"], "node": "542876e4bae2e20d052860458d31a616965a72b8", "parents": ["824c3dcced6c9881646074d1daf13670553f5517"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2091229 - Use Build.CPU_ABI again for the ABI that GeckoView passes to Gecko and crash reports. r=bustage\n\nFor an ARM build running translated on an x86 device, Android rewrites Build.CPU_ABI to the app's ABI but\nleaves Build.SUPPORTED_32_BIT_ABIS listing the host's, so Gecko was told x86 and loaded the wrong per-ABI\ndefault prefs.\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/gecko/mozglue/GeckoLoader.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/gecko/util/HardwareUtils.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/CrashReporter.java"], "git_node": "dd60a4c1fb7de25f6b4fa24b8d1dce91faf8e52d", "git_parents": ["b86afab148b7b6c32181ccf346bf071675b22e5b"], "node": "520f32ab3ab88dd172fa245296a1e6a5fda4600a", "parents": ["542876e4bae2e20d052860458d31a616965a72b8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge autoland to mozilla-central\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aitab_menu_triggers.js", "browser/extensions/webcompat/data/interventions/1878024-g1.globo.com.json", "browser/extensions/webcompat/injections/js/bug1878024-g1.globo.com-fix-account-icon.js", "dom/tests/mochitest/localstorage/test_bug746272-1.html", "dom/tests/mochitest/localstorage/test_bug746272-2.html", "testing/webcompat/interventions/tests/test_1878024_g1_globo_com.py", "third_party/rust/rustix/src/runtime.rs", "third_party/rust/rustix/src/static_assertions.rs"], "git_node": "524e4e57a3321306bc6f9e6fe8bb11a35287dae5", "git_parents": ["7d5d1e5f7a08e693636d192cd2415ae5e0f0ba34", "dd60a4c1fb7de25f6b4fa24b8d1dce91faf8e52d"], "node": "1038c442e5194e713080203d7767f99c87020978", "parents": ["d8629557d7601832802b4c26210e5c026a5aa88f", "520f32ab3ab88dd172fa245296a1e6a5fda4600a"], "tags": []}], "date": 1794973629, "git_changesets": ["ba5ea450d784ff949c86d9ea91b647605c607c05", "ad5922c4a04bead1b5a39e95f9711e6d734f4bf9", "ed53ee0fa55a9a5e4c3fea5cc0ab8bd1710c6a70", "cb34d0d1bb622c0eb72c5b5b53e4f582019ef609", "5055b4fc10a2246f98db5c7ed77a63edfdc19f67", "16d0549b3aefa6a97d122b75ac60f5cd8a1749fc", "80f5157e3420d0609ed7a025e8667da05228af18", "79ec4000542393ba16dd0687aff70e7432f9d453", "0fabfe64c973bfbe6a6dfaa42c73af22884ad9a6", "c158d2c38c310892041037f129f652c052aec6ac", "0ac748d4e5b7fa048f165f8abfcb2aefe2b099e8", "2ae9df4ca28f94d0b5913ab3aedf91a2e401d14a", "c9105d0f3f86036fffc6076deea30ca73f406898", "6c222978a78dffc8fb982ca62f0d069b27711506", "5c25eab23f51f6b24b66105b926d60d8dea7e76c", "7821005d6b7ab7068116e8e426c946328d3f3155", "62df8029554b8095f34c82ad7510bd823cb80073", "faf143cda942b3485e30c21ca03b6885422027d9", "63f37789d191b43917bad85a80dbc1be3c4d4af3", "2b9f461ea07512ed0827ebdfcb4796c3c6ee0d4b", "3701d626d73919fc6419f272330bb000942af092", "aa873b682a582a0e0632eb2ce2dbf05c47dcaabe", "0133535203d54857c9e151273777fc299b175305", "3b0b7eddf670a3e1b53a8ab5fb0e84da1ac43e60", "7d00a75f1194f5503c48b30b420bc710c485b6ad", "78b3e1b5a322ba6252f1acc2861c0ab01fe73d03", "d25e59cbc2245d82d18b0501b6361483b85d157c", "30d6d9080408a3d14260466923be0c71ea865216", "bda12786434add7662ff9d6e0bf1be62aa222973", "6facb2284c410170102e8275e550f4e4fa1f3c85", "514239dc421516b357485b62ea71802ca0c8ce51", "cd18b112cdfa18c3f831ae675ada41ec514d8a68", "7dbbee460f3d150090b0af03a439a90222941b71", "6caa27a93f7b9a8379d626c2aae020e961042156", "ab1572b2b99394feac919777f339d3fc2258b92b", "95dd7e6833c0218fc85c7cc77f1f736f3d9204a4", "e9e551b5ac83fa7cbb9f365ac96d95c3836a8dc4", "b06ca9f08bab306c697741ef958e79bec69325ef", "26fe610cb10b9fedfab0767747c51facb5274eac", "5bddf5b7e8159460d0f61331c5b845145fb08e23", "a05d304ff5bc0d1f106771f794e7b2ac6d35acf2", "f048ce1ecd8dbd7b20742372aa7db3f2a5cd70ca", "29f3f9f040566620f2e2e8fb3cef532c14725715", "cc6a0cf0b752b36fa40810a58e915160ec90b5c8", "8a29d00a6a20f80b81aa5d031cafc85061909488", "15be12047d539e3adf2be373ef0a89b0b6da9bff", "f15e15e14fdb9880df94ab4171f124c3664f3e63", "be29768a0fd7793942bea00fd34373061ca845f8", "73e9eaf502df1577af5134ec9052e93fc4d512a8", "b86afab148b7b6c32181ccf346bf071675b22e5b", "dd60a4c1fb7de25f6b4fa24b8d1dce91faf8e52d", "524e4e57a3321306bc6f9e6fe8bb11a35287dae5"], "user": "rperta@mozilla.com"}, "45813": {"changesets": [{"author": "Florian Zia \u003cfzia@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083046 - Part 1: Test Smart Window auto-model chat telemetry r=jlewis\n\nChoice events already report \"auto\" and request events the routed model, so no new extra is needed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341448\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_auto_model_telemetry.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "1161851ffb5246e27933cb3e7e4c8795b5f4ad04", "git_parents": ["dd60a4c1fb7de25f6b4fa24b8d1dce91faf8e52d"], "node": "9259ec3503a0a16baf2b65589ef692ce9496384a", "parents": ["520f32ab3ab88dd172fa245296a1e6a5fda4600a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Zia \u003cfzia@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083836 - Offer auto-model in the smartbar inline picker r=fluent-reviewers,cdipersio,bolsson,echa\n\nWhen browser.smartwindow.firstrun.singlePageWithAutoModel is enabled the inline model picker lists the auto-model option.\n\nTest steps:\n1. With a Smart Window open, set browser.smartwindow.firstrun.singlePageWithAutoModel to true: Auto appears first in the smartbar picker, marked Recommended.\n2. Pick Auto in a sidebar tab, then set the pref to false: the tab falls back to the default model and Auto leaves the list.\n3. Repeat in a full page Smart Window.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341449\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/Utils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-window/ai-window.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/input-model-select/input-model-select.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_smartbar_model_select.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/aiWindow.ftl"], "git_node": "b18ebf30419d396776a2f78ce2cb93c5fa4d451e", "git_parents": ["1161851ffb5246e27933cb3e7e4c8795b5f4ad04"], "node": "fa0bb537632b6b9de5087f86175ad0cd6b4c3a3e", "parents": ["9259ec3503a0a16baf2b65589ef692ce9496384a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Zia \u003cfzia@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083046 - Part 2: Report the inline model choice in Smart Window chat telemetry r=jlewis\n\nSubmit, response and client error events reported the global model choice. A tab that picked another model in the inline picker was reported with the default.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341767\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-window/ai-window.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_auto_model_telemetry.js"], "git_node": "82081e77c53a2dd4b9d190f34e32c543bfb30991", "git_parents": ["b18ebf30419d396776a2f78ce2cb93c5fa4d451e"], "node": "192a9a72dae0a62417508090a3d9c744a861b948", "parents": ["fa0bb537632b6b9de5087f86175ad0cd6b4c3a3e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Zia \u003cfzia@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083045 - Show the model in the Smart Window action log r=fluent-reviewers,mshillabeer,bolsson,czhou,ai-security-reviewers\n\nWhen the auto model is chosen the action log shows the model that has been selected for a response.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341768\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/PromptLoader.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/Utils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/openAIEngine.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-content/ai-chat-content.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-window/ai-window.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/ChatConversation.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_action_log_model.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_smartbar_model_select.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/head.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/aiWindowContent.ftl"], "git_node": "aa15bff7e204af3c1548bb05dfbef2fb64324093", "git_parents": ["82081e77c53a2dd4b9d190f34e32c543bfb30991"], "node": "c6a157c5c8e8397f23f1f0133cc705fcbd944392", "parents": ["192a9a72dae0a62417508090a3d9c744a861b948"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Zia \u003cfzia@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083045 - Always show the action log for the Auto model r=fluent-reviewers,czhou,flod\n\nReplies generated with the auto model selected always show the action log.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342595\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-content/ai-chat-content.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-window/ai-window.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aichat_content_loader_suppression.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_action_log_model.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/aiWindowContent.ftl"], "git_node": "c5c3c763e6a8ba7046d2b559660c9a195232fd30", "git_parents": ["aa15bff7e204af3c1548bb05dfbef2fb64324093"], "node": "c14c1519c097052ddd837609b0a3bdb38077f417", "parents": ["c6a157c5c8e8397f23f1f0133cc705fcbd944392"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090749 - Make resource://normandy-vendor not content-accessible. r=nimbus-reviewers,beth\n\nIts only consumer is about:studies which can just use it after the previous\npatch.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339321\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/normandy/jar.mn"], "git_node": "07a14c5675a8d9f560fd188b390cda1be1b8982a", "git_parents": ["c5c3c763e6a8ba7046d2b559660c9a195232fd30"], "node": "04df38e20a47def59708d1ef5edac9551271aee4", "parents": ["c14c1519c097052ddd837609b0a3bdb38077f417"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092317 - Clear the IndexedDB databases created by browser_forgetThisSite.js, r=dom-storage-reviewers,asuth.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342369\n", "files": ["dom/indexedDB/test/browser.toml", "dom/indexedDB/test/browser_forgetThisSite.js"], "git_node": "5ff9f89a34f5e7980e16a0b3f704d39929311407", "git_parents": ["07a14c5675a8d9f560fd188b390cda1be1b8982a"], "node": "0fceb4a8dd260a838208a6e78eb66e2905cbcaf7", "parents": ["04df38e20a47def59708d1ef5edac9551271aee4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "MoHan Zhang \u003cmzhang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092730 - Share the AITab source-text budget among tabs instead of splitting it evenly. r=rrando\n\nThe budget was 10,000 characters split evenly, so each of ten tabs got 1,000\ncharacters and facts further down a page never reached the model. A short or\nunreadable tab also held a full share that it did not use.\n\nRaise the budget to 25,000 characters and share it: a section shorter than an\neven share keeps all of its text, and the rest goes to the longer sections.\nTen long tabs now get about 2,500 characters each.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342811\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/aitab/AITab.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_aitab.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_aitab_budget.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "f4758ea3ba972a24d848f0b47afadfbbf6e4734a", "git_parents": ["5ff9f89a34f5e7980e16a0b3f704d39929311407"], "node": "ba5f32738ba3af867c0a479cc32b14c3219243ac", "parents": ["0fceb4a8dd260a838208a6e78eb66e2905cbcaf7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Halberstadt \u003cahal@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2094149 - DOT_GITHUB_OVERRIDE: Add workflow to prune stale dev branches. r=zeid,conduit-reviewers\n\nPushes to firefox-dev and firefox-dev-secure leave `user/` branches\nbehind that are never deleted, and jj users get a new one for every\nchange they push. Delete those whose head commit is older than the\nartifact expiry so the ref count stays bounded.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343552\n", "files": [".github/workflows/prune-try-branches.yml"], "git_node": "1e18aec39ea3a60d3475eb82163bc84e4b47ed6b", "git_parents": ["f4758ea3ba972a24d848f0b47afadfbbf6e4734a"], "node": "07c5218f0d68b1ebb2c451a7544ff8d93a50d819", "parents": ["ba5f32738ba3af867c0a479cc32b14c3219243ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Poon \u003cnpoon@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092620 - [HNT] If last tab is homepage and opening screen is set to last tab, don't open a new homepage tab on cold start r=android-reviewers,gl\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342691\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/Settings.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/SettingsTest.kt"], "git_node": "8115fe23518251ca389f962124908f2486365535", "git_parents": ["1e18aec39ea3a60d3475eb82163bc84e4b47ed6b"], "node": "c63a4c7b7836bc3563444dc3f9e667fc2637dc91", "parents": ["07c5218f0d68b1ebb2c451a7544ff8d93a50d819"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Poon \u003cnpoon@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073324 - [HNT] Change behavior of private browsing notification r=android-reviewers,gl\n\nPBM + foreground -\u003e delete private tabs + navigate to empty private tabs tray\nPBM + background -\u003e delete private tabs + navigate to the most recent normal browsing mode tab or a new normal homepage if none exist\nnormal browsing mode -\u003e delete private tabs\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342779\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/HomeActivity.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/intent/OpenTabsTrayIntentProcessor.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/session/PrivateNotificationService.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/intent/OpenTabsTrayIntentProcessorTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/session/PrivateNotificationServiceTest.kt"], "git_node": "a4f140c57ca9edd55d4d534782c62984cd79d5f7", "git_parents": ["8115fe23518251ca389f962124908f2486365535"], "node": "26c6346a6c5a60276cbf8a0ad4355a2c9eb0a223", "parents": ["c63a4c7b7836bc3563444dc3f9e667fc2637dc91"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vladimir Stepanov \u003cvstepanov@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076762 - Remove Cieara Meador and Chris Dupuis from Firefox:General triage rotation. r=kcochrane\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343703\n", "files": ["browser/base/triage.json"], "git_node": "05c831d441793c247dbcf7b668dea46c34c76fb1", "git_parents": ["a4f140c57ca9edd55d4d534782c62984cd79d5f7"], "node": "1a123a94870f2d74163c4d0a6ac982a70d0f8bc5", "parents": ["26c6346a6c5a60276cbf8a0ad4355a2c9eb0a223"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nina Pypchenko \u003cnpypchenko@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090258 - Part 1: Dragging a framed widget around can occasionally cause the framed site to reload r=fchasen\n\nMoving a widget in the widgets row, by dragging it or with the \"Move\"\nactions, no longer reloads the framed widgets. Crossword, Solitaire,\nTravel and Horoscopes keep their state when they move and when another\nwidget moves past them. Wrexham AFC still reloads, which the next patch\nin this stack fixes.\n\nEach widget sits in its own slot in the row, and a reorder moves the\nslots with `moveBefore`, which keeps an iframe loaded.\n\nThe animation at the end of a drop now eases the scale back along with\nthe rest of the glide, so the widget no longer snaps to its normal size\non the last frame.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343463\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Spaces/Spaces.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Widgets.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/_Widgets.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/_WidgetsRowAd.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/lib/OrderedSlots.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/lib/usePointerReorder.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Spaces.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/Widgets.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/lib/OrderedSlots.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/lib/usePointerReorder.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/jest-setup.mjs"], "git_node": "050c51c7135f5795ef6c257feb8c7c708eae3f1c", "git_parents": ["05c831d441793c247dbcf7b668dea46c34c76fb1"], "node": "8114d4c32aec9d6378f858286562deb962f34b95", "parents": ["1a123a94870f2d74163c4d0a6ac982a70d0f8bc5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nina Pypchenko \u003cnpypchenko@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090258 - Part 2: Stop moz-widget frames reloading when the widget is moved r=fchasen\n\nThe Wrexham AFC card, and any other moz-widget card, no longer reloads\nwhen it moves in the widgets row. Part 1 keeps the other framed widgets\nloaded on a reorder, and this part does the same for moz-widget cards.\n\nFirefox reloads an iframe that is inside a shadow root when an ancestor\nis moved with `moveBefore`, and it keeps an iframe in the light DOM\nloaded. A moz-widget now keeps its iframe outside its shadow root, in\nthe same `frame` slot that chrome documents already use for a\n`\u003cbrowser\u003e`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343464\n", "files": ["browser/components/widgets/content/moz-widget.css", "browser/components/widgets/content/moz-widget.mjs", "browser/components/widgets/tests/chrome/test_moz_widget.html"], "git_node": "615267205aa81fd3527093f50b9dac8f18155733", "git_parents": ["050c51c7135f5795ef6c257feb8c7c708eae3f1c"], "node": "7490404e33563a376364c67ef36d83c8c988b845", "parents": ["8114d4c32aec9d6378f858286562deb962f34b95"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083714 - Part 1: Set the eyedropper \"drawn\" attribute on the container element; r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nThe \"drawn\" attribute only lets DevTools tests know when the eyedropper has\ndrawn the screenshot of the page. It has no effect on the eyedropper itself.\n\nSetting it on the container element, rather than on the root element,\nkeeps this DevTools-only test hook out of the magnifier, so that the next\npatch can move the magnifier out to be shared without having to carry it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339286\n", "files": ["devtools/client/inspector/test/highlighter/browser_inspector_highlighter-eyedropper-clipboard.js", "devtools/client/inspector/test/highlighter/browser_inspector_highlighter-eyedropper-scroll.js", "devtools/server/actors/highlighters/eye-dropper.js"], "git_node": "ab43449cddab24b1d437c3867e9c55d0e161db3d", "git_parents": ["615267205aa81fd3527093f50b9dac8f18155733"], "node": "02a4f873c03cd78fdc323e003b14fa11698edbf8", "parents": ["7490404e33563a376364c67ef36d83c8c988b845"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083714 - Part 2: Move the DevTools eyedropper magnifier to toolkit; r=desktop-theme-reviewers,devtools-reviewers,emilio,nchevobbe,frontend-codestyle-reviewers,mossop\n\nSo that it can be shared with others. The behavior of the DevTools eyedropper\nis kept as is, except for its scrolling state handling:\n- The \"scrolling\" attribute of the eye-dropper-root element is renamed to\n  \"disabled\".\n- The magnifier is disabled until it is drawn with the new screenshot, rather\n  than until scrolling ends, as its screenshot is outdated until then.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339068\n", "files": [".stylelintrc.js", "devtools/client/inspector/test/highlighter/browser_inspector_highlighter-eyedropper-scroll.js", "devtools/server/actors/highlighters/css/highlighters.css", "devtools/server/actors/highlighters/eye-dropper.js", "toolkit/modules/EyeDropperMagnifier.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/moz.build", "toolkit/themes/moz.build", "toolkit/themes/shared/eyedropper-common.css"], "git_node": "f99c2e26fa57b0067485b2f24e1b9ffd5f079642", "git_parents": ["ab43449cddab24b1d437c3867e9c55d0e161db3d"], "node": "fcd23437e48bd45943cb2e5332615f03f6e14e1f", "parents": ["02a4f873c03cd78fdc323e003b14fa11698edbf8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083714 - Part 3: Support pickers not shown in a XUL panel in InputPickerParentCommon; r=emilio\n\nThis is for the eyedropper, which has no panel. Pickers now report through\ncallbacks rather than events dispatched on the panel.\n\nThis should not change the existing behavior.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335385\n", "files": ["toolkit/actors/InputPickerParentCommon.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/InputPickerPanelCommon.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "4e5fa7a212918c0801b63f8d3393b8581750c1a0", "git_parents": ["f99c2e26fa57b0067485b2f24e1b9ffd5f079642"], "node": "ff1d4a5b8a3d28b75bff771911386bf4616c8a8b", "parents": ["fcd23437e48bd45943cb2e5332615f03f6e14e1f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083714 - Part 4: Add initial implementation for eyedropper proposal; r=emilio,desktop-theme-reviewers,webidl,smaug,reusable-components-reviewers,mkennedy\n\nOpening the picker of an \u003cinput type=color eyedropper\u003e, behind the\ndom.input.color_eyedropper.enabled pref, shows an eyedropper over the page,\nusing the magnifier shared with the DevTools eyedropper, and the page is\ncaptured and sampled in the parent process.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335140\n", "files": [".stylelintrc.js", "dom/html/HTMLInputElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLInputElement.h", "dom/html/test/forms/mochitest.toml", "dom/html/test/forms/test_input_color_eyedropper.html", "dom/webidl/HTMLInputElement.webidl", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "toolkit/actors/ColorPickerChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/actors/EyeDropperChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/actors/EyeDropperParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/actors/moz.build", "toolkit/modules/ActorManagerParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/EyeDropper.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/EyeDropperMagnifier.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/moz.build", "toolkit/modules/tests/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/modules/tests/browser/browser_EyeDropper.js", "toolkit/modules/tests/browser/browser_EyeDropper_cancel.js", "toolkit/modules/tests/browser/head_EyeDropper.js", "toolkit/themes/shared/desktop-jar.inc.mn", "toolkit/themes/shared/eyedropper.css", "xpcom/ds/StaticAtoms.py"], "git_node": "46134b1809d2abe405faef11cb870415f447557a", "git_parents": ["4e5fa7a212918c0801b63f8d3393b8581750c1a0"], "node": "286c2ddda98ab9f4cea441e4c45764280bb53910", "parents": ["ff1d4a5b8a3d28b75bff771911386bf4616c8a8b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088446 - Use type-segregated slabs for the frame and display list arenas. r=layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nThis refactors the process-global pres arenas to achieve the following\ngoals:\n\n * No unbounded memory growth: Pages can be decommitted now, while still\n   reserved so that they don't get reused by other types. Note that we\n   still keep slab metadata around, but those are much smaller\n   allocations.\n\n * Better memory locality: Superblocks store a bunch of slabs, which are\n   close together, but can be used for different types each. Each slab\n   is only used for a single type over its lifetime, but this achieves\n   better memory locality between objects of the same type (before that\n   we relied on the allocation order).\n\nThe design is similar to LibPAS IsoHeaps. This is a decent speedometer\nimprovement and addresses some of the microbenchmark regressions that\nwe've seen from making the nsPresArenas process-global.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339496\n", "files": ["layout/base/PresShell.cpp", "layout/base/moz.build", "layout/base/nsPresArena.cpp", "layout/base/nsPresArena.h"], "git_node": "9d2f1e021f0ab77960cea5b54c1d0aa0a3116726", "git_parents": ["46134b1809d2abe405faef11cb870415f447557a"], "node": "7114614b071d7212f1b114f1524ac5b8792245b4", "parents": ["286c2ddda98ab9f4cea441e4c45764280bb53910"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ksenia Berezina \u003ckberezina@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092267 - Update ua_string rules and testing instruction; r=twisniewski,webcompat-reviewers,ai4dev-reviewers,jgraham,suhaib\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342328\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/AGENTS.md"], "git_node": "442fc08004722780d1068931d0f3bd5723e3e61b", "git_parents": ["9d2f1e021f0ab77960cea5b54c1d0aa0a3116726"], "node": "9cf4b3d5878149d7c98035d09d6543f7c9c54088", "parents": ["7114614b071d7212f1b114f1524ac5b8792245b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1952313 - Add the reported testcase r=m_kato\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343019\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/editing/crashtests/backcolor-style-element-in-head.html"], "git_node": "32707bddf8ae80e531af66ad769a4d20ebbc6e2c", "git_parents": ["442fc08004722780d1068931d0f3bd5723e3e61b"], "node": "64a16ee560489ffdea040318426b3ffb7c53a80f", "parents": ["9cf4b3d5878149d7c98035d09d6543f7c9c54088"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eitan Isaacson \u003ceitan@monotonous.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093151 - Update collapsed select value if option text changes. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,Jamie\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343219\n", "files": ["accessible/base/nsAccessibilityService.cpp", "accessible/generic/DocAccessible.cpp", "accessible/html/HTMLSelectAccessible.cpp", "accessible/html/HTMLSelectAccessible.h", "accessible/tests/browser/e10s/browser_caching_value.js"], "git_node": "e170ddd5abe6ad15652ff37ad56d7cc861e5c2cd", "git_parents": ["32707bddf8ae80e531af66ad769a4d20ebbc6e2c"], "node": "b990399fb1699dcc9b727dba3bee817a7affc52d", "parents": ["64a16ee560489ffdea040318426b3ffb7c53a80f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2083714 - Part 4: Add initial implementation for eyedropper proposal; r=emilio,desktop-theme-reviewers,webidl,smaug,reusable-components-reviewers,mkennedy\" for causing failures at browser_EyeDropper.js.\n\nThis reverts commit 46134b1809d2abe405faef11cb870415f447557a.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2083714 - Part 3: Support pickers not shown in a XUL panel in InputPickerParentCommon; r=emilio\"\n\nThis reverts commit 4e5fa7a212918c0801b63f8d3393b8581750c1a0.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2083714 - Part 2: Move the DevTools eyedropper magnifier to toolkit; r=desktop-theme-reviewers,devtools-reviewers,emilio,nchevobbe,frontend-codestyle-reviewers,mossop\"\n\nThis reverts commit f99c2e26fa57b0067485b2f24e1b9ffd5f079642.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2083714 - Part 1: Set the eyedropper \"drawn\" attribute on the container element; r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\"\n\nThis reverts commit ab43449cddab24b1d437c3867e9c55d0e161db3d.\n", "files": [".stylelintrc.js", "devtools/client/inspector/test/highlighter/browser_inspector_highlighter-eyedropper-clipboard.js", "devtools/client/inspector/test/highlighter/browser_inspector_highlighter-eyedropper-scroll.js", "devtools/server/actors/highlighters/css/highlighters.css", "devtools/server/actors/highlighters/eye-dropper.js", "dom/html/HTMLInputElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLInputElement.h", "dom/html/test/forms/mochitest.toml", "dom/html/test/forms/test_input_color_eyedropper.html", "dom/webidl/HTMLInputElement.webidl", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "toolkit/actors/ColorPickerChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/actors/EyeDropperChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/actors/EyeDropperParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/actors/InputPickerParentCommon.sys.mjs", "toolkit/actors/moz.build", "toolkit/modules/ActorManagerParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/EyeDropper.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/EyeDropperMagnifier.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/InputPickerPanelCommon.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/moz.build", "toolkit/modules/tests/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/modules/tests/browser/browser_EyeDropper.js", "toolkit/modules/tests/browser/browser_EyeDropper_cancel.js", "toolkit/modules/tests/browser/head_EyeDropper.js", "toolkit/themes/moz.build", "toolkit/themes/shared/desktop-jar.inc.mn", "toolkit/themes/shared/eyedropper-common.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/eyedropper.css", "xpcom/ds/StaticAtoms.py"], "git_node": "eec25622b95bcdbe75efd5de41eca63d4c54f827", "git_parents": ["e170ddd5abe6ad15652ff37ad56d7cc861e5c2cd"], "node": "ba4f97e5f7f7db94eec43f885ef2e98177bb58aa", "parents": ["b990399fb1699dcc9b727dba3bee817a7affc52d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2088446 - Use type-segregated slabs for the frame and display list arenas. r=layout-reviewers,dshin\" for causing failures at nsPresArena.cpp.\n\nThis reverts commit 9d2f1e021f0ab77960cea5b54c1d0aa0a3116726.\n", "files": ["layout/base/PresShell.cpp", "layout/base/moz.build", "layout/base/nsPresArena.cpp", "layout/base/nsPresArena.h"], "git_node": "b064f2ca548372606bdf8d6a5f0489fcf546115e", "git_parents": ["eec25622b95bcdbe75efd5de41eca63d4c54f827"], "node": "358f6fb5d13c1f1f951b37be6d828d45fa5242c9", "parents": ["ba4f97e5f7f7db94eec43f885ef2e98177bb58aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gela \u003cgmalekpour@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2094273 - Ignore Samsung FreecessController StrictMode violations in debug builds. r=android-reviewers,matt-tighe\n\nThis patch bypasses Samsung's app freezer reads /proc in system_server during startActivity, and the DiskReadViolation which is causing the debug builds to crash. This change does not impact non-debug builds at all because we do not throw DiskReadViolations elsewhere.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343673\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/perf/ThreadPenaltyDeathWithIgnoresListener.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/perf/ThreadPenaltyDeathWithIgnoresListenerTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/resources/FreecessControllerLogcat.txt"], "git_node": "fc449ea9f96371d85998a4a6f38e28cf5766f231", "git_parents": ["b064f2ca548372606bdf8d6a5f0489fcf546115e"], "node": "f6bee4c1281f2d0072b8280550d7ec4175e32f60", "parents": ["358f6fb5d13c1f1f951b37be6d828d45fa5242c9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069243 - Move Container Storage Layer into A-S - part 1 - Enable UniFFI-JS for fxcontainers on Android, r=bdk\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343171\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "docs/rust-components/developing-rust-components/uniffi.md", "dom/chrome-webidl/moz.build", "toolkit/components/moz.build", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/lib.rs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/moz.build", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/config.toml", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/src/lib.rs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/src/pipeline/namespaces.rs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/src/pipeline/nodes.rs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/src/pipeline/root.rs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/src/templates/cpp/FfiDefinitions.cpp", "toolkit/library/rust/shared/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/library/rust/shared/lib.rs"], "git_node": "15570f1f5c902494a20b2ebb2097ea75f0530453", "git_parents": ["fc449ea9f96371d85998a4a6f38e28cf5766f231"], "node": "4fc61d609a7398104b313770378ac7040aff25a7", "parents": ["f6bee4c1281f2d0072b8280550d7ec4175e32f60"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069243 - Move Container Storage Layer into A-S - part 2 - mach uniffi generate r=bdk\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343172\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/uniffi-js/GeneratedScaffolding.cpp"], "git_node": "4e556616af439923a2efd1e6daa2fc006262e194", "git_parents": ["15570f1f5c902494a20b2ebb2097ea75f0530453"], "node": "0b39ca80e94dca7f4711ea82ff0e1b3884507849", "parents": ["4fc61d609a7398104b313770378ac7040aff25a7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069243 - Move Container Storage Layer into A-S - part 3 - Add migration tests r=timhuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329039\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_migratedFile.js"], "git_node": "96b7a91d820a86c4c29fc6cb10c0cc2d0eecf60c", "git_parents": ["4e556616af439923a2efd1e6daa2fc006262e194"], "node": "fd5f965f03ad902f0b4b5e69cf5e7028943e25a1", "parents": ["0b39ca80e94dca7f4711ea82ff0e1b3884507849"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069243 - Move Container Storage Layer into A-S - part 4 - ContextualIdentityService r=timhuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329040\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/contextualidentity/ContextualIdentityService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_basic.js", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_containersStore.js", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_corruptedFile.js", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_migratedFile.js", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_siteAssociations.js", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/xpcshell.toml", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ext_contextual_identities.js"], "git_node": "377a282046065a2251af8dcb76a93d3ef151a838", "git_parents": ["96b7a91d820a86c4c29fc6cb10c0cc2d0eecf60c"], "node": "cc2472bdaeb15ed6608071d11cea7ff2f14a4389", "parents": ["fd5f965f03ad902f0b4b5e69cf5e7028943e25a1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tomislav Jovanovic \u003ctomica@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092345 - Enforce GuardSets for Host header rewrites. r=robwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343387\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/extensions/ExtensionDNR.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ext_dnr_modifyHeaders.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ext_webRequest_host.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/webrequest/WebRequest.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "2011304d5dde801df149532507310e91e3f949dc", "git_parents": ["377a282046065a2251af8dcb76a93d3ef151a838"], "node": "b7b9ae25e24e80cd0ae1b061d2a53822475d4a1b", "parents": ["cc2472bdaeb15ed6608071d11cea7ff2f14a4389"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2094386 - Allow LonghandsToSerialize to check for initial value regardless of pref. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\n`LonghandsToSerialize` serialization typically needs to check if longhands\nare set to their initial values.\n\nThis was specially tedious when a longhand is gated by a pref in Servo,\nbut not in Gecko. Because then the value will be wrapped in an `Option`\nonly in Servo.\n\nThis patch adds some helper methods that take care of that, simplifying\nthe code.\n\nNo behavior change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343762\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/properties/helpers.mako.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/shorthands.rs"], "git_node": "23d48a65eebe2cb7666a455e7558e3c1562323a9", "git_parents": ["2011304d5dde801df149532507310e91e3f949dc"], "node": "bb05b127e183396f7d9f4777657faa3fd9fdb6bf", "parents": ["b7b9ae25e24e80cd0ae1b061d2a53822475d4a1b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maxx Crawford \u003cmcrawford@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2094356 - Send the Travel widget frame an interaction_state action so it can move its hero text clear of the New   badge. r=Dre\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343744\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Travel/Travel.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/useFramedWidgetMessages.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/Travel.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/useFramedWidgetMessages.test.jsx"], "git_node": "630af3ada5173e57472b150d546f26d331c51235", "git_parents": ["23d48a65eebe2cb7666a455e7558e3c1562323a9"], "node": "c7e9c8fc3ac3bae19add2932ef27c307ad724c44", "parents": ["bb05b127e183396f7d9f4777657faa3fd9fdb6bf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maxx Crawford \u003cmcrawford@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2094355 - Pass the home region to the Travel widget frame in its URL fragment. r=Dre\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343745\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Travel/Travel.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/Travel.test.jsx"], "git_node": "8289e23c523afb9fbfef02b5c82432cc815d55ca", "git_parents": ["630af3ada5173e57472b150d546f26d331c51235"], "node": "4eb65b000eb7420946705971765a192ad022e92b", "parents": ["c7e9c8fc3ac3bae19add2932ef27c307ad724c44"], "tags": []}, {"author": "scottdowne \u003csdowne@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046943 - Fixing newtab blocked topics that don't have titles r=jbrown\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343213\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/