91c2bdc5d3b5bd5deae830a6ddb95415", "8dd6ef2d47fd03ecc4f38a3a8f2a82d4d517f23e", "cc3545d78e5d158bb29526e9b4ed9278e06f596d", "eddd109929a104b1dc526ff4d8b5651adfdda18c", "b0520a4696707fc72e19924360f39e333dba1200", "659e59eb6291aa607312584b89d1e9618393f275", "c7c242e07d4ef1ede9907dd466e3b2dfeb86e0de", "11aed36600cf627bd608b8d7d2a23fe6c0b947a2", "71ad0a71fa396878117c6d2981bee8fc5fd063ad", "566bd744b3a3dba1292e2e1ea252da5a57dc3f76", "2edf845c41d7d7b1f61898361be111ade3df2952", "4f55f34c22cf109fd8892aaa3454d682e4b164be", "8ed9d28bd4fce1b4eddcae2efb3de4a8401675d1", "a6ec9352545e446c457dd2ea697d00fbe2e62689", "8eb03a2c70d5f592b199c05f06b61e54d7334fc5", "b6de193c35e44269dd132a71534b75b03688aec9", "ac2a3adc8e7c3374f45b5c95e0f15b844be76b80", "7750f742b9433767f2ffa57ba81235e11fc9629e", "b54e3f1d48c005f39e532840b224646fd7b83f6a", "fa0e1bca0189d6a8d9ecd5379f324e31369cabe8", "98b7cf31f8354e71f5229ace0f8eca660eee8782", "4c56501ca2567456cb4d95900e0968b20eb2ce88", "9acfa3f9a913a6886164447cc1c72a58f1ae2373", "ad051a67437cf7e92d7f5aa7956f5050b6120eac", "20352bab997498e547a0d276380caa83c17029a0", "5d60c295ce8500b43d4daba2ca37a274bd181e9c", "d184f55acd6dc355224e3b4cd8bece869ca7852d", "335d8ff8a6daab1c64b5aeaab871f89a6fc5a179", "93b02a823ff8bfb9682fc0d315777a0f9a40f026", "54651e9be14e395323e95903a04472c1b4d8366e", "63d0a6cc20ee1dd78d7108cb3e786cb44291e824", "db9f8d8c770fb41ad61fb0d4177c7f7d35193019", "7449e38b05e5b7ce1498e18075cdeb6d0943c1ae", "4c24f734d8214b601bab49ad4df00ccc45fdbe4d"], "user": "agoloman@mozilla.com"}, "45814": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2094206 - Stop R8 from changing the field types of generated protobuf messages r=android-reviewers,pollymce\n\nR8 turned CustomizedMenuRecord.schemaVersion_ from an int into a boolean, while protobuf-lite still\nreads and writes it as a 4-byte int, past the end of the field. Nightly then closed shortly after\nlaunch when the menu had a saved customization.\n\nKeep the fields of generated protobuf-lite messages as they are.\nA customization saved by an affected build is ignored once, so the menu returns to its default\nlayout until it is saved again.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343849\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/proguard-rules.pro"], "git_node": "c4e127876a14691b9648ab42a82393de15c4aa20", "git_parents": ["4c24f734d8214b601bab49ad4df00ccc45fdbe4d"], "node": "8f5ddef610d7a95f7a6383682e374746979bba73", "parents": ["031b4a272ec8c9a7ce86f333fd03b9df945d43e7"], "tags": []}], "date": 1795003167, "git_changesets": ["c4e127876a14691b9648ab42a82393de15c4aa20"], "user": "agoloman@mozilla.com"}, "45815": {"changesets": [{"author": "Delia Pop \u003cdpop@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093533 - Create new verifyTabsTrayThreeDotMenuOptionsTest regression UI test for the efficiency framework r=mobiletest-reviewers,aaronmt\n\nInitially, the new verifyTabsTrayThreeDotMenuOptionsTest added an incoming nav edge TabDrawerPage \u2192 SettingsTabsPage (tray three-dot menu \u2192 \"Tab settings\"). That new edge was shorter (Home \u2192 TabDrawer \u2192 SettingsTabs, 2 edges) than the old path (Home \u2192 MainMenu \u2192 Settings \u2192 SettingsTabs, 3 edges), so the pathfinder started entering SettingsTabsPage via the tray for every settingsTabs.navigateToPage().\n\nBut SettingsTabsPage's only back edge was \u2192 SettingsPage via \"Navigate up\" \u2014 valid only when entered from Settings. Entered from the tray, back goes to the tray, so the SettingsPage NAVIGATION_READY checkpoint timed out. This silently broke the already-landed, untouched verifyThePrivacyReportItemTest.\n\n  The fix: gate the back edges by entry surface with a NavigationFact (TAB_SETTINGS_FROM_TRAY):\n  - tray entry edge provides the fact,\n  - the Settings \u2192 SettingsTabs entry edge invalidates it (clears any stale tray marker),\n  - the GO_BACK \u2192 SettingsPage edge forbids it,\n  - a new \u2192 TabDrawerPage PressBack edge requires + invalidates it.\n\nThe UI test successfully passed 25x on Firebase. https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&landoInstance=lando-prod-2025&landoCommitID=121264\nAll efficiency UI tests successfully passed 1x on Firebase. https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&landoInstance=lando-prod-2025&landoCommitID=121263\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343598\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/NavigationState.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/RecentlyClosedTabsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsTabsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/TabDrawerSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/TabbedBrowsingTest.kt"], "git_node": "a32cbdca6f2899ce8f72a95e93183215b2087cfa", "git_parents": ["4c24f734d8214b601bab49ad4df00ccc45fdbe4d"], "node": "310581596fdf12c75a8a7c905257b6a113667e99", "parents": ["031b4a272ec8c9a7ce86f333fd03b9df945d43e7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi Lee \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089931 - Drop credit cards that cannot be decrypted when migrating to the Rust store, instead of failing the migration. r=theidkamp,credential-management-reviewers,joschmidt\n\nA card whose number does not decrypt fails every migration attempt the same\nway, so the profile spends its whole retry budget and stays on the JSON store\nfor good. A number counts as undecryptable when OSKeyStore fails with\nNS_ERROR_FAILURE or NS_ERROR_INVALID_ARG; a cancelled unlock, a shutdown or\nany other export error still fails the attempt.\n\nCards that cannot be decrypted are left out, and the rest migrate, when either\nof these holds:\n\n- Another card's number decrypted in the same attempt. The key store works,\n  so the cards that fail were encrypted under a key it no longer holds.\n\n- Enough attempts have failed, as many as\n  extensions.formautofill.creditCards.storage.rust.dropUndecryptableAfterAttempts\n  says (3 by default), and the last of them failed to decrypt a card too. Of\n  the profiles that had failed three attempts and failed to decrypt again,\n  about 0.2% later migrated. Requiring the previous attempt to have failed\n  the same way keeps a first decryption failure after unrelated errors from\n  dropping cards; the attempts in a row that failed to decrypt are counted in\n  extensions.formautofill.creditCards.storage.rust.migrationUndecryptableAttempts,\n  which any other outcome clears.\n\nMAX_ATTEMPTS goes from 10 to 15. The second rule can take two attempts\npast the threshold to count a decryption failure and then act on it, so a\nprofile close to the cap when it updates, or one that already gave up at 10,\nstill gets them.\n\nDropping cards loses data a later attempt might have read, so it ships off\nand is turned on through the Nimbus feature\nautofill-credit-cards-drop-undecryptable: \"enabled\" sets\nextensions.formautofill.creditCards.storage.rust.dropUndecryptable and\n\"afterAttempts\" sets the attempt threshold.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343057\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser_storage_rust_nimbus.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_rust_autofill_credit_card_migration.js", "modules/libpref/init/all.js", "toolkit/components/formautofill/AutofillStorageMigrator.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml"], "git_node": "67e885fc3acd5ead9a9f6808413f4e913a323623", "git_parents": ["a32cbdca6f2899ce8f72a95e93183215b2087cfa"], "node": "0f2d3b1c91b39c24bbe72bba92d646c01ff726ca", "parents": ["310581596fdf12c75a8a7c905257b6a113667e99"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2094004 - Wait for the window to be resized back in browser_914138_widget_API_overflowable_toolbar.js, r=Gijs.\n\nThis also re-enables the test on Linux, skipped since bug 966190 as unreliable there.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343588\n", "files": ["browser/components/customizableui/test/browser.toml", "browser/components/customizableui/test/browser_914138_widget_API_overflowable_toolbar.js"], "git_node": "0d1f7ff9417b079d04bc8e00dfff8ec50430d69b", "git_parents": ["67e885fc3acd5ead9a9f6808413f4e913a323623"], "node": "81bdc44a2b7dd0f1ae1c2eb86f879c157e51d200", "parents": ["0f2d3b1c91b39c24bbe72bba92d646c01ff726ca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090986 - Evaluate in a new content process in browser_console_eager_eval_resolve.js, r=devtools-reviewers,bomsy.\n\nThe test needs ContentAreaDropListener.sys.mjs to be unloaded and Services.droppedLinkHandler to be unresolved. Its first run loads and resolves them for the rest of the parent process, so a second run in the same browser failed. A tab opened with forceNewProcess gives each run a process where neither has happened yet, which also allows running the test in verify mode. The content process console sandbox's Services goes through the same Services_Resolve hook as the parent process's, so the eager evaluation behavior tested is the same.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340950\n", "files": ["devtools/client/webconsole/test/browser/_browser_console.toml", "devtools/client/webconsole/test/browser/browser_console_eager_eval_resolve.js"], "git_node": "fb7eb0d295d6c13bd1c28027972f7fc767000867", "git_parents": ["0d1f7ff9417b079d04bc8e00dfff8ec50430d69b"], "node": "c58e85790193e7d8949a163ffcc8051a0eec9b8a", "parents": ["81bdc44a2b7dd0f1ae1c2eb86f879c157e51d200"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Banner \u003cstandard8@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2094364 - Fix tests setting the invalidation delay for writing search settings in tests in toolkit/components/search. r=search-reviewers,scunnane\n\nAlso fixes the settings test so that it tests with the correct delay, and sets the initialization status correctly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343743\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/search/tests/xpcshell/head_search.js", "toolkit/components/search/tests/xpcshell/test_settings.js"], "git_node": "20f5ed20077afe5dba3573698bd505524b5d2a87", "git_parents": ["fb7eb0d295d6c13bd1c28027972f7fc767000867"], "node": "328b6ccef3475904b1a93b0867f7ab57df3bf4e7", "parents": ["c58e85790193e7d8949a163ffcc8051a0eec9b8a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Karl Tomlinson \u003ckarlt+@karlt.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075986 catch overflow in filt_len rounding r=padenot,chunmin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331858\n", "files": ["media/libspeex_resampler/06_filter-length-rounding-overflow.patch", "media/libspeex_resampler/moz.yaml", "media/libspeex_resampler/src/resample.c"], "git_node": "2d6249cb79ff8698855abaec1999f14b104a6bbe", "git_parents": ["20f5ed20077afe5dba3573698bd505524b5d2a87"], "node": "5fed3a2394dab8dcd7f2457284c2e1a46a1df114", "parents": ["328b6ccef3475904b1a93b0867f7ab57df3bf4e7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073891 - Give the address bar context menu's Add search engine items accesskeys, and let the check cover that menu. r=urlbar-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,bolsson,daisuke\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342015\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-autofill/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-autofill/browser_inputField_contextmenu_dismissal.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/browser.ftl", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2073891_urlbar_add_engine_accesskeys.py"], "git_node": "8b7941d11018d65080eeaf84dbacadad4395fd14", "git_parents": ["2d6249cb79ff8698855abaec1999f14b104a6bbe"], "node": "b5a669d03b155ea9c9b4ac3d263ffcb73ffcbff2", "parents": ["5fed3a2394dab8dcd7f2457284c2e1a46a1df114"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073892 - Give the address bar result menu's commands accesskeys, and let the check cover that menu. r=urlbar-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,bolsson,daisuke\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342016\n", "files": ["browser/components/search/test/browser/browser_trending_suggestions.js", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderSearchSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/enUS-searchFeatures.ftl", "browser/components/urlbar/private/AddonSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/private/AmpSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/private/MDNSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/private/RealtimeSuggestProvider.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/private/WeatherSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/private/YelpSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-results/browser_acknowledgeFeedbackAndDismissal.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_splitbutton.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/quicksuggest/browser/browser_quicksuggest_realtime_flight_status.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/quicksuggest/browser/browser_quicksuggest_sports.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/browser.ftl", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2073892_urlbar_result_menu_accesskeys.py"], "git_node": "75bf1aa0672c6fe5e89ed430c82a110e3807a961", "git_parents": ["8b7941d11018d65080eeaf84dbacadad4395fd14"], "node": "1bd6a78d66ab425e33c6cc654d0ca4af0f8c8a85", "parents": ["b5a669d03b155ea9c9b4ac3d263ffcb73ffcbff2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eden Chuang \u003cechuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054633 - Validate RemoteWorkerDebugger registration and stop servicing rpc requests from out-of-process workers. r=dom-worker-reviewers,devtools-reviewers,jdescottes,asuth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333571\n", "files": ["devtools/server/connectors/worker-connector.js", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp", "dom/workers/WorkerDebugger.cpp", "dom/workers/nsIWorkerDebugger.idl", "dom/workers/remoteworkers/RemoteWorkerDebuggerManagerParent.cpp", "dom/workers/remoteworkers/RemoteWorkerDebuggerManagerParent.h", "dom/workers/remoteworkers/RemoteWorkerDebuggerParent.cpp", "dom/workers/remoteworkers/RemoteWorkerDebuggerParent.h", "dom/workers/remoteworkers/RemoteWorkerService.cpp"], "git_node": "59ad67f0633a4c418f7f6e0ea8c23e9216cd52c8", "git_parents": ["75bf1aa0672c6fe5e89ed430c82a110e3807a961"], "node": "d6db08e485a48e1346c5805c15f6ed05992109d3", "parents": ["1bd6a78d66ab425e33c6cc654d0ca4af0f8c8a85"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Karl Tomlinson \u003ckarlt+@karlt.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075986 handle resampler initialization failure in AudioSegment::Resample() r=chunmin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331859\n", "files": ["dom/media/AudioSegment.cpp", "dom/media/AudioSegment.h"], "git_node": "aba5706a39ec730ddfcd246099cd16e5a7f16faf", "git_parents": ["59ad67f0633a4c418f7f6e0ea8c23e9216cd52c8"], "node": "576983b0b52ca6b8235cc1100d1876eee1364d21", "parents": ["d6db08e485a48e1346c5805c15f6ed05992109d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Arnaud Bienner \u003cabienner@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090095 - Quota manager: turn on consistency check on release bulids too. r=dom-storage-reviewers,jari\n\nFrom telemetry, this proved to have reduce the number of users experimenting local storage underflows by a factor of ~4.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340401\n", "files": ["dom/quota/ActorsParent.cpp", "dom/quota/CommonMetadata.cpp", "dom/quota/CommonMetadata.h", "dom/quota/OriginInfo.cpp", "dom/quota/OriginInfo.h", "dom/quota/test/gtest/TestQuotaManager.cpp", "dom/quota/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "3ee4d0c1eaa0db9a820c97228f2f475b4ae2aa24", "git_parents": ["aba5706a39ec730ddfcd246099cd16e5a7f16faf"], "node": "40b9a01f7541db41167bf5975302355303299b88", "parents": ["576983b0b52ca6b8235cc1100d1876eee1364d21"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mathieu Leplatre \u003cmathieu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1979320 - Do not log empty list error if remote activity is disabled r=gbeckley,remote-settings-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343643\n", "files": ["services/settings/RemoteSettingsClient.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "e185618a1855f0338637d88ec8778c8cee3cc883", "git_parents": ["3ee4d0c1eaa0db9a820c97228f2f475b4ae2aa24"], "node": "b4a2fe377d3113f93e1e2970a5a55e0c6de10ad6", "parents": ["40b9a01f7541db41167bf5975302355303299b88"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060917 - Part 1: Make ::cue the block that holds the cue lines. r=emilio\n\nThe WebVTT spec applies ::cue to the list of WebVTT Node Objects, the block\nthat holds the cue lines, and applies its background properties to the WebVTT\ncue background box, the inline box around the cue text [1]. We applied ::cue\nto the inline box, and the block had a fixed font. Thus author ::cue rules could\nnot change the line height.\n\nNow the block is the ::cue element and takes all ::cue rules. The inline box\ninherits the background properties from it, and the ::cue block does not paint\nits own background. Thus the background is painted once, behind the text, and\nno new pseudo-element or cascade filter is necessary. The user agent defaults\nof the spec move to the ::cue rule in html.css [2]. These defaults include\ntext-wrap: balance and unicode-bidi: plaintext, so the old workaround that set\nplaintext late is removed.\n\nThe ::cue block keeps its position and size in its style attribute. Only\nprivileged code sets the style attribute of a pseudo-element, so the property\nrestrictions of pseudo-elements no longer apply to it. The cascade now decides\nonce for each rule whether the restriction applies, not for each declaration.\n\n[1] https://w3c.github.io/webvtt/#the-cue-pseudo-element\n[2] https://w3c.github.io/webvtt/#applying-css-properties\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342860\n", "files": ["dom/media/webvtt/vtt.sys.mjs", "layout/painting/nsDisplayList.cpp", "layout/style/res/html.css", "servo/components/style/properties/cascade.rs", "toolkit/themes/shared/media/videocontrols.css"], "git_node": "4f32185a21905b5a91edb60d08f0f1bc0502f61d", "git_parents": ["e185618a1855f0338637d88ec8778c8cee3cc883"], "node": "fb9924488e9d71877686ddf089c31ed7f7bd2c2f", "parents": ["b4a2fe377d3113f93e1e2970a5a55e0c6de10ad6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060917 - Part 2: Remove text-wrap from the properties that ::cue takes. r=emilio\n\nThe WebVTT spec lists the properties that apply to ::cue, and text-wrap is not\none of them [1]. We allowed the text-wrap shorthand there, so a page could turn\noff the text-wrap: balance default that the spec gives the cue [2].\n\nNow ::cue rules from pages drop text-wrap-style. text-wrap-mode still applies,\nbecause white-space is in the list and sets it.\n\nThe new reftest checks that a ::cue rule with text-wrap-style: stable does not\nchange the balanced lines of a cue.\n\n[1] https://w3c.github.io/webvtt/#the-cue-pseudo-element\n[2] https://w3c.github.io/webvtt/#applying-css-properties\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343393\n", "files": ["layout/style/test/property_database.js", "servo/components/style/properties/data.py", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/cue/text-wrap_not_allowed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/cue/text-wrap_not_allowed-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/cue/text-wrap_not_allowed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/support/three_words.vtt"], "git_node": "52fa35799975868e140523d16d362dbaa4e28304", "git_parents": ["4f32185a21905b5a91edb60d08f0f1bc0502f61d"], "node": "9259006d5cc042f5017ac245e1019d33cc372641", "parents": ["fb9924488e9d71877686ddf089c31ed7f7bd2c2f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060917 - Part 3: Update the expectations of the WebVTT reftests that ::cue now passes. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nPart 1 puts ::cue on the block that holds the cue lines, as the spec says [1].\nThus the cues have the correct position, size and line height, and many\nWebVTT reftests now pass.\n\nRemove the failure expectations of these tests. Some differ from their\nreferences by one colour level on some platforms, so they get fuzzy ranges.\ndom_override_cue_line.html still fails on Windows (bug 2088668), and\ninherit_values_from_media_element.html still fails on Android (bug 2088741).\nfontsize_smaller_than_container.tentative.html now fails, because its\nreference does not follow the spec [2].\n\n[1] https://w3c.github.io/webvtt/#the-cue-pseudo-element\n[2] https://github.com/w3c/webvtt/issues/530\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343394\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/dom_override_cue_line.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/evil/media_height_19.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/evil/size_90.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/evil/size_99.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/line_0_is_top.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/line_50_percent.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/one_line_cue_plus_wrapped_cue.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/portrait.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/cue/color_hex.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/cue/color_hsla.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/cue/color_rgba.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/cue/fontsize_smaller_than_container.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/cue/inherit_values_from_media_element.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/cue/outline_properties.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/cue/outline_shorthand.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/cue/white-space_pre-line_wrapped.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/cue_function/class_object/class_namespace.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/cue_function/voice_object/voice_namespace.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/cue_function/white-space_pre-line_wrapped.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/size_50.html.ini"], "git_node": "19033f3c6125427f40a2ed8a1cf2db6c7213b75d", "git_parents": ["52fa35799975868e140523d16d362dbaa4e28304"], "node": "14463f70ae92e6527f25ee45b9deb43208f84478", "parents": ["9259006d5cc042f5017ac245e1019d33cc372641"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060917 - Part 4: Test which cue boxes ::cue styles. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nCheck that the ::cue font reaches the block that holds the cue lines and sets\ntheir height, and that the ::cue background is painted only by the inline box\naround the cue text [1].\n\n[1] https://w3c.github.io/webvtt/#the-cue-pseudo-element\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342861\n", "files": ["dom/media/webvtt/test/mochitest/cue_layout_helpers.js", "dom/media/webvtt/test/mochitest/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/webvtt/test/mochitest/test_webvtt_cue_pseudo_element.html"], "git_node": "0e6093bf02ce379eca0a8d2d185a87c708222ca0", "git_parents": ["19033f3c6125427f40a2ed8a1cf2db6c7213b75d"], "node": "a7ec537f0685e2ad49f6c63590d6dccd0abbbc90", "parents": ["14463f70ae92e6527f25ee45b9deb43208f84478"], "tags": []}, {"author": "f3tch \u003cftech169@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1836288 - [wdspec] Add session not created error to the WebDriver BiDi client. r=Sasha,webdriver-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328600\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/tools/webdriver/webdriver/bidi/error.py"], "git_node": "317308e23045773bdec77615e4e57cc87c26940c", "git_parents": ["0e6093bf02ce379eca0a8d2d185a87c708222ca0"], "node": "5309256d734d9f94501ecd213d98efa1128f824b", "parents": ["a7ec537f0685e2ad49f6c63590d6dccd0abbbc90"], "tags": []}, {"author": "f3tch \u003cftech169@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1836288 - Implement capability matching for 'session.new' command. r=webdriver-reviewers,jdescottes,Sasha\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328480\n", "files": ["remote/jar.mn", "remote/shared/webdriver/BrowserVersion.sys.mjs", "remote/shared/webdriver/Capabilities.sys.mjs", "remote/shared/webdriver/test/xpcshell/test_BrowserVersion.js", "remote/shared/webdriver/test/xpcshell/test_Capabilities.js", "remote/shared/webdriver/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml", "remote/webdriver-bidi/WebDriverBiDiConnection.sys.mjs", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webdriver/bidi/session/new/matching.py.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/session/new/matching.py"], "git_node": "4a40a814a88ad1dd2304c5514f06567662308c36", "git_parents": ["317308e23045773bdec77615e4e57cc87c26940c"], "node": "b0afc1e1d58db1bcbe3cc234983baec831a5cc50", "parents": ["5309256d734d9f94501ecd213d98efa1128f824b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bob Owen \u003cbobowencode@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092415 - Disable native event processing in the GMP process on Windows. r=aosmond\n\nThe GMP process creates no windows and doesn't initialize COM, so it has\nno need for a native event loop. Having one means creating the hidden\nevent window on the sandbox's alternate desktop, which has failed on\nsome machines and crashed the GMP at startup in\nnsAppShell::StaticCreateEventWindow, breaking Widevine playback.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343639\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "44bb731162e857609a82ceef138590aba4ac6575", "git_parents": ["4a40a814a88ad1dd2304c5514f06567662308c36"], "node": "8ba058bb5870c252a71eda884356db65df32118f", "parents": ["b0afc1e1d58db1bcbe3cc234983baec831a5cc50"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Johan Lorenzo \u003cjlorenzo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089560 - part 1: Add Rocky Linux 8 and 10 images and install tests r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340371\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/el-base/Dockerfile", "taskcluster/docker/el-raw/Dockerfile", "taskcluster/kinds/docker-image/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/linux-install-test/kind.yml"], "git_node": "30104b3630d3f33927cfb2f7c56f034561b08b06", "git_parents": ["44bb731162e857609a82ceef138590aba4ac6575"], "node": "780da19085d1c839e6b307b9728f656bca3c8c3e", "parents": ["8ba058bb5870c252a71eda884356db65df32118f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Johan Lorenzo \u003cjlorenzo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089560 - part 2: Add AlmaLinux 8.10 and 10.2 images and install tests r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D340372\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/docker-image/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/linux-install-test/kind.yml"], "git_node": "a58310fb6b0648d82821051bdfa2df349d0cf9b8", "git_parents": ["30104b3630d3f33927cfb2f7c56f034561b08b06"], "node": "a576d649fe01a91cb9f1c52e0bf7d7899e4ed214", "parents": ["780da19085d1c839e6b307b9728f656bca3c8c3e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dave Townsend \u003cdtownsend@oxymoronical.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068016 - Load framed New Tab widgets only once the page has been shown r=Dre\n\nA framed widget's document (crossword, solitaire, horoscopes, travel, and moz-widget cards such as Wrexham AFC) reads its state when it loads, and nothing tells it about later changes. A preloaded newtab loaded these documents while hidden, so opening it showed the state from preload time, e.g. an unsolved crossword after solving it in another tab. Those stale documents could also send events, such as a repeat puzzle_completed.\n\nAdd `usePageShown()` and `useSrcAfterPageShown(src)` next to `usePageVisible`. Every framed widget now holds back its frame URL until the page has been visible once. This covers Crossword, Solitaire, Horoscopes and Travel, and MozWidgetCard, which also covers FramedWidgetCard and extension widgets. After that the frame stays loaded, so switching tabs does not reload it. `usePageVisible` now also re-reads the visibility once its listener is attached, so a page shown between render and that effect is not missed.\n\nTravel's 12s widget_ready timeout and the message listeners now start only once the frame actually loads, so a preloaded tab left unopened can no longer mark Travel unavailable. FramedWidgetCard passes a choice changed while hidden in the first URL it loads, because no frame exists yet to receive `location.replace()`.\n\nChoice for reviewers: frames load when the tab is shown instead of during preload. The alternative was to reload them on show, which would load twice and flash stale content. The trade-off is a short load delay for the widget frames when the tab opens.\n\nNot covered: a newtab that was already visible, then hidden, still keeps its loaded frame. Bug 2079357 (per-container state) is a separate storage-partitioning issue and is not fixed here.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342299\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Crossword/Crossword.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/FramedWidgetCard.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Horoscopes/Horoscopes.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/MozWidgetCard.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Solitaire/Solitaire.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Travel/Travel.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/usePageVisible.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_framed_widgets.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/Crossword.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/FramedWidgetCard.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/usePageVisible.test.jsx"], "git_node": "8bd3f87ef149c29bfc70d879a9a22c6cef07cf0d", "git_parents": ["a58310fb6b0648d82821051bdfa2df349d0cf9b8"], "node": "39832497d6ae59ba935cce34f0737389ecc3e57e", "parents": ["a576d649fe01a91cb9f1c52e0bf7d7899e4ed214"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082300 - futher expectation updates. r=Sasha\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343834\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-multisession.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encrypted-media/drm-mp4-playback-temporary-playduration-keystatus.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "e0ac72cf23c6d0b974b653cc2c9998b841574880", "git_parents": ["8bd3f87ef149c29bfc70d879a9a22c6cef07cf0d"], "node": "e22e903885438d454fe0e1b7759773676cbbb9fe", "parents": ["39832497d6ae59ba935cce34f0737389ecc3e57e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Titouan Thibaud \u003ctthibaud@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2094050 - Put \"Sync this device\" button in Account Settings behind the account-sync-decouple feature flag. r=android-reviewers,sfamisa\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343486\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/account/AccountSettingsFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/xml/account_settings_preferences.xml"], "git_node": "7444d2163d4c2b449a43297bde61a49552baa36a", "git_parents": ["e0ac72cf23c6d0b974b653cc2c9998b841574880"], "node": "374227b370f80cb15c02292d009538aef9a6c1b8", "parents": ["e22e903885438d454fe0e1b7759773676cbbb9fe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan Varga \u003cjvarga@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086032 - Compare CSP hashes without converting them to UTF-8; r=tschuster\n\nThe digest is base64, so it's ASCII. Compare the hash of the hash source with it\nwith EqualsASCII(), instead of converting the hash to UTF-8 for each comparison.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342529\n", "files": ["dom/security/nsCSPUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "a6cab5a8482c1a7608f8025919e0b5c187c18ea1", "git_parents": ["7444d2163d4c2b449a43297bde61a49552baa36a"], "node": "666fa4c5096f8149a22ee573c988aad50e3f4db9", "parents": ["374227b370f80cb15c02292d009538aef9a6c1b8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089155. Remove Legacy Telemetry instrumentation from ImageLib. r=chutten,gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nThese probes have been mirrored to Glean for over a year. The Glean metrics\nstay; only the Legacy definitions and the telemetry_mirror fields go.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343498\n", "files": ["image/SourceBuffer.h", "image/decoders/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Events.yaml", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Histograms.json", "toolkit/components/telemetry/histogram-allowlists.json"], "git_node": "c89f13bf6e68956c56271e3ce805b80a57933b0a", "git_parents": ["a6cab5a8482c1a7608f8025919e0b5c187c18ea1"], "node": "656203616c66de1bd799602ffb53b8c3bcca4132", "parents": ["666fa4c5096f8149a22ee573c988aad50e3f4db9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Graham \u003cjames@hoppipolla.co.uk\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088430 - Fix `packages.txt` actions in `\u003csite\u003e.txt` files r=ahochheiden\n\nThis was running into conflicting requirements; every file had to\nstart with a `requires-python` line, but there could only be one\n`requires-python` line in total.\n\nNow we skip any leading `requires-python` line when the parser is\ninvoked recursively.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339087\n", "files": ["python/mach/mach/requirements.py"], "git_node": "65cc91b2b74b2da01a04143982b45a030ba28119", "git_parents": ["c89f13bf6e68956c56271e3ce805b80a57933b0a"], "node": "d0af44bc51e76b5148ec4ff8457a5f5864f59e47", "parents": ["656203616c66de1bd799602ffb53b8c3bcca4132"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Graham \u003cjames@hoppipolla.co.uk\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088514 - Split wpt site into two, r=Sasha\n\nThings that actually run tests require some compiled dependencies which we can avoid\nin cases where we don't actually want to run the tests.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339472\n", "files": ["python/sites/wpt.txt", "python/sites/wptrunner.txt", "testing/web-platform/mach_commands.py", "testing/web-platform/sites/wpt-base.txt", "testing/web-platform/sites/wptrunner-extra.txt"], "git_node": "bb01e7342d8c51a8c3272bcf68aa7f75e790184e", "git_parents": ["65cc91b2b74b2da01a04143982b45a030ba28119"], "node": "c9e080ce9260ea0a614affcb07efa197af68af05", "parents": ["d0af44bc51e76b5148ec4ff8457a5f5864f59e47"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge autoland to mozilla-central\n", "files": [], "git_node": "e1bdb5893e652b10528c1e5422d3c90ff146b2da", "git_parents": ["c4e127876a14691b9648ab42a82393de15c4aa20", "bb01e7342d8c51a8c3272bcf68aa7f75e790184e"], "node": "a82b583fd69c7e09359742406d8fcbbc575ce2af", "parents": ["8f5ddef610d7a95f7a6383682e374746979bba73", "c9e080ce9260ea0a614affcb07efa197af68af05"], "tags": []}], "date": 1795007003, "git_changesets": ["a32cbdca6f2899ce8f72a95e93183215b2087cfa", "67e885fc3acd5ead9a9f6808413f4e913a323623", "0d1f7ff9417b079d04bc8e00dfff8ec50430d69b", "fb7eb0d295d6c13bd1c28027972f7fc767000867", "20f5ed20077afe5dba3573698bd505524b5d2a87", "2d6249cb79ff8698855abaec1999f14b104a6bbe", "8b7941d11018d65080eeaf84dbacadad4395fd14", "75bf1aa0672c6fe5e89ed430c82a110e3807a961", "59ad67f0633a4c418f7f6e0ea8c23e9216cd52c8", "aba5706a39ec730ddfcd246099cd16e5a7f16faf", "3ee4d0c1eaa0db9a820c97228f2f475b4ae2aa24", "e185618a1855f0338637d88ec8778c8cee3cc883", "4f32185a21905b5a91edb60d08f0f1bc0502f61d", "52fa35799975868e140523d16d362dbaa4e28304", "19033f3c6125427f40a2ed8a1cf2db6c7213b75d", "0e6093bf02ce379eca0a8d2d185a87c708222ca0", "317308e23045773bdec77615e4e57cc87c26940c", "4a40a814a88ad1dd2304c5514f06567662308c36", "44bb731162e857609a82ceef138590aba4ac6575", "30104b3630d3f33927cfb2f7c56f034561b08b06", "a58310fb6b0648d82821051bdfa2df349d0cf9b8", "8bd3f87ef149c29bfc70d879a9a22c6cef07cf0d", "e0ac72cf23c6d0b974b653cc2c9998b841574880", "7444d2163d4c2b449a43297bde61a49552baa36a", "a6cab5a8482c1a7608f8025919e0b5c187c18ea1", "c89f13bf6e68956c56271e3ce805b80a57933b0a", "65cc91b2b74b2da01a04143982b45a030ba28119", "bb01e7342d8c51a8c3272bcf68aa7f75e790184e", "e1bdb5893e652b10528c1e5422d3c90ff146b2da"], "user": "agoloman@mozilla.com"}, "45816": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging f120f5b476c257a5f63446a476768511ada722dc with FIREFOX-ANDROID_161_0b5_BUILD1 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "951f57e1a3b26bceff6f75249012dca8e9623f22", "git_parents": ["3b604583d0e73352f833a9ed6f43d9d3d4ca4090"], "node": "94afbd7737d588599f406f47619be8c74a103801", "parents": ["eb8d4cd85a1e96a5ba48d7d9f8ebe6aee9ae71a0"], "tags": []}], "date": 1795007271, "git_changesets": ["951f57e1a3b26bceff6f75249012dca8e9623f22"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45817": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging f120f5b476c257a5f63446a476768511ada722dc with DEVEDITION_161_0b5_BUILD1 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "809ba1b03a99df470c691fad51a002972d6ed71f", "git_parents": ["951f57e1a3b26bceff6f75249012dca8e9623f22"], "node": "a0e67b2f4610ab128eabde6a5b71fe795e17ee56", "parents": ["94afbd7737d588599f406f47619be8c74a103801"], "tags": []}], "date": 1795007337, "git_changesets": ["809ba1b03a99df470c691fad51a002972d6ed71f"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45818": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging f120f5b476c257a5f63446a476768511ada722dc with FIREFOX_161_0b5_BUILD1 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "893483c7f1f5628a05f5cb74a2bef3c36c16b85e", "git_parents": ["809ba1b03a99df470c691fad51a002972d6ed71f"], "node": "6dcc35fcbcd7b83991108cd3ccc8e0c147d8ca82", "parents": ["a0e67b2f4610ab128eabde6a5b71fe795e17ee56"], "tags": []}], "date": 1795007401, "git_changesets": ["893483c7f1f5628a05f5cb74a2bef3c36c16b85e"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45819": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging f120f5b476c257a5f63446a476768511ada722dc with FIREFOX-ANDROID_161_0b5_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "6e4c9e0519d3bac948b299be0eb5add567314aae", "git_parents": ["893483c7f1f5628a05f5cb74a2bef3c36c16b85e"], "node": "2a7ea3d78ab59cc514560ffd6aea1abaa019f331", "parents": ["6dcc35fcbcd7b83991108cd3ccc8e0c147d8ca82"], "tags": []}], "date": 1795009260, "git_changesets": ["6e4c9e0519d3bac948b299be0eb5add567314aae"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45820": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging f120f5b476c257a5f63446a476768511ada722dc with DEVEDITION_161_0b5_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "dae1d11f1029406736c95ebbf4df71308064ec3f", "git_parents": ["6e4c9e0519d3bac948b299be0eb5add567314aae"], "node": "c9a2b244f13f161a85e599cec0285c61e66be07c", "parents": ["2a7ea3d78ab59cc514560ffd6aea1abaa019f331"], "tags": []}], "date": 1795017367, "git_changesets": ["dae1d11f1029406736c95ebbf4df71308064ec3f"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45821": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging f120f5b476c257a5f63446a476768511ada722dc with FIREFOX_161_0b5_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "ef5d604471cc029b992ae8f2f300711dd4dd5333", "git_parents": ["dae1d11f1029406736c95ebbf4df71308064ec3f"], "node": "d05a30d368fed4b67ffaf9842238817a8b1467d4", "parents": ["c9a2b244f13f161a85e599cec0285c61e66be07c"], "tags": []}], "date": 1795017805, "git_changesets": ["ef5d604471cc029b992ae8f2f300711dd4dd5333"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45822": {"changesets": [{"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051256 - Part 2: Route setHTMLUnsafe() without a sanitizer through SetAndFilterHTML r=tschuster\n\nsetHTMLUnsafe() has a separate fast path when no sanitizer is passed, and it\nparses differently from the default path: it disallows declarative shadow roots\nand ignores the document's quirks mode.\n\nThis change deletes the fast path; SetAndFilterHTML now takes nullable sanitizer\noptions where `null` is the spec's permissive default. The fast path no longer\nmatters now we sanitize while parsing. Privileged documents now get declarative\nshadow roots on this path, so nsTreeSanitizer also sanitizes shadow roots.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328182\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp", "dom/base/nsContentUtils.h", "dom/base/nsTreeSanitizer.cpp", "dom/base/test/test_fragment_sanitization.xhtml", "parser/html/nsHtml5TreeBuilderCppSupplement.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/sanitizer-api/sethtml-with-declarative-shadow-root.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/sethtml-quirks-mode.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/sanitizer-api/sethtml-with-declarative-shadow-root.html"], "git_node": "2b57d3c7506d7a18e0279d290feb488c0be5078f", "git_parents": ["bb01e7342d8c51a8c3272bcf68aa7f75e790184e"], "node": "b3585e0bd839c4e9a6b9da7149f8e967c51fb1fa", "parents": ["c9e080ce9260ea0a614affcb07efa197af68af05"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2094206 - Stop R8 from changing the field types of generated protobuf messages r=android-reviewers,pollymce\n\nR8 turned CustomizedMenuRecord.schemaVersion_ from an int into a boolean, while protobuf-lite still\nreads and writes it as a 4-byte int, past the end of the field. Nightly then closed shortly after\nlaunch when the menu had a saved customization.\n\nKeep the fields of generated protobuf-lite messages as they are.\nA customization saved by an affected build is ignored once, so the menu returns to its default\nlayout until it is saved again.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343849\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/proguard-rules.pro"], "git_node": "16fb0b388c0ca93d651a0369d15f56dac0c6380a", "git_parents": ["2b57d3c7506d7a18e0279d290feb488c0be5078f"], "node": "106516416d55880c422e91df85b1b3ec656af58f", "parents": ["b3585e0bd839c4e9a6b9da7149f8e967c51fb1fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matt Menke \u003cmmenke@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092448 [wpt PR 64564] - Remove test that depends on successful navigation to invalid host name., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRemove test that depends on successful navigation to invalid host name.\n\nblink/web_tests/http/tests/security/document-domain-canonicalizes.html\ndepends on navigating to an HTTP URL with an invalid host name\nsucceeding, due to injecting a successful DNS resolution for that name,\neven though such a DNS resolution should always fail.\n\nThis CL removes that test, and reworks some other tests to provide the\ntest coverage it was meant to provide. This is in preparation for\nmaking navigations to such a URL fail.\n\nThis is a partial reland of\nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8680296,\nwhich was reverted for reasons unrelated to this part of it.\n\nBug: 579450551\nChange-Id: Id7e0e74844005652198643a5c24e082477613ff1\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8690858\nReviewed-by: Tom Sepez \u003ctsepez@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Adam Rice \u003cricea@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: mmenke \u003cmmenke@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1733211}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: be48d4dabb11ef7c55877830d0f8abc913daeb8c\nwpt-pr: 64564\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/origin/relaxing-the-same-origin-restriction/document_domain_setter.html"], "git_node": "60092e345a044cc2bcfe554d56639eda64081584", "git_parents": ["16fb0b388c0ca93d651a0369d15f56dac0c6380a"], "node": "926da536e802c0248e3ac3de412ba6b052a5972f", "parents": ["106516416d55880c422e91df85b1b3ec656af58f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092449 [wpt PR 64570] - [css-mixins] Derive CSSPrivateRule from CSSStyleRule (2.5/N), a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-mixins] Derive CSSPrivateRule from CSSStyleRule (2.5/N)\n\nCSSPrivateRule was introduced as a CSSRule subclass in\nhttps://crrev.com/c/8222046. This CL instead derives it from\nCSSStyleRule, following the CSSOM proposal[0].\n\nSince @private has no selector, selectorText returns an empty string and\nassigning to it has no effect. The inherited style and styleMap APIs\nexpose and mutate declarations in the @private block, translating\nhygienic names through the stylesheet registry introduced by\nhttps://crrev.com/c/8508326.\n\n[0] https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14427\n\nLow-Coverage-Reason: COVERAGE_UNDERREPORTED\nBug: 542651959\nChange-Id: I7f80b533e39528eacf9dd896018f6f54b56019cf\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8415090\nCommit-Queue: Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kevin Babbitt \u003ckbabbitt@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1733341}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 08b65bc5e9b2de475d50a61c5d74905048765b6a\nwpt-pr: 64570\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/private/private-cssom-style-api.tentative.html"], "git_node": "76efd13d6e02aea97d99637af2115764f2afaa6d", "git_parents": ["60092e345a044cc2bcfe554d56639eda64081584"], "node": "7c81aa29abbf32b8d6d3d69854c87d4bda3d2af5", "parents": ["926da536e802c0248e3ac3de412ba6b052a5972f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092449 [wpt PR 64570] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64570\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-mixins/private/private-cssom-style-api.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "99c45e977127ca785a171259f9ceec078591aeda", "git_parents": ["76efd13d6e02aea97d99637af2115764f2afaa6d"], "node": "2acc5404cc8e212486235b25c7ca9b904f3174ba", "parents": ["7c81aa29abbf32b8d6d3d69854c87d4bda3d2af5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092451 [wpt PR 64537] - Fix invalidation on natural size change with non-fixed sizes, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix invalidation on natural size change with non-fixed sizes\n\nThis patch updates LayoutImage::NeedsLayoutOnNaturalSizeChange() to\ncheck LogicalMinHeight() and LogicalMaxHeight() in addition to\nLogicalMinWidth() and LogicalMaxWidth(), ensuring images with\nintrinsic or non-fixed block-axis min/max constraints relayout when\ntheir natural dimensions change.\n\nThis patch was inspired by https://commits.webkit.org/310885@main by\nAhmad Saleem.\n\nChange-Id: Ifaddce66a57beb71ee262979b540c0cb7bc42f37\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8667661\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1733386}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8b4b06ff53a47f1041e0e59f894d9e929963904c\nwpt-pr: 64537\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/image-min-max-content-intrinsic-size-change-009.html"], "git_node": "b069ba5bd6dc9feec781cf4d5b0f45aa895cdfb3", "git_parents": ["99c45e977127ca785a171259f9ceec078591aeda"], "node": "086215b5dc6d8b5e79ce5f42c2fcef1c0b583d05", "parents": ["2acc5404cc8e212486235b25c7ca9b904f3174ba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092451 [wpt PR 64537] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64537\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-sizing/image-min-max-content-intrinsic-size-change-009.html.ini"], "git_node": "4d7eac1c3c6bf60014968c8bb016b4fddb070997", "git_parents": ["b069ba5bd6dc9feec781cf4d5b0f45aa895cdfb3"], "node": "28ff71d4a95899b828ca2e8ed3c592a524db3117", "parents": ["086215b5dc6d8b5e79ce5f42c2fcef1c0b583d05"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Guohui Deng \u003cguohuideng@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092454 [wpt PR 64576] - [LoAF] Null `PerformanceScriptTiming` window once window is detached, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[LoAF] Null `PerformanceScriptTiming` window once window is detached\n\nPerformanceScriptTiming's window attribute should return null once its\nwindow is detached, see\nhttps://w3c.github.io/long-animation-frames/#ref-for-dom-performancescripttiming-window\n\nBug: 576326785\nChange-Id: I58417a266f29f1023c69ff4814b80ba3b205696b\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8693605\nReviewed-by: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Scott Haseley \u003cshaseley@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Guohui Deng \u003cguohuideng@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1733388}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f935e84cb7bb19d10871e13f25b5efdbbe80823c\nwpt-pr: 64576\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/loaf-script-detached-window.html"], "git_node": "9bdf41665890aeb61b489da5197542c2e6234371", "git_parents": ["4d7eac1c3c6bf60014968c8bb016b4fddb070997"], "node": "908ab851a0f2a30060553260e589966aabfa30d4", "parents": ["28ff71d4a95899b828ca2e8ed3c592a524db3117"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092457 [wpt PR 64563] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327987, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[SVG] parsePoint() accepts trailing garbage after the point (#64563)\n\nThis patch aligns WebKit with Gecko / Firefox and Blink / Chromium.\n\nparsePoint() skipped trailing whitespace but ignored the result and never\nchecked that the whole string was consumed, despite its comment saying\nanything except spaces at the end is disallowed. As a result, values like\n\"200,100 junk\" were parsed as (200, 100). Check buffer.atEnd() after skipping\ntrailing spaces and return std::nullopt otherwise, matching the sibling\nnumber-pair parser.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327987\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/325447@main\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 80b7840162a1718aef37cf25570c2f6a04765bfe\nwpt-pr: 64563\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/animations/animateMotion-calcMode-discrete-from-to-trailing-junk.html"], "git_node": "d1e5cfb8f0367de23f0038316ba2e0aa81e6297c", "git_parents": ["9bdf41665890aeb61b489da5197542c2e6234371"], "node": "af07d9cf50aed6702840f8428c14fac1ef6e0d57", "parents": ["908ab851a0f2a30060553260e589966aabfa30d4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092459 [wpt PR 64243] - Fix intrinsic widths under-invalidation for orthogonal roots, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix intrinsic widths under-invalidation for orthogonal roots\n\nAn orthogonal flow root's block-size (determined by layout) contributes\nto its container's inline-size. For orthogonal flow roots,\n`BlockNode::ComputeMinMaxSizes()` lays out the orthogonal subtree to\ndetermine its block-size rather than computing min/max sizes, without\nclearing `IntrinsicLogicalWidthsDirty()` on blocks within the\northogonal subtree (when their inline-size is definite or stretched).\nBecause `IntrinsicLogicalWidthsDirty()` is never cleared on those\nblocks, `InvalidateContainerIntrinsicLogicalWidths()` stops early\nwithout invalidating ancestors of the orthogonal root.\n`ShouldInvalidateBeyond()` cannot be used here because normal blocks\nnested inside the orthogonal root also remain dirty and have the same\nwriting-mode as the orthogonal root.\n\nWhen marking the container chain for full layout in\n`MarkContainerChainForLayout()` outside `PerformLayout()`, call\n`InvalidateContainerIntrinsicLogicalWidths()` when crossing an\northogonal writing-mode boundary (skipping this during layout so\ninterleaved style recalc such as container queries does not invalidate\nancestors already in layout). Also update\n`MarkParentForSpannerOrOutOfFlowPositionedChange()` to use\n`SetChildNeedsLayout()` (with default `kMarkContainerChain`) rather\nthan `kMarkOnlyThis` so that `MarkContainerChainForLayout()` runs and\ninvalidates intrinsic widths when crossing an orthogonal writing-mode\nboundary.\n\nThis patch also deflakes `orthogonal-parent-shrink-to-fit-001.html`.\n\nBug: 568337130\nChange-Id: I5612dbf8233ffe000510f5e323686d5293b76eda\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8522118\nAuto-Submit: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1733472}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ad65e3da226065fbc12c9fe4f61bea408f5bbf1d\nwpt-pr: 64243\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/dynamic-min-content-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/dynamic-min-content-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/dynamic-min-content-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/dynamic-min-content-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/dynamic-min-content-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/orthogonal-container-query-in-shrink-to-fit-flex.html"], "git_node": "92fd0d18762797399091e97d001934f909901fc2", "git_parents": ["d1e5cfb8f0367de23f0038316ba2e0aa81e6297c"], "node": "fe386cf4c16bd6d597c26a7658e7637c72ff892e", "parents": ["af07d9cf50aed6702840f8428c14fac1ef6e0d57"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antony Gakuru \u003cantony123muriithi@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092460 [wpt PR 64583] - script: use encoding-parse-a-url on processing options, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\ntest preload url encoding windows 1252\n\nSigned-off-by: Antony Gakuru \u003cantony123muriithi@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\nscript: test coverage for favicon, prefetch & preload url encoding\n\nSigned-off-by: Antony Gakuru \u003cantony123muriithi@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\nmerge url encoding test files to one\n\nSigned-off-by: Antony Gakuru \u003cantony123muriithi@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\nreturn expected file contents for onload\n\nSigned-off-by: Antony Gakuru \u003cantony123muriithi@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\nappend link to document head before timeout\n\nSigned-off-by: Antony Gakuru \u003cantony123muriithi@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4135a0e0079db7cd0a26d134ae7f2a6d9f8423f6, 3f51a5f745f43e7c84c83fb423a0674571f771e0, 7ffd0ca2f99b5bf60cb56659f52c471e8dd2f3e1, 17f4bef2bbe5bf93fe4ae9d9ddcf50d0a31e638d, 6a0bc5725a3ce342d2e6d023cb0eadc3fcda923d\nwpt-pr: 64583\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/preload/link-url-encoding.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/preload/resources/stash-read.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/preload/resources/stash-url.py"], "git_node": "59558e7cb6d500fd1912328d2435ada21bb6c399", "git_parents": ["92fd0d18762797399091e97d001934f909901fc2"], "node": "60ae7e7263a2c743d78846a8bf62bad93b4a5f80", "parents": ["fe386cf4c16bd6d597c26a7658e7637c72ff892e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092460 [wpt PR 64583] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64583\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/preload/link-url-encoding.html.ini"], "git_node": "ba974fa01f22f48d94b30969082439440f5c57c0", "git_parents": ["59558e7cb6d500fd1912328d2435ada21bb6c399"], "node": "9f01b77644e053ca003bce0376e29ed0805957ff", "parents": ["60ae7e7263a2c743d78846a8bf62bad93b4a5f80"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rahul Singh (EDGE) \u003crahsin@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092461 [wpt PR 64584] - [CSS-link-params] Use colon in param(), a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[CSS-link-params] Use colon in param()\n\nUpdate param() parsing and serialization to use a colon between the\nparameter name and value, following the CSSWG resolution:\nhttps://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14275\n\nUpdate the WPTs and parser tests to use the colon syntax.\n\nBug: 579339308\nChange-Id: Ib2acdaa6ce66b6a21839b6540e79507c9ba9341d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8691587\nReviewed-by: Kevin Babbitt \u003ckbabbitt@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rahul Singh \u003crahsin@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Rahul Singh \u003crahsin@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1733623}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7a1a52c0470d69eb825d5f07808fc36118563a48\nwpt-pr: 64584\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-link-params/inheritance.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-link-params/link-parameters-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-link-params/link-parameters-dynamic.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-link-params/link-parameters-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-link-params/link-parameters-no-interpolation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-link-params/link-parameters-typed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-link-params/link-parameters-valid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-link-params/url-modifier-param-typed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/css-linked-parameters-precedence-1.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/css-linked-parameters-precedence-2.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/img-with-linked-parameters-1.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/img-with-linked-parameters-2.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/img-with-url-fragment-identifiers-1.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/img-with-url-fragment-identifiers-2.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/img-with-url-function-1.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/img-with-url-function-2.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-background-image.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-basic.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-currentcolor-typed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-currentcolor-untyped.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-duplicate-name.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-dynamic.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-fallback.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-geometry.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-invalid-typed-value.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-none.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-per-container.html"], "git_node": "b725905943adb77762a7cdbec7d6d1a5c0203d43", "git_parents": ["ba974fa01f22f48d94b30969082439440f5c57c0"], "node": "a336c237f283c63529fdaa18013dbcda9eec600a", "parents": ["9f01b77644e053ca003bce0376e29ed0805957ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092461 [wpt PR 64584] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64584\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-link-params/inheritance.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-link-params/link-parameters-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-link-params/link-parameters-dynamic.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-link-params/link-parameters-invalid.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-link-params/link-parameters-no-interpolation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-link-params/link-parameters-typed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-link-params/link-parameters-valid.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-link-params/url-modifier-param-typed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/img-with-linked-parameters-1.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/img-with-linked-parameters-2.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-background-image.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-basic.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-currentcolor-untyped.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-dynamic.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-fallback.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/styling/css-linked-parameters/link-parameters-per-container.html.ini"], "git_node": "d53ad257deed5cfa6927ddd476ebb405887d9deb", "git_parents": ["b725905943adb77762a7cdbec7d6d1a5c0203d43"], "node": "1f67f01a666fcd15fa9d8022ffc8d29d02597840", "parents": ["a336c237f283c63529fdaa18013dbcda9eec600a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sarah Drasner \u003csdrasner@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092462 [wpt PR 64586] - [SVG] Don't scale a percentage textPath startOffset by pathLength, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[SVG] Don't scale a percentage textPath startOffset by pathLength\n\nSVG 2 says that pathLength \"has no effect on percentage distance-along-\na-path calculations\", and that when pathLength is zero only\n\"non-percentage\" offsets greater than zero become +Infinity [1]. In\nother words, startOffset=\"50%\" should always land halfway along the\npath as the browser measured it, whatever pathLength says.\n\nWe were resolving percentage offsets against the author's pathLength\nand then multiplying by the pathLength scale factor on top of that.\nWith a non-zero pathLength the two steps cancel out, which is why this\nwent unnoticed. With pathLength=\"0\" the percentage resolves to 0 and\nthe text ends up at the start of the path.\n\nResolve percentages against the computed path length instead, and\nonly apply the scale factor to non-percentage offsets.\n\nThis also brings the 2018 WPT svg/path/distance/pathLength-zero-\npercentage.svg in line with the current spec text: it expected the old\nbehaviour and now contradicts the newer textpath-pathlength-zero-\noffset-percentage.svg. The sibling pathLength-positive-ref.svg already\nshows these percentages unaffected by pathLength, so I think we can\npoint it there and drop its own reference.\n\n[1] https://svgwg.org/svg2-draft/paths.html#PathLengthAttribute\n\nR=fs@opera.com\n\nBug: 562425279\nChange-Id: I53fab2cfe8332a22dd3a6cf52be54a2876545d13\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8604471\nReviewed-by: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Sarah Drasner \u003csdrasner@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Sarah Drasner \u003csdrasner@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1733649}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6accfa9e954d4cad35a6c722ad13c8795451ca5b\nwpt-pr: 64586\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/path/distance/pathLength-zero-percentage-ref.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/path/distance/pathLength-zero-percentage.svg"], "git_node": "9032bd36f0669610d2ec95d0b2512f0bc1924bf1", "git_parents": ["d53ad257deed5cfa6927ddd476ebb405887d9deb"], "node": "6389d5cc1bd3fbe9726ca20454cdd5b67ca37106", "parents": ["1f67f01a666fcd15fa9d8022ffc8d29d02597840"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092462 [wpt PR 64586] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64586\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/svg/path/distance/pathLength-zero-percentage.svg.ini"], "git_node": "e2aa6bea9e9528887cbd7c103e3ee0a8eff70733", "git_parents": ["9032bd36f0669610d2ec95d0b2512f0bc1924bf1"], "node": "d257255c4947d055fb37b59c23858c3a40e73dd8", "parents": ["6389d5cc1bd3fbe9726ca20454cdd5b67ca37106"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Roberto Rodriguez \u003croberto_rodriguez2@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092464 [wpt PR 64554] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323021, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[CSP] Nonce-based CSP is bypassed by dangling markup placed before a nonced \u003clink\u003e\n\nElement::isNonceable() implements the CSP \"is element nonceable\" algorithm\n(https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP3/#is-element-nonceable) which officially only checks for '\u003cscript'\nand '\u003cstyle' in each attribute name and value to catch injected dangling markup and prevent\nan unterminated script start tag from stealing a nonce from a legitimate element.\nThe algorithm currently doesn't check for '\u003clink' even though \u003clink\u003e is nonceable.\n\nFix by also checking for '\u003clink' in each attribute name and value. Nonces apply only to\nscript, style and link elements, so all three are now covered. Chrome has already made this\nchange and has proposed updating the CSP spec (https://github.com/w3c/webappsec-csp/pull/810).\n\nA WPT test exists for checking non-nonceable elements\n(content-security-policy/script-src/non-nonceable-elements.html)\nand WebKit currently fails its '\u003clink' subtests, which this fix addresses. That test only\nchecks attribute values, so add a second similar test to cover attribute names.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323021\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/320263@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 04d9e6322b7aadc8f51f033230508fe3f0f22ce4\nwpt-pr: 64554\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/script-src/non-nonceable-elements-attr-name.html"], "git_node": "6776336471b68d91b6c3ccd074b85e7d04aa7685", "git_parents": ["e2aa6bea9e9528887cbd7c103e3ee0a8eff70733"], "node": "d7d547b2d9f447c8f89c8c3068f778ee75e828db", "parents": ["d257255c4947d055fb37b59c23858c3a40e73dd8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092466 [wpt PR 64588] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326281, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[line-clamp] line-clamp: auto clamps inside a box with a set height\n\n\u003cdiv style=\"line-clamp: auto; max-height: 6lh; white-space: pre\"\u003eLine 1\nLine 2\nLine 3\nLine 4\n\u003cdiv style=\"height: 3lh\"\u003eLine 5\nLine 6\u003c/div\u003eLine 7\u003c/div\u003e\n\nThe block ellipsis should be on Line 4. The auto clamp point was after Line 6, since Lines 5 and 6 fit within max-height,\nbut the block keeps its 3lh height whatever its content, so clamping inside it does not make the line-clamp container\nany shorter than clamping before it, and the container would still go past max-height.\n\nNow when a block of the line-clamp container that does not fit has a set height, or a min-height that does not fit, no\nclamp point inside it is used, and the clamp point is before it (after Line 4).\n\nThe test added as line-clamp-auto-063 is exported as line-clamp-auto-065, its name since https://commits.webkit.org/323995@main, because web-platform-tests has a different line-clamp-auto-063. This includes 064's reference link fix from https://commits.webkit.org/325484@main.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326281\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327750\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=329806\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/322842@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a9939aeb967bc3cb747bfee0e2dd496ee258955e\nwpt-pr: 64588\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-auto-064.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-auto-065.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-auto-067.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-auto-068.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/line-clamp-auto-065-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/line-clamp-auto-067-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/line-clamp-auto-068-ref.html"], "git_node": "976bdacc8eeafd18286c0d6dcdddd4b6aff78bfb", "git_parents": ["6776336471b68d91b6c3ccd074b85e7d04aa7685"], "node": "7050a23355b561c170829dafa504ea3b479de1ba", "parents": ["d7d547b2d9f447c8f89c8c3068f778ee75e828db"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003cahmad.saleem792+github@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092467 [wpt PR 64591] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319182, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nScroll To Text Fragment: simplify MIME-type gate and add mixed-case coverage\n\nFollow-up to 316976@main. ParsedContentType::mimeType() already returns an\nASCII-lowercased essence (setContentType() calls convertToASCIILowercase()),\nso the equalLettersIgnoringASCIICase() comparisons in scrollToTextFragment()\nwere redundant. Compare the parsed MIME type directly against the lowercase\nliterals \"text/html\" and \"text/plain\", and note in a comment that the string\nis already lowercased.\n\nAlso add WPT coverage for a document served with a mixed-case Content-Type\n(\"Text/HTML; charset=UTF-8\") to pin the case-insensitive normalization.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319182\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/316990@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 442073e65773ba7c01790a39523efdafc9016353\nwpt-pr: 64591\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-to-text-fragment/resources/text-html-mixed-case.html.headers"], "git_node": "38c81000a6501be39693b29ce1b82b20131a6226", "git_parents": ["976bdacc8eeafd18286c0d6dcdddd4b6aff78bfb"], "node": "fe2d8079345540994cdddcbc3a753eb4cf8449bf", "parents": ["7050a23355b561c170829dafa504ea3b479de1ba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003cahmad.saleem792+github@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092469 [wpt PR 64590] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=245523, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-pseudo] ::first-letter and ::first-line should reject some properties\n\nThis patch aligns WebKit with Web Specification [1] & [2]:\n\n[1] https://drafts.csswg.org/css-pseudo/#first-line-styling\n[2] https://drafts.csswg.org/css-pseudo/#first-letter-styling\n\nThis patch updates our allowlist for properties, which can be applied to\nfirst-letter and and first-line pseudo-elements similar to others.\n\nWhile updating, we also make both pseudo elements (non-tree abiding) to\nhave animations (based on CSSWG Issue Resolution [3]).\n\n[3] https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12814#issuecomment-4040525212\n\nAdditionally, getComputedStyle(element, \"::first-line\" / \"::first-letter\") now\nresolves the pseudo-element style even when the originating element is not a\nblock container (e.g. display:inline or display:flex), instead of falling back\nto a style inherited from the parent.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=245523\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/325393@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b50134e2950c71ab513b65bef4d6a66af2cd663a\nwpt-pr: 64590\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/first-letter-animate.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/first-line-animate.html"], "git_node": "c1af0f4932f6b0af4cf380d9c3d54e75e933c2fd", "git_parents": ["38c81000a6501be39693b29ce1b82b20131a6226"], "node": "e91c535f2e699b866dd614c35f00ea77d952abdb", "parents": ["fe2d8079345540994cdddcbc3a753eb4cf8449bf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092469 [wpt PR 64590] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64590\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-pseudo/first-letter-animate.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-pseudo/first-line-animate.html.ini"], "git_node": "7d4fa6064197d9e6a827b92f5ccc3ff149e2fc2a", "git_parents": ["c1af0f4932f6b0af4cf380d9c3d54e75e933c2fd"], "node": "f1b9ed725672d5c7eafbba1eb1c77bf827feb712", "parents": ["e91c535f2e699b866dd614c35f00ea77d952abdb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092471 [wpt PR 64592] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326226, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[IFC] An overflowing preserved tab does not wrap to the next line\n\n\u003cdiv style=\"width: 85px; font: 25px Ahem; tab-size: 4\"\u003eX \u003cspan style=\"white-space: pre\"\u003e&#x09;\u003c/span\u003e X\u003c/div\u003e\n\nThe tab does not fit after \"X \" and should wrap to the second line. Overflowing content that is only whitespace\nstays on the line, as it is either trimmed or hangs at the end of the line. A tab with white-space: pre does\nneither, it takes up space, so it now goes through the regular overflow handling and wraps.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326226\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/322759@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: fe9645fc8e7220c600670a28c7f4f15804fa2c26\nwpt-pr: 64592\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/white-space/pre-tab-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/white-space/reference/pre-tab-001-ref.html"], "git_node": "857699dc0b3ade6d911b8754a6637d8005b25985", "git_parents": ["7d4fa6064197d9e6a827b92f5ccc3ff149e2fc2a"], "node": "5a32932693ea7b041a10abcfdc33ae0912be3378", "parents": ["f1b9ed725672d5c7eafbba1eb1c77bf827feb712"], "tags": []}, {"author": "youennf \u003cyouennf@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092473 [wpt PR 64548] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328497, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebCodecs Video encoders should handle rotation/flip (#64548)\n\nWe add support for rotation and mirror in WebCodecs encoders as per specification.\n\nWe keep an active orientation like in spec and rejects when encode is called with a different orientation than the last one.\nWe keep an active output orientation to output a config when orientation is changing.\n\nWe pipe orientation info to the various encoders like done for timestamp and diration.\nWe only support orientation info in the GPU WebCore encoder code paths, not the legacy one that we plan to remove soon.\n\nCovered by added tests.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328497\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1fce1aa9533498ec1069a75bd2dff7715f32151f\nwpt-pr: 64548\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/video-encoder-orientation.https.any.js"], "git_node": "26b00ac46c032e410aecdfd12cb9b23b6a7176e8", "git_parents": ["857699dc0b3ade6d911b8754a6637d8005b25985"], "node": "e127daed886ed2c2cbeaceb279cdbcde574057cf", "parents": ["5a32932693ea7b041a10abcfdc33ae0912be3378"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092473 [wpt PR 64548] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64548\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/serialization-to-shared-and-service-workers.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/video-encoder-orientation.https.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "2af4f806eaad3b95befff0a8fab65b5d52bd6cba", "git_parents": ["26b00ac46c032e410aecdfd12cb9b23b6a7176e8"], "node": "60a8b4e85a8a0449ba2038be21e7a91be2f5d813", "parents": ["e127daed886ed2c2cbeaceb279cdbcde574057cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnoam@webkit.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092475 [wpt PR 64594] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=217820, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nLayoutTests/imported/w3c:\n\nSupport EXIF image resolution in CoreGraphics (macOS/iOS)\nhttps://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=217820\n\nImported density-size-correction tests\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=217820\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/230808@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 26f2f89a2a4f31ede0e883e9714b3ac6a4e8accc\nwpt-pr: 64594\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/density-size-correction/resources/exif-resolution-preapplied-hires.jpg"], "git_node": "36152c8e57378cbaab983d566a571d2faa1d028a", "git_parents": ["2af4f806eaad3b95befff0a8fab65b5d52bd6cba"], "node": "8ed0b4410ab05c2d2d14c4ea3a6ef2e1f6a6ab4c", "parents": ["60a8b4e85a8a0449ba2038be21e7a91be2f5d813"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoav Weiss \u003cyoav.weiss@shopify.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092477 [wpt PR 64599] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=316647, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nNavigation Timing: cross-origin redirect opt-in should be based on destination origin.\n\nThis PR aligns the WebKit implementation with https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/pull/1931 and https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12513,\nand ensures that TAO opt-ins for navigation timing take the destination origin into account.\n\nNew iframe tests, plus test progressions.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=316647\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/317061@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6662bb5ac7dfcf0b31d010d7f402360e00cbf0e3\nwpt-pr: 64599\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-timing/resources/report-navigation-redirect-timing.html"], "git_node": "897e2e80260d860bf043a6880db88f8a4f9c3222", "git_parents": ["36152c8e57378cbaab983d566a571d2faa1d028a"], "node": "60b9f2299b1e1102d2e9d99367f2238f5204e19e", "parents": ["8ed0b4410ab05c2d2d14c4ea3a6ef2e1f6a6ab4c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092478 [wpt PR 64593] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327293, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nImport updated corner shorthand WPTs for css-borders-4\n\nhttps://drafts.csswg.org/css-borders-4/#corner-shorthands\n\nThe corner and corner-* shorthand tests imported from the W3C still assert\nthe old, slash separated prototype grammar. The CSSWG now specifies\n\u003c'border-radius'\u003e || \u003c'corner-shape'\u003e and the matching side and\nsingle-corner forms, resolved in\nhttps://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/11623 and reconfirmed in\nhttps://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13889.\n\nImport the rewrite from\nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8498274, which\nupdates twelve tests and adds corner-top-invalid.html, so that WebKit's\ntest coverage reflects the current grammar. The rewrite is not yet in the\nupstream web-platform-tests repository, and WebKit does not export tests,\nso this applies the Chromium CL's rewrite directly to the imported copies.\n\nRecord the current engine behaviour with the imported baselines. All eleven\nrewritten tests fail against the old grammar in WebKit; the baselines\ncapture that output. corner-top-invalid.html gets a new baseline. The\nreference test corner-shorthand-rendering.html uses declarations that the\nold grammar cannot parse, so it is marked ImageOnlyFailure under this bug\nuntil the grammar correction in 326108 lands and this expectation is\nremoved. corner-top-invalid.html's current baseline is for the old grammar\nand will become all-PASS when that correction lands.\n\nNo product code changes; this is tests only.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327293\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/323802@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a3a36d37aea6ac960ceeea90b54d6f9cab2d5318\nwpt-pr: 64593\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-top-invalid.html"], "git_node": "352e46b10f6fd6636f34c67fde76510bed99b32b", "git_parents": ["897e2e80260d860bf043a6880db88f8a4f9c3222"], "node": "5d86d7c3f1737bda57d232216a3935299ddd5533", "parents": ["60b9f2299b1e1102d2e9d99367f2238f5204e19e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim Nguyen \u003cntim@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092479 [wpt PR 64598] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319831, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[white-space-trim] Add to white-space shorthand syntax\n\n(This is based on Tim Nguyen initial PR)\n\nThe syntax for the white-space shorthand is:\n\nnormal | pre | pre-wrap | pre-line | \u003c'white-space-collapse'\u003e || \u003c'text-wrap-mode'\u003e || \u003c'white-space-trim'\u003e\n\nSee: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text-4/#white-space-property\n\nAdd 'white-space-trim' as the third longhand of the 'white-space' shorthand. The\nlegacy single-keyword forms (normal / pre / pre-wrap / pre-line) map to\n'white-space-trim: none' per the normative table in the spec, so they never combine\nwith a discard-* keyword. Serialization -- both of a declaration block\n(ShorthandSerializer) and of the computed value (Style::Extractor) -- only collapses\nto those legacy keywords when 'white-space-trim' is 'none'; otherwise it appends the\ntrim value and omits the other two longhands when they hold their initial value.\n\n'white-space-trim' is gated on the CSSWhiteSpaceTrimEnabled setting while\n'white-space' is not, so the shorthand parser gates only the consumption of the\ndiscard-* keywords and always sets the 'white-space-trim' longhand. That keeps the\nshorthand round-tripping when the setting is off, and matches how 'font' and\n'font-variant' handle the settings-gated 'font-variant-emoji' longhand.\n\nEditing copies 'white-space-trim' alongside the other two longhands. All three have\nto travel together: a partial longhand set makes the 'white-space' shorthand\nunserializable, so editing would start emitting 'white-space-collapse' /\n'text-wrap-mode' where it used to emit 'white-space'. It is therefore listed with the\ninheritable editing properties even though it is not an inherited property -- if only\nthe context style carries it, the white-space longhands never compare equal to the\ncontext and editing wraps content in redundant spans. The context comparison in\nremoveStyleInContextNotOverridenByMatchedRules also compares values rather than\nCSSValue identity, since 'white-space-trim' serializes to a list for any value other\nthan 'none'.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319831\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/318486@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a08173d03a20aa4410009498980feb9aa45fcb93\nwpt-pr: 64598\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/parsing/white-space-shorthand-longhands.html"], "git_node": "1fcc40c1deb23395f12c8deb279338bef42a5a97", "git_parents": ["352e46b10f6fd6636f34c67fde76510bed99b32b"], "node": "34c894ecabcccc271150e4bbb8d2c24e24501380", "parents": ["5d86d7c3f1737bda57d232216a3935299ddd5533"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092479 [wpt PR 64598] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64598\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-text/parsing/white-space-shorthand-longhands.html.ini"], "git_node": "f1cd5785e801b1f57905f79726af87dc77f516f4", "git_parents": ["1fcc40c1deb23395f12c8deb279338bef42a5a97"], "node": "f8c3b6853345ca1860b5daebd3c747ac196a6de8", "parents": ["34c894ecabcccc271150e4bbb8d2c24e24501380"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Weinig \u003csam@webkit.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092481 [wpt PR 64595] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326533, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Image Redux] Update cross-fade() to match CSS Image 4\n\nFixes the unprefixed cross-fade() to match CSS Image 4 and other browsers.\n\nPreviously, unprefixed cross-fade() used the same grammar as -webkit-cross-fade(), which does\nhave the same grammar as the one defined in CSS Images 4 (https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images-4/#funcdef-cross-fade).\n\nNow, unprefixed cross-fade() uses the new grammar (without support \u003ccolor\u003e for the moment),\nallowing any number of images to cross-faded together. Prefixed -webkit-cross-fade() still\nuses the old grammar and is limited to two images as before.\n\nAdditionally, we now use the spec's algorithms for sizing (https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images-4/#cross-fade-sizing)\nand painting (https://drafts.csswg.org/css-images-4/#cross-fade-painting), including the\ncontext dependent recursive negotiation required. This very subtly changes the way a\ncross-fade of images without natural dimensions might render and new WPT tests for this\nhave been added.\n\nAlso fixes the background-image-interpolation.html test to use test_no_interpolation() rather\nthan test_interpolation(), as is needed for discrete only properties. This matches other image\ninterpolation tests like mask-image-interpolation.html\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326533\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/322918@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2ef8631efaa4b97e6b85c5d2460a649ee10fb3c3\nwpt-pr: 64595\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/cross-fade-natural-size-gradients-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/cross-fade-natural-size-gradients.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/cross-fade-natural-size-image-and-gradient-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/cross-fade-natural-size-image-and-gradient.html"], "git_node": "829940ffa7f8c57b5f9ec5481328ad78cb3a128f", "git_parents": ["f1cd5785e801b1f57905f79726af87dc77f516f4"], "node": "7a28c1de15d01e1fc15a42d693f092f2b4613e40", "parents": ["f8c3b6853345ca1860b5daebd3c747ac196a6de8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Fraser \u003csimon.fraser@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092581 [wpt PR 64596] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323565, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[corner-shape] Some combinations of corner-shape with thick borders have incorrect rendering\n\nThe inside border edge can self-intersect with some combinations of border-width and concave\ncorner shapes; make sure these cases don't result in bad rendering by removing inner corners\nwhen necessary, and computing when the entire inner shape disappears.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323565\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/320826@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b9df77696b5868e88a096af614d6095a99585799\nwpt-pr: 64596\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/inner-corner-collapse001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/inner-corner-collapse001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/inner-corner-collapse002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/inner-corner-collapse002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/inner-corner-collapse003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/inner-corner-collapse003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/inner-corner-intersection004-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/inner-corner-intersection004.html"], "git_node": "b46441e9624f02c588a7e5a2595d82faad36ceec", "git_parents": ["829940ffa7f8c57b5f9ec5481328ad78cb3a128f"], "node": "0b0c62a7ec01bc73a8db53e9abd69aae90f1e995", "parents": ["7a28c1de15d01e1fc15a42d693f092f2b4613e40"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092581 [wpt PR 64596] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64596\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/inner-corner-collapse001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/inner-corner-collapse002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/inner-corner-collapse003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/inner-corner-intersection004.html.ini"], "git_node": "dc289619924cfda2d7953aa80e39f455bdbffe21", "git_parents": ["b46441e9624f02c588a7e5a2595d82faad36ceec"], "node": "13b556488ff2e3d4668dc1b62213f5d9f98e34d3", "parents": ["0b0c62a7ec01bc73a8db53e9abd69aae90f1e995"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Fraser \u003csimon.fraser@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092590 [wpt PR 64597] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322658, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[corner-shape] Incorrect rendering when inner corners intersect\n\nWith larger border thickness and border-radius, adjacent corners of the inner border edge can intesect,\ncausing bad rendering with overlapping and holes.\n\nFix by implementing logic to intersect bezier paths, but we only need to support the simple, monotonic curves\nthat are used by corner-shape. `addSuperellipseCornerCurves` calls functions in CornerShapeUtilities to do this.\nThe intersection logic uses a recursive function (`appendCurveCrossings()`) with a depth limit.\n\nEven non-adjacent corners can intersect (see inner-corner-intersection003.html), which `addSuperellipseCornerCurves()`\nhandles.\n\nAdd API tests for the Bezier functions. BezierUtilitiesTests.cpp wasn't being compiled at all, so add it\nto the target.\n\nBased on work by Lilly Le (@cupidsity).\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322658\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/320287@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b56015dceb98c98f29cba6c3824441240361f725\nwpt-pr: 64597\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/inner-corner-intersection001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/inner-corner-intersection001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/inner-corner-intersection002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/inner-corner-intersection002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/inner-corner-intersection003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/inner-corner-intersection003.html"], "git_node": "fdd26eac99ebc8e1f6312059e90e9f4d21017c1d", "git_parents": ["dc289619924cfda2d7953aa80e39f455bdbffe21"], "node": "4ee9fdd9b2ca1bc44daa0be13b150471edc1f10c", "parents": ["13b556488ff2e3d4668dc1b62213f5d9f98e34d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092590 [wpt PR 64597] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64597\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/inner-corner-intersection001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/inner-corner-intersection002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/inner-corner-intersection003.html.ini"], "git_node": "5eb689616257272be45a082ede3358a683f4f1bc", "git_parents": ["fdd26eac99ebc8e1f6312059e90e9f4d21017c1d"], "node": "be024f8adffb7b7ede292fcb0ef3bcaf513cf354", "parents": ["4ee9fdd9b2ca1bc44daa0be13b150471edc1f10c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092704 [wpt PR 64547] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=329798, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdopting a shadow host with a live collection hits a debug assertion\n\nWhen the old document has a live collection with a valid cache,\nNode::moveTreeToNewScope() takes the slow path. Moving the collection's owner\ninvalidates that cache, which unregisters the collection from the old\ndocument. A shadow root moved after that point can then find the old document\neligible for fast adoption, which fails the assertion in\nmoveShadowTreeToNewDocumentSlowCase(). Moving a tree into a user agent shadow\ntree takes the slow path even when the documents are eligible, so the\nassertion can fail there too.\n\nThe assertion has been too strict since it was added in 273544@main.\nmoveTreeToNewScope() already decides once, and the slow path is correct either\nway, so remove the assertion.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=329798\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4cf02b3278d725f50b058648d00595ea09a5ff86\nwpt-pr: 64547\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/crashtests/adopt-shadow-host-with-live-collection.html"], "git_node": "f835f9166434fd10eff262d154d007e33c05cc98", "git_parents": ["5eb689616257272be45a082ede3358a683f4f1bc"], "node": "656dcfdd0838223b8be94bf1cff4e58e5ce321da", "parents": ["be024f8adffb7b7ede292fcb0ef3bcaf513cf354"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092712 [wpt PR 64601] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=289298, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[macOS wk2 Release] 3 css/css-conditional/container-queries/canvas-as-container-00*.html are flaky failures.\n\ncanvas-as-container-001.html through 004.html focus an element inside a size container canvas and expect the canvas's\n:focus-within style (a green border) to show up. Nothing holds the screenshot back, so it can be taken before the focus change\nis rendered.\n\nLet's make them reftest-wait tests that take the screenshot two frames after focusing the element, and remove their flaky\nexpectations, including canvas-as-container-002.html's (webkit.org/b/295929).\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=289298\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/325138@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1c3ffb7081f2c2d5cb0e0504f66991f09838fd8c\nwpt-pr: 64601\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-conditional/container-queries/canvas-as-container-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-conditional/container-queries/canvas-as-container-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-conditional/container-queries/canvas-as-container-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-conditional/container-queries/canvas-as-container-004.html"], "git_node": "c53878c0e6fe1f46a0484f1a7fd9cec3c0f36f93", "git_parents": ["f835f9166434fd10eff262d154d007e33c05cc98"], "node": "55f66d8a52930e7fdf0c8930dfd3eae48fc36bd7", "parents": ["656dcfdd0838223b8be94bf1cff4e58e5ce321da"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092712 [wpt PR 64601] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64601\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-conditional/container-queries/whitespace-update-after-removal.html.ini"], "git_node": "d5d3276bfb912bf1f4399cd616520137eea4a42d", "git_parents": ["c53878c0e6fe1f46a0484f1a7fd9cec3c0f36f93"], "node": "5bba4f07350b7995f1893b766921d748c37f14ba", "parents": ["55f66d8a52930e7fdf0c8930dfd3eae48fc36bd7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003cahmad.saleem792+github@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092717 [wpt PR 64600] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=245523, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-pseudo] ::first-letter and ::first-line should reject some properties\n\nThis patch aligns WebKit with Web Specification [1] & [2]:\n\n[1] https://drafts.csswg.org/css-pseudo/#first-line-styling\n[2] https://drafts.csswg.org/css-pseudo/#first-letter-styling\n\nThis patch updates our allowlist for properties, which can be applied to\nfirst-letter and and first-line pseudo-elements similar to others.\n\nWhile updating, we also make both pseudo elements (non-tree abiding) to\nhave animations (based on CSSWG Issue Resolution [3]).\n\n[3] https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12814#issuecomment-4040525212\n\nAdditionally, getComputedStyle(element, \"::first-line\" / \"::first-letter\") now\nresolves the pseudo-element style even when the originating element is not a\nblock container (e.g. display:inline or display:flex), instead of falling back\nto a style inherited from the parent.\n\nWebKit's copies of css/css-pseudo/first-line-allowed-properties.html are based on older upstream versions, so this applies WebKit's changes to the current ones.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=245523\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/325393@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5ba5de372f9b947861e3bad8b652afc64ab501b8\nwpt-pr: 64600\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/first-letter-allowed-properties.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/first-line-allowed-properties.html"], "git_node": "0348ca7e5a22427319646b3081b65f58c8a82c00", "git_parents": ["d5d3276bfb912bf1f4399cd616520137eea4a42d"], "node": "eb44bce360e105ce0a2d244fa34e8fdfe8c3bdb9", "parents": ["5bba4f07350b7995f1893b766921d748c37f14ba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092717 [wpt PR 64600] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64600\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-pseudo/first-letter-allowed-properties.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-pseudo/first-line-allowed-properties.html.ini"], "git_node": "e85cd603c446c616e2cc93c2f8186a47b4282f98", "git_parents": ["0348ca7e5a22427319646b3081b65f58c8a82c00"], "node": "caef215b7223c796306ae64db5f17fb03016db05", "parents": ["eb44bce360e105ce0a2d244fa34e8fdfe8c3bdb9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092724 [wpt PR 64602] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327039, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[line-clamp] Floats paint past the block-end content edge of the line-clamp container\n\n\u003cdiv style=\"line-clamp: 2\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"float: left; width: 10px; height: 200px; background: green\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003eLine 1\u003cbr\u003eLine 2\u003cbr\u003eLine 3\u003c/div\u003e\n\nThe float paints all the way down to its bottom, past the line-clamp container.\n\"Within a line-clamp container, floats which have not been made into invisible boxes must be visually clipped to the\nunshaped block-end content edge of the line-clamp container.\"\nhttps://drafts.csswg.org/css-overflow-4/#line-clamp-containers\n\nNow layout marks the visible floats of a line-clamp container as clipped (where it already decides whether they are invisible\nboxes), and they get clipped to the container's block-end content edge (and nowhere else): floats without a layer\nwhen the block that paints them paints them, floats with a layer (and the layers inside them) through the layer clip rects,\nin the space of the float's parent so that a transform on the float does not move the clip.\n\nline-clamp-with-floats-008 and -011 match their reference except for the gradient they paint the green square with\n(the same plain linear-gradient square without line-clamp has the same difference), so they get fuzzy matching.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=327039\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/323390@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c0a89db12ce9111ac2542fb43bbc193de010b81b\nwpt-pr: 64602\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-floats-008.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-floats-011.html"], "git_node": "eb288317c30e4738cbbab061f6225f3c7226b8c7", "git_parents": ["e85cd603c446c616e2cc93c2f8186a47b4282f98"], "node": "fe053c668328b69f1d7f6780985b92c7b4e44645", "parents": ["caef215b7223c796306ae64db5f17fb03016db05"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092729 [wpt PR 64603] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326226, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[IFC] An overflowing preserved tab does not wrap to the next line\n\n\u003cdiv style=\"width: 85px; font: 25px Ahem; tab-size: 4\"\u003eX \u003cspan style=\"white-space: pre\"\u003e&#x09;\u003c/span\u003e X\u003c/div\u003e\n\nThe tab does not fit after \"X \" and should wrap to the second line. Overflowing content that is only whitespace\nstays on the line, as it is either trimmed or hangs at the end of the line. A tab with white-space: pre does\nneither, it takes up space, so it now goes through the regular overflow handling and wraps.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326226\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/322759@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: cee6e1ddc411105f4d0b946fc705851263c256ec\nwpt-pr: 64603\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/block-ellipsis-033.html"], "git_node": "debd5e31005b46f8b7d8e68848e78d7771b38039", "git_parents": ["eb288317c30e4738cbbab061f6225f3c7226b8c7"], "node": "cfc6de8668bd37c69a384460167fe2ce89955dad", "parents": ["fe053c668328b69f1d7f6780985b92c7b4e44645"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092733 [wpt PR 64604] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326228, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[line-clamp] Remove the failure expectations of passing line-clamp tests\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326228\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/322792@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 41cdfdf722d0a519e8ba6ccd961b31a2182b11d7\nwpt-pr: 64604\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/block-ellipsis-quirk-002.html"], "git_node": "880c53b74d5276a01142b4493903ee937abd96d9", "git_parents": ["debd5e31005b46f8b7d8e68848e78d7771b38039"], "node": "116cb7932a3bd2c9ee9a01470c0b4d6371671373", "parents": ["cfc6de8668bd37c69a384460167fe2ce89955dad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092733 [wpt PR 64604] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64604\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/crashtests/line-clamp-empty-line.html.ini"], "git_node": "fa276d907064a51aa9063f9def3a8c8847b29895", "git_parents": ["880c53b74d5276a01142b4493903ee937abd96d9"], "node": "3ab52014b3b8b38a6865f1c73a3e21bcfc78a069", "parents": ["116cb7932a3bd2c9ee9a01470c0b4d6371671373"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Fraser \u003csimon.fraser@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092737 [wpt PR 64607] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323565, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[corner-shape] Some combinations of corner-shape with thick borders have incorrect rendering\n\nThe inside border edge can self-intersect with some combinations of border-width and concave\ncorner shapes; make sure these cases don't result in bad rendering by removing inner corners\nwhen necessary, and computing when the entire inner shape disappears.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323565\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/320826@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 59615788f72d8c2f4f1ac6f9dc4d21d8263ac429\nwpt-pr: 64607\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-inset-shadow.html"], "git_node": "e70e456239bfccea0d05e15b0db050a8022d520b", "git_parents": ["fa276d907064a51aa9063f9def3a8c8847b29895"], "node": "c424e8f709a998f484c8f059ae133090e55a3017", "parents": ["3ab52014b3b8b38a6865f1c73a3e21bcfc78a069"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092737 [wpt PR 64607] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64607\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-inset-shadow.html.ini"], "git_node": "da4ddb842fee6bbd621ce4eb99557290b34919a3", "git_parents": ["e70e456239bfccea0d05e15b0db050a8022d520b"], "node": "220e7bcd5bf9e6be3f8c72119c1aa44c43dfe7ab", "parents": ["c424e8f709a998f484c8f059ae133090e55a3017"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alejandro G. Castro \u003calex@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092744 [wpt PR 64606] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324539, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WPE][GTK] Use distance fields for small paths in the GPU renderer\n\nSkia keeps two different atlas caches for small paths. The bitmap key is\nbuilt from the shape key, the upper 2x2 of the CTM and 8 bits each of the\nsubpixel translation, while the distance field key only holds the shape key\nand the power of two dimension the field was generated at. Any path drawn\nunder an animated transform therefore misses the bitmap atlas on every frame\nand pays a CPU re-raster, a texture upload and the atlas work that follows,\nbut the distance field entry is reused.\n\nSkia already selects distance fields unconditionally on Android for this\nreason. We added support for Skia to allow picking the behaviour when\ncompiling, now it is part of the library and can be enabled with the\nbuild flag: SK_GANESH_SMALL_PATH_DISTANCE_FIELD_ALWAYS.\n\nThis improve Suits for MotionMark in rpi4 and desktop, we are still not\nsure the effect everywhere so we activate it to verify what are we\ngetting.\n\nThe patch just adds the build option in the compilation.\n\nApparently distance field rasterization is not pixel identical to the bitmap\natlas. Edge coverage differs slightly, and that is enough to break nine\nreftests. Updated the tolerances.\n\nThis also includes https://commits.webkit.org/320755@main, which changed the same files.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324539\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/321588@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f66e91b5c814e2f33e2db341a63e46e0145fb37c\nwpt-pr: 64606\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-backgrounds/background-image-centered-with-border-radius.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/outline-027.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/shapes/rect-04.svg"], "git_node": "68cd1ea2868b78395530b6c8b2a866211bf597a3", "git_parents": ["da4ddb842fee6bbd621ce4eb99557290b34919a3"], "node": "a54d831b3514ce045b189a476dfdfd618188d2d2", "parents": ["220e7bcd5bf9e6be3f8c72119c1aa44c43dfe7ab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092744 [wpt PR 64606] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64606\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-backgrounds/animations/background-color-animation-backdrop-infinite-duration-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-ui/crashtests/chrome-bug-467732064.html.ini"], "git_node": "427c3af1a9b73634a8a9fa74f9ebd0e2b6375003", "git_parents": ["68cd1ea2868b78395530b6c8b2a866211bf597a3"], "node": "254f25a49861479251854ece13fc39438c603956", "parents": ["a54d831b3514ce045b189a476dfdfd618188d2d2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Claudio Saavedra \u003ccsaavedra@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092746 [wpt PR 64608] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323205, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[GTK] css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-bevel-overflow.html is an image failure\n\n320287@main retuned this test's fuzzy tolerance for CoreGraphics, lowering\nthe pixel budget from upstream WPT's 256 to 198. On GTK the bevel clip and\nthe reference clip-path rasterize with different anti-aliasing paths in\nSkia's GPU backend, leaving an outline of about 240 pixels along the\ndiamond with a peak difference of 53, so the test fails on pixel count.\n\nRestore the upstream pixel budget and give the per-pixel bound the same\nheadroom sibling tests in this directory use.\n\nThis also includes https://commits.webkit.org/320287@main, which changed the same files.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=323205\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/320418@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e63acbf05fff457d7aa757d13e9cbd00a6396f98\nwpt-pr: 64608\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-bevel-overflow.html"], "git_node": "784961dc34189598e64d5a68ae5b709a6babfe59", "git_parents": ["427c3af1a9b73634a8a9fa74f9ebd0e2b6375003"], "node": "346667861d17b03382c6628a8a55098c34242baf", "parents": ["254f25a49861479251854ece13fc39438c603956"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092754 [wpt PR 64609] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322441, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-text-decor-4] Support percentages in text-decoration-inset\n\nWiden text-decoration-inset from \u003clength\u003e{1,2} to \u003clength-percentage\u003e{1,2}, per\nthe CSSWG resolution on csswg-drafts#8403.\n\nA percentage resolves against the inline size of the decorating box for box-decoration-break: slice, or of the individual box fragment for clone.\nSince a sliced box's inline size spans all of its fragments, TextBoxPainter now sums them (DecoratingBoxFragmentInlineSizes) instead of measuring the fragment being painted.\nThat sum also gives the inline size preceding/following this fragment, so a trimming inset larger than one fragment now carries over\ninto the next - a middle fragment can be trimmed, or vanish, without holding either endpoint of the box.\n\nInk overflow cannot resolve these percentages while building a line, because the basis is not known until every fragment exists.\nInlineContentBuilder therefore collects the decorating boxes whose inset may resolve negative while it walks the display boxes, and\nadds the outward overhang in a follow-up pass over the finished lines.\nStyleDifference compares insets with no basis, where two different percentages would look equal, so a change involving one now requires layout outright.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322441\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/320052@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 46d7800fb1b4c0e25cd80a5c73422d4c5c88890b\nwpt-pr: 64609\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-slice.html"], "git_node": "3e93ac733011351d32cb55d3783d4174273e55c7", "git_parents": ["784961dc34189598e64d5a68ae5b709a6babfe59"], "node": "78cefdddd9d175bc3ed8d7abb3b3b1bcaf174739", "parents": ["346667861d17b03382c6628a8a55098c34242baf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092760 [wpt PR 64605] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=325454, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[line-clamp] line-clamp on a float or an absolutely positioned box is ignored\n\n\u003cdiv style=\"position: absolute; width: 100px; line-clamp: 1\"\u003efirst line second line\u003c/div\u003e\n\nThe box should show one line with an ellipsis. LineClampUpdater keeps the clamp of the containing block out of\nfloats and out-of-flow boxes, but it also returned before looking at the box's own max-lines, so the box never\nclamped. Now it clamps its own content, and its lines still do not count towards an outer clamp since it\nestablishes an independent formatting context.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=325454\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/322551@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2ef1cfbdd9e33223010510a3afeb55c88b4e81d6\nwpt-pr: 64605\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/block-ellipsis-018.html"], "git_node": "72d89fc68390831c80056ea4c4eb69bde973129a", "git_parents": ["3e93ac733011351d32cb55d3783d4174273e55c7"], "node": "64e9c781096c3ad64acb77855d2874b3966a78c0", "parents": ["78cefdddd9d175bc3ed8d7abb3b3b1bcaf174739"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092765 [wpt PR 64613] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=318956, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-ruby] Implement the 'spaces' value for the ruby-overhang property\n\nUpdate 'ruby-overhang' to the current CSS Ruby Layout grammar 'auto | spaces',\nwith 'none' as a legacy value alias of 'spaces'. Previously the property was\n'auto | none', where 'none' fully disabled overhang.\nhttps://drafts.csswg.org/css-ruby-1/#propdef-ruby-overhang\n\n'ruby-overhang: spaces' allows a ruby annotation that is wider than its base to\noverhang adjacent content only over \"spaces\": preserved white space, no-break\nspace and other space separators, half of the advance of a fullwidth opening\n(inline-start) or closing (inline-end) punctuation, and a quarter of the advance\nof a fullwidth middle dot punctuation (either side). 'auto' keeps the\nuser-agent-defined behavior. Because 'none' is now an alias of 'spaces', it no\nlonger fully disables overhang.\n\n'none' is aliased to 'spaces' at parse time, so both the specified and computed\nvalues serialize as 'spaces'. In layout, RubyFormattingContext caps the overhang\ncomputed for the 'spaces' value to the overhangable advance at the adjacent edge,\ncomputed by overhangableSpaceAdvance() from the adjacent edge character's class\nplus already-laid-out geometry and the font size, without re-measuring text:\npreserved white space and tabs use the word-separator box advance; no-break space\nand other space separators use the advance by which the box's visual rect exceeds\nits ink overflow at the edge; and fullwidth opening/closing/middle-dot punctuation\nexpose half/half/quarter of a fullwidth advance (one em), sharing the\nfullWidthAdvance() helper with the existing 0.5ic overhang cap. The only case not\nyet handled is a fullwidth punctuation advance reduced by 'text-spacing-trim'\n(see FIXME).\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=318956\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/317569@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: bc459d819d2e6ce6e724e9860f00701b89fa7d3a\nwpt-pr: 64613\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ruby/parsing/ruby-overhang-valid.html"], "git_node": "626a6f073287408c7f6e910ec616775d0b38a13f", "git_parents": ["72d89fc68390831c80056ea4c4eb69bde973129a"], "node": "65117897cc3c756201a124b36130f11aa84eba64", "parents": ["64e9c781096c3ad64acb77855d2874b3966a78c0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "lilly \u003c173393835+cupidsity@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092772 [wpt PR 64610] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322282, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\ncorner-shape: algorithm for outset curves needs to be updated to match new algorithm\n\nAdopts https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/61696\n\nPasses existing tests\n\nWebKit's copies of css/css-borders/corner-shape/render-corner-shape.html are based on older upstream versions, so this applies WebKit's changes to the current ones.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322282\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/319661@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5d4e4618be799cd512853d3a700218da7bc67546\nwpt-pr: 64610\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-box-shadow-spread-elliptical.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-outline-offset-elliptical.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-scoop.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-superellipse-concave.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-superellipse-scoop.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/render-corner-shape.html"], "git_node": "069003c62cfdf4a6b3468f762e703c803bb27c15", "git_parents": ["626a6f073287408c7f6e910ec616775d0b38a13f"], "node": "65a229b446d5f933986f188adf4dba19734f1305", "parents": ["65117897cc3c756201a124b36130f11aa84eba64"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092772 [wpt PR 64610] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64610\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-box-shadow-spread-elliptical.html.ini"], "git_node": "df00f7a4cfe77545b12e655e0914e0271e710065", "git_parents": ["069003c62cfdf4a6b3468f762e703c803bb27c15"], "node": "29101100ca290c0df39ed522d585dde048b1deaa", "parents": ["65a229b446d5f933986f188adf4dba19734f1305"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092781 [wpt PR 64616] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319587, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WPT] white-space-trim-discard-inner-001.xht colors the brackets blue but its reference leaves them black\n\n\u003cstyle\u003e div { color: blue; } \u003c/style\u003e vs. \u003cstyle\u003e span { color: blue; } \u003c/style\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv\u003e[\u003cspan\u003e1 2\u003c/span\u003e]\u003c/div\u003e\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319587\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/317327@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3e2022aa8e0b8c5d51309c19da14da1394dbf595\nwpt-pr: 64616\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/white-space/white-space-trim-discard-inner-001.xht"], "git_node": "0fa68ba991d6019bf90982302b794b42fef35836", "git_parents": ["df00f7a4cfe77545b12e655e0914e0271e710065"], "node": "221d0c8762013bee36db2779429fad6c55be19d7", "parents": ["29101100ca290c0df39ed522d585dde048b1deaa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092788 [wpt PR 64617] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319211, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[CSS] Support the content property on the ::marker pseudo-element\n\nPer css-lists-3 \u00a73.3, when `content` on a ::marker is not `normal` the marker box\ncontents are generated from the `content` property \"exactly as for ::before\" \u2014 an\nanonymous sequence of strings, images, counters and quotes \u2014 taking precedence\nover both list-style-image and list-style-type. WebCore already parsed `content`\non ::marker (it is in the marker property allowlist) but ignored it at layout and\npaint time, always rendering the list-style marker instead.\n\nRenderListMarker stays a childless RenderBox for the common bullet/number case.\nWhen the computed ::marker style carries content data, RenderTreeBuilder::List\ngives the marker a single anonymous inline-block RenderBlockFlow child that holds\nthe generated content, built by reusing\n\nRenderTreeUpdater::GeneratedContent::createContentRenderers \u2014 the same machinery\n::before/::after use. The marker lays that box out at its max-content width,\noffsets it so its first-line baseline lands on the marker's primary-font baseline\n(so the content sits on the list item's baseline, like a text marker), paints it\nas an atomic inline across all phases, and records its visual/layout overflow.\n\nBecause `content` supersedes list-style, a content marker is never treated as an\nimage (isImage) or a bullet (widthUsesMetricsOfPrimaryFont), and its inline\nmargins follow the text path. `content: none` on ::marker suppresses the marker\nbox entirely. The marker is a text-decoration boundary, so a list's\ntext-decoration no longer propagates into generated marker content. `quotes` is\nadded to the ::marker property allowlist so open-quote/close-quote resolve against\nper-marker quotes (without this, enabling `content` regresses marker-quotes.html).\n\nThe feature is gated behind the CSSMarkerContent preference (status: preview):\nenabled in preview builds and layout tests, off by default in shipping. When\ndisabled, `content` on ::marker is ignored, exactly as before.\n\nStill-failing related tests:\nPre-existing bugs:\n\n  \u2014 the inside marker's max-content width is not propagated into the float's intrinsic width, so the item wraps.\n  Pre-existing inside-marker-in-float behavior, not content.\n  so it gets no marker and does not count in the list ordinal. Pre-existing, unrelated to content generation.\nNeeds work:\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319211\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/317211@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: dda9f5750e3ce6b8e6b074d493506aabc1a8c3b7\nwpt-pr: 64617\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/marker-content-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/marker-content-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/marker-content-003b.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/marker-content-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/marker-content-008.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/marker-content-015.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/marker-content-016.html"], "git_node": "a96271296aa4c65e5091129cd86d7caf2bc81c32", "git_parents": ["0fa68ba991d6019bf90982302b794b42fef35836"], "node": "58010d99f9937f29d5e574fdbf796cff03afbb9f", "parents": ["221d0c8762013bee36db2779429fad6c55be19d7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim Nguyen \u003cntim@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092789 [wpt PR 64611] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319831, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[white-space-trim] Add to white-space shorthand syntax\n\n(This is based on Tim Nguyen initial PR)\n\nThe syntax for the white-space shorthand is:\n\nnormal | pre | pre-wrap | pre-line | \u003c'white-space-collapse'\u003e || \u003c'text-wrap-mode'\u003e || \u003c'white-space-trim'\u003e\n\nSee: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-text-4/#white-space-property\n\nAdd 'white-space-trim' as the third longhand of the 'white-space' shorthand. The\nlegacy single-keyword forms (normal / pre / pre-wrap / pre-line) map to\n'white-space-trim: none' per the normative table in the spec, so they never combine\nwith a discard-* keyword. Serialization -- both of a declaration block\n(ShorthandSerializer) and of the computed value (Style::Extractor) -- only collapses\nto those legacy keywords when 'white-space-trim' is 'none'; otherwise it appends the\ntrim value and omits the other two longhands when they hold their initial value.\n\n'white-space-trim' is gated on the CSSWhiteSpaceTrimEnabled setting while\n'white-space' is not, so the shorthand parser gates only the consumption of the\ndiscard-* keywords and always sets the 'white-space-trim' longhand. That keeps the\nshorthand round-tripping when the setting is off, and matches how 'font' and\n'font-variant' handle the settings-gated 'font-variant-emoji' longhand.\n\nEditing copies 'white-space-trim' alongside the other two longhands. All three have\nto travel together: a partial longhand set makes the 'white-space' shorthand\nunserializable, so editing would start emitting 'white-space-collapse' /\n'text-wrap-mode' where it used to emit 'white-space'. It is therefore listed with the\ninheritable editing properties even though it is not an inherited property -- if only\nthe context style carries it, the white-space longhands never compare equal to the\ncontext and editing wraps content in redundant spans. The context comparison in\nremoveStyleInContextNotOverridenByMatchedRules also compares values rather than\nCSSValue identity, since 'white-space-trim' serializes to a list for any value other\nthan 'none'.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319831\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/318486@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 39ceeba5aad2ab21268ac0ea5af5051639024255\nwpt-pr: 64611\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/parsing/white-space-shorthand.html"], "git_node": "4fd24625066567104f3ce8d7288eddd6dfeae229", "git_parents": ["a96271296aa4c65e5091129cd86d7caf2bc81c32"], "node": "959340aa599d591ae642cd0bb3df06aca20402c2", "parents": ["58010d99f9937f29d5e574fdbf796cff03afbb9f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092789 [wpt PR 64611] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64611\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-text/parsing/white-space-shorthand.html.ini"], "git_node": "50b5806450ab0c53c5f8a84d0bd8d356ae7cd64f", "git_parents": ["4fd24625066567104f3ce8d7288eddd6dfeae229"], "node": "1240b95d2fb95cb1882e789b1b554108f9d45f83", "parents": ["959340aa599d591ae642cd0bb3df06aca20402c2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Fraser \u003csimon.fraser@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092790 [wpt PR 64621] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=317061, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[macOS x86_64] css/css-images tests are image diff failures\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=317061\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/315254@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c24ed48c8401e299ce4f23f4324b72cd278f3a81\nwpt-pr: 64621\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/image-orientation/image-orientation-background-properties.html"], "git_node": "42e536cb1b50c9ecbf83e81a21146bea1480d26a", "git_parents": ["50b5806450ab0c53c5f8a84d0bd8d356ae7cd64f"], "node": "5e764acc406b05581f3d39289cce517cf6e41c75", "parents": ["1240b95d2fb95cb1882e789b1b554108f9d45f83"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoav Weiss \u003cyoav.weiss@shopify.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092796 [wpt PR 64618] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=316647, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nNavigation Timing: cross-origin redirect opt-in should be based on destination origin.\n\nThis PR aligns the WebKit implementation with https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/pull/1931 and https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12513,\nand ensures that TAO opt-ins for navigation timing take the destination origin into account.\n\nNew iframe tests, plus test progressions.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=316647\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/317061@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5a686a30bc8638de1a161d781e4234a661116879\nwpt-pr: 64618\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-timing/redirect-tao.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-timing/resources/redirect-tao-helper.js"], "git_node": "7b4160c1a6acb61a67646ec0e6933e20ffbdafa4", "git_parents": ["42e536cb1b50c9ecbf83e81a21146bea1480d26a"], "node": "d061e4b754b982c689b5a94599eea146292b0e53", "parents": ["5e764acc406b05581f3d39289cce517cf6e41c75"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092796 [wpt PR 64618] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64618\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/navigation-timing/redirect-tao.html.ini"], "git_node": "9d31e89c19b46159fd7102aca12107ddb0eefdfb", "git_parents": ["7b4160c1a6acb61a67646ec0e6933e20ffbdafa4"], "node": "c248439bb76993f28054bf7ef4792f05e5caf942", "parents": ["d061e4b754b982c689b5a94599eea146292b0e53"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Fraser \u003csimon.fraser@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092798 [wpt PR 64622] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=317168, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd pixel tolerance to a couple of tests\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=317168\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/315266@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 793d35a1a281b43ca50964d11fd158df044dbdb0\nwpt-pr: 64622\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-emphasis-punctuation-2.html"], "git_node": "7dd60c6bf5ec7512f5b7e08b3514c9198c035287", "git_parents": ["9d31e89c19b46159fd7102aca12107ddb0eefdfb"], "node": "27c5f39644e7e50ccb9ea11821953bac82fb0ad3", "parents": ["c248439bb76993f28054bf7ef4792f05e5caf942"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003cahmad.saleem792+github@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092802 [wpt PR 64620] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=318206, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMisnamed local static voiceAttr in WebVTTElement::langAttributeName()\n\nThe local NeverDestroyed\u003cQualifiedName\u003e in langAttributeName() was\ncopy-pasted from voiceAttributeName() and left named voiceAttr, even\nthough it holds the \"lang\" attribute name. Rename it to langAttr to\nmatch its purpose.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=318206\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/316239@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b08ca8f669f5c2e683d2b6d26a4e8326991eafe2\nwpt-pr: 64620\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/api/VTTCue/getCueAsHTML.html"], "git_node": "eb6cef65b160b64a437ccb316c99b67a2fb7afd3", "git_parents": ["7dd60c6bf5ec7512f5b7e08b3514c9198c035287"], "node": "a1ebc8a4af26a9da68a79ecbb2b40c8c6bc8d433", "parents": ["27c5f39644e7e50ccb9ea11821953bac82fb0ad3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003cahmad.saleem792+github@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092805 [wpt PR 64619] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319182, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nScroll To Text Fragment: simplify MIME-type gate and add mixed-case coverage\n\nFollow-up to 316976@main. ParsedContentType::mimeType() already returns an\nASCII-lowercased essence (setContentType() calls convertToASCIILowercase()),\nso the equalLettersIgnoringASCIICase() comparisons in scrollToTextFragment()\nwere redundant. Compare the parsed MIME type directly against the lowercase\nliterals \"text/html\" and \"text/plain\", and note in a comment that the string\nis already lowercased.\n\nAlso add WPT coverage for a document served with a mixed-case Content-Type\n(\"Text/HTML; charset=UTF-8\") to pin the case-insensitive normalization.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319182\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/316990@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3fd60c81902d068e470140fd354ac4b5ad39d652\nwpt-pr: 64619\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-to-text-fragment/text-directive-mime-type-parameter.html"], "git_node": "e2f80b3e80b1d1556c5c2b448cb782303961ffd6", "git_parents": ["eb6cef65b160b64a437ccb316c99b67a2fb7afd3"], "node": "66ff187867dd453b6206e40307f7bc0fa935c238", "parents": ["a1ebc8a4af26a9da68a79ecbb2b40c8c6bc8d433"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092805 [wpt PR 64619] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64619\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-to-text-fragment/text-directive-mime-type-parameter.html.ini"], "git_node": "be37f2d34a28a782ec9f6549d88cb78a90a7a565", "git_parents": ["e2f80b3e80b1d1556c5c2b448cb782303961ffd6"], "node": "ccf5794465a9c3895cdd5c31cfafe27d4f6f1c8d", "parents": ["66ff187867dd453b6206e40307f7bc0fa935c238"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Diego De La Toba \u003cd_delatoba@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092806 [wpt PR 64628] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=310211, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[macOS] webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/cue/background_shorthand_css_relative_url.html is a flaky image diff\n\nThe test is flaky because the onplaying event handler called takeScreenshot() immediately after pausing the video.\nThis results in a blank screenshot (no cue text visible) compared against the reference that always shows the text\ndue to video rendering times being slower on debug and release builds under load.\n\nFix in background_shorthand_css_relative_url.html: Replace takeScreenshot() with takeScreenshotDelayed(10)\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=310211\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/310661@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 67d71c0de2b64a9aba9794277302f2b99e7e1ca6\nwpt-pr: 64628\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webvtt/rendering/cues-with-video/processing-model/selectors/cue/background_shorthand_css_relative_url.html"], "git_node": "b7724d3fa9f0162c2abce039df0172d047ef74dd", "git_parents": ["be37f2d34a28a782ec9f6549d88cb78a90a7a565"], "node": "24c4462b33108f2d1b9b4f9eb9579ba651428da8", "parents": ["ccf5794465a9c3895cdd5c31cfafe27d4f6f1c8d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092808 [wpt PR 64624] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=315938, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nImported css/CSS2 reftests report ImageOnlyFailure because the css/CSS2/support/ directory is missing\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=315938\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/314236@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 98424959038e48141023c0c32054d2bbb8161b55\nwpt-pr: 64624\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/CSS2/normal-flow/max-height-applies-to-012.xht", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/CSS2/normal-flow/max-width-applies-to-012.xht", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/CSS2/normal-flow/min-height-applies-to-012.xht", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/CSS2/normal-flow/min-width-applies-to-012.xht", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/CSS2/normal-flow/width-applies-to-012.xht"], "git_node": "23608921f85ad2ba753fbd16d4aec49d065eb02d", "git_parents": ["b7724d3fa9f0162c2abce039df0172d047ef74dd"], "node": "6910ac5fc175b0d2eb257f10c04cef0eee3c9dc3", "parents": ["24c4462b33108f2d1b9b4f9eb9579ba651428da8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Carlos Garcia Campos \u003ccgarcia@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092810 [wpt PR 64625] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=313540, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[GTK][WPE] Enable skia compositor by default\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=313540\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/313297@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f40b6192061a6d663e08472fd8c7463b40336631\nwpt-pr: 64625\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-transforms/perspective-transforms-equivalence.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-transforms/scale-transform-filtered-text.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/backdrop-filter-clip-rect-2.html"], "git_node": "48e99e1ad52fa16b3b509deba397ad9bdb131a7e", "git_parents": ["23608921f85ad2ba753fbd16d4aec49d065eb02d"], "node": "4fc4f0b2b349b9ed0b1b1d20e88b249a18ec241d", "parents": ["6910ac5fc175b0d2eb257f10c04cef0eee3c9dc3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Diego De La Toba \u003cd_delatoba@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092812 [wpt PR 64626] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=309917, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[MacOS IOS] css/css-viewport/zoom/iframe-zoom-nested.html is a flaky image diff\n\nThis test is failing due to two timing issues:\n\n 1. The test file registers its message listener inside the load handler. Each nested leaf.html calls top.postMessage(\"leaf_loaded\") on its own\n  load event, and these messages can arrive before the main window's load fires. When that happens, they're silently dropped and\n takeScreenshot() is never called, causing a timeout.\n 2. The reference files have no waiting mechanism, so the test harness can capture the screenshot before the nested iframes have finished\n loading, causing flaky image failures.\n\n Modified iframe-zoom-nested.html:\n Moved the message listener registration to the top level so it's ready immediately.\n\n Modified iframe-zoom-nested-expected.html and iframe-zoom-nested-ref.html:\n Added reftest-wait and the same message-based waiting mechanism used by the test file.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=309917\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/312232@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 48338c09e39d2eb66c29b831f7eed3441c69a41f\nwpt-pr: 64626\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/reference/iframe-zoom-nested-ref.html"], "git_node": "13e247ea0d6f571cbb9e9d16ae05385572055a73", "git_parents": ["48e99e1ad52fa16b3b509deba397ad9bdb131a7e"], "node": "42a13d921e2052a27ce225197d3d7cc68b1b255c", "parents": ["4fc4f0b2b349b9ed0b1b1d20e88b249a18ec241d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092812 [wpt PR 64626] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64626\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-viewport/zoom/iframe-zoom-nested.html.ini"], "git_node": "5f132764a8f8bf91fdf2ff99c478babac25c0488", "git_parents": ["13e247ea0d6f571cbb9e9d16ae05385572055a73"], "node": "e4f31ef31f65ca67032eff9cd9db88e57f0917bc", "parents": ["42a13d921e2052a27ce225197d3d7cc68b1b255c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Diego De La Toba \u003cd_delatoba@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092814 [wpt PR 64629] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=310680, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[iOS release] css/css-writing-modes/text-orientation-mixed-srl-016.xht is a flaky image diff\n\nThe test is flaky due to small pixel inconsistencies when rendering:\nWithout reftest-wait, screenshots can be taken as soon as the load event fires.\nThe font may be \"loaded\" but may not have completed rendering with it in a fully\nsettled state. The double requestAnimationFrame after fonts.ready\nguarantees both pages have completed at least one full rendering cycle with the final\nfont before the screenshot, making the comparison deterministic.\n\nAll three files (test, ref, expected) received the same two changes:\n\n1. class=\"reftest-wait\" on \u003chtml\u003e\n2. Synchronization script at end of \u003cbody\u003e\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=310680\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/310535@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c2ea31c9c9e4dadc7def9066eff642922d42925c\nwpt-pr: 64629\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/text-orientation-mixed-srl-016-ref.xht", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/text-orientation-mixed-srl-016.xht"], "git_node": "cb337de148a26050e5c8f78594c6f9f09ffba094", "git_parents": ["5f132764a8f8bf91fdf2ff99c478babac25c0488"], "node": "b70792563370b2d75e4cb6d79fbbb5988563d9b6", "parents": ["e4f31ef31f65ca67032eff9cd9db88e57f0917bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092816 [wpt PR 64632] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=303826, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSpeculationRules - Support Clear-Site-Data\n\nThis adds support for `Clear-Site-Data: prefetchCache`.\n\nNo new tests, but existing tests progress.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=303826\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/304470@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d72444def0572a9fbefec2fdaf534a33bfcb8493\nwpt-pr: 64632\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prefetch/clear-prefetch-cache-after-clear-site-data-cache.https.html"], "git_node": "be971d49c4fc64d1cbfe63c141ab273c68c108da", "git_parents": ["cb337de148a26050e5c8f78594c6f9f09ffba094"], "node": "818878dfe2d7989b2759bb30a02f017f680e8a48", "parents": ["b70792563370b2d75e4cb6d79fbbb5988563d9b6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriele Cabrini \u003cgabriele@gabrielecabrini.it\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092817 [wpt PR 64572] - script: Use ensure_pre_insertion_validity in Node.replaceChild, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nscript: Use ensure_pre_insertion_validity in Node.replaceChild\n\nSigned-off-by: Gabriele Cabrini \u003cgabriele@gabrielecabrini.it\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6e8638b1a78a00d3d7e0818cdf1b7cd82143ab30\nwpt-pr: 64572\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/crashtests/replaceChild-host-including-ancestor-crash.html"], "git_node": "8d21823dcde3fdf42784d9d9c7f4387a51a44f71", "git_parents": ["be971d49c4fc64d1cbfe63c141ab273c68c108da"], "node": "a8d1e424b6d10afbb7688436c11e8fb95a1bddfc", "parents": ["818878dfe2d7989b2759bb30a02f017f680e8a48"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim van der Lippe \u003ctvanderlippe@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092820 [wpt PR 64499] - script, net: Set user activation for navigation requests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nscript, net: Set user activation for navigation requests\n\nThe `sec-fetch-user` header should only be set when the window has\nreceived a user interaction. Before, we would always send it for each\nnavigation request, which is wrong.\n\nBased on the investigation in\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/13169 and the WhatWG Matrix chat,\nthe relevant tests turned out to be wrong. They would bless the wrong\nwindow and these tests fail in all browsers. Therefore, this PR also\nupdates the relevant tests and ensures that they pass in all browsers.\n\nCloses https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/13169\n\nTesting: new WPT tests passing and fixed existing tests\n\nSigned-off-by: Tim van der Lippe \u003ctvanderlippe@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 740ca1a1ead7b3e3fc3866ef77f79b689f8129b5\nwpt-pr: 64499\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/metadata/generated/element-a.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/metadata/generated/element-a.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/metadata/generated/element-area.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/metadata/generated/element-area.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/metadata/generated/window-location.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/metadata/generated/window-location.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/metadata/tools/generate.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/metadata/tools/templates/element-a.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/metadata/tools/templates/element-area.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/metadata/tools/templates/window-location.sub.html"], "git_node": "96666921768e2f80cbff1684288e6f1eeec34d6d", "git_parents": ["8d21823dcde3fdf42784d9d9c7f4387a51a44f71"], "node": "b03e616747b486c69a878bf5625f604311de7925", "parents": ["a8d1e424b6d10afbb7688436c11e8fb95a1bddfc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092820 [wpt PR 64499] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64499\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/metadata/generated/element-a.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/metadata/generated/element-area.https.sub.html.ini"], "git_node": "9d17b731b829fe1e62b3471942e0777f39cd2d82", "git_parents": ["96666921768e2f80cbff1684288e6f1eeec34d6d"], "node": "05c68342074b458007e80147d98db9966225cb28", "parents": ["b03e616747b486c69a878bf5625f604311de7925"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003cahmad.saleem792+github@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092827 [wpt PR 64635] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326641, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nrequestIdleCallback callbacks stop running after removing a same-origin iframe that had a pending setTimeout\n\nThis patch aligns WebKit with Gecko / Firefox and Blink / Chromium.\n\nEventLoopTaskGroup::markAsReadyToStop() stops the group's timers, which clears each\ntimer's task. Once that happens, EventLoopTimer::group() returns null, so when the\nowner later drops its EventLoopTimerHandle, the handle's destructor never calls\nremoveScheduledTimer(). That call is the only thing that clears\nEventLoop::m_nextTimerFireTimeCache. The timer is destroyed and quietly drops out of\nthe event loop's weak timer sets, but the cache keeps its old fire time.\n\nSame-origin frames share a WindowEventLoop. When an iframe with a pending setTimeout\nis removed, the parent's event loop keeps reporting the dead timer's fire time. After\nthat time passes, WindowEventLoop::opportunisticallyRunIdleCallbacks() always sees\nwork due immediately, so it keeps re-arming the idle timer and never starts an idle\nperiod. Idle callbacks without a timeout never run until some other timer is\nscheduled in that event loop.\n\nAlso, EventLoop::nextTimerFireTime() did not skip stopped timers. A stopped TimerBase\nreports a fire time of 0, so any stopped timer that was still referenced made it look\nas if timer work was already overdue.\n\nFix both: clear the fire-time cache after markAsReadyToStop() stops the group's\ntimers, and ignore inactive timers when computing the next fire time.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=326641\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/323148@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b46d36d7cab1a037890acd8668a7b51f1615e2a8\nwpt-pr: 64635\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/lint.ignore", "testing/web-platform/tests/requestidlecallback/callback-after-removed-frame-with-pending-timeout.html"], "git_node": "98a309a564c85356aa9719e141930e8eb27b6017", "git_parents": ["9d17b731b829fe1e62b3471942e0777f39cd2d82"], "node": "94e059217df710d3dc107f56bc6e82b995344c56", "parents": ["05c68342074b458007e80147d98db9966225cb28"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092842 [wpt PR 64528] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=329441, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nA page in the back/forward cache shares processes with a document of the page in the same browsing context group\n\nSince 324033@main, a same-site navigation can move the main frame to another\nprocess when only one of the documents has a Document-Isolation-Policy. The page\nstays in its browsing context group, so the document that goes into the\nback/forward cache keeps sharing the group's processes with the new one. A frame\nof the new document could then be sent to a process where the page's WebPage is\nthe cached one, and never load, which made\nlocation-replace-keeps-entry.tentative.https.html time out after\nisolate-and-require-corp.tentative.https.html. And evicting the cached document\nclosed the new document's remote pages.\n\nNow, under site isolation, a document doesn't go into the back/forward cache\nwhen the next one stays in its group, and a cached document is dropped when the\npage goes back or forward past it to a document in its group. This loses the\nback/forward cache for same-site navigations between documents with and without\na policy, which 324262@main enabled, until the multi-process back/forward cache\ncan keep a cached document in its process's WebPage.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=329441\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 34833c35d1d7cbb7955f47615e740b5101e370ff\nwpt-pr: 64528\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/back-forward-cache-same-origin-frames.tentative.https.html"], "git_node": "b5dde6a5f14d935a5a2aa8ca47f954e902562085", "git_parents": ["98a309a564c85356aa9719e141930e8eb27b6017"], "node": "4e79e34b87a274ca478edc9eb68207338786ab37", "parents": ["94e059217df710d3dc107f56bc6e82b995344c56"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoav Weiss \u003cyoav.weiss@shopify.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092844 [wpt PR 64630] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=306605, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSpeculationRules - JSON rules with no charset interpreted as UTF-8\n\nThis PR aligns the implementation with the spec and enforces UTF-8 encoding on external JSON rules.\nThis resolves the issue, as resources without explicit encoding will now be properly processed.\n\nNo new test files, but added new test cases.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=306605\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/306513@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 87ee4a732dd360c9fc18826971b2ebd82cbb3b95\nwpt-pr: 64630\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prefetch/out-of-document-rule-set.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prefetch/resources/ruleset.py"], "git_node": "d3fc740448879afa404d2d4b72d949880eee624c", "git_parents": ["b5dde6a5f14d935a5a2aa8ca47f954e902562085"], "node": "8213a1de0dbff33da93dc3edfcbe6f2fa7b0ff71", "parents": ["4e79e34b87a274ca478edc9eb68207338786ab37"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Javier Fern\u00e1ndez Garc\u00eda-Boente \u003cjfernandez@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092847 [wpt PR 64573] - [css-backgrounds] Initial value handling in the background shorthand, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-backgrounds] Initial value handling in the background shorthand\n\nThe 'background' shorthand has two bugs, and they have to be fixed\ntogether.\n\nFirst, it stores the CSS-wide keyword 'initial' for every longhand the\nauthor left out, so reading one back reports the keyword:\n\n    el.style.background = 'none';\n    el.style.backgroundAttachment;  // \"initial\", should be \"scroll\"\n\ncss-cascade-5 section 3 says a missing sub-property is assigned its\ninitial value, not the keyword that stands for it. css-backgrounds-3\nsection 2.10 says the same for this shorthand: it \"first sets the\ncorresponding value of each of background-image ... to that property's\ninitial value\". Every other engine reports \"scroll\".\n\nSecond, the serializer omits only the literal keyword, not values that\nare equal to the initial value:\n\n    el.style.background = 'repeat';\n    el.style.background;  // \"repeat\", should be \"none\"\n\nCSSOM says a component that can be omitted without changing the meaning\nof the value must be omitted. See also crbug.com/40423296.\n\nFixing only the first bug would make \"background: none\" serialize as\n\"none 0% 0% / auto repeat scroll padding-box border-box transparent\", so\nthis CL does both.\n\nBug: 40894424, 552675460, 40423296, 552689413,\nChange-Id: Iae1e6b01252f3a6f2d9aa89e2236abe1c7f1404a\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8301652\nCommit-Queue: Javier Fernandez \u003cjfernandez@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1733797}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ad73e06c5972cf5fbd913bcb118ab7b1b12804c1\nwpt-pr: 64573\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/parsing/mask-shorthand-serialization.html"], "git_node": "b46a4d4d03725a9ef55f70d029d573ec89693f40", "git_parents": ["d3fc740448879afa404d2d4b72d949880eee624c"], "node": "c7e35c8024d6ab6059f65099a18d7b5f5b0432ff", "parents": ["8213a1de0dbff33da93dc3edfcbe6f2fa7b0ff71"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoav Weiss \u003cyoav.weiss@shopify.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092848 [wpt PR 64633] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=295193, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nImplement speculation rules - same origin conservative prefetch\n\nThis implements an initial version of same-origin prefetch speculation rules.\n\nThe feature enables prefetching an HTML document ahead of time (\"immediate\" eagerness),\nor when the user started clicking an anchor element pointing at it (\"conservative\" eagerness).\nThat prefetched document is then used when the user actually navigates to this URL,\nresulting in significant performance improvements.\nSubresources of the prefetched document are not yet loaded before navigation, nor does it begin its processing.\n\nHTML spec PR for speculation rules: https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11426\nSpec for the prefetch parts: https://wicg.github.io/nav-speculation/prefetch.html\n\nAlso give speculation-rules/prefetch/clear-prefetch-cache-after-clear-site-data-cache.https.html a long timeout. It runs close to the default one, so CI flags it as slow whenever clear-site-data-cache.py changes.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=295193\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/300829@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c12e894440724feae77c323e6d3df00146ef8621\nwpt-pr: 64633\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/clear-site-data/support/clear-site-data-cache.py"], "git_node": "a4c5015a88de2f68169581a32a0e17ecaad9e9d5", "git_parents": ["b46a4d4d03725a9ef55f70d029d573ec89693f40"], "node": "dc370da3e793610d3eb59d916fbd26f061225e42", "parents": ["c7e35c8024d6ab6059f65099a18d7b5f5b0432ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Fraser \u003csimon.fraser@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092850 [wpt PR 64649] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=316018, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nIMPORT(314164@main): [iOS] css/css-images tests are failing with image diffs\n\nUpstream has its own fuzzy tolerance for css/css-images/gradients-with-border.html, css/css-images/multiple-position-color-stop-linear.html, so this raises each range to cover both.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=316018\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/315248@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 831c21436f8865de17be0f2334482cf4d701b1e6\nwpt-pr: 64649\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/gradients-with-border.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/multiple-position-color-stop-linear.html"], "git_node": "11998d7b2776edb257040f9188653a17fe7fee30", "git_parents": ["a4c5015a88de2f68169581a32a0e17ecaad9e9d5"], "node": "a2bc8de91a679aff11c0114e52f33fe55ee8e8f6", "parents": ["dc370da3e793610d3eb59d916fbd26f061225e42"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alejandro G. Castro \u003calex@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092854 [wpt PR 64645] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324539, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WPE][GTK] Use distance fields for small paths in the GPU renderer\n\nSkia keeps two different atlas caches for small paths. The bitmap key is\nbuilt from the shape key, the upper 2x2 of the CTM and 8 bits each of the\nsubpixel translation, while the distance field key only holds the shape key\nand the power of two dimension the field was generated at. Any path drawn\nunder an animated transform therefore misses the bitmap atlas on every frame\nand pays a CPU re-raster, a texture upload and the atlas work that follows,\nbut the distance field entry is reused.\n\nSkia already selects distance fields unconditionally on Android for this\nreason. We added support for Skia to allow picking the behaviour when\ncompiling, now it is part of the library and can be enabled with the\nbuild flag: SK_GANESH_SMALL_PATH_DISTANCE_FIELD_ALWAYS.\n\nThis improve Suits for MotionMark in rpi4 and desktop, we are still not\nsure the effect everywhere so we activate it to verify what are we\ngetting.\n\nThe patch just adds the build option in the compilation.\n\nApparently distance field rasterization is not pixel identical to the bitmap\natlas. Edge coverage differs slightly, and that is enough to break nine\nreftests. Updated the tolerances.\n\nUpstream has its own fuzzy tolerance for css/css-transforms/transform-input-017.html, so this raises each range to cover both.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=324539\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/321588@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: be2b3e4491291114fa3ff5b379e7318f49e15235\nwpt-pr: 64645\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-transforms/transform-input-017.html"], "git_node": "c8e7552c11c1e1db24d2c5f77ff24202a414d23a", "git_parents": ["11998d7b2776edb257040f9188653a17fe7fee30"], "node": "397263869e45f1ff8cc2afe0a300acfc1e4f1663", "parents": ["a2bc8de91a679aff11c0114e52f33fe55ee8e8f6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nikolas Zimmermann \u003cnzimmermann@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092856 [wpt PR 64648] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=315455, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[GTK][WPE] Bump wkdev-sdk to Ubuntu 26.04 based SDK\n\nSwitch to Ubuntu 26.04 \"Resolute Raccoon\" based SDK and rebaseline the\nglib results affected by the new toolchain.\n\nThe wkdev SDK base image moved from Ubuntu 24.04 (libxml2 2.9.14) to\nUbuntu 26.04 (libxml2 2.15.2). The newer libxml2 reworded several XML\nparser diagnostics, which surface in test output, so need to rebaseline.\n\nThese are message-only changes from the parser, with no behavioural\nchange in WebKit. The remaining rebaselines are unrelated to libxml2:\nSelectors API conformance progressions, x-mac-thai decoding now parsing\ncorrectly after the ICU update, and SVG render-tree sub-pixel precision\ndiffs from the new toolchain math.\n\nUpstream has its own fuzzy tolerance for css/css-backgrounds/border-radius-clipping-with-transform-001.html, css/css-transforms/transform-background-001.html, css/css-transforms/transform-background-002.html, so this raises each range to cover both.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=315455\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/315785@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 57e727d101ddc771b04aeb247d3809639fa4b730\nwpt-pr: 64648\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-backgrounds/border-radius-clipping-with-transform-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-transforms/transform-background-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-transforms/transform-background-002.html"], "git_node": "8b6761d3cbb4ae1560befac75b9f300b4966470d", "git_parents": ["c8e7552c11c1e1db24d2c5f77ff24202a414d23a"], "node": "a3066763420a8c864fa6f6b9670a37f43a3ef5df", "parents": ["397263869e45f1ff8cc2afe0a300acfc1e4f1663"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092862 [wpt PR 64646] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322441, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-text-decor-4] Support percentages in text-decoration-inset\n\nWiden text-decoration-inset from \u003clength\u003e{1,2} to \u003clength-percentage\u003e{1,2}, per\nthe CSSWG resolution on csswg-drafts#8403.\n\nA percentage resolves against the inline size of the decorating box for box-decoration-break: slice, or of the individual box fragment for clone.\nSince a sliced box's inline size spans all of its fragments, TextBoxPainter now sums them (DecoratingBoxFragmentInlineSizes) instead of measuring the fragment being painted.\nThat sum also gives the inline size preceding/following this fragment, so a trimming inset larger than one fragment now carries over\ninto the next - a middle fragment can be trimmed, or vanish, without holding either endpoint of the box.\n\nInk overflow cannot resolve these percentages while building a line, because the basis is not known until every fragment exists.\nInlineContentBuilder therefore collects the decorating boxes whose inset may resolve negative while it walks the display boxes, and\nadds the outward overhang in a follow-up pass over the finished lines.\nStyleDifference compares insets with no basis, where two different percentages would look equal, so a change involving one now requires layout outright.\n\nUpstream has its own fuzzy tolerance for css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-009.html, so this raises each range to cover both.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322441\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/320052@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5ab87b9008e016a236f3eb02104bcb4bd1426ba4\nwpt-pr: 64646\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-009.html"], "git_node": "da0c850cb02f34e87013edcb87eb279270327b04", "git_parents": ["8b6761d3cbb4ae1560befac75b9f300b4966470d"], "node": "5152bb8eaab1b087dc1da22d003159ca45be5eeb", "parents": ["a3066763420a8c864fa6f6b9670a37f43a3ef5df"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antti Koivisto \u003cantti@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092864 [wpt PR 64644] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328165, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Cocoa] CoreGraphics draws uninitialized blurred areas for a blur style\n\nTransparencyLayerContextSwitcher nests a transparency layer for each CGStyle\nfilter. When an effect has outsets, such as blur, the filter region extends\nbeyond the imageRect. WebKit fills the imageRect with the target element's\ndrawing, but CoreGraphics may modify pixels within the imageRect and can also\npopulate the filterRegion, which equals imageRect plus the outsets.\n\nTesting some filter layout tests on macOS 27 revealed that the outset area of\nthe transparency layer is sometimes left uninitialized, producing garbage pixels\nwhen a blur style is applied. The issue disappears when accelerated drawing is\ndisabled, suggesting a system framework bug; it has been reported internally as\nrdar://190563103.\n\nThe workaround is to clear the filterRegion after all transparency layers have\nbeen created. A CSS filter's filterRegion is the union of the filterRegions of\nits individual effects, and each effect's filterRegion is its imageRect expanded\nby that effect's outset.\n\nCovered by: css3/filters/effect-combined.html\n            css3/filters/filter-on-overflow-hidden.html\n\nUpstream has its own fuzzy tolerance for css/filter-effects/backdrop-filters-saturate.html, so this raises each range to cover both.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=328165\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324350@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: edd61ca19aa3717491e3aa3146a7dfeca5807967\nwpt-pr: 64644\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/backdrop-filters-saturate.html"], "git_node": "3fee25f2ea492febcb6f4ec1fc12696ebe3eb941", "git_parents": ["da0c850cb02f34e87013edcb87eb279270327b04"], "node": "fa00bceb1c09f27820c51589dc55d44e2293980e", "parents": ["5152bb8eaab1b087dc1da22d003159ca45be5eeb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092870 [wpt PR 64647] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319178, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-text-decor-4] Implement the text-decoration-inset property\n\nAdd the CSS Text Decoration Level 4 'text-decoration-inset' property\n(auto | \u003clength\u003e{1,2}), gated behind the cssTextDecorationInsetEnabled setting.\n\nThe property adjusts the start and end endpoints of the line decorations drawn by\na decorating box (underline, overline, line-through). A positive \u003clength\u003e moves\nan endpoint inward, trimming the decoration; a negative \u003clength\u003e moves it outward,\nextending it. A single value applies to both endpoints; two values are the start\nand the end. 'auto' lets the UA choose an inset so that two adjacent identical\nunderlined elements do not appear to share a single continuous underline (e.g.\nfor Chinese, where underlining is a form of punctuation); it is distinct from 0.\n\n1. It is stored as a new Style::TextDecorationInset value type (a keyword-or-length-\npair) in NonInheritedRareData, parsed grammar-driven, and animated by computed\nvalue.\n2. The inset is applied at paint time in TextBoxPainter, which shifts the\ndecoration's inline origin and shrinks/grows its length (because text-decoration-\ninset and box-decoration-break are not inherited, a decoration that propagates\nfrom an ancestor box down to the (root inline) box that paints it)\n3. box-decoration-break is then honored via the inline box's closed edges: with 'slice' the start\ninset only affects the first fragment's start edge and the end inset the last\nfragment's end edge; with 'clone' both edges of every fragment are inset.\n4. Endpoints are also gated on the marked-text piece that actually reaches the box's\nlogical start/end, so a decoration split into several marked texts (selection,\ndocument markers, highlights) stays continuous instead of being trimmed at the\ninterior boundaries.\n5. Because a negative inset extends the decoration past the text\nbox, decoration ink overflow is expanded by the outward amount, and StyleDifference\ntreats an inset change as affecting repaint and visual overflow so dynamic/animated\nchanges invalidate correctly.\n\nHorizontal and vertical writing modes (including sideways-rl/lr and orthogonal\nblocks), in both inline directions, are supported, as is the text-decoration-skip-\nink interaction (its skip gaps are measured against the underline's bounding box,\nwhich already tracks the inset-shifted origin, so they stay aligned to the glyphs).\nAcross a bidi direction boundary the decoration is painted one segment per run; the\ncomponent of the inset that shifts the decoration as a whole is applied to every\nsegment (so the seam between runs moves with it rather than being pinned), while the\nextend/trim overhang is applied only at the segment reaching the decoration's visual\nstart/end.\n\nUpstream has its own fuzzy tolerance for css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-008.html, so this raises each range to cover both.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319178\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/317230@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0169c9a1600fb78f097de1da05fd287c2e69eafd\nwpt-pr: 64647\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-008.html"], "git_node": "40eaa2d86648826385764dab6ed75ca6d013f0ae", "git_parents": ["3fee25f2ea492febcb6f4ec1fc12696ebe3eb941"], "node": "8a14755372565b5e41cf90f08f06c5033e208de9", "parents": ["fa00bceb1c09f27820c51589dc55d44e2293980e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003cahmad.saleem792+github@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092914 [wpt PR 64653] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=317524, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nArrayBuffer-backed I420/NV12 VideoFrame with codedHeight larger than visibleRect.height renders chroma offset\n\nThis patch aligns WebKit with Gecko / Firefox and Blink / Chromium.\n\nA buffer-backed VideoFrame is laid out for its coded size, with visibleRect only\ncropping the output. But createI420/createI420A/createNV12 derived each chroma\nplane's offset from the visible output height instead of the coded plane height,\nso a frame whose codedHeight exceeds visibleRect.height (e.g. coded 1920x1088\nshown as 1920x1080, or 320x196 shown as 320x180) read the bottom Y rows as chroma,\nproducing a chroma offset. Use the coded plane height (sourceHeight /\ndestinationOffset) for the offsets; the output size and crop are unchanged\n\nUpstream has changed this file since WebKit last imported it, so this adds the test to upstream's current version.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=317524\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/315742@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6603f3efbdd761402ff957c82b3616a26f92b4cd\nwpt-pr: 64653\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/videoFrame-copyTo.any.js"], "git_node": "1dee53c2579649908707033fe9e8c606c21d8137", "git_parents": ["40eaa2d86648826385764dab6ed75ca6d013f0ae"], "node": "0533525a70c2128860717b7822d35683b5d3fb2c", "parents": ["8a14755372565b5e41cf90f08f06c5033e208de9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092914 [wpt PR 64653] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64653\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/videoFrame-copyTo.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "b75095c3f1bfacee2f4e15dee254e85d291aed10", "git_parents": ["1dee53c2579649908707033fe9e8c606c21d8137"], "node": "69962bfccb51512ba5db668103cc36bcd03bc8af", "parents": ["0533525a70c2128860717b7822d35683b5d3fb2c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Fraser \u003csimon.fraser@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092917 [wpt PR 64650] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=317061, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[macOS x86_64] css/css-images tests are image diff failures\n\nUpstream has its own fuzzy tolerance for css/css-images/tiled-radial-gradients.html, so this raises each range to cover both.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=317061\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/315254@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 63e2cf0eed65ac43b69c81dc1b74f14e8452c3ce\nwpt-pr: 64650\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/tiled-radial-gradients.html"], "git_node": "c68803271015a7a2d88c91731f10c1a8305d001d", "git_parents": ["b75095c3f1bfacee2f4e15dee254e85d291aed10"], "node": "479a61a83935ec44671651bfcecb920478de783e", "parents": ["69962bfccb51512ba5db668103cc36bcd03bc8af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jean-Yves Avenard \u003cjya@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092919 [wpt PR 64652] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=281816, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAll MediaRecorderPrivate should be running in the web content process.\n\nWe extend on the work started with the MediaRecorderPrivateWriterWebM introduced in 285061@main.\nWe add a new MediaRecorderPrivateEncoder that performs the encoding, encoded frames interleaving management\nand writing through the specialised MediaRecorderPrivateWriter.\n\nThis new MediaRecorderPrivate can encode into any audio codec supported by AVFoundation (though only opus and AAC is enabled for now)\nand all video codecs supported by VideoEncoder with webm (vp8, vp9) and mp4 (h264, h265, av1).\n\nThe code runs in its dedicated WorkQueue.\n\nOne of the key change which added a significant amount of technical complexity is that while we will generate 2s GOP\na call to MediaRecorder.requestData() will return fully playable media segment, formed such as each new segment starts\nwith a keyframe. The generated media is MSE compatible.\nThis way, the page fully controls the duration of the media segments generated by either setting\na time slice when creating a MediaRecorder or calling requestData() at regular interval.\n\nWhen a new segment is required by the page, we flush all pending frames received to that point. As the audio encoder\nhas a certain latency, we may need to wait for a future audio frame to come which would allow the audio for the\ncurrent time to be available. When we are streaming, this is not a problem ; however if the recording has been paused\nno audio will be coming. So instead will fully drain the encoder. As a side effect, resuming the recording\nmay cause an audible silence for the duration of the codec delay (55ms with Opus content).\nIn practice, this may not be noticeable as pausing and resuming a recording would produce noticeable\nartifacts with audio.\n\nAnother technical change with the previous webm recorder is that the video time is now set to use\nthe start time of the last appended audio frame rather than the end. This too is also a consequence of the audio encoder\nhaving a set latency and allowed for some simplifications in the code.\n\nThe new MediaRecorder add supports for the codec to be set and the mimetype for the content generated will\nbe mostly accurate (we use static values with common profiles rather than attempting to determing accurately\nthings like the codec level and profile.\n\nThe RemoteMediaRecorder being no longer used is fully removed along the related files.\nThe class MediaRecorderProvider and its overrides are removed.\n\nTests amended and corrected to reflect the more accurate behaviors.\n\nUpstream has changed this file since WebKit last imported it, so this applies the change to upstream's current version. Its video regexes now also allow x- subtypes, so digits are allowed in the other alternative.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=281816\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/285726@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 97c87111393ac39e33e4f6f5d08b8f4c3cdb82eb\nwpt-pr: 64652\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/mediacapture-record/MediaRecorder-mimetype.html"], "git_node": "fecf107a77c06dbc9aa1fd6c413088f8963fcdb1", "git_parents": ["c68803271015a7a2d88c91731f10c1a8305d001d"], "node": "d4bba0bd2f3fa4b4449cb9b244449dfe6611f17e", "parents": ["479a61a83935ec44671651bfcecb920478de783e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Fraser \u003csimon.fraser@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092930 [wpt PR 64651] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=316939, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nREGRESSION(6/11/2026)?: [macOS iOS] largest-contentful-paint/image-TAO.sub.html is a flaky text failure\n\nThe test was failing with values like \"expected a number greater than or equal to 36.00000000000001 but got 36\".\nThis happens because `performance.now()` is coarsened with a resolution of 1ms, and `entry.renderTime` with 4ms.\nFloating point rounding can cause the reduced-resolution \"now\" time to be fractionally less than the renderTime.\n\nFix with an epsilon of 0.1ms.\n\nUpstream has changed this file since WebKit last imported it, so this applies the change to upstream's current version.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=316939\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/315230@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8a899f0ea33d56be93e2e6d69a21cfb6ded5a580\nwpt-pr: 64651\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/largest-contentful-paint/resources/largest-contentful-paint-helpers.js"], "git_node": "42be437ab3cec342fc7645e48a1e3650a6f47e06", "git_parents": ["fecf107a77c06dbc9aa1fd6c413088f8963fcdb1"], "node": "a50005c6579d13d357cdfdeff4b9da484b275641", "parents": ["d4bba0bd2f3fa4b4449cb9b244449dfe6611f17e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maxim Gorin \u003ccode@mxmgorin.dev\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092932 [wpt PR 64346] - webgl: Keep the sized internal format of texImage2D images, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nwebgl: Keep the sized internal format of texImage2D images\n\nSigned-off-by: Maxim Gorin \u003ccode@mxmgorin.dev\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e536d333f702d979b5136f4dc0c01b27463b444b\nwpt-pr: 64346\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webgl/copyTexImage2D-unsized-effective-format.html"], "git_node": "640450d685291dc765f2ad2e83e5fb554fe1bed4", "git_parents": ["42be437ab3cec342fc7645e48a1e3650a6f47e06"], "node": "baa6370a8c35890d4446772d1bd8ca85ba418f0b", "parents": ["a50005c6579d13d357cdfdeff4b9da484b275641"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Narfinger \u003cNarfinger@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092934 [wpt PR 64639] - script: Use saturating addition in contenteditable code to avoid overflow, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nadd testcase\n\nSigned-off-by: Narfinger \u003cNarfinger@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n\n--\nmove to range\n\nSigned-off-by: Narfinger \u003cNarfinger@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3f85f057355e04d1040414f9afe1a4bb9be16f10, 31985ff3eee794fb564d5af21160c770aa936b52\nwpt-pr: 64639\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/selection/range-larger-than-u32-crash.html"], "git_node": "b74b620e09c9523e38aa0d1868e9007553313abf", "git_parents": ["640450d685291dc765f2ad2e83e5fb554fe1bed4"], "node": "7c5b319af4ccc9c2561c16742ea0b4746491de41", "parents": ["baa6370a8c35890d4446772d1bd8ca85ba418f0b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092935 [wpt PR 64660] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=305221, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[subpixel-inline-layout] Test cases rely on specific default font metrics (part3)\n\nLike webkit.org/b/305212 and 305215, this change removes ambiguity around the assumption that no half-leading is present.\n(see ^^ for details.)\n\nThis includes loading /fonts/ahem.css, from https://commits.webkit.org/325583@main.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=305221\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=329911\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/305395@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: dfced2b3f6913535f8cc6075f29a0cf026255c64\nwpt-pr: 64660\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-position/position-absolute-in-inline-002.html"], "git_node": "2aa15763203e8610649e07c30226579e80516005", "git_parents": ["b74b620e09c9523e38aa0d1868e9007553313abf"], "node": "2a546a84b935672b891eb58b46b3fd6a96a781cf", "parents": ["7c5b319af4ccc9c2561c16742ea0b4746491de41"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092937 [wpt PR 64657] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=17757, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n\u003cbr /\u003e's as direct children of \u003cul\u003e between every two adjecent \u003cli\u003e elements causes misalignment\n\nWhen you set line-height on a \u003cbr\u003e element (e.g. br { line-height: 200px }),\nthe line containing the \u003cbr\u003e should be 200px tall. Instead, the \u003cbr\u003e's\nline-height was completely ignored and the line used the default font height.\n\nTwo things were wrong:\n\n1. inlineLevelBoxAffectsLineBox() returned false for all line break boxes,\n   meaning the \u003cbr\u003e's layout bounds never contributed to the line box height.\n   Fixed: return true when the \u003cbr\u003e has an explicit (non-normal) line-height.\n\n2. The layout bounds for line break boxes were computed using only the parent\n   inline box's font metrics, ignoring the \u003cbr\u003e's own line-height. Fixed:\n   when line-height is explicit, apply the standard CSS half-leading model --\n   compute the leading (line-height minus font metrics height), split it\n   equally above and below the baseline, same as any inline box.\n\nIn quirks mode, there's an additional issue: when a \u003cbr\u003e is the only\ncontentful box on a line, it tells its parent (the root inline box) that\nit has \"content.\" This causes the root inline box's font-metrics-based\nlayout bounds (18px) to stretch the line, regardless of the \u003cbr\u003e's own\nline-height. With explicit line-height, the \u003cbr\u003e should not mark the\nparent as having content -- the \u003cbr\u003e's own layout bounds should drive\nthe line height directly. This lets line-height: 0 collapse the line\nto zero, matching the behavior of other browsers in quirks mode.\n\nThis includes the references and spec links from https://commits.webkit.org/325582@main.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=17757\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=329910\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/310839@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8a8956a2260ac28cbf6d2b041ca2ad1670d14199\nwpt-pr: 64657\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/br-line-height-shrink-quirks-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/br-line-height-shrink-quirks.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/br-line-height-shrink-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/br-line-height-shrink.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/br-line-height-stretch-quirks-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/br-line-height-stretch-quirks.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/br-line-height-zero-quirks-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/br-line-height-zero-quirks.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/br-line-height-zero-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-inline/br-line-height-zero.html"], "git_node": "092d9b0ac034a8f70490c85402484e4f1b51f90a", "git_parents": ["2aa15763203e8610649e07c30226579e80516005"], "node": "8fbfaa2b2ef909b26381254572594fb4012636d6", "parents": ["2a546a84b935672b891eb58b46b3fd6a96a781cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092937 [wpt PR 64657] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64657\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-inline/br-line-height-shrink-quirks.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-inline/br-line-height-stretch-quirks.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-inline/br-line-height-zero-quirks.html.ini"], "git_node": "eac9e824d52322efe4898ff38a8fdceb82c22423", "git_parents": ["092d9b0ac034a8f70490c85402484e4f1b51f90a"], "node": "29cd8964410df79d52cc41103d8340225bf58d5a", "parents": ["8fbfaa2b2ef909b26381254572594fb4012636d6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092942 [wpt PR 64656] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319178, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-text-decor-4] Implement the text-decoration-inset property\n\nAdd the CSS Text Decoration Level 4 'text-decoration-inset' property\n(auto | \u003clength\u003e{1,2}), gated behind the cssTextDecorationInsetEnabled setting.\n\nThe property adjusts the start and end endpoints of the line decorations drawn by\na decorating box (underline, overline, line-through). A positive \u003clength\u003e moves\nan endpoint inward, trimming the decoration; a negative \u003clength\u003e moves it outward,\nextending it. A single value applies to both endpoints; two values are the start\nand the end. 'auto' lets the UA choose an inset so that two adjacent identical\nunderlined elements do not appear to share a single continuous underline (e.g.\nfor Chinese, where underlining is a form of punctuation); it is distinct from 0.\n\n1. It is stored as a new Style::TextDecorationInset value type (a keyword-or-length-\npair) in NonInheritedRareData, parsed grammar-driven, and animated by computed\nvalue.\n2. The inset is applied at paint time in TextBoxPainter, which shifts the\ndecoration's inline origin and shrinks/grows its length (because text-decoration-\ninset and box-decoration-break are not inherited, a decoration that propagates\nfrom an ancestor box down to the (root inline) box that paints it)\n3. box-decoration-break is then honored via the inline box's closed edges: with 'slice' the start\ninset only affects the first fragment's start edge and the end inset the last\nfragment's end edge; with 'clone' both edges of every fragment are inset.\n4. Endpoints are also gated on the marked-text piece that actually reaches the box's\nlogical start/end, so a decoration split into several marked texts (selection,\ndocument markers, highlights) stays continuous instead of being trimmed at the\ninterior boundaries.\n5. Because a negative inset extends the decoration past the text\nbox, decoration ink overflow is expanded by the outward amount, and StyleDifference\ntreats an inset change as affecting repaint and visual overflow so dynamic/animated\nchanges invalidate correctly.\n\nHorizontal and vertical writing modes (including sideways-rl/lr and orthogonal\nblocks), in both inline directions, are supported, as is the text-decoration-skip-\nink interaction (its skip gaps are measured against the underline's bounding box,\nwhich already tracks the inset-shifted origin, so they stay aligned to the glyphs).\nAcross a bidi direction boundary the decoration is painted one segment per run; the\ncomponent of the inset that shifts the decoration as a whole is applied to every\nsegment (so the seam between runs moves with it rather than being pinned), while the\nextend/trim overhang is applied only at the segment reaching the decoration's visual\nstart/end.\n\nThis includes the references and spec links from https://commits.webkit.org/325582@main.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319178\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=329910\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/317230@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 081e5cc919946f348534ed90b6d0548004479964\nwpt-pr: 64656\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-auto-notref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-auto.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-bidi-seam-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-bidi-seam.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-line-through-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-line-through.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-marked-text-gap-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-marked-text-gap.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-negative-notref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-negative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-not-inherited-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-not-inherited.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-one-value-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-one-value.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-overline-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-overline.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-trims-underline-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-trims-underline.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-zero-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-zero.html"], "git_node": "06650357adc9e3dcc2d1d3c9f9cdc47e230bc114", "git_parents": ["eac9e824d52322efe4898ff38a8fdceb82c22423"], "node": "4d90dfa8fc42330876d7a5d0f82f8e6decf997ce", "parents": ["29cd8964410df79d52cc41103d8340225bf58d5a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092944 [wpt PR 64659] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=305264, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[subpixel-inline-layout] Test cases rely on specific default font metrics (part4)\n\nLike webkit.org/b/305212, 305215 and 305221, this change removes ambiguity around the assumption that no half-leading is present.\n\nThis includes loading /fonts/ahem.css, from https://commits.webkit.org/325583@main.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=305264\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=329911\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/305462@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c1562d9698737bf71b9bd9d91a275141052a978e\nwpt-pr: 64659\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/filter-cb-abspos-inline-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/filter-cb-abspos-inline-002.html"], "git_node": "2a0972c732df8698a2c2f57c8f8f33cc3ced70d1", "git_parents": ["06650357adc9e3dcc2d1d3c9f9cdc47e230bc114"], "node": "8cf45486602f64915c339a45fb9d4eb4ed7401cb", "parents": ["4d90dfa8fc42330876d7a5d0f82f8e6decf997ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092944 [wpt PR 64659] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64659\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/filter-effects/filter-cb-abspos-inline-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/filter-effects/filter-cb-abspos-inline-002.html.ini"], "git_node": "15dd191ff369bd58b144f2c6c1586fd37908aebb", "git_parents": ["2a0972c732df8698a2c2f57c8f8f33cc3ced70d1"], "node": "e11bf456e680a86be880ca0fee90a54d2e197d42", "parents": ["8cf45486602f64915c339a45fb9d4eb4ed7401cb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Baradlay \u003czalan@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092945 [wpt PR 64655] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322441, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-text-decor-4] Support percentages in text-decoration-inset\n\nWiden text-decoration-inset from \u003clength\u003e{1,2} to \u003clength-percentage\u003e{1,2}, per\nthe CSSWG resolution on csswg-drafts#8403.\n\nA percentage resolves against the inline size of the decorating box for box-decoration-break: slice, or of the individual box fragment for clone.\nSince a sliced box's inline size spans all of its fragments, TextBoxPainter now sums them (DecoratingBoxFragmentInlineSizes) instead of measuring the fragment being painted.\nThat sum also gives the inline size preceding/following this fragment, so a trimming inset larger than one fragment now carries over\ninto the next - a middle fragment can be trimmed, or vanish, without holding either endpoint of the box.\n\nInk overflow cannot resolve these percentages while building a line, because the basis is not known until every fragment exists.\nInlineContentBuilder therefore collects the decorating boxes whose inset may resolve negative while it walks the display boxes, and\nadds the outward overhang in a follow-up pass over the finished lines.\nStyleDifference compares insets with no basis, where two different percentages would look equal, so a change involving one now requires layout outright.\n\nThis includes the references and spec links from https://commits.webkit.org/325582@main.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=322441\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=329910\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/320052@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 52041a16d37ab4dc01c9d5bd53153d85b9dc9945\nwpt-pr: 64655\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-clone-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-clone.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-equivalence-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-equivalence.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-negative-grow-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-negative-grow.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-negative-incremental-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-negative-incremental.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-negative-layer-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-negative-layer.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-negative-multiline-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-negative-multiline.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-negative-propagated-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-negative-propagated.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-negative-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-negative-repaint-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-negative-repaint.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-negative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-padding-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-padding.html"], "git_node": "407c6e17b75891a97c097d41935ae04eecece173", "git_parents": ["15dd191ff369bd58b144f2c6c1586fd37908aebb"], "node": "40f84d443b3e3b4d242cc738071b722c14a094af", "parents": ["e11bf456e680a86be880ca0fee90a54d2e197d42"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092945 [wpt PR 64655] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64655\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-clone.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-negative-multiline.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-text-decor/text-decoration-inset-percentage-padding.html.ini"], "git_node": "0ccb78a1a89d0d6ca93de1e774f2d3f4c9542c64", "git_parents": ["407c6e17b75891a97c097d41935ae04eecece173"], "node": "f528ffef1cedf3692000554059ca5632c2c3335a", "parents": ["40f84d443b3e3b4d242cc738071b722c14a094af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086348 [wpt PR 64257] - [chromium-bidi] Fix dedicated worker owner realm attachment race, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[chromium-bidi] Fix dedicated worker owner realm attachment race\n\n- Fix dedicated worker realm creation and owner association when a\n  worker is spawned during navigation, and fix dedicated worker context\n  isolation in `get_realms.py`.\n- Previously, worker target attachment detached the worker if the parent\n  session's default window realm was not yet registered in RealmStorage,\n  and `get_realms.py` leaked a dedicated worker across subtests while\n  navigating a backgrounded tab on Android.\n- Keep the dedicated worker target attached when its parent browsing\n  context exists, resolve or await the parent context's default realm\n  when the worker execution context is created, and isolate the worker\n  subtests in `get_realms.py`.\n\nTAG=agy\n\nFixed: 576640075\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.linux:Linux Tests|webdriver_wpt_tests\nCq-Include-Trybots: luci.chromium.try\u200b:linux-webdriver-bidi-rel,linux-blink-rel,android-15-chrome-blink-rel\nChange-Id: I63434640e4346585bf382dcf0d5f4ecaea435aa6\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8664210\nCommit-Queue: Maksim Sadym \u003csadym@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Nikolay Vitkov \u003cnvitkov@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1733930}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: dc70b6d329a2566317f18562ec14449b9272be39\nwpt-pr: 64257\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/script/get_realms/get_realms.py"], "git_node": "1ccf8b7a51230a54c108ab105e042b77d4f9f121", "git_parents": ["0ccb78a1a89d0d6ca93de1e774f2d3f4c9542c64"], "node": "717a49746c514d0ee65d0afb20b22ad361774fad", "parents": ["f528ffef1cedf3692000554059ca5632c2c3335a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086348 [wpt PR 64257] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64257\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/bidi/script/get_realms/type.py.ini"], "git_node": "143be7667042e8532a52ec937536d1bb9f5f3b0c", "git_parents": ["1ccf8b7a51230a54c108ab105e042b77d4f9f121"], "node": "68e445bc35e3003340a683db2aa3538aa9c2ed21", "parents": ["717a49746c514d0ee65d0afb20b22ad361774fad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brent Fulgham \u003cbfulgham@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092948 [wpt PR 64589] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=325512, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFragment URLs for SVG documents in object, embed, or iframe should not scroll\n\nScrolling to a fragment inside a same-origin SVG document loaded in an\n\u003cobject\u003e or \u003ciframe\u003e propagated to the parent document, so a page embedding\ndemo.svg#some-id below the fold loaded scrolled down to the embed.\n\nMatch Chrome: a fragment that names an element in an SVG document in a\nsubframe sets :target and applies the SVG view, but scrolls neither the SVG\ndocument nor the embedding document. Top-level SVG documents still scroll to\nthe target, and HTML subdocuments keep scrolling their parent, as CSSOM\nView's scroll-into-view steps specify. That includes an HTML document in a\nforeignObject of an embedded SVG document, which scrolls the SVG document\nand the top-level document in both Chrome and WebKit.\n\nAlso give scroll-target-into-view-fragment-in-same-origin-subframe.html and embedded-svg-document-fragment-does-not-scroll-parent.tentative.html a long timeout, as they take close to the default one.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=325512\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/324862@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 022a99df64d021beef99ad42bc244475b608ee7b\nwpt-pr: 64589\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom-view/scroll-target-into-view-fragment-in-same-origin-subframe.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom-view/support/scroll-to-fragment-target.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/scroll-to-fragid/embedded-svg-document-fragment-does-not-scroll-parent.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/scroll-to-fragid/embedded-svg-document-fragment-does-not-scroll-svg-document.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/scroll-to-fragid/html-fragment-in-svg-foreign-object-scrolls-ancestors.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/scroll-to-fragid/resources/foreign-object-html-frame.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/scroll-to-fragid/resources/fragment-target.svg", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/scroll-to-fragid/resources/tall-fragment-target.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/scroll-to-fragid/resources/tall-fragment-target.svg"], "git_node": "df705392c207d1c47bd9ab5d4f0922eae08adb7e", "git_parents": ["143be7667042e8532a52ec937536d1bb9f5f3b0c"], "node": "aea1a44f17c2198c0abec8d28450f448c1054a4b", "parents": ["68e445bc35e3003340a683db2aa3538aa9c2ed21"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092948 [wpt PR 64589] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64589\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/cssom-view/scroll-target-into-view-fragment-in-same-origin-subframe.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/scroll-to-fragid/embedded-svg-document-fragment-does-not-scroll-parent.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/scroll-to-fragid/embedded-svg-document-fragment-does-not-scroll-svg-document.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/scroll-to-fragid/html-fragment-in-svg-foreign-object-scrolls-ancestors.html.ini"], "git_node": "5344b83b9d60702f759585b79992de46082aac0c", "git_parents": ["df705392c207d1c47bd9ab5d4f0922eae08adb7e"], "node": "0c7208877f8e170fbc996aa5259fe06858e3b3dd", "parents": ["aea1a44f17c2198c0abec8d28450f448c1054a4b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078016 [wpt PR 63242] - HTML: test noopener popups opened from cross-origin isolated pages, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nHTML: test noopener popups opened from cross-origin isolated pages\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a96f1c801e6f88e0e8f1f23ee2830fc72cadffbd\nwpt-pr: 63242\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/cross-origin-opener-policy/noopener-popup-cross-origin-isolation.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/cross-origin-opener-policy/noopener-popup-cross-origin-isolation.https.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/cross-origin-opener-policy/resources/report-cross-origin-isolation.html"], "git_node": "bff80f0c85032706d21ea3d6a0d548cdfbcf1891", "git_parents": ["5344b83b9d60702f759585b79992de46082aac0c"], "node": "5bd059c9b2c0b6b39362889164b8bf8481e31253", "parents": ["0c7208877f8e170fbc996aa5259fe06858e3b3dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080971 [wpt PR 63569] - Document-Isolation-Policy does not apply to shared and service workers, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDocument-Isolation-Policy does not apply to shared and service workers\n\nThese tests were copied from the Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy tests and\nexpected a Document-Isolation-Policy on a shared or service worker script to\napply to the worker's own requests, and blob: and data: shared workers to\ninherit the policy of their owner or of the blob URL creator.\n\nA shared or service worker is in its own agent cluster and can use\nCross-Origin-Embedder-Policy directly. As the explainer says of service\nworkers, a Document-Isolation-Policy for them would look exactly like\nCross-Origin-Embedder-Policy. Inheriting the policy from the document that\ncreates a shared worker, as the explainer and the specification have it,\nwould make the policy of a worker shared by several documents depend on which\nof them created it. See\nhttps://github.com/WICG/document-isolation-policy/issues/13\n\nExpect the policy to have no effect in shared-workers.tentative.https.html,\ncredentialless-shared-worker.https.tentative.window.js, and\ncredentialless-service-worker.https.tentative.window.js, and add a\nshared-workers.tentative.https.html subtest for an owner with the policy.\nRemove the shared worker variants of the credentialless Cache Storage tests\nand the shared worker environment of the reporting tests, which only tested\nthe policy applying.\n\nAlso rename the Cache Storage tests' service_worker variant to\ndocument_with_service_worker, as it runs in a document controlled by a service\nworker rather than in the service worker, and remove the\ncreateSharedWorkerContext() helper, which nothing uses anymore.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 43f66fcb72f7ef1b1cacdfc97e789ba5e34f92fb\nwpt-pr: 63569\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/credentialless-cache-storage-from-credentialless.https.tentative.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/credentialless-cache-storage-from-none.https.tentative.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/credentialless-cache-storage-from-require-corp.https.tentative.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/credentialless-service-worker.https.tentative.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/credentialless-shared-worker.https.tentative.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/reporting-cache-storage-corp.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/reporting-subresource-corp.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/resources/common.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/document-isolation-policy/shared-workers.tentative.https.html"], "git_node": "4261a15c071ad2879f9346fa802318301a6a60df", "git_parents": ["bff80f0c85032706d21ea3d6a0d548cdfbcf1891"], "node": "7fcc31fcd91bb0ffe4263a31173aaa8a23e7cbe8", "parents": ["5bd059c9b2c0b6b39362889164b8bf8481e31253"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080971 [wpt PR 63569] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 63569\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/document-isolation-policy/credentialless-cache-storage-from-credentialless.https.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/document-isolation-policy/credentialless-cache-storage-from-none.https.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/document-isolation-policy/credentialless-service-worker.https.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/document-isolation-policy/credentialless-shared-worker.https.tentative.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "900316d8e39b803752f0f4c5a6a20fd8f90e4626", "git_parents": ["4261a15c071ad2879f9346fa802318301a6a60df"], "node": "d619f6e867a201fd4a9776ef5ca10165bdebeebf", "parents": ["7fcc31fcd91bb0ffe4263a31173aaa8a23e7cbe8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Sneddon \u003cgsnedders@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092954 [wpt PR 64319] - Avoid timeouts from HTML-in-Canvas tests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAvoid timeouts from HTML-in-Canvas tests\n\nCurrently on wpt.fyi, looking at\n/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/ at 5958ffed26d:\n\n- Chrome takes 1m 21s of which 0m 0s is TIMEOUTs.\n- Edge takes 1m 32s of which 0m 0s is TIMEOUTs.\n- Firefox takes 25m 10s of which 24m 18s is TIMEOUTs.\n- Safari takes 20m 7s of which 18m 46s is TIMEOUTs.\n\nLocally, this takes Firefox down to 29s and Safari to 1m 37s.\n\n--\nfixup! Avoid timeouts from HTML-in-Canvas tests\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 08c50c49588d6afe4405cb79fa4b2eea22078549, 58db7d2234e3e98902d431a22747cd0b4e567849\nwpt-pr: 64319\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/common/reftest-wait.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/animated-clip-path.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/animated-gif-pinned-to-element-image.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/animated-gif.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-in-custom-element-multiple.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-in-custom-element.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/changes-in-paint-event.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/changing-size-in-paint-event.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/fullscreen-child-crash.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/fullscreen-crash.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/hit-test/low-dpi-hit-test.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/iframe.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/ink-overflow.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/invalidation-during-onpaint.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/moved-webgl-canvas.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-invalidation-crash.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-outside-invalidation-crash.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-scroll-crash.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/target-text-ignored-overlay-path-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/resources/CanvasWidget.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/scale.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/scroller-crash.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/video.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/resources/wait-for-canvas-paint.js"], "git_node": "3faf789c379feaaaee87408a2be37785ca13e7e1", "git_parents": ["900316d8e39b803752f0f4c5a6a20fd8f90e4626"], "node": "52e1e2e122f5b5b1184a29bf1f19f1ed206de212", "parents": ["d619f6e867a201fd4a9776ef5ca10165bdebeebf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092954 [wpt PR 64319] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64319\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-animations/inherited-animation-opacity.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-animations/inherited-animation-transform.html.ini"], "git_node": "b6e92a58dd1e458390830e6ce48805899ef1b30e", "git_parents": ["3faf789c379feaaaee87408a2be37785ca13e7e1"], "node": "db3ff0bbcc5914066b060d58cf1bce24b47f357c", "parents": ["52e1e2e122f5b5b1184a29bf1f19f1ed206de212"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antti Koivisto \u003cantti@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092958 [wpt PR 64667] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=329439, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nREGRESSION (318779@main): Text selection highlight is not visible for github.com (#64667)\n\nGitHub sets only custom properties in :root::selection. Since 318779@main highlight pseudo-element styles\ninherit through the highlight cascade, so every element on the page gets a ::selection style. We used\nthe colors of any ::selection style we found, here a transparent background, so the selection was invisible.\n\nImplement paired defaults:\n\nhttps://drafts.csswg.org/css-pseudo-4/#paired-defaults\n\nThe UA default highlight colors are now used unless color or background-color has a cascaded value from\nthe author origin, or inherits one through the highlight cascade. A new style bit records this.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=329439\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/325357@main\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a51ef50ac17afd80b59df6c7015a489836ea3000\nwpt-pr: 64667\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/highlight-cascade/highlight-paired-cascade-007-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/highlight-cascade/highlight-paired-cascade-007.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/highlight-cascade/highlight-paired-cascade-008-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-pseudo/highlight-cascade/highlight-paired-cascade-008.html"], "git_node": "9d36940c4dc47092dc667636e0c2dfdab5deb95b", "git_parents": ["b6e92a58dd1e458390830e6ce48805899ef1b30e"], "node": "77e558e079266cbc96756d63b5c5a7f12bf4ffff", "parents": ["db3ff0bbcc5914066b060d58cf1bce24b47f357c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092958 [wpt PR 64667] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64667\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-pseudo/highlight-cascade/highlight-paired-cascade-008.html.ini"], "git_node": "698c2f516fd77563078166e1a40b9b9a5110bf41", "git_parents": ["9d36940c4dc47092dc667636e0c2dfdab5deb95b"], "node": "38132245b54e1d827943a0805c1856337ed7bf9e", "parents": ["77e558e079266cbc96756d63b5c5a7f12bf4ffff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Fraser \u003csimon.fraser@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092962 [wpt PR 64614] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319703, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Scroll snap] Respect scroll-snap-align for `scrollToAnchor()` and `scrollIntoView()`\n\n`scroll-snap-align`[1] should impact scrolling to anchors, and scrollIntoView per spec.\n\nAdd `adjustScrollAlignmentForScrollSnapAlign()` which computes alignment, and call it\nfrom `LocalFrameView::scrollToAnchor()` and `Element::scrollIntoView()`. In the latter\ncase, it should only override the chosen alignment if the `options` dict doesn't already\ncontain alignment data.\n\n[1] https://drafts.csswg.org/css-scroll-snap-1/#scroll-snap-align\n[2] https://drafts.csswg.org/css-scroll-snap-1/#choosing\n\nThis fixes css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-target-align-001.html and css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-target-align-002.html\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319703\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/317495@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f11952171336ef78505d615f9330658a1bdeef37\nwpt-pr: 64614\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-target-align-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/scroll-target-align-002.html"], "git_node": "d14106f74da9809be11107839664e30c4d1ee361", "git_parents": ["698c2f516fd77563078166e1a40b9b9a5110bf41"], "node": "0496d408ce2f6759c0674ae670748deebfef7d2e", "parents": ["38132245b54e1d827943a0805c1856337ed7bf9e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Youenn Fablet \u003cyouenn@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092965 [wpt PR 64612] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=320083, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd support for sending stream upload data from WebProcess to Network process\n\nAt stream upload start, we assign the FormData a PendingStreamState object.\nThis PendingStreamState object will be given data from the request's ReadableStream via a ReadableStreamToSharedBufferSink.\nThis PendingStreamState object is converyed through the FormData up to WebResourceLoader.\nWebResourceLoader will read the data from the PendingStreamState and send it through IPC to NetworkResourceLoader.\n\nNetworkResourceLoader will then give that data to the PendingStreamState object which will give it to CFNetwork.\n\nCovered by enabled tests.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=320083\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/317846@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 06953bd885cf882beff16c34b2f5abac90c0f24a\nwpt-pr: 64612\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/api/basic/request-upload.h2.any.js"], "git_node": "9f773398b3efb8fdf6ed7a75789536fc78a0de26", "git_parents": ["d14106f74da9809be11107839664e30c4d1ee361"], "node": "788019da76ef1c5a946d840300a8c4b8a5009d13", "parents": ["0496d408ce2f6759c0674ae670748deebfef7d2e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antti Koivisto \u003cantti@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092970 [wpt PR 64668] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=329793, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[layout box merge] Remove the anonymous inline wrappers around display: contents text\n\nA text box with a display:contents DOM parent was wrapped in an anonymous inline\nbox so it could have a unique style. Text boxes now carry a style separately\nfrom the parent element so this is no longer necessary.\n\nThis patch removes the wrapping. This is observable in some very specific cases\nwhere the wrapper acted as an inline box. The new behavior aligns us with the\ncss-inline-3 spec and Firefox:\n\n- The line-height of a display:contents element no longer applies to its text.\n  The line-height of the parent box does.\n- The font of the text stretches the line like a fallback font, only when the\n  line-height of the parent box is normal.\n- In quirks mode the text is content of the parent box, so the line height of\n  the parent box still applies.\n\nIn SVG, text in a display:contents tspan is now shifted with the baseline-shift\nof the parent box, following css-display-3.\n\nInline layout handles text whose style differs from its parent box. The text\nsits on the baseline of its parent inline box and its run rect uses its own font\nmetrics. Wrapping and ink overflow use the text style. The text only fast paths\ntake the text style from the root and its inline boxes, so content with such\ntext doesn't use them. SVG layout and painting take the inherited properties\nfrom the text and baseline-shift, alignment-baseline, outline and vector-effect\nfrom the parent box.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=329793\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/325558@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 221a3887aa459c27acf17f209f805f7738f74200\nwpt-pr: 64668\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-display/display-contents-svg-tspan-baseline-shift-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-display/display-contents-svg-tspan-baseline-shift.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-display/display-contents-svg-tspan-text-fill-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-display/display-contents-svg-tspan-text-fill.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-display/display-contents-text-line-height-quirks.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-display/display-contents-text-line-height-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-display/display-contents-text-line-height.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-display/display-contents-text-only-content-properties-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-display/display-contents-text-only-content-properties.html"], "git_node": "39ec46612b7965690fca5c8f9465ad6e5e3ef1e2", "git_parents": ["9f773398b3efb8fdf6ed7a75789536fc78a0de26"], "node": "ccfbef2b95138c41086fee006f957f0c664bf1e0", "parents": ["788019da76ef1c5a946d840300a8c4b8a5009d13"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092970 [wpt PR 64668] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64668\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-display/display-contents-svg-tspan-baseline-shift.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-display/display-contents-svg-tspan-text-fill.html.ini"], "git_node": "f487b50482e36a2bdcd013c1e81091c029afaadf", "git_parents": ["39ec46612b7965690fca5c8f9465ad6e5e3ef1e2"], "node": "d76ed7377c26c6f062cd3a0bf917adac76ac5680", "parents": ["ccfbef2b95138c41086fee006f957f0c664bf1e0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon Fraser \u003csimon.fraser@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092972 [wpt PR 64615] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319616, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\ncss/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-shape-011.html fails\n\nThis test had arcs with a single radius, requiring us to implement the single-radius\nlogic \u003chttps://drafts.csswg.org/css-shapes-1/#typedef-shape-arc-command\u003e.\n\nUpstream keeps its larger maxDifference (0-127); only totalPixels is raised, to cover WebKit.\n\nWebKit-Bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319616\nWebKit-Canonical-Link: https://commits.webkit.org/317397@main\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7fd1634711e3308dc559cd8bc2b665853d5d8350\nwpt-pr: 64615\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/clip-path-shape-011.html"], "git_node": "17c2761a2c4666869893d5adbd0e0de8bd310598", "git_parents": ["f487b50482e36a2bdcd013c1e81091c029afaadf"], "node": "f7348b78fa3b8ad873c062e3b683ba3f04481a3f", "parents": ["d76ed7377c26c6f062cd3a0bf917adac76ac5680"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092987 [wpt PR 64666] - Preserve autofill state on no-op option.selected assignments, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nPreserve autofill state on no-op option.selected assignments\n\nIn crrev.com/c/8300572, HTMLOptionElement::setSelectedForBinding was\nchanged to call SetSelectedState and OptionSelectionStateChanged\ndirectly when SelectedcontentSpec2 is enabled instead of calling\nSetSelected. Because SetSelected returns early when the option's\nselectedness does not change, bypassing it caused no-op assignments\n(such as re-assigning option.selected = true on an already-selected\noption or option.selected = false on an unselected option) to call\nSelectOption with WebAutofillState::kNotFilled, clearing the \u003cselect\u003e\nelement's autofilled state and notifying AutofillAgent of a user edit.\nFix this by restoring the SetSelected call in setSelectedForBinding.\n\nThis change aligns with https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/13005, where\nsetting the selected IDL attribute on an \u003coption\u003e element only updates\n\u003cselectedcontent\u003e elements when selectedness changes. There is another\npatch coming soon to implement the changes from that spec pr.\n\nFixed: 580550670\nChange-Id: I9b6208cfceb4593c3c4ec21336d227685d4614ce\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8700606\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1734083}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 28fe6a77c30cd6602c87e1e80f69d37c1d52990c\nwpt-pr: 64666\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/customizable-select/selectedcontent.html"], "git_node": "0a1a3344e5f17877c1d34954c123eb73245abfe7", "git_parents": ["17c2761a2c4666869893d5adbd0e0de8bd310598"], "node": "e56a65870bff07080968d647acdfb3d5310cefca", "parents": ["f7348b78fa3b8ad873c062e3b683ba3f04481a3f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Liu \u003clcdavid@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092988 [wpt PR 64565] - [scroll-snap] Don't treat unreachable snap areas as visible, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[scroll-snap] Don't treat unreachable snap areas as visible\n\nSnapSearchResult::visible_range() returns a valid range even when the\nsnap area is entirely outside the snapport. Use RangeF::Intersect()\ninstead to exclude snap areas outside the snapport. Add\nRangeF::ClosedRange() to represent a closed [min, max] range, so that\nareas touching the edge are still considered visible.\n\nAdd WPT snap-to-visible-areas-unreachable.html, covering a snap area in\nnegative overflow, a snap area clipped past the scrollable overflow, and\nzero-width snap areas at the start and end edges.\n\nBug: 473576119\nChange-Id: I06f5cae9389766958b6941223dc8bb3be20c9b09\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8575644\nReviewed-by: Colin Blundell \u003cblundell@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David Liu \u003clcdavid@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1734096}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: efcaa5bb87434ac5c4b258e0aefc87d9552c1ebc\nwpt-pr: 64565\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/snap-to-visible-areas-unreachable.html"], "git_node": "8ef9d7ff730509645e778cc926aa07bd1c9e3b9b", "git_parents": ["0a1a3344e5f17877c1d34954c123eb73245abfe7"], "node": "fb86a771d66c62b1bd137ca7f280a4d41ecbb109", "parents": ["e56a65870bff07080968d647acdfb3d5310cefca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092988 [wpt PR 64565] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 64565\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-scroll-snap/snap-to-visible-areas-unreachable.html.ini"], "git_node": "68e992a018af14453f6942ecbc5b5d7b5e3b5ba5", "git_parents": ["8ef9d7ff730509645e778cc926aa07bd1c9e3b9b"], "node": "c3a666578c84a9a586cb11e6c5e57e32644f5757", "parents": ["fb86a771d66c62b1bd137ca7f280a4d41ecbb109"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092992 [wpt PR 64405] - Invalidate subtree paint when effect reference filters change in place, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nInvalidate subtree paint when effect reference filters change in place\n\nCross-origin frames, plugins, and view-transition content layers strip\nancestor SVG reference filters either during PrePaint\n(SetupContextForFrame) or when recording foreign layers during Paint\n(EmbeddedContentPainter::RemoveSvgFilterPaint and\nEmbeddedContentPainter::EffectForViewTransitionContent).\n\nTrack HasReferenceFilter() changes across ObjectPaintProperties effect\nnodes in FragmentPaintPropertyTreeBuilder::UpdateForSelf and\nPaintPropertyTreeBuilder::InitPaintProperties, and force both an\nisolation-piercing property update and full subtree paint invalidation\nso stacked descendants re-record with the updated effect chain.\n\nR=pdr@chromium.org, szager@chromium.org\n\nBug: 578057132\nChange-Id: I87da722dd22a32ab32d8a5829af65a63143d3fb7\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8674898\nReviewed-by: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1734126}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c38fed4ca156576fc8c743b5b383370ccca4b606\nwpt-pr: 64405\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/iframe-cross-origin-svg-filter-dynamic.tentative.sub.https.html"], "git_node": "1978a11fd2e7c6ca411bef94efab217113b44f8a", "git_parents": ["68e992a018af14453f6942ecbc5b5d7b5e3b5ba5"], "node": "819a435f6a7cb64b4267d5c968a8ec287ace60d9", "parents": ["c3a666578c84a9a586cb11e6c5e57e32644f5757"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093108 - [wpt-sync] Update web-platform-tests to c38fed4ca156576fc8c743b5b383370ccca4b606, a=testonly\n\nMANUAL PUSH: wpt sync bot\n\nwpt-head: c38fed4ca156576fc8c743b5b383370ccca4b606\nwpt-type: landing\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/clipboard-apis/clipboard-copy-selection-line-break.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-conditional/container-queries/whitespace-update-after-removal.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-images/cross-fade-natural-size-gradients.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-images/cross-fade-natural-size-image-and-gradient.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-link-params/link-parameters-typed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-link-params/url-modifier-param-typed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/editing/other/paste-as-plaintext-data.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/editing/plaintext-only/paste.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/encoding/streams/realms.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/metadata/generated/window-location.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/focus/focus-restoration-in-different-site-iframes-window.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/focus/focus-restoration-in-different-site-iframes.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/focus/focus-restoration-in-same-site-iframes-window.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/anchor-positioning.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/animated-clip-path.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/animated-gif-pinned-to-element-image.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/animated-gif.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/backdrop-filter-nested.tentative.html.ini", "testing/