[]}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1939711: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["dom/media/webcodecs/VideoFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "e0f792ad1d1810c89e64db1fcd3cfd6f6fd8665a", "git_parents": ["5351ebe376b18008816d18ab52760fffd2cc7f8b"], "node": "401b0448ea19457d0d77989bba9153c4a0bc8f42", "parents": ["3e7091e9b42fab8346d85f5732020d444e28fb70"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2094410 - Map superblocks in terms of the actual page size. r=layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nPer https://developer.android.com/guide/practices/page-sizes,\n16kb page sizes are not uncommon on Android, so this should ensure\nwe can always decommit memory on those devices.\n\nI tested this by faking PR_GetPageSize()'s return value to 16k on\nLinux, fwiw.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343770\n", "files": ["layout/base/nsPresArena.cpp", "layout/base/nsPresArena.h"], "git_node": "b5fc93e535720ce8698d8de833fe7bac1bc85e6e", "git_parents": ["e0f792ad1d1810c89e64db1fcd3cfd6f6fd8665a"], "node": "854ded272750580e0ea44f2b974fd73991c87ea5", "parents": ["401b0448ea19457d0d77989bba9153c4a0bc8f42"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Luong \u003cgabriel.luong@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093867 - Create the migrated tab group before restoring its tabs r=android-reviewers,android-tabs-reviewers,jdelorenzo\n\n- Restored tabs are already assigned to the closed tab group when they are added, so they no longer show as ungrouped tabs in the tabs tray\n- A failed tab group write no longer leaves ungrouped tabs behind that get duplicated on the next migration attempt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343443\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/tabgroups-storage/src/testFixtures/kotlin/mozilla/components/feature/tabgroups/storage/fakes/FakeTabGroupRepository.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/collections/migration/CollectionsToTabGroupsMigration.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/collections/migration/CollectionsToTabGroupsMigrationTest.kt"], "git_node": "c889ebdfe63ec12ea38fe9bd8e50709ffef5b581", "git_parents": ["b5fc93e535720ce8698d8de833fe7bac1bc85e6e"], "node": "b88921b90f62cd3537566186c0fcc1700099df44", "parents": ["854ded272750580e0ea44f2b974fd73991c87ea5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Luong \u003cgabriel.luong@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093965 - Exclude tabs in closed tab groups from the homepage recent tabs r=android-reviewers,android-tabs-reviewers,jdelorenzo\n\n- Tabs in closed tab groups are hidden from the tabs tray but could still be shown as the homepage recent tab\n- Inactive tabs are still allowed to keep the current recent tab behavior\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343444\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/tabdata-coordinator/src/testFixtures/java/mozilla/components/feature/tabdata/coordinator/fakes/FakeTabDataCoordinator.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ext/BrowserState.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/HomeFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/recenttabs/RecentTabsListFeature.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ext/BrowserStateTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/RecentTabsListFeatureTest.kt"], "git_node": "be4c9fa3f5d411401a46cc2878ae5c0cedd00aed", "git_parents": ["c889ebdfe63ec12ea38fe9bd8e50709ffef5b581"], "node": "c260e01d87e0a484d060c0870f50c4b932d4c0a5", "parents": ["b88921b90f62cd3537566186c0fcc1700099df44"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@intuitionlibrary.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092494 - Resolve a backdrop-filter in a pass-through wrapper from the enclosing surface. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nA WRAPS_BACKDROP_FILTER stacking context is not a backdrop root, so the\nbackdrop must include what both its ancestors and the wrapper itself drew\nbefore the filter. When such a wrapper's complex clips are all rounded\nrectangles, don't give it a surface for them, so it draws into the enclosing\nsurface and its primitives apply the clips. Only skip a wrapper that still has\na surface of its own, and root the backdrop capture at the nearest picture\nwith a surface.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342988\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/clip.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_building.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/backdrop-filter-in-backface-hidden-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/backdrop-filter-in-backface-hidden.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/backdrop-filter-in-clip-surface-content-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/backdrop-filter-in-clip-surface-content.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/backdrop-filter-in-clip-surface.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/backdrop-filter-in-image-mask-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/backdrop-filter-in-image-mask.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/reftest.list", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/filter-effects/backdrop-filter-in-backface-hidden-transform.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/filter-effects/backdrop-filter-in-transform-clip-surface-content.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/backdrop-filter-in-backface-hidden-transform-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/backdrop-filter-in-backface-hidden-transform.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/backdrop-filter-in-transform-clip-surface-content-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/backdrop-filter-in-transform-clip-surface-content.html"], "git_node": "e4ac6b17d3c6d08b98942f5135f8367c2af3f14b", "git_parents": ["be4c9fa3f5d411401a46cc2878ae5c0cedd00aed"], "node": "e1f77c5853cec593200c8ede7a7ef27092348d29", "parents": ["c260e01d87e0a484d060c0870f50c4b932d4c0a5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dana Keeler \u003cdkeeler@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092921 - remote pkcs#11 modules: handle empty profile paths and NSS initialization failure r=jschanck\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D344102\n", "files": ["security/certverifier/NSSCertDBTrustDomain.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/PKCS11ModuleChild.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/test_pkcs11_remote_process_empty_path.js", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/xpcshell-smartcards-remote.toml"], "git_node": "7e6ccce8ece4f1f657b3f49caf0fad15be34dd81", "git_parents": ["e4ac6b17d3c6d08b98942f5135f8367c2af3f14b"], "node": "e7a99a40a0722dacd2336533b488315143e142cc", "parents": ["e1f77c5853cec593200c8ede7a7ef27092348d29"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2094410 - Map memory ourselves in nsPresArena. r=layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nNot sure this is totally worth doing. The potential improvements\nhere are:\n\n * In terms of memory reporting, without this patch purged memory keeps\n   showing as heap-allocated by mozjemalloc, which would show up as\n   heap-unclassified.\n\n * For this exact request, mozjemalloc adds a guard page and rounds up\n   to its 1 MiB chunk size. So a 1 MiB superblock occupied a 2 MiB\n   virtual mapping for its entire lifetime. This only affects virtual\n   addresses, but those are not free in 32-bit systems.\n\nThen again, this is not _trivial_. So I think I lean towards taking it\nbut I could also see an argument for dropping it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343772\n", "files": ["layout/base/nsPresArena.cpp"], "git_node": "fa9ceeae60c7513c76d9e6c35625aada7c50be00", "git_parents": ["7e6ccce8ece4f1f657b3f49caf0fad15be34dd81"], "node": "5dcbbae981ac39c5de94d2f76219019bb192502f", "parents": ["e7a99a40a0722dacd2336533b488315143e142cc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eden Chuang \u003cechuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2090122 - Disconnect ServiceWorker and ServiceWorkerRegistration from their global when unlinked. r=dom-worker-reviewers,asuth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D341750\n", "files": ["dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorker.cpp", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerRegistration.cpp"], "git_node": "fb14d7b55ed9a3ac33ea61b988df11d1dce87a57", "git_parents": ["fa9ceeae60c7513c76d9e6c35625aada7c50be00"], "node": "a1f3389a27c860ad2b0e035c8368b1ecc762d614", "parents": ["5dcbbae981ac39c5de94d2f76219019bb192502f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bryan Olsson \u003cbolsson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2094818 - Add localizer comment for the Arc browser name. r=flod,fluent-reviewers DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D344078\n", "files": ["browser/locales/en-US/browser/migrationWizard.ftl"], "git_node": "f94d9181761525c9ce7d5bac0520508c5c474814", "git_parents": ["fb14d7b55ed9a3ac33ea61b988df11d1dce87a57"], "node": "9672e164429a5e9c803142aa5089b4641be53178", "parents": ["a1f3389a27c860ad2b0e035c8368b1ecc762d614"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bryan Olsson \u003cbolsson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2093755 - Remove trailing period from the HNT mobile card button label. r=fluent-reviewers,omc-reviewers,flod,emcminn\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343327\n", "files": ["browser/locales/en-US/browser/newtab/onboarding.ftl", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2093755_hnt_card_mobile_button_punctuation.py"], "git_node": "81e32dab43c6b55377b6d78c6ebeaecfb5d6650c", "git_parents": ["f94d9181761525c9ce7d5bac0520508c5c474814"], "node": "ebecbabefd2284de435a37d430a8817d2ab5c480", "parents": ["9672e164429a5e9c803142aa5089b4641be53178"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emily Wachowiak \u003cewachowiak@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2094756 - Use title case for New Tab widget menu and submenu items. r=maxx,fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nCapitalize the multi-word items in the New Tab widget menus (for example\n\"Hide Widget\", \"Change Size\", \"Learn More\") in newtab.ftl and\nnewtabPreview.ftl, as decided by the widgets UX writing owner. The change\nis casing only: string IDs and wording are unchanged, so existing\ntranslations stay valid. \"Powered by\" items and single-word items are\nunchanged, and screen-reader-only labels are not touched.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D344045\n", "files": ["browser/locales-preview/newtabPreview.ftl", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl"], "git_node": "d6ee25fa113c6e8e9122a8f306fce97dcc2005ff", "git_parents": ["81e32dab43c6b55377b6d78c6ebeaecfb5d6650c"], "node": "36a3fe4ee5876be839235a3551b4b484e3007897", "parents": ["ebecbabefd2284de435a37d430a8817d2ab5c480"], "tags": []}, {"author": "chloezhouny \u003cchloezhouny@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075706 - Reduce the gap between the model name and description in the Smart Window model picker r=echa\n\nEach model's name and description were almost as far apart as two\nseparate rows, so they did not look like one item. A smaller gap keeps\neach pair together, and the bigger gap now falls between rows.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D344122\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/input-model-select/input-model-select.css"], "git_node": "5896a34f3f8ef00c49e1ea556924a324074a47ad", "git_parents": ["d6ee25fa113c6e8e9122a8f306fce97dcc2005ff"], "node": "3353678049bae735edb20ca23eba2645d106ecd3", "parents": ["36a3fe4ee5876be839235a3551b4b484e3007897"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ting-Yu Lin \u003ctlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2094239 - Add comments to each value in FrameChildListID. r=layout-reviewers,boris\n\nAlso move Absolute and PushedAbsolute after the overflow container lists, so\nthat the lists for in-flow children are together.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D344101\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsFrameList.h"], "git_node": "97905669a0fc51e32690ae9f5aaf7f471347aad4", "git_parents": ["5896a34f3f8ef00c49e1ea556924a324074a47ad"], "node": "8c0997825ddc7b374977fcd01343b7fe79e109c8", "parents": ["3353678049bae735edb20ca23eba2645d106ecd3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2092494 - Resolve a backdrop-filter in a pass-through wrapper from the enclosing surface. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\" for causing wr testa failures at css/filter-effects\n\nThis reverts commit e4ac6b17d3c6d08b98942f5135f8367c2af3f14b.\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/clip.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_building.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/backdrop-filter-in-backface-hidden-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/backdrop-filter-in-backface-hidden.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/backdrop-filter-in-clip-surface-content-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/backdrop-filter-in-clip-surface-content.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/backdrop-filter-in-clip-surface.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/backdrop-filter-in-image-mask-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/backdrop-filter-in-image-mask.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/reftest.list", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/filter-effects/backdrop-filter-in-backface-hidden-transform.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/filter-effects/backdrop-filter-in-transform-clip-surface-content.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/backdrop-filter-in-backface-hidden-transform-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/backdrop-filter-in-backface-hidden-transform.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/backdrop-filter-in-transform-clip-surface-content-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/filter-effects/backdrop-filter-in-transform-clip-surface-content.html"], "git_node": "406a027723f005a999a127fd07f18183dd694ad7", "git_parents": ["97905669a0fc51e32690ae9f5aaf7f471347aad4"], "node": "fd151ee24a42c41dfdea940186cc9f66efa2f883", "parents": ["8c0997825ddc7b374977fcd01343b7fe79e109c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Taimur Hasan \u003cthasan@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2092311 - Speed up the Google Docs extraction test with larger httpd.js segments. r=ai-platform-reviewers,nordzilla\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342435\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pageextractor/tests/browser/browser_google_docs_extraction.js"], "git_node": "c6bcc937d2a78305fcf5e8004bcd7decdc2e2dd0", "git_parents": ["406a027723f005a999a127fd07f18183dd694ad7"], "node": "322feeb75f1786df6574260039cec356e635184a", "parents": ["fd151ee24a42c41dfdea940186cc9f66efa2f883"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Taimur Hasan \u003cthasan@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086888 - Extend the expiry of page_extractor.phase to Firefox 169. r=ai-platform-reviewers,valentinp\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D342434\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pageextractor/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "21f930349525417a52175119271b05e6c74a013e", "git_parents": ["c6bcc937d2a78305fcf5e8004bcd7decdc2e2dd0"], "node": "58fc654018b1341ef847725aab7486de8918c63e", "parents": ["322feeb75f1786df6574260039cec356e635184a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ed Lee \u003cedilee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2094871 - part 1: move the Smart Form Fill source tabs and flow telemetry out of SmartFormFillParent r=omarg\n\nSmartFormFillSources owns which tabs each form draws from, the tab-selector dialog and page-text extraction; the page-text budget and the number of tabs considered become firefox.js prefs\n\nSmartFormFillTelemetry now tracks each form's flow, field decisions and source-editor use, and implements the controller's RequestObserver callbacks; the controller still only receives callbacks, as asked in D317197, and this is the follow-up D325479 left for later\n\nSmartFormFillParent.sys.mjs drops under 1,500 lines and off the AGENTS.md list, as does ChatStore.sys.mjs after bug 2091433 part 3\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343760\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/AGENTS.md", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/actors/SmartFormFillParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/SmartFormFillController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/SmartFormFillSources.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/SmartFormFillTelemetry.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/moz.build"], "git_node": "cc90457d785e222b92c2c54cab70177ecf85ef0e", "git_parents": ["21f930349525417a52175119271b05e6c74a013e"], "node": "f54d89f8c727f5c0712a371d3a9431a12f9273a9", "parents": ["58fc654018b1341ef847725aab7486de8918c63e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ed Lee \u003cedilee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2094871 - part 2: move the Smart Window toolbar buttons out of AIWindow r=gcardieri\n\nAIWindowToolbarButtons owns the ask button and the switcher, Organize Tabs and monitor CustomizableUI buttons with private members, its own observers and the monitor attention API\n\nthe Organize Tabs and monitor panels take their widget IDs and overflow anchor from it, and the buttons and SpecialMessageActions call AutoTabGrouping and MonitorPanel directly instead of through AIWindowUI\n\nAIWindow.sys.mjs drops under 1,500 lines and off the AGENTS.md list\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D343759\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/AGENTS.md", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AIWindow.sys.mjs", "bro